{"id": "8", "question": "what is the difference between tartate and succinate", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between tartate and succinate is their chemical derivation: succinate is derived from succinic acid while tartrate is derived from tartaric acid. Additionally, succinate is an extended-release drug that stays in the bloodstream for 24 hours, making it a once-per-day pill. On the other hand, tartrate is an immediate-release drug that does not stay in the bloodstream for 24 hours and needs to be taken at regular intervals. Another important difference is that succinate has a greater dehydrating effect and may cause side effects like constipation and dry mouth, whereas tartrate may cause diarrhea and sleep issues like insomnia or unusual dreams.", "pred": "The key difference between tartate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartate is derived from the tartaric acid.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The key difference between tartate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartate is derived from the tartaric acid.", "cot": "[\"The key difference between tartate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartate is derived from the tartaric acid.\", \"The key difference between tartarate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartarate is derived from the tartaric acid.\", \"The key difference between tartrate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartrate is derived from the tartaric acid.\", \"The key difference between tartate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartate is derived from the tartaric acid. Succinic acid is ethan-1,2-dicarboxylic acid. Succinate form of metoprolol is an extended release drug and it plays its role in the circulatory system for 24 hours. However, the tartrate form of metoprolol does not appear in the blood stream for 24 hours because metoprolol tartrate is an immediate-release drug.\"]", "time_sec": 15.655, "generation_time_seconds": 14.6562, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8876, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 1376, 6672, 1948, 44815, 349, 323, 20038, 3277, 374, 429, 20038, 3277, 374, 14257, 504, 279, 20038, 92335, 13621, 323, 44815, 349, 374, 14257, 504, 279, 44815, 277, 292, 13621, 13, 151645], "pred": "The key difference between tartate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartate is derived from the tartaric acid.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.103140950202942, "g_worst_claim": 1.103140950202942, "g_content": 1.8655792872111003, "g_traj_mean": 1.0711240768432617}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 1376, 6672, 1948, 44815, 277, 349, 323, 20038, 3277, 374, 429, 20038, 3277, 374, 14257, 504, 279, 20038, 92335, 13621, 323, 44815, 277, 349, 374, 14257, 504, 279, 44815, 277, 292, 13621, 13, 151645], "pred": "The key difference between tartarate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartarate is derived from the tartaric acid.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0656304078943588, "g_worst_claim": 1.0656304078943588, "g_content": 1.9394184748331706, "g_traj_mean": 1.0385900735855103}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 1376, 6672, 1948, 12183, 376, 349, 323, 20038, 3277, 374, 429, 20038, 3277, 374, 14257, 504, 279, 20038, 92335, 13621, 323, 12183, 376, 349, 374, 14257, 504, 279, 44815, 277, 292, 13621, 13, 151645], "pred": "The key difference between tartrate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartrate is derived from the tartaric acid.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1250840355368221, "g_worst_claim": 1.1250840355368221, "g_content": 2.158784866333008, "g_traj_mean": 1.0929970741271973}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 1376, 6672, 1948, 44815, 349, 323, 20038, 3277, 374, 429, 20038, 3277, 374, 14257, 504, 279, 20038, 92335, 13621, 323, 44815, 349, 374, 14257, 504, 279, 44815, 277, 292, 13621, 13, 88179, 92335, 13621, 374, 8372, 276, 12, 16, 11, 17, 1737, 292, 277, 2011, 88, 415, 13621, 13, 88179, 3277, 1352, 315, 2270, 453, 1080, 337, 374, 458, 11577, 4879, 5506, 323, 432, 11088, 1181, 3476, 304, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 369, 220, 17, 19, 4115, 13, 4354, 11, 279, 12183, 376, 349, 1352, 315, 2270, 453, 1080, 337, 1558, 537, 4994, 304, 279, 6543, 4269, 369, 220, 17, 19, 4115, 1576, 2270, 453, 1080, 337, 12183, 376, 349, 374, 458, 13922, 44724, 5506, 13, 151645], "pred": "The key difference between tartate and succinate is that succinate is derived from the succinic acid and tartate is derived from the tartaric acid. Succinic acid is ethan-1,2-dicarboxylic acid. Succinate form of metoprolol is an extended release drug and it plays its role in the circulatory system for 24 hours. However, the tartrate form of metoprolol does not appear in the blood stream for 24 hours because metoprolol tartrate is an immediate-release drug.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7300896950752702, "g_worst_claim": 0.6633928087022569, "g_content": 2.6808119274321056, "g_traj_mean": 1.7216248512268066}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 28.89, "GAVIE-Rel": 3.3, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "16", "question": "wat is dna", "gt": "Based on the given passages, DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid) is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone, with the base pairs forming the ladder's rungs and the sugar and phosphate molecules forming the vertical sidepieces of the ladder. The order of the nitrogen bases in a DNA sequence forms genes, which provide the instructions for making proteins.", "pred": "DNA, or deoxyribonucleic acid, is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone. It is the hereditary material in humans and almost all other organisms. DNA contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and one of four nitrogen bases: adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines the genetic code, which in the language of the cell, tells cells how to make proteins. DNA also has the ability to replicate, making copies of itself.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "DNA, or deoxyribonucleic acid, is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone. It is the hereditary material in humans and almost all other organisms. DNA contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and one of four nitrogen bases: adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines the genetic code, which in the language of the cell, tells cells how to make proteins. DNA also has the ability to replicate, making copies of itself.", "cot": "[\"DNA is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The four types of nitrogen bases are adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines DNA's instructions, or genetic code, which tells cells how to make proteins. DNA is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone.\", \"DNA, or deoxyribonucleic acid, is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone. It is the hereditary material in humans and almost all other organisms. DNA contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and one of four nitrogen bases: adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines the genetic code, which in the language of the cell, tells cells how to make proteins. DNA also has the ability to replicate, making copies of itself.\", \"DNA is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone. DNA is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base (adenine, thymine, guanine, or cytosine). The order of these bases determines DNA's instructions, or genetic code, and forms genes that tell cells how to make proteins. DNA's role in the cell is to store genetic information and replicate itself.\", \"DNA is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and one of the four nitrogen bases: adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines the genetic code, which instructs cells on how to make proteins.\"]", "time_sec": 23.032, "generation_time_seconds": 22.0147, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0053, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [55320, 374, 264, 30384, 292, 13621, 429, 5610, 279, 18929, 11221, 1483, 304, 279, 4401, 323, 30201, 315, 678, 3881, 5382, 43204, 323, 1045, 40968, 13, 1084, 374, 1865, 705, 315, 34615, 2598, 30384, 354, 3341, 11, 1817, 8482, 264, 78006, 1874, 11, 264, 13163, 1874, 11, 323, 264, 46403, 2331, 13, 576, 3040, 4494, 315, 46403, 23092, 525, 99113, 482, 320, 32, 701, 270, 1600, 482, 320, 51, 701, 1675, 91256, 320, 38, 701, 323, 9503, 42581, 482, 320, 34, 568, 576, 1973, 315, 1493, 23092, 26569, 15552, 594, 11221, 11, 476, 18929, 2038, 11, 892, 10742, 7761, 1246, 311, 1281, 27796, 13, 15552, 374, 264, 1990, 11338, 941, 14122, 553, 2331, 13530, 12392, 311, 264, 13163, 62737, 92373, 55427, 13, 151645], "pred": "DNA is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base. The four types of nitrogen bases are adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines DNA's instructions, or genetic code, which tells cells how to make proteins. DNA is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.93774351910775, "g_worst_claim": 0.017073456730161394, "g_content": 1.717434777153863, "g_traj_mean": 0.9493257999420166}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [55320, 11, 476, 409, 60163, 1897, 263, 22147, 292, 13621, 11, 374, 264, 1990, 11338, 941, 14122, 553, 2331, 13530, 12392, 311, 264, 13163, 62737, 92373, 55427, 13, 1084, 374, 279, 1059, 94354, 3684, 304, 12677, 323, 4558, 678, 1008, 43204, 13, 15552, 5610, 279, 18929, 11221, 1483, 304, 279, 4401, 323, 30201, 315, 678, 3881, 5382, 43204, 323, 1045, 40968, 13, 1084, 374, 1865, 705, 315, 34615, 2598, 30384, 354, 3341, 11, 1817, 8482, 264, 78006, 1874, 11, 264, 13163, 1874, 11, 323, 825, 315, 3040, 46403, 23092, 25, 99113, 482, 320, 32, 701, 270, 1600, 482, 320, 51, 701, 1675, 91256, 320, 38, 701, 323, 9503, 42581, 482, 320, 34, 568, 576, 1973, 315, 1493, 23092, 26569, 279, 18929, 2038, 11, 892, 304, 279, 4128, 315, 279, 2779, 11, 10742, 7761, 1246, 311, 1281, 27796, 13, 15552, 1083, 702, 279, 5726, 311, 45013, 11, 3259, 10993, 315, 5086, 13, 151645], "pred": "DNA, or deoxyribonucleic acid, is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone. It is the hereditary material in humans and almost all other organisms. DNA contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and one of four nitrogen bases: adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines the genetic code, which in the language of the cell, tells cells how to make proteins. DNA also has the ability to replicate, making copies of itself.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7762434295181663, "g_worst_claim": 0.019771633403641835, "g_content": 1.3151998050877305, "g_traj_mean": 0.7783781886100769}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [55320, 374, 264, 30384, 292, 13621, 429, 5610, 279, 18929, 11221, 1483, 304, 279, 4401, 323, 30201, 315, 678, 3881, 5382, 43204, 323, 1045, 40968, 13, 1084, 374, 264, 1990, 11338, 941, 14122, 553, 2331, 13530, 12392, 311, 264, 13163, 62737, 92373, 55427, 13, 15552, 374, 1865, 705, 315, 34615, 2598, 30384, 354, 3341, 11, 1817, 8482, 264, 78006, 1874, 11, 264, 13163, 1874, 11, 323, 264, 46403, 2331, 320, 21140, 482, 11, 270, 1600, 482, 11, 1675, 91256, 11, 476, 9503, 42581, 482, 568, 576, 1973, 315, 1493, 23092, 26569, 15552, 594, 11221, 11, 476, 18929, 2038, 11, 323, 7586, 20727, 429, 3291, 7761, 1246, 311, 1281, 27796, 13, 15552, 594, 3476, 304, 279, 2779, 374, 311, 3553, 18929, 1995, 323, 45013, 5086, 13, 151645], "pred": "DNA is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is a double helix formed by base pairs attached to a sugar-phosphate backbone. DNA is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and a nitrogen base (adenine, thymine, guanine, or cytosine). The order of these bases determines DNA's instructions, or genetic code, and forms genes that tell cells how to make proteins. DNA's role in the cell is to store genetic information and replicate itself.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0621757771187081, "g_worst_claim": 0.41475290060043335, "g_content": 1.6929166024191338, "g_traj_mean": 0.9502401947975159}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [55320, 374, 264, 30384, 292, 13621, 429, 5610, 279, 18929, 11221, 1483, 304, 279, 4401, 323, 30201, 315, 678, 3881, 5382, 43204, 323, 1045, 40968, 13, 1084, 374, 1865, 705, 315, 34615, 2598, 30384, 354, 3341, 11, 1817, 8482, 264, 78006, 1874, 11, 264, 13163, 1874, 11, 323, 825, 315, 279, 3040, 46403, 23092, 25, 99113, 482, 320, 32, 701, 270, 1600, 482, 320, 51, 701, 1675, 91256, 320, 38, 701, 323, 9503, 42581, 482, 320, 34, 568, 576, 1973, 315, 1493, 23092, 26569, 279, 18929, 2038, 11, 892, 21066, 82, 7761, 389, 1246, 311, 1281, 27796, 13, 151645], "pred": "DNA is a nucleic acid that contains the genetic instructions used in the development and functioning of all known living organisms and some viruses. It is made up of molecules called nucleotides, each containing a phosphate group, a sugar group, and one of the four nitrogen bases: adenine (A), thymine (T), guanine (G), and cytosine (C). The order of these bases determines the genetic code, which instructs cells on how to make proteins.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6234491290795106, "g_worst_claim": -0.005240890596594129, "g_content": 1.1194237499702266, "g_traj_mean": 0.5896912813186646}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.61, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.8, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "20", "question": "how to grill a porterhouse", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nThe provided passages do not contain any information or instructions on how to grill a Porterhouse steak specifically. While they do provide general guidance on setting up a grill and preparing the grill grate, they do not offer any specific advice or steps for cooking a Porterhouse steak. Therefore, I cannot provide a response based on the given passages.", "pred": "To grill a porterhouse, follow these steps:\n\n1. Leave the section closest to you coal-free.\n2. Replace the grill grate.\n3. If using a gas grill, set it up for three-zone grilling.\n4. Keep it hot, keep it clean, keep it lubricated: When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil. \n\nThese steps are based on the provided passages and are intended to prepare the grill for cooking the porterhouse steak.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To grill a porterhouse, follow these steps:\n\n1. Leave the section closest to you coal-free.\n2. Replace the grill grate.\n3. If using a gas grill, set it up for three-zone grilling.\n4. Keep it hot, keep it clean, keep it lubricated: When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil. \n\nThese steps are based on the provided passages and are intended to prepare the grill for cooking the porterhouse steak.", "cot": "[\"To grill a porterhouse, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Leave the section closest to you coal-free.\\n2. Replace the grill grate.\\n3. If using a gas grill, set it up for three-zone grilling.\\n4. Keep it hot, keep it clean, keep it lubricated: When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil.\\n\\nThese steps ensure that the grill is properly prepared for cooking the porterhouse steak.\", \"To grill a porterhouse, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Leave the section closest to you coal-free.\\n2. Replace the grill grate.\\n3. If using a gas grill, set it up for three-zone grilling.\\n4. Keep it hot, keep it clean, keep it lubricated: When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil. \\n\\nThese steps are based on the provided passages and are intended to prepare the grill for cooking the porterhouse steak.\", \"To grill a porterhouse, leave the section closest to you coal-free. Replace the grill grate. If using a gas grill, set it up for three-zone grilling. Keep it hot, keep it clean, keep it lubricated: When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil.\", \"To grill a porterhouse, follow these steps:\\n1. Leave the section closest to you coal-free.\\n2. Replace the grill grate.\\n3. If using a gas grill, set it up for three-zone grilling.\\n4. Keep it hot, keep it clean, keep it lubricated: When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil.\"]", "time_sec": 19.769, "generation_time_seconds": 18.8987, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8601, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 39058, 264, 87186, 7675, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 25193, 279, 3772, 18093, 311, 498, 11497, 12577, 624, 17, 13, 29558, 279, 39058, 85354, 624, 18, 13, 1416, 1667, 264, 6819, 39058, 11, 738, 432, 705, 369, 2326, 77763, 1081, 9400, 624, 19, 13, 13655, 432, 4017, 11, 2506, 432, 4240, 11, 2506, 432, 53394, 657, 25, 3197, 279, 39058, 85354, 374, 4017, 11, 4240, 432, 448, 264, 39058, 15625, 11, 1221, 53394, 349, 432, 448, 264, 39058, 5590, 261, 476, 264, 47035, 5567, 42613, 72207, 304, 35481, 5590, 382, 9485, 7354, 5978, 429, 279, 39058, 374, 10277, 10030, 369, 17233, 279, 87186, 7675, 48959, 13, 151645], "pred": "To grill a porterhouse, follow these steps:\n\n1. Leave the section closest to you coal-free.\n2. Replace the grill grate.\n3. If using a gas grill, set it up for three-zone grilling.\n4. Keep it hot, keep it clean, keep it lubricated: When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil.\n\nThese steps ensure that the grill is properly prepared for cooking the porterhouse steak.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.365143847528589, "g_worst_claim": 0.14173408349355063, "g_content": 2.6954443359375, "g_traj_mean": 1.9542196989059448}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 39058, 264, 87186, 7675, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 25193, 279, 3772, 18093, 311, 498, 11497, 12577, 624, 17, 13, 29558, 279, 39058, 85354, 624, 18, 13, 1416, 1667, 264, 6819, 39058, 11, 738, 432, 705, 369, 2326, 77763, 1081, 9400, 624, 19, 13, 13655, 432, 4017, 11, 2506, 432, 4240, 11, 2506, 432, 53394, 657, 25, 3197, 279, 39058, 85354, 374, 4017, 11, 4240, 432, 448, 264, 39058, 15625, 11, 1221, 53394, 349, 432, 448, 264, 39058, 5590, 261, 476, 264, 47035, 5567, 42613, 72207, 304, 35481, 5590, 13, 4710, 9485, 7354, 525, 3118, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 323, 525, 10602, 311, 10549, 279, 39058, 369, 17233, 279, 87186, 7675, 48959, 13, 151645], "pred": "To grill a porterhouse, follow these steps:\n\n1. Leave the section closest to you coal-free.\n2. Replace the grill grate.\n3. If using a gas grill, set it up for three-zone grilling.\n4. Keep it hot, keep it clean, keep it lubricated: When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil. \n\nThese steps are based on the provided passages and are intended to prepare the grill for cooking the porterhouse steak.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.3658241635417494, "g_worst_claim": 0.14173408349355063, "g_content": 2.6336892934945912, "g_traj_mean": 1.8706618547439575}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 39058, 264, 87186, 7675, 11, 5274, 279, 3772, 18093, 311, 498, 11497, 12577, 13, 29558, 279, 39058, 85354, 13, 1416, 1667, 264, 6819, 39058, 11, 738, 432, 705, 369, 2326, 77763, 1081, 9400, 13, 13655, 432, 4017, 11, 2506, 432, 4240, 11, 2506, 432, 53394, 657, 25, 3197, 279, 39058, 85354, 374, 4017, 11, 4240, 432, 448, 264, 39058, 15625, 11, 1221, 53394, 349, 432, 448, 264, 39058, 5590, 261, 476, 264, 47035, 5567, 42613, 72207, 304, 35481, 5590, 13, 151645], "pred": "To grill a porterhouse, leave the section closest to you coal-free. Replace the grill grate. If using a gas grill, set it up for three-zone grilling. Keep it hot, keep it clean, keep it lubricated: When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.5613203703490717, "g_worst_claim": 1.3944132668631417, "g_content": 3.460227754380968, "g_traj_mean": 2.4695370197296143}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 39058, 264, 87186, 7675, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 25193, 279, 3772, 18093, 311, 498, 11497, 12577, 624, 17, 13, 29558, 279, 39058, 85354, 624, 18, 13, 1416, 1667, 264, 6819, 39058, 11, 738, 432, 705, 369, 2326, 77763, 1081, 9400, 624, 19, 13, 13655, 432, 4017, 11, 2506, 432, 4240, 11, 2506, 432, 53394, 657, 25, 3197, 279, 39058, 85354, 374, 4017, 11, 4240, 432, 448, 264, 39058, 15625, 11, 1221, 53394, 349, 432, 448, 264, 39058, 5590, 261, 476, 264, 47035, 5567, 42613, 72207, 304, 35481, 5590, 13, 151645], "pred": "To grill a porterhouse, follow these steps:\n1. Leave the section closest to you coal-free.\n2. Replace the grill grate.\n3. If using a gas grill, set it up for three-zone grilling.\n4. Keep it hot, keep it clean, keep it lubricated: When the grill grate is hot, clean it with a grill brush, then lubricate it with a grill oiler or a folded paper towel dipped in vegetable oil.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.5382884535492893, "g_worst_claim": 0.1419262488683065, "g_content": 3.1094589233398438, "g_traj_mean": 2.235154867172241}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 25.24, "GAVIE-Rel": 2.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "21", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "gt": "Magellan of Virginia is the Behavioral Health Services Administrator for the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services. They administer behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. The site is also for providers, offering them resources like weekly Q&A sessions each Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. where they can address their questions and issues. Additionally, they offer continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses, approved by organizations like the American Psychological Association and the Association of Social Work Boards.", "pred": "Magellan of Virginia is the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They ensure quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees, partnering with members, providers, and stakeholders.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Magellan of Virginia is the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They ensure quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees, partnering with members, providers, and stakeholders.", "cot": "[\"Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They host weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.\", \"Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They host provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.\", \"Magellan of Virginia is the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They ensure quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees, partnering with members, providers, and stakeholders.\", \"Magellan of Virginia offers continuing education clock hours/credits for the e-learning courses listed on a specific page, and it is approved to offer CE clock hours/credits by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB). Magellan of Virginia also serves as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs, ensuring quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees. The site is for members receiving behavioral health services, their families and friends, and providers, with the mission to improve the overall health and well-being of Virginians. Additionally, Magellan of Virginia hosts a weekly call each Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. for all providers to address their questions and issues.\"]", "time_sec": 15.353, "generation_time_seconds": 14.8218, "selection_time_seconds": 0.5224, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [32915, 84786, 315, 12989, 5707, 35595, 2820, 3516, 369, 3613, 36091, 304, 12989, 748, 33029, 323, 434, 1402, 1637, 7468, 13, 2379, 3468, 17059, 9109, 1207, 35021, 15704, 389, 79423, 504, 220, 16, 281, 744, 13, 311, 220, 17, 25, 18, 15, 281, 744, 13, 151645], "pred": "Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They host weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.771091545952691, "g_worst_claim": 0.45557530721028644, "g_content": 3.012045487113621, "g_traj_mean": 1.9784746170043945}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [32915, 84786, 315, 12989, 5707, 35595, 2820, 3516, 369, 3613, 36091, 304, 12989, 748, 33029, 323, 434, 1402, 1637, 7468, 13, 2379, 3468, 9109, 1207, 35021, 15704, 389, 79423, 504, 220, 16, 281, 744, 13, 311, 220, 17, 25, 18, 15, 281, 744, 13, 151645], "pred": "Magellan 