{"id": "22", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "gt": "Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They ensure the delivery of quality behavioral health services to Virginia Medicaid enrollees and work towards improving the overall health and well-being of Virginians. They also offer continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses and host weekly Q&A sessions for providers to address their questions and issues.", "pred": "Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They host weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They host weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.", "cot": "[\"Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They host weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.\", \"Magellan of Virginia provides continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses and hosts weekly Provider Q&A Sessions on Fridays.\", \"Based on the information provided in the passages, Magellan of Virginia offers continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses through the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB). Additionally, Magellan of Virginia serves as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for Virginia Medicaid and FAMIS programs, ensuring quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees. They also provide provider Q&A sessions on Fridays.\", \"Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. The company ensures quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees and works to improve the overall health and well-being of Virginians. They also offer continuing education clock hours/credits for their e-learning courses, approved by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB). Additionally, Magellan of Virginia hosts a weekly call each Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. known as Provider Q&A Sessions, which is open to all providers to address their questions and issues.\"]", "time_sec": 15.47, "generation_time_seconds": 14.8961, "selection_time_seconds": 0.5675, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [32915, 84786, 315, 12989, 5707, 35595, 2820, 3516, 369, 3613, 36091, 304, 12989, 748, 33029, 323, 434, 1402, 1637, 7468, 13, 2379, 3468, 17059, 9109, 1207, 35021, 15704, 389, 79423, 504, 220, 16, 281, 744, 13, 311, 220, 17, 25, 18, 15, 281, 744, 13, 151645], "pred": "Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They host weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7588981085984166, "g_worst_claim": 0.4417937331729465, "g_content": 2.9847428695015283, "g_traj_mean": 1.9580119848251343}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [32915, 84786, 315, 12989, 5707, 14354, 6731, 8866, 4115, 14, 55769, 369, 384, 70756, 13980, 323, 18432, 17059, 22916, 1207, 35021, 30800, 389, 79423, 13, 151645], "pred": "Magellan of Virginia provides continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses and hosts weekly Provider Q&A Sessions on Fridays.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 3.649142150878906, "g_worst_claim": 3.649142150878906, "g_content": 4.908059120178223, "g_traj_mean": 3.524913787841797}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": tr