{"id": "24", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nMagellan of Virginia does offer continuing education clock hours/credits for their e-learning courses. According to passage 1, Magellan is approved to offer CE clock hours/credits by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB).\n\nAdditionally, Magellan of Virginia has been selected by the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services (DMAS) to serve as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. This is mentioned in passage 2.\n\nFinally, Magellan of Virginia offers a Provider Q&A Session every Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. for providers to address their questions and issues. This is mentioned in passage 3.", "pred": "Magellan of Virginia provides provider Q&A sessions on Fridays. These sessions are open to all providers and take place each Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. The sessions are designed for providers to address their questions and issues. These calls continue until further notice.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Magellan of Virginia provides provider Q&A sessions on Fridays. These sessions are open to all providers and take place each Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. The sessions are designed for providers to address their questions and issues. These calls continue until further notice.", "cot": "[\"Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They host weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.\", \"Magellan of Virginia provides provider Q&A sessions on Fridays. These sessions are open to all providers and take place each Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. The sessions are designed for providers to address their questions and issues. These calls continue until further notice.\", \"Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They also offer continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses and host weekly provider Q&A sessions.\", \"Based on the information provided in the passages, Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services in Virginia, specifically for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They offer continuing education clock hours/credits through e-learning courses and host weekly provider Q&A sessions.\"]", "time_sec": 12.808, "generation_time_seconds": 12.1012, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6986, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [32915, 84786, 315, 12989, 5707, 35595, 2820, 3516, 369, 3613, 36091, 304, 12989, 748, 33029, 323, 434, 1402, 1637, 7468, 13, 2379, 3468, 17059, 9109, 1207, 35021, 15704, 389, 79423, 504, 220, 16, 281, 744, 13, 311, 220, 17, 25, 18, 15, 281, 744, 13, 151645], "pred": "Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They host weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8543383076077413, "g_worst_claim": 0.4388776620229085, "g_content": 3.318434010381284, "g_traj_mean": 2.0937893390655518}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [32915, 84786, 315, 12989, 5707, 9109, 1207, 35021, 15704, 389, 79423, 13, 4220, 15704, 525, 1787, 311, 678, 12565, 323, 1896, 1992, 1817, 6602, 504, 220, 16, 281, 744, 13, 311, 220, 17, 25, 18, 15, 281, 744, 13, 576, 15704, 525, 6188, 369, 12565, 311, 2621, 862, 4755, 323, 4714, 13, 4220, 6738, 3060, 3080, 4623, 5293, 13, 151645], "pred": "Magellan of Virginia provides provider Q&A sessions on Fridays. These sessions are open to all providers and take place each Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. The sessions are designed for providers to address their questions and issues. These calls continue until further notice.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.221969542660556, "g_worst_claim": 0.3646175066630046, "g_content": 3.1331075032552085, "g_traj_mean": 2.0666069984436035}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [32915, 84786, 315, 12989, 5707, 35595, 2820, 3516, 369, 3613, 36091, 304, 12989, 594, 33029, 323, 434, 1402, 1637, 7468, 13, 2379, 1083, 3010, 14354, 6731, 8866, 4115, 14, 55769, 369, 384, 70756, 13980, 323, 3468, 17059, 9109, 1207, 35021, 15704, 13, 151645], "pred": "Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They also offer continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses and host weekly provider Q&A sessions.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.9236025129045755, "g_worst_claim": 2.3071190970284596, "g_content": 4.119610595703125, "g_traj_mean": 2.868427276611328}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 1995, 3897, 304, 279, 46769, 11, 6879, 84786, 315, 12989, 374, 264, 9109, 315, 35595, 2820, 3516, 304, 12989, 11, 11689, 369, 3613, 36091, 304, 12989, 594, 33029, 323, 434, 1402, 1637, 7468, 13, 2379, 3010, 14354, 6731, 8866, 4115, 14, 55769, 1526, 384, 70756, 13980, 323, 3468, 17059, 9109, 1207, 35021, 15704, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the information provided in the passages, Magellan of Virginia is a provider of behavioral health services in Virginia, specifically for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They offer continuing education clock hours/credits through e-learning courses and host weekly provider Q&A sessions.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.867318702500964, "g_worst_claim": 0.5145601166619195, "g_content": 3.2227369739163305, "g_traj_mean": 2.142465591430664}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "err