{"id": "26", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.\n\nThe provided passages do not mention anything about Magellan of Virginia's status as a provider or its relationship with other providers. Passage 1 discusses Magellan's ability to offer continuing education credits, while Passage 2 explains its role as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator for Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Passage 3 mentions a weekly call for providers to ask questions and address issues, but it does not provide information about Magellan's status as a provider. Therefore, I cannot answer the question based on the given passages.", "pred": "Magellan of Virginia provides a range of services to Virginia Medicaid enrollees and their families. These services include continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses through the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB). They also administer behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Magellan has a mission to ensure quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees. Partnering with members, providers, and stakeholders, they work to improve the overall health and well-being of Virginians. Magellan also hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. to address any questions or issues that providers may have.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Magellan of Virginia provides a range of services to Virginia Medicaid enrollees and their families. These services include continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses through the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB). They also administer behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Magellan has a mission to ensure quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees. Partnering with members, providers, and stakeholders, they work to improve the overall health and well-being of Virginians. Magellan also hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. to address any questions or issues that providers may have.", "cot": "[\"Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They host weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.\", \"Answer: Magellan of Virginia provides continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses approved by organizations such as the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB). They also administer behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia's Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Additionally, Magellan of Virginia hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.\", \"Magellan of Virginia provides a range of services to Virginia Medicaid enrollees and their families. These services include continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses through the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB). They also administer behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. Magellan has a mission to ensure quality behavioral health services are delivered to Virginia Medicaid enrollees. Partnering with members, providers, and stakeholders, they work to improve the overall health and well-being of Virginians. Magellan also hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. to address any questions or issues that providers may have.\", \"Based on the provided information, Magellan of Virginia is a company that offers continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses related to behavioral health services. They have been approved by the American Psychological Association (APA) and the Association of Social Work Boards (ASWB). Magellan of Virginia also serves as the Behavioral Health Services Administrator (BHSA) for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They provide quality behavioral health services to Virginia Medicaid enrollees and partner with members, providers, and stakeholders to improve healthcare delivery and overall health and well-being of Virginians. Additionally, they host provider Q&A sessions on Fridays for all providers to address their questions and issues.\"]", "time_sec": 19.652, "generation_time_seconds": 19.1198, "selection_time_seconds": 0.5236, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [32915, 84786, 315, 12989, 5707, 35595, 2820, 3516, 369, 3613, 36091, 304, 12989, 748, 33029, 323, 434, 1402, 1637, 7468, 13, 2379, 3468, 17059, 9109, 1207, 35021, 15704, 389, 79423, 504, 220, 16, 281, 744, 13, 311, 220, 17, 25, 18, 15, 281, 744, 13, 151645], "pred": "Magellan of Virginia provides behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. They host weekly provider Q&A sessions on Fridays from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8570858031984356, "g_worst_claim": 0.4589236577351888, "g_content": 3.2718794449515967, "g_traj_mean": 2.0888020992279053}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 6879, 84786, 315, 12989, 5707, 14354, 6731, 8866, 4115, 14, 55769, 369, 384, 70756, 13980, 11792, 553, 11104, 1741, 438, 279, 3693, 68969, 10024, 320, 88669, 8, 323, 279, 10024, 315, 9784, 5547, 71086, 320, 1911, 52868, 568, 2379, 1083, 26093, 35595, 2820, 3516, 369, 3613, 36091, 304, 12989, 594, 33029, 323, 434, 1402, 1637, 7468, 13, 22406, 11, 6879, 84786, 315, 12989, 18432, 17059, 9109, 1207, 35021, 15704, 389, 79423, 504, 220, 16, 281, 744, 13, 311, 220, 17, 25, 18, 15, 281, 744, 13, 15