ll-being of Virginians. Additionally, they host provider Q&A sessions on Fridays for all providers to address their questions and issues.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7576031780156713, "g_worst_claim": 0.2495843768119812, "g_content": 2.9972462373621322, "g_traj_mean": 1.9179953336715698}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 22.97, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "27", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "To fix a door that won't lock, first try to align the door latch with the hole in the strike plate. If the latch is misaligned, you can perform a lipstick test to see where the latch contacts the strike plate. If it contacts too high or too low, tighten all the door's hinge screws. You may also need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb or move the strike plate. If this doesn't work, shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb, pry it up until it comes loose and remove it. Replace the door stop back on the jamb, set back 1/4 inch from its original location. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "pred": "If the latch still doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, you can use the \"lipstick test\" to check the alignment. If the latch contacts the strike plate too high or too low, make sure all the door's hinge screws are tight.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "If the latch still doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, you can use the \"lipstick test\" to check the alignment. If the latch contacts the strike plate too high or too low, make sure all the door's hinge screws are tight.", "cot": "[\"To fix a door that won't lock, you can try the following steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut the door and try to lock it.** If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. **Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.** Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n3. **Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.**\\n4. **Lace the door stop back on the jamb.** Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop.\\n5. **Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.** The door should now shut and lock normally.\\n\\nIf the door latch won't catch, you may also need to:\\n- **Enlarge the latch hole in the jamb.**\\n- **Tighten the hinges first.**\\n- **Enlarge the strike plate hole.**\\n- **Move the strike plate.**\\n\\nIf the latch still doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, you can use the \\\"lipstick test\\\" to check the alignment. If the latch contacts the strike plate too high or too low, make sure all the door's hinge screws are tight.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, you should first shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, first try closing the door and attempting to lock it. If it doesn't lock, open the door and tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. Align the door stop using the distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off and nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.\\n\\nAnswer: To fix a door that won't lock, first try closing the door and attempting to lock it. If it doesn't lock, open the door and tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. Align the door stop using the distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off and nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, you can try the following steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut the door and try to lock it.** If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. **Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.** Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n3. **Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.** Be sure to set the door stop back on the jamb.\\n4. **Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.** You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this line to align the door stop.\\n5. **Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.** The door should now shut and lock normally.\"]", "time_sec": 37.099, "generation_time_seconds": 35.9402, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1402, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 498, 646, 1430, 279, 2701, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2016, 332, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 334, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 17, 13, 3070, 23879, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 334, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 624, 18, 13, 3070, 10253, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 13, 1019, 19, 13, 3070, 43, 578, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 334, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 13, 5443, 419, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 20, 