4, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 11, 6243, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 13, 49472, 279, 6006, 2936, 1667, 279, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 323, 30995, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "pred": "To fix a door that won't lock, first try closing the door and attempting to lock it. If it doesn't lock, open the door and tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. Align the door stop using the distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off and nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0527261949901898, "g_worst_claim": -0.0011847779298057924, "g_content": 1.546016486116158, "g_traj_mean": 1.036105990409851}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 498, 646, 1430, 279, 2701, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2016, 332, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 334, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 17, 13, 3070, 23879, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 334, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 624, 18, 13, 3070, 10253, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 13, 334, 2823, 2704, 311, 738, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 624, 19, 13, 3070, 1649, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 13, 334, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 13, 5443, 419, 1555, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 20, 13, 3070, 45, 604, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 13, 334, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. **Shut the door and try to lock it.** If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. **Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.** Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\n3. **Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.** Be sure to set the door stop back on the jamb.\n4. **Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.** You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this line to align the door stop.\n5. **Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.** The door should now shut and lock normally.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.694127720543273, "g_worst_claim": 0.1149903933207194, "g_content": 2.4625217334644214, "g_traj_mean": 1.6975514888763428}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 35.48, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "28", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "To fix a door that won't lock, you can try the following steps based on the given passages:\n1. Close the door and attempt to lock it.\n2. If it doesn't lock, open the door and use a chisel to tap and pry off the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Remove the top door stop as well.\n3. Place the door stop back on the jamb, aligning it 1/4 inch from its original location using the distinct line left behind.\n4. Nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on.\n5. If the latch still doesn't catch, tighten the hinges first.\n6. Enlarge the latch hole in the jamb if necessary.\n7. Enlarge the strike plate hole or move the strike plate if the latch doesn't align with it.\n8. Ensure all the door's hinge screws are tight.\nFollowing these steps should help fix the door lock issue.", "pred": "To fix a door that won't lock, first shut the door and try to lock it. If it still won't lock, open the door and tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Once the door stop is removed, set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To fix a door that won't lock, first shut the door and try to lock it. If it still won't lock, open the door and tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Once the door stop is removed, set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "cot": "[\"To fix a door that won't lock, you can try the following steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut the door and try to lock it.** If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. **Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.** Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n3. **Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.**\\n4. **Lace the door stop back on the jamb.** Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop.\\n5. **Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.** The door should now shut and lock normally.\\n\\nIf the door latch won't catch, you may also need to:\\n- **Enlarge the latch hole in the jamb.**\\n- **Tighten the hinges first.**\\n- **Enlarge the strike plate hole.**\\n- **Move the strike plate.**\\n\\nIf the latch still doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, you can use the \\\"lipstick test\\\" to check the alignment. If the latch contacts the strike plate too high or too low, make sure all the door's hinge screws are tight.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, you can try the following steps:\\n\\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. Use a chisel to remove the door stop on the striker side of the jamb by tapping it under the door stop until it comes loose. Remove the door stop on top as well.\\n3. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\\n4. Use the chisel to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\\n5. After completing these steps, the door should shut and lock normally.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, first shut the door and try to lock it. If it still won't lock, open the door and tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Once the door stop is removed, set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut the Door and Try to Lock It**: If the door won't lock, open it first. This step helps identify if the issue is with the lock mechanism or the door itself.\\n\\n2. **Tap the End of a Chisel Under the Door Stop**: Use a chisel to tap under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. This action helps loosen the door stop.\\n\\n3. **Pry Up on It Until It Comes Loose and Remove It**: Continue prying until the door stop comes loose and can be removed. This step is crucial as it allows access to the internal components of the door.\\n\\n4. **Remove the Door Stop on Top**: Remove the door stop on the top as well. This ensures all fasteners are removed, allowing for easier adjustment.\\n\\n5. **Reattach the Door Stop**: Once the door stop is loose, you can reattach it by setting it back on the jamb. Adjust it by moving it back 1/4 inch from its original location. This step helps realign the door stop for proper function.\\n\\n6. **Align the Door Stop**: Ensure the door stop is aligned properly. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this line as a guide to align the door stop accurately.\\n\\n7. **Nail the Side and Top Pieces of Door Stop Back On**: Secure the side and top pieces of the door stop back onto the jamb. This step ensures the door stop is firmly in place.\\n\\n8. **Test the Door**: After reattaching the door stop, test the door to ensure it shuts and locks normally. This final check confirms that all adjustments have been made correctly.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively fix a door that won't lock. Each step is designed to ensure the door stop is properly aligned and secured, allowing the door to function correctly.\"]", "time_sec": 38.074, "generation_time_seconds": 37.2562, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8083, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 498, 646, 1430, 279, 2701, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2016, 332, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 334, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 17, 13, 3070, 23879, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 334, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 624, 18, 13, 3070, 10253, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 13, 1019, 19, 13, 3070, 43, 578, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 334, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 13, 5443, 419, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 20, 13, 3070, 45, 604, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 13, 334, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 382, 2679, 279, 6006, 56926, 2765, 944, 2287, 11, 498, 1231, 1083, 1184, 311, 510, 12, 3070, 1702, 16767, 279, 56926, 14178, 304, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 1019, 12, 3070, 51, 491, 268, 279, 79834, 1156, 13, 1019, 12, 3070, 1702, 16767, 279, 13169, 11968, 14178, 13, 1019, 12, 3070, 9860, 279, 13169, 11968, 13, 56177, 2679, 279, 56926, 2058, 3171, 944, 5285, 448, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 13169, 11968, 11, 498, 646, 990, 279, 330, 33115, 29033, 1273, 1, 311, 1779, 279, 17189, 13, 1416, 279, 56926, 18508, 279, 13169, 11968, 2238, 1550, 476, 2238, 3347, 11, 1281, 2704, 678, 279, 6006, 594, 75593, 44922, 525, 10296, 13, 151645], "pred": "If the latch still doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, you can use the \"lipstick test\" to check the alignment. If the latch contacts the strike plate too high or too low, make sure all the door's hinge screws are tight.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8274301488258773, "g_worst_claim": 0.08418271938959758, "g_content": 2.734780640728706, "g_traj_mean": 1.800842046737671}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 498, 646, 1430, 279, 2701, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 48274, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 17, 13, 5443, 264, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 553, 52628, 432, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 13, 10783, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 624, 18, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 624, 20, 13, 4636, 26568, 1493, 7354, 11, 279, 6006, 1265, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\n2. Use a chisel to remove the door stop on the striker side of the jamb by tapping it under the door stop until it comes loose. Remove the door stop on top as well.\n3. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\n4. Use the chisel to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n5. After completing these steps, the door should shut and lock normally.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5975281969361583, "g_worst_claim": 0.072030504544576, "g_content": 2.073175372499408, "g_traj_mean": 1.5318900346755981}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1156, 9311, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2058, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 323, 15239, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 13, 9646, 279, 6006, 2936, 374, 6963, 11, 738, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 13, 5443, 419, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "pred": "To fix a door that won't lock, first shut the door and try to lock it. If it still won't lock, open the door and tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Once the door stop is removed, set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8807428725040711, "g_worst_claim": 0.017332497451986586, "g_content": 2.7961319211929565, "g_traj_mean": 1.9808013439178467}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2016, 332, 279, 24191, 323, 9735, 311, 15701, 1084, 95518, 1416, 279, 6006, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 432, 1156, 13, 1096, 3019, 8609, 10542, 421, 279, 4265, 374, 448, 279, 5296, 16953, 476, 279, 6006, 5086, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 23879, 279, 3972, 315, 264, 910, 65294, 9449, 279, 24191, 14215, 95518, 5443, 264, 521, 65294, 311, 15239, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 1096, 1917, 8609, 82742, 279, 6006, 2936, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 47, 884, 3138, 389, 1084, 28970, 1084, 53228, 86002, 323, 10783, 1084, 95518, 15003, 548, 7024, 3080, 279, 6006, 2936, 4041, 20174, 323, 646, 387, 6963, 13, 1096, 3019, 374, 16587, 438, 432, 6147, 2615, 311, 279, 5306, 6813, 315, 279, 6006, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 13021, 279, 24191, 14215, 389, 6909, 95518, 10783, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 1909, 438, 1632, 13, 1096, 25351, 678, 4937, 18223, 525, 6963, 11, 10693, 369, 8661, 27075, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 693, 16330, 279, 24191, 14215, 95518, 9646, 279, 6006, 2936, 374, 20174, 11, 498, 646, 312, 16330, 432, 553, 6243, 432, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 27196, 432, 553, 7218, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 13, 1096, 3019, 8609, 1931, 622, 279, 6006, 2936, 369, 6169, 729, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 10069, 279, 24191, 14215, 95518, 29279, 279, 6006, 2936, 374, 26118, 10277, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 13, 5443, 419, 1555, 438, 264, 8474, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 29257, 382, 22, 13, 3070, 45, 604, 279, 16659, 323, 6909, 67540, 315, 24191, 14215, 6841, 1913, 95518, 34502, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 9666, 315, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 8630, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 1096, 3019, 25351, 279, 6006, 2936, 374, 31520, 304, 1992, 382, 23, 13, 3070, 2271, 279, 24191, 95518, 4636, 312, 1587, 11829, 279, 6006, 2936, 11, 1273, 279, 6006, 311, 5978, 432, 88578, 323, 31676, 14279, 13, 1096, 1590, 1779, 42396, 429, 678, 32974, 614, 1012, 1865, 12440, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 13444, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 13, 8886, 3019, 374, 6188, 311, 5978, 279, 6006, 2936, 374, 10277, 26118, 323, 26430, 11, 10693, 279, 6006, 311, 729, 12440, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can effectively fix a door that won't lock. Each step is designed to ensure the door stop is properly aligned and secured, allowing the door to function correctly.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7930331789879186, "g_worst_claim": -0.06544818083445231, "g_content": 1.2298609275185601, "g_traj_mean": 0.8774998784065247}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 54.75, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "30", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to fix a door that won't lock:\n\nPassage 1 provides tips on how to repair stuck or frozen door locks, keys that don’t work, and latches that don’t latch. However, it does not specifically address the issue of a door that won't lock.\n\nPassage 2 provides instructions on how to fix a door that won't shut or lock properly by removing the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and aligning it back on. This method might work for doors that won't lock due to a misaligned door stop.\n\nPassage 3 provides additional troubleshooting steps for when a door latch won't catch due to misalignment with the strike plate. This passage suggests enlarging the latch hole in the jamb, tightening the hinges, and moving the strike plate to align with the latch.\n\nIn summary, there is no definitive solution in the provided passages to fix a door that won't lock directly. However, these passages provide general tips and troubleshooting steps that may help identify and resolve related issues such as misaligned door stops or latches. If the problem persists after trying these methods, it may be best to consult a professional locksmith or carpenter.", "pred": "To fix a door that won't lock, first try shutting the door and attempting to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Then, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry up on it until it comes loose, then remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Afterward, align the door stop back on the jamb by setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. This should create a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it was removed. Use this line to align the door stop and nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To fix a door that won't lock, first try shutting the door and attempting to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Then, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry up on it until it comes loose, then remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Afterward, align the door stop back on the jamb by setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. This should create a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it was removed. Use this line to align the door stop and nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "cot": "[\"To fix a door that won't lock, you can try the following steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut the door and try to lock it.** If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. **Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.** Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n3. **Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.**\\n4. **Lace the door stop back on the jamb.** Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop.\\n5. **Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.** The door should now shut and lock normally.\\n\\nIf the door latch won't catch, you may also need to:\\n- **Enlarge the latch hole in the jamb.**\\n- **Tighten the hinges first.**\\n- **Enlarge the strike plate hole.**\\n- **Move the strike plate.**\\n\\nIf the latch still doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, you can use the \\\"lipstick test\\\" to check the alignment. If the latch contacts the strike plate too high or too low, make sure all the door's hinge screws are tight.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, close the door and try to lock it. If it doesn't lock, open the door and tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back a quarter inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.\\n\\nAnother possible fix if the latch hole in the jamb is too small is to enlarge it. Tighten the hinges first, and then enlarge the strike plate hole. Move the strike plate. If the door latch won't catch because it doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, make sure all the door's hinge screws are tight.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, you should first try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door and use the end of a chisel to tap under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and then remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Next, place the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. This should create a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this line to align the door stop and then nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on. The door should now close and lock normally.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, first try shutting the door and attempting to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Then, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry up on it until it comes loose, then remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Afterward, align the door stop back on the jamb by setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. This should create a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it was removed. Use this line to align the door stop and nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.\"]", "time_