6, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 323, 990, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 311, 15239, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 1221, 4057, 432, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 13, 9295, 11, 1992, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 11, 6243, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 13, 1096, 1265, 1855, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 13, 5443, 419, 1555, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 323, 1221, 30995, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 9666, 315, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 3265, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "pred": "To fix a door that won't lock, you should first try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door and use the end of a chisel to tap under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and then remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Next, place the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. This should create a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this line to align the door stop and then nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on. The door should now close and lock normally.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7816510320734416, "g_worst_claim": 1.0253677368164062, "g_content": 2.6619288517878608, "g_traj_mean": 1.817789077758789}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1156, 1430, 50026, 279, 6006, 323, 19405, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 13, 5005, 11, 15239, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 323, 81279, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 11, 1221, 4057, 432, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 13, 4636, 1606, 11, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 553, 6243, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 13, 1096, 1265, 1855, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 572, 6963, 13, 5443, 419, 1555, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 323, 30995, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 9666, 315, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "pred": "To fix a door that won't lock, first try shutting the door and attempting to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Then, tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry up on it until it comes loose, then remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Afterward, align the door stop back on the jamb by setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. This should create a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it was removed. Use this line to align the door stop and nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7813249833789684, "g_worst_claim": 1.0734708574083116, "g_content": 2.6301299586440576, "g_traj_mean": 1.8174309730529785}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 24.04, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "31", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to fix a door that won't lock:\n\n1. Check the door stop: According to passage 2, if the door won't lock, try tapping the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Then, place the door stop back on the jamb, setting it back 1/4 inch from its original location. This should allow the door to shut and lock normally.\n2. Adjust the latch hole: If the latch doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, you may need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb, as suggested in passage 3. Before doing so, tighten the hinges first. Additionally, you may need to enlarge the strike plate hole and move the strike plate.\n\nIf the passages do not provide sufficient information to answer the question, the response would be: \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "pred": "This method helps to ensure that the door operates smoothly and securely when locked.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "This method helps to ensure that the door operates smoothly and securely when locked.", "cot": "[\"To fix a door that won't lock, you can try the following steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut the door and try to lock it.** If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. **Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.** Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n3. **Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.**\\n4. **Lace the door stop back on the jamb.** Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop.\\n5. **Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.** The door should now shut and lock normally.\\n\\nIf the door latch won't catch, you may also need to:\\n- **Enlarge the latch hole in the jamb.**\\n- **Tighten the hinges first.**\\n- **Enlarge the strike plate hole.**\\n- **Move the strike plate.**\\n\\nIf the latch still doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, you can use the \\\"lipstick test\\\" to check the alignment. If the latch contacts the strike plate too high or too low, make sure all the door's hinge screws are tight.\", \"If the door won't lock, the first step is to close the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door and tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, first shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Close the door and try to lock it. If it doesn't lock, open the door.\\n2. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n3. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\\n4. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop.\\n5. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.\\n\\nThis method helps to ensure that the door operates smoothly and securely when locked.\"]", "time_sec": 29.477, "generation_time_seconds": 28.5612, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9078, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 498, 646, 1430, 279, 2701, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2016, 332, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 334, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 17, 13, 3070, 23879, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 334, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 624, 18, 13, 3070, 10253, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 13, 1019, 19, 13, 3070, 43, 578, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 334, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 13, 5443, 419, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 20, 13, 3070, 45, 604, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 13, 334, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 382, 2679, 279, 6006, 56926, 2765, 944, 2287, 11, 498, 1231, 1083, 1184, 311, 510, 12, 3070, 1702, 16767, 279, 56926, 14178, 304, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 1019, 12, 3070, 51, 491, 268, 279, 79834, 1156, 13, 1019, 12, 3070, 1702, 16767, 279, 13169, 11968, 14178, 13, 1019, 12, 3070, 9860, 279, 13169, 11968, 13, 56177, 2679, 279, 56926, 2058, 3171, 944, 5285, 448, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 13169, 11968, 11, 498, 646, 990, 279, 330, 33115, 29033, 1273, 1, 311, 1779, 279, 17189, 13, 1416, 279, 56926, 18508, 279, 13169, 11968, 2238, 1550, 476, 22