 2.142784744406503, "g_worst_claim": 0.9231603486197335, "g_content": 2.996901512145996, "g_traj_mean": 2.063842535018921}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1156, 9311, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 13, 36134, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 13, 5443, 419, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "pred": "To fix a door that won't lock, first shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0334989778019397, "g_worst_claim": 1.1003137164645724, "g_content": 2.9960131645202637, "g_traj_mean": 2.1016855239868164}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 13032, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 3171, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 17, 13, 36134, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 624, 18, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 624, 19, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 13, 5443, 419, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 20, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 382, 1986, 1714, 8609, 311, 5978, 429, 279, 6006, 26057, 38411, 323, 51023, 979, 16061, 13, 151645], "pred": "This method helps to ensure that the door operates smoothly and securely when locked.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7870540857609702, "g_worst_claim": 0.2211779276529948, "g_content": 2.498504247420873, "g_traj_mean": 1.756371259689331}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 1.64, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "32", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a possible solution to fix a door that won't lock:\n\n1. Check if the door stops are properly aligned. If the door stops are not aligned, use a chisel to remove the door stop on the striker side of the jamb and pry it up until it comes loose. Remove the door stop and use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Place the door stop back on the jamb and set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\n2. Check if the latch hole in the jamb is properly aligned with the strike plate. If the latch doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, tighten the hinges first. Then, enlarge the strike plate hole. Move the strike plate if necessary.\n\nIf these steps do not solve the problem, it may be necessary to seek further assistance from a professional locksmith or carpenter.", "pred": "5. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "5. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "cot": "[\"To fix a door that won't lock, you can try the following steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut the door and try to lock it.** If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. **Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb.** Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n3. **Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.**\\n4. **Lace the door stop back on the jamb.** Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop.\\n5. **Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.** The door should now shut and lock normally.\\n\\nIf the door latch won't catch, you may also need to:\\n- **Enlarge the latch hole in the jamb.**\\n- **Tighten the hinges first.**\\n- **Enlarge the strike plate hole.**\\n- **Move the strike plate.**\\n\\nIf the latch still doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, you can use the \\\"lipstick test\\\" to check the alignment. If the latch contacts the strike plate too high or too low, make sure all the door's hinge screws are tight.\", \"First, close the door. If it won't lock, open the door. Tap the end of a chisel under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, you should follow these steps:\\n\\n1. First, shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\\n2. Use the end of a chisel to tap under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n3. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\\n4. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location.\\n5. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop.\\n6. Nail the side and top piece of door stop back on.\\n7. The door should now shut and lock normally.\\n8. If the latch doesn't align with the hole in the strike plate, you may need to enlarge the latch hole in the jamb, tighten the hinges, enlarge the strike plate hole, and move the strike plate.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you should be able to fix a door that won't lock.\", \"To fix a door that won't lock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shut the door and try to lock it. If it won't lock, open the door.\\n\\n2. Take a chisel and tap the end under the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Pry up on it until it comes loose and remove it.\\n\\n3. Use the chisel to remove the door stop on top as well.\\n\\n4. Lace the door stop back on the jamb. Set it back 1/4 inch from its original location. You should see a distinct line in the paint, stain, or varnish where it came off. Use this to align the door stop.\\n\\n5. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.\"]", "time_sec": 32.438, "generation_time_seconds": 31.1123, "selection_time_seconds": 1.3124, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 498, 646, 1430, 279, 2701, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2016, 332, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 334, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 17, 13, 3070, 23879, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 334, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 624, 18, 13, 3070, 10253, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 13, 1019, 19, 13, 3070, 43, 578, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 334, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 13, 5443, 419, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 20, 13, 3070, 45, 604, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 13, 334, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 382, 2679, 279, 6006, 56926, 2765, 944, 2287, 11, 498, 1231, 1083, 1184, 311, 510, 12, 3070, 1702, 16767, 279, 56926, 14178, 304, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 1019, 12, 3070, 51, 491, 268, 279, 79834, 1156, 13, 1019, 12, 3070, 1702, 16767, 279, 13169, 11968, 14178, 13, 1019, 12, 3070, 9860, 279, 13169, 11968, 13, 56177, 2679, 279, 56926, 2058, 317