nd lock normally.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.022367815278534, "g_worst_claim": 0.753143310546875, "g_content": 3.2030145677469544, "g_traj_mean": 2.180593490600586}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 498, 1265, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5512, 11, 9311, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 624, 17, 13, 5443, 279, 835, 315, 264, 521, 65294, 311, 15239, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 624, 18, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 624, 19, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 624, 20, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 13, 5443, 419, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 624, 21, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 624, 22, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 624, 23, 13, 1416, 279, 56926, 3171, 944, 5285, 448, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 13169, 11968, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 52644, 279, 56926, 14178, 304, 279, 502, 2969, 11, 66745, 279, 79834, 11, 52644, 279, 13169, 11968, 14178, 11, 323, 3271, 279, 13169, 11968, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 1265, 387, 2952, 311, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you should be able to fix a door that won't lock.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7674231905089552, "g_worst_claim": -0.028528983776385967, "g_content": 2.4743256521697092, "g_traj_mean": 1.6260169744491577}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 6006, 429, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 48274, 279, 6006, 323, 1430, 311, 5296, 432, 13, 1416, 432, 2765, 944, 5296, 11, 1787, 279, 6006, 382, 17, 13, 11778, 264, 521, 65294, 323, 15239, 279, 835, 1212, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 279, 43941, 3108, 315, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 73414, 705, 389, 432, 3080, 432, 4041, 20174, 323, 4057, 432, 382, 18, 13, 5443, 279, 521, 65294, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 2936, 389, 1909, 438, 1632, 382, 19, 13, 74139, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 279, 502, 2969, 13, 2573, 432, 1182, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 504, 1181, 4024, 3728, 13, 1446, 1265, 1490, 264, 12460, 1555, 304, 279, 6177, 11, 51964, 11, 476, 762, 96839, 1380, 432, 3697, 1007, 13, 5443, 419, 311, 5285, 279, 6006, 2936, 382, 20, 13, 74428, 279, 3108, 323, 1909, 6573, 315, 279, 6006, 2936, 1182, 389, 13, 576, 6006, 1265, 1431, 9311, 323, 5296, 14279, 13, 151645], "pred": "5. Nail the side and top piece of the door stop back on. The door should now shut and lock normally.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8443791281766206, "g_worst_claim": 0.30675331751505536, "g_content": 2.6025476590008805, "g_traj_mean": 1.8443669080734253}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 15.25, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "33", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "To cook pollock, first preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper and place them on the baking sheet. Layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which should take about 15 minutes. If desired, turn the oven off, place two slices of cheese on each fillet and return fish to the oven to allow cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.", "pred": "To cook pollock, follow these steps: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit (175 degrees Celsius). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with sliced onions, green peppers, and tomatoes. Bake the pollock in the preheated oven until it is cooked and flakes easily, which takes about 15 minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To cook pollock, follow these steps: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit (175 degrees Celsius). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with sliced onions, green peppers, and tomatoes. Bake the pollock in the preheated oven until it is cooked and flakes easily, which takes about 15 minutes.", "cot": "[\"To cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\n4. After the fillets have cooked, turn off the oven.\\n5. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n6. Return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\\n\\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\", \"To cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Place the pollock fillets on a baking sheet.\\n4. Layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\\n5. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\\n6. Turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n7. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.\\n\\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, place the fillets on a baking sheet, layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices, bake until the fish is cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fish to the oven to allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.\", \"1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\\n4. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they are cooked and flakes easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\n5. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n6. Return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, taking about 3 minutes.\", \"To cook pollock, follow these steps: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit (175 degrees Celsius). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with sliced onions, green peppers, and tomatoes. Bake the pollock in the preheated oven until it is cooked and flakes easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\"]", "time_sec": 26.391, "generation_time_seconds": 25.7248, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6605, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 52074, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 4636, 279, 1461, 9942, 614, 29105, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 624, 20, 13, 10771, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 21, 13, 3411, 279, 1461, 9942, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 382, 16141, 25, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 701, 3200, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 11, 22544, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 11, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 11, 323, 470, 279, 1461, 9942, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6182771883339324, "g_worst_claim": 