0, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "To cook pollock, first preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit (175 degrees Celsius). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which takes about 15 minutes. Turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fish to the oven. Allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1356493650766415, "g_worst_claim": 0.4073515189321418, "g_content": 1.6289511626621462, "g_traj_mean": 1.1173443794250488}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 2014, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 1461, 9942, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 624, 19, 13, 22735, 279, 1461, 9942, 448, 37327, 11, 6176, 24353, 11, 323, 41020, 34254, 624, 20, 13, 52074, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 21, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 23387, 624, 22, 13, 10771, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 23, 13, 3411, 279, 1461, 9942, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "To cook pollock, follow these steps:", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0504808194797288, "g_worst_claim": -0.0036024153232574463, "g_content": 1.3324228102161038, "g_traj_mean": 0.9237757325172424}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 85.71, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "35", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "To cook pollock, first, preheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Then, season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Next, place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. Bake in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes, or until the fish flakes easily. If desired, you can also add cheese on top of the pollock fillets and bake for an additional 3 minutes to melt the cheese.", "pred": "To cook pollock, preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes. After removing the fish from the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet. Return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To cook pollock, preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes. After removing the fish from the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet. Return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "cot": "[\"To cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\n4. After the fillets have cooked, turn off the oven.\\n5. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n6. Return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\\n\\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\", \"To cook pollock, you first need to preheat your oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. After seasoning, place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with slices of onion, green pepper, and tomatoes. Then, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they are cooked and the flesh flakes easily, which should take about 15 minutes.\", \"Step 1: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\\nStep 2: Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\nStep 3: Bake the pollock fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flakes easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\nStep 4: After the pollock fillets have cooked, remove them from the oven.\\nStep 5: Place two slices of cheese on top of each fillet.\\nStep 6: Return the pollock fillets with cheese to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\\nAnswer:[Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit, season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the pollock fillets until they have cooked and flakes easily, which takes about 15 minutes, place two slices of cheese on top of each fillet, return the pollock fillets with cheese to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.]\", \"To cook pollock, preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes. After removing the fish from the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet. Return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\"]", "time_sec": 27.42, "generation_time_seconds": 26.7277, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6843, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 52074, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 4636, 279, 1461, 9942, 614, 29105, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 624, 20, 13, 10771, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 21, 13, 3411, 279, 1461, 9942, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 382, 16141, 25, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 701, 3200, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 11, 22544, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 11, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 11, 323, 470, 279, 1461, 9942, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6229605811089257, "g_worst_claim": -0.07362164949115954, "g_content": 0.7015066659578713, "g_traj_mean": 0.5335631966590881}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1