{"id": "36", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to cook pollock:\n\nPassage 1:\n\n* Spray a baking sheet with butter-flavored cooking spray.\n* Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n* Place the fillets on the baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n* Bake in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n\nPassage 2:\n\n* Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n* Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n* Bake the fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n\nPassage 3:\n\n* Bake the pollock fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily.\n* Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on top of each fillet.\n* Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.\n\nTherefore, to cook pollock, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n2. Place the fillets on a baking sheet or in the oven.\n3. Cook the pollock until it flakes easily, either by baking it in the oven or on the stovetop.\n4. Add cheese to the pollock if desired and return it to the oven to melt the cheese.", "pred": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "cot": "[\"To cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\n4. After the fillets have cooked, turn off the oven.\\n5. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n6. Return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\\n\\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\", \"To cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Bake the pollock fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flaked easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\n4. Turn off the oven.\\n5. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n6. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\", \"To cook pollock, first preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they are cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\", \"To cook pollock, you can follow these steps: \\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit (175 degrees Celsius).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and the flesh flakes easily, which usually takes about 15 minutes. \\n\\nAfter baking, you can turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet. Then place the fillets back in the oven and allow the cheese to melt for approximately 3 minutes.\"]", "time_sec": 23.951, "generation_time_seconds": 23.0642, "selection_time_seconds": 0.88, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 52074, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 4636, 279, 1461, 9942, 614, 29105, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 624, 20, 13, 10771, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 21, 13, 3411, 279, 1461, 9942, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 382, 16141, 25, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 701, 3200, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 11, 22544, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 11, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 11, 323, 470, 279, 1461, 9942, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and retur