o 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they are cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.184612697821397, "g_worst_claim": 0.6543990687320107, "g_content": 1.2697054545084636, "g_traj_mean": 1.0250070095062256}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 25, 715, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 61347, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 52074, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 279, 24955, 81623, 6707, 11, 892, 5990, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 4710, 6025, 27815, 11, 498, 646, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 13, 5005, 1992, 279, 1461, 9942, 1182, 304, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 369, 13187, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "To cook pollock, you can follow these steps: \n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit (175 degrees Celsius).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and the flesh flakes easily, which usually takes about 15 minutes. \n\nAfter baking, you can turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet. Then place the fillets back in the oven and allow the cheese to melt for approximately 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9855768990936844, "g_worst_claim": -0.3082028428713481, "g_content": 1.2487335205078125, "g_traj_mean": 0.9437354207038879}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 42.55, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "37", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can cook pollock:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C) (Passage 2).\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper (Passage 1 and 2).\n3. Place the pollock fillets on a baking sheet lined with butter-flavored cooking spray (Passage 1).\n4. Add onion, green pepper, and tomato slices to the baking sheet (Passage 1).\n5. Bake the pollock fillets in the preheated oven for about 15 minutes, or until the fish has cooked and flakes easily (Passage 1 and 2).\n6. To add cheesy flavor, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fish to the oven for an additional 3 minutes (Passage 3).\n\nNote that Passage 3 does not provide any specific instructions for cooking the pollock, but rather suggests adding cheese to the existing dish.", "pred": "1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray.\n3. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n4. Place the fillets on the baking sheet.\n5. Layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n6. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\n7. Turn off the oven.\n8. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n9. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray.\n3. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n4. Place the fillets on the baking sheet.\n5. Layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n6. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\n7. Turn off the oven.\n8. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n9. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.", "cot": "[\"To cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\n4. After the fillets have cooked, turn off the oven.\\n5. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n6. Return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\\n\\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\", \"To cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\n4. Turn off the oven.\\n5. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n6. Return the fish to the oven and let the cheese melt for about 3 minutes.\\n\\nAnswer: Bake pollock in the oven until it flakes easily, then add cheese and cook until melted.\", \"1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray.\\n3. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n4. Place the fillets on the baking sheet.\\n5. Layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\\n6. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\\n7. Turn off the oven.\\n8. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n9. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.\", \"1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).  \\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.  \\n3. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.  \\n4. Turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet.  \\n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.\"]", "time_sec": 25.492, "generation_time_seconds": 24.6975, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7847, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 52074, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 4636, 279, 1461, 9942, 614, 29105, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 624, 20, 13, 10771, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 21, 13, 3411, 279, 1461, 9942, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 382, 16141, 25, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 701, 3200, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 11, 22544, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 11, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 11, 323, 470, 279, 1461, 9942, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6275007566263348, "g_worst_claim": -0.07169020803351152, "g_content": 0.7280481810210854, "g_traj_mean": 0.5420217514038086}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 52074, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 23387, 624, 20, 13, 10771, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 21, 13, 3411, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 1077, 279, 17163, 28999, 369, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 382, 16141, 25, 52074, 1471, 1023, 304, 279, 23387, 3080, 432, 81623, 6707, 11, 1221, 912, 17163, 323, 4296, 3080, 49359, 13, 151645], "pred": "Bake pollock in the oven until it flakes easily, then add cheese and cook until melted.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0148979924141328, "g_worst_claim": 0.12854799857506385, "g_content": 1.1860208026433394, "g_traj_mean": 0.8942098617553711}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 60561, 264, 27815, 10834, 448, 14100, 87240, 17233, 22899, 624, 18, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 1461, 9942, 389, 279, 27815, 10834, 624, 20, 13, 22735, 279, 1461, 9942, 448, 37327, 11, 6176, 24353, 11, 323, 41020, 34254, 624, 21, 13, 52074, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 22, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 23387, 624, 23, 13, 10771, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 24, 13, 3411, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\n2. Spray a baking sheet with butter flavored cooking spray.\n3. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\n4. Place the fillets on the baking sheet.\n5. Layer the fillets with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\n6. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.\n7. Turn off the oven.\n8. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\n9. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2587423285475863, "g_worst_claim": 0.1304875910282135, "g_content": 1.893493887094351, "g_traj_mean": 1.1238995790481567}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 568, 2303, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 13, 2303, 18, 13, 52074, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 2303, 19, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 23387, 11, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 13, 2303, 20, 13, 3411, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).  \n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.  \n3. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, about 15 minutes.  \n4. Turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet.  \n5. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1413171670248365, "g_worst_claim": 0.24111169576644897, "g_content": 1.9476307713708212, "g_traj_mean": 1.1525143384933472}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 67.8, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.8, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "38", "question": "how to cook pollock?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to cook pollock:\n\nPreheat the oven to 350°F (175°C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper or aluminum foil. You can also add sliced onions, green peppers, and tomatoes on top of the fillets. Bake for 15 minutes or until the fish flakes easily with a fork. If desired, top with cheese and return to the oven for an additional 3 minutes or until the cheese is melted.\n\nTherefore, the answer is not \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "pred": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "cot": "[\"To cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n3. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes.\\n4. After the fillets have cooked, turn off the oven.\\n5. Place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n6. Return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\\n\\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.\", \"To cook pollock, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit (175 degrees Celsius). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with slices of onion, green pepper, and tomato. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they are cooked through and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes. Once the fish is cooked, turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet. Return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, taking about 3 minutes.\", \"To cook pollock, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices. Bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily, which takes about 15 minutes. Turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fish to the oven to allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.\\n\\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily (about 15 minutes), turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fish to the oven to allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.\", \"To cook pollock, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\\n\\n2. Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper.\\n\\n3. Place the seasoned fish on a baking sheet and layer it with onion, green pepper, and tomato slices.\\n\\n4. Bake the fish in the preheated oven until it has cooked and flakes easily, for about 15 minutes.\\n\\n5. Turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet.\\n\\n6. Return the fish to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, for about 3 minutes.\\n\\nAfter following these steps, the pollock will be cooked and ready to serve.\"]", "time_sec": 30.06, "generation_time_seconds": 29.2612, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7878, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 624, 18, 13, 52074, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 4636, 279, 1461, 9942, 614, 29105, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 624, 20, 13, 10771, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 624, 21, 13, 3411, 279, 1461, 9942, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 382, 16141, 25, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 701, 3200, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 11, 22544, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 614, 29105, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 11, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 11, 323, 470, 279, 1461, 9942, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they have cooked and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes, turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, which takes about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6071808009701117, "g_worst_claim": -0.08007256608260305, "g_content": 0.6776457345613869, "g_traj_mean": 0.5157262086868286}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1191, 553, 855, 383, 1095, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 61347, 568, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 13, 10771, 279, 1461, 9942, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 323, 6193, 1105, 448, 34254, 315, 37327, 11, 6176, 24353, 11, 323, 41020, 13, 52074, 279, 1461, 9942, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 525, 29105, 1526, 323, 1320, 726, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 9646, 279, 7640, 374, 29105, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 13, 3411, 279, 1461, 9942, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 4633, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "To cook pollock, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit (175 degrees Celsius). Season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper. Place the fillets on a baking sheet and layer them with slices of onion, green pepper, and tomato. Bake the fillets in the preheated oven until they are cooked through and flake easily, which takes about 15 minutes. Once the fish is cooked, turn off the oven and place two slices of cheese on each fillet. Return the fillets to the oven and allow the cheese to melt, taking about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0120119636589948, "g_worst_claim": 0.40304996853783015, "g_content": 1.5130265669389205, "g_traj_mean": 0.9428581595420837}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1191, 553, 855, 383, 1095, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 568, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 13, 10771, 279, 1461, 9942, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 323, 6193, 1105, 448, 37327, 11, 6176, 24353, 11, 323, 41020, 34254, 13, 52074, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 892, 4990, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 23387, 11, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 11, 323, 470, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 311, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 369, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 382, 16141, 25, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 701, 3200, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 11, 22544, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 7640, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 320, 9096, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 701, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 11, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 11, 323, 470, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 311, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 369, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C), season the pollock fillets with paprika and black pepper, bake in the preheated oven until the fish has cooked and flakes easily (about 15 minutes), turn off the oven, place two slices of cheese on each fillet, and return the fish to the oven to allow the cheese to melt for about 3 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.779047375581186, "g_worst_claim": -0.026985962139932734, "g_content": 0.9965918404715401, "g_traj_mean": 0.6608813405036926}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1471, 1023, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 22, 20, 12348, 356, 3593, 17, 13, 14263, 279, 1471, 1023, 1461, 9942, 448, 25298, 40454, 323, 3691, 24353, 382, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 51514, 7640, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 323, 6193, 432, 448, 37327, 11, 6176, 24353, 11, 323, 41020, 34254, 382, 19, 13, 52074, 279, 7640, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 432, 702, 29105, 323, 81623, 6707, 11, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 382, 20, 13, 11999, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 1992, 1378, 34254, 315, 17163, 389, 1817, 1461, 1149, 382, 21, 13, 3411, 279, 7640, 311, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 17163, 311, 28999, 11, 369, 911, 220, 18, 4420, 382, 6025, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 279, 1471, 1023, 686, 387, 29105, 323, 5527, 311, 8683, 13, 151645], "pred": "After following these steps, the pollock will be cooked and ready to serve.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.98239334050145, "g_worst_claim": 0.11588907241821289, "g_content": 1.3004544576009114, "g_traj_mean": 0.9003350734710693}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.37, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "39", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, you can run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic, then scrape it off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. Be careful not to damage the dryer's interior. You can then apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Afterward, rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. You can mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water, dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water. Some plastic may be extremely difficult to remove, in which case you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun and then peel it off. If not all plastic comes off, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can effectively remove plastic from your clothes dryer.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "By following these steps, you can effectively remove plastic from your clothes dryer.", "cot": "[\"To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Run the Dryer on a Regular Setting for 20 Minutes**: This helps soften the plastic, making it easier to remove.\\n\\n2. **Scrape the Plastic Off**: Use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to carefully remove the plastic. Be cautious not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n\\n3. **Apply Nail Polish Remover**: Mix 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover with a clean cloth. Rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n\\n4. **Rinse with a Damp Cloth**: Use a damp cloth to rinse the area where the plastic was removed.\\n\\n5. **Use Laundry Soap Solution**: Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again.\\n\\n6. **Rinse Thoroughly**: Rinse the area with a cloth dipped in clean water to ensure all residue is removed.\\n\\nIf the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, consider heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic. However, if you cannot remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. In such cases, it is recommended to call a service technician for assistance.\", \"To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Softening the Plastic**: Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. This helps make it easier to scrape off.\\n\\n2. **Scraping the Plastic**: Use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to gently scrape the plastic off the dryer's interior. Be careful not to damage the dryer's interior during this process.\\n\\n3. **Dissolving the Plastic**: Apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the area where the plastic is located to dissolve it.\\n\\n4. **Rinsing the Area**: Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse off the nail polish remover.\\n\\n5. **Cleaning with Soap**: Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again to further clean it.\\n\\n6. **Final Rinse**: Rinse the area well with a cloth dipped in clean water to remove any remaining soap and nail polish remover.\\n\\n7. **Additional Tips**:\\n   - Jupiterimages/BananaStock/Getty Images suggests that a plastic coated bib or zip top bag won’t melt in a dryer unless using the high heat setting, but even with high heat, it won’t cause serious damage.\\n   - Heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun may help make it easier to peel off, but it may not remove all of it. In such cases, replacing the drum or the entire dryer may be necessary. If opting for a replacement, it is recommended to call a service technician.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively remove plastic from your clothes dryer.\", \"To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Softening the Plastic**: Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. This helps make it easier to remove.\\n\\n2. **Scraping the Plastic**: Use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to scrape the plastic off the dryer's interior. Be careful not to damage the dryer's interior during this process.\\n\\n3. **Applying Nail Polish Remover**: Apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. This helps loosen the plastic and makes it easier to remove.\\n\\n4. **Rinsing with Water**: Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. This step ensures that no residue remains.\\n\\n5. **Cleaning with Soap and Water**: Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again. This helps in removing any remaining plastic without damaging the dryer's interior.\\n\\nIf the plastic is still difficult to remove, you might consider heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun to make it easier to peel off. However, if you are not able to remove all the plastic, it might be necessary to replace the dryer drum or even the entire dryer. It is recommended to call a service technician for such repairs to avoid further damage or complications.\", \"To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, you can follow these steps:\\n1. Use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to scrape the plastic off the dryer's interior.\\n2. Apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n3. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\\n4. Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water and dip a clean cloth in this solution.\\n5. Rub the area again with the soapy cloth.\\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\n\\nIf the plastic is tightly adhered and difficult to remove, you may need to heat it with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic, but if not, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, I recommend calling a service technician to complete this type of repair.\"]", "time_sec": 46.6, "generation_time_seconds": 45.5846, "selection_time_seconds": 1.008, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 6727, 279, 30841, 261, 389, 264, 28800, 20037, 369, 220, 17, 15, 40999, 95518, 1096, 8609, 79945, 279, 12188, 11, 3259, 432, 8661, 311, 4057, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 3326, 19842, 279, 36008, 4114, 95518, 5443, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 311, 15516, 4057, 279, 12188, 13, 2823, 45778, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 28497, 74428, 31984, 4926, 1975, 95518, 19219, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 92100, 315, 30995, 44029, 76248, 448, 264, 4240, 27292, 13, 12839, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 49, 258, 325, 448, 264, 422, 1121, 83635, 95518, 5443, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 3082, 1380, 279, 12188, 572, 6963, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 10253, 81632, 60631, 12478, 95518, 19219, 220, 16, 41284, 315, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 3015, 13, 55047, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 323, 10273, 279, 3082, 1549, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 49, 258, 325, 663, 14438, 398, 95518, 57368, 325, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 311, 5978, 678, 48132, 374, 6963, 382, 2679, 279, 12188, 374, 9016, 5000, 311, 4057, 11, 2908, 23579, 432, 448, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 13, 9646, 31713, 11, 498, 1231, 387, 2952, 311, 57112, 1007, 279, 12188, 13, 4354, 11, 421, 498, 4157, 4057, 678, 279, 12188, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 476, 279, 4453, 46622, 13, 758, 1741, 5048, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 1618, 264, 2473, 53511, 369, 12994, 13, 151645], "pred": "If 