3, 1096, 8609, 304, 17592, 894, 9664, 12188, 2041, 33346, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 382, 2679, 279, 12188, 374, 2058, 5000, 311, 4057, 11, 498, 2578, 2908, 23579, 432, 448, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 311, 1281, 432, 8661, 311, 57112, 1007, 13, 4354, 11, 421, 498, 525, 537, 2952, 311, 4057, 678, 279, 12188, 11, 432, 2578, 387, 5871, 311, 8290, 279, 46622, 23196, 476, 1496, 279, 4453, 46622, 13, 1084, 374, 11102, 311, 1618, 264, 2473, 53511, 369, 1741, 30186, 311, 5648, 4623, 5557, 476, 35405, 13, 151645], "pred": "If the plastic is still difficult to remove, you might consider heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun to make it easier to peel off. However, if you are not able to remove all the plastic, it might be necessary to replace the dryer drum or even the entire dryer. It is recommended to call a service technician for such repairs to avoid further damage or complications.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7941131452776815, "g_worst_claim": 0.06332082407815116, "g_content": 1.281954465991389, "g_traj_mean": 0.9127671122550964}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 633, 12188, 700, 315, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 5443, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 311, 57128, 279, 12188, 1007, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 17, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 92100, 315, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 624, 18, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 624, 19, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 41284, 315, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 3015, 323, 23604, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 624, 20, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 1549, 448, 279, 773, 9667, 27292, 624, 21, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 382, 2679, 279, 12188, 374, 38969, 34951, 291, 323, 5000, 311, 4057, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 8628, 432, 448, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 13, 9646, 31713, 11, 498, 1231, 387, 2952, 311, 57112, 1007, 279, 12188, 11, 714, 421, 537, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 476, 279, 4453, 46622, 13, 1416, 498, 1366, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 11, 358, 6934, 8098, 264, 2473, 53511, 311, 4583, 419, 943, 315, 12733, 13, 151645], "pred": "If the plastic is tightly adhered and difficult to remove, you may need to heat it with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic, but if not, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. If you want to replace the drum, I recommend calling a service technician to complete this type of repair.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3434229610432684, "g_worst_claim": 0.23887741565704346, "g_content": 1.760124929327714, "g_traj_mean": 1.3464215993881226}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 10.26, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "40", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is a brief answer to the question:\n\nTo get plastic out of a clothes dryer, first, run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Then, scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, being careful not to damage the dryer's interior. Next, apply nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rinse the area with a damp cloth and then mix liquid laundry soap with water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again. Finally, rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "pred": "If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, consider heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic. However, if you cannot remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. In such cases, it is recommended to call a service technician for assistance.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, consider heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic. However, if you cannot remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. In such cases, it is recommended to call a service technician for assistance.", "cot": "[\"To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Run the Dryer on a Regular Setting for 20 Minutes**: This helps soften the plastic, making it easier to remove.\\n\\n2. **Scrape the Plastic Off**: Use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to carefully remove the plastic. Be cautious not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n\\n3. **Apply Nail Polish Remover**: Mix 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover with a clean cloth. Rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n\\n4. **Rinse with a Damp Cloth**: Use a damp cloth to rinse the area where the plastic was removed.\\n\\n5. **Use Laundry Soap Solution**: Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again.\\n\\n6. **Rinse Thoroughly**: Rinse the area with a cloth dipped in clean water to ensure all residue is removed.\\n\\nIf the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, consider heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic. However, if you cannot remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. In such cases, it is recommended to call a service technician for assistance.\", \"To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Softening the Plastic**: Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. This makes it easier to remove without causing damage.\\n\\n2. **Scraping**: Use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to carefully scrape the softened plastic off the dryer's interior. Be cautious to avoid damaging the dryer's interior.\\n\\n3. **Dissolving with Nail Polish Remover**: Apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic area until the plastic dissolves. This helps in loosening and removing the plastic more efficiently.\\n\\n4. **Rinsing**: After applying the nail polish remover, rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse off the remover and any remaining plastic.\\n\\n5. **Cleaning with Soap Solution**: Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again to ensure the plastic is thoroughly removed.\\n\\n6. **Final Rinse**: Rinse the area well with a cloth dipped in clean water to remove any soap residue.\\n\\n7. **Optional: Heating with a Hair Dryer or Heat Gun**: If the plastic is particularly stubborn, you can heat the dryer drum with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic. If this does not work, it might be necessary to replace the drum or the entire dryer, especially if it is damaged beyond repair.\\n\\n8. **Professional Help**: If you are unsure about the extent of the damage or if the process is too difficult, it is recommended to call a service technician for a professional repair.\\n\\nThese steps should help effectively remove plastic from your clothes dryer, ensuring it remains functional and safe for use.\", \"Answer: To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, use a nail polish remover and a cloth. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to the cloth and rub it over the area of the dryer where the plastic is located. Rinse the area with a damp cloth. Mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water, and dip a clean cloth in the solution. Rub the area again and rinse with a clean cloth dipped in water.\", \"To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Identify the type of plastic**: Determine if the plastic is soft or hard. Soft plastic can often be softened by heat, while hard plastic may require scraping or soaking.\\n\\n2. **Heat the plastic**: If the plastic is soft, use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the area. This will help make the plastic more pliable and easier to remove. Be cautious with this method, as overheating could damage the dryer's interior.\\n\\n3. **Scrape the plastic**: Once the plastic is heated, use a wooden spatula or a plastic paint scraper to gently scrape the plastic off the surface of the dryer. Be careful not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n\\n4. **Dissolve the plastic**: If the plastic is not easily removable, apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. This method works particularly well for soft plastics.\\n\\n5. **Rinse the area**: After applying the nail polish remover, rinse the area with a damp cloth to remove any remaining residue. \\n\\n6. **Clean the coil (if applicable)**: If the plastic is stuck to the dryer's heating element or other parts, soak a cloth in an acetone-based nail polish remover and leave it on the element for 5 minutes. Use the cloth to scrub off the plastic, then wipe the coils clean with a damp cloth. Rinse the coils with a solution of warm water and dish soap to remove any residue.\\n\\n7. **Replace damaged parts**: If the plastic is too difficult to remove or has caused significant damage to the dryer, you may need to replace the damaged parts, such as the drum or the entire dryer. In such cases, it is recommended to call a service technician for assistance.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can safely and effectively remove plastic from a clothes dryer, ensuring it continues to function properly.\"]", "time_sec": 44.203, "generation_time_seconds": 43.0228, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1681, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 6727, 279, 30841, 261, 389, 264, 28800, 20037, 369, 220, 17, 15, 40999, 95518, 1096, 8609, 79945, 279, 12188, 11, 3259, 432, 8661, 311, 4057, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 3326, 19842, 279, 36008, 4114, 95518, 5443, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 311, 15516, 4057, 279, 12188, 13, 2823, 45778, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 28497, 74428, 31984, 4926, 1975, 95518, 19219, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 92100, 315, 30995, 44029, 76248, 448, 264, 4240, 27292, 13, 12839, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 49, 258, 325, 448, 264, 422, 1121, 83635, 95518, 5443, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 3082, 1380, 279, 12188, 572, 6963, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 10253, 81632, 60631, 12478, 95518, 19219, 220, 16, 41284, 315, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 3015, 13, 55047, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 323, 10273, 279, 3082, 1549, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 49, 258, 325, 663, 14438, 398, 95518, 57368, 325, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 27292,