41, 448, 264, 4240, 27292, 72207, 304, 3015, 13, 151645], "pred": "To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, use a nail polish remover and a cloth. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to the cloth and rub it over the area of the dryer where the plastic is located. Rinse the area with a damp cloth. Mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water, and dip a clean cloth in the solution. Rub the area again and rinse with a clean cloth dipped in water.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3443460429309173, "g_worst_claim": 0.1237266713922674, "g_content": 1.6352297194460605, "g_traj_mean": 1.0892568826675415}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 28301, 1437, 279, 943, 315, 12188, 95518, 29901, 421, 279, 12188, 374, 8413, 476, 2588, 13, 24079, 12188, 646, 3545, 387, 89058, 553, 8628, 11, 1393, 2588, 12188, 1231, 1373, 81438, 476, 77346, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 61306, 279, 12188, 95518, 1416, 279, 12188, 374, 8413, 11, 990, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 311, 8628, 279, 3082, 13, 1096, 686, 1492, 1281, 279, 12188, 803, 625, 2156, 323, 8661, 311, 4057, 13, 2823, 45778, 448, 419, 1714, 11, 438, 71289, 1095, 1410, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 3326, 19842, 279, 12188, 95518, 9646, 279, 12188, 374, 31713, 11, 990, 264, 22360, 62883, 5607, 476, 264, 12188, 6177, 88034, 311, 29273, 57128, 279, 12188, 1007, 279, 7329, 315, 279, 46622, 13, 2823, 16585, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 35, 1038, 3948, 279, 12188, 95518, 1416, 279, 12188, 374, 537, 6707, 53791, 11, 3796, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 92100, 315, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 13, 1096, 1714, 4278, 7945, 1632, 369, 8413, 67286, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 49, 258, 325, 279, 3082, 95518, 4636, 18950, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 11, 73241, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 4057, 894, 9664, 48132, 13, 4710, 21, 13, 3070, 27529, 279, 39660, 320, 333, 8415, 32295, 25, 1416, 279, 12188, 374, 15700, 311, 279, 46622, 594, 23579, 2392, 476, 1008, 5479, 11, 60692, 264, 27292, 304, 458, 64702, 603, 5980, 30995, 44029, 76248, 323, 5274, 432, 389, 279, 2392, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 5443, 279, 27292, 311, 44901, 1007, 279, 12188, 11, 1221, 39094, 279, 70760, 4240, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 70760, 448, 264, 6291, 315, 8205, 3015, 323, 12000, 26785, 311, 4057, 894, 48132, 382, 22, 13, 3070, 23107, 20123, 5479, 95518, 1416, 279, 12188, 374, 2238, 5000, 311, 4057, 476, 702, 8881, 5089, 5557, 311, 279, 46622, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 8290, 279, 20123, 5479, 11, 1741, 438, 279, 23196, 476, 279, 4453, 46622, 13, 758, 1741, 5048, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 1618, 264, 2473, 53511, 369, 12994, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 21000, 323, 13444, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 22573, 432, 9539, 311, 729, 10277, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can safely and effectively remove plastic from a clothes dryer, ensuring it continues to function properly.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6087984380835769, "g_worst_claim": -0.09353544314702351, "g_content": 0.9733104601583845, "g_traj_mean": 0.6497249603271484}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 11.32, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "42", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to remove plastic from a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic, then scrape it off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. (Passage 1)\n2. Heat the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun to make it easier to peel off. Once heated, use a cloth to peel off the plastic. (Passage 2)\n3. Soak a cloth in an acetone-based nail polish remover and use it to scrub the remaining plastic off of the element after leaving it on the element for 5 minutes. Then, wipe the coils with a clean, damp cloth and remove any remaining residue with a cloth dipped in a solution of warm water and dish soap. (Passage 3)\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to remove plastic from the drum of a clothes dryer.", "pred": "To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again.\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\nThese steps should help remove the plastic from the dryer without causing serious damage.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again.\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\nThese steps should help remove the plastic from the dryer without causing serious damage.", "cot": "[\"To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Run the Dryer on a Regular Setting for 20 Minutes**: This helps soften the plastic, making it easier to remove.\\n\\n2. **Scrape the Plastic Off**: Use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to carefully remove the plastic. Be cautious not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n\\n3. **Apply Nail Polish Remover**: Mix 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover with a clean cloth. Rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n\\n4. **Rinse with a Damp Cloth**: Use a damp cloth to rinse the area where the plastic was removed.\\n\\n5. **Use Laundry Soap Solution**: Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again.\\n\\n6. **Rinse Thoroughly**: Rinse the area with a cloth dipped in clean water to ensure all residue is removed.\\n\\nIf the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, consider heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic. However, if you cannot remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. In such cases, it is recommended to call a service technician for assistance.\", \"Instructions. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it.Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again.Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\", \"To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Softening the Plastic**: Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. This helps make it easier to remove.\\n\\n2. **Scraping the Plastic**: Use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to carefully scrape the plastic off the dryer's interior. Take care not to damage the dryer's surface.\\n\\n3. **Dissolving the Plastic**: Apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. This helps loosen any remaining plastic.\\n\\n4. **Rinsing**: Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse off the nail polish remover. This ensures no residue remains.\\n\\n5. **Cleaning the Area**: Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again to remove any soap residue.\\n\\n6. **Final Rinsing**: Rinse the area thoroughly with a cloth dipped in clean water to ensure all the soap and plastic are removed.\\n\\nIf the plastic is particularly stubborn, you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic. However, be careful not to overheat the dryer, as this could cause damage.\\n\\nIf the plastic is very difficult to remove, you might need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. In such cases, it is recommended to call a service technician for assistance.\", \"To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n3. Apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\\n5. Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again.\\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\nThese steps should help remove the plastic from the dryer without causing serious damage.\"]", "time_sec": 37.54, "generation_time_seconds": 36.7178, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8128, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 6727, 279, 30841, 261, 389, 264, 28800, 20037, 369, 220, 17, 15, 40999, 95518, 1096, 8609, 79945, 279, 12188, 11, 3259, 432, 8661, 311, 4057, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 3326, 19842, 279, 36008, 4114, 95518, 5443, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 311, 15516, 4057, 279, 12188, 13, 2823, 45778, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 28497, 74428, 31984, 4926, 1975, 95518, 19219, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 92100, 315, 30995, 44029, 76248, 448, 264, 4240, 27292, 13, 12839, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 49, 258, 325, 448, 264, 422, 1121, 83635, 95518, 5443, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 3082, 1380, 279, 12188, 572, 6963, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 10253, 81632, 60631, 12478, 95518, 19219, 220, 16, 41284, 315, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 3015, 13, 55047, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 323, 10273, 279, 3082, 1549, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 49, 258, 325, 663, 14438, 398, 95518, 57368, 325, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 311, 5978, 678, 48132, 374, 6963, 382, 2679, 279, 12188, 374, 9016, 5000, 311, 4057, 11, 2908, 23579, 432, 448, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 13, 9646, 31713, 11, 498, 1231, 387, 2952, 311, 57112, 1007, 279, 12188, 13, 4354, 11, 421, 498, 4157, 4057, 678, 279, 12188, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 476, 279, 4453, 46622, 13, 758, 1741, 5048, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 1618, 264, 2473, 53511, 369, 12994, 13, 151645], "pred": "If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, consider heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic. However, if you cannot remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. In such cases, it is recommended to call a service technician for assistance.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1247840527638793, "g_worst_claim": -0.0328387200832367, "g_content": 1.5078948726498984, "g_traj_mean": 1.125815749168396}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [55291, 13, 6452, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 37920, 13, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 11, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 2013, 392, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 37920, 13, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 3015, 13, 55047, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 11, 323, 10273, 279, 3082, 1549, 2013, 258, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 13, 151645], "pred": "Instructions. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it.Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again.Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8432954233484615, "g_worst_claim": 0.9241687774658203, "g_content": 2.3393343607584636, "g_traj_mean": 1.