ian for assistance.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.789770870949589, "g_worst_claim": -0.12366985190998424, "g_content": 1.2879305359319593, "g_traj_mean": 0.9064089059829712}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 6452, 279, 46622, 389, 264, 5792, 6243, 369, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 311, 79945, 279, 12188, 624, 17, 13, 2463, 19842, 279, 12188, 1007, 448, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 624, 18, 13, 20552, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 92100, 315, 30995, 44029, 76248, 311, 264, 4240, 27292, 323, 10273, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 624, 19, 13, 12839, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 30995, 44029, 76248, 624, 20, 13, 19219, 220, 16, 41284, 315, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 3015, 13, 55047, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 323, 10273, 279, 3082, 1549, 624, 21, 13, 57368, 325, 1632, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 624, 9485, 7354, 1265, 1492, 4057, 279, 12188, 504, 279, 46622, 2041, 14381, 6001, 5557, 13, 151645], "pred": "To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again.\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\nThese steps should help remove the plastic from the dryer without causing serious damage.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3723218149188008, "g_worst_claim": 0.4941798845926921, "g_content": 1.6801934591153773, "g_traj_mean": 1.3351651430130005}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.17, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 4.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "43", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to get plastic out of a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n4. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n\nIf the plastic is still difficult to remove, you can try heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun before attempting to scrape it off. However, if the plastic cannot be removed completely, it may be necessary to replace the drum or the entire dryer.", "pred": "To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, use a plastic scraper to remove any hardened plastic. Soak a cloth in acetone-based nail polish remover and leave it on the element for about 5 minutes. Then, use the cloth to scrub the remaining plastic off of the element. Wipe the coils with a clean, damp cloth. To remove any remaining nail polish remover residue, soak another cloth in a solution of warm water and dish soap, then rinse the coils with water.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, use a plastic scraper to remove any hardened plastic. Soak a cloth in acetone-based nail polish remover and leave it on the element for about 5 minutes. Then, use the cloth to scrub the remaining plastic off of the element. Wipe the coils with a clean, damp cloth. To remove any remaining nail polish remover residue, soak another cloth in a solution of warm water and dish soap, then rinse the coils with water.", "cot": "[\"To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Run the Dryer on a Regular Setting for 20 Minutes**: This helps soften the plastic, making it easier to remove.\\n\\n2. **Scrape the Plastic Off**: Use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to carefully remove the plastic. Be cautious not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n\\n3. **Apply Nail Polish Remover**: Mix 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover with a clean cloth. Rub the plastic to dissolve it.\\n\\n4. **Rinse with a Damp Cloth**: Use a damp cloth to rinse the area where the plastic was removed.\\n\\n5. **Use Laundry Soap Solution**: Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again.\\n\\n6. **Rinse Thoroughly**: Rinse the area with a cloth dipped in clean water to ensure all residue is removed.\\n\\nIf the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, consider heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic. However, if you cannot remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. In such cases, it is recommended to call a service technician for assistance.\", \"Answer: To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, use a plastic scraper to remove any hardened plastic. Soak a cloth in acetone-based nail polish remover and leave it on the element for about 5 minutes. Then, use the cloth to scrub the remaining plastic off of the element. Wipe the coils with a clean, damp cloth. To remove any remaining nail polish remover residue, soak another cloth in a solution of warm water and dish soap, then rinse the coils with water.\", \"To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these detailed steps:\\n\\n1. **Initial Softening**: Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. This step makes it easier to remove the plastic without causing damage to the dryer's interior.\\n\\n2. **Scraping**: Use a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper to carefully scrape the plastic off the dryer's surface. Take care not to damage the dryer's painted synthetic enamel coating, which is designed to withstand heat and wear.\\n\\n3. **Dissolving the Plastic**: Apply 1 to 2 teaspoons of nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic area to dissolve it. This step helps in breaking down the plastic, making it easier to remove.\\n\\n4. **Rinsing**: After applying the nail polish remover, rinse the area with a damp cloth. This helps to remove any remaining residue from the nail polish remover.\\n\\n5. **Cleaning Solution**: Mix 1 teaspoon of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again. This step helps in cleaning the area thoroughly.\\n\\n6. **Final Rinse**: Rinse the area well with a cloth dipped in clean water to ensure all the cleaning solutions are removed.\\n\\n7. **Heating Method**: If the plastic is particularly difficult to remove, you can try heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun. This can make the plastic more pliable and easier to peel off. However, be cautious to avoid damaging the dryer or its components.\\n\\n8. **Replacement**: If the plastic cannot be removed after heating, you may need to replace the drum or even the entire dryer. It is advisable to call a service technician for this type of repair to ensure it is done correctly.\\n\\n9. **Coils and Elements**: If the plastic is on the coils or elements of the dryer, follow these steps:\\n   - Remove the ice and scrape off the hardened plastic using a plastic scraper.\\n   - Soak a cloth in an acetone-based nail polish remover and leave it on the element for 5 minutes. This allows the nail polish remover to break down and remove the plastic.\\n   - Use the soaked cloth to scrub off the remaining plastic from the element.\\n   - Wipe the coils with a clean, damp cloth to ensure they are free of plastic and nail polish remover residue.\\n   - Clean any remaining residue with a cloth dipped in a solution of warm water and dish soap, then rinse the coils with water.\\n\\nBy following\", \"To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes** to soften any plastic that may have been added to the dryer.\\n2. **Scrape** the softened plastic off the dryer using a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. Be careful not to damage the dryer's interior.\\n3. **Apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover** to a clean cloth and rub the area to dissolve any remaining plastic.\\n4. **Rub the area with a damp cloth** to rinse off the nail polish remover.\\n5. **Mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup of water**, dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again.\\n6. **Rinse well** with a cloth dipped in clean water.\\n7. If the plastic is very stubborn, you can **heat the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun**. The heat may help peel off the plastic.\\n8. If heating doesn't work, you may need to **replace the drum or the entire dryer**. It is recommended to call a service technician to handle this type of repair.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively remove plastic from your clothes dryer.\"]", "time_sec": 45.486, "generation_time_seconds": 44.4678, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0063, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 6727, 279, 30841, 261, 389, 264, 28800, 20037, 369, 220, 17, 15, 40999, 95518, 1096, 8609, 79945, 279, 12188, 11, 3259, 432, 8661, 311, 4057, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 3326, 19842, 279, 36008, 4114, 95518, 5443, 264, 22360, 476, 12188, 62883, 5607, 476, 6177, 88034, 311, 15516, 4057, 279, 12188, 13, 2823, 45778, 537, 311, 5557, 279, 46622, 594, 14791, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 28497, 74428, 31984, 4926, 1975, 95518, 19219, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 92100, 315, 30995, 44029, 76248, 448, 264, 4240, 27292, 13, 12839, 279, 12188, 311, 72639, 432, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 49, 258, 325, 448, 264, 422, 1121, 83635, 95518, 5443, 264, 40269, 27292, 311, 73241, 279, 3082, 1380, 279, 12188, 572, 6963, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 10253, 81632, 60631, 12478, 95518, 19219, 220, 16, 41284, 315, 14473, 34089, 26785, 448, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 3015, 13, 55047, 264, 4240, 27292, 304, 419, 6291, 323, 10273, 279, 3082, 1549, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 49, 258, 325, 663, 14438, 398, 95518, 57368, 325, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 27292, 72207, 304, 4240, 3015, 311, 5978, 678, 48132, 374, 6963, 382, 2679, 279, 12188, 374, 9016, 5000, 311, 4057, 11, 2908, 23579, 432, 448, 264, 6869, 46622, 476, 8628, 6038, 13, 9646, 31713, 11, 498, 1231, 387, 2952, 311, 57112, 1007, 279, 12188, 13, 4354, 11, 421, 498, 4157, 4057, 678, 279, 12188, 11, 498, 1231, 1184, 311, 8290, 279, 23196, 476, 279, 4453, 46622, 13, 758, 1741, 5048, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 1618, 264, 2473, 53511, 369, 12994, 13, 151645], "pred": "If the plastic is extremely difficult to remove, consider heating it with a hair dryer or heat gun. Once heated, you may be able to peel off the plastic. However, if you cannot remove all the plastic, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer. In such cases, it is recommended to call a service technician for assistance.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1146646585041706, "g_worst_claim": -0.029605910181999207, "g_content": 1.5004898939675433, "g_traj_mean": 1.1184132099151611}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 2014, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 11, 990, 264, 12188, 88034, 311, 4057, 894, 70736, 12188, 13, 2055, 585, 264, 27292, 304, 64702, 603, 5980, 30995, 44029, 76248, 323, 5274, 432, 389, 279, 2392, 369, 911, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 5005, 11, 990, 279, 27292, 311, 44901, 279, 9664, 12188, 1007, 315, 279, 2392, 13, 467, 3444, 279, 70760, 448, 264, 4240, 11, 40269, 27292, 13, 2014, 4057, 894, 9664, 30995, 44029, 76248, 48132, 11, 60692, 2441, 27292, 304, 264, 6291, 315, 8205, 3015, 323, 12000, 26785, 11, 1221, 73