to 20 minutes.\n4. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding.\n5. Cook the bratwursts on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.345283736473353, "g_worst_claim": 0.7219513602878737, "g_content": 1.5086054368452593, "g_traj_mean": 1.0423424243927002}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 2014, 4296, 1411, 1862, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 2340, 865, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 438, 807, 4296, 624, 17, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 264, 3460, 5591, 3338, 448, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 624, 18, 13, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 39058, 85354, 323, 855, 19963, 279, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 369, 220, 16, 15, 311, 220, 16, 19, 4420, 11, 13054, 22930, 311, 13876, 41047, 624, 21, 13, 52932, 448, 279, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 382, 1986, 1714, 25351, 429, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 374, 29105, 41047, 323, 26364, 11, 26160, 894, 5214, 315, 916, 1015, 10746, 279, 44597, 476, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 5086, 13, 151645], "pred": "To cook brats, follow these steps:", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2981918602328413, "g_worst_claim": 0.12680694262186687, "g_content": 1.8203296946055854, "g_traj_mean": 1.1469180583953857}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 76.36, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "78", "question": "how to cook brats", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to cook brats:\n\nStep 1: Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n\nStep 2: Lightly oil the grate.\n\nStep 3: Combine beer and onions in a large pot, bring to a boil, and submerge the bratwurst. Add red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n\nStep 4: Simmer the bratwurst in the beer mixture for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly.\n\nStep 5: Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and grill it on the preheated grill for an additional 5 to 10 minutes, turning occasionally, until browned and cooked through.\n\nStep 6: Serve the bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side dish.\n\nNote: It's important to prick the bratwurst with a fork before cooking to prevent them from exploding while cooking. Also, cooked bratwurst can be stored in the fridge for up to 5 days or frozen for up to 3 months.", "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer; add the red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n5. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n6. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\n7. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n8. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\n9. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer; add the red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n5. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n6. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\n7. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n8. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\n9. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "cot": "[\"To cook brats, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\\n2. Lightly oil the grill grate.\\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture, adding red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\\n5. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\\n6. Place the bratwurst in the pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\\n7. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n8. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\\n9. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\", \"1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer; add the red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\\n5. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\\n6. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\\n7. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n8. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\\n9. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\", \"Cook brats by following these steps:\\n\\n1. In a large pot, combine beer and onions and bring to a boil.\\n\\n2. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture, along with red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\\n\\n3. Reduce heat to low and continue cooking the onions for 10 to 12 minutes.\\n\\n4. Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture.\\n\\n5. Lightly oil the grill grate and preheat the grill to medium-high heat.\\n\\n6. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\\n\\n7. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\\n\\nIn an alternative method:\\n\\n1. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\\n\\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\\n\\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n\\n4. Preheat the grill to medium-high heat.\\n\\n5. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.\\n\\nBoth methods ensure that the bratwurst is cooked thoroughly while adding flavor to the dish.\", \"Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding. Place them in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat. Lightly oil the grate. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\"]", "time_sec": 29.315, "generation_time_seconds": 28.2899, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0169, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1411, 1862, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 624, 17, 13, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 39058, 85354, 624, 18, 13, 46812, 279, 12883, 323, 44597, 304, 264, 3460, 3338, 26, 4446, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 19, 13, 3719, 19052, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 12883, 20980, 11, 7842, 2518, 24353, 81623, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 12021, 11, 323, 24353, 624, 20, 13, 2340, 865, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 438, 807, 4296, 624, 21, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 3338, 448, 279, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 624, 22, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 11, 13054, 3055, 11, 369, 220, 20, 311, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 624, 24, 13, 52932, 448, 279, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grill grate.\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture, adding red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n5. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n6. Place the bratwurst in the pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\n7. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n8. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\n9. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2864533961361289, "g_worst_claim": 0.11439628899097443, "g_content": 1.8332428803315033, "g_traj_mean": 1.1652249097824097}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 624, 17, 13, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 85354, 624, 18, 13, 46812, 279, 12883, 323, 44597, 304, 264, 3460, 3338, 26, 4446, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 19, 13, 3719, 19052, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 12883, 26, 912, 279, 2518, 24353, 81623, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 12021, 11, 323, 24353, 624, 20, 13, 2340, 865, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 438, 807, 4296, 624, 21, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 264, 3460, 5591, 3338, 448, 279, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 624, 22, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 11, 13054, 3055, 11, 369, 220, 20, 311, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 624, 24, 13, 52932, 448, 279, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer; add the red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n5. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n6. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\n7. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n8. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\n9. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4042826588006343, "g_worst_claim": 0.1106085479259491, "g_content": 2.163374764578683, "g_traj_mean": 1.2784425020217896}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [58382, 1411, 1862, 553, 2701, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 758, 264, 3460, 3338, 11, 15963, 12883, 323, 44597, 323, 4446, 311, 264, 43690, 382, 17, 13, 3719, 19052, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 12883, 20980, 11, 3156, 448, 2518, 24353, 81623, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 12021, 11, 323, 24353, 382, 18, 13, 52153, 8628, 311, 3347, 323, 3060, 17233, 279, 44597, 369, 220, 16, 15, 311, 220, 16, 17, 4420, 382, 19, 13, 10783, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 504, 279, 12883, 20980, 382, 20, 13, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 39058, 85354, 323, 855, 19963, 279, 39058, 311, 11051, 27561, 8628, 382, 21, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 11, 13054, 3055, 11, 369, 220, 20, 311, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 382, 22, 13, 52932, 448, 279, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 382, 641, 458, 10555, 1714, 1447, 16, 13, 2340, 865, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 438, 807, 4296, 382, 17, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 264, 3460, 5591, 3338, 448, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 382, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 382, 19, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 39058, 311, 11051, 27561, 8628, 382, 20, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 369, 220, 16, 15, 311, 220, 16, 19, 4420, 11, 13054, 22930, 311, 5978, 1496, 293, 50420, 382, 20629, 5413, 5978, 429, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 374, 29105, 26364, 1393, 7842, 17172, 311, 279, 12000, 13, 151645], "pred": "Both methods ensure that the bratwurst is cooked thoroughly while adding flavor to the dish.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1888256565132613, "g_worst_claim": 0.3367915153503418, "g_content": 1.5182412954477162, "g_traj_mean": 0.9356081485748291}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [3533, 865, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 13, 10771, 1105, 304, 264, 3460, 5591, 3338, 448, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 13, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 85354, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 369, 220, 16, 15, 311, 220, 16, 19, 4420, 11, 13054, 22930, 311, 13876, 41047, 13, 52932, 448, 279, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "Prick bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding. Place them in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat. Lightly oil the grate. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4992227319515115, "g_worst_claim": 0.7317902825095437, "g_content": 2.0320573286576704, "g_traj_mean": 1.4000813961029053}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 61.88, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "79", "question": "how to cook brats", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief guide on how to cook brats:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. Combine beer, onions, red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper in a large pot. Bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture.\n5. Reduce heat to medium and cook for 10 to 12 minutes.\n6. Remove the bratwurst from the beer mixture and place them on the preheated grill.\n7. Cook the bratwurst for 5 to 10 minutes, turning once.\n8. Serve the bratwurst with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\n\nSo, to cook brats, you first prepare the grill, then cook the bratwurst in a beer mixture before grilling them until they're done.", "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. In a large pot, combine the beer, onions, butter, and bratwurst.\n4. Bring to a boil and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n5. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n6. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n7. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly.\n8. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\n3. In a large pot, combine the beer, onions, butter, and bratwurst.\n4. Bring to a boil and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n5. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n6. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n7. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly.\n8. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "cot": "[\"To cook brats, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\\n2. Lightly oil the grill grate.\\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture, adding red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\\n5. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\\n6. Place the bratwurst in the pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\\n7. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n8. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\\n9. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\", \"To cook brats, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat (as mentioned in passage 3).\\n2. Lightly oil the grill grate (as mentioned in passage 2).\\n3. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding while cooking (as mentioned in passage 2).\\n4. Place the bratwurst and onions in a large pot with butter and beer (as mentioned in passage 2).\\n5. Bring the pot to a simmer over medium heat, and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes (as mentioned in passage 2).\\n6. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly (as mentioned in passage 2).\\n7. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side (as mentioned in passage 1).\\n\\nThese steps will help you cook brats properly and enjoy a delicious meal.\", \"To cook bratwursts, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding while cooking.\\n2. Place the bratwurst in a large stock pot with onions, butter, and beer.\\n3. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n4. Preheat the grill to medium-high heat.\\n5. Lightly oil the grill grate.\\n6. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to ensure even browning.\\n\\nThis method ensures that the bratwurst is cooked thoroughly while maintaining its texture and flavor.\", \"To cook brats, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\\n2. Lightly oil the grate.\\n3. In a large pot, combine the beer, onions, butter, and bratwurst.\\n4. Bring to a boil and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n5. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\\n6. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n7. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly.\\n8. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.\"]", "time_sec": 28.211, "generation_time_seconds": 27.3652, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8391, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1411, 1862, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 624, 17, 13, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 39058, 85354, 624, 18, 13, 46812, 279, 12883, 323, 44597, 304, 264, 3460, 3338, 26, 4446, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 19, 13, 3719, 19052, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 12883, 20980, 11, 7842, 2518, 24353, 81623, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 12021, 11, 323, 24353, 624, 20, 13, 2340, 865, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 438, 807, 4296, 624, 21, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 304, 279, 3338, 448, 279, 44597, 11, 14100, 11, 323, 12883, 624, 22, 13, 10771, 279, 3338, 916, 11051, 8628, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 11, 13054, 3055, 11, 369, 220, 20, 311, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 624, 24, 13, 52932, 448, 279, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat.\n2. Lightly oil the grill grate.\n3. Combine the beer and onions in a large pot; bring to a boil.\n4. Submerge the bratwurst in the beer mixture, adding red pepper flakes, garlic powder, salt, and pepper.\n5. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n6. Place the bratwurst in the pot with the onions, butter, and beer.\n7. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n8. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill, turning once, for 5 to 10 minutes.\n9. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3164517694152482, "g_worst_claim": 0.12210185825824738, "g_content": 1.8291223886850718, "g_traj_mean": 1.1752066612243652}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1411, 1862, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 27561, 8628, 320, 300, 9733, 304, 21085, 220, 18, 4292, 17, 13, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 39058, 85354, 320, 300, 9733, 304, 21085, 220, 17, 4292, 18, 13, 2340, 865, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 448, 264, 22435, 311, 5358, 1105, 504, 72645, 1393, 17233, 320, 300, 9733, 304, 21085, 220, 17, 4292, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 323, 44597, 304, 264, 3460, 3338, 448, 14100, 323, 12883, 320, 300, 9733, 304, 21085, 220, 17, 4292, 20, 13, 39124, 279, 3338, 311, 264, 61815, 916, 11051, 8628, 11, 323, 61815, 369, 220, 16, 20, 311, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 320, 300, 9733, 304, 21085, 220, 17, 4292, 21, 13, 12514, 279, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 389, 279, 855, 383, 657, 39058, 369, 220, 16, 15, 311, 220, 16, 19, 4420, 11, 13054, 22930, 311, 13876, 41047, 320, 300, 9733, 304, 21085, 220, 17, 4292, 22, 13, 52932, 448, 279, 12883, 20980, 438, 264, 60276, 476, 3108, 320, 300, 9733, 304, 21085, 220, 16, 3593, 9485, 7354, 686, 1492, 498, 4296, 1411, 1862, 10277, 323, 4669, 264, 17923, 15145, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps will help you cook brats properly and enjoy a delicious meal.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9044974931985409, "g_worst_claim": 0.17316242853800456, "g_content": 0.9570687831133261, "g_traj_mean": 0.8127294778823853}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 1411, 266, 86, 32612, 82, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 23