 and bratwurst.\n4. Bring to a boil and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n5. Prick the bratwurst with a fork to prevent them from exploding as they cook.\n6. Place the pot over medium heat and simmer for 15 to 20 minutes.\n7. Cook the bratwurst on the preheated grill for 10 to 14 minutes, turning occasionally to brown evenly.\n8. Serve with the beer mixture as a topping or side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.086536293345339, "g_worst_claim": 0.37918020884195963, "g_content": 1.2788148910280257, "g_traj_mean": 0.9429017901420593}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 58.28, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "80", "question": "symptoms and causes of ibs", "gt": "The cause of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) is unknown. However, it is believed to be a result of abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, disruption in communication between the brain and the GI tract, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances. Risk factors may include abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (either too fast or slow, or too strong), hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food. Symptoms of IBS can include diarrhea, constipation, or alternating between the two, belly pains or cramps that worsen after meals and feel better after a bowel movement, as well as a lot of gas or bloating.", "pred": "Causes of irritable bowel syndrome are thought to result from a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. It is believed to be due to a number of factors, including alteration in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Causes of irritable bowel syndrome are thought to result from a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. It is believed to be due to a number of factors, including alteration in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.", "cot": "[\"Symptoms of IBS include diarrhea, constipation, and alternating between the two. People with IBS often experience belly pains or cramps, especially after meals, and may have a lot of gas or bloating. The causes of IBS are not fully understood, but it is believed to be due to a combination of factors, including abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines, hypersensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.\", \"Symptoms of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) include diarrhea (often described as violent episodes of diarrhea), constipation, and constipation alternating with diarrhea. Belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement. A lot of gas or bloating.\\n\\nCauses of irritable bowel syndrome are thought to result from a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. It is believed to be due to a number of factors, including alteration in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.\", \"Symptoms of IBS include diarrhea, constipation, alternating constipation and diarrhea, belly pains or cramps, and a lot of gas or bloating. Causes of IBS are thought to result from abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract.\", \"Symptoms of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) include diarrhea (often described as violent episodes of diarrhea), constipation, and alternating between constipation and diarrhea. People with IBS may also experience belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, which often get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement. Additionally, there is a lot of gas or bloating.\\n\\nCauses of irritable bowel syndrome are currently unknown, but it is thought to result from a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. It is also believed to be due to a number of factors, including alteration in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances. Risk factors for IBS include abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines, hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities, possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food.\"]", "time_sec": 23.2, "generation_time_seconds": 22.263, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9283, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [27912, 51173, 315, 358, 7347, 2924, 68293, 11, 733, 48586, 11, 323, 72362, 1948, 279, 1378, 13, 8853, 448, 358, 7347, 3545, 3139, 35417, 50166, 476, 1560, 14647, 11, 5310, 1283, 20969, 11, 323, 1231, 614, 264, 2696, 315, 6819, 476, 14211, 1095, 13, 576, 11137, 315, 358, 7347, 525, 537, 7225, 15985, 11, 714, 432, 374, 11585, 311, 387, 4152, 311, 264, 10601, 315, 9363, 11, 2670, 34563, 19029, 315, 279, 14889, 323, 2613, 38308, 1543, 11, 86652, 47837, 311, 6646, 11, 323, 3607, 71629, 3020, 13, 151645], "pred": "Symptoms of IBS include diarrhea, constipation, and alternating between the two. People with IBS often experience belly pains or cramps, especially after meals, and may have a lot of gas or bloating. The causes of IBS are not fully understood, but it is believed to be due to a combination of factors, including abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines, hypersensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1482217028091004, "g_worst_claim": 0.20667624473571777, "g_content": 2.3160546439034597, "g_traj_mean": 1.091199517250061}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [27912, 51173, 315, 6216, 22533, 65258, 27339, 320, 3256, 50, 8, 2924, 68293, 320, 60817, 7481, 438, 16401, 17770, 315, 68293, 701, 733, 4