 to pain, and food intolerances. Risk factors include abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (too fast or slow, or too strong), hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities, possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food.\"]", "time_sec": 22.305, "generation_time_seconds": 21.5691, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7228, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [27912, 51173, 315, 358, 7347, 2924, 68293, 11, 733, 48586, 11, 323, 72362, 1948, 279, 1378, 13, 8853, 448, 358, 7347, 3545, 3139, 35417, 50166, 476, 1560, 14647, 11, 5310, 1283, 20969, 11, 323, 1231, 614, 264, 2696, 315, 6819, 476, 14211, 1095, 13, 576, 11137, 315, 358, 7347, 525, 537, 7225, 15985, 11, 714, 432, 374, 11585, 311, 387, 4152, 311, 264, 10601, 315, 9363, 11, 2670, 34563, 19029, 315, 279, 14889, 323, 2613, 38308, 1543, 11, 86652, 47837, 311, 6646, 11, 323, 3607, 71629, 3020, 13, 151645], "pred": "Symptoms of IBS include diarrhea, constipation, and alternating between the two. People with IBS often experience belly pains or cramps, especially after meals, and may have a lot of gas or bloating. The causes of IBS are not fully understood, but it is believed to be due to a combination of factors, including abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines, hypersensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1692771265001007, "g_worst_claim": 0.1892772674560547, "g_content": 2.3597298758370537, "g_traj_mean": 1.1047264337539673}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [27912, 51173, 315, 6216, 22533, 65258, 27339, 320, 3256, 50, 8, 2924, 68293, 11, 733, 48586, 11, 323, 733, 48586, 72362, 448, 68293, 13, 96585, 50166, 476, 1560, 14647, 11, 5990, 304, 279, 4722, 4279, 315, 279, 35417, 11, 429, 633, 10960, 1283, 20969, 323, 2666, 2664, 1283, 264, 65258, 7203, 13, 362, 2696, 315, 6819, 476, 14211, 1095, 382, 22571, 4776, 315, 6216, 22533, 65258, 27339, 320, 3256