{"id": "84", "question": "symptoms and causes of ibs", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here are the symptoms and causes of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) based on the given passages:\n\nSymptoms:\n\n* Diarrhea (often described as violent episodes of diarrhea)\n* Constipation\n* Constipation alternating with diarrhea\n* Belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement\n* A lot of gas or bloating\n\nCauses:\n\n* Abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements\n* Increased awareness of bodily functions\n* Disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract\n* Alterations in the GI tract motility\n* Abnormal nervous system signals\n* Increased sensitivity to pain\n* Food intolerances\n* Poor absorption of sugars or acids in food\n\nIt's worth noting that the exact cause of IBS is still unknown, and it's believed to be a complex interaction of various factors.", "pred": "Causes of IBS are currently unknown but are thought to be due to a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. It is also believed to be due to alteration in the gastrointestinal tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances. Risk factors thought to cause IBS include abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (too fast or slow, or too strong), hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities, possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Causes of IBS are currently unknown but are thought to be due to a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. It is also believed to be due to alteration in the gastrointestinal tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances. Risk factors thought to cause IBS include abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (too fast or slow, or too strong), hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities, possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food.", "cot": "[\"Symptoms of IBS include diarrhea, constipation, and alternating between the two. People with IBS often experience belly pains or cramps, especially after meals, and may have a lot of gas or bloating. The causes of IBS are not fully understood, but it is believed to be due to a combination of factors, including abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines, hypersensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.\", \"Symptoms of IBS include diarrhea (often described as violent episodes of diarrhea), constipation, constipation alternating with diarrhea, belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement, and a lot of gas or bloating.\\n\\nCauses of IBS are currently unknown but are thought to be due to a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. It is also believed to be due to alteration in the gastrointestinal tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances. Risk factors thought to cause IBS include abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (too fast or slow, or too strong), hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities, possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food.\", \"Symptoms of IBS include diarrhea (often described as violent episodes of diarrhea), constipation, constipation alternating with diarrhea, belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement, a lot of gas or bloating. Causes of IBS are believed to be due to a number of factors, including alteration in the gastrointestinal tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.\", \"Symptoms of IBS include diarrhea, constipation, alternating between the two, belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement, and a lot of gas or bloating.\\n\\nCauses of IBS are thought to result from a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. Other factors include alteration in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.\"]", "time_sec": 22.016, "generation_time_seconds": 21.4075, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6008, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [27912, 51173, 315, 358, 7347, 2924, 68293, 11, 733, 48586, 11, 323, 72362, 1948, 279, 1378, 13, 8853, 448, 358, 7347, 3545, 3139, 35417, 50166, 476, 1560, 14647, 11, 5310, 1283, 20969, 11, 323, 1231, 614, 264, 2696, 315, 6819, 476, 14211, 1095, 13, 576, 11137, 315, 358, 7347, 525, 537, 7225, 15985, 11, 714, 432, 374, 11585, 311, 387, 4152, 311, 264, 10601, 315, 9363, 11, 2670, 34563, 19029, 315, 279, 14889, 323, 2613, 38308, 1543, 11, 86652, 47837, 311, 6646, 11, 323, 3607, 71629, 3020, 13, 151645], "pred": "Symptoms of IBS include diarrhea, constipation, and alternating between the two. People with IBS often experience belly pains or cramps, especially after meals, and may have a lot of gas or bloating. The causes of IBS are not fully understood, but it is believed to be due to a combination of factors, including abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines, hypersensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1474701118163575, "g_worst_claim": 0.17869490385055542, "g_content": 2.3541724068777903, "g_traj_mean": 1.0981080532073975}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [27912, 51173, 315, 358, 7347, 2924, 68293, 320, 60817, 7481, 438, 16401, 17770, 315, 68293, 701, 733, 48586, 11, 733, 48586, 72362, 448, 68293, 11, 35417, 50166, 476, 1560, 14647, 11, 5990, 304, 279, 4722, 4279, 315, 279, 35417, 11, 429, 633, 10960, 1283, 20969, 323, 2666, 2664, 1283, 264, 65258, 7203, 11, 323, 264, 2696, 315, 6819, 476, 14211, 1095, 382, 22571, 4776, 315, 358, 7347, 525, 5023, 9788, 714, 525, 3381, 311, 387, 4152, 311, 264, 10601, 315, 34563, 79211, 41829, 19029, 11, 7172, 17526, 315, 47031, 5746, 11, 323, 264, 43119, 304, 279, 10535, 1948, 279, 8109, 323, 279, 48509, 41829, 13, 1084, 374, 1083, 11585, 311, 387, 4152, 311, 72581, 304, 279, 79211, 41829, 3852, 1403, 11, 34563, 22596, 1849, 17289, 11, 7172, 26443, 311, 6646, 11, 323, 3607, 71629, 3020, 13, 31288, 9363, 3381, 311, 5240, 358, 7347, 2924, 34563, 19029, 315, 279, 14889, 323, 2613, 38308, 1543, 320, 36127, 4937, 476, 6301, 11, 476, 2238, 3746, 701, 86652, 47837, 311, 6646, 504, 264, 2480, 65258, 476, 6819, 11, 323, 3607, 73533, 42379, 11, 10767, 8881, 553, 7852, 43125, 315, 69813, 476, 32869, 304, 3607, 13, 151645], "pred": "Causes of IBS are currently unknown but are thought to be due to a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. It is also believed to be due to alteration in the gastrointestinal tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances. Risk factors thought to cause IBS include abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (too fast or slow, or too strong), hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities, possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0089902961096353, "g_worst_claim": 0.8919402412746263, "g_content": 3.14613179957613, "g_traj_mean": 1.9776188135147095}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [27912, 51173, 315, 358, 7347, 2924, 68293, 320, 60817, 7481, 438, 16401, 17770, 315, 68293, 701, 733, 48586, 11, 733, 48586, 72362, 448, 68293, 11, 35417, 50166, 476, 1560, 14647, 11, 5990, 304, 279, 4722, 4279, 315, 279, 35417, 11, 429, 633, 10960, 1283, 20969, 323, 2666, 2664, 1283, 264, 65258, 7203, 11, 264, 2696, 315, 6819, 476, 14211, 1095, 13, 73005, 315, 358, 7347, 525, 11585, 311, 387, 4152, 311, 264, 1372, 315, 9363, 11, 2670, 72581, 304, 279, 79211, 41829, 3852, 1403, 11, 34563, 22596, 1849, 17289, 11, 7172, 26443, 311, 6646, 11, 323, 3607, 71629, 3020, 13, 151645], "pred": "Symptoms of IBS include diarrhea (often described as violent episodes of diarrhea), constipation, constipation alternating with diarrhea, belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement, a lot of gas or bloating. Causes of IBS are believed to be due to a number of factors, including alteration in the gastrointestinal tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.912473364698859, "g_worst_claim": 0.9207689921061198, "g_content": 3.02882042709662, "g_traj_mean": 1.8664122819900513}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [27912, 51173, 315, 358, 7347, 2924, 68293, 11, 733, 48586, 11, 72362, 1948, 279, 1378, 11, 35417, 50166, 476, 1560, 14647, 11, 5990, 304, 279, 4722, 4279, 315, 279, 35417, 11, 429, 633, 10960, 1283, 20969, 323, 2666, 2664, 1283, 264, 65258, 7203, 11, 323, 264, 2696, 315, 6819, 476, 14211, 1095, 382, 22571, 4776, 315, 358, 7347, 525, 3381, 311, 1102, 504, 264, 10601, 315, 34563, 79211, 320, 28034, 8, 41829, 19029, 11, 7172, 17526, 315, 47031, 5746, 11, 323, 264, 43119, 304, 279, 10535, 1948, 279, 8109, 323, 279, 48509, 41829, 13, 6944, 9363, 2924, 72581, 304, 279, 79211, 320, 28034, 8, 41829, 3852, 1403, 11, 34563, 22596, 1849, 17289, 11, 7172, 26443, 311, 6646, 11, 323, 3607, 71629, 3020, 13, 151645], "pred": "Causes of IBS are thought to result from a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. Other factors include alteration in the gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7944947946236214, "g_worst_claim": 0.7578057765960693, "g_content": 2.828341567725466, "g_traj_mean": 1.6345665454864502}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.78, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "85", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "To prepare a blood slide, first sterilize a needle with a flame. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add a small drop of blood to one end. Then, take another clean slide and holding it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry and label clearly. Once dried, place them in the provided slide transport containers. Always avoid coming into contact with another person's blood and if it is unavoidable, wear rubber gloves.", "pred": "First sterilize the needle with a flame. Place clean glass slide on a flat surface. Add one small drop of blood to one end. Take another clean slide, and holding at an angle of about 45 deg, touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Make 2 smears, allow to air dry, and label clearly. Once dried place in the provided slide transport containers.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "First sterilize the needle with a flame. Place clean glass slide on a flat surface. Add one small drop of blood to one end. Take another clean slide, and holding at an angle of about 45 deg, touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Make 2 smears, allow to air dry, and label clearly. Once dried place in the provided slide transport containers.", "cot": "[\"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\\n\\nThese steps ensure that the blood is spread evenly and thinly on the slide, which is essential for viewing and analysis.\", \"Include all details that support the answer.\\n\\n- To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n  1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n  2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n  3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n  4. Touch the blood with one end of the second slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n  5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n  6. Make 2 smears and allow them to air dry.\\n  7. Label the slides clearly.\\n  8. Once the slides are dried, place them in the provided slide transport containers.\", \"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add one small drop of blood to one end.\\n2. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees. Touch the blood on the first slide with one end of the second slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n3. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n4. Make 2 smears if necessary and allow them to air dry.\\n5. Label the slides clearly.\\n6. Once the slides are dried, place them in the provided slide transport containers.\\n\\nFor additional safety, ensure the materials used are sterilized and consider adult supervision, especially when pricking the finger.\", \"First sterilize the needle with a flame. Place clean glass slide on a flat surface. Add one small drop of blood to one end. Take another clean slide, and holding at an angle of about 45 deg, touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Make 2 smears, allow to air dry, and label clearly. Once dried place in the provided slide transport containers.\"]", "time_sec": 24.373, "generation_time_seconds": 23.3945, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9703, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 21, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 11, 2138, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 11, 323, 2383, 1105, 9355, 624, 22, 13, 9646, 31620, 11, 1992, 279, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 382, 9485, 7354, 5978, 429, 279, 6543, 374, 8865, 41047, 323, 98431, 389, 279, 14983, 11, 892, 374, 7565, 369, 20102, 323, 6358, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps ensure that the blood is spread evenly and thinly on the slide, which is essential for viewing and analysis.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.698609452055361, "g_worst_claim": 0.24109508196512858, "g_content": 1.9374324798583984, "g_traj_mean": 1.3806942701339722}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [22283, 678, 3565, 429, 1824, 279, 4226, 382,