, 2086, 14983, 773, 429, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 18, 13, 22950, 279, 2086, 14983, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 19, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 421, 5871, 323, 2138, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 624, 20, 13, 9402, 279, 21521, 9355, 624, 21, 13, 9646, 279, 21521, 525, 31620, 11, 1992, 1105, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 382, 2461, 5107, 7149, 11, 5978, 279, 7236, 1483, 525, 65640, 1506, 323, 2908, 6683, 37117, 11, 5310, 979, 548, 16272, 279, 14317, 13, 151645], "pred": "For additional safety, ensure the materials used are sterilized and consider adult supervision, especially when pricking the finger.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6982670410553906, "g_worst_claim": 0.3154349128405253, "g_content": 1.9909289129849137, "g_traj_mean": 1.4174869060516357}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [5338, 65640, 551, 279, 30309, 448, 264, 34578, 13, 10771, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 11, 323, 9963, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 5254, 11, 5796, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 13, 22950, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 11, 2138, 311, 3720, 9058, 11, 323, 2383, 9355, 13, 9646, 31620, 1992, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 13, 151645], "pred": "First sterilize the needle with a flame. Place clean glass slide on a flat surface. Add one small drop of blood to one end. Take another clean slide, and holding at an angle of about 45 deg, touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Make 2 smears, allow to air dry, and label clearly. Once dried place in the provided slide transport containers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.6083545899008684, "g_worst_claim": 1.576631228129069, "g_content": 3.2512420654296874, "g_traj_mean": 2.396130323410034}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 84.29, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.8, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "86", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "To prepare a blood slide, you will need a clean glass slide and a drop of blood. Place the slide on a flat surface and add a small drop of blood to one end of the slide. Take another clean slide and touch the blood with one end at a 45-degree angle so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly before placing them in slide transport containers.", "pred": "1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end.\n3. Take another clean slide and, holding it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n4. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end.\n3. Take another clean slide and, holding it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n4. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.", "cot": "[\"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\\n\\nThese steps ensure that the blood is spread evenly and thinly on the slide, which is essential for viewing and analysis.\", \"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the second slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\\n\\nThese steps will help you create a blood smear for examination.\", \"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Clean the Glass Slide**: Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. **Add Blood**: Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. **Create the Smear**: Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n4. **Repeat if Necessary**: Make 2 smears if needed.\\n5. **Allow to Air Dry**: Allow the smears to air dry completely.\\n6. **Label Clearly**: Once dried, clearly label the slides.\\n7. **Store**: Place the dried slides in the provided slide transport containers.\\n\\nThis process ensures a clear and identifiable blood smear for examination.\", \"1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end.\\n3. Take another clean slide and, holding it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n4. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\"]", "time_sec": 23.717, "generation_time_seconds": 22.899, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8108, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 21, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 11, 2138, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 11, 323, 2383, 1105, 9355, 624, 22, 13, 9646, 31620, 11, 1992, 279, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 382, 9485, 7354, 5978, 429, 279, 6543, 374, 8865, 41047, 323, 98431, 389, 279, 14983, 11, 892, 374, 7565, 369, 20102, 323, 6358, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps ensure that the blood is spread evenly and thinly on the slide, which is essential for viewing and analysis.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6843017709915278, "g_worst_claim": 0.21352580388387044, "g_content": 1.9316810607910155, "g_traj_mean": 1.3701751232147217}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 2086, 14983, 773, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 21, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 11, 2138, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 11, 323, 2383, 1105, 9355, 624, 22, 13, 9646, 31620, 11, 1992, 279, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 382, 9485, 7354, 686, 1492, 498, 1855, 264, 6543, 80503, 369, 23568, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps will help you create a blood smear for examination.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7738433579603827, "g_worst_claim": 0.3666451772054036, "g_content": 1.9618460915305398, "g_traj_mean": 1.4206339120864868}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 27529, 279, 20734, 43364, 95518, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 3070, 2212, 20070, 95518, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 3070, 4021, 279, 4388, 682, 95518, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 429, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 13, 22950, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 19, 13, 3070, 38718, 421, 94533, 95518, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 421, 4362, 624, 20, 13, 3070, 18605, 311, 6553, 30841, 95518, 26530, 279, 1525, 7444, 311, 3720, 9058, 6587, 624, 21, 13, 3070, 2476, 53404, 95518, 9646, 31620, 11, 9355, 2383, 279, 21521, 624, 22, 13, 3070, 6093, 95518, 10771, 279, 31620, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 382, 1986, 1882, 25351, 264, 2797, 323, 71350, 6543, 80503, 369, 23568, 13, 151645], "pred": "This process ensures a clear and identifiable blood smear for examination.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5190218631447232, "g_worst_claim": 0.28158462047576904, "g_content": 2.018455898638853, "g_traj_mean": 1.401884913444519}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 11, 9963, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 11, 5796, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 13, 22950, 279, 2086, 14983, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 19, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 11, 2138, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 11, 323, 2383, 1105, 9355, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end.\n3. Take another clean slide and, holding it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n4. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7692640366222736, "g_worst_claim": 0.7322210470835367, "g_content": 2.235156331743513, "g_traj_mean": 1.5765950679779053}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 75.41, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "88", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "Sure, I'd be happy to help you with that! Here are the steps to prepare a blood slide based on the provided passages:\n\n1. First, sterilize a needle with a flame as described in Passage 1.\n2. Next, obtain a blood sample by pricking your finger or using a blood donation kit. This will require adult supervision, especially if you are doing it yourself.\n3. Place a drop of blood towards one end of a clean glass slide as instructed in Passage 2.\n4. Take another clean slide and, holding it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide through capillary action. Gently push the blood along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Repeat this step to make two smears.\n5. Allow the smears to air dry completely before labeling them clearly and placing them in the provided slide transport containers as suggested in Passage 3.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "These steps ensure that the blood is spread evenly and thinly on the slide, which is essential for viewing and analysis.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "These steps ensure that the blood is spread evenly and thinly on the slide, which is essential for viewing and analysis.", "cot": "[\"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\\n\\nThese steps ensure that the blood is spread evenly and thinly on the slide, which is essential for viewing and analysis.\", \"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\", \"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Set Up**: Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. **Add Blood**: Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. **Smear**: Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees. Touch the blood with one end of the slide and allow the blood to run along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood.\\n4. **Repeat**: If needed, make a second smear.\\n5. **Dry**: Allow the smears to air dry completely.\\n6. **Label**: Clearly label the slides once they are dried.\\n7. **Store**: Place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\\n\\nThis process ensures that you have a thin, well-prepared blood smear ready for examination.\", \"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the second slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push the second slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make two smears and allow them to air dry.\\n7. Label the slides clearly once they are dried.\\n8. Place the dried slides in the provided slide transport containers for storage or analysis.\\n\\nThis method ensures that the blood smear is thin and well-distributed, making it easier to examine under a microscope.\"]", "time_sec": 25.858, "generation_time_seconds": 24.9977, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8503, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 21, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 11, 2138, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 11, 323, 2383, 1105, 9355, 624, 22, 13, 9646, 31620, 11, 1992, 279, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 382, 9485, 7354, 5978, 429, 279, 6543, 374, 8865, 41047, 323, 98431, 389, 279, 14983, 11, 892, 374, 7565, 369, 20102, 323, 6358, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps ensure that the blood is spread evenly and thinly on the slide, which is essential for viewing and analysis.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6837447309396558, "g_worst_claim": 0.22176863352457682, "g_content": 1.9280010223388673, "g_traj_mean": 1.3673955202102661}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 429, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 21, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 11, 2138, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 11, 323, 2383, 1105, 9355, 624, 22, 13, 9646, 31620, 11, 1992, 279, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 13, 151645], "pred": "To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8991331983094264, "g_worst_claim": 0.35121317704518634, "g_content": 2.1547932216099333, "g_traj_mean": 1.5206247568130493}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 1649, 3138, 95518, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 3070, 2212, 20070, 95518, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 3070, 10673, 682, 95518, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 323, 2138, 279, 6543, 311, 1598, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 13, 22950, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 1855, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 19, 13, 3070, 38718, 95518, 1416, 4362, 11, 1281, 264, 2086, 80503, 624, 20, 13, 3070, 85215, 95518, 26530, 279, 1525, 7444, 311, 3720, 9058, 6587, 624, 21, 13, 3070, 2476, 95518, 53404, 2383, 279, 21521, 3055, 807, 525, 31620, 624, 22, 13, 3070, 6093, 95518, 10771, 279, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 382, 1986, 1882, 25351, 429, 498, 614, 264, 15430, 11, 1632, 21334, 7212, 6543, 80503, 5527, 369, 23568, 13, 151645], "pred": "This process ensures that you have a thin, well-prepared blood smear ready for examination.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1674747263217193, "g_worst_claim": 0.19431461228264701, "g_content": 1.8112041766826923, "g_traj_mean": 1.1859500408172607}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 2086, 14983, 773, 429, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 279, 2086, 14983, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 21, 13, 7405, 1378, 1525, 7444, 323, 2138, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 624, 22, 13, 9402, 279, 21521, 9355, 3055, 807, 525, 31620, 624, 23, 13, 10771, 279, 31620, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 369, 5819, 476, 6358, 382, 1986, 1714, 25351, 429, 279, 6543, 80503, 374, 15430, 323, 1632, 1737, 25146, 11, 3259, 432, 8661, 311, 20961, 1212, 264, 72657, 13, 151645], "pred": "This method ensures that the blood smear is thin and well-distributed, making it easier to examine under a microscope.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.340980988746191, "g_worst_claim": -0.0007117340962092081, "g_content": 1.6508452675559304, "g_traj_mean": 1.1904728412628174}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 4.55, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "89", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here are the steps to prepare a blood slide:\n\n1. Sterilize the needle with a flame before using it to prick your finger or obtain blood from another source.\n2. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\n3. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\n4. Hold another clean slide at an angle of about 45 degrees and gently touch the blood with one end of the slide, allowing the blood to run along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n5. Carefully push the slide along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n6. Repeat step 4 and 5 to make two smears.\n7. Allow the slides to air dry.\n8. Label the slides clearly once they are dry.\n9. Place the slides in provided slide transport containers.\n\nNote: It is important to avoid coming into contact with another person's blood, and to wear rubber gloves if it is unavoidable.", "pred": "To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add one small drop of blood to one end.\n2. Take another clean slide, hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees, and touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n3. Push the slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n4. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\n5. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add one small drop of blood to one end.\n2. Take another clean slide, hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees, and touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\n3. Push the slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\n4. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\n5. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.", "cot": "[\"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\\n7. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\\n\\nThese steps ensure that the blood is spread evenly and thinly on the slide, which is essential for viewing and analysis.\", \"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps as outlined in the provided passages:\\n\\n1. **Place a Clean Glass Slide on a Flat Surface**: Start by placing a clean glass slide on a flat, stable surface. This surface should be clean and free of any debris that could contaminate the slide.\\n\\n2. **Add a Small Drop of Blood to One End**: Using a clean, sterilized needle (which is mentioned in the first passage), carefully add a small drop of blood to one end of the slide. The drop should be small enough to ensure that the blood is not immediately spread across the slide but is instead contained at one end.\\n\\n3. **Create the Smear**: Take another clean slide and hold it at an approximate angle of 45 degrees. Gently touch the end of this second slide to the drop of blood on the first slide. The second slide should be held in such a way that it touches the blood at an angle, allowing the blood to run along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n\\n4. **Push the Second Slide Along the Length of the First Slide**: Carefully push the second slide along the length of the first slide, ensuring that the blood is spread evenly and thinly. This process is designed to create a thin, continuous layer of blood on the first slide, which is essential for viewing the blood cells under a microscope.\\n\\n5. **Repeat the Process**: To ensure a good spread and to prepare for any mistakes, repeat the above steps by creating a second smear on the first slide.\\n\\n6. **Allow to Air Dry**: After creating the smears, allow them to air dry. This step is crucial as it ensures that the blood cells do not stick to the slide and allows the slide to be stored properly.\\n\\n7. **Label Clearly and Store**: Once the slides are dry, label each slide clearly with the date and the person’s name or identification number if applicable. Store the slides in the provided slide transport containers, ensuring they are protected from damage and contaminants.\\n\\nBy following these detailed steps, you can prepare a blood slide suitable for viewing under a microscope.\", \"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface.\\n2. Add one small drop of blood to one end of the slide.\\n3. Take another clean slide and hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees.\\n4. Touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n5. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n6. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\\n7. Once dried, place them in the provided slide transport containers.\", \"To prepare a blood slide, follow these steps:\\n1. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add one small drop of blood to one end.\\n2. Take another clean slide, hold it at an angle of about 45 degrees, and touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action.\\n3. Push the slide carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood.\\n4. Make 2 smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly.\\n5. Once dried, place the slides in the provided slide transport containers.\"]", "time_sec": 32.437, "generation_time_seconds": 31.4689, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9607, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10771, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 7329, 624, 17, 13, 2691, 825, 2613, 5943, 315, 6543, 311, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 624, 18, 13, 11778, 2441, 4240, 14983, 323, 3331, 432, 518, 458, 9210, 315, 911, 220, 19, 20, 12348, 624, 19, 13, 19338, 279, 6543, 448, 825, 835, 315, 279, 14983, 773, 279, 6543, 8473, 3156, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 14983, 553, 2062, 34505, 1917, 624, 20, 13, 22950, 15516, 3156, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 1156, 14983, 311, 8193, 264, 15430, 80503, 315, 6543, 624, 21, 13, 7405, 220, 17, 1525, 7444, 11, 2138, 1105, 311, 3720, 9058, 11, 323, 2383, 1105, 9355, 624, 22, 13, 9646, 31620, 11, 1992, 279, 21521, 304, 279, 3897, 14983, 7557, 23853, 382, 9485, 7354, 5978, 429, 279, 6543, 374, 8865, 41047, 323, 98431, 389, 279, 14983, 11, 892, 374, 7565, 369, 20102, 323, 6358, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps ensure that the blood is spread evenly and thinly on the slide, which is essential for viewing and analysis.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.676470721392594, "g_worst_claim": 0.25056788126627605, "g_content": 1.9032745361328125, "g_traj_mean": 1.359816551208496}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 10549, 264, 6543, 14983, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 438, 32640, 304, 279, 3897, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 17371, 264, 9590, 20734, 43364, 389, 264, 23577, 26963, 95518, 5145, 553, 24047, 264, 4240, 8991, 14983, 389, 264, 10063, 11, 15175, 7329, 13, 1096, 7329, 1265, 387, 4240, 323, 1910, 315, 894, 33998, 429, 1410, 683, 309, 3277, 279, 14983, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 2212, 264, 14994, 1