 and the driest year in 1934 having only 24.97 inches of measured rain. Additionally, there have been instances of extreme snowfall, with the most snowfall recorded in 1979 in Rockford at 74.5 inches in one season.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1249276712502294, "g_worst_claim": 0.32173556089401245, "g_content": 1.703789774576823, "g_traj_mean": 1.183016300201416}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 72925, 9104, 304, 41351, 11, 21591, 11, 3639, 4180, 11, 374, 31871, 553, 1293, 11, 8205, 11, 65938, 79669, 11, 323, 80875, 11, 92921, 84982, 13, 576, 19879, 11136, 2088, 504, 220, 17, 17, 58472, 311, 220, 23, 20, 58472, 11, 448, 8848, 21025, 3685, 220, 18, 58472, 476, 37168, 3403, 220, 24, 17, 58472, 13, 151645], "pred": "Typical weather in Indianapolis, Indiana, United States, is characterized by long, warm, humid summers, and chilly, windy winters. The temperatures typically range from 22°F to 85°F, with rare drops below 3°F or rises above 92°F.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4618019227267933, "g_worst_claim": 0.48567994435628253, "g_content": 2.2903125, "g_traj_mean": 1.4632723331451416}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [641, 41351, 11, 21591, 11, 279, 79669, 525, 1293, 11, 8205, 11, 65938, 11, 323, 14401, 26, 279, 84982, 525, 80875, 323, 92921, 26, 323, 432, 374, 27037, 73549, 1042, 4778, 13, 151645], "pred": "In Indianapolis, Indiana, the summers are long, warm, humid, and wet; the winters are chilly and windy; and it is partly cloudy year round.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.042621803283691, "g_worst_claim": 1.8971757888793945, "g_content": 3.2347046988351003, "g_traj_mean": 2.0298683643341064}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "100", "question": "how to sync audiobook from iphone to itunes", "gt": "To sync an audiobook from iPhone to iTunes, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open iTunes on your computer.\n2. Turn on the Manually manage music setting in iTunes.\n3. Download the audiobook from iTunes onto your iPhone.\n4. Connect your iPhone to the USB cable and plug the other end of the USB cable into a USB port on the computer.\n5. Wait for iTunes to sync the audiobook to your iPhone.\n6. After the sync is complete, the audiobook will be on your iPhone.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 6.494, "generation_time_seconds": 5.8806, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6074, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.0883883386850357, "g_worst_claim": -0.0883883386850357, "g_content": -0.1427575945854187, "g_traj_mean": -0.07869019359350204}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.0883883386850357, "g_worst_claim": -0.0883883386850357, "g_content": -0.1427575945854187, "g_traj_mean": -0.07869019359350204}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.0883883386850357, "g_worst_claim": -0.0883883386850357, "g_content": -0.1427575945854187, "g_traj_mean": -0.07869019359350204}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.0883883386850357, "g_worst_claim": -0.0883883386850357, "g_content": -0.1427575945854187, "g_traj_mean": -0.07869019359350204}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "101", "question": "how to sync audiobook from iphone to itunes", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to sync audiobooks from an iPhone to iTunes:\n\n1. Turn on the Manually manage music setting in iTunes.\n2. Download the audiobook you want from iTunes.\n3. Connect your iPhone to the computer via USB cable.\n4. Click on \"Audiobooks\" on the left task pane of the iTunes window.\n5. Select the audiobook you want to sync by clicking on its title.\n6. Click \"Sync Audiobooks\" and choose the audiobooks you want to transfer.\n7. Click \"Apply\" to start the syncing process.\n\nAlternatively, you can use Syncios Audiobook Transfer to transfer audiobooks from your iPhone to iTunes. The software allows two-way transfer of files, so you can not only backup files to your PC but also transfer audiobooks from your PC to your iPhone. Here are the steps to use Syncios Audiobook Transfer:\n\n1. Launch Syncios Audiobook Transfer on your computer.\n2. Connect your iPhone to the computer via USB cable.\n3. Click on \"Audiobooks\" on the top menu bar.\n4. Select the audiobooks you want to transfer and click \"Export\" to save them to your computer.\n5. Alternatively, you can also click \"Import\" to add new audiobooks from your computer to your iPhone.\n6. Click \"Apply\" to start the transfer process.\n\nNote that the above steps are based on the assumption that you have already turned on the Manually manage music setting in iTunes. If you have not done so, you will need to do so before attempting to sync your audiobooks.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 6.715, "generation_time_seconds": 6.0831, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6247, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.08913374692201614, "g_worst_claim": -0.08913374692201614, "g_content": -0.14384706020355226, "g_traj_mean": -0.07933840155601501}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.08913374692201614, "g_worst_claim": -0.08913374692201614, "g_content": -0.14384706020355226, "g_traj_mean": -0.07933840155601501}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.08913374692201614, "g_worst_claim": -0.08913374692201614, "g_content": -0.14384706020355226, "g_traj_mean": -0.07933840155601501}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.08913374692201614, "g_worst_claim": -0.08913374692201614, "g_content": -0.14384706020355226, "g_traj_mean": -0.07933840155601501}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 3.16, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "102", "question": "how to sync audiobook from iphone to itunes", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to sync audiobooks from iPhone to iTunes:\n\n1. Connect your iPhone to your computer using a USB cable.\n2. Open iTunes on your computer.\n3. Click on the \"Audiobooks\" tab on the left side of the iTunes window.\n4. Check the boxes next to the audiobooks you want to sync to your iPhone.\n5. Click the \"Sync Audiobooks\" button and choose the audiobooks you want to transfer or select \"All Audiobooks\" to transfer all of them to your iPhone.\n6. Click \"Apply\" at the bottom of the screen to finish the syncing process.\n\nAlternatively, you can use Syncios Audiobook Transfer to transfer audiobooks from your computer to your iOS device. To do this, follow these steps:\n\n1. Launch Syncios Audiobook Transfer on your computer.\n2. Connect your iPhone to your computer using a USB cable.\n3. Click on the \"Books\" tab on the top menu bar.\n4. Select the audiobooks you want to transfer from your computer to your iPhone.\n5. Click the \"Import\" button to transfer the selected audiobooks to your iPhone.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"To sync audiobooks from an iPhone to iTunes, please follow these instructions:\\n1. Launch iTunes on your computer.\\n2. Connect your iPhone to the PC using a USB cable.\\n3. Click on the name of your iPhone under \\\"Devices\\\" in the left column of the iTunes window.\\n4. Choose \\\"Books\\\" above the main iTunes window.\\n5. Select the audiobooks you want to transfer.\\n6. Click \\\"Sync Audiobooks\\\" and then choose the audiobooks you want to transfer or select \\\"All Audiobooks\\\" to transfer all of them to the iPhone.\\n7. Click \\\"Apply\\\" at the bottom of the screen to finish the syncing process.\\n8. If you want to add new audiobooks from your PC to your iOS devices, click \\\"Import\\\" and select the audiobooks you want to transfer.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 12.286, "generation_time_seconds": 11.2908, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9893, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.08760025352239609, "g_worst_claim": -0.08760025352239609, "g_content": -0.14281452894210817, "g_traj_mean": -0.0779891386628151}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.08760025352239609, "g_worst_claim": -0.08760025352239609, "g_content": -0.14281452894210817, "g_traj_mean": -0.0779891386628151}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 12811, 46368, 674, 14685, 504, 458, 12167, 311, 13025, 11, 4486, 1795, 1493, 11221, 510, 16, 13, 23205, 13025, 389, 697, 6366, 624, 17, 13, 13015, 697, 12167, 311, 279, 6673, 1667, 264, 11348, 14652, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 829, 315, 697, 12167, 1212, 330, 40835, 1, 304, 279, 2115, 3250, 315, 279, 13025, 3241, 624, 19, 13, 22201, 330, 24341, 1, 3403, 279, 1887, 13025, 3241, 624, 20, 13, 8427, 279, 46368, 674, 14685, 498, 1366, 311, 8317, 624, 21, 13, 9189, 330, 12154, 39828, 674, 14685, 1, 323, 1221, 5157, 279, 46368, 674, 14685, 498, 1366, 311, 8317, 476, 3293, 330, 2403, 39828, 674, 14685, 1, 311, 8317, 678, 315, 1105, 311, 279, 12167, 624, 22, 13, 9189, 330, 28497, 1, 518, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 4171, 311, 6248, 279, 96145, 1882, 624, 23, 13, 1416, 498, 1366, 311, 912, 501, 46368, 674, 14685, 504, 697, 6673, 311, 697, 16048, 7611, 11, 4205, 330, 11511, 1, 323, 3293, 279, 46368, 674, 14685, 498, 1366, 311, 8317, 13, 151645], "pred": "To sync audiobooks from an iPhone to iTunes, please follow these instructions:\n1. Launch iTunes on your computer.\n2. Connect your iPhone to the PC using a USB cable.\n3. Click on the name of your iPhone under \"Devices\" in the left column of the iTunes window.\n4. Choose \"Books\" above the main iTunes window.\n5. Select the audiobooks you want to transfer.\n6. Click \"Sync Audiobooks\" and then choose the audiobooks you want to transfer or select \"All Audiobooks\" to transfer all of them to the iPhone.\n7. Click \"Apply\" at the bottom of the screen to finish the syncing process.\n8. If you want to add new audiobooks from your PC to your iOS devices, click \"Import\" and select the audiobooks you want to transfer.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0279875460995656, "g_worst_claim": -0.08456897735595703, "g_content": 1.3774852752685547, "g_traj_mean": 0.9235711097717285}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.08760025352239609, "g_worst_claim": -0.08760025352239609, "g_content": -0.14281452894210817, "g_traj_mean": -0.0779891386628151}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 4.14, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "103", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "The various systems in the human body work together to ensure its normal functioning. For instance, the urinary system works with all other systems to clean the blood by removing waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. This includes organs like the kidneys and lower intestines. Similarly, the respiratory system also collaborates with all other systems to provide oxygen to all body parts and remove carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. The respiratory system comprises the nose, larynx, trachea, and lungs.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by supporting each other in maintaining normal bodily functions. For example, the urinary system works closely with the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems to clean waste products from the body. Similarly, the respiratory system works closely with the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems to provide oxygen and remove carbon dioxide. Additionally, the reproductive and endocrine systems also work together to maintain overall health and function.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by supporting each other in maintaining normal bodily functions. For example, the urinary system works closely with the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems to clean waste products from the body. Similarly, the respiratory system works closely with the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems to provide oxygen and remove carbon dioxide. Additionally, the reproductive and endocrine systems also work together to maintain overall health and function.", "cot": "[\"The body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.\", \"The body systems work together to maintain normal functioning. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems by including the kidneys and lower intestines. Similarly, the respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems, including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous systems, collaborate to ensure the body's overall health and well-being.\", \"The body systems work together to maintain normal functioning. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from other systems, while the respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide. These systems are interconnected and collaborative in their roles within the human body.\", \"Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by supporting each other in maintaining normal bodily functions. For example, the urinary system works closely with the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems to clean waste products from the body. Similarly, the respiratory system works closely with the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems to provide oxygen and remove carbon dioxide. Additionally, the reproductive and endocrine systems also work together to maintain overall health and function.\"]", "time_sec": 16.606, "generation_time_seconds": 15.727, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8721, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 553, 1817, 1849, 28720, 311, 279, 8084, 30201, 315, 279, 2487, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 3871, 504, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 576, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 369, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 504, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 151645], "pred": "The body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2505677289471906, "g_worst_claim": 0.04303254187107086, "g_content": 2.077694660908467, "g_traj_mean": 1.3126907348632812}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 311, 10306, 4622, 30201, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 3871, 504, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 553, 2670, 279, 80860, 323, 4722, 38308, 1543, 13, 34239, 11, 279, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 369, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 504, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 4220, 5942, 11, 2670, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 835, 77638, 11, 42645, 774, 11, 22077, 11, 41789, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 11, 50596, 311, 5978, 279, 2487, 594, 8084, 2820, 323, 1632, 32751, 13, 151645], "pred": "The body systems work together to maintain normal functioning. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems by including the kidneys and lower intestines. Similarly, the respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. These systems, including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous systems, collaborate to ensure the body's overall health and well-being.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2548660053195906, "g_worst_claim": -0.5601004362106323, "g_content": 2.132071940104167, "g_traj_mean": 1.267688512802124}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 311, 10306, 4622, 30201, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 3871, 504, 1008, 5942, 11, 1393, 279, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 369, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 13, 4220, 5942, 525, 82316, 323, 39706, 304, 862, 12783, 2878, 279, 3738, 2487, 13, 151645], "pred": "The body systems work together to maintain normal functioning. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from other systems, while the respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide. These systems are interconnected and collaborative in their roles within the human body.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4471256114187694, "g_worst_claim": 0.47351036752973286, "g_content": 1.4938072204589843, "g_traj_mean": 1.2193210124969482}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 553, 12613, 1817, 1008, 304, 20337, 4622, 47031, 5746, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 4278, 15148, 448, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 311, 4240, 12291, 3871, 504, 279, 2487, 13, 34239, 11, 279, 41531, 1849, 4278, 15148, 448, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 311, 3410, 23552, 323, 4057, 12499, 39489, 13, 22406, 11, 279, 41789, 323, 835, 77638, 5942, 1083, 975, 3786, 311, 10306, 8084, 2820, 323, 729, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together by supporting each other in maintaining normal bodily functions. For example, the urinary system works closely with the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems to clean waste products from the body. Similarly, the respiratory system works closely with the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems to provide oxygen and remove carbon dioxide. Additionally, the reproductive and endocrine systems also work together to maintain overall health and function.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.864042702893502, "g_worst_claim": -0.0003430561886893378, "g_content": 1.514681690144089, "g_traj_mean": 0.9073867797851562}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.32, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "104", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "The body systems work together in order to maintain the normal functioning of the human body. These systems include the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous systems. Each system has its own specific functions, but they also work in conjunction with one another to ensure the overall well-being of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from various systems such as the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. Similarly, the respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "pred": "The body systems work together in a coordinated manner to maintain normal functioning. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary and nervous systems.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The body systems work together in a coordinated manner to maintain normal functioning. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary and nervous systems.", "cot": "[\"The body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.\", \"The body systems work together by each system performing specific functions that are crucial for the overall functioning of the body. For example, the respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide, while the urinary system cleans waste products from various systems including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The skeletal system provides support and protection for the body, and the muscular system allows for movement and maintaining body posture. The digestive system breaks down food into nutrients that the body needs, and the circulatory system distributes these nutrients throughout the body. The endocrine system, through hormones, regulates various body processes such as growth, metabolism, and reproduction. The lymphatic system helps to fight infections and remove waste from the body, and the immune system defends against harmful pathogens. The reproductive system plays a role in the continuation of the species. These systems work in harmony to maintain the body's internal balance and to ensure the survival of the individual.\", \"The body systems work together to maintain homeostasis and support various bodily functions. The skeletal system provides structure and support, the muscular system facilitates movement, the digestive system processes nutrients, the respiratory system supplies oxygen and expels carbon dioxide, the circulatory system distributes oxygen, nutrients, and hormones throughout the body, the urinary system removes waste products, the endocrine system regulates hormonal activities, the lymphatic system helps in immunity and fluid balance, and the immune system defends against pathogens. Each system contributes to the overall health and functioning of the body, depending on the specific needs and demands of the body at any given time.\", \"The body systems work together in a coordinated manner to maintain normal functioning. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary and nervous systems.\"]", "time_sec": 19.742, "generation_time_seconds": 18.9139, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8229, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 553, 1817, 1849, 28720, 311, 279, 8084, 30201, 315, 279, 2487, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 3871, 504, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 576, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 369, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 504, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 151645], "pred": "The body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2528367106178226, "g_worst_claim": 0.03970950096845627, "g_content": 2.080211536304371, "g_traj_mean": 1.321921467781067}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 553, 1817, 1849, 16380, 3151, 5746, 429, 525, 16587, 369, 279, 8084, 30201, 315, 279, 2487, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 311, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 11, 1393, 279, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 3871, 504, 5257, 5942, 2670, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 