45, "g_content": 0.920723036964341, "g_traj_mean": 0.5778607130050659}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 311, 10306, 2114, 535, 10718, 323, 1824, 5257, 47031, 5746, 13, 576, 68297, 1849, 5707, 5944, 323, 1824, 11, 279, 51092, 1849, 72533, 7203, 11, 279, 58971, 1849, 11364, 36393, 11, 279, 41531, 1849, 16720, 23552, 323, 1343, 2010, 12499, 39489, 11, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 95735, 23552, 11, 36393, 11, 323, 43215, 6814, 279, 2487, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 28160, 12291, 3871, 11, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 79312, 73118, 7488, 11, 279, 42645, 774, 1849, 8609, 304, 39268, 323, 15590, 8172, 11, 323, 279, 22077, 1849, 80960, 2348, 77184, 13, 8886, 1849, 42972, 311, 279, 8084, 2820, 323, 30201, 315, 279, 2487, 11, 11649, 389, 279, 3151, 3880, 323, 18154, 315, 279, 2487, 518, 894, 2661, 882, 13, 151645], "pred": "The body systems work together to maintain homeostasis and support various bodily functions. The skeletal system provides structure and support, the muscular system facilitates movement, the digestive system processes nutrients, the respiratory system supplies oxygen and expels carbon dioxide, the circulatory system distributes oxygen, nutrients, and hormones throughout the body, the urinary system removes waste products, the endocrine system regulates hormonal activities, the lymphatic system helps in immunity and fluid balance, and the immune system defends against pathogens. Each system contributes to the overall health and functioning of the body, depending on the specific needs and demands of the body at any given time.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.3133135670410759, "g_worst_claim": -0.07093195120493571, "g_content": 0.42783235822405136, "g_traj_mean": 0.296476274728775}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 304, 264, 46572, 11566, 311, 10306, 4622, 30201, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 3871, 504, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 576, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 369, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 504, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 151645], "pred": "The body systems work together in a coordinated manner to maintain normal functioning. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary and nervous systems.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.587235219405145, "g_worst_claim": 0.7214260896046957, "g_content": 2.1288638867829976, "g_traj_mean": 1.4823031425476074}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 66.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.8, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "105", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how the body systems work together:\n\n1. The skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, and nervous systems all work together to help keep the body functioning normally. (Passage 1)\n2. The urinary system works closely with all other systems of the body to clean blood from the body and remove waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. (Passage 2)\n3. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the body systems work together in the following ways:\n\n* The skeletal system provides support and structure for the body, while the muscular system helps move the body and its parts.\n* The digestive system breaks down food into nutrients that can be absorbed and used by the body, while the respiratory system provides oxygen for energy production.\n* The circulatory system delivers oxygenated blood to the body's cells and removes carbon dioxide, while the urinary system removes waste products from the blood.\n* The endocrine system produces hormones that regulate various bodily functions, including growth and development, metabolism, and reproductive processes.\n* The lymphatic system helps defend the body against infection and disease, while the immune system fights off foreign invaders.\n* The nervous system controls and coordinates the body's functions, including movement, sensation, and thought processes.\n\nOverall, the body's systems work together in a complex interplay to maintain homeostasis and ensure the proper functioning of the body.", "pred": "The body systems work together to keep the body functioning normally. Some systems work closely with others, such as the urinary system, which cleans waste products from several other systems including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from several other systems including the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The body systems work together to keep the body functioning normally. Some systems work closely with others, such as the urinary system, which cleans waste products from several other systems including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from several other systems including the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "cot": "[\"The body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.\", \"Based on the given passages, the human body systems work together in the following way:\\n\\n1. **Skeletal System**: Supports the body and provides structure for muscle attachment. It helps with movement, protection of vital organs, and production of blood cells.\\n\\n2. **Muscular System**: Composed of muscles that enable movement, posture, and body warmth. Muscles work in conjunction with the nervous system to facilitate coordinated actions.\\n\\n3. **Digestive System**: Processes food, absorbs nutrients, and eliminates waste. It interacts with the circulatory system to transport absorbed nutrients to cells and with the immune system to detect and respond to pathogens.\\n\\n4. **Respiratory System**: Supplies oxygen to the body and expels carbon dioxide. It works closely with the circulatory system to distribute oxygen to tissues and remove carbon dioxide, which is produced by cells during metabolism.\\n\\n5. **Circulatory System**: Transporting oxygen, nutrients, hormones, and waste products throughout the body. It regulates body temperature and pH, and helps in maintaining fluid balance.\\n\\n6. **Urinary System**: Filters blood to remove waste products, excess water, and electrolytes. It works with the digestive and circulatory systems to maintain fluid balance and regulate electrolyte levels.\\n\\n7. **Endocrine System**: Regulates metabolism, growth, development, and reproduction through the secretion of hormones. It interacts with the nervous system to coordinate responses to internal and external stimuli.\\n\\n8. **Lymphatic System**: Part of the immune system, it circulates lymph fluid to fight infections and remove waste products. It works with the immune system to protect the body against pathogens.\\n\\n9. **Immune System**: Defends the body against pathogens and foreign substances. It works with the lymphatic system to respond to infections and with the endocrine system to regulate immune responses.\\n\\n10. **Reproductive System**: Produces sex cells and initiates sexual development. It works with the endocrine system to coordinate reproductive functions.\\n\\n11. **Nervous System**: Controls and coordinates bodily functions through the transmission of signals. It works with all other systems to integrate and respond to stimuli from the environment.\\n\\nEach system is interconnected and interdependent, forming a complex network that ensures the body functions as a whole. For example, the urinary system works closely with the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, and circulatory systems to clean blood and remove waste products. Similarly, the respiratory system works with the skeletal, muscular, digestive, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems to provide oxygen and remove carbon dioxide\", \"Several systems in the human body work together to help keep it functioning normally. These systems include the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous systems. The urinary system works closely with all other systems of the body to clean blood, removing waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system also works closely with all other systems to provide oxygen for all body parts and remove carbon dioxide.\", \"The body systems work together to keep the body functioning normally. Some systems work closely with others, such as the urinary system, which cleans waste products from several other systems including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from several other systems including the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.\"]", "time_sec": 29.02, "generation_time_seconds": 28.2682, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7454, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 553, 1817, 1849, 28720, 311, 279, 8084, 30201, 315, 279, 2487, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 3871, 504, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 576, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 369, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 504, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 151645], "pred": "The body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2703505172799616, "g_worst_claim": 0.04376643896102905, "g_content": 2.0738319190772803, "g_traj_mean": 1.3270362615585327}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 3738, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 304, 279, 2701, 1616, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 50, 85155, 739, 95518, 66446, 279, 2487, 323, 5707, 5944, 369, 15747, 19984, 13, 1084, 8609, 448, 7203, 11, 9135, 315, 16198, 35753, 11, 323, 5670, 315, 6543, 7761, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 61598, 21366, 739, 95518, 1198, 3865, 315, 23648, 429, 7283, 7203, 11, 47278, 11, 323, 2487, 40363, 13, 5331, 18638, 975, 304, 31446, 448, 279, 22596, 1849, 311, 27596, 46572, 6168, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 45217, 533, 739, 95518, 62303, 3607, 11, 90011, 36393, 11, 323, 59844, 12291, 13, 1084, 83161, 448, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 7557, 41001, 36393, 311, 7761, 323, 448, 279, 22077, 1849, 311, 11140, 323, 5889, 311, 77184, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 1061, 5565, 5269, 739, 95518, 50252, 23552, 311, 279, 2487, 323, 1343, 2010, 12499, 39489, 13, 1084, 4278, 15148, 448, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 16417, 23552, 311, 38781, 323, 4057, 12499, 39489, 11, 892, 374, 8947, 553, 7761, 2337, 37997, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 34, 2437, 37120, 739, 95518, 16742, 287, 23552, 11, 36393, 11, 43215, 11, 323, 12291, 3871, 6814, 279, 2487, 13, 1084, 79312, 2487, 9315, 323, 36043, 11, 323, 8609, 304, 20337, 15590, 8172, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 54515, 3287, 739, 95518, 45012, 6543, 311, 4057, 12291, 3871, 11, 13623, 3015, 11, 323, 72296, 2338, 13, 1084, 4278, 448, 279, 58971, 323, 4225, 37120, 5942, 311, 10306, 15590, 8172, 323, 36277, 72296, 665, 5866, 382, 22, 13, 3070, 3727, 77638, 739, 95518, 3184, 23156, 37997, 11, 6513, 11, 4401, 11, 323, 38556, 1526, 279, 85967, 315, 43215, 13, 1084, 83161, 448, 279, 22596, 1849, 311, 16184, 14507, 311, 5306, 323, 9250, 55588, 382, 23, 13, 3070, 43, 31700, 774, 739, 95518, 3660, 315, 279, 22077, 1849, 11, 432, 4225, 23156, 42645, 15590, 311, 4367, 28920, 323, 4057, 12291, 3871, 13, 1084, 4278, 448, 279, 22077, 1849, 311, 6016, 279, 2487, 2348, 77184, 382, 24, 13, 3070, 50739, 2886, 739, 95518, 3892, 1412, 279, 2487, 2348, 77184, 323, 7214, 32055, 13, 1084, 4278, 448, 279, 42645, 774, 1849, 311, 5889, 311, 28920, 323, 448, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 311, 36277, 22077, 14507, 382, 16, 15, 13, 3070, 693, 33270, 739, 95518, 12042, 1603, 1839, 7761, 323, 12672, 973, 7244, 4401, 13, 1084, 4278, 448, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 311, 16184, 41789, 5746, 382, 16, 16, 13, 3070, 45, 648, 782, 739, 95518, 32070, 323, 13934, 47031, 5746, 1526, 279, 18368, 315, 17289, 13, 1084, 4278, 448, 678, 1008, 5942, 311, 31072, 323, 5889, 311, 55588, 504, 279, 4573, 382, 4854, 1849, 374, 82316, 323, 946, 37555, 11, 29064, 264, 6351, 3922, 429, 25351, 279, 2487, 5746, 438, 264, 4361, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 4278, 15148, 448, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 323, 4225, 37120, 5942, 311, 4240, 6543, 323, 4057, 12291, 3871, 13, 34239, 11, 279, 41531, 1849, 4278, 448, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 311, 3410, 23552, 323, 4057, 12499, 39489], "pred": "Each system is interconnected and interdependent, forming a complex network that ensures the body functions as a whole. For example, the urinary system works closely with the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, and circulatory systems to clean blood and remove waste products. Similarly, the respiratory system works with the skeletal, muscular, digestive, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems to provide oxygen and remove carbon dioxide", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.23909256355880254, "g_worst_claim": -0.17941226561864218, "g_content": 0.40783802543099473, "g_traj_mean": 0.2481006681919098}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [34762, 5942, 304, 279, 3738, 2487, 975, 3786, 311, 1492, 2506, 432, 30201, 14279, 13, 4220, 5942, 2924, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 835, 77638, 11, 42645, 774, 11, 22077, 11, 41789, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 576, 71635, 1849, 4278, 15148, 448, 678, 1008, 5942, 315, 279, 2487, 311, 4240, 6543, 11, 17592, 12291, 3871, 504, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 576, 41531, 1849, 1083, 4278, 15148, 448, 678, 1008, 5942, 311, 3410, 23552, 369, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 4057, 12499, 39489, 13, 151645], "pred": "Several systems in the human body work together to help keep it functioning normally. These systems include the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous systems. The urinary system works closely with all other systems of the body to clean blood, removing waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system also works closely with all other systems to provide oxygen for all body parts and remove carbon dioxide.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3873320532751878, "g_worst_claim": -0.08111593127250671, "g_content": 1.8678165011935763, "g_traj_mean": 1.2747278213500977}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 311, 2506, 279, 2487, 30201, 14279, 13, 4329, 5942, 975, 15148, 448, 3800, 11, 1741, 438, 279, 71635, 1849, 11, 892, 34194, 12291, 3871, 504, 3807, 1008, 5942, 2670, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 576, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 369, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 504, 3807, 1008, 5942, 2670, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 151645], "pred": "The body systems work together to keep the body functioning normally. Some systems work closely with others, such as the urinary system, which cleans waste products from several other systems including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from several other systems including the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.204579476900652, "g_worst_claim": 0.07209499180316925, "g_content": 2.0946668541949727, "g_traj_mean": 1.346176028251648}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.82, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "106", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the body systems work together as follows:\n\nThe skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, and reproductive systems all work together to help keep the body functioning normally. The urinary system helps to clean waste products from the other systems, while the respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the other systems. The nervous system plays a crucial role in coordinating the functions of all the other systems.", "pred": "The body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "cot": "[\"The body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.\", \"The body systems work together by coordinating their functions to maintain optimal body function. For example, the respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide, which is essential for the functioning of the muscular and other systems. The urinary system cleans waste products from several other systems, including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The skeletal and muscular systems support movement and provide structural support, which is necessary for the respiratory and circulatory systems to function properly. The circulatory system transports oxygen and nutrients to all parts of the body, which is essential for the functioning of the endocrine and nervous systems. These systems work in concert to maintain the body's overall health and function.\", \"The systems in the human body work together to help keep it functioning normally. For example, the urinary system works closely with other systems of the body, cleaning waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems, and including the kidneys and lower intestines. The respiratory system also works closely with all other systems, providing oxygen for all body parts and removing carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems, including the nose, larynx, trachea, and the lungs. This cooperation allows the body to maintain homeostasis and function effectively.\", \"The human body systems work together through a process where each system interacts and complements the others to maintain overall bodily function and health. For example, the urinary system works in conjunction with the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, and circulatory systems to clean the blood from waste products. Additionally, the respiratory system collaborates with the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems to provide oxygen and remove carbon dioxide. These interactions are crucial for the body's continuous operation and survival.\"]", "time_sec": 18.707, "generation_time_seconds": 18.197, "selection_time_seconds": 0.5055, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 553, 1817, 1849, 28720, 311, 279, 8084, 30201, 315, 279, 2487, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 3871, 504, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 576, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 369, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 504, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 151645], "pred": "The body systems work together by each system contributing to the overall functioning of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The respiratory system provides oxygen for all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2501596239910406, "g_worst_claim": 0.03510835021734238, "g_content": 2.055208360826647, "g_traj_mean": 1.3110431432724}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 553, 65415, 862, 5746, 311, 10306, 22823, 2487, 729, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 41531, 1849, 5707, 23552, 311, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 28160, 12499, 39489, 11, 892, 374, 7565, 369, 279, 30201, 315, 279, 51092, 323, 1008, 5942, 13, 576, 71635, 1849, 34194, 12291, 3871, 504, 3807, 1008, 5942, 11, 2670, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 576, 68297, 323, 51092, 5942, 1824, 7203, 323, 3410, 23759, 1824, 11, 892, 374, 5871, 369, 279, 41531, 323, 4225, 37120, 5942, 311, 729, 10277, 13, 576, 4225, 37120, 1849, 68069, 23552, 323, 36393, 311, 678, 5479, 315, 279, 2487, 11, 892, 374, 7565, 369, 279, 30201, 315, 279, 835, 77638, 323, 22596, 5942, 13, 4220, 5942, 975, 304, 20830, 311, 10306, 279, 2487, 594, 8084, 2820, 323, 729, 13, 151645], "pred": "The body systems work together by coordinating their functions to maintain optimal body function. For example, the respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide, which is essential for the functioning of the muscular and other systems. The urinary system cleans waste products from several other systems, including the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. The skeletal and muscular systems support movement and provide structural support, which is necessary for the respiratory and circulatory systems to function properly. The circulatory system transports oxygen and nutrients to all parts of the body, which is essential for the functioning of the endocrine and nervous systems. These systems work in concert to maintain the body's overall health and function.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7470300721170553, "g_worst_claim": 0.08633915015629359, "g_content": 0.9810318417019315, "g_traj_mean": 0.6671814322471619}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 5942, 304, 279, 3738, 2487, 975, 3786, 311, 1492, 2506, 432, 30201, 14279, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 4278, 15148, 448, 1008, 5942, 315, 279, 2487, 11, 15826, 12291, 3871, 504, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 11, 323, 2670, 279, 80860, 323, 4722, 38308, 1543, 13, 576, 41531, 1849, 1083, 4278, 15148, 448, 678, 1008, 5942, 11, 8241, 23552, 369, 678, 2487, 5479, 323, 17592, 12499, 39489, 504, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 11, 2670, 279, 19142, 11, 326, 658, 23357, 11, 489, 1777, 64, 11, 323, 279, 44174, 13, 1096, 23046, 6147, 279, 2487, 311, 10306, 2114, 535, 10718, 323, 729, 13444, 13, 151645], "pred": "The systems in the human body work together to help keep it functioning normally. For example, the urinary system works closely with other systems of the body, cleaning waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems, and including the kidneys and lower intestines. The respiratory system also works closely with all other systems, providing oxygen for all body parts and removing carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems, including the nose, larynx, trachea, and the lungs. This cooperation allows the body to maintain homeostasis and function effectively.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5447897355664861, "g_worst_claim": 0.2779180109500885, "g_content": 2.1763860983926744, "g_traj_mean": 1.4079302549362183}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 3738, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 1526, 264, 1882, 1380, 1817, 1849, 83161, 323, 1907, 1368, 279, 3800, 311, 10306, 8084, 47031, 729, 323, 2820, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 71635, 1849, 4278, 304, 31446, 448, 279, 68297, 11, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 41531, 11, 323, 4225, 37120, 5942, 311, 4240, 279, 6543, 504, 12291, 3871, 13, 22406, 11, 279, 41531, 1849, 11182, 973, 448, 279, 51092, 11, 58971, 11, 68297, 11, 4225, 37120, 11, 71635, 11, 323, 22596, 5942, 311, 3410, 23552, 323, 4057, 12499, 39489, 13, 4220, 21880, 525, 16587, 369, 279, 2487, 594, 19259, 5666, 323, 19661, 13, 151645], "pred": "The human body systems work together through a process where each system interacts and complements the others to maintain overall bodily function and health. For example, the urinary system works in conjunction with the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, and circulatory systems to clean the blood from waste products. Additionally, the respiratory system collaborates with the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems to provide oxygen and remove carbon dioxide. These interactions are crucial for the body's continuous operation and survival.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8261412267084721, "g_worst_claim": 0.2981101732987624, "g_content": 1.4817219543457032, "g_traj_mean": 0.9063764810562134}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 63.37, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "107", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "The Windward and Leeward Islands are part of the Lesser Antilles of the Caribbean Sea. The Windward Islands are in the southeast and are exposed to the northeast trade winds, hence they receive more rain and are wetter. On the other hand, the Leeward Islands are located in the northwest and are away from the wind, making them drier.", "pred": "The Windward Islands are part of the Lesser Antilles of the Caribbean Sea and are southeastern islands of the Caribbean. They're called the Windward Islands because they're exposed to the wind (\"windward\") of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies). On the other hand, the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands of the Lesser Antilles and are part of the Caribbean Sea. They're called the Leeward Islands because they're away from the wind (\"lee\"). The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands get more rain, are wetter, and are on the side of the mountain closest to the ocean, while the Leeward Islands are the farthest from shore and are drier but still get rain.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The Windward Islands are part of the Lesser Antilles of the Caribbean Sea and are southeastern islands of the Caribbean. They're called the Windward Islands because they're exposed to the wind (\"windward\") of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies). On the other hand, the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands of the Lesser Antilles and are part of the Caribbean Sea. They're called the Leeward Islands because they're away from the wind (\"lee\"). The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands get more rain, are wetter, and are on the side of the mountain closest to the ocean, while the Leeward Islands are the farthest from shore and are drier but still get rain.", "cot": "[\"The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter, being the side of the mountain closest to the ocean. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, though they still receive some rain.\", \"The Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter, and they are the side of the mountain that is closest to the ocean. The Leeward Islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, but they still receive some rain.\", \"Based on the provided passages, the difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward gets more rain, is wetter, and is the side of the mountain that is closest to the ocean. On the other hand, the leeward is the farthest from shore and is drier but still gets rain.\", \"The Windward Islands are part of the Lesser Antilles of the Caribbean Sea and are southeastern islands of the Caribbean. They're called the Windward Islands because they're exposed to the wind (\\\"windward\\\") of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies). On the other hand, the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands of the Lesser Antilles and are part of the Caribbean Sea. They're called the Leeward Islands because they're away from the wind (\\\"lee\\\"). The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands get more rain, are wetter, and are on the side of the mountain closest to the ocean, while the Leeward Islands are the farthest from shore and are drier but still get rain.\"]", "time_sec": 15.94, "generation_time_seconds": 15.2603, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6733, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 1967, 24035, 323, 22087, 1606, 22235, 374, 429, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 5258, 803, 11174, 323, 525, 14401, 465, 11, 1660, 279, 3108, 315, 279, 16301, 18093, 311, 279, 17951, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 279, 3041, 60843, 504, 279, 30184, 323, 525, 294, 7253, 11, 3498, 807, 2058, 5258, 1045, 11174, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter, being the side of the mountain closest to the ocean. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, though they still receive some rain.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6579953421761977, "g_worst_claim": 1.1365769704182942, "g_content": 2.5834615880792793, "g_traj_mean": 1.4703937768936157}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 22087, 1606, 22235, 5258, 803, 11174, 323, 525, 14401, 465, 11, 323, 807, 525, 279, 3108, 315, 279, 16301, 429, 374, 18093, 311, 279, 17951, 13, 576, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 279, 3041, 60843, 504, 279, 30184, 323, 525, 294, 7253, 11, 714, 807, 2058, 5258, 1045, 11174, 13, 151645], "pred": "The Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter, and they are the side of the mountain that is closest to the ocean. The Leeward Islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, but they still receive some rain.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7371882699784778, "g_worst_claim": 1.191333293914795, "g_content": 3.4455692768096924, "g_traj_mean": 1.7259650230407715}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 279, 6672, 1948, 279, 512, 24035, 323, 9956, 1606, 29000, 374, 429, 279, 9956, 1606, 5221, 803, 11174, 11, 374, 14401, 465, 11, 323, 374, 279, 3108, 315, 279, 16301, 429, 374, 18093, 311, 279, 17951, 13, 1913, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 279, 512, 24035, 374, 279, 3041, 60843, 504, 30184, 323, 374, 294, 7253, 714, 2058, 5221, 11174, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the provided passages, the difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward gets more rain, is wetter, and is the side of the mountain that is closest to the ocean. On the other hand, the leeward is the farthest from shore and is drier but still gets rain.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4451267251195565, "g_worst_claim": 0.7122729619344076, "g_content": 2.613144787875089, "g_traj_mean": 1.571792483329773}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 949, 315, 279, 13907, 6755, 30255, 315, 279, 34274, 15029, 323, 525, 82109, 29000, 315, 279, 34274, 13, 2379, 2299, 2598, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 1576, 807, 2299, 14900, 311, 279, 9956, 3489, 19154, 1606, 899, 315, 279, 40829, 6559, 28492, 320, 44707, 1782, 2300, 48101, 568, 1913, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 279, 10200, 30282, 29000, 315, 279, 13907, 6755, 30255, 323, 525, 949, 315, 279, 34274, 15029, 13, 2379, 2299, 2598, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 1576, 807, 2299, 3123, 504, 279, 9956, 3489, 8501, 1827, 576, 6672, 1948, 279, 1967, 24035, 323, 22087, 1606, 22235, 374, 429, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 633, 803, 11174, 11, 525, 14401, 465, 11, 323, 525, 389, 279, 3108, 315, 279, 16301, 18093, 311, 279, 17951, 11, 1393, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 279, 3041, 60843, 504, 30184, 323, 525, 294, 7253, 714, 2058, 633, 11174, 13, 151645], "pred": "The Windward Islands are part of the Lesser Antilles of the Caribbean Sea and are southeastern islands of the Caribbean. They're called the Windward Islands because they're exposed to the wind (\"windward\") of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies). On the other hand, the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands of the Lesser Antilles and are part of the Caribbean Sea. They're called the Leeward Islands because they're away from the wind (\"lee\"). The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands get more rain, are wetter, and are on the side of the mountain closest to the ocean, while the Leeward Islands are the farthest from shore and are drier but still get rain.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.328586449172228, "g_worst_claim": 0.42920671809803357, "g_content": 2.002823153409091, "g_traj_mean": 1.337121605873108}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.51, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "108", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "The Windward Islands are exposed to the wind of the northeast trade winds and are located on the southeastern side of the Caribbean Sea. The Leeward Islands, on the other hand, are located on the northwestern side of the Lesser Antilles and are away from the wind. The windward side receives more rain and is wetter, while the leeward side is drier but still receives some rain.", "pred": "The leeward islands are the northwestern islands of the Lesser Antilles, while the windward islands are southeastern islands of the Caribbean. Windward islands are exposed to the wind (windward) of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies), and the leeward islands are the farthest from shore and are drier but still get rain. The windward islands get more rain, are wetter, and are the side of the mountain that is closest to the ocean.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The leeward islands are the northwestern islands of the Lesser Antilles, while the windward islands are southeastern islands of the Caribbean. Windward islands are exposed to the wind (windward) of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies), and the leeward islands are the farthest from shore and are drier but still get rain. The windward islands get more rain, are wetter, and are the side of the mountain that is closest to the ocean.", "cot": "[\"The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter, being the side of the mountain closest to the ocean. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, though they still receive some rain.\", \"The Windward Islands are exposed to the wind and get more rain, making them wetter and closer to the ocean. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier, though they still receive some rainfall.\", \"The leeward islands are the northwestern islands of the Lesser Antilles, while the windward islands are southeastern islands of the Caribbean. Windward islands are exposed to the wind (windward) of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies), and the leeward islands are the farthest from shore and are drier but still get rain. The windward islands get more rain, are wetter, and are the side of the mountain that is closest to the ocean.\", \"The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands are closer to the wind and therefore get more rain, being wetter. On the other hand, the Leeward Islands are farther from the shore and thus drier but still receive some rain.\"]", "time_sec": 13.38, "generation_time_seconds": 12.6025, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7733, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 1967, 24035, 323, 22087, 1606, 22235, 374, 429, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 5258, 803, 11174, 323, 525, 14401, 465, 11, 1660, 279, 3108, 315, 279, 16301, 18093, 311, 279, 17951, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 279, 3041, 60843, 504, 279, 30184, 323, 525, 294, 7253, 11, 3498, 807, 2058, 5258, 1045, 11174, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter, being the side of the mountain closest to the ocean. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, though they still receive some rain.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7065696667283128, "g_worst_claim": 1.1873939832051594, "g_content": 2.5939639698375356, "g_traj_mean": 1.5189462900161743}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 14900, 311, 279, 9956, 323, 633, 803, 11174, 11, 3259, 1105, 14401, 465, 323, 12128, 311, 279, 17951, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 3123, 504, 279, 9956, 323, 525, 294, 7253, 11, 3498, 807, 2058, 5258, 1045, 52858, 13, 151645], "pred": "The Windward Islands are exposed to the wind and get more rain, making them wetter and closer to the ocean. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier, though they still receive some rainfall.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5601446628570557, "g_worst_claim": 0.5800091879708427, "g_content": 3.0396156311035156, "g_traj_mean": 1.4989851713180542}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 512, 24035, 29000, 525, 279, 10200, 30282, 29000, 315, 279, 13907, 6755, 30255, 11, 1393, 279, 9956, 1606, 29000, 525, 82109, 29000, 315, 279, 34274, 13, 22087, 1606, 29000, 525, 14900, 311, 279, 9956, 320, 19154, 1606, 8, 315, 279, 40829, 6559, 28492, 320, 44707, 1782, 2300, 48101, 701, 323, 279, 512, 24035, 29000, 525, 279, 3041, 60843, 504, 30184, 323, 525, 294, 7253, 714, 2058, 633, 11174, 13, 576, 9956, 1606, 29000, 633, 803, 11174, 11, 525, 14401, 465, 11, 323, 525, 279, 3108, 315, 279, 16301, 429, 374, 18093, 311, 279, 17951, 13, 151645], "pred": "The leeward islands are the northwestern islands of the Lesser Antilles, while the windward islands are southeastern islands of the Caribbean. Windward islands are exposed to the wind (windward) of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies), and the leeward islands are the farthest from shore and are drier but still get rain. The windward islands get more rain, are wetter, and are the side of the mountain that is closest to the ocean.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5127974773703812, "g_worst_claim": 0.7488542795181274, "g_content": 2.425734165736607, "g_traj_mean": 1.647377610206604}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 1967, 24035, 323, 22087, 1606, 22235, 374, 429, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 12128, 311, 279, 9956, 323, 8916, 633, 803, 11174, 11, 1660, 14401, 465, 13, 1913, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 42626, 504, 279, 30184, 323, 8450, 294, 7253, 714, 2058, 5258, 1045, 11174, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands are closer to the wind and therefore get more rain, being wetter. On the other hand, the Leeward Islands are farther from the shore and thus drier but still receive some rain.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1559296992787145, "g_worst_claim": 0.9637235005696615, "g_content": 1.7842768618935032, "g_traj_mean": 1.1277897357940674}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 63.16, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "109", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the Windward Islands are located in the southeastern part of the Caribbean Sea and are exposed to the wind (\"windward\") of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies), while the Leeward Islands are located in the northwestern part of the Lesser Antilles and are away from the wind (\"lee\"). The main difference between them is their exposure to the wind and the resulting climate. The Windward Islands get more rain and are wetter due to their exposure to the wind, while the Leeward Islands are drier but still get rain.", "pred": "The difference between the Leeward Islands and the Windward Islands lies in their exposure to the trade winds. The Windward Islands are exposed to the northeast trade winds, which bring more rain and humidity to these islands. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are located further away from the wind, resulting in less rainfall and generally drier conditions. Despite being exposed to the trade winds, the Leeward Islands still receive some precipitation, but it is less than what the Windward Islands experience.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The difference between the Leeward Islands and the Windward Islands lies in their exposure to the trade winds. The Windward Islands are exposed to the northeast trade winds, which bring more rain and humidity to these islands. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are located further away from the wind, resulting in less rainfall and generally drier conditions. Despite being exposed to the trade winds, the Leeward Islands still receive some precipitation, but it is less than what the Windward Islands experience.", "cot": "[\"The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter, being the side of the mountain closest to the ocean. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, though they still receive some rain.\", \"The difference between the leeward and windward islands, as mentioned in the passages, is that the windward islands receive more rain and are wetter due to being exposed to the wind of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies). In contrast, the leeward islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, but they still receive some rain.\", \"The difference between the Leeward Islands and the Windward Islands lies in their exposure to the trade winds. The Windward Islands are exposed to the northeast trade winds, which bring more rain and humidity to these islands. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are located further away from the wind, resulting in less rainfall and generally drier conditions. Despite being exposed to the trade winds, the Leeward Islands still receive some precipitation, but it is less than what the Windward Islands experience.\", \"The Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands of the Lesser Antilles, while the Windward Islands are southeastern islands. The Windward Islands are exposed to the wind, receiving more rain and being wetter, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind, being drier but still receiving some rain.\"]", "time_sec": 14.665, "generation_time_seconds": 13.9375, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7226, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 1967, 24035, 323, 22087, 1606, 22235, 374, 429, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 5258, 803, 11174, 323, 525, 14401, 465, 11, 1660, 279, 3108, 315, 279, 16301, 18093, 311, 279, 17951, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 279, 3041, 60843, 504, 279, 30184, 323, 525, 294, 7253, 11, 3498, 807, 2058, 5258, 1045, 11174, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter, being the side of the mountain closest to the ocean. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, though they still receive some rain.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6675271042239614, "g_worst_claim": 1.1153780619303386, "g_content": 2.6147627397017046, "g_traj_mean": 1.474582552909851}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 512, 24035, 323, 9956, 1606, 29000, 11, 438, 9733, 304, 279, 46769, 11, 374, 429, 279, 9956, 1606, 29000, 5258, 803, 11174, 323, 525, 14401, 465, 4152, 311, 1660, 14900, 311, 279, 9956, 315, 279, 40829, 6559, 28492, 320, 44707, 1782, 2300, 48101, 568, 758, 12872, 11, 279, 512, 24035, 29000, 525, 279, 3041, 60843, 504, 279, 30184, 323, 525, 294, 7253, 11, 714, 807, 2058, 5258, 1045, 11174, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between the leeward and windward islands, as mentioned in the passages, is that the windward islands receive more rain and are wetter due to being exposed to the wind of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies). In contrast, the leeward islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, but they still receive some rain.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.077130192925254, "g_worst_claim": 0.30699682235717773, "g_content": 1.4811949157714843, "g_traj_mean": 1.19124174118042}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 323, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 15448, 304, 862, 14338, 311, 279, 6559, 28492, 13, 576, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 14900, 311, 279, 40829, 6559, 28492, 11, 892, 4446, 803, 11174, 323, 37093, 311, 1493, 29000, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 7407, 4623, 3123, 504, 279, 9956, 11, 12942, 304, 2686, 52858, 323, 8789, 294, 7253, 4682, 13, 17715, 1660, 14900, 311, 279, 6559, 28492, 11, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 2058, 5258, 1045, 59950, 11, 714, 432, 374, 2686, 1091, 1128, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 3139, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between the Leeward Islands and the Windward Islands lies in their exposure to the trade winds. The Windward Islands are exposed to the northeast trade winds, which bring more rain and humidity to these islands. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are located further away from the wind, resulting in less rainfall and generally drier conditions. Despite being exposed to the trade winds, the Leeward Islands still receive some precipitation, but it is less than what the Windward Islands experience.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.5472576458066228, "g_worst_claim": 0.07833914160728454, "g_content": 0.9216345853583757, "g_traj_mean": 0.5348724126815796}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 279, 10200, 30282, 29000, 315, 279, 13907, 6755, 30255, 11, 1393, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 82109, 29000, 13, 576, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 14900, 311, 279, 9956, 11, 12308, 803, 11174, 323, 1660, 14401, 465, 11, 1393, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 3123, 504, 279, 9956, 11, 1660, 294, 7253, 714, 2058, 12308, 1045, 11174, 13, 151645], "pred": "The Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands of the Lesser Antilles, while the Windward Islands are southeastern islands. The Windward Islands are exposed to the wind, receiving more rain and being wetter, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind, being drier but still receiving some rain.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1466917100578848, "g_worst_claim": 0.4391963698647239, "g_content": 2.0792404810587564, "g_traj_mean": 1.1445742845535278}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "111", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is their exposure to the wind and precipitation. The Windward Islands are exposed to the northeasterly trade winds and receive more rainfall, making them wetter and more humid, while the Leeward Islands are located on the leeward side of the mountains and receive less rainfall, making them drier. Therefore, the answer to the question is:\n\nThe Windward Islands are wetter and more humid due to their exposure to the northeasterly trade winds, while the Leeward Islands are drier and receive less rainfall.", "pred": "The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter, being the side of the mountain closest to the ocean. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, though they still receive some rain.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter, being the side of the mountain closest to the ocean. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, though they still receive some rain.", "cot": "[\"The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter, being the side of the mountain closest to the ocean. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, though they still receive some rain.\", \"The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter because they are closer to the wind (\\\"windward\\\") of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies), whereas the Leeward Islands, which are further from the wind (\\\"lee\\\"), receive less rain and are drier.\", \"The difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands get more rain, are wetter, and are the side of the mountain that is closest to the ocean. On the other hand, the leeward islands are the farthest from shore and are drier but still get rain.\", \"The difference between the leeward and windward islands, based on the provided passages, is that the windward islands receive more rain, are wetter, and are the side of the mountain closest to the ocean. The leeward islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier.\"]", "time_sec": 12.827, "generation_time_seconds": 12.0254, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7933, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 1967, 24035, 323, 22087, 1606, 22235, 374, 429, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 5258, 803, 11174, 323, 525, 14401, 465, 11, 1660, 279, 3108, 315, 279, 16301, 18093, 311, 279, 17951, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 279, 3041, 60843, 504, 279, 30184, 323, 525, 294, 7253, 11, 3498, 807, 2058, 5258, 1045, 11174, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter, being the side of the mountain closest to the ocean. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, though they still receive some rain.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.644650332210384, "g_worst_claim": 1.0576569239298503, "g_content": 2.501483743840998, "g_traj_mean": 1.4467947483062744}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 1967, 24035, 323, 22087, 1606, 22235, 374, 429, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 5258, 803, 11174, 323, 525, 14401, 465, 1576, 807, 525, 12128, 311, 279, 9956, 3489, 19154, 1606, 899, 315, 279, 40829, 6559, 28492, 320, 44707, 1782, 2300, 48101, 701, 19853, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 11, 892, 525, 4623, 504, 279, 9956, 3489, 8501, 3975, 5258, 2686, 11174, 323, 525, 294, 7253, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter because they are closer to the wind (\"windward\") of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies), whereas the Leeward Islands, which are further from the wind (\"lee\"), receive less rain and are drier.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6358352286016775, "g_worst_claim": -0.02246650494635105, "g_content": 1.1335826542066492, "g_traj_mean": 1.0931427478790283}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 512, 24035, 323, 9956, 1606, 29000, 374, 429, 279, 9956, 1606, 29000, 633, 803, 11174, 11, 525, 14401, 465, 11, 323, 525, 279, 3108, 315, 279, 16301, 429, 374, 18093, 311, 279, 17951, 13, 1913, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 279, 512, 24035, 29000, 525, 279, 3041, 60843, 504, 30184, 323, 525, 294, 7253, 714, 2058, 633, 11174, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands get more rain, are wetter, and are the side of the mountain that is closest to the ocean. On the other hand, the leeward islands are the farthest from shore and are drier but still get rain.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6106982893214787, "g_worst_claim": 1.0221914291381835, "g_content": 2.4303805033365884, "g_traj_mean": 1.5295213460922241}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 512, 24035, 323, 9956, 1606, 29000, 11, 3118, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 374, 429, 279, 9956, 1606, 29000, 5258, 803, 11174, 11, 525, 14401, 465, 11, 323, 525, 279, 3108, 315, 279, 16301, 18093, 311, 279, 17951, 13, 576, 512, 24035, 29000, 525, 279, 3041, 60843, 504, 279, 30184, 323, 525, 294, 7253, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between the leeward and windward islands, based on the provided passages, is that the windward islands receive more rain, are wetter, and are the side of the mountain closest to the ocean. The leeward islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9971134040843357, "g_worst_claim": -0.005481548607349396, "g_content": 2.1158044815063475, "g_traj_mean": 1.1368738412857056}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 34.09, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "112", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between the Windward Islands and the Leeward Islands is their exposure to the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies). The Windward Islands are exposed to the wind and are therefore wetter and receive more rainfall, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier, but still receive some rainfall. Additionally, the Windward Islands are located southeast of the Caribbean Sea, while the Leeward Islands are located northwest of the Caribbean Sea.", "pred": "The difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands are exposed to the wind, receive more rain, and are the side of the mountain closest to the ocean, while the leeward islands are the farthest from shore and receive less rain.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands are exposed to the wind, receive more rain, and are the side of the mountain closest to the ocean, while the leeward islands are the farthest from shore and receive less rain.", "cot": "[\"The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter, being the side of the mountain closest to the ocean. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, though they still receive some rain.\", \"The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands, as described in the passages, is that the Windward Islands are the southeastern islands of the Caribbean that are exposed to the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies), while the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands of the Lesser Antilles that are away from the wind (\\\"lee\\\"). Specifically, the Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter because they are closer to the ocean, whereas the Leeward Islands, being farther from the shore and still getting some rain, are drier.\", \"The difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands are exposed to the wind, receive more rain, and are the side of the mountain closest to the ocean, while the leeward islands are the farthest from shore and receive less rain.\", \"The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands, while the Windward Islands are the southeastern islands. The Leeward Islands are away from the wind (\\\"lee\\\"), while the Windward Islands are exposed to the wind (\\\"windward\\\") of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies).\"]", "time_sec": 14.438, "generation_time_seconds": 13.8449, "selection_time_seconds": 0.5835, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 1967, 24035, 323, 22087, 1606, 22235, 374, 429, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 5258, 803, 11174, 323, 525, 14401, 465, 11, 1660, 279, 3108, 315, 279, 16301, 18093, 311, 279, 17951, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 279, 3041, 60843, 504, 279, 30184, 323, 525, 294, 7253, 11, 3498, 807, 2058, 5258, 1045, 11174, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter, being the side of the mountain closest to the ocean. In contrast, the Leeward Islands are the farthest from the shore and are drier, though they still receive some rain.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6537801651727584, "g_worst_claim": 1.082337220509847, "g_content": 2.5725955963134766, "g_traj_mean": 1.4549360275268555}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 1967, 24035, 323, 22087, 1606, 22235, 11, 438, 7481, 304, 279, 46769, 11, 374, 429, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 279, 82109, 29000, 315, 279, 34274, 429, 525, 14900, 311, 279, 40829, 6559, 28492, 320, 44707, 1782, 2300, 48101, 701, 1393, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 279, 10200, 30282, 29000, 315, 279, 13907, 6755, 30255, 429, 525, 3123, 504, 279, 9956, 3489, 8501, 1827, 44763, 11, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 5258, 803, 11174, 323, 525, 14401, 465, 1576, 807, 525, 12128, 311, 279, 17951, 11, 19853, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 11, 1660, 42626, 504, 279, 30184, 323, 2058, 3709, 1045, 11174, 11, 525, 294, 7253, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands, as described in the passages, is that the Windward Islands are the southeastern islands of the Caribbean that are exposed to the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies), while the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands of the Lesser Antilles that are away from the wind (\"lee\"). Specifically, the Windward Islands receive more rain and are wetter because they are closer to the ocean, whereas the Leeward Islands, being farther from the shore and still getting some rain, are drier.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.054473964474068, "g_worst_claim": 0.5109012921651205, "g_content": 2.0821386337280274, "g_traj_mean": 1.1658939123153687}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 512, 24035, 323, 9956, 1606, 29000, 374, 429, 279, 9956, 1606, 29000, 525, 14900, 311, 279, 9956, 11, 5258, 803, 11174, 11, 323, 525, 279, 3108, 315, 279, 16301, 18093, 311, 279, 17951, 11, 1393, 279, 512, 24035, 29000, 525, 279, 3041, 60843, 504, 30184, 323, 5258, 2686, 11174, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between the leeward and windward islands is that the windward islands are exposed to the wind, receive more rain, and are the side of the mountain closest to the ocean, while the leeward islands are the farthest from shore and receive less rain.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5825109228943335, "g_worst_claim": 0.6451828263022683, "g_content": 2.463011968703497, "g_traj_mean": 1.2006319761276245}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 1967, 24035, 323, 22087, 1606, 22235, 374, 429, 279, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 279, 10200, 30282, 29000, 11, 1393, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 279, 82109, 29000, 13, 576, 1967, 24035, 22235, 525, 3123, 504, 279, 9956, 3489, 8501, 3975, 1393, 279, 22087, 1606, 22235, 525, 14900, 311, 279, 9956, 3489, 19154, 1606, 899, 315, 279, 40829, 6559, 28492, 320, 44707, 1782, 2300, 48101, 568, 151645], "pred": "The difference between the Leeward and Windward Islands is that the Leeward Islands are the northwestern islands, while the Windward Islands are the southeastern islands. The Leeward Islands are away from the wind (\"lee\"), while the Windward Islands are exposed to the wind (\"windward\") of the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies).", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0327037507837469, "g_worst_claim": -0.14705076217651367, "g_content": 1.310338897705078, "g_traj_mean": 1.0959844589233398}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "113", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "gt": "To transfer water shares, the seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of it. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer. After these steps, a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner. If the original certificate is lost, an additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, which is furnished by the Company and must be signed and notarized.", "pred": "Water shares are transferred by the seller returning the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and signing the back of the certificate.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Water shares are transferred by the seller returning the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and signing the back of the certificate.", "cot": "[\"Water shares can be transferred by returning the Water Stock Certificate assigned to the seller and signing the back of the certificate. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer, and a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\", \"Water shares are transferred by the seller returning the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and signing the back of the certificate.\", \"Water shares are transferred through the following steps:\\n1. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate.\\n2. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership.\\n3. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\\n4. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\", \"A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer. An additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form.\"]", "time_sec": 11.951, "generation_time_seconds": 11.0938, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8522, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28253, 13248, 646, 387, 22409, 553, 13451, 279, 9959, 12648, 31402, 12607, 311, 279, 22856, 323, 15971, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 15748, 13, 576, 501, 6372, 315, 279, 3343, 1969, 3410, 11064, 315, 15278, 13, 362, 11060, 315, 400, 22, 20, 13, 15, 15, 1969, 387, 7171, 311, 1882, 279, 8317, 11, 323, 264, 501, 9959, 12648, 31402, 686, 387, 10897, 311, 279, 501, 6372, 315, 3255, 13, 151645], "pred": "Water shares can be transferred by returning the Water Stock Certificate assigned to the seller and signing the back of the certificate. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer, and a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.78753976422067, "g_worst_claim": 1.0478707551956177, "g_content": 2.6232816423688616, "g_traj_mean": 1.8671308755874634}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28253, 13248, 525, 22409, 553, 279, 22856, 13451, 279, 9959, 12648, 31402, 429, 572, 12607, 311, 1105, 323, 15971, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 15748, 13, 151645], "pred": "Water shares are transferred by the seller returning the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and signing the back of the certificate.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.6405294799804686, "g_worst_claim": 2.6405294799804686, "g_content": 4.159631093343099, "g_traj_mean": 2.4903945922851562}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28253, 13248, 525, 22409, 1526, 279, 2701, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 576, 22856, 1969, 470, 279, 9959, 12648, 31402, 429, 572, 12607, 311, 1105, 323, 1841, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 15748, 624, 17, 13, 576, 501, 6372, 315, 279, 3343, 1969, 3410,