{"id": "115", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "gt": "Based on the given passages, water shares can be transferred through the issuance of a new Water Stock Certificate to the new owner of record after paying a fee of $75.00. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate assigned to them and sign the back of the certificate. The new owner must provide proof of ownership before a transfer can be processed. Additionally, an additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form, which is furnished by the company and must be signed and notarized.", "pred": "Water shares can be transferred by returning the Water Stock Certificate assigned to the seller and providing proof of ownership. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer, and a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record. Additionally, an additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Water shares can be transferred by returning the Water Stock Certificate assigned to the seller and providing proof of ownership. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer, and a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record. Additionally, an additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form.", "cot": "[\"Water shares can be transferred by returning the Water Stock Certificate assigned to the seller and signing the back of the certificate. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer, and a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\", \"A Water Stock Certificate transfer can be initiated by the seller returning the Water Stock Certificate that was assigned to them and signing the back of the certificate.\", \"To trans