{"id": "117", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "gt": "Based on the given passages, water shares can be transferred as follows:\n\n1. The current owner of the Water Stock Certificate must return the original certificate to the company and sign the back of the certificate.\n2. The new owner must provide proof of ownership and pay a fee of $75.00 to process the transfer.\n3. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\n\nPlease note that the passages only refer to the transfer of Water Stock Certificates and do not provide information on other types of water rights or transfers. Therefore, if the question is asking about other types of water rights or transfers, I would be unable to answer based on the given passages.", "pred": "A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.", "cot": "[\"Water shares can be transferred by returning the Water Stock Certificate assigned to the seller and signing the back of the certificate. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer, and a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.\", \"A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process a Water Stock Certificate transfer.\", \"Water shares can be transferred by returning the Water Stock Certificate assigned to the seller and signing the back of the certificate. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership, and a fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer. A new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record. An additional fee of $75.00 must be paid when filing a Lost Certificate Affidavit form.\", \"Water shares can be transferred through a process that involves several steps. The 