{"id": "120", "question": "teresa name meaning", "gt": "The name Teresa is of Greek origin and means \"Reap; from Therasia\" or \"Harvester\". It is also a Spanish and Italian name and is associated with two popular saints, Teresa of Avila and Therese of Lisieux. The name Theresa is a variation of Teresa and also means \"Reaper; from Therasia\". The etymology of the name is uncertain, but it is thought to come from the Greek words \"therizein\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester\" or \"theros\" meaning \"summer\".", "pred": "Teresa has different meanings in various languages and cultures based on the given passages. In Greek, the name Teresa means \"Reap; from Therasia,\" while in Italian and Spanish, it means \"Harvester.\" Additionally, in Spanish, Teresa can also refer to two popular saints, \"Teresa of Avila\" and \"Therese of Lisieux.\"", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Teresa has different meanings in various languages and cultures based on the given passages. In Greek, the name Teresa means \"Reap; from Therasia,\" while in Italian and Spanish, it means \"Harvester.\" Additionally, in Spanish, Teresa can also refer to two popular saints, \"Teresa of Avila\" and \"Therese of Lisieux.\"", "cot": "[\"The name Teresa has different meanings depending on the language:\\n\\n- In Greek, the name Teresa means \\\"Reap; from Therasia.\\\"\\n- In American, the name Teresa means \\\"Reap; from Therasia.\\\"\\n- In Italian, the name Teresa means \\\"Harvester.\\\"\\n- In Spanish, the name Teresa means \\\"Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux'.\\\"\\n\\nThe name Theresa is also a Greek baby name, and in Greek, the meaning of the name Theresa is \\\"Reaper; from Therasia.\\\"\", \"Teresa has different meanings in various languages and cultures based on the given passages. In Greek, the name Teresa means \\\"Reap; from Therasia,\\\" while in Italian and Spanish, it means \\\"Harvester.\\\" Additionally, in Spanish, Teresa can also refer to two popular saints, \\\"Teresa of Avila\\\" and \\\"Therese of Lisieux.\\\"\", \"Based on the provided passages, the name \\\"Teresa\\\" has different meanings in various cultures:\\n\\n- In Greek, the name Teresa is derived from Therasia and means \\\"Reap; from Therasia.\\\"\\n- In Italian, Teresa is a name meaning \\\"Harvester.\\\"\\n- In Spanish and Portuguese, Teresa represents two popular saints, Teresa of Avila and Therese of Lisieux.\\n- In Greek, Theresa is derived from Therasia and means \\\"Reaper; from Therasia.\\\"\\n\\nThus, the name Teresa has diverse cultural significances, primarily revolving around the themes of harvesting and saints in Spanish and Portuguese cultures, and \\\"reap\\\" in Greek and Italian cultures.\", \"The name Teresa, with meanings including \\\"Harvester\\\" in Italian and \\\"Reaper\\\" in Greek, reflects its origins in a period when agricultural practices were central to society.\"]", "time_sec": 16.924, "generation_time_seconds": 16.0626, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8521, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 829, 63440, 702, 2155, 49700, 11649, 389, 279, 4128, 1447, 12, 758, 17860, 11, 279, 829, 63440, 3363, 330, 693, 391, 26, 504, 663, 9247, 685, 10040, 12, 758, 3693, 11, 279, 829, 63440, 3363, 330, 693, 391, 26, 504, 663, 9247, 685, 10040, 12, 758, 14811, 11, 279, 829, 63440, 3363, 330, 26490, 82738, 10040, 12, 758, 15154, 11, 279, 829, 63440, 3363, 330, 675, 315, 1378, 5411, 67120, 364, 51, 37586, 315, 7519, 10524, 6, 323, 364, 1001, 261, 2367, 315, 43072, 52719, 6, 2217, 785, 829, 42712, 374, 1083, 264, 17860, 8770, 829, 11, 323, 304, 17860, 11, 279, 7290, 315, 279, 829, 42712, 374, 330, 693, 3191, 26, 504, 663, 9247, 685, 1189, 151645], "pred": "The name Teresa has different meanings depending on the language:\n\n- In Greek, the name Teresa means \"Reap; from Therasia.\"\n- In American, the name Teresa means \"Reap; from Therasia.\"\n- In Italian, the name Teresa means \"Harvester.\"\n- In Spanish, the name Teresa means \"Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux'.\"\n\nThe name Theresa is also a Greek baby name, and in Greek, the meaning of the name Theresa is \"Reaper; from Therasia.\"", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.682457909412896, "g_worst_claim": 0.7003456950187683, "g_content": 2.151471274239676, "g_traj_mean": 1.5667299032211304}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [51, 37586, 702, 2155, 49700, 304, 5257, 15459, 323, 26735, 3118, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 13, 758, 17860, 11, 279, 829, 63440, 3363, 330, 693, 391, 26, 504, 663, 9247, 685, 1335, 1393, 304, 14811, 323, 15154, 11, 432, 3363, 330, 26490, 82738, 1189, 22406, 11, 304, 15154, 11, 63440, 646, 1083, 8300, 311, 1378, 5411, 67120, 11, 330, 51, 37586, 315, 7519, 10524, 1, 323, 330, 1001, 261, 2367, 315, 43072, 52719, 1189, 151645], "pred": "Teresa has different meanings in various languages and cultures based on the given passages. In Greek, the name Teresa means \"Reap; from Therasia,\" while in Italian and Spanish, it means \"Harvester.\" Additionally, in Spanish, Teresa can also refer to two popular saints, \"Teresa of Avila\" and \"Therese of Lisieux.\"", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7697916195448802, "g_worst_claim": 0.7937618494033813, "g_content": 2.0514183044433594, "g_traj_mean": 1.5738543272018433}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 279, 829, 330, 51, 37586, 1, 702, 2155, 49700, 304, 5257, 26735, 1447, 12, 758, 17860, 11, 279, 829, 63440, 374, 14257, 504, 663, 9247, 685, 323, 3363, 330, 693, 391, 26, 504, 663, 9247, 685, 10040, 12, 758, 14811, 11, 63440, 374, 264, 829, 7290, 330, 26490, 82738, 10040, 12, 758, 15154, 323, 42188, 11, 63440, 10868, 1378, 5411, 67120, 11, 63440, 315, 7519, 10524, 323, 22450, 2367, 315, 43072, 52719, 624, 12, 758, 17860, 11, 42712, 374, 