{"id": "123", "question": "teresa name meaning", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the meaning of the name Teresa is:\n\n* Reap; from Therasia (Greek)\n* Reaper; from Therasia (American)\n* Harvester (Italian)\n* Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux' (Spanish)\n\nIt is also mentioned that the name Teresa is a Greek baby name, an American baby name, an Italian baby name, and a Spanish baby name.\n\nTherefore, the meaning of the name Teresa can vary depending on the culture and language, but it generally means \"reaper\" or \"harvester\", and is also associated with the names of two popular saints.", "pred": "In Greek, the name Theresa means \"Reaper; from Therasia,\" and in Italian, it means \"Harvester.\"", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "In Greek, the name Theresa means \"Reaper; from Therasia,\" and in Italian, it means \"Harvester.\"", "cot": "[\"The name Teresa has different meanings depending on the language:\\n\\n- In Greek, the name Teresa means \\\"Reap; from Therasia.\\\"\\n- In American, the name Teresa means \\\"Reap; from Therasia.\\\"\\n- In Italian, the name Teresa means \\\"Harvester.\\\"\\n- In Spanish, the name Teresa means \\\"Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux'.\\\"\\n\\nThe name Theresa is also a Greek baby name, and in Greek, the meaning of the name Theresa is \\\"Reaper; from Therasia.\\\"\", \"Reap; from Therasia in Greek, Harvester in Italian, Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux' in Spanish\", \"In Greek, the name Theresa means \\\"Reaper; from Therasia,\\\" and in Italian, it means \\\"Harvester.\\\"\", \"The name Teresa is derived from the Greek word \\\"therizein,\\\" meaning \\\"to harvest\\\" or \\\"harvester.\\\"\"]", "time_sec": 12.46, "generation_time_seconds": 11.5818, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8715, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 829, 63440, 702, 2155, 49700, 11649, 389, 279, 4128, 1447, 12, 758, 17860, 11, 279, 829, 63440, 3363, 330, 693, 391, 26, 504, 663, 9247, 685, 10040, 12, 758, 3693, 11, 279, 829, 63440, 3363, 330, 693, 391, 26, 504, 663, 9247, 685, 10040, 12, 758, 14811, 11, 279, 829, 63440, 3363, 330, 26490, 82738, 10040, 12, 758, 15154, 11, 279, 829, 63440, 3363, 330, 675, 315, 1378, 5411, 67120, 364, 51, 37586, 315, 7519, 10524, 6, 323, 364, 1001, 261, 2367, 315, 43072, 52719, 6, 2217, 785, 829, 42712, 374, 1083, 264, 17860, 8770, 829, 11, 323, 304, 17860, 11, 279, 7290, 315, 279, 829, 42712, 374, 330, 693, 3191, 26, 504, 663, 9247, 685, 1189, 151645], "pred": "The name Teresa has different meanings depending on the language:\n\n- In Greek, the name Teresa means \"Reap; from Therasia.\"\n- In American, the name Teresa means \"Reap; from Therasia.\"\n- In Italian, the name Teresa means \"Harvester.\"\n- In Spanish, the name Teresa means \"Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux'.\"\n\nThe name Theresa is also a Greek baby name, and in Greek, the meaning of the name Theresa is \"Reaper; from Therasia.\"", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6982224583795922, "g_worst_claim": 0.6235523819923401, "g_content": 2.1878963652111234, "g_traj_mean": 1.5702135562896729}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [693, 391, 26, 504, 663, 9247, 685, 304, 17860, 11, 5227, 82738, 304, 14811, 11, 3988, 315, 1378, 5411, 67120, 364, 51, 37586, 315, 7519, 10524, 6, 323, 364, 1001, 261, 2367, 315, 43072, 52719, 6, 304, 15154, 151645], "pred": "Reap; from Therasia in Greek, Harvester in Italian, Name of two popular saints 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux' in Spanish", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 3.7922479491302936, "g_worst_claim": 2.1116590085236924, "g_content": 4.660099347432454, "g_traj_mean": 3.0317225456237793}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [641, 17860, 11, 279, 829, 42712, 3363, 330, 693, 3191, 26, 504, 663, 9247, 685, 1335, 323, 304, 14811, 11, 432, 3363, 330, 26490, 82738, 1189, 151645], "pred": "In Greek, the name Theresa means \"Reaper; from Therasia,\" and in Italian, it means \"Harvester.\"", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.2598996074111373, "g_worst_claim": 1.1743000348409016, "g_content": 3.1159658432006836, "g_traj_mean": 2.7155916690826416}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 829, 63440, 374, 14257, 504, 279, 17860, 3409, 330, 696, 551, 258, 1335, 7290, 330, 983, 23429, 1, 476, 330, 12982, 82738, 1189, 151645], "pred": "The name Teresa is derived from the Greek word \"therizein,\" meaning \"to harvest\" or \"harvester.\"", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4650761286417644, "g_worst_claim": 1.4650761286417644, "g_content": 2.2716202206081815, "g_traj_mean": 1.412611722946167}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 22.86, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "124", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "To build a lean-to shed, start by preparing the site with a 4\" layer of compacted gravel. Cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4\" and set and level them according to the shed building plans. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4\" and six joists at 44 3/4\". Assemble the floor and place it on the skids as indicated in the floor framing section of the plans. Check for squareness and anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles. Cut two more 4 x 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids and, when the frame is square, toenail the floor joists to the skids. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. The size of the shed can be adjusted as needed.", "pred": "Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4x4 skids to the necessary lengths (as specified in the passages) and set them on the gravel. Following this, cut two 2x6 rim joists and six joists to the correct dimensions and assemble the floor on the skids, ensuring it is square. Finally, anchor the frame to the skids with joist clip angles. These steps ensure the shed has a solid, level foundation.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4x4 skids to the necessary lengths (as specified in the passages) and set them on the gravel. Following this, cut two 2x6 rim joists and six joists to the correct dimensions and assemble the floor on the skids, ensuring it is square. Finally, anchor the frame to the skids with joist clip angles. These steps ensure the shed has a solid, level foundation.", "cot": "[\"Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches and set them on the gravel, ensuring they are level. Then, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, checking for square, and then secure the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\", \"To build a lean-to shed, you need to follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Prepare the site with a 4\\\" layer of compacted gravel.\\n2. Cut two 4 x 4 skids at 70 2/4\\\".\\n3. Set and level the skids following the shed building plans.\\n4. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4\\\" and six joists at 44 3/4\\\".\\n5. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\\n6. Check for square and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\\n\\nFor the walls, the process is different:\\n\\n1. Cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids.\\n2. Position the frame on the skids, and when square, toenail the floor joists to the skids.\\n3. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\\n4. Construct the walls separately and then raise them onto the frame.\\n\\nThe shed dimensions are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, but you can easily expand its dimensions in increments of 2 or 4 feet.\", \"Based on the given passages, the steps for building a lean-to shed include:\\n\\n1. **Site Preparation and Skids**: Prepare the site with a 4\\\" layer of compacted gravel. Cut the two 4 x 4 skids to the required length (70 2/4\\\" as mentioned in passage 1). Set and level these skids.\\n\\n2. **Floor Framing**: Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4 \\\" and six joists at 44 3/4\\\". Assemble the floor and place it on the skids. Check for square and anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\\n\\n3. **Wall Construction**: The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\\n\\n4. **Floor Joists and Flooring**: Cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids. Position the frame on the skids and toenail the floor joists to the skids. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\\n\\nThese steps ensure a stable and properly constructed lean-to shed.\", \"Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4x4 skids to the necessary lengths (as specified in the passages) and set them on the gravel. Following this, cut two 2x6 rim joists and six joists to the correct dimensions and assemble the floor on the skids, ensuring it is square. Finally, anchor the frame to the skids with joist clip angles. These steps ensure the shed has a solid, level foundation.\"]", "time_sec": 29.884, "generation_time_seconds": 28.9632, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9147, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [30133, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 13, 5512, 11, 10549, 279, 2747, 553, 34644, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 13, 9295, 11, 3931, 1378, 220, 19, 856, 220, 19, 1901, 3365, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 738, 1105, 389, 279, 41523, 11, 22573, 807, 525, 2188, 13, 5005, 11, 3931, 1378, 220, 17, 856, 220, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 323, 1992, 432, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 13295, 369, 9334, 11, 323, 1221, 9767, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 13, 151645], "pred": "Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4 x 4 