686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 13, 5512, 11, 10549, 279, 2747, 553, 34644, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 13, 9295, 11, 3931, 1378, 220, 19, 87, 19, 1901, 3365, 311, 279, 5871, 28316, 320, 300, 5189, 304, 279, 46769, 8, 323, 738, 1105, 389, 279, 41523, 13, 22713, 419, 11, 3931, 1378, 220, 17, 87, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 311, 279, 4396, 15336, 323, 41740, 279, 6422, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 22573, 432, 374, 9334, 13, 17375, 11, 17105, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 13, 4220, 7354, 5978, 279, 24354, 702, 264, 6437, 11, 2188, 16266, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4x4 skids to the necessary lengths (as specified in the passages) and set them on the gravel. Following this, cut two 2x6 rim joists and six joists to the correct dimensions and assemble the floor on the skids, ensuring it is square. Finally, anchor the frame to the skids with joist clip angles. These steps ensure the shed has a solid, level foundation.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1947171565813894, "g_worst_claim": -0.31025052070617676, "g_content": 2.3587330409458707, "g_traj_mean": 1.3702166080474854}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 39.47, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "125", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the process of building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site with compacted gravel, cutting and setting the 4 x 4 skids, cutting and assembling the floor with 2 x 6 rim joists and joists, anchoring the frame to the skids, attaching tongue-and-groove plywood flooring, constructing the walls separately, and raising them onto the frame.", "pred": "Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Then, cut two 4 x 4 skids to the appropriate length and set and level them. Next, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists and six joists at specified lengths. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids. Ensure the frame is square and anchor it to the skids. For the walls, construct them separately and then raise them onto the frame.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Then, cut two 4 x 4 skids to the appropriate length and set and level them. Next, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists and six joists at specified lengths. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids. Ensure the frame is square and anchor it to the skids. For the walls, construct them separately and then raise them onto the frame.", "cot": "[\"Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches and set them on the gravel, ensuring they are level. Then, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, checking for square, and then secure the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\", \"Building a lean-to shed involves several detailed steps. Firstly, ensure the site is prepared with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Then, cut and set two 4x4 skids as the foundation, following the specified dimensions. Next, cut two 2x6 rim joists and six joists, ensuring they are set at the correct lengths as per the shed building plans. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids, checking for squareness. Secure the frame to the skids with joist clip angles. For the walls, they are constructed separately and raised onto the frame. The shed dimensions shown are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, but they can be expanded in increments of 2 or 4 feet.\", \"Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Then, cut two 4 x 4 skids to the appropriate length and set and level them. Next, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists and six joists at specified lengths. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids. Ensure the frame is square and anchor it to the skids. For the walls, construct them separately and then raise them onto the frame.\", \"Answer: Building a lean-to shed involves several steps, including preparing the site, constructing the floor, and assembling the walls. The first passage provides step-by-step instructions for building a lean-to shed, including the preparation of the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel and setting two 4 x 4 skids at 70 2/4 inches. The second passage explains how to position the frame on the skids and toenail the floor joists to the skids. Finally, the third passage suggests that the shed can be easily expanded in increments of 2 or 4 feet to increase its size.\"]", "time_sec": 22.771, "generation_time_seconds": 22.0587, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7042, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [30133, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 13, 5512, 11, 10549, 279, 2747, 553, 34644, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 13, 9295, 11, 3931, 1378, 220, 19, 856, 220, 19, 1901, 3365, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 738, 1105, 389, 279, 41523, 11, 22573, 807, 525, 2188, 13, 5005, 11, 3931, 1378, 220, 17, 856, 220, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 323, 1992, 432, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 13295, 369, 9334, 11, 323, 1221, 9767, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 13, 151645], "pred": "Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches and set them on the gravel, ensuring they are level. Then, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, checking for square, and then secure the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7500350003204648, "g_worst_claim": 0.9770188331604004, "g_content": 2.480347430119749, "g_traj_mean": 1.6059857606887817}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [30133, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 11682, 7354, 13, 76695, 11, 5978, 279, 2747, 374, 10030, 448, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 13, 5005, 11, 3931, 323, 738, 1378, 220, 19, 87, 19, 1901, 3365, 438, 279, 16266, 11, 2701, 279, 5189, 15336, 13, 9295, 11, 3931, 1378, 220, 17, 87, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 11, 22573, 807, 525, 738, 518, 279, 4396, 28316, 438, 817, 279, 24354, 4752, 6649, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 323, 738, 432, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 13295, 369, 9334, 2090, 13, 34502, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 13, 1752, 279, 14285, 11, 807, 525, 20346, 25156, 323, 9226, 8630, 279, 4034, 13, 576, 24354, 15336, 6839, 525, 220, 21, 7541, 1293, 553, 220, 19, 7541, 6884, 11, 714, 807, 646, 387, 17183, 304, 61600, 315, 220, 17,