, "g_worst_claim": 1.0438964631822374, "g_content": 2.569704328264509, "g_traj_mean": 1.675098180770874}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 16858, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 11, 2670, 20045, 279, 2747, 11, 49353, 279, 6422, 11, 323, 80659, 279, 14285, 13, 576, 1156, 21085, 5707, 3019, 14319, 29208, 11221, 369, 4752, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 11, 2670, 279, 17975, 315, 279, 2747, 448, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 323, 6243, 1378, 220, 19, 856, 220, 19, 1901, 3365, 518, 220, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 14924, 13, 576, 2086, 21085, 14758, 1246, 311, 2309, 279, 4034, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 323, 99034, 604, 279, 6422, 7647, 1671, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 13, 17375, 11, 279, 4843, 21085, 13230, 429, 279, 24354, 646, 387, 6707, 17183, 304, 61600, 315, 220, 17, 476, 220, 19, 7541, 311, 5263, 1181, 1379, 13, 151645], "pred": "Building a lean-to shed involves several steps, including preparing the site, constructing the floor, and assembling the walls. The first passage provides step-by-step instructions for building a lean-to shed, including the preparation of the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel and setting two 4 x 4 skids at 70 2/4 inches. The second passage explains how to position the frame on the skids and toenail the floor joists to the skids. Finally, the third passage suggests that the shed can be easily expanded in increments of 2 or 4 feet to increase its size.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2531827192053648, "g_worst_claim": 0.6835456848144531, "g_content": 1.920670403374566, "g_traj_mean": 1.3764744997024536}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.19, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "126", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "Building a lean-to shed involves preparing the site, cutting and assembling the skids, flooring, and walls. To prepare the site, a 4\" layer of compacted gravel is recommended. The skids are cut to 70 2/4\" and set and leveled according to the shed building plans. Two 2 x 6 rim joists are cut at 7 3/4\" and six joists at 44 3/4\". The floor is assembled and set on the skids, checked for square, and anchored to the skids with four joist clip angles. The walls are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. Pressure-treated 4 by 4s are used for the skids, while 2 by 4s are used for the rim joists and flooring. 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood is attached to the frame for the flooring.", "pred": "In another method mentioned, two pressure-treated 4 by 4s are cut to 6 feet for the skids. The frame is then positioned on these skids and toenailed the floor joists to the skids. Finally, 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring is attached onto the frame. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "In another method mentioned, two pressure-treated 4 by 4s are cut to 6 feet for the skids. The frame is then positioned on these skids and toenailed the floor joists to the skids. Finally, 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring is attached onto the frame. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.", "cot": "[\"Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches and set them on the gravel, ensuring they are level. Then, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, checking for square, and then secure the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\", \"The process of building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4\\\" layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut the two 4 x 4 skids to the required length and set them on the gravel, ensuring they are level. Following this, cut the two 2 x 6 rim joists and six joists to the specified lengths. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, checking for square and then anchoring the frame to the skids with joist clip angles. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\", \"Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. Firstly, the site should be prepared with a 4\\\" layer of compacted gravel. The two 4x4 skids should be cut to a length of 70 2/4 inches and set on the ground at an even level according to the plans provided for the shed. Two 2x6 rim joists are then cut to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists are cut to a length of 44 3/4 inches. These joists are assembled and set on the skids as described in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans. The floor is checked for squareness and anchored to the skids with four joist clip angles. \\n\\nIn another method mentioned, two pressure-treated 4 by 4s are cut to 6 feet for the skids. The frame is then positioned on these skids and toenailed the floor joists to the skids. Finally, 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring is attached onto the frame. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\", \"Answer: Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by compacting it with a 4 inch layer of gravel. Next, cut two 4x4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches and set them on the site to level. Then, cut two 2x6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor onto the skids, making sure it is square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles. Finally, position the frame on the skids and toenail the floor joists to the skids. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\"]", "time_sec": 25.485, "generation_time_seconds": 24.6383, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8404, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [30133, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 13, 5512, 11, 10549, 279, 2747, 553, 34644, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 13, 9295, 11, 3931, 1378, 220, 19, 856, 220, 19, 1901, 3365, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 738, 1105, 389, 279, 41523, 11, 22573, 807, 525, 2188, 13, 5005, 11, 3931, 1378, 220, 17, 856, 220, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 323, 1992, 432, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 13295, 369, 9334, 11, 323, 1221, 9767, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 13, 151645], "pred": "Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches and set them on the gravel, ensuring they are level. Then, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, checking for square, and then secure the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7723317279702142, "g_worst_claim": 1.0362079620361329, "g_content": 2.479188512583248, "g_traj_mean": 1.6104683876037598}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 1882, 315, 4752, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 13, 5512, 11, 10549, 279, 2747, 553, 34644, 264, 220, 19, 1, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 13, 9295, 11, 3931, 279, 1378, 220, 19, 856, 220, 19, 1901, 3365, 311, 279, 2567, 3084, 323, 738, 1105, 389, 279, 41523, 11, 22573, 807, 525, 2188, 13, 22713, 419, 11, 3931, 279, 1378, 220, 17, 856, 220, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 311, 279, 5189, 28316, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 323, 1992, 432, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 13295, 369, 9334, 323, 1221, 33230, 5503, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 13, 576, 14285, 369, 279, 24354, 525, 20346, 25156, 323, 1221, 9226, 8630, 279, 4034, 13, 151645], "pred": "The process of building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4\" layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut the two 4 x 4 skids to the required length and set them on the gravel, ensuring they are level. Following this, cut the two 2 x 6 rim joists and six joists to the specified lengths. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, checking for square and then anchoring the frame to the skids with joist clip angles. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.547243996117647, "g_worst_claim": 0.5417957782745362, "g_content": 2.72693028943292, "g_traj_mean": 1.6390159130096436}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [30133, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 13, 76695, 11, 279, 2747, 1265, 387, 10030, 448, 264, 220, 19, 1, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 13, 576, 1378, 220, 19, 87, 19, 1901, 3365, 1265, 387, 3931, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 738, 389, 279, 4910, 518, 458, 1496, 2188, 4092, 311, 279, 6649, 3897, 369, 279, 24354, 13, 9043, 220, 17, 87, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 525, 1221, 3931, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 525, 3931, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 13, 4220, 7647, 1671, 525, 34005, 323, 738, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 438, 7481, 304, 279, 6422, 57949, 3772, 315, 279, 15651, 4686, 24354, 6649, 13, 576, 6422, 374, 10067, 369, 9334, 2090, 323, 77119, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 13, 4710, 641, 2441, 1714, 9733, 11, 1378, 7262, 87086, 220, 19, 553, 220, 19, 82, 525, 3931, 311, 220, 21, 7541, 369, 279, 1901, 3365, 13, 576, 4034, 374, 1221, 34228, 389, 1493, 1901, 3365, 323, 99034, 5687, 279, 6422, 7647, 1671, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 13, 17375, 11, 220, 18, 14, 19, 24241, 24459, 9777, 2371, 299, 994, 87898, 36148, 374, 12392, 8630, 279, 4034, 13, 576, 14285, 369, 279, 24354, 525, 20346, 25156, 323, 1221, 9226, 8630, 279, 4034, 13, 151645], "pred": "In another method mentioned, two pressure-treated 4 by 4s are cut to 6 feet for the skids. The frame is then positioned on these skids and toenailed the floor joists to the skids. Finally, 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring is attached onto the frame. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.726835030423245, "g_worst_claim": 1.1516049702962239, "g_content": 2.622000388728762, "g_traj_mean": 1.6105314493179321}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 16858, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 13, 5512, 11, 10549, 279, 2747, 553, 16830, 287, 432, 448, 264, 220, 19, 17122, 6193, 315, 41523, 13, 9295, 11, 3931, 1378, 220, 19, 87, 19, 1901, 3365, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 738, 1105, 389, 279, 2747, 311, 2188, 13, 5005, 11, 3931, 1378, 220, 17, 87, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 8630, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 3259, 2704, 432, 374, 9334, 11, 323, 1221, 17105, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 13, 17375, 11, 2309, 279, 4034, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 323, 99034, 604, 279, 6422, 7647, 1671, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 13, 576, 14285, 369, 279, 24354, 525, 20346, 25156, 323, 1221, 9226, 8630, 279, 4034, 13, 151645], "pred": "Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by compacting it with a 4 inch layer of gravel. Next, cut two 4x4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches and set them on the site to level. Then, cut two 2x6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor onto the skids, making sure it is square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles. Finally, position the frame on the skids and toenail the floor joists to the skids. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5817734934827985, "g_worst_claim": 1.1622039477030437, "g_content": 2.5979881809182364, "g_traj_mean": 1.526641845703125}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 44.04, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "127", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "Sure! Here's my attempt to answer your question based on the provided passages:\n\nHow do you prepare the site for building a lean-to shed?\n\nAccording to passage 1, step 1, you should prepare the site by laying down a 4\" layer of compacted gravel. This will provide a stable base for the shed's foundation. Additionally, passage 2 mentions cutting two pressure-treated 4x4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids, which will serve as the foundation for the shed. Finally, passage 3 provides instructions for building the shed's floor, including cutting rim joists to a length of 6 feet. Based on these passages, it appears that preparing the site involves laying down a layer of gravel and setting the skids in place before constructing the floor.", "pred": "Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches and set them on the gravel, ensuring they are level. Then, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, checking for square, and then secure the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches and set them on the gravel, ensuring they are level. Then, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, checking for square, and then secure the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.", "cot": "[\"Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches and set them on the gravel, ensuring they are level. Then, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, checking for square, and then secure the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\", \"Based on the provided passages, building a lean-to shed involves several steps. Firstly, the site needs to be prepared with a 4″ layer of compacted gravel. Then, the skids (2 pressure-treated 4 by 4s) are cut to a length of 6 feet and set on the gravel. The floor is built by cutting 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4 ” and six joists at 44 3/4″. These joists are assembled and set on the skids, checking for square and anchoring the frame to the skids with joist clip angles. The floor is then constructed by attaching 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame. The walls are constructed separately and raised onto the frame.\\nAnswer:[Based on the provided passages, building a lean-to shed involves several steps. Firstly, the site needs to be prepared with a 4″ layer of compacted gravel. Then, the skids (2 pressure-treated 4 by 4s) are cut to a length of 6 feet and set on the gravel. The floor is built by cutting 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4 ” and six joists at 44 3/4″. These joists are assembled and set on the skids, checking for square and anchoring the frame to the skids with joist clip angles. The floor is then constructed by attaching 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame. The walls are constructed separately and raised onto the frame.]\", \"Building a lean-to shed involves a step-by-step process that includes preparing the site, constructing the floor, and raising the walls. Here are the details:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Site:**\\n   - Place a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel to prepare the ground.\\n\\n2. **Construct the Floor:**\\n   - Cut two 4x4 skids to a length of 6 feet each.\\n   - Set and level the skids according to the provided shed building plans.\\n   - Cut two 2x6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches.\\n   - Assemble the floor and position it on the skids as indicated in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\\n   - Check the floor for square and then secure the frame to the skids using four joist clip angles.\\n   - Alternatively, toenail the floor joists to the skids when the frame is square.\\n   - Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\\n\\n3. **Construct the Walls:**\\n   - The walls are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame.\\n\\n4. **Dimensions:**\\n   - The shed in the example is 6 feet long by 4 feet wide, but you can easily expand its dimensions in increments of 2 or 4 feet.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can build a sturdy and functional lean-to shed.\", \"To build a lean-to shed, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\\n2. Cut two 4x4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches.\\n3. Set and level the skids following the shed building plans.\\n4. Cut two 2x6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches.\\n5. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\\n6. Check for square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\\n7. Cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids.\\n8. Position the frame on the skids, and, when square, toenail the floor joists to the skids.\\n9. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\\n10. Build the shed walls separately and then raise them onto the frame.\"]", "time_sec": 36.261, "generation_time_seconds": 35.2405, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0141, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [30133, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 13, 5512, 11, 10549, 279, 2747, 553, 34644, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 13, 9295, 11, 3931, 1378, 220, 19, 856, 220, 19, 1901, 3365, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 738, 1105, 389, 279, 41523, 11, 22573, 807, 525, 2188, 13, 5005, 11, 3931, 1378, 220, 17, 856, 220, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 323, 1992, 432, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 13295, 369, 9334, 11, 323, 1221, 9767, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 13, 151645], "pred": "Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches and set them on the gravel, ensuring they are level. Then, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, checking for square, and then secure the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7787412001027, "g_worst_claim": 0.9326961517333985, "g_content": 2.470999545738345, "g_traj_mean": 1.6049683094024658}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 4752, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 13, 76695, 11, 279, 2747, 3880, 311, 387, 10030, 448, 264, 220, 19, 21580, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 13, 5005, 11, 279, 1901, 3365, 320, 17, 7262, 87086, 220, 19, 553, 220, 19, 82, 8, 525, 3931, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 21, 7541, 323, 738, 389, 279, 41523, 13, 576, 6422, 374, 5798, 553, 14376, 220, 17, 856, 220, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 518, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 18987, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 518, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 21580, 13, 4220, 7647, 1671, 525, 34005, 323, 738, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 13295, 369, 9334, 323, 33230, 5503, 279, 4034, 31