ue, "token_ids": [1249, 1936, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 2747, 448, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 624, 17, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 19, 87, 19, 1901, 3365, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 14924, 624, 18, 13, 2573, 323, 2188, 279, 1901, 3365, 2701, 279, 24354, 4752, 6649, 624, 19, 13, 19649, 1378, 220, 17, 87, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 624, 20, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 323, 738, 432, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 438, 6839, 304, 279, 6422, 57949, 3772, 315, 279, 15651, 4686, 24354, 6649, 624, 21, 13, 4248, 369, 9334, 11, 323, 1221, 17105, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 624, 22, 13, 19649, 1378, 7262, 87086, 220, 19, 553, 220, 19, 82, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 21, 7541, 369, 279, 1901, 3365, 624, 23, 13, 12380, 279, 4034, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 323, 11, 979, 9334, 11, 99034, 604, 279, 6422, 7647, 1671, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 624, 24, 13, 48384, 220, 18, 14, 19, 24241, 24459, 9777, 2371, 299, 994, 87898, 36148, 8630, 279, 4034, 624, 16, 15, 13, 7854, 279, 24354, 14285, 25156, 323, 1221, 4828, 1105, 8630, 279, 4034, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Prepare the site with a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel.\n2. Cut two 4x4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches.\n3. Set and level the skids following the shed building plans.\n4. Cut two 2x6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches.\n5. Assemble the floor and set it on the skids as shown in the floor framing section of the lean-to shed plans.\n6. Check for square, and then anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\n7. Cut two pressure-treated 4 by 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids.\n8. Position the frame on the skids, and, when square, toenail the floor joists to the skids.\n9. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\n10. Build the shed walls separately and then raise them onto the frame.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.870388636588691, "g_worst_claim": -0.10930846134821574, "g_content": 2.5549827938988097, "g_traj_mean": 1.6894652843475342}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 31.29, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "129", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "What are the dimensions of the shed in passage 3?\n\nThe dimensions of the shed in passage 3 are 6 feet long by 4 feet wide.", "pred": "Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches and set them on the gravel, ensuring they are level. Then, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, checking for square, and then secure the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches and set them on the gravel, ensuring they are level. Then, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, checking for square, and then secure the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.", "cot": "[\"Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches and set them on the gravel, ensuring they are level. Then, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, checking for square, and then secure the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.\", \"Building a lean-to shed involves several steps, as described in the provided passages. Initially, the site is prepared by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. The two 4x4 skids are prepared by cutting them to the necessary length and setting them up at the correct height. This is followed by the installation of two 2x6 rim joists and six joists, which are cut to specific lengths as per the shed building plans. The floor is then assembled and set on the skids, ensuring it is square and anchored properly. The frame is then checked for squareness and secured with four joist clip angles. When the frame is square, the floor joists are tongued and grooved onto the frame, followed by the attachment of plywood flooring. Walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. This process ensures that the shed is built with the correct dimensions and structural integrity.\", \"Building a lean-to shed involves several steps, including preparing the site and constructing the floor and walls. According to the provided passages, the process begins with preparing the site by laying a 4″ layer of compacted gravel. Next, two 4 x 4 skids are cut to a specific length (70 2/4″) and set on the site, ensuring they are level. Following this, two 2 x 6 rim joists are cut and assembled to form the floor, which is then placed on the skids. The floor assembly is checked for square and anchored to the skids with joist clip angles for stability.\\n\\nFor the floor, two pressure-treated 4 by 4s are cut to a length of 6 feet for the skids, and the frame is positioned on the skids. Once the frame is square, the floor joists are toenailed to the skids for additional support. Additionally, 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring is attached to the frame.\\n\\nThe walls of the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame, but the specific details about the wall construction are not provided in the given passages. \\n\\nBuilding the shed itself begins with the floor framing, as described in passage 3. Using two pressure-treated 2 by 4s cut to a length of 6 feet for the rim joists, the shed's dimensions can be easily expanded in increments of 2 or 4 feet, as mentioned.\", \"To build a lean-to shed, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Prepare the site: Start by compacting the area with a 4-inch layer of gravel. This ensures a stable foundation for the shed.\\n\\n2. Cut the skids: Measure two 4x4 wooden skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches. These skids will serve as the base structure for the shed.\\n\\n3. Level the skids: Place and level the two skids according to the instructions provided in the lean-to shed plans.\\n\\n4. Cut the rim joists and joists: Measure and cut two 2x6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches, and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches.\\n\\n5. Assemble the floor: Arrange the floor joists and set them on the skids. Make sure the frame is square. Then, secure the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles. \\n\\n6. Construct the walls: The walls are built separately and lifted onto the floor frame. \\n\\n7. Install the flooring: After the frame is assembled, attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame.\\n\\nBy following these detailed steps, you can construct a sturdy lean-to shed.\"]", "time_sec": 33.219, "generation_time_seconds": 32.4781, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7334, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [30133, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 13, 5512, 11, 10549, 279, 2747, 553, 34644, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 13, 9295, 11, 3931, 1378, 220, 19, 856, 220, 19, 1901, 3365, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 738, 1105, 389, 279, 41523, 11, 22573, 807, 525, 2188, 13, 5005, 11, 3931, 1378, 220, 17, 856, 220, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 323, 1992, 432, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 13295, 369, 9334, 11, 323, 1221, 9767, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 13, 151645], "pred": "Building a lean-to shed involves several steps. First, prepare the site by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. Next, cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4 inches and set them on the gravel, ensuring they are level. Then, cut two 2 x 6 rim joists to a length of 7 3/4 inches and six joists to a length of 44 3/4 inches. Assemble the floor and place it on the skids, checking for square, and then secure the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8072516096962823, "g_worst_claim": 0.9986599922180176, "g_content": 2.5168707175332994, "g_traj_mean": 1.629229187965393}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [30133, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 11, 438, 7481, 304, 279, 3897, 46769, 13, 58556, 11, 279, 2747, 374, 10030, 553, 34644, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 13, 576, 1378, 220, 19, 87, 19, 1901, 3365, 525, 10030, 553, 14376, 1105, 311, 279, 5871, 3084, 323, 6243, 1105, 705, 518, 279, 4396, 2608, 13, 1096, 374, 8110, 553, 279, 13713, 315, 1378, 220, 17, 87, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 11, 892, 525, 3931, 311, 3151, 28316, 438, 817, 279, 24354, 4752, 6649, 13, 576, 6422, 374, 1221, 34005, 323, 738, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 22573, 432, 374, 9334, 323, 77119, 10277, 13, 576, 4034, 374, 1221, 10067, 369, 9334, 2090, 323, 26430, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 13, 3197, 279, 4034, 374, 9334, 11, 279, 6422, 7647, 1671, 525, 21365, 3260, 323, 10487, 4941, 8630, 279, 4034, 11, 8110, 553, 279, 19984, 315, 87898, 36148, 13, 71178, 369, 279, 24354, 525, 20346, 25156, 323, 1221, 9226, 8630, 279, 4034, 13, 1096, 1882, 25351, 429, 279, 24354, 374, 5798, 448, 279, 4396, 15336, 323, 23759, 16614, 13, 151645], "pred": "Building a lean-to shed involves several steps, as described in the provided passages. Initially, the site is prepared by laying a 4-inch layer of compacted gravel. The two 4x4 skids are prepared by cutting them to the necessary length and setting them up at the correct height. This is followed by the installation of two 2x6 rim joists and six joists, which are cut to specific lengths as per the shed building plans. The floor is then assembled and set on the skids, ensuring it is square and anchored properly. The frame is then checked for squareness and secured with four joist clip angles. When the frame is square, the floor joists are tongued and grooved onto the frame, followed by the attachment of plywood flooring. Walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. This process ensures that the shed is built with the correct dimensions and structural integrity.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2991903707480008, "g_worst_claim": 0.3545770049095154, "g_content": 2.3843055276309744, "g_traj_mean": 1.3366485834121704}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [30133, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 17601, 3807, 7354, 11, 2670, 20045, 279, 2747, 323, 49353, 279, 6422, 323, 14285, 13, 10548, 311, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 279, 1882, 12033, 448, 20045, 279, 2747, 553, 34644, 264, 220, 19, 21580, 6193, 315, 16830, 291, 41523, 13, 9295, 11, 1378, 220, 19, 856, 220, 19, 1901, 3365, 525, 3931, 311, 264, 3151, 3084, 320, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 21580, 8, 323, 738, 389, 279, 2747, 11, 22573, 807, 525, 2188, 13, 22713, 419, 11, 1378, 220, 17, 856, 220, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 525, 3931, 323, 34005, 311, 1352, 279, 6422, 11, 892, 374, 1221, 9099, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 13, 576, 6422, 14614, 374, 10067, 369, 9334, 323, 77119, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 369, 19753, 382, 2461, 279, 6422, 11, 1378, 7262, 87086, 220, 19, 553, 220, 19, 82, 525, 3931, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 21, 7541, 369, 279, 1901, 3365, 11, 323, 279, 4034, 374, 34228, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 13, 9646, 279, 4034, 374, 9334, 11, 279, 6422, 7647, 1671, 525, 99034, 5687, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 369, 5107, 1824, 13, 22406, 11, 220, 18, 14, 19, 24241, 24459, 9777, 2371, 299, 994, 87898, 36148, 374, 12392, 311, 279, 4034, 382, 785, 14285, 315, 279, 24354, 525, 20346, 25156, 323, 1221, 9226, 8630, 279, 4034, 11, 714, 279, 3151, 3565, 911, 279, 7002, 8086, 525, 537, 3897, 304, 279, 2661, 46769, 13, 4710, 30133, 279, 24354, 5086, 12033, 448, 279, 6422, 57949, 11, 438, 7481, 304, 21085, 220, 18, 13, 12091, 1378, 7262, 87086, 220, 17, 553, 220, 19, 82, 3931, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 21, 7541, 369, 279, 30130, 7647, 1671, 11, 279, 24354, 594, 15336, 646, 387, 6707, 17183, 304, 61600, 315, 220, 17, 476, 220, 19, 7541, 11, 438, 9733, 13, 151645], "pred": "Building the shed itself begins with the floor framing, as described in passage 3. Using two pressure-treated 2 by 4s cut to a length of 6 feet for the rim joists, the shed's dimensions can be easily expanded in increments of 2 or 4 feet, as mentioned.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3428711519011645, "g_worst_claim": 0.2580273449420929, "g_content": 2.3360823446245336, "g_traj_mean": 1.4427107572555542}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1936, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 2747, 25, 5145, 553, 16830, 287, 279, 3082, 448, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 41523, 13, 1096, 25351, 264, 15175, 16266, 369, 279, 24354, 382, 17, 13, 19649, 279, 1901, 3365, 25, 34104, 1378, 220, 19, 87, 19, 22360, 1901, 3365, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 15, 220, 17, 14, 19, 14924, 13, 4220, 1901, 3365, 686, 8683, 438, 279, 2331, 5944, 369, 279, 24354, 382, 18, 13, 9395, 279, 1901, 3365, 25, 10771, 323, 2188, 279, 1378, 1901, 3365, 4092, 311, 279, 11221, 3897, 304, 279, 15651, 4686, 24354, 6649, 382, 19, 13, 19649, 279, 30130, 7647, 1671, 323, 7647, 1671, 25, 34104, 323, 3931, 1378, 220, 17, 87, 21, 30130, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 22, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 11, 323, 4743, 7647, 1671, 311, 264, 3084, 315, 220, 19, 19, 220, 18, 14, 19, 14924, 382, 20, 13, 1634, 15790, 279, 6422, 25, 40580, 279, 6422, 7647, 1671, 323, 738, 1105, 389, 279, 1901, 3365, 13, 7405, 2704, 279, 4034, 374, 9334, 13, 5005, 11, 9767, 279, 4034, 311, 279, 1901, 3365, 448, 3040, 7647, 380, 12327, 25941, 13, 4710, 21, 13, 18678, 279, 14285, 25, 576, 14285, 525, 5798, 25156, 323, 29731, 8630, 279, 6422, 4034, 13, 4710, 22, 13, 19242, 279, 36148, 25, 4636, 279, 4034, 374, 34005, 11, 15498, 220, 18, 14, 19, 24241, 24459, 9777, 2371, 299, 994, 87898, 36148, 8630, 279, 4034, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 11682, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 9245, 264, 44552, 15651, 4686, 24354, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these detailed steps, you can construct a sturdy lean-to shed.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9881167562001318, "g_worst_claim": -0.0947485864162445, "g_content": 1.6770652770996093, "g_traj_mean": 1.064212441444397}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 8.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "130", "question": "difference between vietnam and india", "gt": "The passages suggest that trends in India are more typical than those in Vietnam, particularly in the area of education. Vietnam's education system is described as relatively equitable, where poorer children receive the same treatment as their better-off counterparts. In contrast, India's early focus was on getting children into school, which involved setting up schools, and training teachers. Politically, India supported Vietnam's independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War. Both countries have a history of colonialism, with India being a former colony of the United Kingdom and Vietnam of France. Post-colonization, India experienced division and conflict among Hindus, Muslims and Sikhs. Cultural and economic links between India and Vietnam date back to the 2nd century.", "pred": "The passage does not provide a comprehensive difference between Vietnam and India.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The passage does not provide a comprehensive difference between Vietnam and India.", "cot": "[\"The passage does not provide a direct comparison between Vietnam and India. However, it does mention that the trends in India are more typical than those in Vietnam, and that Vietnam's education system is relatively equitable, meaning poorer children receive the same deal as those who are better-off. Additionally, the passage notes that India supported Vietnam's independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War, while also supporting unification of Vietnam. The passage also mentions that India and Vietnam have strong bilateral relations and cultural and economic links dating back to the 2nd century.\", \"The trends in India are much more typical than those in Vietnam. India had a focus on getting children into school, which involved looking at resources and facilities, setting up schools, and training teachers. Vietnam, on the other hand, has a relatively equitable education system where poorer children receive the same deal as those who are better-off. India supported Vietnam's independence from France, opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War, and supported unification of Vietnam. During the Vietnam War, India supported the North, albeit not by conducting military hostilities against the South. The Republic of India and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam enjoy strong bilateral relations. Cultural and economic links between India and Vietnam date back to the 2nd century. The Indic Chăm Pa kingdom had some influence on Vietnamese music.\", \"The passage does not provide a comprehensive difference between Vietnam and India.\", \"The passage discusses the differences between Vietnam and India in terms of education and historical and cultural connections. In education, Vietnam's school system is relatively equitable, meaning poorer children receive the same quality of education as those who are better off, whereas the focus in India was more on getting children into school in the first place. In terms of history and culture, Vietnam has strong bilateral relations with India, and there are cultural and economic links between the two countries that date back to the 2nd century. India supported Vietnam's independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War, while France and the United Kingdom were both colonial powers that lost colonies around the same time, including India and Vietnam.\"]", "time_sec": 18.276, "generation_time_seconds": 17.3011, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9675, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 21085, 1558, 537, 3410, 264, 2118, 12313, 1948, 22500, 323, 6747, 13, 4354, 11, 432, 1558, 6286, 429, 279, 18339, 304, 6747, 525, 803, 14260, 1091, 1846, 304, 22500, 11, 323, 429, 22500, 594, 6731, 1849, 374, 12040, 76009, 11, 7290, 65181, 2841, 5258, 279, 1852, 3484, 438, 1846, 879, 525, 2664, 12462, 13, 22406, 11, 279, 21085, 8388, 429, 6747, 7248, 22500, 594, 23665, 504, 9625, 323, 16087, 3693, 21587, 304, 279, 22500, 5004, 11, 1393, 1083, 12613, 650, 2404, 315, 22500, 13, 576, 21085, 1083, 33845, 429, 6747, 323, 22500, 614, 3746, 51203, 4300, 323, 12752, 323, 6955, 7746, 4924, 1182, 311, 279, 220, 17, 303, 9294, 13, 151645], "pred": "The passage does not provide a direct comparison between Vietnam and India. However, it does mention that the trends in India are more typical than those in Vietnam, and that Vietnam's education system is relatively equitable, meaning poorer children receive the same deal as those who are better-off. Additionally, the passage notes that India supported Vietnam's independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War, while also supporting unification of Vietnam. The passage also mentions that India and Vietnam have strong bilateral relations and cultural and economic links dating back to the 2nd century.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9829106477696568, "g_worst_claim": 0.9856654680692233, "g_content": 2.878026326497396, "g_traj_mean": 1.8538275957107544}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 18339, 304, 6747, 525, 1753, 803, 14260, 1091, 1846, 304, 22500, 13, 6747, 1030, 264, 5244, 389, 3709, 2841, 1119, 2906, 11, 892, 6398, 3330, 518, 4963, 323, 12786, 11, 6243, 705, 8682, 11, 323, 4862, 13336, 13, 22500, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 702, 264, 12040, 76009, 6731, 1849, 1380, 65181, 2841, 5258, 279, 1852, 3484, 438, 1846, 879, 525, 2664, 12462, 13, 6747, 7248, 22500, 594, 23665, 504, 9625, 11, 16087, 3693, 21587, 304, 279, 22500, 5004, 11, 323, 7248, 650, 2404, 315, 22500, 13, 11954, 279, 22500, 5004, 11, 6747, 7248, 279, 4787, 11, 42069, 537, 553, 30374, 6277, 3468, 4298, 2348, 279, 4882, 13, 576, 5429, 315, 6747, 323, 279, 56110, 5429, 315, 22500, 4669, 3746, 51203, 4300, 13, 40233, 323, 6955, 7746, 1948, 6747, 323, 22500, 2400, 1182, 311, 279, 220, 17, 303, 9294, 13, 576, 2263, 292, 910, 77354, 15681, 25079, 1030, 1045, 10173, 389, 48477, 4627, 13, 151645], "pred": "The trends in India are much more typical than those in Vietnam. India had a focus on getting children into school, which involved looking at resources and facilities, setting up schools, and training teachers. Vietnam, on the other hand, has a relatively equitable education system where poorer children receive the same deal as those who are better-off. India supported Vietnam's independence from France, opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War, and supported unification of Vietnam. During the Vietnam War, India supported the North, albeit not by conducting military hostilities against the South. The Republic of India and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam enjoy strong bilateral relations. Cultural and economic links between India and Vietnam date back to the 2nd century. The Indic Chăm Pa kingdom had some influence on Vietnamese music.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.4675897552226798, "g_worst_claim": 1.0346843004226685, "g_content": 3.7314572024655033, "g_traj_mean": 2.4664552211761475}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 21085, 1558, 537, 3410, 264, 15817, 6672, 1948, 22500, 323, 6747, 13, 151645], "pred": "The passage does not provide a comprehensive difference between Vietnam and India.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1882272133460412, "g_worst_claim": 1.1882272133460412, "g_content": 1.3194019794464111, "g_traj_mean": 1.118313193321228}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 21085, 34334, 279, 11799, 1948, 22500, 323, 6747, 304, 3793, 315, 6731, 323, 13656, 323, 12752, 13234, 13, 758, 6731, 11, 22500, 594, 2906, 1849, 374, 12040, 76009, 11, 7290, 65181, 2841, 5258, 279, 1852, 4271, 315, 6731, 438, 1846, 879, 525, 2664, 1007, 11, 19853, 279, 5244, 304, 6747, 572, 803, 389, 3709, 2841, 1119, 2906, 304, 279, 1156, 1992, 13, 758, 3793, 315, 3840, 323, 7674, 11, 22500, 702, 3746, 51203, 4300, 448, 6747, 11, 323, 1052, 525, 12752, 323, 6955, 7746, 1948, 279, 1378, 5837, 429, 2400, 1182, 311, 279, 220, 17, 303, 9294, 13, 6747, 7248, 22500, 594, 23665, 504, 9625, 323, 16087, 3693, 21587, 304, 279, 22500, 5004, 11, 1393, 9625, 323, 279, 3639, 15072, 1033, 2176, 36583, 13430, 429, 5558, 47928, 2163, 279, 1852, 882, 11, 2670, 6747, 323, 22500, 13, 151645], "pred": "The passage discusses the differences between Vietnam and India in terms of education and historical and cultural connections. In education, Vietnam's school system is relatively equitable, meaning poorer children receive the same quality of education as those who are better off, whereas the focus in India was more on getting children into school in the first place. In terms of history and culture, Vietnam has strong bilateral relations with India, and there are cultural and economic links between the two countries that date back to the 2nd century. India supported Vietnam's independence from France and opposed American involvement in the Vietnam War, while France and the United Kingdom were both colonial powers that lost colonies around the same time, including India and Vietnam.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.370486780025277, "g_worst_claim": 0.014205529221466609, "g_content": 2.0888233729771204, "g_traj_mean": 1.4754101037979126}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 6.59, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "132", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, but keep the skins of the individual cloves intact. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves to expose them. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves. Season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices if you like. Roasting time is dependent on the size of the cloves and may take up to 45 minutes or an hour for larger cloves. Once roasted, the garlic cloves can be stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.", "pred": "To roast individual garlic cloves, preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To roast individual garlic cloves, preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "cot": "[\"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"To roast individual garlic cloves, preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"To roast individual garlic cloves, preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\"]", "time_sec": 22.963, "generation_time_seconds": 22.0942, "selection_time_seconds": 0.862, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 4292, 17, 13, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 34439, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 11, 45966, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 13, 362, 54304, 258, 7215, 4278, 2244, 369, 419, 11, 438, 432, 13598, 279, 30635, 53220, 504, 20097, 2163, 624, 20, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 1968, 11, 1667, 697, 19225, 311, 10273, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 11, 14900, 30635, 84288, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4924585633732936, "g_worst_claim": 0.27875633239746095, "g_content": 1.7