1, 3108, 705, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 1968, 11, 1667, 697, 19225, 311, 10273, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 11, 14900, 30635, 84288, 13, 151645], "pred": "To roast individual garlic cloves, preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4920857116665467, "g_worst_claim": 0.28042083978652954, "g_content": 1.9305713653564454, "g_traj_mean": 1.7257390022277832}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 4292, 17, 13, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 34439, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 11, 45966, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 13, 362, 54304, 258, 7215, 4278, 2244, 369, 419, 11, 438, 432, 13598, 279, 30635, 53220, 504, 20097, 2163, 624, 20, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 1968, 11, 1667, 697, 19225, 311, 10273, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 11, 14900, 30635, 84288, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4924585633732936, "g_worst_claim": 0.27875633239746095, "g_content": 1.7845189947831004, "g_traj_mean": 1.553099274635315}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 75.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "133", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "To roast individual garlic cloves, preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the garlic bulb, leaving the skins of the cloves intact. Cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of the cloves to expose them. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up, and drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, rubbing it over the cloves. Roast the cloves in the preheated oven for about 45 minutes to an hour, or until they are softened. Store the roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.", "pred": "Preheat the oven to 400°F (205° C), peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, place the garlic heads in a baking pan with the cut side up, drizzle with olive oil, and roast in the oven for the recommended time based on clove size.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Preheat the oven to 400°F (205° C), peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, place the garlic heads in a baking pan with the cut side up, drizzle with olive oil, and roast in the oven for the recommended time based on clove size.", "cot": "[\"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"Answer:\\nTo roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n\\n3. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\\n\\n4. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\\n\\n5. Roast the garlic in the preheated oven for about 45 minutes to an hour, depending on the size of the cloves. Note that it may take up to 45 minutes or even an hour for your cloves to soften if they are large.\\n\\n6. Once roasted, the garlic cloves will be soft and fragrant. Store them in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.\", \"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\\n\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\\n\\n6. Roast the garlic in the preheated oven for the appropriate time based on the size of the cloves, which can take up to 45 minutes or even an hour for large cloves.\\n\\n7. Once done, store the roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.\\n\\nOptional step: Season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices, if you like. For kick, add some cayenne or chipotle pepper powder, Cajun seasoning mix, or curry powder. Dried oregano, marjoram, thyme, rosemary, tarragon, or basil work well, too. Choose seasonings to complement the food you're using the roasted garlic with.\", \"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\\n\\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to 400°F (205° C), peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, place the garlic heads in a baking pan with the cut side up, drizzle with olive oil, and roast in the oven for the recommended time based on clove size.\"]", "time_sec": 34.329, "generation_time_seconds": 33.3498, "selection_time_seconds": 0.973, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 4292, 17, 13, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 34439, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 11, 45966, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 2