, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 264, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 11, 1992, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 448, 279, 3931, 3108, 705, 11, 1353, 43137, 448, 32113, 5590, 11, 323, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 279, 11102, 882, 3118, 389, 5292, 586, 1379, 13, 151645], "pred": "Preheat the oven to 400°F (205° C), peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, place the garlic heads in a baking pan with the cut side up, drizzle with olive oil, and roast in the oven for the recommended time based on clove size.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1694725895025764, "g_worst_claim": -0.07114521520478385, "g_content": 1.2168686965416218, "g_traj_mean": 1.0938589572906494}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 56.07, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "135", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "Here are brief answers to the question on how to roast individual garlic cloves based on the provided passages:\n\nPassage 1: The passage does not provide information on how to roast individual garlic cloves specifically. However, it does mention that larger garlic cloves may take up to an hour to soften when roasted, so it is possible to assume that smaller cloves will take less time.\n\nPassage 2: This passage provides some options for seasoning the garlic before roasting, but it does not provide instructions on how to roast individual garlic cloves.\n\nPassage 3: This passage provides a method for roasting entire garlic heads, but it does not address how to roast individual garlic cloves. The passage does mention that cutting the top of the garlic bulb and exposing the individual cloves can help them roast more evenly, but it does not provide specific instructions on how to do this.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head.\n6. Rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n7. Roast the garlic in the oven for the time mentioned in the passage, based on the size of your garlic cloves.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head.\n6. Rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n7. Roast the garlic in the oven for the time mentioned in the passage, based on the size of your garlic cloves.", "cot": "[\"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Preheat the Oven**: Set your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. **Prepare the Garlic**: Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the garlic bulb, leaving the skins of the individual cloves intact. Use a sharp knife to cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of each clove to expose them.\\n3. **Arrange on a Pan**: Place the garlic heads, cut side up, in a baking pan. A muffin pan is especially useful because it prevents the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\\n4. **Drizzle Olive Oil**: Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each garlic head. Use your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the exposed garlic cloves.\\n\\nThis method ensures that the garlic cloves are evenly coated with olive oil and have plenty of surface area to roast and become soft and flavorful.\", \"1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head.\\n6. Rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\\n7. Roast the garlic in the oven for the time mentioned in the passage, based on the size of your garlic cloves.\", \"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\\n\\nThis method ensures that the garlic cloves are evenly coated with olive oil and will roast evenly in the oven, enhancing their flavor and making them easy to peel after roasting.\"]", "time_sec": 27.102, "generation_time_seconds": 26.2181, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8757, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 4292, 17, 13, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 34439, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 11, 45966, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 13, 362, 54304, 258, 7215, 4278, 2244, 369, 419, 11, 438, 432, 13598, 279, 30635, 53220, 504, 20097, 2163, 624, 20, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 1968, 11, 1667, 697, 19225, 311, 10273, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 11, 14900, 30635, 84288, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.504296273274465, "g_worst_claim": 0.2771267573038737, "g_content": 1.7822189331054688, "g_traj_mean": 1.545498013496399}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 4703, 19963, 279, 86113, 95518, 2573, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 4292, 17, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 94725, 95518, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 34439, 13, 5443, 264, 17232, 21430, 311, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 1817, 5292, 586, 311, 28141, 1105, 624, 18, 13, 3070, 79235, 389, 264, 10990, 95518, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 11, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 13, 362, 54304, 258, 7215, 374, 5310, 5390, 1576, 432, 27934, 279, 30635, 53220, 504, 20097, 2163, 624, 19, 13, 3070, 8847, 43137, 46714, 15526, 95518, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 315, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 30635, 1968, 13, 5443, 697, 19225, 311, 10273, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 14900, 3