_mean_claim": 1.4730351402791575, "g_worst_claim": 0.7889714241027832, "g_content": 1.8198858896891277, "g_traj_mean": 1.4187736511230469}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 11616, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 34439, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 264, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 11, 45966, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 13, 362, 54304, 258, 7215, 4278, 2244, 369, 419, 438, 432, 13598, 279, 30635, 53220, 504, 20097, 2163, 624, 20, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 1968, 11, 1667, 697, 19225, 311, 10273, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 11, 14900, 30635, 84288, 382, 1986, 1714, 25351, 429, 279, 30635, 84288, 525, 41047, 48382, 448, 32113, 5590, 323, 686, 57685, 41047, 304, 279, 23387, 11, 46494, 862, 17172, 323, 3259, 1105, 4135, 311, 57112, 1283, 926, 14725, 13, 151645], "pred": "This method ensures that the garlic cloves are evenly coated with olive oil and will roast evenly in the oven, enhancing their flavor and making them easy to peel after roasting.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.375440908555116, "g_worst_claim": 0.02626121502656203, "g_content": 1.4928199281083776, "g_traj_mean": 1.343809723854065}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 27.66, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "136", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "Sure! Here's how to roast individual garlic cloves based on the provided passages:\n\nTo roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of each clove, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up.\n5. Drizzle a couple of teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n6. Season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices, if desired.\n7. Roast the garlic in the preheated oven for up to 45 minutes or until the cloves are softened to your liking.\n8. Store roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.\n\nNote that the roasting time may vary depending on the size of your garlic cloves, so check on them periodically to avoid overcooking.", "pred": "4. Season with olive oil: Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "4. Season with olive oil: Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "cot": "[\"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. \\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\\n6. After roasting, the garlic cloves will be softened and can be stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.\\n\\nOptional seasoning: Season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices, if you like. For extra flavor, you can add some cayenne or chipotle pepper powder, Cajun seasoning mix, curry powder, dried oregano, marjoram, thyme, rosemary, tarragon, or basil. Choose seasonings that complement the food you're using the roasted garlic with.\\n\\nAnswer: Roast individual garlic cloves by preheating the oven to 400°F (205°C), peeling and cutting the garlic, placing them in a baking pan, and drizzling olive oil over them. Optionally season with herbs and spices.\", \"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Prepare your garlic: Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n\\n2. Preheat your oven: Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C).\\n\\n3. Arrange the garlic: Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\\n\\n4. Season with olive oil: Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\"]", "time_sec": 31.085, "generation_time_seconds": 30.1364, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9402, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 4292, 17, 13, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 34439, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 11, 45966, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 13, 362, 54304, 258, 7215, 4278, 2244, 369, 419, 11, 438, 432, 13598, 279, 30635, 53220, 504, 20097, 2163, 624, 20, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 1968, 11, 1667, 697, 19225, 311, 10273, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 11, 14900, 3