{"id": "137", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. (A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.)\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\n6. Roast in the preheated oven for 45 minutes to an hour, or until the cloves are softened.\n7. Store roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.\n\nYou can also season the garlic cloves to taste with herbs and spices before roasting.", "pred": "To roast individual garlic cloves, preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves. Roast the garlic in the oven until the cloves are soft, which may take up to 45 minutes or even an hour for large cloves.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To roast individual garlic cloves, preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves. Roast the garlic in the oven until the cloves are soft, which may take up to 45 minutes or even an hour for large cloves.", "cot": "[\"To roast individual garlic cloves, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"Roasting individual garlic cloves.\\nMethod 1: Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\", \"To roast individual garlic cloves, preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves. Roast the garlic in the oven until the cloves are soft, which may take up to 45 minutes or even an hour for large cloves.\", \"Answer: Preheat the oven to 400°F (205° C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.\"]", "time_sec": 23.104, "generation_time_seconds": 22.3692, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7304, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 4292, 17, 13, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 34439, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 11, 45966, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 13, 362, 54304, 258, 7215, 4278, 2244, 369, 419, 11, 438, 432, 13598, 279, 30635, 53220, 504, 20097, 2163, 624, 20, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 1968, 11, 1667, 697, 19225, 311, 10273, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 11, 14900, 30635, 84288, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C).\n2. Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic.\n3. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic.\n4. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. A muffin pan works great for this, as it keeps the garlic bulbs from rolling around.\n5. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4925140520648954, "g_worst_claim": 0.2726571083068848, "g_content": 1.7793697557951276, "g_traj_mean": 1.5327975749969482}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [11830, 14725, 3842, 30635, 84288, 624, 3523, 220, 16, 25, 4968, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 11616, 356, 568, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 34439, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 264, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 11, 45966, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 1968, 11, 1667, 697, 19225, 311, 10273, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 11, 14900, 30635, 84288, 13, 151645], "pred": "Roasting individual garlic cloves.\nMethod 1: Preheat your oven to 400°F (205° C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.499556959841035, "g_worst_claim": 0.6188700795173645, "g_content": 1.9899476066468254, "g_traj_mean": 1.6497206687927246}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 855, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 30937, 568, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 34439, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 11, 45966, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 1968, 11, 1667, 697, 19225, 311, 10273, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 11, 14900, 30635, 84288, 13, 11830, 559, 279, 30635, 304, 279, 23387, 3080, 279, 84288, 525, 8413, 11, 892, 1231, 1896, 705, 311, 220, 19, 20, 4420, 476, 1496, 458, 6460, 369, 3460, 84288, 13, 151645], "pred": "To roast individual garlic cloves, preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves. Roast the garlic in the oven until the cloves are soft, which may take up to 45 minutes or even an hour for large cloves.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4030930996165445, "g_worst_claim": 0.314900279045105, "g_content": 1.7486254374186199, "g_traj_mean": 1.4785864353179932}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 58472, 320, 17, 15, 20, 11616, 356, 568, 88594, 323, 37867, 279, 25298, 722, 15955, 13617, 315, 279, 4361, 30635, 45812, 11, 9380, 34439, 279, 49950, 315, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 13, 12091, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 3931, 220, 16, 14, 19, 311, 264, 220, 16, 14, 17, 17122, 504, 279, 1909, 315, 84288, 11, 45966, 279, 3842, 84288, 315, 30635, 13, 10771, 279, 30635, 14629, 304, 264, 27815, 7215, 11, 3931, 3108, 705, 13, 2926, 43137, 264, 5625, 92100, 315, 32113, 5590, 916, 1817, 14900, 1968, 11, 1667, 697, 19225, 311, 10273, 279, 32113, 5590, 916, 678, 279, 3931, 11, 14900, 30635, 84288, 13, 151645], "pred": "Preheat the oven to 400°F (205° C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the whole garlic bulb, leaving intact the skins of the individual cloves of garlic. Using a sharp knife, cut 1/4 to a 1/2 inch from the top of cloves, exposing the individual cloves of garlic. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up. Drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, using your fingers to rub the olive oil over all the cut, exposed garlic cloves.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5314860686426135, "g_worst_claim": 0.639793872833252, "g_content": 2.1542314989813445, "g_traj_mean": 1.7870163917541504}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 77.55, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "138", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the Income Tax Act, when an asset is discarded but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded as per section 43(6). This is done under the block concept, where all assets of the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset. Any changes to the block's value must abide by the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961. Additionally, the assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, even if it's not used for the purposes of business or profession in that year and subsequent years.", "pred": "When an asset is discarded, as per the Income Tax Act, under the block concept, the scrap value of the asset is reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "When an asset is discarded, as per the Income Tax Act, under the block concept, the scrap value of the asset is reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded.", "cot": "[\"When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is governed by section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"Answer: According to the Income Tax Act, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset is permitted to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is regulated by section 43(6) and must be in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"When an asset is discarded, under the Income Tax Act, the scrap value of the asset is reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment allows the assessee to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, even if the asset is not used for the purposes of business or profession in the subsequent years.\", \"When an asset is discarded, as per the Income Tax Act, under the block concept, the scrap value of the asset is reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded.\"]", "time_sec": 13.897, "generation_time_seconds": 12.9124, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9755, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [4498, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 26702, 553, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is governed by section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.2313654603205637, "g_worst_claim": 1.0922534730699327, "g_content": 2.382662565811821, "g_traj_mean": 1.918520450592041}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 10548, 311, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 374, 15129, 311, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 34219, 553, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 323, 1969, 387, 304, 18353, 448, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "According to the Income Tax Act, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset is permitted to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is regulated by section 43(6) and must be in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8256062942081028, "g_worst_claim": 1.1753869586520724, "g_content": 2.312989627613741, "g_traj_mean": 1.7642426490783691}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [4498, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 11, 1212, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 374, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 6147, 279, 79040, 4060, 311, 3717, 93089, 389, 279, 32147, 897, 315, 279, 43210, 9329, 11, 1496, 421, 279, 9329, 374, 537, 1483, 369, 279, 9895, 315, 2562, 476, 4808, 304, 279, 17420, 1635, 13, 151645], "pred": "When an asset is discarded, under the Income Tax Act, the scrap value of the asset is reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment allows the assessee to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, even if the asset is not used for the purposes of business or profession in the subsequent years.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5300274234702775, "g_worst_claim": 0.19880000750223795, "g_content": 2.346004363029234, "g_traj_mean": 1.733373999595642}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [4498, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 11, 438, 817, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 1212, 279, 2504, 7286, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 374, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 151645], "pred": "When an asset is discarded, as per the Income Tax Act, under the block concept, the scrap value of the asset is reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.244137831890222, "g_worst_claim": 0.18697023391723633, "g_content": 2.869810665355009, "g_traj_mean": 2.0605814456939697}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.01, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "139", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded. The block concept is followed, where assets of the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are grouped together and considered as a single asset. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, even if it is not used for business or profession in that year and subsequent years.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is governed by section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"When an asset is discarded, the treatment under the Income Tax Act is governed by section 43(6). This section permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. The block concept involves considering all assets within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation as a single asset. Alterations to the value of the block must strictly adhere to the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961. Additionally, the assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening WDV (Written Down Value) of the asset minus the scrap value.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"The treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act involves reducing the scrap value of the asset from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded, according to section 43(6). Any alterations to the value of the block must strictly adhere to the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\"]", "time_sec": 15.249, "generation_time_seconds": 14.3459, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8969, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [4498, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 26702, 553, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is governed by section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.2714036136817626, "g_worst_claim": 1.0955621931287978, "g_content": 2.433671702509341, "g_traj_mean": 1.9528117179870605}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [4498, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 11, 279, 6380, 1212, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 374, 26702, 553, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 568, 1096, 3772, 28690, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 311, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 576, 2504, 7286, 17601, 12831, 678, 11770, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 438, 264, 3175, 9329, 13, 42851, 804, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 1969, 25470, 48453, 311, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 22406, 11, 279, 79040, 4060, 374, 19867, 311, 3717, 93089, 389, 279, 32147, 897, 315, 279, 43210, 9329, 11, 892, 374, 279, 8568, 467, 61971, 320, 35624, 6285, 5162, 8, 315, 279, 9329, 27283, 279, 20843, 897, 13, 151645], "pred": "When an asset is discarded, the treatment under the Income Tax Act is governed by section 43(6). This section permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. The block concept involves considering all assets within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation as a single asset. Alterations to the value of the block must strictly adhere to the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961. Additionally, the assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is the opening WDV (Written Down Value) of the asset minus the scrap value.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.829629632357826, "g_worst_claim": 1.1234832090490006, "g_content": 2.727657195060484, "g_traj_mean": 1.8008805513381958}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.3200437128543854, "g_worst_claim": -0.3200437128543854, "g_content": -0.5062402725219727, "g_traj_mean": -0.28443413972854614}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6380, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 438, 817, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 17601, 17719, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 11, 4092, 311, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 568, 5765, 59986, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 1969, 25470, 48453, 311, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "The treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act involves reducing the scrap value of the asset from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded, according to section 43(6). Any alterations to the value of the block must strictly adhere to the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9912310892942724, "g_worst_claim": 1.90319453