{"id": "140", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that when an asset is discarded by a business but not sold, the Income Tax Act allows the scrap value of the asset to be deducted from the opening work-in-progress (WDV) of such asset in the previous year in which it was discarded. This reduction is taken into account while computing the depreciation expense for the subsequent years. However, any changes made to the value of the block must be made strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of Income Tax Act 1961.", "pred": "If an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. Any alterations to the value of the block have to be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of Income Tax Act, 1961.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "If an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. Any alterations to the value of the block have to be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of Income Tax Act, 1961.", "cot": "[\"When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is governed by section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"Under the Income Tax Act, if an asset is discarded rather than sold, its scrap value can be deducted from the block in the previous year in which the asset was discarded. According to the block concept, all assets within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered a single asset. Any adjustments to the value of this block must strictly adhere to the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. Under the block concept, all the assets falling within the same class and subject to same rate of depreciation are clubbed together and considered as single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block have to be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"If an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. Any alterations to the value of the block have to be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of Income Tax Act, 1961.\"]", "time_sec": 16.017, "generation_time_seconds": 15.0361, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9749, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [4498, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 26702, 553, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is governed by section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.310973268776124, "g_worst_claim": 1.1076971689860027, "g_content": 2.4621273538340693, "g_traj_mean": 1.9766854047775269}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16250, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 421, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 4751, 1091, 6088, 11, 1181, 20843, 897, 646, 387, 95504, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 279, 9329, 572, 43210, 13, 10548, 311, 279, 2504, 7286, 11, 678, 11770, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 525, 6509, 264, 3175, 9329, 13, 5765, 32974, 311, 279, 897, 315, 419, 2504, 1969, 25470, 48453, 311, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "Under the Income Tax Act, if an asset is discarded rather than sold, its scrap value can be deducted from the block in the previous year in which the asset was discarded. According to the block concept, all assets within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered a single asset. Any adjustments to the value of this block must strictly adhere to the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9447262516728159, "g_worst_claim": 0.7613052792019315, "g_content": 2.6404470443725585, "g_traj_mean": 1.773909568786621}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [4498, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 28690, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 311, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 9449, 279, 2504, 7286, 11, 678, 279, 11770, 15679, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 525, 6335, 2721, 3786, 323, 6509, 438, 3175, 9329, 13, 5765, 59986, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 614, 311, 387, 25470, 304, 18353, 448, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. Under the block concept, all the assets falling within the same class and subject to same rate of depreciation are clubbed together and considered as single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block have to be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.6852726821899413, "g_worst_claim": 2.1489271545410156, "g_content": 3.104389105902778, "g_traj_mean": 2.3472092151641846}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [2679, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 5765, 59986, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 614, 311, 387, 25470, 304, 18353, 448, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "If an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. Any alterations to the value of the block have to be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.7358742125279747, "g_worst_claim": 2.3564426715557394, "g_content": 3.1174319231951677, "g_traj_mean": 2.3838319778442383}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 63.64, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "141", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\nAccording to passage 1, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This reduction is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act.\n\nPassage 3 further states that the assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset (i.e., opening WDV of such asset less scrap value) even though such discarded asset is not used for the purposes of business or profession in such year and subsequent years.\n\nTherefore, the treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is to reduce the block value of the asset by the scrap value in the previous year in which it is discarded, and to claim depreciation on the residual value of the asset in the year of discard and subsequent years.", "pred": "When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, its scrap value can be reduced from the block in the previous year as per section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act. This treatment is part of the block concept, where all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are clubbed together and considered as a single asset. Alterations to the value of the block must strictly follow the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, its scrap value can be reduced from the block in the previous year as per section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act. This treatment is part of the block concept, where all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are clubbed together and considered as a single asset. Alterations to the value of the block must strictly follow the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "cot": "[\"When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is governed by section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, its scrap value can be reduced from the block in the previous year as per section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act. This treatment is part of the block concept, where all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are clubbed together and considered as a single asset. Alterations to the value of the block must strictly follow the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"When an asset is discarded by the business and not sold, section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961 permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. Under the block concept, all the assets falling within the same class and subject to same rate of depreciation are clubbed together and considered as a single asset. Any alterations to the value of the block have to be strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\\n\\nThe assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, which is the opening written-down value (WDV) of the asset minus the scrap value, even though the discarded asset is not used for the purposes of business or profession in subsequent years.\", \"The treatment for an asset discarded under the Income Tax Act is as follows:\\n\\n1. **Block Concept Application**: All assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset under the block concept.\\n\\n2. **Reduction in Block Value**: If an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, section 43(6) permits the scrap value of the asset to be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded.\\n\\n3. **Depreciation Calculation**: The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, which is calculated as the opening WDV (Write Down Value) of the asset minus the scrap value. This means the depreciation claim is based on the residual value of the asset, even if it is not used for business or professional purposes in subsequent years.\\n\\nIn summary, the treatment involves reducing the block value by the scrap value when an asset is discarded, and the residual value is used for depreciation purposes.\"]", "time_sec": 23.037, "generation_time_seconds": 22.383, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6457, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [4498, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 26702, 553, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is governed by section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.308849882964351, "g_worst_claim": 1.1386451721191406, "g_content": 2.462390899658203, "g_traj_mean": 1.9749342203140259}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [4498, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 1181, 20843, 897, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 438, 817, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 949, 315, 279, 2504, 7286, 11, 1380, 678, 11770, 15679, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 525, 6335, 2721, 3786, 323, 6509, 438, 264, 3175, 9329, 13, 42851, 804, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 1969, 25470, 1795, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, its scrap value can be reduced from the block in the previous year as per section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act. This treatment is part of the block concept, where all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are clubbed together and considered as a single asset. Alterations to the value of the block must strictly follow the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1906814563348425, "g_worst_claim": 1.7536659240722656, "g_content": 2.763435695482337, "g_traj_mean": 1.981125831604004}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [4498, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 323, 537, 6088, 11, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 28690, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 311, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 9449, 279, 2504, 7286, 11, 678, 279, 11770, 15679, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 525, 6335, 2721, 3786, 323, 6509, 438, 264, 3175, 9329, 13, 5765, 59986, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 614, 311, 387, 25470, 304, 18353, 448, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 382, 785, 79040, 4060, 374, 19867, 311, 3717, 93089, 389, 279, 32147, 897, 315, 1741, 43210, 9329, 11, 892, 374, 279, 8568, 5326, 14875, 897, 320, 17563, 53, 8, 315, 279, 9329, 27283, 279, 20843, 897, 11, 1496, 3498, 279, 43210, 9329, 374, 537, 1483, 369, 279, 9895, 315, 2562, 476, 4808, 304, 17420, 1635, 13, 151645], "pred": "The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, which is the opening written-down value (WDV) of the asset minus the scrap value, even though the discarded asset is not used for the purposes of business or profession in subsequent years.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9903535818427818, "g_worst_claim": 1.2883112980769231, "g_content": 2.5760591634114585, "g_traj_mean": 1.8158621788024902}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6380, 369, 458, 9329, 43210, 1212, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 374, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 4713, 34355, 7323, 95518, 2009, 11770, 15679, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 525, 6509, 438, 264, 3175, 9329, 1212, 279, 2504, 7286, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 6033, 2654, 304, 8362, 5162, 95518, 1416, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 28690, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 311, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 7839, 2758, 7101, 74216, 95518, 576, 79040, 4060, 374, 19867, 311, 3717, 93089, 389, 279, 32147, 897, 315, 279, 43210, 9329, 11, 892, 374, 16588, 438, 279, 8568, 467, 61971, 320, 7985, 6285, 5162, 8, 315, 279, 9329, 27283, 279, 20843, 897, 13, 1096, 3363, 279, 93089, 3717, 374, 3118, 389, 279, 32147, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 11, 1496, 421, 432, 374, 537, 1483, 369, 2562, 476, 6584, 9895, 304, 17420, 1635, 382, 641, 12126, 11, 279, 6380, 17601, 17719, 279, 2504, 897, 553, 279, 20843, 897, 979, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 11, 323, 279, 32147, 897, 374, 1483, 369, 93089, 9895, 13, 151645], "pred": "In summary, the treatment involves reducing the block value by the scrap value when an asset is discarded, and the residual value is used for depreciation purposes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3434162823804348, "g_worst_claim": 0.105285784777473, "g_content": 2.017626011625249, "g_traj_mean": 1.4328042268753052}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.42, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "142", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\nThe scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded, as per Section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act. The block concept applies to all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation, and any alterations to the value of the block must be made in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act. The assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset (i.e., opening WDV of such asset less scrap value) even if the asset is not used for business or professional purposes in that year or subsequent years.\n\nTherefore, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is to reduce the scrap value from the block in the previous year and claim depreciation on the residual value.", "pred": "When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, according to the Income Tax Act, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is permitted under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act. The block concept, which groups assets within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation, allows for alterations to the value of the block to be made in accordance with Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, according to the Income Tax Act, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is permitted under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act. The block concept, which groups assets within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation, allows for alterations to the value of the block to be made in accordance with Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "cot": "[\"When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is governed by section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, according to the Income Tax Act, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is permitted under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act. The block concept, which groups assets within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation, allows for alterations to the value of the block to be made in accordance with Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. Any alterations to the value of the block must be made in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 14.036, "generation_time_seconds": 13.158, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8701, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [4498, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 26702, 553, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is governed by section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.3139128508391207, "g_worst_claim": 1.074639426337348, "g_content": 2.434844804846722, "g_traj_mean": 1.9773484468460083}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [4498, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 4092, 311, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 1096, 6380, 374, 15129, 1212, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 13, 576, 2504, 7286, 11, 892, 5203, 11770, 2878, 279, 1852, 536, 323, 3832, 311, 279, 1852, 4379, 315, 93089, 11, 6147, 369, 59986, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 311, 387, 1865, 304, 18353, 448, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, according to the Income Tax Act, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This treatment is permitted under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act. The block concept, which groups assets within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation, allows for alterations to the value of the block to be made in accordance with Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1214707021023127, "g_worst_claim": 0.6120364325387138, "g_content": 2.6107177734375, "g_traj_mean": 1.951642394065857}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [4498, 458, 9329, 374, 43210, 553, 279, 2562, 714, 537, 6088, 11, 1212, 3772, 220, 19, 18, 7, 21, 8, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 279, 20843, 897, 315, 279, 9329, 646, 387, 11046, 504, 279, 2504, 304, 279, 3681, 1042, 304, 892, 1741, 9329, 374, 43210, 13, 5765, 59986, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2504, 1969, 387, 1865, 304, 18353, 448, 279, 19156, 315, 15585, 16824, 422, 315, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 11, 220, 16, 24, 21, 16, 13, 151645], "pred": "When an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. Any alterations to the value of the block must be made in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1426104760356037, "g_worst_claim": 1.1336545944213867, "g_content": 2.2718549786191997, "g_traj_mean": 1.9434479475021362}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.3209407925605774, "g_worst_claim": -0.3209407925605774, "g_content": -0.5076005935668946, "g_traj_mean": -0.28528717160224915}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.26, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "144", "question": "how to sew a zipper gusset", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can successfully sew a zipper gusset onto your project.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "By following these steps, you can successfully sew a zipper gusset onto your project.", "cot": "[\"To sew a zipper gusset, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Fabric**: Trace the pattern onto the fabric and cut it out. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\\n\\n2. **Pin the Gusset**: Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper, ensuring the right sides are facing each other. The gusset should be placed 1/4 inch away from the center of the zipper.\\n\\n3. **Sew the Gusset**: Change the presser foot to a zipper foot and sew a line near the seam line to secure the position. This will help in aligning the gusset properly.\\n\\n4. **Attach the Gusset Lining**: Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the gusset with the right side facing down. Stitch on the seam line.\\n\\n5. **Flip and Top Stitch**: Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset and top stitch near the seam line. Repeat this step for the other side of the zipper gusset.\\n\\n6. **Secure the Gusset**: Change the presser foot back to a normal foot and stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset to ensure the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.\\n\\n7. **Finish the Gusset**: Lightly press the piping seam allowance at the curve. Place the zipper gusset on the pencil case body, aligning the ends to the center markings. Sew from marking to marking at both ends. Place the lining on top of them with the right side facing down.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can successfully sew a zipper gusset onto your project.\", \"To sew a zipper gusset, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Fabrics**: Trace all pattern pieces onto the fabric and cut them out. Ensure you have the correct measurements for the gusset.\\n\\n2. **Prepare the Zipper**:\\n   - Make a zipper sandwich by placing the lining fabric face up, followed by the zipper, and then the outer fabric right side facing down.\\n   - Align the three edges and sew across the top between the edge of your zipper sandwich and the zipper teeth using a zipper foot.\\n   - Repeat this process for the other side of the zipper.\\n\\n3. **Align the Gusset and Zipper**:\\n   - Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper, ensuring the right sides are facing each other. The gusset should be placed 1/4 inch away from the center of the zipper.\\n   - Change the presser foot to a zipper foot and sew a line near to the seam line to secure the position.\\n\\n4. **Secure the Gusset**:\\n   - Place the zipper gusset lining on top with the right side facing down. Stitch on the seam line.\\n   - Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset and top stitch near the seam line.\\n   - Repeat the process for the other side of the zipper gusset.\\n\\n5. **Finish the Gusset**:\\n   - The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2 inch.\\n   - Change the presser foot back to a normal foot and stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset to ensure the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.\\n\\n6. **Attach the Gusset to the Main Fabric**:\\n   - Flip lightly on the piping seam allowance at the curve.\\n   - Place the zipper gusset on the pencil case body, with the ends aligned to the center markings.\\n   - Sew from marking to marking at both ends.\\n   - Place the lining on top of them with the right side facing down.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can successfully sew a zipper gusset onto your project.\", \"To sew a zipper gusset, you should first place 1 piece of lining fabric face up, then the zipper, and then the outer fabric right side facing down. Line up the three edges. With a zipper foot, sew across the top between the edge of your zipper sandwich and the zipper teeth (closer to the zipper feet). After finishing, the fabric should go all the way to the end of the zipper.\", \"To sew a zipper gusset, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Fabric**: Trace the pattern to the rest of the fabric and cut it out. Measure and mark the necessary positions for the zipper gusset.\\n\\n2. **Assemble the Gusset**: Place the lining fabric face up, then the zipper, and the outer fabric right side facing down. Align the edges and sew a line across the top between the edge of the zipper sandwich and the zipper teeth (closer to the zipper teeth) using a zipper foot. \\n\\n3. **Secure the Position**: Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper, 1/4 inch away from the center, with right sides facing each other. Change the presser foot to a zipper foot and sew a line near the seam line to secure the position.\\n\\n4. **Attach the Lining**: Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the gusset with right sides facing down. Stitch on the seam line. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset and top stitch near the seam line. Repeat this for the other side of the zipper gusset.\\n\\n5. **Secure the Gusset**: Stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.\\n\\n6. **Final Adjustments**: If needed, adjust the width of the zipper gusset to ensure it fits properly. Lightly press the piping seam allowance at the curve. Place the zipper gusset on the pencil case body, aligning the ends to the center markings. Sew from marking to marking at both ends. Place the lining on top of them with right sides facing down and sew as per the previous steps.\\n\\nBy following these detailed steps, you can effectively sew a zipper gusset onto your project.\"]", "time_sec": 44.974, "generation_time_seconds": 43.9862, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9802, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 22352, 264, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 36307, 95518, 27163, 279, 5383, 8630, 279, 13055, 323, 3931, 432, 700, 13, 7405, 264, 2421, 61936, 3143, 279, 1909, 2936, 315, 279, 68761, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 19861, 279, 81379, 746, 95518, 17471, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 311, 279, 68761, 11, 22573, 279, 1290, 11067, 525, 12880, 1817, 1008, 13, 576, 342, 355, 746, 1265, 387, 9099, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 3123, 504, 279, 4126, 315, 279, 68761, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 50, 365, 279, 81379, 746, 95518, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 311, 264, 68761, 4478, 323, 22352, 264, 1555, 3143, 279, 26396, 1555, 311, 9767, 279, 2309, 13, 1096, 686, 1492, 304, 5285, 287, 279, 342, 355, 746, 10277, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 30485, 279, 81379, 746, 444, 5740, 95518, 10771, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 35371, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 342, 355, 746, 448, 279, 1290, 3108, 12880, 1495, 13, 67923, 389, 279, 26396, 1555, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 46808, 323, 6909, 67923, 95518, 40284, 279, 35371, 311, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 1887, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 323, 1909, 32861, 3143, 279, 26396, 1555, 13, 44801, 419, 3019, 369, 279, 1008, 3108, 315, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 49813, 279, 81379, 746, 95518, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 1182, 311, 264, 4622, 4478, 323, 32861, 389, 279, 26396, 40358, 2163, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 311, 5978, 279, 1887, 323, 35371, 13055, 15498, 3786, 28821, 382, 22, 13, 3070, 25664, 279, 81379, 746, 95518, 8658, 398, 3493, 279, 76479, 26396, 40358, 518, 279, 15655, 13, 10771, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 389, 279, 46118, 1142, 2487, 11, 5285, 287, 279, 10335, 311, 279, 4126, 64072, 13, 49213, 504, 34924, 311, 34924, 518, 2176, 10335, 13, 10771, 279, 35371, 389, 1909, 315, 1105, 448, 279, 1290, 3108, 12880, 1495, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 7790, 22352, 264, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 8630, 697, 2390, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can successfully sew a zipper gusset onto your pr