9, 315, 1105, 448, 1290, 11067, 12880, 1495, 323, 22352, 438, 817, 279, 3681, 7354, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 11682, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 13444, 22352, 264, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 8630, 697, 2390, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these detailed steps, you can effectively sew a zipper gusset onto your project.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5382049361163874, "g_worst_claim": 0.21285941050602838, "g_content": 2.2889796170321377, "g_traj_mean": 1.5098017454147339}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "146", "question": "how to sew a zipper gusset", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to sew a zipper gusset:\n\n1. Make a casing in the side seams by stitching the outer edge of the gusset and the back side seam.\n2. Slide the boning right down into the casing.\n3. Push the seam allowance to the back and tack the casing to the lining, if necessary, so it doesn't move.\n4. Make a zipper sandwich by placing one piece of lining fabric face up, followed by the zipper, and then the outer fabric right side facing down.\n5. Sew across the top of the zipper sandwich with a zipper foot, making sure to line up the three edges.\n6. Repeat the process for the other side of the zipper.\n7. Trace all pattern pieces to the remaining fabric and cut them out.\n8. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper, with the right sides facing each other, and sew a line near the seam line to secure the position.\n9. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the zipper gusset, with the right sides facing down, and stitch along the seam line.\n10. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset and top stitch near the seam line.\n11. Repeat the process for the other side of the zipper gusset.\n12. The width of the zipper between the gusset should measure 1/2\".\n13. Change the presser foot back to a normal foot and stitch along the seam allowance around the zipper gusset to attach the main and lining fabrics together nicely.\n\nTherefore, to sew a zipper gusset, you need to make a casing in the side seams, insert the boning, make a zipper sandwich, sew the zipper gusset to the zipper, and attach the lining to the zipper gusset.", "pred": "By following these detailed steps, you can successfully sew a zipper gusset, ensuring it is well-aligned and securely attached to the main gusset and lining fabric.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "By following these detailed steps, you can successfully sew a zipper gusset, ensuring it is well-aligned and securely attached to the main gusset and lining fabric.", "cot": "[\"To sew a zipper gusset, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Fabric**: Trace the pattern onto the fabric and cut it out. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\\n\\n2. **Pin the Gusset**: Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper, ensuring the right sides are facing each other. The gusset should be placed 1/4 inch away from the center of the zipper.\\n\\n3. **Sew the Gusset**: Change the presser foot to a zipper foot and sew a line near the seam line to secure the position. This will help in aligning the gusset properly.\\n\\n4. **Attach the Gusset Lining**: Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the gusset with the right side facing down. Stitch on the seam line.\\n\\n5. **Flip and Top Stitch**: Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset and top stitch near the seam line. Repeat this step for the other side of the zipper gusset.\\n\\n6. **Secure the Gusset**: Change the presser foot back to a normal foot and stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset to ensure the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.\\n\\n7. **Finish the Gusset**: Lightly press the piping seam allowance at the curve. Place the zipper gusset on the pencil case body, aligning the ends to the center markings. Sew from marking to marking at both ends. Place the lining on top of them with the right side facing down.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can successfully sew a zipper gusset onto your project.\", \"To sew a zipper gusset, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Fabric and Zipper**: \\n   - Trace and cut out the pattern for the zipper gusset.\\n   - Cut the lining fabric and the outer fabric according to the pattern.\\n\\n2. **Pin and Align the Zipper**:\\n   - Pin the zipper gusset to the main gusset, ensuring the right sides are facing each other.\\n   - Align the gusset with the main gusset and the zipper teeth, ensuring the gusset is centered.\\n\\n3. **Sew the Gusset**:\\n   - Change the presser foot to a zipper foot.\\n   - Sew a line near the seam line to secure the position of the zipper.\\n\\n4. **Attach the Gusset to the Zipper**:\\n   - Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the main gusset with the right side facing down.\\n   - Stitch on the seam line.\\n\\n5. **Create the Gusset Shape**:\\n   - Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset.\\n   - Top stitch near the seam line.\\n\\n6. **Secure the Gusset**:\\n   - Repeat the sewing process for the other side of the zipper gusset.\\n\\n7. **Finish the Gusset**:\\n   - Measure the width of the zipper in between the gusset to ensure it is 1/2 inch.\\n   - Change the presser foot back to the normal foot and stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset to attach the main and lining fabrics nicely.\\n\\n8. **Final Touches**:\\n   - Flip lightly on the piping seam allowance at the curve.\\n   - Place the zipper gusset on the pencil case body, aligning the ends with the center markings.\\n   - Sew from marking to marking at both ends.\\n\\nBy following these detailed steps, you can successfully sew a zipper gusset, ensuring it is well-aligned and securely attached to the main gusset and lining fabric.\", \"To sew a zipper gusset, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Fabric**: Trace the pattern onto the fabric and cut out the required pieces. This includes the main zipper gusset piece and the lining pieces.\\n\\n2. **Attach the Lining**: Place the lining fabric face up, followed by the zipper, and then the outer fabric face down. Align the three edges and sew across the top between the edge of the zipper sandwich and the zipper teeth using a zipper foot.\\n\\n3. **Secure the Position**: Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4\\\" away from the center) with right sides facing each other.\\n\\n4. **Sew the Gusset**: Change the presser foot to a zipper foot, and sew a line near the seam line to secure the position.\\n\\n5. **Attach the Gusset Lining**: Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the main gusset with right sides facing down. Stitch on the seam line.\\n\\n6. **Flip and Topstitch**: Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset, and topstitch near the seam line. Repeat this process for the other side of the zipper gusset.\\n\\n7. **Stitch Seam Allowance**: Change the presser foot back to a normal foot, and stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset, ensuring the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.\\n\\n8. **Final Touches**:\\n   - **Piping Seams**: If necessary, lightly stitch the piping seam allowance at the curve.\\n   - **Placement and Sewing**: Place the zipper gusset on the pencil case body, aligning the ends to the center markings. Sew from marking to marking at both ends.\\n   - **Final Layers**: Place the lining on top of them with right sides facing down, ensuring proper alignment.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can successfully sew a zipper gusset, which adds functionality and a unique design element to your project.\", \"To sew a zipper gusset, you need to:\\n1. Trace all pattern pieces to the rest of the fabric and cut.\\n2. Make a few stitches near the top stop of the zipper.\\n3. Pin the zipper gusset to the zipper (1/4\\\" away from the center) with right side facing each other.\\n4. Change the presser foot to a zipper foot and sew a line near the seam line to secure the position.\\n5. Place the zipper gusset lining on top of the gusset with right side facing down and stitch on the seam line.\\n6. Flip the lining to the bottom of the main zipper gusset and top stitch near the seam line.\\n7. Repeat sewing on the other side of the zipper gusset.\\n8. The width of the zipper in between the gusset should measure 1/2\\\". Change the presser foot back to a normal foot and stitch on the seam allowance around the zipper gusset so that the main and lining fabric attach together nicely.\"]", "time_sec": 47.852, "generation_time_seconds": 46.829, "selection_time_seconds": 1.015, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 22352, 264, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 36307, 95518, 27163, 279, 5383, 8630, 279, 13055, 323, 3931, 432, 700, 13, 7405, 264, 2421, 61936, 3143, 279, 1909, 2936, 315, 279, 68761, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 19861, 279, 81379, 746, 95518, 17471, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 311, 279, 68761, 11, 22573, 279, 1290, 11067, 525, 12880, 1817, 1008, 13, 576, 342, 355, 746, 1265, 387, 9099, 220, 16, 14, 19, 17122, 3123, 504, 279, 4126, 315, 279, 68761, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 50, 365, 279, 81379, 746, 95518, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 311, 264, 68761, 4478, 323, 22352, 264, 1555, 3143, 279, 26396, 1555, 311, 9767, 279, 2309, 13, 1096, 686, 1492, 304, 5285, 287, 279, 342, 355, 746, 10277, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 30485, 279, 81379, 746, 444, 5740, 95518, 10771, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 35371, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 342, 355, 746, 448, 279, 1290, 3108, 12880, 1495, 13, 67923, 389, 279, 26396, 1555, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 46808, 323, 6909, 67923, 95518, 40284, 279, 35371, 311, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 1887, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 323, 1909, 32861, 3143, 279, 26396, 1555, 13, 44801, 419, 3019, 369, 279, 1008, 3108, 315, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 49813, 279, 81379, 746, 95518, 10388, 279, 3493, 261, 4478, 1182, 311, 264, 4622, 4478, 323, 32861, 389, 279, 26396, 40358, 2163, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 311, 5978, 279, 1887, 323, 35371, 13055, 15498, 3786, 28821, 382, 22, 13, 3070, 25664, 279, 81379, 746, 95518, 8658, 398, 3493, 279, 76479, 26396, 40358, 518, 279, 15655, 13, 10771, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 389, 279, 46118, 1142, 2487, 11, 5285, 287, 279, 10335, 311, 279, 4126, 64072, 13, 49213, 504, 34924, 311, 34924, 518, 2176, 10335, 13, 10771, 279, 35371, 389, 1909, 315, 1105, 448, 279, 1290, 3108, 12880, 1495, 38