{"id": "158", "question": "how to factory reset a htc one vx", "gt": "To factory reset an HTC One VX, you can follow the steps mentioned in passage 3. Slide the Notifications panel open, tap on Storage, then Factory data reset, and finally tap on Reset phone and Erase everything.", "pred": "To factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Notifications panel.\n2. Tap on Storage Factory data reset.\n3. Tap on Reset phone and then Erase everything.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Notifications panel.\n2. Tap on Storage Factory data reset.\n3. Tap on Reset phone and then Erase everything.", "cot": "[\"To factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open, and then tap.\\n2. Tap Storage Factory data reset.\\n3. Tap Reset phone, and then tap Erase everything.\\n\\nAnswer: To factory reset an HTC One VX, slide the Notifications panel open, tap Storage Factory data reset, tap Reset phone, and then tap Erase everything.\", \"To factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open and tap on the settings icon.\\n2. Tap on Storage Factory data reset.\\n3. Tap on Reset phone and then tap on Erase everything.\\n\\nIt's recommended to back up any important data and files before proceeding with a factory reset.\", \"To factory reset an HTC One VX, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Open the Notifications panel and tap on the option to access storage.\\n2. Tap on \\\"Factory Data Reset.\\\"\\n3. Tap \\\"Reset phone\\\" and then confirm by tapping \\\"Erase everything.\\\"\\n\\nThese steps will initiate the factory reset process on your HTC One VX.\", \"To factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Open the Notifications panel.\\n2. Tap on Storage Factory data reset.\\n3. Tap on Reset phone and then Erase everything.\"]", "time_sec": 13.708, "generation_time_seconds": 12.6889, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0137, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 8633, 7585, 458, 48267, 3776, 78177, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 43364, 279, 52938, 6945, 1787, 11, 323, 1221, 15239, 624, 17, 13, 36134, 14693, 16937, 821, 7585, 624, 18, 13, 36134, 16932, 4540, 11, 323, 1221, 15239, 9740, 519, 4297, 382, 16141, 25, 2014, 8633, 7585, 458, 48267, 3776, 78177, 11, 14983, 279, 52938, 6945, 1787, 11, 15239, 14693, 16937, 821, 7585, 11, 15239, 16932, 4540, 11, 323, 1221, 15239, 9740, 519, 4297, 13, 151645], "pred": "To factory reset an HTC One VX, slide the Notifications panel open, tap Storage Factory data reset, tap Reset phone, and then tap Erase everything.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1655104787028454, "g_worst_claim": -0.041404839605093, "g_content": 1.189420740655128, "g_traj_mean": 1.0546542406082153}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 8633, 7585, 264, 48267, 3776, 78177, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 43364, 279, 52938, 6945, 1787, 323, 15239, 389, 279, 5003, 4603, 624, 17, 13, 36134, 389, 14693, 16937, 821, 7585, 624, 18, 13, 36134, 389, 16932, 4540, 323, 1221, 15239, 389, 9740, 519, 4297, 382, 2132, 594, 11102, 311, 1182, 705, 894, 2989, 821, 323, 3542, 1573, 38447, 448, 264, 8633, 7585, 13, 151645], "pred": "To factory reset a HTC One VX, follow these steps:\n\n1. Slide the Notifications panel open and tap on the settings icon.\n2. Tap on Storage Factory data reset.\n3. Tap on Reset phone and then tap on Erase everything.\n\nIt's recommended to back up any important data and files before proceeding with a factory reset.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.534451489095335, "g_worst_claim": 0.3188183705012004, "g_content": 1.6076089011298285, "g_traj_mean": 1.225084900856018}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 8633, 7585, 458, 48267, 3776, 78177, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16