412, 821, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can create a clear and effective graph to represent your research data.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.5073238097167975, "g_worst_claim": 0.007178205251693726, "g_content": 0.6765813654119318, "g_traj_mean": 0.46836280822753906}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 264, 4771, 369, 697, 3412, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 28301, 1437, 279, 3990, 315, 12165, 95518, 29901, 279, 943, 315, 4771, 429, 1850, 27976, 697, 821, 13, 7718, 4494, 2924, 3619, 38999, 11, 1555, 38999, 11, 323, 4349, 26131, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 47504, 2885, 95518, 48995, 279, 821, 498, 1184, 311, 4009, 304, 279, 4771, 13, 29279, 279, 821, 374, 13382, 323, 9760, 311, 697, 3412, 4755, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 3851, 279, 12165, 95518, 20678, 697, 4771, 264, 2797, 323, 52844, 2265, 429, 14758, 1128, 279, 4771, 374, 911, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 35, 24308, 279, 24613, 95518, 98881, 389, 279, 5452, 369, 279, 379, 35321, 11, 22573, 432, 29257, 10868, 279, 2088, 315, 2750, 304, 697, 821, 13, 27196, 279, 5452, 438, 5871, 311, 5648, 49871, 4152, 311, 1602, 79053, 14507, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 4021, 279, 12165, 95518, 5443, 4771, 5567, 476, 264, 4771, 287, 5392, 311, 1855, 279, 5042, 4771, 13, 7405, 2704, 1817, 3619, 594, 2608, 374, 21117, 349, 311, 279, 1379, 315, 279, 5582, 432, 10868, 13, 1416, 1667, 264, 3619, 4771, 11, 1894, 279, 15904, 311, 912, 9124, 14303, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 19432, 323, 8550, 482, 95518, 4248, 697, 4771, 369, 31273, 323, 13403, 13, 27196, 894, 5424, 429, 525, 24416, 476, 37209, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 1855, 264, 4771, 429, 13444, 91506, 697, 3412, 14613, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can create a graph that effectively communicates your research findings.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.5872481551408997, "g_worst_claim": -0.29561829566955566, "g_content": 0.8818154124032079, "g_traj_mean": 0.5862981677055359}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 1995, 3897, 1447, 16, 13, 1446, 1265, 1156, 6530, 678, 279, 821, 9760, 311, 697, 3412, 624, 17, 13, 98881, 389, 279, 943, 315, 4771, 498, 1366, 311, 1855, 13, 576, 21085, 33845, 429, 264, 3619, 4771, 374, 5390, 369, 9027, 35495, 4221, 11059, 11, 1741, 438, 279, 3311, 315, 52858, 2337, 2155, 3951, 476, 5461, 36432, 304, 2155, 5302, 624, 18, 13, 1416, 498, 10279, 311, 990, 264, 3619, 4771, 11, 2265, 697, 4771, 323, 8253, 279, 2608, 315, 279, 4771, 3118, 389, 279, 821, 498, 614, 14548, 624, 19, 13, 7405, 2704, 1817, 3619, 594, 2608, 10868, 279, 1379, 315, 279, 5582, 432, 33210, 311, 13, 1096, 686, 3410, 264, 2797, 323, 9124, 13042, 315, 697, 821, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 1855, 264, 3619, 4771, 429, 13444, 10868, 697, 3412, 821, 323, 8609, 304, 26297, 2155, 11059, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can create a bar graph that effectively represents your research data and helps in comparing different categories.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8906402563683901, "g_worst_claim": 0.2498835650357333, "g_content": 1.258212407430013, "g_traj_mean": 0.9053166508674622}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.2812748849391937, "g_worst_claim": -0.2812748849391937, "g_content": -0.4466694355010986, "g_traj_mean": -0.25004488229751587}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 12.83, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "170", "question": "how to soften sugar", "gt": "To soften brown sugar, you can place it in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Then put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil and cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. To make hardened granulated sugar soft again, preheat an oven to its lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove the sugar from its package and put it in an ovenproof container. Place it in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon and if it starts to fall apart, turn the oven off and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.", "pred": "To soften sugar, you can follow the method described in passage 2. Preheat your oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees). Remove the sugar from its packaging and place it in an ovenproof container that can hold the sugar. Put the container in the warm oven for about 15 minutes. After 15 minutes, tap the sugar with a spoon. If the sugar starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. It's important to store granulated sugar in an airtight container and keep it in a cool, dry location to prevent it from becoming moist and developing lumps.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To soften sugar, you can follow the method described in passage 2. Preheat your oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees). Remove the sugar from its packaging and place it in an ovenproof container that can hold the sugar. Put the container in the warm oven for about 15 minutes. After 15 minutes, tap the sugar with a spoon. If the sugar starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. It's important to store granulated sugar in an airtight container and keep it in a cool, dry location to prevent it from becoming moist and developing lumps.", "cot": "[\"To soften sugar, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **For Brown Sugar:**\\n   - Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar.\\n   - Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil.\\n   - Cover tightly.\\n   - Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days.\\n\\n2. **For Granulated Sugar:**\\n   - Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees.\\n   - Remove the sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar.\\n   - Place the sugar in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes.\\n   - Tap the sugar with a spoon.\\n   - If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out.\\n   - Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.\\n   - Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\\n   - When it gets moist, it develops lumps.\\n\\nBy following these methods, you can effectively soften both brown and granulated sugar.\", \"To soften sugar, you can follow the method described in passage 2. Preheat your oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees). Remove the sugar from its packaging and place it in an ovenproof container that can hold the sugar. Put the container in the warm oven for about 15 minutes. After 15 minutes, tap the sugar with a spoon. If the sugar starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. It's important to store granulated sugar in an airtight container and keep it in a cool, dry location to prevent it from becoming moist and developing lumps.\", \"Based on the provided passages, here are ways to soften sugar:\\n\\n1. For brown sugar: Keep it sealed in an airtight container, limit air exposure, and pack it into the smallest container possible.\\n2. For granulated sugar: Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees), place the sugar in an ovenproof container, and warm it for approximately 15 minutes. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.\\n\\nAnswer: To soften sugar, you can either keep brown sugar sealed in an airtight container with limited air exposure and packed into the smallest container possible, or for granulated sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees), place the sugar in an ovenproof container, and warm it for approximately 15 minutes. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.\", \"To soften sugar, you can use one of the following methods:\\n\\n1. For brown sugar:\\n   - Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over it.\\n   - Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil.\\n   - Cover tightly.\\n   - Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days.\\n\\n2. For granulated sugar:\\n   - Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, around 150-200 degrees.\\n   - Remove the sugar from the package and place it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar.\\n   - Place the sugar in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes.\\n   - Tap the sugar with a spoon.\\n   - If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out.\\n   - Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.\\n   - Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\\n   - When it gets moist, it will develop lumps.\"]", "time_sec": 31.885, "generation_time_seconds": 30.9264, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9526, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 79945, 13163, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2461, 10471, 30919, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 10771, 13876, 13163, 304, 264, 12188, 5476, 448, 264, 2613, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 476, 46399, 916, 279, 13163, 624, 256, 481, 10224, 264, 40269, 5567, 42613, 476, 25859, 7989, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 12188, 14, 98957, 624, 256, 481, 17757, 38969, 624, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 40269, 5567, 42613, 304, 264, 5625, 315, 2849, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 2461, 26524, 7757, 30919, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 11, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 624, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 13163, 504, 279, 6328, 323, 2182, 432, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 429, 686, 3331, 279, 13163, 624, 256, 481, 10771, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 8205, 23387, 369, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 256, 481, 36134, 279, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 624, 256, 481, 1416, 432, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 5274, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 624, 256, 481, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 624, 256, 481, 9129, 390, 13120, 388, 13163, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 320, 1921, 279, 44944, 4292, 256, 481, 3197, 432, 5221, 20507, 11, 432, 38571, 326, 11793, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 5413, 11, 498, 646, 13444, 79945, 2176, 13876, 323, 15732, 7757, 13163, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these methods, you can effectively soften both brown and granulated sugar.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4476342447488233, "g_worst_claim": 0.15650975704193115, "g_content": 2.1269850583420586, "g_traj_mean": 1.3996949195861816}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 79945, 13163, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 279, 1714, 7481, 304, 21085, 220, 17, 13, 4968, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 320, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 568, 10783, 279, 13163, 504, 1181, 23189, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 429, 646, 3331, 279, 13163, 13, 10224, 279, 5476, 304, 279, 8205, 23387, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 4636, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 11, 15239, 279, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 13, 1416, 279, 13163, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 5274, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 13, 1084, 594, 2989, 311, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 323, 2506, 432, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 10454, 20507, 323, 11220, 326, 11793, 13, 151645], "pred": "To soften sugar, you can follow the method described in passage 2. Preheat your oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees). Remove the sugar from its packaging and place it in an ovenproof container that can hold the sugar. Put the container in the warm oven for about 15 minutes. After 15 minutes, tap the sugar with a spoon. If the sugar starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. It's important to store granulated sugar in an airtight container and keep it in a cool, dry location to prevent it from becoming moist and developing lumps.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2929754662785475, "g_worst_claim": 0.13012165824572244, "g_content": 1.9714888254801433, "g_traj_mean": 1.2514663934707642}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 1588, 525, 5510, 311, 79945, 13163, 1447, 16, 13, 1752, 13876, 13163, 25, 13655, 432, 19046, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 11, 3930, 3720, 14338, 11, 323, 3769, 432, 1119, 279, 24632, 5476, 3204, 624, 17, 13, 1752, 15732, 7757, 13163, 25, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 320, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 701, 1992, 279, 13163, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 11, 323, 8205, 432, 369, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 1416, 432, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 5274, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 13, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 382, 16141, 25, 2014, 79945, 13163, 11, 498, 646, 2987, 2506, 13876, 13163, 19046, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 448, 7199, 3720, 14338, 323, 19375, 1119, 279, 24632, 5476, 3204, 11, 476, 369, 15732, 7757, 13163, 11, 855, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 320, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 701, 1992, 279, 13163, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 11, 323, 8205, 432, 369, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 1416, 432, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 5274, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 13, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 13, 151645], "pred": "To soften sugar, you can either keep brown sugar sealed in an airtight container with limited air exposure and packed into the smallest container possible, or for granulated sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees), place the sugar in an ovenproof container, and warm it for approximately 15 minutes. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9545195197098361, "g_worst_claim": -0.10716274380683899, "g_content": 1.2524490356445312, "g_traj_mean": 0.7860385775566101}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 79945, 13163, 11, 498, 646, 990, 825, 315, 279, 2701, 5413, 1447, 16, 13, 1752, 13876, 13163, 510, 256, 481, 10771, 13876, 13163, 304, 264, 12188, 5476, 448, 264, 2613, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 476, 46399, 916, 432, 624, 256, 481, 10224, 264, 40269, 5567, 42613, 476, 25859, 7989, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 12188, 14, 98957, 624, 256, 481, 17757, 38969, 624, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 40269, 5567, 42613, 304, 264, 5625, 315, 2849, 382, 17, 13, 1752, 15732, 7757, 13163, 510, 256, 481, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 11, 2163, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 624, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 13163, 504, 279, 6328, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 429, 686, 3331, 279, 13163, 624, 256, 481, 10771, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 8205, 23387, 369, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 256, 481, 36134, 279, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 624, 256, 481, 1416, 432, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 5274, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 624, 256, 481, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 624, 256, 481, 9129, 390, 13120, 388, 13163, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 320, 1921, 279, 44944, 4292, 256, 481, 3197, 432, 5221, 20507, 11, 432, 686, 2225, 326, 11793, 13, 151645], "pred": "2. For granulated sugar:\n   - Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, around 150-200 degrees.\n   - Remove the sugar from the package and place it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar.\n   - Place the sugar in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes.\n   - Tap the sugar with a spoon.\n   - If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out.\n   - Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.\n   - Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\n   - When it gets moist, it will develop lumps.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5080629091521656, "g_worst_claim": -0.04188603535294533, "g_content": 2.127544071363366, "g_traj_mean": 1.4178531169891357}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 63.58, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "172", "question": "how to soften sugar", "gt": "To soften sugar, place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove damp paper towel in a couple of days. Alternatively, preheat oven to lowest temperature (150-200 degrees) and remove sugar from package. Put in an ovenproof container and place in the warm oven for 15 minutes. Tap sugar with a spoon and if it starts to fall apart, turn oven off and leave sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location.", "pred": "To soften sugar, follow these steps: For brown sugar, place it in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar, put a damp paper towel or napkin on top, and cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. For granulated sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees), place the sugar in an ovenproof container that holds the sugar, and leave it in the oven for about 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon; if it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container. Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location and avoid the refrigerator. When it gets moist, it develops lumps.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To soften sugar, follow these steps: For brown sugar, place it in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar, put a damp paper towel or napkin on top, and cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. For granulated sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees), place the sugar in an ovenproof container that holds the sugar, and leave it in the oven for about 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon; if it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container. Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location and avoid the refrigerator. When it gets moist, it develops lumps.", "cot": "[\"To soften sugar, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **For Brown Sugar:**\\n   - Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar.\\n   - Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil.\\n   - Cover tightly.\\n   - Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days.\\n\\n2. **For Granulated Sugar:**\\n   - Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees.\\n   - Remove the sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar.\\n   - Place the sugar in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes.\\n   - Tap the sugar with a spoon.\\n   - If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out.\\n   - Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.\\n   - Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\\n   - When it gets moist, it develops lumps.\\n\\nBy following these methods, you can effectively soften both brown and granulated sugar.\", \"Answer: To soften sugar, you can preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees), place the sugar in an ovenproof container, and leave it in the warm oven for about 15 minutes. After tapping the sugar with a spoon, if it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and let the sugar dry out for an hour or two. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location.\", \"To soften sugar, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. For brown sugar: Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove damp paper towel in a couple of days.\\n\\n2. For granulated sugar: Preheat oven to lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove sugar from the package and put in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Place in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn oven off and leave sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out.\\n\\nAlways store granulated sugar in an airtight container and store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\", \"To soften sugar, follow these steps: For brown sugar, place it in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar, put a damp paper towel or napkin on top, and cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. For granulated sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees), place the sugar in an ovenproof container that holds the sugar, and leave it in the oven for about 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon; if it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container. Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location and avoid the refrigerator. When it gets moist, it develops lumps.\"]", "time_sec": 27.115, "generation_time_seconds": 26.049, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0604, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 79945, 13163, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2461, 10471, 30919, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 10771, 13876, 13163, 304, 264, 12188, 5476, 448, 264, 2613, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 476, 46399, 916, 279, 13163, 624, 256, 481, 10224, 264, 40269, 5567, 42613, 476, 25859, 7989, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 12188, 14, 98957, 624, 256, 481, 17757, 38969, 624, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 40269, 5567, 42613, 304, 264, 5625, 315, 2849, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 2461, 26524, 7757, 30919, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 11, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 624, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 13163, 504, 279, 6328, 323, 2182, 432, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 429, 686, 3331, 279, 13163, 624, 256, 481, 10771, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 8205, 23387, 369, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 256, 481, 36134, 279, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 624, 256, 481, 1416, 432, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 5274, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 624, 256, 481, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 624, 256, 481, 9129, 390, 13120, 388, 13163, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 320, 1921, 279, 44944, 4292, 256, 481, 3197, 432, 5221, 20507, 11, 432, 38571, 326, 11793, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 5413, 11, 498, 646, 13444, 79945, 2176, 13876, 323, 15732, 7757, 13163, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these methods, you can effectively soften both brown and granulated sugar.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.468147799062453, "g_worst_claim": 0.14960312843322754, "g_content": 2.1541834565782056, "g_traj_mean": 1.4078259468078613}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 2014, 79945, 13163, 11, 498, 646, 855, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 320, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 701, 1992, 279, 13163, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 11, 323, 5274, 432, 304, 279, 8205, 23387, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 4636, 52628, 279, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 11, 421, 432, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 1077, 279, 13163, 9058, 700, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 13, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 323, 390, 13120, 388, 13163, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 13, 151645], "pred": "To soften sugar, you can preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees), place the sugar in an ovenproof container, and leave it in the warm oven for about 15 minutes. After tapping the sugar with a spoon, if it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and let the sugar dry out for an hour or two. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5018980400902882, "g_worst_claim": 0.6930257252284459, "g_content": 2.294933864048549, "g_traj_mean": 1.384785532951355}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 79945, 13163, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1752, 13876, 13163, 25, 10771, 13876, 13163, 304, 264, 12188, 5476, 448, 264, 2613, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 476, 46399, 916, 279, 13163, 13, 10224, 264, 40269, 5567, 42613, 476, 25859, 7989, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 12188, 14, 98957, 13, 17757, 38969, 13, 10783, 40269, 5567, 42613, 304, 264, 5625, 315, 2849, 382, 17, 13, 1752, 15732, 7757, 13163, 25, 4968, 19963, 23387, 311, 15457, 9315, 11, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 13, 10783, 13163, 504, 279, 6328, 323, 2182, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 429, 686, 3331, 279, 13163, 13, 10771, 304, 279, 8205, 23387, 369, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 36134, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 13, 1416, 432, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 23387, 1007, 323, 5274, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 382, 37095, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 323, 3553, 390, 13120, 388, 13163, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 320, 1921, 279, 44944, 568, 151645], "pred": "Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8587644555455163, "g_worst_claim": 0.2358749508857727, "g_content": 2.451859238568474, "g_traj_mean": 1.7943999767303467}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 79945, 13163, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 25, 1752, 13876, 13163, 11, 1992, 432, 304, 264, 12188, 5476, 448, 264, 2613, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 476, 46399, 916, 279, 13163, 11, 2182, 264, 40269, 5567, 42613, 476, 25859, 7989, 389, 1909, 11, 323, 3421, 38969, 13, 10783, 279, 40269, 5567, 42613, 304, 264, 5625, 315, 2849, 13, 1752, 15732, 7757, 13163, 11, 855, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 320, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 701, 1992, 279, 13163, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 429, 9982, 279, 13163, 11, 323, 5274, 432, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 36134, 279, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 26, 421, 432, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 5274, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 13, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 13, 9129, 390, 13120, 388, 13163, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 323, 5648, 279, 44944, 13, 3197, 432, 5221, 20507, 11, 432, 38571, 326, 11793, 13, 151645], "pred": "To soften sugar, follow these steps: For brown sugar, place it in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar, put a damp paper towel or napkin on top, and cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days. For granulated sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees), place the sugar in an ovenproof container that holds the sugar, and leave it in the oven for about 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon; if it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container. Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location and avoid the refrigerator. When it gets moist, it develops lumps.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6492731786164219, "g_worst_claim": 0.36107892990112306, "g_content": 2.3209577560424806, "g_traj_mean": 1.5674197673797607}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 85.53, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "173", "question": "how to soften sugar", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to soften sugar:\n\n1. To soften brown sugar, place it in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar, and cover tightly. Remove the damp paper towel after a couple of days. (Passage 1)\n2. To soften hardened granulated sugar, preheat the oven to a low temperature (150-200°F), remove the sugar from its package, and place it in an ovenproof container. Warm the sugar in the oven for about 15 minutes, then tap it with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, leave it in the oven for a longer period of time to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container. (Passage 2)\n3. To keep brown sugar soft, pack it into the smallest container possible to minimize air exposure. (Passage 3)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide information on how to soften other types of sugar, such as confectioner's sugar.", "pred": "To soften sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees) and place the sugar in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Put the container in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon to help it soften. If the sugar starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To soften sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees) and place the sugar in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Put the container in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon to help it soften. If the sugar starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location.", "cot": "[\"To soften sugar, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **For Brown Sugar:**\\n   - Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar.\\n   - Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil.\\n   - Cover tightly.\\n   - Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days.\\n\\n2. **For Granulated Sugar:**\\n   - Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees.\\n   - Remove the sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar.\\n   - Place the sugar in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes.\\n   - Tap the sugar with a spoon.\\n   - If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out.\\n   - Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.\\n   - Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\\n   - When it gets moist, it develops lumps.\\n\\nBy following these methods, you can effectively soften both brown and granulated sugar.\", \"To soften sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees) and place the sugar in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Put the container in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon to help it soften. If the sugar starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location.\", \"To soften sugar, follow the steps mentioned in the passage:\\n\\n1. For brown sugar: Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove damp paper towel in a couple of days.\\n\\n2. For granulated sugar: Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Place in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container. Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator). When it gets moist, it develops lumps.\", \"To soften sugar, you can place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove damp paper towel in a couple of days.\"]", "time_sec": 23.615, "generation_time_seconds": 22.7028, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9045, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 79945, 13163, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2461, 10471, 30919, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 10771, 13876, 13163, 304, 264, 12188, 5476, 448, 264, 2613, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 476, 46399, 916, 279, 13163, 624, 256, 481, 10224, 264, 40269, 5567, 42613, 476, 25859, 7989, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 12188, 14, 98957, 624, 256, 481, 17757, 38969, 624, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 40269, 5567, 42613, 304, 264, 5625, 315, 2849, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 2461, 26524, 7757, 30919, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 11, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 624, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 13163, 504, 279, 6328, 323, 2182, 432, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 429, 686, 3331, 279, 13163, 624, 256, 481, 10771, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 8205, 23387, 369, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 256, 481, 36134, 279, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 624, 256, 481, 1416, 432, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 5274, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 624, 256, 481, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 624, 256, 481, 9129, 390, 13120, 388, 13163, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 320, 1921, 279, 44944, 4292, 256, 481, 3197, 432, 5221, 20507, 11, 432, 38571, 326, 11793, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 5413, 11, 498, 646, 13444, 79945, 2176, 13876, 323, 15732, 7757, 13163, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these methods, you can effectively soften both brown and granulated sugar.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4234905753860856, "g_worst_claim": -0.015479016304016113, "g_content": 2.135902011517397, "g_traj_mean": 1.393198847770691}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 79945, 13163, 11, 855, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 320, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 8, 323, 1992, 279, 13163, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 429, 686, 3331, 279, 13163, 13, 10224, 279, 5476, 304, 279, 8205, 23387, 369, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 36134, 279, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 311, 1492, 432, 79945, 13, 1416, 279, 13163, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 5274, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 13, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 323, 390, 13120, 388, 13163, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 13, 151645], "pred": "To soften sugar, preheat the oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees) and place the sugar in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Put the container in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap the sugar with a spoon to help it soften. If the sugar starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.573305880816984, "g_worst_claim": 1.166452407836914, "g_content": 2.312689208984375, "g_traj_mean": 1.4539285898208618}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 79945, 13163, 11, 1795, 279, 7354, 9733, 304, 279, 21085, 1447, 16, 13, 1752, 13876, 13163, 25, 10771, 13876, 13163, 304, 264, 12188, 5476, 448, 264, 2613, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 476, 46399, 916, 279, 13163, 13, 10224, 264, 40269, 5567, 42613, 476, 25859, 7989, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 12188, 14, 98957, 13, 17757, 38969, 13, 10783, 40269, 5567, 42613, 304, 264, 5625, 315, 2849, 382, 17, 13, 1752, 15732, 7757, 13163, 25, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 11, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 13, 10783, 13163, 504, 279, 6328, 323, 2182, 432, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 429, 686, 3331, 279, 13163, 13, 10771, 304, 279, 8205, 23387, 369, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 36134, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 13, 1416, 432, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 5274, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 13, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 13, 9129, 390, 13120, 388, 13163, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 320, 1921, 279, 44944, 568, 3197, 432, 5221, 20507, 11, 432, 38571, 326, 11793, 13, 151645], "pred": "2. For granulated sugar: Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees. Remove sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar. Place in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. Tap sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container. Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator). When it gets moist, it develops lumps.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8872007259530388, "g_worst_claim": 0.03592163750103542, "g_content": 2.4331197214650584, "g_traj_mean": 1.7570093870162964}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 79945, 13163, 11, 498, 646, 1992, 13876, 13163, 304, 264, 12188, 5476, 448, 264, 2613, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 476, 46399, 916, 279, 13163, 13, 10224, 264, 40269, 5567, 42613, 476, 25859, 7989, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 12188, 14, 98957, 13, 17757, 38969, 13, 10783, 40269, 5567, 42613, 304, 264, 5625, 315, 2849, 13, 151645], "pred": "To soften sugar, you can place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove damp paper towel in a couple of days.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.222354847012144, "g_worst_claim": 1.8960976600646973, "g_content": 2.6652442669046335, "g_traj_mean": 2.1122562885284424}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.68, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.3, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "175", "question": "how to soften sugar", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to soften sugar:\n\n1. Place brown sugar in an airtight container with a damp paper towel or napkin on top. Cover tightly and let it sit for a couple of days. Remove the damp paper towel, and the sugar should be soft. (Passage 1)\n2. Preheat the oven to a low temperature (150-200 degrees), place hardened granulated sugar in an ovenproof container, and tap it with a spoon after 15 minutes. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave it in for an hour or two to dry out completely. Store granulated sugar in an airtight container. (Passage 2)\n3. Keep brown sugar soft by storing it in an airtight container with minimal air space between the sugar and the lid. Pack the sugar into the smallest container possible. (Passage 3)", "pred": "To soften sugar, it is recommended to place the sugar in an ovenproof container and warm it in the oven at a low temperature (150-200 degrees) for approximately 15 minutes. After warming, tap the sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. It is important to store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location, away from refrigerators.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To soften sugar, it is recommended to place the sugar in an ovenproof container and warm it in the oven at a low temperature (150-200 degrees) for approximately 15 minutes. After warming, tap the sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. It is important to store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location, away from refrigerators.", "cot": "[\"To soften sugar, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **For Brown Sugar:**\\n   - Place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar.\\n   - Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil.\\n   - Cover tightly.\\n   - Remove the damp paper towel in a couple of days.\\n\\n2. **For Granulated Sugar:**\\n   - Preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, 150-200 degrees.\\n   - Remove the sugar from the package and put it in an ovenproof container that will hold the sugar.\\n   - Place the sugar in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes.\\n   - Tap the sugar with a spoon.\\n   - If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out.\\n   - Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container.\\n   - Store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\\n   - When it gets moist, it develops lumps.\\n\\nBy following these methods, you can effectively soften both brown and granulated sugar.\", \"To soften sugar, you can preheat your oven to the lowest temperature (150-200 degrees) and place the sugar in an ovenproof container. Leave it in the oven for approximately 15 minutes, and then tap the sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and store confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location (not the refrigerator).\", \"To soften sugar, you can preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, around 150-200 degrees. Remove the sugar from its packaging and place it in an ovenproof container that fits the sugar snugly. Put the container in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. If the sugar starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location. When the sugar gets moist, it will develop lumps.\", \"To soften sugar, it is recommended to place the sugar in an ovenproof container and warm it in the oven at a low temperature (150-200 degrees) for approximately 15 minutes. After warming, tap the sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. It is important to store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location, away from refrigerators.\"]", "time_sec": 23.761, "generation_time_seconds": 23.021, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7354, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 79945, 13163, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2461, 10471, 30919, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 10771, 13876, 13163, 304, 264, 12188, 5476, 448, 264, 2613, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 476, 46399, 916, 279, 13163, 624, 256, 481, 10224, 264, 40269, 5567, 42613, 476, 25859, 7989, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 12188, 14, 98957, 624, 256, 481, 17757, 38969, 624, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 40269, 5567, 42613, 304, 264, 5625, 315, 2849, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 2461, 26524, 7757, 30919, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 279, 15457, 9315, 11, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 624, 256, 481, 10783, 279, 13163, 504, 279, 6328, 323, 2182, 432, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 429, 686, 3331, 279, 13163, 624, 256, 481, 10771, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 8205, 23387, 369, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 256, 481, 36134, 279, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 624, 256, 481, 1416, 432, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 5274, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 624, 256, 481, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 624, 256, 481, 9129, 390, 13120, 388, 13163, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 320, 1921, 279, 44944, 4292, 256, 481, 3197, 432, 5221, 20507, 11, 432, 38571, 326, 11793, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 5413, 11, 498, 646, 1344