20, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 1416, 279, 13163, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 5274, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 13, 23240, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 323, 390, 13120, 388, 13163, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 13, 3197, 279, 13163, 5221, 20507, 11, 432, 686, 2225, 326, 11793, 13, 151645], "pred": "To soften sugar, you can preheat the oven to the lowest temperature, around 150-200 degrees. Remove the sugar from its packaging and place it in an ovenproof container that fits the sugar snugly. Put the container in the warm oven for approximately 15 minutes. If the sugar starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Always store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location. When the sugar gets moist, it will develop lumps.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5928518537835126, "g_worst_claim": 0.915194034576416, "g_content": 2.308869821053964, "g_traj_mean": 1.4395124912261963}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 79945, 13163, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 1992, 279, 13163, 304, 458, 23387, 15780, 5476, 323, 8205, 432, 304, 279, 23387, 518, 264, 3347, 9315, 320, 16, 20, 15, 12, 17, 15, 15, 12348, 8, 369, 13187, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 4636, 23867, 11, 15239, 279, 13163, 448, 264, 45505, 13, 1416, 432, 8471, 311, 4399, 10747, 11, 2484, 1007, 279, 23387, 323, 5274, 279, 13163, 304, 279, 23387, 369, 458, 6460, 476, 1378, 311, 6587, 9058, 700, 13, 1084, 374, 2989, 311, 3553, 15732, 7757, 13163, 304, 458, 264, 2106, 491, 5476, 323, 390, 13120, 388, 13163, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 9058, 3728, 11, 3123, 504, 29377, 2973, 13, 151645], "pred": "To soften sugar, it is recommended to place the sugar in an ovenproof container and warm it in the oven at a low temperature (150-200 degrees) for approximately 15 minutes. After warming, tap the sugar with a spoon. If it starts to fall apart, turn off the oven and leave the sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. It is important to store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location, away from refrigerators.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8339136632911945, "g_worst_claim": 0.927002931252504, "g_content": 2.3952301025390623, "g_traj_mean": 1.4669109582901}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.7, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "179", "question": "how to change the sleep time on my computer", "gt": "Sure, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to change the sleep time on my computer\" based on the given passages:\n\nTo change the sleep time on your computer, follow these steps:\n\n1. Click the Start menu and select Control Panel.\n2. In the Control Panel, click on Power Options.\n3. In the Power Options window, click on \"Change when the computer sleeps\" on the left side of the window.\n4. In the \"Put the computer to sleep\" section, change the duration of time to the desired amount of time you want the computer to sit idle before it goes to sleep.\n5. Alternatively, you can also toggle off the option to enter Sleep mode automatically.\n\nIf you are using Windows 10, you can also search for \"Power Options\" in the taskbar search box and select it to open the Power Options window.\n\nIf you are using Windows 8.1 / Windows RT 8.1, you can move your mouse to the lower left-hand corner of the screen, right-click the Start button, and select Shut down or sign out, and then select Shut down.", "pred": "1. Click Start Menu to load the Help Center.\n2. Enter Power Management Settings in the search field.\n3. Click Change Power Management settings.\n4. The Power Options window will then appear.\n5. On the left side of the window, click Change when the computer sleeps.\n6. Change the Put the computer to sleep entry with the desired amount of time you will allow the computer to sit idle before it sleeps, or automatically turn off its option to enter into Sleep mode.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Click Start Menu to load the Help Center.\n2. Enter Power Management Settings in the search field.\n3. Click Change Power Management settings.\n4. The Power Options window will then appear.\n5. On the left side of the window, click Change when the computer sleeps.\n6. Change the Put the computer to sleep entry with the desired amount of time you will allow the computer to sit idle before it sleeps, or automatically turn off its option to enter into Sleep mode.", "cot": "[\"To change the sleep time on your computer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Click Start Menu to load the Help Center.\\n2. Enter Power Management Settings in the search field.\\n3. Click Change Power Management settings.\\n4. The Power Options window will then appear.\\n5. On the left side of the window, click Change when the computer sleeps.\\n6. Change the Put the computer to sleep entry with the desired amount of time you will allow the computer to sit idle before it sleeps, or automatically turn off its option to enter into Sleep mode.\", \"To change the sleep time on your computer, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Click Start Menu to load the Help Center.\\n2. Enter Power Management Settings in the search field.\\n3. Click Change Power Management settings.\\n4. The Power Options window will then appear.\\n5. On the left side of the window, click Change when the computer sleeps.\\n6. Change the Put the computer to sleep entry with the desired amount of time you will allow the computer to sit idle before it sleeps, or automatically turn off its option to enter into Sleep mode.\\n\\nThese steps will allow you to adjust the sleep time according to your preference.\", \"To change the sleep time on your computer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Click Start Menu to load the Control Panel.\\n2. Open Power Options by typing \\\"power options\\\" in the search field and selecting it.\\n3. On the left side of the Power Options window, click \\\"Change when the computer sleeps.\\\"\\n4. In the \\\"Put the computer to sleep\\\" entry, change the setting to the desired amount of time you will allow the computer to idle before it sleeps, or select the \\\"Automatically turn off\\\" option to enter into Sleep mode.\\n5. Click \\\"Save changes\\\" or \\\"Apply\\\" to apply the changes.\", \"To change the sleep time on your computer, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Open Power Options**:\\n   - For Windows 7: Click Start Menu, enter \\\"Control Panel\\\" in the search field, and open it.\\n   - For Windows 8 and 8.1: Click Start, select Control Panel, and then click Power Options.\\n   - For Windows 10: Click the Start button, type \\\"power options\\\" in the search field, and select Power Options.\\n\\n2. **Adjust Sleep Settings**:\\n   - Open the Power Options window.\\n   - In the left pane, click \\\"Change when the computer sleeps.\\\"\\n   - In the right pane, you can set how long the computer waits before entering Sleep mode automatically. Adjust the slider to the desired time, or select \\\"Never\\\" to keep the computer awake.\\n\\n3. **Automatic Sleep Setting**:\\n   - If you want the computer to go to sleep automatically after no activity, choose \\\"Put the computer to sleep\\\" and adjust the slider to the appropriate time.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can easily modify the sleep behavior of your Windows-based computer.\"]", "time_sec": 23.831, "generation_time_seconds": 23.0718, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7522, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 2297, 279, 6084, 882, 389, 697, 6366, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 9189, 5145, 9738, 311, 2795, 279, 11479, 5832, 624, 17, 13, 11252, 7420, 9551, 11296, 304, 279, 2711, 2070, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 10388, 7420, 9551, 5003, 624, 19, 13, 576, 7420, 14566, 3241, 686, 1221, 4994, 624, 20, 13, 1913, 279, 2115, 3108, 315, 279, 3241, 11, 4205, 10388, 979, 279, 6366, 71390, 624, 21, 13, 10388, 279, 10224, 279, 6366, 311, 6084, 4343, 448, 279, 12685, 3311, 315, 882, 498, 686, 2138, 279, 6366, 311, 2444, 27647, 1573, 432, 71390, 11, 476, 9463, 2484, 1007, 1181, 2999, 311, 3725, 1119, 23774, 3856, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Click Start Menu to load the Help Center.\n2. Enter Power Management Settings in the search field.\n3. Click Change Power Management settings.\n4. The Power Options window will then appear.\n5. On the left side of the window, click Change when the computer sleeps.\n6. Change the Put the computer to sleep entry with the desired amount of time you will allow the computer to sit idle before it sleeps, or automatically turn off its option to enter into Sleep mode.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.2338662819460633, "g_worst_claim": 0.731319268544515, "g_content": 2.4596681756488348, "g_traj_mean": 2.032003164291382}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 2297, 279, 6084, 882, 389, 697, 6366, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 9189, 5145, 9738, 311, 2795, 279, 11479, 5832, 624, 17, 13, 11252, 7420, 9551, 11296, 304, 279, 2711, 2070, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 10388, 7420, 9551, 5003, 624, 19, 13, 576, 7420, 14566, 3241, 686, 1221, 4994, 624, 20, 13, 1913, 279, 2115, 3108, 315, 279, 3241, 11, 4205, 10388, 979, 279, 6366, 71390, 624, 21, 13, 10388, 279, 10224, 279, 6366, 311, 6084, 4343, 448, 279, 12685, 3311, 315, 882, 498, 686, 2138, 279, 6366, 311, 2444, 27647, 1573, 432, 71390, 11, 476, 9463, 2484, 1007, 1181, 2999, 311, 3725, 1119, 23774, 3856, 382, 9485, 7354, 686, 2138, 498, 311, 7500, 279, 6084, 882, 4092, 311, 697, 21933, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps will allow you to adjust the sleep time according to your preference.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.025303095371822, "g_worst_claim": 0.11549302339553832, "g_content": 2.240612839207505, "g_traj_mean": 1.7794238328933716}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 2297, 279, 6084, 882, 389, 697, 6366, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 9189, 5145, 9738, 311, 2795, 279, 7779, 18946, 624, 17, 13, 5264, 7420, 14566, 553, 19496, 330, 13175, 2606, 1, 304, 279, 2711, 2070, 323, 26301, 432, 624, 18, 13, 1913, 279, 2115, 3108, 315, 279, 7420, 14566, 3241, 11, 4205, 330, 4072, 979, 279, 6366, 71390, 10040, 19, 13, 758, 279, 330, 19103, 279, 6366, 311, 6084, 1, 4343, 11, 2297, 279, 6243, 311, 279, 12685, 3311, 315, 882, 498, 686, 2138, 279, 6366, 311, 27647, 1573, 432, 71390, 11, 476, 3293, 279, 330, 41072, 7022, 2484, 1007, 1, 2999, 311, 3725, 1119, 23774, 3856, 624, 20, 13, 9189, 330, 8784, 4344, 1, 476, 330, 28497, 1, 311, 3796, 279, 4344, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Click Start Menu to load the Control Panel.\n2. Open Power Options by typing \"power options\" in the search field and selecting it.\n3. On the left side of the Power Options window, click \"Change when the computer sleeps.\"\n4. In the \"Put the computer to sleep\" entry, change the setting to the desired amount of time you will allow the computer to idle before it sleeps, or select the \"Automatically turn off\" option to enter into Sleep mode.\n5. Click \"Save changes\" or \"Apply\" to apply the changes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1870781263747774, "g_worst_claim": 0.19149208068847656, "g_content": 1.2719081190765882, "g_traj_mean": 1.0723326206207275}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 2297, 279, 6084, 882, 389, 697, 6366, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 5002, 7420, 14566, 334, 510, 256, 481, 1752, 5515, 220, 22, 25, 9189, 5145, 9738, 11, 3725, 330, 3273, 18946, 1, 304, 279, 2711, 2070, 11, 323, 1787, 432, 624, 256, 481, 1752, 5515, 220, 23, 323, 220, 23, 13, 16, 25, 9189, 5145, 11, 3293, 7779, 18946, 11, 323, 1221, 4205, 7420, 14566, 624, 256, 481, 1752, 5515, 220, 16, 15, 25, 9189, 279, 5145, 3137, 11, 943, 330, 13175, 2606, 1, 304, 279, 2711, 2070, 11, 323, 3293, 7420, 14566, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 38616, 23774, 11296, 334, 510, 256, 481, 5264, 279, 7420, 14566, 3241, 624, 256, 481, 758, 279, 2115, 37322, 11, 4205, 330, 4072, 979, 279, 6366, 71390, 10040, 256, 481, 758, 279, 1290, 37322, 11, 498, 646, 738, 1246, 1293, 279, 6366, 46936, 1573, 16262, 23774, 3856, 9463, 13, 27196, 279, 21412, 311, 279, 12685, 882, 11, 476, 3293, 330, 26155, 1, 311, 2506, 279, 6366, 34347, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 62790, 23774, 20037, 334, 510, 256, 481, 1416, 498, 1366, 279, 6366, 311, 728, 311, 6084, 9463, 1283, 902, 5702, 11, 5157, 330, 19103, 279, 6366, 311, 6084, 1, 323, 7500, 279, 21412, 311, 279, 8311, 882, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 6707, 5602, 279, 6084, 7709, 315, 697, 5515, 5980, 6366, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can easily modify the sleep behavior of your Windows-based computer.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.4043069807218088, "g_worst_claim": -0.13139914274215697, "g_content": 0.4931583949497768, "g_traj_mean": 0.34340009093284607}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.9, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "180", "question": "psychological effects of hugging", "gt": "Hugging has significant psychological effects. It creates a warm feeling that affects the entire body, akin to the effect of many drugs operating simultaneously. This could be due to the feeling of a loving embrace, leading to good relationships and emotional intimacy. It also enhances empathy and listening skills, which can lead to a psychological hug. Furthermore, research has found that hugging can significantly reduce worries about mortality and boost self-esteem. This soothing effect can be achieved even when hugging an inanimate object like a teddy bear.", "pred": "Hugging can have a variety of psychological effects. According to the passage, it can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages. Furthermore, it can reduce worry and existential fear, as demonstrated in a study published in the journal Psychological Science. The passage also notes that hugging can provide a psychological hug, which can be experienced through empathy and listening skills.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Hugging can have a variety of psychological effects. According to the passage, it can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages. Furthermore, it can reduce worry and existential fear, as demonstrated in a study published in the journal Psychological Science. The passage also notes that hugging can provide a psychological hug, which can be experienced through empathy and listening skills.", "cot": "[\"Hugging can have significant psychological effects. It can reduce worry of mortality, as shown in a study published in the journal Psychological Science. Additionally, hugging can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages, as mentioned in the passage on empathy and listening skills. The use of empathy and listening skills during a conversation can make the other person feel like they are receiving a psychological hug.\", \"Answer: The psychological effects of hugging include reduced worry and existential fears, as demonstrated in a study published in the journal Psychological Science. Hugs, even when with inanimate objects like a teddy bear, help soothe individuals' existential fears.\", \"Psychological effects of hugging include: \\n- Feeling good and warm, which is attributed not only to the physical embrace but also to a deeper physiological response.\\n- Reduced worry of mortality, as hugging, even with an inanimate object, soothes existential fears.\\n- Improved relationships and emotional intimacy, as hugging can evoke feelings similar to a \\\"psychological hug\\\" through the use of empathy and listening skills.\", \"Hugging can have a variety of psychological effects. According to the passage, it can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages. Furthermore, it can reduce worry and existential fear, as demonstrated in a study published in the journal Psychological Science. The passage also notes that hugging can provide a psychological hug, which can be experienced through empathy and listening skills.\"]", "time_sec": 14.411, "generation_time_seconds": 13.5994, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8063, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [39, 35268, 646, 614, 5089, 23187, 6239, 13, 1084, 646, 7949, 10955, 315, 28428, 11, 438, 6839, 304, 264, 3920, 4652, 304, 279, 8322, 68969, 9965, 13, 22406, 11, 305, 35268, 646, 2990, 311, 1661, 11871, 11, 14269, 65164, 11, 323, 6247, 46351, 11, 438, 9733, 304, 279, 21085, 389, 47351, 323, 14289, 7361, 13, 576, 990, 315, 47351, 323, 14289, 7361, 2337, 264, 10435, 646, 1281, 279, 1008, 1697, 2666, 1075, 807, 525, 12308, 264, 23187, 29784, 13, 151645], "pred": "Hugging can have significant psychological effects. It can reduce worry of mortality, as shown in a study published in the journal Psychological Science. Additionally, hugging can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages, as mentioned in the passage on empathy and listening skills. The use of empathy and listening skills during a conversation can make the other person feel like they are receiving a psychological hug.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.427818423070949, "g_worst_claim": 0.9102606773376465, "g_content": 3.502675909745066, "g_traj_mean": 2.0784707069396973}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 576, 23187, 6239, 315, 305, 35268, 2924, 11046, 10955, 323, 66639, 23209, 11, 438, 20459, 304, 264, 3920, 4652, 304, 279, 8322, 68969, 9965, 13, 472, 13299, 11, 1496, 979, 448, 304, 22030, 6171, 1075, 264, 41223, 10258, 11722, 11, 1492, 43176, 1782, 7775, 6, 66639, 23209, 13, 151645], "pred": "The psychological effects of hugging include reduced worry and existential fears, as demonstrated in a study published in the journal Psychological Science. Hugs, even when with inanimate objects like a teddy bear, help soothe individuals' existential fears.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8540061354637145, "g_worst_claim": 0.9054928620656332, "g_content": 2.5410740192119894, "g_traj_mean": 1.7565799951553345}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [68703, 5729, 6239, 315, 305, 35268, 2924, 25, 715, 12, 73558, 1661, 323, 8205, 11, 892, 374, 29606, 537, 1172, 311, 279, 6961, 26732, 714, 1083, 311, 264, 19117, 52094, 2033, 624, 12, 79469, 10955, 315, 28428, 11, 438, 305, 35268, 11, 1496, 448, 458, 304, 22030, 1633, 11, 43176, 6375, 66639, 23209, 624, 12, 58123, 11871, 323, 14269, 65164, 11, 438, 305, 35268, 646, 94163, 15650, 4428, 311, 264, 330, 91009, 5729, 29784, 1, 1526, 279, 990, 315, 47351, 323, 14289, 7361, 13, 151645], "pred": "Psychological effects of hugging include: \n- Feeling good and warm, which is attributed not only to the physical embrace but also to a deeper physiological response.\n- Reduced worry of mortality, as hugging, even with an inanimate object, soothes existential fears.\n- Improved relationships and emotional intimacy, as hugging can evoke feelings similar to a \"psychological hug\" through the use of empathy and listening skills.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.2656391838075702, "g_worst_claim": 1.370203971862793, "g_content": 3.2762056986490884, "g_traj_mean": 1.9648618698120117}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [39, 35268, 646, 614, 264, 8045, 315, 23187, 6239, 13, 10548, 311, 279, 21085, 11, 432, 646, 2990, 311, 1661, 11871, 11, 14269, 65164, 11, 323, 6247, 46351, 13, 23405, 11, 432, 646, 7949, 10955, 323, 66639, 8679, 11, 438, 20459, 304, 264, 3920, 4652, 304, 279, 8322, 68969, 9965, 13, 576, 21085, 1083, 8388, 429, 305, 35268, 646, 3410, 264, 23187, 29784, 11, 892, 646, 387, 10321, 1526, 47351, 323, 14289, 7361, 13, 151645], "pred": "Hugging can have a variety of psychological effects. According to the passage, it can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages. Furthermore, it can reduce worry and existential fear, as demonstrated in a study published in the journal Psychological Science. The passage also notes that hugging can provide a psychological hug, which can be experienced through empathy and listening skills.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9325701288154176, "g_worst_claim": 1.0371143341064453, "g_content": 3.535819782930262, "g_traj_mean": 1.7444981336593628}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 40.38, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "181", "question": "psychological effects of hugging", "gt": "Hugging has physiological benefits and can have a similar effect on the body as certain drugs. It can also lead to emotional intimacy and happy relationships. Hugging and touch, even with inanimate objects, can help reduce existential fears and worry about mortality.", "pred": "In summary, hugging can lead to a variety of psychological benefits, including increased empathy, reduced existential fears, improved self-esteem, and enhanced overall well-being.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "In summary, hugging can lead to a variety of psychological benefits, including increased empathy, reduced existential fears, improved self-esteem, and enhanced overall well-being.", "cot": "[\"Hugging can have significant psychological effects. It can reduce worry of mortality, as shown in a study published in the journal Psychological Science. Additionally, hugging can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages, as mentioned in the passage on empathy and listening skills. The use of empathy and listening skills during a conversation can make the other person feel like they are receiving a psychological hug.\", \"Psychological effects of hugging include:\\n\\n1. Increased feelings of empathy and emotional intimacy: According to the second passage, empathic listening can sometimes lead to good relationships and a feeling as though the listener is receiving a psychological hug.\\n\\n2. Reduced existential fears: The third passage states that hugging, even with an inanimate object like a teddy bear, can significantly reduce worry about mortality and existential fears.\\n\\n3. Improved self-esteem: Research published in the journal Psychological Science showed that hugs and touch can help individuals feel better about themselves.\\n\\n4. Enhanced well-being: The first passage mentions that hugging provides a warm feeling in the heart and affects the entire body, which suggests it has positive psychological effects on well-being.\\n\\nIn summary, hugging can lead to a variety of psychological benefits, including increased empathy, reduced existential fears, improved self-esteem, and enhanced overall well-being.\", \"Hugging has been shown to have psychological effects, including reducing worry, as demonstrated in a study published in Psychological Science where hugging, even with an inanimate object like a teddy bear, helped soothe individuals’ existential fears.\", \"Research published in the journal Psychological Science revealed that hugs and touch significantly reduce worry of mortality. Hugging can help soothe individuals' existential fears.\"]", "time_sec": 15.547, "generation_time_seconds": 14.9919, "selection_time_seconds": 0.5517, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [39, 35268, 646, 614, 5089, 23187, 6239, 13, 1084, 646, 7949, 10955, 315, 28428, 11, 438, 6839, 304, 264, 3920, 4652, 304, 279, 8322, 68969, 9965, 13, 22406, 11, 305, 35268, 646, 2990, 311, 1661, 11871, 11, 14269, 65164, 11, 323, 6247, 46351, 11, 438, 9733, 304, 279, 21085, 389, 47351, 323, 14289, 7361, 13, 576, 990, 315, 47351, 323, 14289, 7361, 2337, 264, 10435, 646, 1281, 279, 1008, 1697, 2666, 1075, 807, 525, 12308, 264, 23187, 29784, 13, 151645], "pred": "Hugging can have significant psychological effects. It can reduce worry of mortality, as shown in a study published in the journal Psychological Science. Additionally, hugging can lead to good relationships, emotional intimacy, and happy marriages, as mentioned in the passage on empathy and listening skills. The use of empathy and listening skills during a conversation can make the other person feel like they are receiving a psychological hug.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.3815748193176276, "g_worst_claim": 0.8875552813212076, "g_content": 3.471798946982936, "g_traj_mean": 