{"id": "195", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question:\n\nTo attach multiple picture frames together, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding.\n2. Lay them beside each other to see if you like the effect.\n3. Put two frames together back to back, and mark the hinge placement. The placement must be the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure that the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.\n4. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\n5. Repeat the process for additional frames, ensuring that the hinge placement is consistent across all frames.\n6. Attach a hanging wire to the back of the grouped frames and hang them up.\n\nTherefore, the answer is: Select frames with the same wood molding, lay them together, mark hinge placement, attach hinges, and attach a hanging wire to the back.", "pred": "Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "cot": "[\"Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\", \"Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\", \"Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames. This ensures that the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.\", \"Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\"]", "time_sec": 7.495, "generation_time_seconds": 6.8194, "selection_time_seconds": 0.671, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [30485, 1378, 2613, 79834, 311, 279, 20913, 11067, 315, 279, 14087, 13, 151645], "pred": "Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 4.09960397084554, "g_worst_claim": 4.09960397084554, "g_content": 6.650733402797154, "g_traj_mean": 4.032876491546631}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [30485, 1378, 2613, 79834, 311, 279, 20913, 11067, 315, 279, 14087, 13, 151645], "pred": "Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 4.09960397084554, "g_worst_claim": 4.09960397084554, "g_content": 6.650733402797154, "g_traj_mean": 4.032876491546631}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [30485, 1378, 2613, 79834, 311, 279, 20913, 11067, 315, 279, 14087, 13, 1096, 25351, 429, 279, 40041, 9185, 2498, 51023, 389, 279, 1965, 1909, 13, 151645], "pred": "Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames. This ensures that the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 3.6702123299623146, "g_worst_claim": 3.23764654306265, "g_content": 5.976460048130581, "g_traj_mean": 3.565603494644165}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [30485, 1378, 2613, 79834, 311, 279, 20913, 11067, 315, 279, 14087, 13, 151645], "pred": "Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 4.09960397084554, "g_worst_claim": 4.09960397084554, "g_content": 6.650733402797154, "g_traj_mean": 4.032876491546631}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 11.97, "GAVIE-Rel": 2.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "197", "question": "leasing meaning", "gt": "Leasing refers to a process in which a firm obtains the use of fixed assets by making contractual, periodic, and tax-deductible payments to the owner of those assets. The lessee is the party receiving the services or assets under the lease contract, while the lessor is the owner of the assets.", "pred": "Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed asset for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed asset for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets.", "cot": "[\"Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed asset for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets.\", \"Leasing is a contractual arrangement in which an entity (the lessee) pays another entity (the lessor) for the use of a certain fixed asset. The lessee receives the services or assets under the lease contract, and the lessor is the owner of the assets. The relationship between the tenant and the landlord is called a tenancy, and can be for a fixed or an indefinite period of time. The consideration for the lease is called rent.\", \"Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed assets for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets.\", \"Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed asset for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets.\"]", "time_sec": 12.788, "generation_time_seconds": 12.1678, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6148, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [2304, 4422, 374, 264, 1882, 553, 892, 264, 7474, 646, 6851, 279, 990, 315, 264, 3654, 8356, 9329, 369, 892, 432, 1969, 2291, 264, 4013, 315, 75443, 11, 38345, 11, 3742, 77812, 14173, 13, 576, 3541, 4060, 374, 279, 13964, 315, 279, 3516, 476, 279, 11770, 1212, 279, 25064, 5116, 323, 279, 2686, 269, 374, 279, 6372, 315, 279, 11770, 13, 151645], "pred": "Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed asset for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.544211323299105, "g_worst_claim": 1.625958760579427, "g_content": 3.433112144470215, "g_traj_mean": 2.1660537719726562}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [2304, 4422, 374, 264, 75443, 26112, 304, 892, 458, 5387, 320, 1782, 3541, 4060, 8, 21241, 2441, 5387, 320, 1782, 2686, 269, 8, 369, 279, 990, 315, 264, 3654, 8356, 9329, 13, 576, 3541, 4060, 21189, 279, 3516, 476, 11770, 1212, 279, 25064, 5116, 11, 323, 279, 2686, 269, 374, 279, 6372, 315, 279, 11770, 13, 576, 5025, 1948, 279, 25239, 323, 279, 40147, 374, 2598, 264, 5779, 6572, 11, 323, 646, 387, 369, 264, 8356, 476, 458, 80856, 4168, 315, 882, 13, 576, 17879, 369, 279, 25064, 374, 2598, 8016, 13, 151645], "pred": "Leasing is a contractual arrangement in which an entity (the lessee) pays another entity (the lessor) for the use of a certain fixed asset. The lessee receives the services or assets under the lease contract, and the lessor is the owner of the assets. The relationship between the tenant and the landlord is called a tenancy, and can be for a fixed or an indefinite period of time. The consideration for the lease is called rent.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3542654765284314, "g_worst_claim": 0.7919791828502308, "g_content": 2.00683353969029, "g_traj_mean": 1.2342181205749512}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [2304, 4422, 374, 264, 1882, 553, 892, 264, 7474, 646, 6851, 279, 990, 315, 264, 3654, 8356, 11770, 369, 892, 432, 1969, 2291, 264, 4013, 315, 75443, 11, 38345, 11, 3742, 77812, 14173, 13, 576, 3541, 4060, 374, 279, 13964, 315, 279, 3516, 476, 279, 11770, 1212, 279, 25064, 5116, 323, 279, 2686, 269, 374, 279, 6372, 315, 279, 11770, 13, 151645], "pred": "Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed assets for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.6329147437262157, "g_worst_claim": 1.578631083170573, "g_content": 3.592890421549479, "g_traj_mean": 2.239431619644165}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [2304, 4422, 374, 264, 1882, 553, 892, 264, 7474, 646, 6851, 279, 990, 315, 264, 3654, 8356, 9329, 369, 892, 432, 1969, 2291, 264, 4013, 315, 75443, 11, 38345, 11, 3742, 77812, 14173, 13, 576, 3541, 4060, 374, 279, 13964, 315, 279, 3516, 476, 279, 11770, 1212, 279, 25064, 5116, 323, 279, 2686, 269, 374, 279, 6372, 315, 279, 11770, 13, 151645], "pred": "Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed asset for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.544211323299105, "g_worst_claim": 1.625958760579427, "g_content": 3.433112144470215, "g_traj_mean": 2.1660537719726562}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 64.15, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "199", "question": "what causes necrotizing fasciitis", "gt": "Necrotizing fasciitis is caused primarily by bacteria, specifically group A beta-hemolytic streptococci, also known as Streptococcus pyogenes. This is the same bacteria that causes strep throat, impetigo, and rheumatic fever. Other bacteria types, such as staphylococcus, are also associated with the disease. The bacteria infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin. Prior trauma, such as a cut or scrape, insect bite, burn, or needle puncture wound can serve as a source of infection as well as surgical incision sites and various surgical procedures. In rare cases, fungi can lead to this condition.", "pred": "Necrotizing fasciitis is commonly caused by group A Streptococcus (GAS) bacteria. Other types of bacteria, such as staphylococcus and others, may also be associated with the disease.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Necrotizing fasciitis is commonly caused by group A Streptococcus (GAS) bacteria. Other types of bacteria, such as staphylococcus and others, may also be associated with the disease.", "cot": "[\"Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria, including group A Streptococcus (GAS), staphylococcus, and others. These bacteria can infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin. In some cases, the infections caused by these bacteria can be mild, but in rare cases, they can cause a more dangerous infection that can destroy skin, fat, and the tissue covering the muscles within a very short time.\", \"Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria. Some of these bacteria also cause infections such as strep throat and impetigo. Usually the infections caused by these bacteria are mild. However, in rare cases they can cause a more dangerous infection.\", \"Necrotizing fasciitis is commonly caused by group A Streptococcus (GAS) bacteria. Other types of bacteria, such as staphylococcus and others, may also be associated with the disease.\", \"Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria. Some of these bacteria also cause infections such as strep throat and impetigo. Usually the infections caused by these bacteria are mild.\"]", "time_sec": 12.28, "generation_time_seconds": 11.6158, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6588, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [45, 757, 4640, 4849, 15195, 72, 19435, 374, 8881, 553, 3807, 12829, 315, 23157, 11, 2670, 1874, 362, 35672, 417, 509, 91311, 320, 38, 1911, 701, 357, 1342, 88, 1074, 91311, 11, 323, 3800, 13, 4220, 23157, 646, 33427, 279, 58815, 15195, 685, 11, 264, 6193, 315, 4564, 533, 19847, 3685, 279, 6787, 13, 758, 1045, 5048, 11, 279, 28920, 8881, 553, 1493, 23157, 646, 387, 23034, 11, 714, 304, 8848, 5048, 11, 807, 646, 5240, 264, 803, 11406, 18873, 429, 646, 6921, 6787, 11, 8664, 11, 323, 279, 19847, 18202, 279, 23648, 2878, 264, 1602, 2805, 882, 13, 151645], "pred": "Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria, including group A Streptococcus (GAS), staphylococcus, and others. These bacteria can infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin. In some cases, the infections caused by these bacteria can be mild, but in rare cases, they can cause a more dangerous infection that can destroy skin, fat, and the tissue covering the muscles within a very short time.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3317826701535118, "g_worst_claim": 0.34242773056030273, "g_content": 2.375880543778582, "g_traj_mean": 1.296658992767334}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [45, 757, 4640, 4849, 15195, 72, 19435, 374, 8881, 553, 3807, 12829, 315, 23157, 13, 4329, 315, 1493, 23157, 1083, 5240, 28920, 1741, 438, 5412, 79, 27591, 323, 3163, 295, 7836, 13, 32967, 279, 28920, 8881, 553, 1493, 23157, 525, 23034, 13, 4354, 11, 304, 8848, 5048,