IE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "203", "question": "what causes necrotizing fasciitis", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main cause of necrotizing fasciitis is bacterial infection, specifically group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes) and Staphylococcus. Additionally, other types of bacteria have also been associated with the disease. Trauma, such as cuts, scrapes, insect bites, burns, or needle puncture wounds, can also play a role in the development of necrotizing fasciitis. Surgical incision sites and various surgical procedures can also serve as a source of infection. Therefore, the answer is: Bacterial infection, including group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes) and Staphylococcus, and trauma.", "pred": "Necrotizing fasciitis is commonly caused by group A Streptococcus (GAS) bacteria, which is the same type of bacteria that causes strep throat. However, several types of bacteria, such as staphylococcus and others, have also been associated with the disease. The bacteria infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Necrotizing fasciitis is commonly caused by group A Streptococcus (GAS) bacteria, which is the same type of bacteria that causes strep throat. However, several types of bacteria, such as staphylococcus and others, have also been associated with the disease. The bacteria infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin.", "cot": "[\"Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria, including group A Streptococcus (GAS), staphylococcus, and others. These bacteria can infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin. In some cases, the infections caused by these bacteria can be mild, but in rare cases, they can cause a more dangerous infection that can destroy skin, fat, and the tissue covering the muscles within a very short time.\", \"Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria, including group A Streptococcus (GAS), staphylococcus, and others. These bacteria can infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin, leading to the destruction of skin, fat, and the tissue covering the muscles. The infection is also known as flesh-eating bacteria and can be dangerous, especially in severe cases.\", \"Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria, with group A Streptococcus (GAS) being the most common cause. This bacterium is also responsible for infections like strep throat and impetigo. Other bacteria, such as staphylococcus, can also lead to necrotizing fasciitis. The infection occurs when these bacteria infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin.\", \"Necrotizing fasciitis is commonly caused by group A Streptococcus (GAS) bacteria, which is the same type of bacteria that causes strep throat. However, several types of bacteria, such as staphylococcus and others, have also been associated with the disease. The bacteria infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin.\"]", "time_sec": 15.697, "generation_time_seconds": 14.8698, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8231, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [45, 757, 4640, 4849, 15195, 72, 19435, 374, 8881, 553, 3807, 12829, 315, 23157, 11, 2670, 1874, 362, 35672, 417, 509, 91311, 320, 38, 1911, 701, 357, 1342, 88, 1074, 91311, 11, 323, 3800, 13, 4220, 23157, 646, 33427, 279, 58815, 15195, 685, 11, 264, 6193, 315, 4564, 533, 19847, 3685, 279, 6787, 13, 758, 1045, 5048, 11, 279, 28920, 8881, 553, 1493, 23157, 646, 387, 23034, 11, 714, 304, 8848, 5048, 11, 807, 646, 5240, 264, 803, 11406, 18873, 429, 646, 6921, 6787, 11, 8664, 11, 323, 279, 19847, 18202, 279, 23648, 2878, 264, 1602, 2805, 882, 13, 151645], "pred": "Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria, including group A Streptococcus (GAS), staphylococcus, and others. These bacteria can infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin. In some cases, the infections caused by these bacteria can be mild, but in rare cases, they can cause a more dangerous infection that can destroy skin, fat, and the tissue covering the muscles within a very short time.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3345567449776814, "g_worst_claim": 0.349893028085882, "g_content": 2.374631742151772, "g_traj_mean": 1.304134488105774}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [45, 757, 4640, 4849, 15195, 72, 19435, 374, 8881, 553, 3807, 12829, 315, 23157, 11, 2670, 1874, 362, 35672, 417, 509, 91311, 320, 38, 1911, 701, 357, 1342, 88, 1074, 91311, 11, 323, 3800, 13, 4220, 23157, 646, 33427, 279, 58815, 15195, 685, 11, 264, 6193, 315, 4564, 533, 19847, 3685, 279, 6787, 11, 6388, 311, 279, 19258, 315, 6787, 11, 8664, 11, 323, 279, 19847, 18202, 279, 23648, 13, 576, 18873, 374, 1083, 3881, 438, 24955, 5655, 1095, 23157, 323, 646, 387, 11406, 11, 5310, 304, 15386, 5048, 13, 151645], "pred": "Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria, including group A Streptococcus (GAS), staphylococcus, and others. These bacteria can infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin, leading to the destruction of skin, fat, and the tissue covering the muscles. The infection is also known as flesh-eating bacteria and can be dangerous, especially in severe cases.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1105779224057906, "g_worst_claim": 0.349893028085882, "g_content": 1.774074872334798, "g_traj_mean": 1.0736511945724487}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [45, 757, 4640, 4849, 15195, 72, 19435, 374, 8881, 553, 3807, 12829, 315, 23157, 11, 448, 1874, 362, 35672, 417, 509, 91311, 320, 38, 1911, 8, 1660, 279, 1429, 4185, 5240, 13, 1096, 17398, 2356, 374, 1083, 8480, 369, 28920, 1075, 5412, 79, 27591, 323, 3163, 295, 7836, 13, 6944, 23157, 11, 1741, 438, 357, 1342, 88, 1074, 91311, 11, 646, 1083, 2990, 311, 19053, 4640, 4849, 15195, 72, 19435, 13, 576, 18873, 13666, 979, 1493, 23157, 33427, 279, 58815, 15195, 685, 11, 264, 6193, 315, 4564, 533, 19847, 3685, 279, 6787, 13, 151645], "pred": "Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by several kinds of bacteria, with group A Streptococcus (GAS) being the most common cause. This bacterium is also responsible for infections like strep throat and impetigo. Other bacteria, such as staphylococcus, can also lead to necrotizing fasciitis. The infection occurs when these bacteria infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7897437084592388, "g_worst_claim": 0.07915150035511363, "g_content": 1.5626481952089253, "g_traj_mean": 0.7926064133644104}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [45, 757, 4640, 4849, 15195, 72, 19435, 374, 16626, 8881, 553, 1874, 362, 35672, 417, 509, 91311, 320, 38, 1911, 8, 23157, 11, 892, 374, 279, 1852, 943, 315, 23157, 429, 11137, 5412, 79, 27591, 13, 4354, 11, 3807, 4494, 315, 23157, 11, 1741, 438, 357, 1342, 88, 1074, 91311, 323, 3800, 11, 614, 1083, 1012, 5815, 448, 279, 8457, 13, 576, 23157, 33427, 279, 58815, 15195, 685, 11, 264, 6193, 315, 4564, 533, 19847, 3685, 279, 6787, 13, 151645], "pred": "Necrotizing fasciitis is commonly caused by group A Streptococcus (GAS) bacteria, which is the same type of bacteria that causes strep throat. However, several types of bacteria, such as staphylococcus and others, have also been associated with the disease. The bacteria infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2122313306629597, "g_worst_claim": 0.5434082104609563, "g_content": 2.015059607369559, "g_traj_mean": 1.1132532358169556}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 24.49, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "204", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "gt": "Chard, also known as Swiss chard, is a vegetable with large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It has a flavor that is stronger and more assertive than spinach, and some people find it bitter. Chard can be eaten raw in salads when it's young, but mature leaves and stalks are usually cooked or sautéed. Chard is actually a type of beet that is grown for its leaves rather than its root. It can produce white, yellow, or red leaf stalks. Chard is highly perishable and should be kept in the refrigerator for only 2 to 3 days.", "pred": "Chard is a leafy green vegetable that is similar to spinach but with a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden. Chard is extremely perishable, so keep refrigerator storage time to a minimum.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Chard is a leafy green vegetable that is similar to spinach but with a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden. Chard is extremely perishable, so keep refrigerator storage time to a minimum.", "cot": "[\"Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.\", \"Chard is a type of leafy green vegetable that has been cultivated from the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. It is known for its large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor, sometimes described as bitter. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked.\", \"Chard is a leafy green vegetable that is similar to spinach but with a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden. Chard is extremely perishable, so keep refrigerator storage time to a minimum.\", \"Swiss chard is a leafy green vegetable that is very similar to spinach. It has fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks.\"]", "time_sec": 12.999, "generation_time_seconds": 12.3829, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6124, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1143, 567, 374, 264, 48012, 429, 702, 1012, 11882, 369, 15933, 5670, 518, 279, 20284, 315, 5819, 3704, 18003, 13, 1084, 374, 458, 18879, 39445, 43086, 429, 11367, 1894, 311, 279, 35481, 13551, 13, 151645], "pred": "Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1578963552202497, "g_worst_claim": 1.5129507609776087, "g_content": 3.4772717793782553, "g_traj_mean": 2.2495081424713135}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1143, 567, 374, 264, 943, 315, 15933, 88, 6176, 35481, 429, 702, 1012, 66066, 504, 279, 9396, 48012, 11, 34243, 73160, 285, 1186, 2154, 13, 3594, 275, 7523, 13, 1084, 374, 3881, 369, 1181, 3460, 11, 282, 642, 8503, 714, 27582, 5538, 6176, 10901, 323, 12045, 11, 41854, 54872, 82, 13, 910, 567, 374, 4428, 311, 67698, 714, 702, 264, 16245, 11, 803, 2060, 533, 17172, 