{"id": "205", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "gt": "Chard is a vegetable that has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked or sautéed. Chard is in the same subspecies as beetroot and is cultivated for leaf production. It can be harvested while the leaves are young and tender or after maturity when the stems are slightly tougher. Chard is perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator for a minimum amount of time.", "pred": "Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.", "cot": "[\"Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.\", \"Chard is a type of beetle that has been selected for its leaf production, resulting in leaves that are white, yellow, or red. It can be harvested while the leaves are young and tender or after maturity, when the leaves have slightly tougher stems. Chard is a colorful ornamental that adds beauty to the vegetable garden.\", \"Chard is a beet that has been cultivated mainly for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is known for its large, fleshy, deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive, and some would say, bitter flavor.\", \"Chard is a type of leafy green vegetable that is closely related to beets. It is characterized by its thick, crisp stalks and large, deep green leaves. Chard is similar to spinach in that it is also a leafy green vegetable, but it has a stronger, more assertive flavor. The bitterness of chard is less pronounced when it is cooked.\"]", "time_sec": 15.163, "generation_time_seconds": 14.5733, "selection_time_seconds": 0.5825, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1143, 567, 374, 264, 48012, 429, 702, 1012, 11882, 369, 15933, 5670, 518, 279, 20284, 315, 5819, 3704, 18003, 13, 1084, 374, 458, 18879, 39445, 43086, 429, 11367, 1894, 311, 279, 35481, 13551, 13, 151645], "pred": "Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1553528376988003, "g_worst_claim": 1.5537945883614677, "g_content": 3.3645428975423175, "g_traj_mean": 2.2373621463775635}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1143, 567, 374, 264, 943, 315, 97386, 429, 702, 1012, 4091, 369, 1181, 15933, 5670, 11, 12942, 304, 10901, 429, 525, 4158, 11, 13753, 11, 476, 2518, 13, 1084, 646, 387, 66472, 1393, 279, 10901, 525, 3908, 323, 27582, 476, 1283, 47161, 11, 979, 279, 10901, 614, 10078, 48231, 43714, 13, 910, 567, 374, 264, 33866, 39445, 43086, 429, 11367, 13143, 311, 279, 35481, 13551, 13, 151645], "pred": "Chard is a type of beetle that has been selected for its leaf production, resulting in leaves that are white, yellow, or red. It can be harvested while the leaves are young and tender or after maturity, when the leaves have slightly tougher stems. Chard is a colorful ornamental that adds beauty to the vegetable garden.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5059635271344864, "g_worst_claim": 1.1594608851841517, "g_content": 2.7524400438581194, "g_traj_mean": 1.4693177938461304}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1143, 567, 374, 264, 48012, 429, 702, 1012,