{"id": "206", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "gt": "Based on the given passages, Swiss chard (also known as just plain chard) is a type of beet plant that has been selected for its leaf production rather than storage root formation. It produces large, tender deep green leaves with thick, crisp stalks. The leaves have a more assertive and sometimes bitter taste compared to spinach. Swiss chard is a perishable vegetable and should be stored in the refrigerator. It can be used raw in salads or cooked like in pizzoccheri.", "pred": "Swiss chard, also known as just plain chard, has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach, but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavour.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Swiss chard, also known as just plain chard, has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach, but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavour.", "cot": "[\"Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.\", \"Swiss chard is a vegetable that has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It is similar to spinach, but with a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavour. Chard is used in cooking, and it can be cooked or sauteed, and its bitterness fades with cooking, leaving a refined flavor which is more delicate than that of cooked spinach. Chard is also used in salads.\", \"Based on the provided passages, Swiss chard, also known as plain chard, is a leafy green vegetable that has large, fleshy, and tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is part of the beetroot (garden beet) family, which are cultivated descendants of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. Chard is an attractive ornamental plant that adds color to the vegetable garden.\", \"Swiss chard, also known as just plain chard, has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach, but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavour.\"]", "time_sec": 13.972, "generation_time_seconds": 13.3593, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6079, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1143, 567, 374, 264, 48012, 429, 702, 1012, 11882, 369, 15933, 5670, 518, 279, 20284, 315, 5819, 3704, 18003, 13, 1084, 374, 458, 18879, 39445, 43086, 429, 11367, 1894, 311, 279, 35481, 13551, 13, 151645], "pred": "Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.142151246752058, "g_worst_claim": 1.5278516496930803, "g_content": 3.3844212849934894, "g_traj_mean": 2.241471290588379}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [13218, 1038, 521, 567, 374, 264, 35481, 429, 702, 3460, 11, 282, 642, 8503, 714, 27582, 5538, 6176, 10901, 323, 12045, 11, 41854, 54872, 82, 13, 1084, 374, 4428, 311, 67698, 11, 714, 448, 264, 16245, 11, 803, 2060, 533, 320, 14689, 1744, 11, 25180, 8, 46597, 13, 910, 567, 374, 1483, 304, 17233, 11, 323, 432, 646, 387, 29105, 476, 822, 1070, 291, 11, 323, 1181, 78996, 86409, 448, 17233, 11, 9380, 264, 37191, 17172, 892, 374, 803, 35201, 1091, 429, 315, 29105, 67698, 13, 910, 567, 374, 1083, 1483, 304, 76752, 13, 151645], "pred": "Swiss chard is a vegetable that has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It is similar to spinach, but with a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavour. Chard is used in cooking, and it can be cooked or sauteed, and its bitterness fades with cooking, leaving a refined flavor which is more delicate than that of cooked spinach. Chard is also used in salads.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9121784853494246, "g_worst_claim": 0.25384485721588135, "g_content": 3.130532960633974, "g_traj_mean": 1.971510410308838}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 29691, 521, 567, 11, 1083, 3881, 438, 14396, 521, 567, 11, 374, 264, 15933, 88, 6176, 35481, 429, 702, 3460, 11, 282, 642, 8503, 11, 323, 27582, 5538, 6176, 10901, 323, 12045, 11, 41854, 54872, 82, 13, 1084, 374, 4428, 311, 67698, 714, 702, 264, 16245, 11, 803, 2060, 533, 320, 14689, 1744, 11, 25180, 8, 17172, 13, 29160, 3908, 521, 567, 646, 387, 1483, 7112, 304, 76752, 11, 1393, 14851, 521, 567, 10901, 323, 54872, 82, 525, 11136, 29105, 13, 910, 567, 374, 949, 315, 279, 48012, 2888, 320, 70, 8341, 48012, 8, 2997, 11, 892, 525, 66066, 48346, 315, 279, 9396, 48012, 11, 34243, 73160, 285, 1186, 2154, 13, 3594, 275, 7523, 13, 910, 567, 374, 458, 18879, 39445, 43086, 6008, 429, 11367, 1894, 311, 279, 35481, 13551, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the provided passages, Swiss chard, also known as plain chard, is a leafy green vegetable that has large, fleshy, and tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked. Chard is part of the beetroot (garden beet) family, which are cultivated descendants of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima. Chard is an attractive ornamental plant that adds color to the vegetable garden.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7327292793401448, "g_worst_claim": 0.4221169948577881, "g_content": 2.6846781084614415, "g_traj_mean": 1.624919056892395}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [13218, 1038, 521, 567, 11, 1083, 3881, 438, 1101, 14396, 521, 567, 11, 702, 3460, 11, 282, 642, 8503, 714, 27582, 5538, 6176, 10901, 323, 12045, 11, 41854, 54872, 82, 13, 910, 567, 374, 4428, 311, 67698, 11, 714, 702, 264, 16245, 11, 803, 2060, 533, 320, 14689, 1744, 11, 25180, 8, 46597, 13, 151645], "pred": "Swiss chard, also known as just plain chard, has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach, but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavour.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.3060862327550913, "g_worst_claim": 1.036334650857108, "g_content": 3.400785966352983, "g_traj_mean": 2.2209725379943848}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.19, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "207", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is what can be inferred about the vegetable \"chard\":\n\n* Chard is a type of beet (Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima) that has been chosen for leaf production over storage root formation.\n* Chard has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks.\n* The flavor of chard is similar to spinach but with a stronger, more assertive taste (some consider it bitter).\n* Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked to reduce bitterness and bring out a refined flavor.\n* Chard is an attractive ornamental plant that adds color to the vegetable garden.\n* Chard is perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator to minimize spoilage.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What is chard vegetable?\" is: A beet variety (Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima) grown for leaf production, characterized by large, fleshy leaves and stalks with a strong, bitter flavor that becomes more refined with cooking.", "pred": "Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.", "cot": "[\"Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.\", \"Swiss chard is a type of vegetable, also known as just plain chard, that has large, fleshy, but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor, some describing it as bitter. Chard is a beet that has been cultivated for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It can be harvested while the leaves are young and tender or after maturity, when they have larger, slightly tougher stems. Chard can be used fresh in salads or cooked, and its bitterness fades with cooking, leaving a refined flavor more delicate than that of cooked spinach.\", \"Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.\", \"Chard is a type of leafy green vegetable. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor, which some people find bitter. It is often cooked, and its bitterness fades during cooking, resulting in a refined flavor that is more delicate than that of cooked spinach.\"]", "time_sec": 14.3, "generation_time_seconds": 13.5975, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6949, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1143, 567, 374, 264, 48012, 429, 702, 1012, 11882, 369, 15933, 5670, 518, 279, 20284, 315, 5819, 3704, 18003, 13, 1084, 374, 458, 18879, 39445, 43086, 429, 11367, 1894, 311, 279, 35481, 13551, 13, 151645], "pred": "Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1869935989379883, "g_worst_claim": 1.5512800216674805, "g_content": 3.4863934834798176, "g_traj_mean": 2.2759366035461426}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [13218, 1038, 521, 567, 374, 264, 943, 315, 35481, 11, 1083, 3881, 438, 1101, 14396, 521, 567, 11, 429, 702, 3460, 11, 282, 642, 8503, 11, 714, 27582, 5538, 6176, 10901, 323, 12045, 11, 41854, 54872, 82, 13, 1084, 374, 4428, 311, 67698, 714, 702, 264, 16245, 11, 803, 2060, 533, 17172, 11, 1045, 22692, 432, 438, 25180, 13, 910, 567, 374, 264, 48012, 429, 702, 1012, 66066, 369, 15933, 5670, 518, 279, 20284, 315, 5819, 3704, 18003, 13, 1084, 646, 387, 66472, 1393, 279, 10901, 525, 3908, 323, 27582, 476, 1283, 47161, 11, 979, 807, 614, 8131, 11, 10078, 48231, 43714, 13, 910, 567, 646, 387, 1483, 7722, 304, 76752, 476, 29105, 11, 323, 1181, 78996, 86409, 448, 17233, 11, 9380, 264, 37191, 17172, 803, 35201, 1091, 429, 315, 29105, 67698, 13, 151645], "pred": "Swiss chard is a type of vegetable, also known as just plain chard, that has large, fleshy, but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor, some describing it as bitter. Chard is a beet that has been cultivated for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It can be harvested while the leaves are young and tender or after maturity, when they have larger, slightly tougher stems. Chard can be used fresh in salads or cooked, and its bitterness fades with cooking, leaving a refined flavor more delicate than that of cooked spinach.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8666357074544466, "g_worst_claim": 0.6389839865944602, "g_content": 2.797790795041804, "g_traj_mean": 1.836557149887085}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1143, 567, 374, 264, 48012, 429, 702, 1012, 11882, 369, 15933, 5670, 518, 279, 20284, 315, 5819, 3704, 18003, 13, 1084, 374, 458, 18879, 39445, 43086, 429, 11367, 1894, 311, 279, 35481, 13551, 13, 151645], "pred": "Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1869935989379883, "g_worst_claim": 1.5512800216674805, "g_content": 3.4863934834798176, "g_traj_mean": 2.2759366035461426}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1143, 567, 374, 264, 943, 315, 15933, 88, 6176, 35481, 13, 1084, 702, 3460, 11, 282, 642, 8503, 714, 27582, 5538, 617