{"id": "209", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "gt": "Based on the given passages, chard is a type of vegetable that belongs to the same subspecies as beetroot and is characterized by its large, fleshy leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It has a stronger, more assertive flavor than spinach and can be used raw in salads or cooked like in pizzoccheri. Chard is a beet that has been selected for leaf production rather than storage root formation and can be harvested when young and tender or after maturity. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden, but it is extremely perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator for a maximum of 2-3 days.", "pred": "Chard is a leafy green vegetable that is related to beets. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor compared to spinach. It can be used raw in salads or cooked, and its bitterness fades with cooking, leaving a refined flavor which is more delicate than that of cooked spinach. Chard is an attractive ornamental vegetable that adds color to the vegetable garden.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Chard is a leafy green vegetable that is related to beets. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor compared to spinach. It can be used raw in salads or cooked, and its bitterness fades with cooking, leaving a refined flavor which is more delicate than that of cooked spinach. Chard is an attractive ornamental vegetable that adds color to the vegetable garden.", "cot": "[\"Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.\", \"The passage does not provide a definition for what chard is.\", \"Swiss chard is a leafy green vegetable that is related to beets. It has large, fleshy deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked.\", \"Chard is a leafy green vegetable that is related to beets. It has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. Chard has a stronger, more assertive (some think, bitter) flavor compared to spinach. It can be used raw in salads or cooked, and its bitterness fades with cooking, leaving a refined flavor which is more delicate than that of cooked spinach. Chard is an attractive ornamental vegetable that adds color to the vegetable garden.\"]", "time_sec": 12.819, "generation_time_seconds": 11.9982, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8114, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1143, 567, 374, 264, 48012, 429, 702, 1012, 11882, 369, 15933, 5670, 518, 279, 20284, 315, 5819, 3704, 18003, 13, 1084, 374, 458, 18879, 39445, 43086, 429, 11367, 1894, 311, 279, 35481, 13551, 13, 151645], "pred": "Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.189480781555176, "g_worst_claim": 1.5535821914672852, "g_content": 3.4666460673014323, "g_traj_mean": 2.2674076557159424}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 21085, 1558, 537, 3410, 264, 7271, 369, 1128, 521, 567, 374, 13, 151645], "pred": "The passage does not provide a definition for what chard is.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7756550128643329, "g_worst_claim": 0.7756550128643329, "g_content": 0.38543573021888733, "g_traj_mean": 0.723877489566803}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [13218, 1038, 521, 567, 374, 264, 15933, 88, 6176, 35481, 429, 374, 