{"id": "210", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom, meaning all the atoms in an element have the same number of protons. Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. The individual components of a mixture can be physically separated from each other. Mixtures have variable compositions and show the properties of their constituent substances. Elements and compounds just mix together to form a mixture and no new compound is formed.", "pred": "Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom, where all atoms of the substance have the same number of protons. Compounds are also pure substances, but they are made up of two or more different elements that are chemically bonded together. Mixtures, on the other hand, are not pure substances; they are a combination of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded. Mixtures can have a variable composition, meaning the proportions of the components can vary, and they retain the properties of the individual constituents.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom, where all atoms of the substance have the same number of protons. Compounds are also pure substances, but they are made up of two or more different elements that are chemically bonded together. Mixtures, on the other hand, are not pure substances; they are a combination of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded. Mixtures can have a variable composition, meaning the proportions of the components can vary, and they retain the properties of the individual constituents.", "cot": "[\"Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. In other words, all of the atoms in an element will have the same number of protons. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Compounds are also pure substances. Mixtures can be separated by physical means, while elements and compounds can be separated by physical means.\", \"Elements are composed of only one type of atom and are the purest form of a chemical substance.\\nCompounds are substances composed of two or more different elements and are pure substances. The elements in a compound are chemically bonded and retain their own identity.\\nMixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts are not chemically bonded and retain their own identity. Mixtures have a variable composition and the components can be separated by physical methods.\", \"Elements, compounds, and mixtures differ in their composition and how their components are bonded. Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom, whereas compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements that are chemically bonded. Mixtures, on the other hand, are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Mixtures can contain two or more substances that are relatively easy to separate.\", \"Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom, where all atoms of the substance have the same number of protons. Compounds are also pure substances, but they are made up of two or more different elements that are chemically bonded together. Mixtures, on the other hand, are not pure substances; they are a combination of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded. Mixtures can have a variable composition, meaning the proportions of the components can vary, and they retain the properties of the individual constituents.\"]", "time_sec": 19.199, "generation_time_seconds": 18.1574, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0329, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [11868, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 323, 525, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 13, 758, 1008, 4244, 11, 678, 315, 279, 32199, 304, 458, 2392, 686, 614, 279, 1852, 1372, 315, 462, 34411, 13, 19219, 18513, 525, 264, 6961, 10601, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 315, 279, 20980, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 773, 14060, 862, 1828, 9569, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 32055, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 1083, 10526, 32055, 13, 19219, 18513, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 11, 1393, 5424, 323, 31146, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 13, 151645], "pred": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. In other words, all of the atoms in an element will have the same number of protons. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Compounds are also pure substances. Mixtures can be separated by physical means, while elements and compounds can be separated by physical means.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1665513176692932, "g_worst_claim": 0.6728347937266032, "g_content": 1.5711208767361111, "g_traj_mean": 1.2906312942504883}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [11868, 525, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 323, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 624, 13552, 3095, 525, 32055, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 323, 525, 10526, 32055, 13, 576, 5424, 304, 264, 23628, 525, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 14060, 862, 1828, 9569, 624, 58083, 18513, 525, 264, 6961, 10601, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 14060, 862, 1828, 9569, 13, 19219, 18513, 614, 264, 3890, 18037, 323, 279, 6813, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 5413, 13, 151645], "pred": "Elements are composed of only one type of atom and are the purest form of a chemical substance.\nCompounds are substances composed of two or more different elements and are pure substances. The elements in a compound are chemically bonded and retain their own identity.\nMixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts are not chemically bonded and retain their own identity. Mixtures have a variable composition and the components can be separated by physical methods.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0978567533923271, "g_worst_claim": 0.6597505807876587, "g_content": 1.5821693234327363, "g_traj_mean": 1.070563554763794}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [11868, 11, 31146, 11, 323, 6514, 18513, 1745, 304, 862, 18037, 323, 1246, 862, 6813, 525, 69141, 13, 34157, 525, 10526, 32055, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 11, 19853, 31146, 525, 32055, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 429, 525, 8424, 2673, 69141, 13, 19219, 18513, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 525, 6961, 27459, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 315, 279, 20980, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 773, 14060, 862, 1828, 9569, 13, 19219, 18513, 646, 6644, 1378, 476, 803, 32055, 429, 525, 12040, 4135, 311, 8651, 13, 151645], "pred": "Elements, compounds, and mixtures differ in their composition and how their components are bonded. Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom, whereas compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements that are chemically bonded. Mixtures, on the other hand, are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Mixtures can contain two or more substances that are relatively easy to separate.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.938117864346304, "g_worst_claim": 0.12787851691246033, "g_content": 1.7457144601004464, "g_traj_mean": 1.0727201700210571}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [11868, 525, 10526, 32055, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 11, 1380, 678, 32199, 315, 279, 19699, 614, 279, 1852, 1372, 315, 462, 34411, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 1083, 10526, 32055, 11, 714, 807, 525, 1865, 705, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 429, 525, 8424, 2673, 69141, 3786, 13, 19219, 18513, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 525, 537, 10526, 32055, 26, 807, 525, 264, 10601, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 6813, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 13, 19219, 18513, 646, 614, 264, 3890, 18037, 11, 7290, 279, 48792, 315, 279, 6813, 646, 13289, 11, 323, 807, 14060, 279, 5888, 315, 279, 3842, 50620, 13, 151645], "pred": "Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom, where all atoms of the substance have the same number of protons. Compounds are also pure substances, but they are made up of two or more different elements that are chemically bonded together. Mixtures, on the other hand, are not pure substances; they are a combination of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded. Mixtures can have a variable composition, meaning the proportions of the components can vary, and they retain the properties of the individual constituents.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.45114904988886767, "g_worst_claim": -0.0603506326675415, "g_content": 0.6302280426025391, "g_traj_mean": 0.4010932147502899}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 62.69, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "211", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom, with all atoms having the same number of protons. Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded, allowing for easy separation of the components using physical methods.", "pred": "Mixtures contain two or more substances, such as the atmosphere, which can be physically separated. Elements, on the other hand, are composed of only one type of atom, and their properties can be separated by physical means. Compounds are substances made up of two or more different elements, with the properties of the constituent elements combined.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Mixtures contain two or more substances, such as the atmosphere, which can be physically separated. Elements, on the other hand, are composed of only one type of atom, and their properties can be separated by physical means. Compounds are substances made up of two or more different elements, with the properties of the constituent elements combined.", "cot": "[\"Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. In other words, all of the atoms in an element will have the same number of protons. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Compounds are also pure substances. Mixtures can be separated by physical means, while elements and compounds can be separated by physical means.\", \"Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom, while compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Mixtures, on the other hand, are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Additionally, elements and compounds can be separated by physical means, and mixtures can be easily separated by physical methods.\", \"Mixtures contain two or more substances, such as the atmosphere, which can be physically separated. Elements, on the other hand, are composed of only one type of atom, and their properties can be separated by physical means. Compounds are substances made up of two or more different elements, with the properties of the constituent elements combined.\", \"Elements:\\nElements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. All of the atoms in an element will have the same number of protons.\\n\\nCompounds:\\nCompounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Compounds are also pure substances. The elements in a compound are chemically bonded together, resulting in a mixture where the parts are not easily separable.\\n\\nMixtures:\\nMixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts are not chemically bonded. The elements and compounds in a mixture retain their own identity and can be separated by physical means.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n1) Elements are composed of a single type of atom, while compounds and mixtures consist of two or more different elements.\\n2) Elements are pure substances, whereas compounds and mixtures may not be pure.\\n3) The elements in a compound are chemically bonded, while the constituents of a mixture are not.\\n4) Elements cannot be separated by physical means, while compounds and mixtures can be separated by physical methods.\"]", "time_sec": 21.754, "generation_time_seconds": 20.9747, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7716, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [11868, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 323, 525, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 13, 758, 1008, 4244, 11, 678, 315, 279, 32199, 304, 458, 2392, 686, 614, 279, 1852, 1372, 315, 462, 34411, 13, 19219, 18513, 525, 264, 6961, 10601, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 315, 279, 20980, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 773, 14060, 862, 1828, 9569, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 32055, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 1083, 10526, 32055, 13, 19219, 18513, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 11, 1393, 5424, 323, 31146, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 13, 151645], "pred": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. In other words, all of the atoms in an element will have the same number of protons. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Compounds are also pure substances. Mixtures can be separated by physical means, while elements and compounds can be separated by physical means.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.170409235728694, "g_worst_claim": 0.7048590977986654, "g_content": 1.5302383422851562, "g_traj_mean": 1.276476502418518}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [11868, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 323, 525, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 11, 1393, 31146, 525, 32055, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 13, 19219, 18513, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 525, 6961, 27459, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 315, 279, 20980, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 773, 14060, 862, 1828, 9569, 13, 22406, 11, 5424, 323, 31146, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 11, 323, 6514, 18513, 646, 387, 6707, 18663, 553, 6961, 5413, 13, 151645], "pred": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom, while compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Mixtures, on the other hand, are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Additionally, elements and compounds can be separated by physical means, and mixtures can be easily separated by physical methods.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3043136732506029, "g_worst_claim": 0.6954702536265055, "g_content": 1.7054548997145433, "g_traj_mean": 1.296134352684021}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [58083, 18513, 6644, 1378, 476, 803, 32055, 11, 1741, 438, 279, 16566, 11, 892, 646, 387, 21893, 18663, 13, 34157, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 525, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 11, 323, 862, 5888, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 32055, 1865, 705, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 11, 448, 279, 5888, 315, 279, 74064, 5424, 10856, 13, 151645], "pred": "Mixtures contain two or more substances, such as the atmosphere, which can be physically separated. Elements, on the other hand, are composed of only one type of atom, and their properties can be separated by physical means. Compounds are substances made up of two or more different elements, with the properties of the constituent elements combined.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9272798669304265, "g_worst_claim": 0.20209701244647688, "g_content": 1.329454750850283, "g_traj_mean": 0.8259490728378296}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [11868, 510, 11868, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 323, 525, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 13, 2009, 315, 279, 32199, 304, 458, 2392, 686, 614, 279, 1852, 1372, 315, 462, 34411, 382, 13552, 3095, 510, 13552, 3095, 525, 32055, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 1083, 10526, 32055, 13, 576, 5424, 304, 264, 23628, 525, 8424, 2673, 69141, 3786, 11, 12942, 304, 264, 20980, 1380, 279, 5479, 525, 537, 6707, 4836, 480, 382, 58083, 18513, 510, 58083, 18513, 525, 264, 6961, 10601, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 13, 576, 5424, 323, 31146, 304, 264, 20980, 14060, 862, 1828, 9569, 323, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 382, 35, 58326, 510, 16, 8, 34157, 525, 23415, 315, 264, 3175, 943, 315, 19124, 11, 1393, 31146, 323, 6514, 18513, 6685, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 624, 17, 8, 34157, 525, 10526, 32055, 11, 19853, 31146, 323, 6514, 18513, 1231, 537, 387, 10526, 624, 18, 8, 576, 5424, 304, 264, 23628, 525, 8424, 2673, 69141, 11, 1393, 279, 50620, 315, 264, 20980, 525, 537, 624, 19, 8, 34157, 4157, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 11, 1393, 31146, 323, 6514, 18513, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 5413, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences:\n1) Elements are composed of a single type of atom, while compounds and mixtures consist of two or more different elements.\n2) Elements are pure substances, whereas compounds and mixtures may not be pure.\n3) The elements in a compound are chemically bonded, while the constituents of a mixture are not.\n4) Elements cannot be separated by physical means, while compounds and mixtures can be separated by physical methods.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.4872975382154545, "g_worst_claim": 0.028824942807356518, "g_content": 0.6905055668043054, "g_traj_mean": 0.5733668804168701}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.37, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "212", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Here are my answers to the question based on the provided passages:\n\nQ: What are the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures?\nA: Based on the passages provided, here are the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures:\n\nElements:\n\n* Are the purest form of a chemical substance (Passage 3)\n* Consist of only one type of atom with the same number of protons (Passage 3)\n\nCompounds:\n\n* Are substances composed of two or more different elements (Passage 3)\n* Are also pure substances (Passage 3)\n\nMixtures:\n\n* Contain two or more substances that are relatively easy to separate (Passage 1)\n* Have a variable composition (Passage 2)\n* Show the properties of their constituent substances (Passage 2)\n* Can be separated by physical means (Passage 2)", "pred": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. In other words, all of the atoms in an element will have the same number of protons. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Compounds are also pure substances. Mixtures can be separated by physical means, while elements and compounds can be separated by physical means.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. In other words, all of the atoms in an element will have the same number of protons. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Compounds are also pure substances. Mixtures can be separated by physical means, while elements and compounds can be separated by physical means.", "cot": "[\"Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. In other words, all of the atoms in an element will have the same number of protons. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Compounds are also pure substances. Mixtures can be separated by physical means, while elements and compounds can be separated by physical means.\", \"Elements, compounds, and mixtures differ in several ways:\\n\\n1. **Composition**:\\n   - **Elements**: Consist of only one type of atom. For example, oxygen (O) and carbon (C) are elements.\\n   - **Compounds**: Composed of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. For example, water (H₂O) is a compound made of hydrogen (H) and oxygen (O) atoms.\\n   - **Mixtures**: Contain two or more substances present in variable proportions. For example, air is a mixture of nitrogen, oxygen, carbon dioxide, and other gases.\\n\\n2. **Separability**:\\n   - **Elements**: Cannot be separated by physical means because their atoms are tightly bonded. For example, iron (Fe) cannot be separated into pure iron by simple physical methods.\\n   - **Compounds**: Can be separated by physical means because they are composed of different elements. For example, table salt (NaCl) can be separated into sodium (Na) and chlorine (Cl) by physical methods.\\n   - **Mixtures**: Can be separated into their constituent substances by physical means. For example, air can be separated into its components (oxygen, nitrogen, etc.) through distillation or other physical processes.\\n\\n3. **Formation**:\\n   - **Elements**: Formed by a single type of atom. Elements are pure substances.\\n   - **Compounds**: Formed by the combination of two or more different elements. Compounds are also pure substances.\\n   - **Mixtures**: Formed by the combination of elements or compounds where the parts retain their own identity. Mixtures are not pure substances.\\n\\n4. **Properties**:\\n   - **Elements**: Display the properties of their constituent atoms. For example, copper (Cu) is a conductor of electricity, and carbon (C) can form various allotropes (diamond, graphite).\\n   - **Compounds**: Display the properties of the compounds formed. For example, carbon dioxide (CO₂) is a gas at room temperature, and sodium chloride (NaCl) is a solid.\\n   - **Mixtures**: Show the properties of the constituent substances. For example, a solution of salt and water displays the properties of both salt and water.\\n\\nIn summary, elements are composed of a single type of atom and are the purest form of a chemical substance. Compounds are made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together and are also pure substances. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds\", \"Elements, compounds, and mixtures have several differences.\\n\\nElements are composed of only one type of atom, and all of the atoms in an element will have the same number of protons. This makes them the purest form of a chemical substance.\\n\\nCompounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements. These elements are chemically bonded together, resulting in a different chemical composition than the individual elements. Compounds are also pure substances.\\n\\nMixtures, unlike elements and compounds, do not have a fixed composition. They are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Mixtures can be separated by physical means.\\n\\nAdditionally, mixtures are variable in composition, meaning that they can have different proportions of the constituent substances. Elements and compounds, on the other hand, have a fixed composition, and their properties will not change regardless of the proportion of the individual elements or compounds present.\\n\\nFurthermore, the ease with which elements can be separated from each other is different from that of compounds and mixtures. Compounds and mixtures can have their individual components chemically bonded or physically combined, respectively, making them more difficult to separate from each other.\", \"Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance composed of only one type of atom, while compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Mixtures can be separated by physical means, while elements and compounds can be separated by physical means as well.\"]", "time_sec": 35.885, "generation_time_seconds": 34.6475, "selection_time_seconds": 1.2287, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [11868, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 323, 525, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 13, 758, 1008, 4244, 11, 678, 315, 279, 32199, 304, 458, 2392, 686, 614, 279, 1852, 1372, 315, 462, 34411, 13, 19219, 18513, 525, 264, 6961, 10601, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 315, 279, 20980, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 773, 14060, 862, 1828, 9569, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 32055, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 1083, 10526, 32055, 13, 19219, 18513, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 11, 1393, 5424, 323, 31146, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 13, 151645], "pred": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. In other words, all of the atoms in an element will have the same number of protons. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Compounds are also pure substances. Mixtures can be separated by physical means, while elements and compounds can be separated by physical means.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1574687669557828, "g_worst_claim": 0.6765431298149956, "g_content": 1.540443589952257, "g_traj_mean": 1.2781106233596802}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [11868, 11, 31146, 11, 323, 6514, 18513, 1745, 304, 3807, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 75683, 334, 510, 256, 481, 3070, 11868, 95518, 7292, 380, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 23552, 320, 46, 8, 323, 12499, 320, 34, 8, 525, 5424, 624, 256, 481, 3070, 13552, 3095, 95518, 1198, 3865, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 8424, 2673, 69141, 3786, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 3015, 320, 39, 31807, 46, 8, 374, 264, 23628, 1865, 315, 34684, 320, 39, 8, 323, 23552, 320, 46, 8, 32199, 624, 256, 481, 3070, 58083, 18513, 95518, 2093, 466, 1378, 476, 803, 32055, 3042, 304, 3890, 48792, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 3720, 374, 264, 20980, 315, 46403, 11, 23552, 11, 12499, 39489, 11, 323, 1008, 44512, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 14492, 2897, 334, 510, 256, 481, 3070, 11868, 95518, 34655, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 1576, 862, 32199, 525, 38969, 69141, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 11001, 320, 6123, 8, 4157, 387, 18663, 1119, 10526, 11001, 553, 4285, 6961, 5413, 624, 256, 481, 3070, 13552, 3095, 95518, 2980, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 1576, 807, 525, 23415, 315, 2155, 5424, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 1965, 12021, 320, 16193, 5066, 8, 646, 387, 18663, 1119, 38595, 320, 16193, 8, 323, 84106, 320, 5066, 8, 553, 6961, 5413, 624, 256, 481, 3070, 58083, 18513, 95518, 2980, 387, 18663, 1119, 862, 74064, 32055, 553, 6961, 3363, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 3720, 646, 387, 18663, 1119, 1181, 6813, 320, 78, 18936, 11, 46403, 11, 4992, 6138, 1526, 1582, 66084, 476, 1008, 6961, 11364, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 59458, 334, 510, 256, 481, 3070, 11868, 95518, 3377, 291, 553, 264, 3175, 943, 315, 19124, 13, 34157, 525, 10526, 32055, 624, 256, 481, 3070, 13552, 3095, 95518, 3377, 291, 553, 279, 10601, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 1083, 10526, 32055, 624, 256, 481, 3070, 58083, 18513, 95518, 3377, 291, 553, 279, 10601, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 14060, 862, 1828, 9569, 13, 19219, 18513, 525, 537, 10526, 32055, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 7903, 334, 510, 256, 481, 3070, 11868, 95518, 10623, 279, 5888, 315, 862, 74064, 32199, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 23285, 320, 44819, 8, 374, 264, 60756, 315, 17728, 11, 323, 12499, 320, 34, 8, 646, 1352, 5257, 84174, 887, 288, 320, 88576, 11, 94173, 4292, 256, 481, 3070, 13552, 3095, 95518, 10623, 279, 5888, 315, 279, 31146, 14122, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 12499, 39489, 320, 8281, 31807, 8, 374, 264, 6819, 518, 3054, 9315, 11, 323, 38595, 81782, 320, 16193, 5066, 8, 374, 264, 6437, 624, 256, 481, 3070, 58083, 18513, 95518, 6928, 279, 5888, 315, 279, 74064, 32055, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 264, 6291, 315, 12021, 323, 3015, 18689, 279, 5888, 315, 2176, 12021, 323, 3015, 382, 641, 12126, 11, 5424, 525, 23415, 315, 264, 3175, 943, 315, 19124, 323, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 1865, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 8424, 2673, 69141, 3786, 323, 525, 1083, 10526, 32055, 13, 19219, 18513, 525, 6961, 27459, 315, 5424, 476, 31146], "pred": "In summary, elements are composed of a single type of atom and are the purest form of a chemical substance. Compounds are made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together and are also pure substances. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.19569072865881362, "g_worst_claim": -0.08838816881179809, "g_content": 0.3915574573335193, "g_traj_mean": 0.21033161878585815}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [11868, 11, 31146, 11, 323, 6514, 18513, 614, 3807, 11799, 382, 11868, 525, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 11, 323, 678, 315, 279, 32199, 304, 458, 2392, 686, 614, 279, 1852, 1372, 315, 462, 34411, 13, 1096, 3643, 1105, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 382, 13552, 3095, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 525, 32055, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 13, 4220, 5424, 525, 8424, 2673, 69141, 3786, 11, 12942, 304, 264, 2155, 11483, 18037, 1091, 279, 3842, 5424, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 1083, 10526, 32055, 382, 58083, 18513, 11, 19836, 5424, 323, 31146, 11, 653, 537, 614, 264, 8356, 18037, 13, 2379, 525, 6961, 27459, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 315, 279, 20980, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 773, 14060, 862, 1828, 9569, 13, 19219, 18513, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 382, 49574, 11, 6514, 18513, 525, 3890, 304, 18037, 11, 7290, 429, 807, 646, 614, 2155, 48792, 315, 279, 74064, 32055, 13, 34157, 323, 31146, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 614, 264, 8356, 18037, 11, 323, 862, 5888, 686, 537, 2297, 15484, 315, 279, 21117, 315, 279, 3842, 5424, 476, 31146, 3042, 382, 56317, 11, 279, 14219, 448, 892, 5424, 646, 387, 18663, 504, 1817, 1008, 374, 2155, 504, 429, 315, 31146, 323, 6514, 18513, 13, 13317, 3095, 323, 6514, 18513, 646, 614, 862, 3842, 6813, 8424, 2673, 69141, 476, 21893, 10856, 11, 15576, 11, 3259, 1105, 803, 5000, 311, 8651, 504, 1817, 1008, 13, 151645], "pred": "Furthermore, the ease with which elements can be separated from each other is different from that of compounds and mixtures. Compounds and mixtures can have their individual components chemically bonded or physically combined, respectively, making them more difficult to separate from each other.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.5547084690910341, "g_worst_claim": -0.050625985860824584, "g_content": 0.8541486358642578, "g_traj_mean": 0.6757408380508423}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [11868, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 11, 1393, 31146, 525, 32055, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 13, 19219, 18513, 525, 264, 6961, 10601, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 315, 279, 20980, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 773, 14060, 862, 1828, 9569, 13, 19219, 18513, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 11, 1393, 5424, 323, 31146, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 438, 1632, 13, 151645], "pred": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance composed of only one type of atom, while compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Mixtures can be separated by physical means, while elements and compounds can be separated by physical means as well.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0857033537421032, "g_worst_claim": 0.41260859701368546, "g_content": 1.6383593709845292, "g_traj_mean": 1.2701265811920166}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 49.65, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "213", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are:\n\n* Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. They have a fixed composition and cannot be broken down into simpler substances by physical means.\n* Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements that are chemically bonded together. They have a fixed composition and are pure substances.\n* Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and retain their own identity. They have a variable composition and can be separated by physical means.\n\nTherefore, the key differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are their composition, bonding, and separability. Elements are homogeneous and have a fixed composition, compounds are heterogeneous and have a fixed composition, and mixtures are heterogeneous and have a variable composition. Additionally, elements and compounds are chemically bonded, while mixtures are not.", "pred": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. In other words, all of the atoms in an element will have the same number of protons. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Compounds are also pure substances. Mixtures can be separated by physical means, while elements and compounds can be separated by physical means.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. In other words, all of the atoms in an element will have the same number of protons. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Compounds are also pure substances. Mixtures can be separated by physical means, while elements and compounds can be separated by physical means.", "cot": "[\"Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. In other words, all of the atoms in an element will have the same number of protons. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Compounds are also pure substances. Mixtures can be separated by physical means, while elements and compounds can be separated by physical means.\", \"elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity.\", \"Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom, while compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. Mixtures, on the other hand, are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts are not chemically bonded and retain their own identity. Mixtures can be easily separated by physical means, whereas the separation of elements and compounds requires chemical means. Another key difference is that mixtures have a variable composition, while compounds have a fixed composition.\", \"Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. In other words, all of the atoms in an element will have the same number of protons. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Compounds are also pure substances. A mixture is a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Mixtures can be easily separated by physical methods, and the components can be identified and characterized individually.\"]", "time_sec": 17.845, "generation_time_seconds": 17.0029, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8333, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [11868, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 323, 525, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 13, 758, 1008, 4244, 11, 678, 315, 279, 32199, 304, 458, 2392, 686, 614, 279, 1852, 1372, 315, 462, 34411, 13, 19219, 18513, 525, 264, 6961, 10601, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 315, 279, 20980, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 773, 14060, 862, 1828, 9569, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 32055, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 1083, 10526, 32055, 13, 19219, 18513, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 11, 1393, 5424, 323, 31146, 646, 387, 18663, 553, 6961, 3363, 13, 151645], "pred": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. In other words, all of the atoms in an element will have the same number of protons. Mixtures are a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Compounds are also pure substances. Mixtures can be separated by physical means, while elements and compounds can be separated by physical means.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1654994862862555, "g_worst_claim": 0.6591343879699707, "g_content": 1.5340157402886285, "g_traj_mean": 1.27944564