can be easily separated by physical means, whereas the separation of elements and compounds requires chemical means. Another key difference is that mixtures have a variable composition, while compounds have a fixed composition.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8022219363042625, "g_worst_claim": 0.2248615367071969, "g_content": 1.1927063611088966, "g_traj_mean": 0.9068213105201721}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [11868, 525, 279, 10526, 267, 1352, 315, 264, 11483, 19699, 323, 525, 23415, 315, 1172, 825, 943, 315, 19124, 13, 758, 1008, 4244, 11, 678, 315, 279, 32199, 304, 458, 2392, 686, 614, 279, 1852, 1372, 315, 462, 34411, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 32055, 23415, 315, 1378, 476, 803, 2155, 5424, 13, 13317, 3095, 525, 1083, 10526, 32055, 13, 362, 20980, 374, 264, 6961, 10601, 315, 5424, 476, 31146, 1380, 279, 5479, 315, 279, 20980, 525, 537, 8424, 2673, 69141, 323, 773, 14060, 862, 1828, 9569, 13, 19219, 18513, 646, 387, 6707, 18663, 553, 6961, 5413, 11, 323, 279, 6813, 646, 387, 10820, 323, 31871, 31299, 13, 151645], "pred": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. In other words, all of the atoms in an element will have the same number of protons. Compounds are substances composed of two or more different elements. Compounds are also pure substances. A mixture is a physical combination of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. Mixtures can be easily separated by physical methods, and the components can be identified and characterized individually.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0257231514470109, "g_worst_claim": 0.46863865852355957, "g_content": 1.3412956237792968, "g_traj_mean": 1.1856272220611572}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 56.63, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "214", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "To properly wash wine glasses, you should scrub them by hand as it's the safest cleaning method. First, lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. If hot water and mild detergent can’t get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.", "pred": "To wash wine glasses properly, you can use baking soda and hot water to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To wash wine glasses properly, you can use baking soda and hot water to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.", "cot": "[\"To wash wine glasses properly, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Hand Wash**: The safest method is to scrub the glasses by hand. Lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n\\n2. **Detergent Use**: Use a small amount of detergent, applying it only where needed, such as in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. This helps prevent soap from flavoring your next glass of wine.\\n\\n3. **Protect the Stem**: Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\\n\\n4. **Dry with a Cloth**: After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n\\n5. **Baking Soda Method**: If hot water and mild detergent don't work, use baking soda. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n\\n6. **Stemware Brush**: For the inside of the glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that your wine glasses are thoroughly and safely cleaned.\", \"To wash wine glasses properly, you can use baking soda and hot water to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\", \"To properly wash wine glasses, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Hand Wash**: The safest method is to scrub the glasses by hand. Lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n2. **Detergent**: Use a small amount of detergent, applied only where it's needed – at the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Avoid using too much detergent as it may leave a flavor in your next glass of wine.\\n3. **Cradle the Bowl**: Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the delicate stem.\\n4. **Dry with a Cloth**: After washing, rinse thoroughly with hot water and dry the glass using a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n\\nThese steps will ensure that your wine glasses are clean and ready for use without any chips or spots.\", \"To wash wine glasses properly, you can follow these steps:\\n1. For stubborn wine residue, use baking soda dissolved in hot water, allowing it to stand in the glass for a few minutes.\\n2. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\\n3. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n4. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed – in the bottom of the glass and around the rim.\\n5. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\\n6. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\"]", "time_sec": 25.331, "generation_time_seconds": 24.7117, "selection_time_seconds": 0.612, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 11369, 13078, 28147, 10277, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2314, 5985, 95518, 576, 61744, 1714, 374, 311, 44901, 279, 28147, 553, 1424, 13, 43924, 264, 42613, 304, 279, 19309, 1573, 21274, 432, 448, 4017, 3015, 13, 5985, 825, 8991, 518, 264, 882, 311, 5648, 5557, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 35, 1404, 15772, 5443, 95518, 5443, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 90134, 11, 18950, 432, 1172, 1380, 4362, 11, 1741, 438, 304, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 8991, 323, 2163, 279, 30130, 13, 1096, 8609, 5358, 26785, 504, 17172, 287, 697, 1790, 8991, 315, 13078, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 61547, 279, 80848, 95518, 4553, 71355, 279, 19212, 315, 279, 8991, 304, 825, 1424, 1393, 27686, 311, 6016, 279, 19101, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 85215, 448, 264, 83635, 95518, 4636, 96039, 287, 26364, 448, 4017, 3015, 11, 9058, 279, 13078, 28147, 448, 264, 10876, 57920, 12577, 27292, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 8003, 82945, 476, 19828, 52333, 42613, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 33, 1765, 96072, 6730, 95518, 1416, 4017, 3015, 323, 23034, 90134, 1513, 944, 975, 11, 990, 27815, 38862, 13, 51032, 3948, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 38862, 448, 4017, 3015, 323, 1077, 432, 2498, 304, 279, 8991, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 13, 576, 38862, 686, 72639, 894, 32147, 13078, 34951, 287, 311, 279, 8991, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 623, 336, 1664, 32988, 95518, 1752, 279, 4766, 315, 279, 8991, 11, 990, 264, 19101, 1664, 15625, 448, 8413, 12, 824, 309, 1411, 65943, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 5978, 429, 697, 13078, 28147, 525, 26364, 323, 21000, 27722, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can ensure that your wine glasses are thoroughly and safely cleaned.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4981271621922456, "g_worst_claim": 0.27789849042892456, "g_content": 2.060289510091146, "g_traj_mean": 1.4489636421203613}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 11369, 13078, 28147, 10277, 11, 498, 646, 990, 27815, 38862, 323, 4017, 3015, 311, 4057, 894, 51396, 13078, 48132, 13, 51032, 3948, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 38862, 448, 4017, 3015, 323, 1077, 432, 2498, 304, 279, 8991, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 13, 576, 38862, 686, 72639, 894, 32147, 13078, 34951, 287, 311, 279, 8991, 13, 151645], "pred": "To wash wine glasses properly, you can use baking soda and hot water to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8595008601119747, "g_worst_claim": 1.6079058329264322, "g_content": 2.5086501549030173, "g_traj_mean": 1.8669257164001465}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 10277, 11369, 13078, 28147, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2314, 5985, 95518, 576, 61744, 1714, 374, 311, 44901, 279, 28147, 553, 1424, 13, 43924, 264, 42613, 304, 279, 19309, 1573, 21274, 432, 448, 4017, 3015, 13, 5985, 825, 8991, 518, 264, 882, 311, 5648, 5557, 624, 17, 13, 3070, 35, 1404, 15772, 95518, 5443, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 90134, 11, 9251, 1172, 1380, 432, 594, 4362, 1365, 518, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 8991, 323, 2163, 279, 30130, 13, 34006, 1667, 2238, 1753, 90134, 438, 432, 1231, 5274, 264, 17172, 304, 697, 1790, 8991, 315, 13078, 624, 18, 13, 3070, 34, 13281, 273, 279, 20288, 95518, 4553, 71355, 279, 19212, 315, 279, 8991, 304, 825, 1424, 1393, 27686, 311, 6016, 279, 35201, 19101, 624, 19, 13, 3070, 85215, 448, 264, 83635, 95518, 4636, 27686, 11, 73241, 26364, 448, 4017, 3015, 323, 9058, 279, 8991, 1667, 264, 10876, 57920, 12577, 27292, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 8003, 82945, 476, 19828, 52333, 42613, 382, 9485, 7354, 686, 5978, 429, 697, 13078, 28147, 525, 4240, 323, 5527, 369, 990, 2041, 894, 23595, 476, 18773, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps will ensure that your wine glasses are clean and ready for use without any chips or spots.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2024005348635287, "g_worst_claim": 0.11900822321573894, "g_content": 1.5287186195110452, "g_traj_mean": 1.1582715511322021}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 11369, 13078, 28147, 10277, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 1752, 51396, 13078, 48132, 11, 990, 27815, 38862, 55667, 304, 4017, 3015, 11, 10693, 432, 311, 2498, 304, 279, 8991, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 17, 13, 5443, 264, 19101, 1664, 15625, 448, 8413, 12, 824, 309, 1411, 65943, 311, 4240, 279, 4766, 315, 279, 8991, 624, 18, 13, 5985, 825, 13078, 8991, 518, 264, 882, 311, 5648, 5557, 624, 19, 13, 5443, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 90134, 1172, 1380, 432, 594, 4362, 1365, 304, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 8991, 323, 2163, 279, 30130, 624, 20, 13, 4553, 71355, 279, 19212, 315, 279, 8991, 304, 825, 1424, 1393, 27686, 311, 6016, 279, 19101, 624, 21, 13, 4636, 96039, 287, 26364, 448, 4017, 3015, 11, 9058, 279, 13078, 28147, 448, 264, 10876, 57920, 12577, 27292, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 8003, 82945, 476, 19828, 52333, 42613, 13, 151645], "pred": "To wash wine glasses properly, you can follow these steps:\n1. For stubborn wine residue, use baking soda dissolved in hot water, allowing it to stand in the glass for a few minutes.\n2. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\n3. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\n4. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed – in the bottom of the glass and around the rim.\n5. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n6. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6959183540323959, "g_worst_claim": 0.20691609382629395, "g_content": 1.9265889061821833, "g_traj_mean": 1.5123213529586792}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 47.89, "GAVIE-Rel": 3.3, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "215", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "To wash wine glasses properly, start by using hot water and mild detergent to clean the outside of the glass. If there are stubborn wine residues, use baking soda to dissolve them by mixing a small amount of soda with hot water and letting it sit in the glass for a few minutes. For cleaning the inside of the glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. Rinse thoroughly with hot water and dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth. To avoid damage, wash one wine glass at a time, use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed, and cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "pred": "To wash wine glasses properly, you can use baking soda if hot water and mild detergent are not effective. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass. Alternatively, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. The safest cleaning method for your wine glasses is to scrub them by hand, using a small amount of detergent only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To wash wine glasses properly, you can use baking soda if hot water and mild detergent are not effective. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass. Alternatively, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. The safest cleaning method for your wine glasses is to scrub them by hand, using a small amount of detergent only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "cot": "[\"To wash wine glasses properly, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Hand Wash**: The safest method is to scrub the glasses by hand. Lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n\\n2. **Detergent Use**: Use a small amount of detergent, applying it only where needed, such as in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. This helps prevent soap from flavoring your next glass of wine.\\n\\n3. **Protect the Stem**: Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\\n\\n4. **Dry with a Cloth**: After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n\\n5. **Baking Soda Method**: If hot water and mild detergent don't work, use baking soda. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n\\n6. **Stemware Brush**: For the inside of the glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that your wine glasses are thoroughly and safely cleaned.\", \"To properly wash wine glasses, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Hand Wash**: The safest method is to scrub the glasses by hand. Lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n\\n2. **Detergent**: Use a small amount of detergent, but only where it's needed – in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. This helps avoid flavoring the next glass of wine.\\n\\n3. **Brush**: Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass. This ensures a thorough clean.\\n\\n4. **Dry**: After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n\\n5. **Baking Soda Method**: For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that your wine glasses are clean and ready for use without causing damage or leaving any residue that could affect the taste of the wine.\", \"To wash wine glasses properly, you should follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Hand Wash**: The safest method is to scrub the wine glasses by hand to avoid chips and spots. Place a clean towel in the sink before adding hot water to protect the glass.\\n   \\n2. **Detergent Use**: Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed, such as at the bottom of the glass and around the rim. This prevents the soap from flavoring your next glass of wine.\\n\\n3. **Protect the Stem**: Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. This ensures that both the bowl and the stem are cleaned thoroughly without any damage.\\n\\n4. **Rinse and Dry**: After washing, rinse the glasses thoroughly with hot water and dry them using a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n\\n5. **Clean with Baking Soda (Optional)**: For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water and let it sit in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n\\n6. **Clean with a Stemware Brush (Optional)**: If available, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively clean your wine glasses without damaging them and ensure they are ready for the next use.\", \"To wash wine glasses properly, you can use baking soda if hot water and mild detergent are not effective. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass. Alternatively, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. The safest cleaning method for your wine glasses is to scrub them by hand, using a small amount of detergent only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\"]", "time_sec": 35.535, "generation_time_seconds": 34.8009, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7288, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 11369, 13078, 28147, 10277, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2314, 5985, 95518, 576, 61744, 1714, 374, 311, 44901, 279, 28147, 553, 1424, 13, 43924, 264, 42613, 304, 279, 19309, 1573, 21274, 432, 448, 4017, 3015, 13, 5985, 825, 8991, 518, 264, 882, 311, 5648, 5557, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 35, 1404, 15772, 5443, 95518, 5443, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 90134, 11, 18950, 432, 1172, 1380, 4362, 11, 1741, 438, 304, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 8991, 323, 2163, 279, 30130, 13, 1096, 8609, 5358, 26785, 504, 17172, 287, 697, 1790, 8991, 315, 13078, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 61547, 279, 80848, 95518, 4553, 71355, 279, 19212, 315, 279, 8991, 304, 825, 1424, 1393, 27686, 311, 6016, 279, 19101, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 85215, 448, 264, 83635, 95518, 4636, 96039, 287, 26364, 448, 4017, 3015, 11, 9058, 279, 13078, 28147, 448, 264, 10876, 57920, 12577, 27292, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 8003, 82945, 476, 19828, 52333, 42613, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 33, 1765, 96072, 6730, 95518, 1416, 4017, 3015, 323, 23034, 90134, 1513, 944, 975, 11, 990, 27815, 38862, 13, 51032, 3948, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 38862, 448, 4017, 301