{"id": "216", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are the steps to properly wash wine glasses:\n\n1. If hot water and mild detergent cannot remove wine residue, use baking soda to dissolve and loosen the adhesive residue (Passage 1).\n2. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles and rinse thoroughly with hot water (Passage 2).\n3. For hand cleaning, lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water and wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage (Passage 3). Use a small amount of detergent and only in the bottom of the glass and around the rim to avoid flavoring future wine. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "To wash wine glasses properly, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass. Following that, rinse them thoroughly with hot water and dry them with a microfiber or flour sack towel. For a hand wash, lay a towel in the sink, fill it with hot water, and wash one glass at a time. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed, such as at the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To wash wine glasses properly, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass. Following that, rinse them thoroughly with hot water and dry them with a microfiber or flour sack towel. For a hand wash, lay a towel in the sink, fill it with hot water, and wash one glass at a time. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed, such as at the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "cot": "[\"To wash wine glasses properly, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Hand Wash**: The safest method is to scrub the glasses by hand. Lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n\\n2. **Detergent Use**: Use a small amount of detergent, applying it only where needed, such as in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. This helps prevent soap from flavoring your next glass of wine.\\n\\n3. **Protect the Stem**: Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\\n\\n4. **Dry with a Cloth**: After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\\n\\n5. **Baking Soda Method**: If hot water and mild detergent don't work, use baking soda. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass.\\n\\n6. **Stemware Brush**: For the inside of the glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that your wine glasses are thoroughly and safely cleaned.\", \"To wash wine glasses properly, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass. Following that, rinse them thoroughly with hot water and dry them with a microfiber or flour sack towel. For a hand wash, lay a towel in the sink, fill it with hot water, and wash one glass at a time. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed, such as at the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\", \"To wash wine glasses properly, follow these steps:\\n1. Lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage.\\n2. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim.\\n3. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\\n4. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.\", \"To properly wash wine glasses, you can use baking soda and mild detergent, or a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. For hand washing, lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water, and wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed, in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\"]", "time_sec": 23.661, "generation_time_seconds": 23.0349, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6202, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 11369, 13078, 28147, 10277, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2314, 5985, 95518, 576, 61744, 1714, 374, 311, 44901, 279, 28147, 553, 1424, 13, 43924, 264, 42613, 304, 279, 19309, 1573, 21274, 432, 448, 4017, 3015, 13, 5985, 825, 8991, 518, 264, 882, 311, 5648, 5557, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 35, 1404, 15772, 5443, 95518, 5443, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 90134, 11, 18950, 432, 1172, 1380, 4362, 11, 1741, 438, 304, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 8991, 323, 2163, 279, 30130, 13, 1096, 8609, 5358, 26785, 504, 17172, 287, 697, 1790, 8991, 315, 13078, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 61547, 279, 80848, 95518, 4553, 71355, 279, 19212, 315, 279, 8991, 304, 825, 1424, 1393, 27686, 311, 6016, 279, 19101, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 85215, 448, 264, 83635, 95518, 4636, 96039, 287, 26364, 448, 4017, 3015, 11, 9058, 279, 13078, 28147, 448, 264, 10876, 57920, 12577, 27292, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 8003, 82945, 476, 19828, 52333, 42613, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 33, 1765, 96072, 6730, 95518, 1416, 4017, 3015, 323, 23034, 90134, 1513, 944, 975, 11, 990, 27815, 38862, 13, 51032, 3948, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 38862, 448, 4017, 3015, 323, 1077, 432, 2498, 304, 279, 8991, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 13, 576, 38862, 686, 72639, 894, 32147, 13078, 34951, 287, 311, 279, 8991, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 623, 336, 