 hand washing, lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water, and wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of detergent and use it only where it's needed, in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8897387419498806, "g_worst_claim": 1.1661068309437146, "g_content": 2.3662557399019284, "g_traj_mean": 1.9547337293624878}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.14, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "221", "question": "how to peel potatoes fast", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to peel potatoes fast:\n\n1. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n2. Boil the potatoes for about 15 minutes.\n3. Place the potatoes in a bowl of ice water and swish them around for a few seconds.\n4. Remove the potatoes from the water and remove the skin.\n\nAlternatively, you can also try the following method:\n\n1. Cut the potato skin, making a cut all around the potato lengthwise.\n2. Boil the potato in a pot of boiling water.\n3. Plunge the potato in ice water for 10 seconds.\n4. Rub the potato with both hands, and the skin should fall right off.\n\nThese methods should help you peel potatoes quickly and efficiently.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can peel potatoes quickly and efficiently.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "By following these steps, you can peel potatoes quickly and efficiently.", "cot": "[\"To peel potatoes fast, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Score the Potatoes**: Use a knife to score the potatoes all the way around the center. This helps the skin to come off more easily.\\n\\n2. **Boil the Potatoes**: Place the scored potatoes in a pot of boiling water and boil them for about 15 minutes.\\n\\n3. **Cool the Potatoes**: After boiling, quickly transfer the potatoes to a bowl of ice water. This sudden change in temperature causes the skin to peel off more easily.\\n\\n4. **Remove the Skin**: Once the potatoes are cooled, remove them from the ice water and use your hands to rub the skin off. The skin should come off easily.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can peel potatoes quickly and efficiently.\", \"To peel potatoes fast, follow these steps: \\n\\nStep 1: Cut the potato skin. Make a cut all around the potato, lengthwise. Try to slice only the skin, not the actual potato.  \\nStep 2: Boil it. Put the potato in a pot of boiling water.  \\nStep 3: Cool it off. Plunge the potato in ice water for 10 seconds. The surface of the potato will shrink, while the center remains hot.  \\nStep 4: Remove the skin. Rub the potato with both hands and watch the skin fall right off.\", \"To peel potatoes fast, follow these steps:\\n1. Cut the potato skin: Make a cut all around the potato, lengthwise, trying to slice only the skin, not the actual potato.\\n2. Boil it: Put the potato in a pot of boiling water.\\n3. Cool it off: Plunge the potato in ice water for 10 seconds. The surface of the potato will shrink, while the center remains hot.\\n4. Remove the skin: Rub the potato with both hands and watch the skin fall right off.\\n\\nThis method helps to separate the skin from the potato quickly, making the peeling process much faster than traditional methods.\", \"1. Place washed whole, unpeeled potatoes into a pot and cover with cold water.\\n2. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\\n3. With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\\n4. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\\n5. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\\n6. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\\n7. Remove your potatoe from the water and remove the skin.\"]", "time_sec": 22.114, "generation_time_seconds": 21.4785, "selection_time_seconds": 0.628, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 57112, 34167, 4937, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 10570, 279, 13706, 20187, 95518, 5443, 264, 21430, 311, 5456, 279, 34167, 678, 279, 1616, 2163, 279, 4126, 13, 1096, 8609, 279, 6787, 311, 2525, 1007, 803, 6707, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 1233, 321, 279, 13706, 20187, 95518, 10771, 279, 16548, 34167, 304, 264, 3338, 315, 49837, 3015, 323, 43690, 1105, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 56750, 279, 13706, 20187, 95518, 4636, 49837, 11, 6157, 8317, 279, 34167, 311, 264, 19212, 315, 9853, 3015, 13, 1096, 10968, 2297, 304, 9315, 11137, 279, 6787, 311, 57112, 1007, 803, 6707, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 13021, 279, 26951, 95518, 9646, 279, 34167, 525, 64310, 11, 4057, 1105, 504, 279, 9853, 3015, 323, 990, 697, 6078, 311, 10273, 279, 6787, 1007, 13, 576, 6787, 1265, 2525, 1007, 6707, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 57112, 34167, 6157, 323, 29720, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can peel potatoes quickly and efficiently.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.5015044278936522, "g_worst_claim": -0.021939046680927277, "g_content": 0.62829473744268, "g_traj_mean": 0.47021955251693726}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 57112, 34167, 4937, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 25, 4710, 8304, 220, 16, 25, 19649, 279, 38734, 6787, 13, 7405, 264, 3931, 678, 2163, 279, 38734, 11, 3084, 4482, 13, 9735, 311, 15983, 1172, 279, 6787, 11, 537, 279, 5042, 38734, 13, 2303, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 2516, 321, 432, 13, 10224, 279, 38734, 304, 264, 3338, 315, 49837, 3015, 13, 2303, 8304, 220, 18, 25, 23931, 432, 1007, 13, 1818, 13884, 279, 38734, 304, 9853, 3015, 369, 220, 16, 15, 6486, 13, 576, 7329, 315, 279, 38734, 686, 28900, 11, 1393, 279, 4126, 8458, 4017, 13, 2303, 8304, 220, 19, 25, 10783, 279, 6787, 13, 12839, 279, 38734, 448, 2176, 6078, 323, 3736, 279, 6787, 4399, 1290, 1007, 13, 151645], "pred": "To peel potatoes fast, follow these steps: \n\nStep 1: Cut the potato skin. Make a cut all around the potato, lengthwise. Try to slice only the skin, not the actual potato.  \nStep 2: Boil it. Put the potato in a pot of boiling water.  \nStep 3: Cool it off. Plunge the potato in ice water for 10 seconds. The surface of the potato will shrink, while the center remains hot.  \nStep 4: Remove the skin. Rub the potato with both hands and watch the skin fall right off.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5245594327864216, "g_worst_claim": 0.44494375586509705, "g_content": 2.079416628237124, "g_traj_mean": 1.5472297668457031}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 57112, 34167, 4937, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 19649, 279, 38734, 6787, 25, 7405, 264, 3931, 678, 2163, 279, 38734, 11, 3084, 4482, 11, 4460, 311, 15983, 1172, 279, 6787, 11, 537, 279, 5042, 38734, 624, 17, 13, 2516, 321, 432, 25, 10224, 279, 38734, 304, 264, 3338, 315, 49837, 3015, 624, 18, 13, 23931, 432, 1007, 25, 1818, 13884, 279, 38734, 304, 9853, 3015, 369, 220, 16, 15, 6486, 13, 576, 7329, 315, 279, 38734, 686, 28900, 11, 1393, 279, 4126, 8458, 4017, 624, 19, 13, 10783, 279, 6787, 25, 12839, 279, 38734, 448, 2176, 6078, 323, 3736, 279, 6787, 4399, 1290, 1007, 382, 1986, 1714, 8609, 311, 8651, 279, 6787, 504, 279, 38734, 6157, 11, 3259, 279, 1051, 20058, 1882, 1753, 10596, 1091, 8606, 5413, 13, 151645], "pred": "This method helps to separate the skin from the potato quickly, making the peeling process much faster than traditional methods.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6499917616251636, "g_worst_claim": 0.2444600842215798, "g_content": 1.8363336230081224, "g_traj_mean": 1.4721455574035645}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16, 13, 10771, 37493, 4361, 11, 650, 375, 40089, 34167, 1119, 264, 3338, 323, 3421, 448, 9255, 3015, 624, 17, 13, 39124, 264, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 18, 13, 3085, 264, 21430, 11, 5456, 697, 34167, 678, 279, 1616, 2163, 279, 4126, 624, 19, 13, 10771, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3338, 323, 43690, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 476, 773, 624, 20, 13, 31166, 264, 19212, 315, 9853, 3015, 323, 1992, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3015, 624, 21, 13, 4492, 812, 432, 2163, 369, 264, 2421, 6486, 1101, 3322, 773, 429, 432, 748, 7010, 3322, 311, 3705, 624, 22, 13, 10783, 697, 38734, 68, 504, 279, 3015, 323, 4057, 279, 6787, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Place washed whole, unpeeled potatoes into a pot and cover with cold water.\n2. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\n3. With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\n4. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\n5. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\n6. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\n7. Remove your potatoe from the water and remove the skin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.2110155021023545, "g_worst_claim": 0.8171510696411133, "g_content": 1.9943608302696079, "g_traj_mean": 1.8088434934616089}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 14.89, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "223", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, to fix a lift valve in a toilet, you should follow these steps:\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain.\n3. Install a new flapper valve and chain.\n4. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n5. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n6. Push the solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and secure it tightly.\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm closest to the edge.\n8. Use pliers to securely fasten the chain.\n9. Turn the water valve back on.\n10. Test the flush of the toilet and adjust the chain if needed.\n\nNote: The given passages provide step-by-step instructions for fixing a lift valve in a toilet.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can effectively fix the lift valve in your toilet.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "By following these steps, you can effectively fix the lift valve in your toilet.", "cot": "[\"To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut off the water supply valve**: Locate the water supply valve under the sink or behind the toilet and turn it clockwise to shut off the water supply to the toilet.\\n\\n2. **Remove the old flapper valve**: Carefully remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Be sure to remove any broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n\\n3. **Prepare the new lift chain**: If necessary, adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links. This ensures the chain is the correct length for the new flapper valve.\\n\\n4. **Install the new flapper valve**: Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end of the lift arm will hang freely in the air.\\n\\n5. **Connect the new lift chain**: Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n\\n6. **Turn on the water supply**: Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\\n\\n7. **Check for correct operation**: Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively fix the lift valve in your toilet.\", \"To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\\n3. Remove what's left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n7. When you're satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n11. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\\n12. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n13. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n14. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\", \"To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet** by locating it behind the toilet tank and turning it clockwise to close the valve.\\n2. **Remove the old flapper valve** by gently sliding it off the mounting arms. Be sure to remove all remnants of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n3. **Open the water valve** to fill the tank. Once the tank is full, flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n4. **Adjust the lift chain** by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links if necessary. This ensures the chain operates smoothly.\\n5. **Cut off the excess lift chain** to prevent it from getting tangled and ensure a neat installation.\\n6. **Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle**. If your replacement part includes a screw, tighten it securely.\\n7. **Push the other end of the lift arm until there is no more give and it is secure**. It should hang freely in the air.\\n8. **Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm**, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n9. **Turn the water valve back on** and test the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\\n10. **Check for proper operation** and ensure the toilet flushes smoothly. If there are any issues, make further adjustments as needed.\", \"To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\\n3. Remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n7. Cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\\n13. Use the pliers to ensure it is securely fastened.\\n14. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n15. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\"]", "time_sec": 42.721, "generation_time_seconds": 42.0804, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6333, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2016, 332, 1007, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 95518, 95210, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 1212, 279, 19309, 476, 4815, 279, 26214, 323, 2484, 432, 65670, 311, 9311, 1007, 279, 3015, 8149, 311, 279, 26214, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 13021, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 95518, 10627, 3641, 4057, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 13, 2823, 2704, 311, 4057, 894, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 501, 11893, 8781, 95518, 1416, 5871, 11, 7500, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 13, 1096, 25351, 279, 8781, 374, 279, 4396, 3084, 369, 279, 501, 1320, 3106, 31430, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 24690, 279, 501, 1320, 3106, 31430, 95518, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 13, 1416, 264, 21966, 374, 5230, 448, 697, 949, 11, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 13, 22950, 432, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 13, 576, 1008, 835, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 686, 14678, 25580, 304, 279, 3720, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 14611, 279, 501, 11893, 8781, 95518, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 11, 892, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 5443, 625, 4813, 311, 1281, 2704, 432, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 19389, 389, 279, 3015, 8149, 95518, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 1273, 700, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 13, 1416, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 382, 22, 13, 3070, 3973, 369, 4396, 5666, 95518, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 323, 18198, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 13444, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 697, 26214, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can effectively fix the lift valve in your toilet.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.337950555749286, "g_worst_claim": 0.11268765276128595, "g_content": 1.8316982977404566, "g_traj_mean": 1.257012128829956}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 1417, 27440, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 624, 18, 13, 10783, 1128, 594, 2115, 315, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 19, 13, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 624, 20, 13, 57626, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 624, 22, 13, 3197, 498, 2299, 19527, 11, 3931, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 624, 23, 13, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 264, 21966, 374, 5230, 448, 697, 949, 11, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 624, 16, 15, 13, 22950, 432, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 13, 576, 1008, 835, 686, 14678, 25580, 304, 279, 3720, 624, 16, 16, 13, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 1096, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 17, 13, 5443, 279, 625, 4813, 311, 1281, 2704, 432, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 624, 16, 18, 13, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 1273, 700, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 624, 16, 19, 13, 1416, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove what's left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n7. When you're satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n11. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n12. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n13. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n14. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1221615145443278, "g_worst_claim": 0.5362457036972046, "g_content": 2.6495179735924586, "g_traj_mean": 1.845154047012329}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2016, 332, 1007, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 334, 553, 71891, 432, 4815, 279, 26214, 12896, 323, 13054, 432, 65670, 311, 3265, 279, 31430, 624, 17, 13, 3070, 13021, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 334, 553, 29273, 33832, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 13, 2823, 2704, 311, 4057, 678, 72340, 315, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 18, 13, 3070, 5002, 279, 3015, 31430, 334, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 13, 9646, 279, 12896, 374, 2480, 11, 18198, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 624, 19, 13, 3070, 38616, 279, 11893, 8781, 334, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 421, 5871, 13, 1096, 25351, 279, 8781, 26057, 38411, 624, 20, 13, 3070, 37666, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 334, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 323, 5978, 264, 28485, 13713, 624, 21, 13, 3070, 16644, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 334, 13, 1416, 697, 13723, 949, 5646, 264, 21966, 11, 66745, 432, 51023, 624, 22, 13, 3070, 16644, 279, 1008, 835, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 334, 13, 1084, 1265, 14678, 25580, 304, 279, 3720, 624, 23, 13, 3070, 14611, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 97219, 892, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 5443, 625, 4813, 311, 1281, 2704, 432, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 624, 24, 13, 3070, 19389, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 334, 323, 1273, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 13, 1416, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 15, 13, 3070, 3973, 369, 6169, 5666, 334, 323, 5978, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 38411, 13, 1416, 1052, 525, 894, 4714, 11, 1281, 4623, 32974, 438, 4362, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. **Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet** by locating it behind the toilet tank and turning it clockwise to close the valve.\n2. **Remove the old flapper valve** by gently sliding it off the mounting arms. Be sure to remove all remnants of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. **Open the water valve** to fill the tank. Once the tank is full, flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n4. **Adjust the lift chain** by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links if necessary. This ensures the chain operates smoothly.\n5. **Cut off the excess lift chain** to prevent it from getting tangled and ensure a neat installation.\n6. **Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle**. If your replacement part includes a screw, tighten it securely.\n7. **Push the other end of the lift arm until there is no more give and it is secure**. It should hang freely in the air.\n8. **Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm**, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n9. **Turn the water valve back on** and test the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\n10. **Check for proper operation** and ensure the toilet flushes smoothly. If there are any issues, make further adjustments as needed.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4241567979835714, "g_worst_claim": 0.1615002155303955, "g_content": 2.101260986328125, "g_traj_mean": 1.3637475967407227}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 1417, 27440, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 624, 18, 13, 10783, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 19, 13, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 624, 20, 13, 57626, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 624, 22, 13, 19649, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 624, 23, 13, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 624, 24, 13, 1416, 264, 21966, 374, 5230, 448, 697, 949, 11, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 624, 16, 15, 13, 22950, 432, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 624, 16, 16, 13, 576, 1008, 835, 686, 14678, 25580, 304, 279, 3720, 624, 16, 17, 13, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 11, 892, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 16, 18, 13, 5443, 279, 625, 4813, 311, 5978, 432, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 624, 16, 19, 13, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 1273, 700, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 624, 16, 20, 13, 1416, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 151645], "pred": "To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n5. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n6. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n7. Cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n8. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\n9. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\n10. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\n11. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n12. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n13. Use the pliers to ensure it is securely fastened.\n14. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n15. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.10610673178224, "g_worst_claim": 0.5344822009404501, "g_content": 2.655124439912684, "g_traj_mean": 1.776357889175415}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 10.34, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "224", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Turn off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Fill the tank by turning on the water valve and then flushing the toilet. Adjust the lift chain as needed by moving the metal clip up or down a few links. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n5. Push the solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. Make sure it is securely fastened.\n6. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If it flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it tighter on the lift arm.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can effectively fix the lift valve in your toilet.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "By following these steps, you can effectively fix the lift valve in your toilet.", "cot": "[\"To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut off the water supply valve**: Locate the water supply valve under the sink or behind the toilet and turn it clockwise to shut off the water supply to the toilet.\\n\\n2. **Remove the old flapper valve**: Carefully remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Be sure to remove any broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n\\n3. **Prepare the new lift chain**: If necessary, adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links. This ensures the chain is the correct length for the new flapper valve.\\n\\n4. **Install the new flapper valve**: Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end of the lift arm will hang freely in the air.\\n\\n5. **Connect the new lift chain**: Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n\\n6. **Turn on the water supply**: Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\\n\\n7. **Check for correct operation**: Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively fix the lift valve in your toilet.\", \"To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n4. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n5. When you're satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n6. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\\n7. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n8. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\\n9. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n10. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n4. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n5. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n6. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n7. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\\n8. The other end will hang freely in the air. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\\n9. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n10. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n11. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\"]", "time_sec": 32.693, "generation_time_seconds": 31.7909, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8961, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2016, 332, 1007, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 95518, 95210, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 1212, 279, 19309, 476, 4815, 279, 26214, 323, 2484, 432, 65670, 311, 9311, 1007, 279, 3015, 8149, 311, 279, 26214, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 13021, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 95518, 10627, 3641, 4057, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 13, 2823, 2704, 311, 4057, 894, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 501, 11893, 8781, 95518, 1416, 5871, 11, 7500, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 13, 1096, 25351, 279, 8781, 374, 279, 4396, 3084, 369, 279, 501, 1320, 3106, 31430, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 24690, 279, 501, 1320, 3106, 31430, 95518, 22950, 27