{"id": "226", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to fix a lift valve in a toilet:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve and any remaining pieces of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Install the new flapper valve and connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, making sure it is securely fastened.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to test for correct operation.\n5. Adjust the chain as needed to ensure a proper flush. Cut off any excess chain to prevent tangling.\n\nNote: If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "pred": "1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n4. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n5. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n6. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n7. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n8. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n9. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n10. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n11. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\n4. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n5. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n6. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n7. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\n8. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\n9. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\n10. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\n11. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "cot": "[\"To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut off the water supply valve**: Locate the water supply valve under the sink or behind the toilet and turn it clockwise to shut off the water supply to the toilet.\\n\\n2. **Remove the old flapper valve**: Carefully remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Be sure to remove any broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n\\n3. **Prepare the new lift chain**: If necessary, adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links. This ensures the chain is the correct length for the new flapper valve.\\n\\n4. **Install the new flapper valve**: Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end of the lift arm will hang freely in the air.\\n\\n5. **Connect the new lift chain**: Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n\\n6. **Turn on the water supply**: Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\\n\\n7. **Check for correct operation**: Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively fix the lift valve in your toilet.\", \"To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut off the Water Supply**: Turn off the water supply valve to the toilet to ensure safety while working.\\n2. **Remove the Old Flapper Valve**: Carefully remove the old flapper valve from its mounting arms. If the lift chain is broken, extract the remaining pieces from the lift arm.\\n3. **Prepare the Lift Arm**: Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is part of your kit, screw it in tightly. Ensure the lift arm is securely connected by pushing it until there is no more give and it is firmly in place. The other end of the lift arm should hang freely.\\n4. **Connect the Chain**: Attach the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This hole should be the one closest to the edge of the lift arm. Securely fasten the chain using pliers.\\n5. **Reconnect the Water Supply**: Turn the water valve back on.\\n6. **Test the Flush**: Test the flush of the toilet to check if everything is working correctly. If the flush is slow, adjust the chain on the lift arm to make it a little tighter.\\n7. **Check for Proper Operation**: Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to verify that it operates correctly. If necessary, fine-tune the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links until the flushing mechanism works smoothly.\\n\\nBy carefully following these steps, you can effectively fix a lift valve in a toilet, ensuring proper flushing and maintenance of the plumbing system.\", \"To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n4. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n5. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n6. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n7. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n8. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\\n9. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n10. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n11. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\", \"To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Turn off the Water Supply**: Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. **Remove the Old Flapper Valve**: Slip off the flapper valve from the mounting arms and remove the remaining parts of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n3. **Install the New Flapper Valve**: Push the small solid end of the new toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\\n4. **Secure the Lift Arm**: Push the lift arm until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n5. **Connect the Chain**: Connect the lift chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened.\\n6. **Turn on the Water Supply**: Turn the water valve back on.\\n7. **Test the Flush**: Test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\\n8. **Check and Adjust**: Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links. When you're satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can fix the lift valve in your toilet effectively.\"]", "time_sec": 44.686, "generation_time_seconds": 43.8355, "selection_time_seconds": 0.845, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2016, 332, 1007, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 95518, 95210, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 1212, 279, 19309, 476, 4815, 279, 26214, 323, 2484, 432, 65670, 311, 9311, 1007, 279, 3015, 8149, 311, 279, 26214, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 13021, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 95518, 10627, 3641, 4057, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 13, 2823, 2704, 311, 4057, 894, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 501, 11893, 8781, 95518, 1416, 5871, 11, 7500, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 13, 1096, 25351, 279, 8781, 374, 279, 4396, 3084, 369, 279, 501, 1320, 3106, 31430, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 24690, 279, 501, 1320, 3106, 31430, 95518, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 13, 1416, 264, 21966, 374, 5230, 448, 697, 949, 11, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 13, 22950, 432, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 13, 576, 1008, 835, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 686, 14678, 25580, 304, 279, 3720, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 14611, 279, 501, 11893, 8781, 95518, 13015, 279, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 11, 892, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 5443, 625, 4813, 311, 1281, 2704, 432, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 19389, 389, 279, 3015, 8149, 95518, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 323, 1273, 700, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 13, 1416, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 382, 22, 13, 3070, 3973, 369, 4396, 5666, 95518, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 323, 18198, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 13444, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 697, 26214, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can effectively fix the lift valve in your toilet.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3316032439069823, "g_worst_claim": 0.11473289403048428, "g_content": 1.826129296582616, "g_traj_mean": 1.2558728456497192}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 264, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2016, 332, 1007, 279, 9959, 29809, 95518, 11999, 1007, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 311, 5978, 7149, 1393, 3238, 624, 17, 13, 3070, 13021, 279, 10621, 2988, 3106, 44293, 95518, 10627, 3641, 4057, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 504, 1181, 33639, 11715, 13, 1416, 279, 11893, 8781, 374, 10865, 11, 8649, 279, 9664, 9666, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 18, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 52435, 12990, 95518, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 13, 1416, 264, 21966, 374, 949, 315, 697, 16138, 11, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 13, 29279, 279, 11893, 6773, 374, 51023, 8433, 553, 17461, 432, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 31520, 304, 1992, 13, 576, 1008, 835, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 1265, 14678, 25580, 624, 19, 13, 3070, 14611, 279, 28525, 95518, 483