g_traj_mean": 1.9044997692108154}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 19389, 1007, 279, 9959, 29809, 95518, 1417, 27440, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 311, 279, 26214, 624, 17, 13, 3070, 13021, 279, 10621, 2988, 3106, 44293, 95518, 58532, 1007, 279, 1320, 3106, 31430, 504, 279, 33639, 11715, 323, 4057, 279, 9664, 5479, 315, 279, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 18, 13, 3070, 24690, 279, 1532, 2988, 3106, 44293, 95518, 22950, 279, 2613, 6437, 835, 315, 279, 501, 26214, 11893, 6773, 1119, 279, 18198, 3705, 13, 1416, 264, 21966, 374, 5230, 448, 697, 949, 11, 21966, 432, 304, 38969, 624, 19, 13, 3070, 49813, 279, 52435, 12990, 95518, 22950, 279, 11893, 6773, 3080, 1052, 374, 902, 803, 2968, 323, 432, 374, 9767, 13, 576, 1008, 835, 686, 14678, 25580, 304, 279, 3720, 624, 20, 13, 3070, 14611, 279, 28525, 95518, 13015, 279, 11893, 8781, 311, 279, 4843, 14178, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 11, 892, 374, 279, 14178, 18093, 311, 279, 6821, 315, 279, 11893, 6773, 13, 5443, 625, 4813, 311, 5978, 432, 374, 51023, 4937, 6758, 624, 21, 13, 3070, 19389, 389, 279, 9959, 29809, 95518, 11999, 279, 3015, 31430, 1182, 389, 624, 22, 13, 3070, 2271, 279, 57626, 95518, 3393, 700, 279, 18198, 315, 279, 26214, 13, 1416, 279, 26214, 18198, 288, 13970, 11, 7500, 279, 8781, 311, 1281, 432, 264, 2632, 62962, 389, 279, 11893, 6773, 624, 23, 13, 3070, 3973, 323, 27196, 95518, 5264, 279, 3015, 31430, 311, 5155, 279, 12896, 323, 18198, 279, 26214, 311, 1779, 369, 4396, 5666, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 1349, 4250, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 13, 3197, 498, 2299, 19527, 11, 3931, 1007, 279, 13623, 11893, 8781, 311, 5358, 432, 504, 3709, 92841, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 697, 26214, 13444, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can fix the lift valve in your toilet effectively.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.487172916754424, "g_worst_claim": 0.09102786671031605, "g_content": 2.116098416905825, "g_traj_mean": 1.4793955087661743}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.14, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "227", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here's a brief answer on how to fix a lift valve in a toilet based on the given passages:\n\nTo fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Install a new flapper valve and chain for a 1.6 gallon per flush toilet.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n5. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links if necessary. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n6. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included, screw it in tightly.\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened.\n8. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can effectively fix the lift valve in your toilet.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "By following these steps, you can effectively fix the lift valve in your toilet.", "cot": "[\"To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut off the water supply valve**: Locate the water supply valve under the sink or behind the toilet and turn it clockwise to shut off the water supply to the toilet.\\n\\n2. **Remove the old flapper valve**: Carefully remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Be sure to remove any broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n\\n3. **Prepare the new lift chain**: If necessary, adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links. This ensures the chain is the correct length for the new flapper valve.\\n\\n4. **Install the new flapper valve**: Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end of the lift arm will hang freely in the air.\\n\\n5. **Connect the new lift chain**: Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n\\n6. **Turn on the water supply**: Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\\n\\n7. **Check for correct operation**: Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively fix the lift valve in your toilet.\", \"To fix the lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Shut off the water supply**: Ensure that the water supply valve to the toilet is closed to prevent water from flowing to the tank.\\n\\n2. **Remove the old flapper valve**: Carefully remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. This will allow access to the internal parts of the toilet.\\n\\n3. **Inspect and replace the lift chain**: Check the lift chain for any damage or wear. If necessary, replace the broken lift chain from the lift arm. Ensure that the chain is properly connected to the flapper valve.\\n\\n4. **Replace the lift chain**: If the lift chain is damaged, replace it with a new one. Make sure the chain is properly looped around the lift arm and the flapper valve.\\n\\n5. **Test the toilet**: After replacing the lift chain, turn on the water supply valve and flush the toilet. Check for proper operation. If the toilet does not flush correctly, adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n\\n6. **Secure the lift chain**: Make sure the lift chain is securely fastened by tightening the metal clip. Cut off any excess chain to prevent tangling.\\n\\n7. **Test again**: Turn the water supply valve back on and test the flush again. Adjust the chain if necessary to ensure the toilet flushes properly.\\n\\n8. **Final check**: Ensure that the flush handle is securely connected and that the chain is not too tight or loose. Test the toilet one last time to confirm that it is functioning correctly.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively fix and replace the lift valve in a toilet.\", \"Answer: To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove what’s left of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n3. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n4. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. This is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n5. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\\n6. Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links. When you’re satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\", \"To fix a lift valve in a toilet, you need to follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Shutoff the water supply valve to the toilet.\\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank.\\n4. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\\n5. If needed, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\\n6. When you're satisfied, cut off the excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\\n7. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle.\\n8. If a screw is included with your part, screw it in tightly.\\n9. Push it until there is no more give and it is secure.\\n10. The other end will hang freely in the air.\\n11. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm.\\n12. Use the pliers to make sure it is securely fastened.\\n13. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet.\\n14. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\"]", "time_sec": 44.489, "generation_time_seconds": 43.6835, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7982, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 5046, 279, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 2016, 332, 1007, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 95518, 95210, 279, 3015, 8149, 31430, 1212, 279, 19309, 476, 4815, 279, 26214, 323, 2484, 432, 65670, 311, 9311, 1007, 279, 3015, 8149, 311, 279, 26214, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 13021, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 95518, 10627, 3641, 4057, 279, 2310, 1320, 3106, 31430, 553, 63702, 432, 1007, 279, 33639, 11715, 13, 2823, 2704, 311, 4057, 894, 10865, 11893, 8781, 504, 279, 11893, 6773, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 501, 11893, 8781, 95518, 1416, 5871, 11, 7500, 279, 11893, 8781, 553, 7218, 279, 9317, 12327, 705, 476, 1495, 264, 5625, 315, 7746, 13, 1096, 25351, 279, 8781, 374, 279, 4396, 3084, 369, 279, 501, 1320, 3106, 31430, 382, 19, 13, 30