{"id": "231", "question": "oil stain on concrete driveway", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question \"How do you remove oil stains from a concrete driveway?\"\n\nTo remove oil stains from a concrete driveway, you can use one of the following methods:\n\n1. Oven cleaner, goop hand cleaner, and carburetor cleaner (as mentioned in Passage 1).\n2. A commercial-grade cleaner applied with a brush or broom, followed by scrubbing with a pressure washer (as described in Passage 3).\n\nBefore starting the cleaning process, it is recommended to wash away any dirt or debris from the affected area (Passage 2). Additionally, it is important to avoid using high-pressure hoses to clean the stain, as this can push the oil deeper into the pavement (Passage 2).\n\nIt is also noted that the size of the oil spill and the length of time the stain has been present will affect the method of removal (Passage 3). For small and stubborn stains, the poultice method may be effective (Passage 2).", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Answer: Oil stains on a concrete driveway can be cleaned using various methods. Here are a few approaches:\\n\\n1. **Using Pressure Washer**: Apply a commercial-grade cleaner to the oil stain, then scrub with a brush or broom. Add detergent to your pressure washer and begin spraying. Move at an even pace and keep the nozzle at the same distance from the surface of the concrete at all times to ensure no streaking occurs. This method is effective for larger oil spills.\\n\\n2. **Poultice Method**: If you have a fresh or small, stubborn stain, you may want to use the poultice method to get out the stain. This involves applying a poultice to the stain and allowing it to soften the oil before scrubbing it off.\\n\\n3. **Using a High-Pressure Hose**: Clean the area with water from a hose or bucket. However, avoid using a high-pressure hose, as it could push the oil deeper into the pavement.\\n\\nBefore cleaning, ensure to wash off any dirt and debris that is in the way of the oil stain on your driveway.\"]", "time_sec": 13.413, "generation_time_seconds": 12.4421, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9618, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.16758041083812714, "g_worst_claim": -0.16758041083812714, "g_content": -0.2625732421875, "g_traj_mean": -0.1488625407218933}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.16758041083812714, "g_worst_claim": -0.16758041083812714, "g_content": -0.2625732421875, "g_traj_mean": -0.1488625407218933}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.16758041083812714, "g_worst_claim": -0.16758041083812714, "g_content": -0.2625732421875, "g_traj_mean": -0.1488625407218933}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 15526, 62463, 389, 264, 14175, 52142, 646, 387, 27722, 1667, 5257, 5413, 13, 5692, 525, 264, 2421, 19827, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 16429, 38990, 96082, 95518, 20552, 264, 8353, 40227, 31881, 311, 279, 5590, 51964, 11, 1221, 44901, 448, 264, 15625, 476, 2896, 316, 13, 2691, 90134, 311, 697, 7262, 52892, 323, 3161, 82536, 13, 14561, 518, 458, 1496, 17857, 323, 2506, 279, 81881, 518, 279, 1852, 6010, 504, 279, 7329, 315, 279, 14175, 518, 678