{"id": "233", "question": "average weather sausalito", "gt": "The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September and the lowest is 50 degrees in December. The city gets 34 inches of rain per year, with the most precipitation occurring in January. Snowfall is non-existent. On average, there are 256 sunny days per year. The July high is around 69 degrees and the January low is 43. The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, however, the pollution index is 61% worse.", "pred": "Based on the provided passage, the average monthly temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September and 50 degrees in December. The average precipitation is 34 inches per year, with the highest precipitation occurring in January (0 inches). The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, while the pollution index is 61% worse than the national average. The average US city gets 26 inches of snow per year, but Sausalito has 0 inches. There are an average of 256 sunny days per year in Sausalito.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passage, the average monthly temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September and 50 degrees in December. The average precipitation is 34 inches per year, with the highest precipitation occurring in January (0 inches). The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, while the pollution index is 61% worse than the national average. The average US city gets 26 inches of snow per year, but Sausalito has 0 inches. There are an average of 256 sunny days per year in Sausalito.", "cot": "[\"The average weather in Sausalito can be described as follows:\\n\\n- The highest monthly average temperature in September is 58 degrees.\\n- The lowest monthly average temperature in December is 50 degrees.\\n- The most monthly precipitation occurs in January with 0 inches.\\n- The air quality index in Sausalito is 13% better than the national average.\\n- The pollution index in Sausalito is 61% worse than the national average.\\n- Sausalito gets 34 inches of rain per year, which is less than the US average of 39 inches.\\n- Snowfall is 0 inches, which is less than the average US city's 26 inches of snow per year.\\n- There are 56 days with any measurable precipitation.\\n- On average, there are 256 sunny days per year in Sausalito.\\n- The July high is around 69 degrees.\\n- The January low is 43 degrees.\\n- Sperling's comfort index for Sausalito is a 84 out of 100, indicating a more comfortable year-round climate compared to the US average of 54.\\n- The US average for the comfort index is 54.\\n- The index is based on the total number of days annually within the comfort range of 70-80 degrees, and a penalty is applied for days of excessive humidity.\\n\\nAnswer: The average weather in Sausalito includes a high monthly average temperature of 58 degrees in September, a low monthly average temperature of 50 degrees in December, and a monthly precipitation of 0 inches in January. The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, while the pollution index is 61% worse than the national average. Sausalito receives 34 inches of rain per year, which is less than the US average of 39 inches, and has no snowfall. There are 56 days with any measurable precipitation, and an average of 256 sunny days per year. The July high is around 69 degrees, and the January low is 43 degrees. Sperling's comfort index for Sausalito is a 84 out of 100, indicating a more comfortable year-round climate compared to the US average of 54.\", \"Average temperature: The average temperature in Sausalito ranges from 43 degrees in January to 69 degrees in July. Average precipitation: Sausalito receives 34 inches of rain per year, which is less than the US average of 39 inches.\", \"To determine the average weather in Sausalito, we can look at the data provided in the two given passages.\\n\\n1. **Temperature**:\\n   - The highest monthly average temperature in September is 58 degrees, and the lowest monthly average temperature in December is 50 degrees. The average temperature of Sausalito can be inferred as falling between these two extremes. A reasonable estimate can be around the middle, which would be approximately 54 degrees.\\n\\n2. **Rainfall**:\\n   - According to Passage 1, the most monthly precipitation in Sausalito occurs in January with 0 inches. According to Passage 2, Sausalito gets 34 inches of rain per year. We can use this information to determine the average monthly rainfall: \\\\( \\\\frac{34 \\\\text{ inches}}{12 \\\\text{ months}} = 2.83 \\\\text{ inches per month}\\\\).\\n\\n3. **Sunny Days**:\\n   - Passage 2 mentions that on average, there are 256 sunny days per year in Sausalito. This suggests that about \\\\( \\\\frac{256}{365} \\\\) of the days are sunny, which is approximately 70% of the days.\\n\\n4. **Comfort Index**:\\n   - The comfort index for Sausalito is given as 84 out of 100, where a higher score indicates a more comfortable year-around climate. The US average for the comfort index is 54. The comfort index is based on the total number of days annually within the comfort range of 70-80 degrees and applies a penalty for days of excessive humidity.\\n\\n5. **Other Conditions**:\\n   - Sausalito does not get any snowfall (Passage 2).\\n   - The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, but this does not directly contribute to the average weather.\\n\\nCombining these factors:\\n- Average temperature: Approximately 54 degrees.\\n- Average rainfall: Approximately 2.83 inches per month.\\n- Sunny days: Approximately 70% of the days.\\n- Comfort index: 84 out of 100.\\n\\nAnswer: The average weather in Sausalito is characterized by an average temperature of 54 degrees, average rainfall of 2.83 inches per month, and approximately 70% sunny days.\", \"Based on the provided passage, the average monthly temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September and 50 degrees in December. The average precipitation is 34 inches per year, with the highest precipitation occurring in January (0 inches). The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, while the pollution index is 61% worse than the national average. The average US city gets 26 inches of snow per year, but Sausalito has 0 inches. There are an average of 256 sunny days per year in Sausalito.\"]", "time_sec": 42.878, "generation_time_seconds": 41.8342, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0368, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 5461, 9104, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 646, 387, 7481, 438, 11017, 1447, 12, 576, 8426, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 6122, 374, 220, 20, 23, 12348, 624, 12, 576, 15457, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 6652, 374, 220, 20, 15, 12348, 624, 12, 576, 1429, 15088, 59950, 13666, 304, 6058, 448, 220, 15, 14924, 624, 12, 576, 3720, 4271, 1922, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 374, 220, 16, 18, 4, 2664, 1091, 279, 5313, 5461, 624, 12, 576, 24761, 1922, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 374, 220, 21, 16, 4, 10960, 1091, 279, 5313, 5461, 624, 12, 328, 79074, 6357, 5221, 220, 18, 19, 14924, 315, 11174, 817, 1042, 11, 892, 374, 2686, 1091, 279, 2274, 5461, 315, 220, 18, 24, 14924, 624, 12, 18901, 13464, 374, 220, 15, 14924, 11, 892, 374, 2686, 1091, 279, 5461, 2274, 3283, 594, 220, 17, 21, 14924, 315, 11794, 817, 1042, 624, 12, 2619, 525, 220, 20, 21, 2849, 448, 894, 65203, 59950, 624, 12, 1913, 5461, 11, 1052, 525, 220, 17, 20, 21, 39698, 2849, 817, 1042, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 624, 12, 576, 5768, 1550, 374, 2163, 220, 21, 24, 12348, 624, 12, 576, 6058, 3347, 374, 220, 19, 18, 12348, 624, 12, 328, 712, 2718, 594, 6838, 1922, 369, 328, 79074, 6357, 374, 264, 220, 23, 19, 700, 315, 220, 16, 15, 15, 11, 18860, 264, 803, 10655, 1042, 21015, 9977, 7707, 311, 279, 2274, 5461, 315, 220, 20, 19, 624, 12, 576, 2274, 5461, 369, 279, 6838, 1922, 374, 220, 20, 19, 624, 12, 576, 1