{"id": "235", "question": "average weather sausalito", "gt": "Average weather in Sausalito can vary depending on the time of year. For example, during September, the average temperature is 58 degrees Fahrenheit (15 degrees Celsius), while in January, it is only 43 degrees Fahrenheit (4 degrees Celsius). The most precipitation occurs in January with 0 inches. However, throughout the year, the number of days with measurable precipitation is 56, and there are an average of 256 sunny days.", "pred": "Sausalito, California has an average temperature of 69 degrees in July and 43 degrees in January. Sausalito also gets 34 inches of rain per year.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Sausalito, California has an average temperature of 69 degrees in July and 43 degrees in January. Sausalito also gets 34 inches of rain per year.", "cot": "[\"The average weather in Sausalito can be described as follows:\\n\\n- The highest monthly average temperature in September is 58 degrees.\\n- The lowest monthly average temperature in December is 50 degrees.\\n- The most monthly precipitation occurs in January with 0 inches.\\n- The air quality index in Sausalito is 13% better than the national average.\\n- The pollution index in Sausalito is 61% worse than the national average.\\n- Sausalito gets 34 inches of rain per year, which is less than the US average of 39 inches.\\n- Snowfall is 0 inches, which is less than the average US city's 26 inches of snow per year.\\n- There are 56 days with any measurable precipitation.\\n- On average, there are 256 sunny days per year in Sausalito.\\n- The July high is around 69 degrees.\\n- The January low is 43 degrees.\\n- Sperling's comfort index for Sausalito is a 84 out of 100, indicating a more comfortable year-round climate compared to the US average of 54.\\n- The US average for the comfort index is 54.\\n- The index is based on the total number of days annually within the comfort range of 70-80 degrees, and a penalty is applied for days of excessive humidity.\\n\\nAnswer: The average weather in Sausalito includes a high monthly average temperature of 58 degrees in September, a low monthly average temperature of 50 degrees in December, and a monthly precipitation of 0 inches in January. The air quality index is 13% better than the national average, while the pollution index is 61% worse than the national average. Sausalito receives 34 inches of rain per year, which is less than the US average of 39 inches, and has no snowfall. There are 56 days with any measurable precipitation, and an average of 256 sunny days per year. The July high is around 69 degrees, and the January low is 43 degrees. Sperling's comfort index for Sausalito is a 84 out of 100, indicating a more comfortable year-round climate compared to the US average of 54.\", \"Sausalito, California has an average temperature of 69 degrees in July and 43 degrees in January. Sausalito also gets 34 inches of rain per year.\", \"Average temperature in Sausalito: The average temperature in Sausalito is relatively mild, with the highest monthly average temperature being 58 degrees in September and the lowest monthly average temperature being 50 degrees in December. Snowfall: There is no snowfall in Sausalito. Precipitation: The most monthly precipitation in Sausalito occurs in January with 0 inches. The annual precipitation in Sausalito is 34 inches, which is lower than the US average of 39 inches.\", \"The average weather in Sausalito can be described as follows:\\n\\n- **Temperature:** \\n  - The highest monthly average temperature in Sausalito is 58 degrees in September.\\n  - The lowest monthly average temperature is 50 degrees in December.\\n  - The July high is around 69 degrees.\\n  - The January low is 43 degrees.\\n\\n- **Precipitation:** \\n  - Sausalito receives 34 inches of rain per year, compared to the US average of 39 inches.\\n  - Snowfall is 0 inches, while the average US city gets 26 inches of snow per year.\\n  - There are 56 days with any measurable precipitation annually.\\n\\n- **Air Quality and Comfort Index:** \\n  - The air quality index in Sausalito is 13% better than the national average.\\n  - The Sperling's comfort index for Sausalito is 84 out of 100, indicating a more comfortable year-round climate.\\n  - The US average for the comfort index is 54.\\n  - A higher score indicates a more comfortable year-round climate.\\n\\n- **Other Weather Details:** \\n  - There are 256 sunny days per year in Sausalito, California.\\n  - The number of days with any measurable precipitation is 56.\\n\\n- **Seasonal Differences:** \\n  - Sausalito experiences mild temperatures with a higher average in September (58 degrees) and a lower average in December (50 degrees).\\n  - There is no significant snowfall, and the comfort index is high, suggesting a pleasant climate year-round.\\n\\nOverall, Sausalito enjoys a mild and temperate climate with relatively low precipitation and an average annual temperature that is higher than the US national average.\"]", "time_sec": 36.261, "generation_time_seconds": 35.2496, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0035, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 5461, 9104, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 646, 387, 7481, 438, 11017, 1447, 12, 576, 8426, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 6122, 374, 220, 20, 23, 12348, 624, 12, 576, 15457, 15088, 5461, 9315, 304, 6652, 374, 220, 20, 15, 12348, 624, 12, 576, 1429, 15088, 59950, 13666, 304, 6058, 448, 220, 15, 14924, 624, 12, 576, 3720, 4271, 1922, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 374, 220, 16, 18, 4, 2664, 1091, 279, 5313, 5461, 624, 12, 576, 24761, 1922, 304, 328, 79074, 6357, 374, 220, 21, 16, 4, 10960, 1091, 279, 5313, 5461, 624, 12, 328, 79074, 6357, 5221, 220, 18, 19, 14924, 315, 11174, 817, 1042, 11, 892, 374, 2686, 1091, 279, 2274, 5461, 315, 220, 18, 24, 14924, 624, 12, 18901, 13464, 374, 220, 15, 14924, 11, 892