y receives only 34 inches of rain annually, compared to the US average of 39 inches. Sausalito's air quality is better than the national average, but its pollution level is worse. The city enjoys a Mediterranean climate with an average annual temperature range from 43 degrees in January to 69 degrees in July, and it has 256 sunny days per year.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9193252658897936, "g_worst_claim": -0.5108054478963217, "g_content": 1.1235566896812939, "g_traj_mean": 0.8252089619636536}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 61.88, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.9, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "240", "question": "how do crab traps work", "gt": "Based on the given passages, a crab trap is a large square metal cage with a system of nets inside that allows crabs to enter through a narrow slit at the top. To set the trap, the ends with lead-ins are placed in the water and the crabs are attracted to the free meal offered by the trap. The Alaska Department of Fish and Game recommends using king crab pots that range from 6 by 6 feet to 8 by 8 feet with heights between 2 and 3 feet. Over time, these mechanisms may disable the trap, preventing it from ghost fishing.", "pred": "Crab traps work by allowing crabs to enter but not escape. They are large square metal cages, typically about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide, with lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom, leading to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. The crabs must crawl up the leads to reach the entrance.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Crab traps work by allowing crabs to enter but not escape. They are large square metal cages, typically about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide, with lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom, leading to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. The crabs must crawl up the leads to reach the entrance.", "cot": "[\"Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out. The crab pot is a large square about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide. Two ends have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.\", \"Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out.\", \"Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps or pots are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out. The crab pots are designed to be about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide with lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.\", \"Crab traps work by allowing crabs to enter but not escape. They are large square metal cages, typically about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide, with lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom, leading to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. The crabs must crawl up the leads to reach the entrance.\"]", "time_sec": 16.42, "generation_time_seconds": 15.8169, "selection_time_seconds": 0.5952, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [16001, 370, 44560, 975, 553, 1667, 264, 1849, 315, 52457, 4766, 264, 3460, 9317, 35360, 1865, 315, 9067, 476, 10063, 9317, 11294, 429, 374, 48580, 448, 9509, 15904, 13, 576, 44560, 525, 6188, 311, 2138, 1560, 3435, 304, 714, 537, 1077, 1105, 700, 13, 576, 59412, 3338, 374, 264, 3460, 9334, 911, 220, 17, 7541, 1550, 323, 220, 23, 7541, 6884, 13, 9043, 10335, 614, 2990, 21853, 429, 9210, 1119, 279, 22862, 504, 279, 11067, 323, 5622, 311, 264, 15026, 78030, 911, 220, 17, 7541, 1119, 279, 3338, 13, 1096, 78030, 374, 279, 1172, 19809, 1119, 279, 22862, 13, 576, 1560, 3435, 13083, 807, 1969, 45664, 705, 279, 11508, 311, 633, 311, 862, 1910, 15145, 13, 151645], "pred": "Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out. The crab pot is a large square about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide. Two ends have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.486949376157441, "g_worst_claim": 1.305976359049479, "g_content": 3.6877557927911933, "g_traj_mean": 2.7173256874084473}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16001, 370, 44560, 975, 553, 1667, 264, 1849, 315, 52457, 4766, 264, 3460, 9317, 35360, 1865, 315, 9067, 476, 10063, 9317, 11294, 429, 374, 48580, 448, 9509, 15904, 13, 576, 44560, 525, 6188, 311, 2138, 1560, 3435, 304, 714, 537, 1077, 1105, 700, 13, 151645], "pred": "Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1218642925393993, "g_worst_claim": 1.3104263305664063, "g_content": 3.6270078576129414, "g_traj_mean": 2.3386940956115723}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16001, 370, 44560, 975, 553, 1667, 264, 1849, 315, 52457, 4766, 264, 3460, 9317, 35360, 1865, 315, 9067, 476, 10063, 9317, 11294, 429, 374, 48580, 448, 9509, 15904, 13, 576, 44560, 476, 50031, 525, 6188, 311, 2138, 1560, 3435, 304, 714, 537, 1077, 1105, 700, 13, 576, 59412, 50031, 525, 6188, 311, 387, 911, 220, 17, 7541, 1550, 323, 220, 23, 7541, 6884, 448, 2990, 21853, 429, 9210, 1119, 279, 22862, 504, 279, 11067, 323, 5622, 311, 264, 15026, 78030, 911, 220, 17, 7541, 1119, 279, 3338, 13, 1096, 78030, 374, 279, 1172, 19809, 1119, 279, 22862, 13, 576, 1560, 3435, 13083, 807, 1969, 45664, 705, 279, 11508, 311, 633, 311, 862, 1910, 15145, 13, 151645], "pred": "Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps or pots are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out. The crab pots are designed to be about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide with lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.3873836654402214, "g_worst_claim": 1.6348285675048828, "g_content": 3.343602498372396, "g_traj_mean": 2.5364127159118652}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16001, 370, 44560, 975, 553, 10693, 1560, 3435, 311, 3725, 714, 537, 12449, 13, 2379, 525, 3460, 9334, 9317, 80847, 11, 11136, 911, 220, 17, 7541, 1550, 323, 220, 23, 7541, 6884, 11, 448, 2990, 21853, 429, 9210, 1119, 279, 22862, 504, 279, 11067, 323, 5622, 11, 6388, 311, 264, 15026, 78030, 911, 220, 17, 7541, 1119, 279, 3338, 13, 576, 1560, 3435, 1969, 45664, 705, 279, 11508, 311, 5545, 279, 19809, 13, 151645], "pred": "Crab traps work by allowing crabs to enter but not escape. They are large square metal cages, typically about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide, with lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom, leading to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. The crabs must crawl up the leads to reach the entrance.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.108836316654825, "g_worst_claim": 1.2053101403372628, "g_content": 2.990937401266659, "g_traj_mean": 2.1121952533721924}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.01, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "242", "question": "how do crab traps work", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how crab traps work:\n\nCrab traps are made of a metal cage with a system of nets inside, which are designed to allow crabs to enter but not escape. The traps have two leads that angle into the pot from the sides and bottom, leading to a narrow slit entrance. The crabs crawl up the leads to reach the bait inside the pot, but cannot exit through the slit. The pot is designed to keep the crabs inside until they can be retrieved by the fisherman.\n\nAdditionally, according to passage 3, crab pots can be equipped with mechanisms that disable them over time, preventing them from continuing to catch crabs after they have been abandoned or become lost. These mechanisms can include biodegradable mesh or dissolvable cords.", "pred": "Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out. The crab pot is a large square about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide. Two ends have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out. The crab pot is a large square about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide. Two ends have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.", "cot": "[\"Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out. The crab pot is a large square about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide. Two ends have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.\", \"Crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The traps or pots are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out. The crab pot is a large square about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide. Two ends have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crabs realize they must crawl up the leads to get to their free meal.\", \"Based on the provided passage, crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. These traps allow crabs to enter through a narrow slit but do not let them exit. The crabs must crawl up the leads to get to the free meal inside the trap.\", \"The crab traps work by using a system of nets inside a large metal cage made of wire or flat metal mesh that is reinforced with steel bars. The pots are designed to allow crabs in but not let them out. This is achieved by having a large square about 2 feet high and 8 feet wide trap with two ends that have lead-ins that angle into the trap from the sides and bottom to a narrow slit about 2 feet into the pot. This slit is the only entrance into the trap. The crab pots make the big catches in the crab-fishing world.\"]", "time_sec": 18.868, "generation_time_seconds": 18.1588, "selection_time_seconds": 0.705, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout"