{"id": "248", "question": "difference between feha and ada", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's a brief answer to the question:\n\nThe main difference between FEHA and ADA is that FEHA applies to all employers in California, regardless of size or sector, while ADA applies to private employers with 4 to 15 employees and does not cover public employers. Additionally, FEHA has a broader definition of disability, requiring only that a mental or physical disability limit a major life activity, whereas ADA requires a substantial limitation.", "pred": "The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects a broader range of employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability to be present, whereas the ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects a broader range of employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability to be present, whereas the ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.", "cot": "[\"The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, whereas the FEHA affects more employees, and it doesn’t distinguish between private and public employers like the ADA does.\", \"The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects more employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, the ADA requires a physical or mental impairment substantially limiting a major life activity, whereas FEHA only requires a mental and physical disability limiting a major life activity.\", \"One difference between the FEHA (the Fair Employment and Housing Act) and the ADA (Americans with Disabilities Act) is that the ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, whereas the FEHA affects more employees, and it doesn’t distinguish between private and public employers like the ADA does.\", \"The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects a broader range of employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability to be present, whereas the ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.\"]", "time_sec": 12.621, "generation_time_seconds": 12.1273, "selection_time_seconds": 0.4904, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 429, 614, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 11, 19853, 279, 27931, 17020, 21501, 803, 8256, 11, 323, 432, 3171, 1405, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 1075, 279, 78325, 1558, 13, 151645], "pred": "The ADA applies to all employers in the private sector that have four to fifteen employees, whereas the FEHA affects more employees, and it doesn’t distinguish between private and public employers like the ADA does.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.6289297717848634, "g_worst_claim": 1.7250853220621745, "g_content": 3.5961422390407987, "g_traj_mean": 2.6082301139831543}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 78325, 16790, 311, 678, 22426, 304, 279, 869, 10486, 448, 3040, 311, 36655, 8256, 11, 1393, 279, 27931, 17020, 21501, 803, 8256, 323, 1558, 537, 32037, 1948, 869, 323, 584, 22426, 13, 22406, 11, 279, 78325, 7460, 264, 6961, 476, 10502, 52217, 31202, 32894, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 11, 19853, 27931, 17020, 1172, 7460, 264, 10502, 323, 6961, 27254, 32894, 264, 3598, 2272, 5702, 1