sector with four to fifteen employees, while the FEHA affects a broader range of employees and does not distinguish between private and public employers. Additionally, FEHA requires a disability to be present, whereas the ADA requires a physical or mental impairment that substantially limits a major life activity.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7388385450138766, "g_worst_claim": 0.5998580596026253, "g_content": 2.2017542521158853, "g_traj_mean": 1.7076855897903442}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.56, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "249", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "gt": "To grill pork chops according to allrecipes.com, start by preheating an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse the pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat and allow to stand for 10 minutes. Finally, grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "pred": "[The steps to grill pork chops are: preheat an outdoor grill to medium heat and lightly oil the grate, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined, rinse the pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture, massage the spice rub into the meat and allow it to stand for 10 minutes, and grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.]", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "[The steps to grill pork chops are: preheat an outdoor grill to medium heat and lightly oil the grate, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined, rinse the pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture, massage the spice rub into the meat and allow it to stand for 10 minutes, and grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.]", "cot": "[\"To grill pork chops, preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"To grill pork chops, preheat an outdoor grill to medium heat and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse the pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat and allow it to stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\\n\\nAnswer:[The steps to grill pork chops are: preheat an outdoor grill to medium heat and lightly oil the grate, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined, rinse the pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture, massage the spice rub into the meat and allow it to stand for 10 minutes, and grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.]\", \"Grill pork chops for medium heat, using an outdoor grill. Lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse the pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat and allow to stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"To grill pork chops, preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\"]", "time_sec": 22.882, "generation_time_seconds": 22.2883, "selection_time_seconds": 0.5892, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 39058, 35067, 90078, 11, 855, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 8628, 11, 323, 33404, 5590, 279, 85354, 13, 758, 264, 19212, 11, 6514, 3786, 279, 51514, 12021, 11, 3691, 24353, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 37327, 16723, 11, 25298, 40454, 11, 73188, 12570, 34448, 19187, 11, 323, 16205, 17172, 287, 3080, 26364, 10856, 13, 57368, 325, 35067, 90078, 11, 323, 84847, 279, 14401, 90078, 389, 2176, 11067, 448, 279, 41686, 20980, 13, 3085, 697, 6078, 11, 6245, 279, 41686, 10273, 1119, 279, 13041, 26, 2138, 311, 2498, 369, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 13, 49848, 279, 90078, 916, 24614, 8628, 3080, 902, 5021, 18217, 4766, 11, 911, 220, 16, 17, 4420, 817, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "To grill pork chops, preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5030185143152874, "g_worst_claim": 0.4834144910176595, "g_content": 2.036549009125808, "g_traj_mean": 1.686827540397644}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 39058, 35067, 90078, 11, 855, 19