ly 12 minutes per side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2990289945286715, "g_worst_claim": 0.08703101674715678, "g_content": 1.4221630096435547, "g_traj_mean": 1.2597962617874146}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 68.63, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "251", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "gt": "To grill pork chops according to the instructions provided in Allrecipes.com, follow these steps: \n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat. \n2. Lightly oil the grate. \n3. Mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until well combined. \n4. Rinse pork chops and sprinkle them with the spice mixture on both sides. \n5. Massage the spice rub into the meat and let it stand for 10 minutes. \n6. Grill the chops over indirect heat for about 12 minutes per side, or until they are no longer pink inside.", "pred": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\n2. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\n2. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "cot": "[\"To grill pork chops, preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate.\\n2. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined.\\n3. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture.\\n4. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes.\\n5. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"1) Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. 2) In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. 3) Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. 4) With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes. 5) Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\", \"Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.\"]", "time_sec": 18.632, "generation_time_seconds": 17.9045, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7168, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 39058, 35067, 90078, 11, 855, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 8628, 11, 323, 33404, 559