t an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4977814617538332, "g_worst_claim": 0.5311055183410645, "g_content": 2.2920290860262784, "g_traj_mean": 1.7009727954864502}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 4968, 19963, 458, 15789, 39058, 369, 11051, 8628, 11, 323, 33404, 5590, 279, 85354, 13, 758, 264, 19212, 11, 6514, 3786, 51514, 12021, 11, 3691, 24353, 11, 30635, 16723, 11, 37327, 16723, 11, 25298, 40454, 11, 73188, 12570, 34448, 19187, 11, 323, 16205, 17172, 287, 3080, 26364, 10856, 13, 57368, 325, 35067, 90078, 11, 323, 84847, 279, 14401, 90078, 389, 2176, 11067, 448, 279, 41686, 20980, 13, 3085, 697, 6078, 11, 6245, 279, 41686, 10273, 1119, 279, 13041, 26, 2138, 311, 2498, 369, 220, 16, 15, 4420, 13, 49848, 279, 90078, 916, 24614, 8628, 3080, 902, 5021, 18217, 4766, 11, 911, 220, 16, 17, 4420, 817, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat; allow to stand for 10 minutes. Grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4376164472424662, "g_worst_claim": 0.5294500589370728, "g_content": 2.2327799115862166, "g_traj_mean": 1.691789150238037}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.4, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "255", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "gt": "To clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house and remove the cover.\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole of the vent.\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding it out of the joint.\n4. Use the dryer vent brush to remove lint from both the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\n6. Additionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning that area as well.\n7. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter and remove the lint filter frame for easier access to clean.\n8. This thorough cleaning will help your dryer run efficiently and reduce the risk of house fires.\n\nNote: The information provided in the given passages is sufficient to answer the question.", "pred": "Step 1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\nStep 2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\nStep 3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\nStep 4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\nStep 5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Step 1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\nStep 2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\nStep 3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\nStep 4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\nStep 5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.", "cot": "[\"To clean the dryer vent, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\n\\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.\", \"To clean a dryer vent, follow these detailed steps:\\n\\n1. **Locate the Dryer Vent Cover**: Find the cover on the outside of your house where the dryer vent is located.\\n\\n2. **Remove the Cover**: Take off the cover. The vent duct should be able to slide out easily if it's not fastened or sealed to the exterior of the house.\\n\\n3. **Clean the Inside of the Hole**: Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from inside the hole.\\n\\n4. **Disconnect the Vent**: Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n\\n5. **Clean the Vent**: Again, use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n\\n6. **Reconnect the Vent**: Reattach the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\n\\n7. **Optional Additional Steps**:\\n   - **Remove the Bottom Front Panel**: If you want to clean the bottom front panel of the dryer, do so by removing it.\\n   - **Clean Around the Lint Filter**: Pay attention to the area around the lint filter. Removing the lint filter frame can provide easier access to lint deposits, making it easier to clean thoroughly. A vacuum nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning.\\n   - **Ensure the Dryer Runs Efficiently**: Cleaning the dryer vent and other areas related to the lint buildup can help the dryer run as efficiently as possible.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively clean your dryer vent, ensuring it operates efficiently and reduces the risk of fire hazards.\", \"Step 1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\nStep 2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\nStep 3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\nStep 4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\nStep 5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\", \"To clean the dryer vent, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\n7. Optionally, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also.\\n8. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too.\\n9. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained & a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning.\\n10. It will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.\"]", "time_sec": 33.475, "generation_time_seconds": 32.336, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1331, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4240, 279, 46622, 10378, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 95210, 279, 46622, 10378, 3421, 389, 279, 4889, 315, 697, 3753, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 3421, 26, 279, 10378, 44239, 1265, 14983, 1290, 700, 421, 432, 4436, 944, 4937, 6758, 476, 19046, 311, 279, 2114, 594, 27263, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 4766, 279, 14178, 624, 19, 13, 10783, 279, 10378, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 553, 6975, 837, 23593, 279, 10378, 41904, 323, 33832, 279, 10378, 700, 315, 279, 45711, 34731, 10284, 624, 20, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 279, 10378, 438, 1632, 438, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 624, 21, 13, 1032, 6459, 279, 10378, 323, 3271, 279, 46622, 1182, 2348, 279, 7002, 382, 49574, 11, 498, 1231, 1366, 311, 4057, 279, 5622, 4065, 6945, 315, 279, 46622, 323, 4240, 1052, 1083, 13, 11471, 6529, 311, 279, 3082, 2163, 279, 57920, 4051, 11, 2238, 13, 3216, 17592, 279, 57920, 4051, 4034, 11, 8661, 2615, 311, 57920, 33651, 646, 387, 18163, 11, 323, 264, 9283, 81881, 646, 387, 42478, 304, 369, 264, 803, 17423, 15826, 13, 1096, 686, 1083, 1492, 697, 46622, 1598, 438, 29720, 438, 432, 646, 13, 151645], "pred": "Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0015192844017764, "g_worst_claim": 0.20355170965194702, "g_content": 2.386412143707275