 700, 421, 432, 4436, 944, 4937, 6758, 476, 19046, 311, 279, 2114, 594, 27263, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 4766, 279, 14178, 624, 19, 13, 10783, 279, 10378, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 553, 6975, 837, 23593, 279, 10378, 41904, 323, 33832, 279, 10378, 700, 315, 279, 45711, 34731, 10284, 624, 20, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 279, 10378, 438, 1632, 438, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 624, 21, 13, 1032, 6459, 279, 10378, 323, 3271, 279, 46622, 1182, 2348, 279, 7002, 624, 22, 13, 96195, 11, 4057, 279, 5622, 4065, 6945, 315, 279, 46622, 323, 4240, 1052, 1083, 624, 23, 13, 11471, 6529, 311, 279, 3082, 2163, 279, 57920, 4051, 11, 2238, 624, 24, 13, 3216, 17592, 279, 57920, 4051, 4034, 11, 8661, 2615, 311, 57920, 33651, 646, 387, 18163, 609, 264, 9283, 81881, 646, 387, 42478, 304, 369, 264, 803, 17423, 15826, 624, 16, 15, 13, 1084, 686, 1083, 1492, 697, 46622, 1598, 438, 29720, 438, 432, 646, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\n7. Optionally, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also.\n8. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too.\n9. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained & a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning.\n10. It will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0623162643139272, "g_worst_claim": 0.2331330974896749, "g_content": 2.392633056640625, "g_traj_mean": 1.9313074350357056}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.29, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "256", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "gt": "To clean your dryer vent, follow these steps:\n\n1. Remove the outside cover on the vent.\n2. Use a special lint brush with an extendable handle to clean the inside of the pipe.\n3. If possible, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there as well.\n4. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter and clean it thoroughly.\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.", "pred": "To clean the dryer vent, follow these steps:\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To clean the dryer vent, follow these steps:\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.", "cot": "[\"To clean the dryer vent, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\n\\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.\", \"To clean a dryer vent:\\n\\n1. **Locate the dryer vent cover**: Find the cover that is located on the outside of your house.\\n\\n2. **Remove the vent cover**: Unscrew or remove the cover so you can access the vent duct inside. The vent duct should slide out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n\\n3. **Clean the inside of the vent duct**: Use a dryer vent brush with an extendable handle to remove the lint from inside the hole.\\n\\n4. **Disconnect the vent**: Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n\\n5. **Clean the vent at the back**: Use the dryer vent brush to remove lint from the vent duct as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n\\n6. **Reconnect the vent**: After cleaning both the inside and outside of the vent duct, reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively clean the dryer vent and maintain the efficiency of your dryer.\", \"To clean the dryer vent, follow these steps:\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\", \"To clean the dryer vent, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\n\\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also, and pay attention to the area around the lint filter. By removing the lint filter frame, you can have easier access to lint deposits and use a vacuum nozzle for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.\"]", "time_sec": 30.474, "generation_time_seconds": 29.4715, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9937, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4240, 279, 46622, 10378, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 95210, 279, 46622, 10378, 3421, 389, 279, 4889, 315, 697, 3753, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 3421, 26, 279, 10378, 44239, 1265, 14983, 1290, 700, 421, 432, 4436, 944, 4937, 6758, 476, 19046, 311, 279, 2114, 594, 27263, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 4766, 279, 14178, 624, 19, 13, 10783, 279, 10378, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 553, 6975, 837, 2