 from inside the hole.\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7326230728875531, "g_worst_claim": 0.2641777992248535, "g_content": 2.054573920465285, "g_traj_mean": 1.6374412775039673}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4240, 279, 46622, 10378, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 95210, 279, 46622, 10378, 3421, 389, 279, 4889, 315, 697, 3753, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 3421, 26, 279, 10378, 44239, 1265, 14983, 1290, 700, 421, 432, 4436, 944, 4937, 6758, 476, 19046, 311, 279, 2114, 594, 27263, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 4766, 279, 14178, 624, 19, 13, 10783, 279, 10378, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 553, 6975, 837, 23593, 279, 10378, 41904, 323, 33832, 279, 10378, 700, 315, 279, 45711, 34731, 10284, 624, 20, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 279, 10378, 438, 1632, 438, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 624, 21, 13, 1032, 6459, 279, 10378, 323, 3271, 279, 46622, 1182, 2348, 279, 7002, 382, 49574, 11, 498, 1231, 1366, 311, 4057, 279, 5622, 4065, 6945, 315, 279, 46622, 323, 4240, 1052, 1083, 11, 323, 2291, 6529, 311, 279, 3082, 2163, 279, 57920, 4051, 13, 3216, 17592, 279, 57920, 4051, 4034, 11, 498, 646, 614, 8661, 2615, 311, 57920, 33651, 323, 990, 264, 28202, 81881, 369, 264, 803, 17423, 15826, 13, 1096, 686, 1083, 1492, 697, 46622, 1598, 438, 29720, 438, 432, 646, 13, 151645], "pred": "Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also, and pay attention to the area around the lint filter. By removing the lint filter frame, you can have easier access to lint deposits and use a vacuum nozzle for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8949478457802127, "g_worst_claim": 0.28216036160786945, "g_content": 2.259432253630265, "g_traj_mean": 1.8108832836151123}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 47.93, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "257", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here are the steps to clean a dryer vent based on the provided passages:\n\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house (passage 1) and remove it by sliding it out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the exterior (step 2).\n2. Use a dryer vent brush to remove lint from the hole where the vent connects to the dryer (step 3).\n3. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint (step 4).\n4. Clean the lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer using the dryer vent brush (step 4).\n5. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall (step 5).\n6. If desired, remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean the area around the lint filter (passage 2).\n7. Use a vacuum nozzle to clean the lint deposits in the area around the lint filter frame (passage 2).\n\nNote: Passage 3 provides additional information but does not provide specific instructions for cleaning the dryer vent. Therefore, these steps are based on the information provided in passages 1-2.", "pred": "Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "cot": "[\"To clean the dryer vent, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\n\\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.\", \"To clean the dryer vent, follow these steps:\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn’t fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\", \"To clean the dryer vent, you need to follow several steps:\\nStep 1: Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\nStep 2: Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\nStep 3: Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\nStep 4: Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\nStep 5: Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\nStep 6: Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\n\\nYou may also want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained & a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. It will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.\", \"To clean a dryer vent, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Locate the dryer vent cover on the outside of your house.\\n2. Remove the cover; the vent duct should slide right out if it isn't fastened or sealed to the home's exterior.\\n3. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from inside the hole.\\n4. Remove the vent from the back of the dryer by unscrewing the vent clamp and sliding the vent out of the elbow-shaped joint.\\n5. Using your dryer vent brush, remove the lint from the vent as well as the hole in the back of the dryer.\\n6. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall.\\n\\nAdditionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there, as well as pay attention to the area around the lint filter. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.\"]", "time_sec": 31.466, "generation_time_seconds": 30.619, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7929, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4240, 279, 46622, 10378, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 95210, 279, 46622, 10378, 3421, 389, 279, 4889, 315, 697, 3753, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 3421, 26, 279, 10378, 44239, 1265, 14983, 1290, 700, 421, 432, 4436, 944, 4937, 6758, 476, 19046, 311, 279, 2114, 594, 27263, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 4766, 279, 14178, 624, 19, 13, 10783, 279, 10378, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 553, 6975, 837, 23593, 279, 10378, 41904, 323, 33832, 279, 10378, 700, 315, 279, 45711, 34731, 10284, 624, 20, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 279, 10378, 438, 1632, 438, 279, 14178, 304, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 624, 21, 13, 1032, 6459, 279, 10378, 323, 3271, 279, 46622, 1182, 2348, 279, 7002, 382, 49574, 11, 498, 1231, 1366, 311, 4057, 279, 5622, 4065, 6945, 315, 279, 46622, 323, 4240, 1052, 1083, 13, 11471, 6529, 311, 279, 3082, 2163, 279, 57920, 4051, 11, 2238, 13, 3216, 17592, 279, 57920, 4051, 4034, 11, 8661, 2615, 311, 57920, 33651, 646, 387, 18163, 11, 323, 264, 9283, 81881, 646, 387, 42478, 304, 369, 264, 803, 17423, 15826, 13, 1096, 686, 1083, 1492, 697, 46622, 1598, 438, 29720, 438, 432, 646, 13, 151645], "pred": "Additionally, you may want to remove the bottom front panel of the dryer and clean there also. Pay attention to the area around the lint filter, too. By removing the lint filter frame, easier access to lint deposits can be gained, and a vac nozzle can be slipped in for a more thorough cleaning. This will also help your dryer run as efficiently as it can.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0092769681279883, "g_worst_claim": 0.5121264060338339, "g_content": 2.414015611012777, "g_traj_mean": 1.8976327180862427}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4240, 279, 46622, 10378, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 95210, 279, 46622, 10378, 3421, 389, 279, 4889, 315, 697, 3753, 624, 17, 13, 10783, 279, 3421, 26, 279, 10378, 44239, 1265, 14983, 1290, 700, 421, 432, 4436, 1405, 4937, 6758, 476, 19046, 311, 279, 2114, 594, 27263, 624, 18, 13, 12091, 697, 46622, 10378, 15625, 11, 4057, 279, 57920, 504, 4766, 279, 14178, 624, 19, 13, 10783, 279, 10378, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 46622, 553, 6975, 837, 23593, 279, 