{"id": "280", "question": "what is severe osteoporosis", "gt": "Based on the given passages, severe osteoporosis refers to a advanced stage of the disease where the bones have weakened significantly, leading to severe bone loss and increased risk of fractures. At this stage, symptoms such as back pain, loss of height, and fractures are more pronounced and frequent. The risk of fractures is particularly high in the spine, hips, and wrists, and can occur even without a fall or injury.\n\nIn summary, severe osteoporosis is characterized by significant bone weakening, heightened risk of fractures, and more pronounced symptoms.", "pred": "Without treatment, a person with severe osteoporosis is likely to experience multiple fractures, most often in the spine or hips, which support the body's weight. Fractures of the spine can occur even without a fall or an injury, as the bones of the spine become so weak that they start to compress.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Without treatment, a person with severe osteoporosis is likely to experience multiple fractures, most often in the spine or hips, which support the body's weight. Fractures of the spine can occur even without a fall or an injury, as the bones of the spine become so weak that they start to compress.", "cot": "[\"Severe osteoporosis is characterized by symptoms such as back pain, loss of height over time with a stooped posture, and fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones. Without treatment, a person with severe osteoporosis is likely to have fractures, most often in the spine or hips (which support the body's weight) or in the wrists from bracing against a fall. Fractures of the spine can happen even without a fall or an injury, as the bones of the spine become so weak that they start to compress.\", \"Severe osteoporosis often manifests with symptoms such as back pain, a loss of height over time with a stooped posture, and fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones. Without proper treatment, individuals with severe osteoporosis are at high risk of experiencing fractures, particularly in the spine or hips, which can occur even without a fall or significant trauma. The bones of the spine can become so weak that they start to compress, leading to further complications.\", \"Severe osteoporosis can be characterized by symptoms such as back pain, loss of height over time with stooped posture, and fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones. It is a condition that typically has no symptoms until significant bone damage has already occurred. Without proper treatment, individuals with severe osteoporosis are more likely to experience fractures, particularly in the spine or hips (which support the body's weight) or in the wrists from bracing against a fall. The severity of the condition can lead to fractures even without a fall or injury, as the bones of the spine become so weak that they start to compress.\", \"Based on the provided passages, severe osteoporosis can be characterized by the following symptoms once the bones have been weakened by bone density loss:\\n\\n1. Back pain.\\n2. Loss of height over time with a stooped posture.\\n3. Fractures of the vertebrae, wrists, hips, or other bones.\\n\\nWithout treatment, a person with severe osteoporosis is likely to experience multiple fractures, most often in the spine or hips, which support the body's weight. Fractures of the spine can occur even without a fall or an injury, as the bones of the spine become so weak that they start to compress.\"]", "time_sec": 21.051, "generation_time_seconds": 20.2264, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8186, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1514, 19289, 51268, 88666, 10704, 374, 31871, 553, 13495, 1741, 438, 1182, 6646, 11, 4709, 315, 2608, 916, 882, 448, 264, 42032, 16367, 47278, 11, 323, 77232, 315, 279,