{"id": "286", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "gt": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 325-350 degrees Fahrenheit. If you don't have time to defrost the roast, put it in the oven at 250 F for about an hour. Afterwards, take it out and season it with salt, pepper, and any seasonings you prefer, such as thyme, oregano or garlic. Rub the surface with 2 tsp. of olive oil. Place the roast in a roasting pan with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards, and put it back in the oven for about 1.5 to 3 hours depending on its size, or about 20-30 minutes per pound. Make sure the roast is cooked thoroughly by using a meat thermometer; the internal temperature should reach 150 degrees Fahrenheit. Once it is cooked, cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "pred": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "cot": "[\"To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\", \"To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\", \"Start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\", \"To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\"]", "time_sec": 21.806, "generation_time_seconds": 20.5359, "selection_time_seconds": 1.2591, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 264, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 11, 1191, 553, 855, 383, 1095, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 13, 10224, 279, 19690, 35067, 76960, 304, 264, 25600, 27815, 7215, 389, 1909, 315, 264, 926, 14725, 29659, 448, 279, 8664, 315, 279, 35067, 76960, 12880, 43954, 13, 12514, 279, 35067, 76960, 369, 911, 220, 17, 15, 12, 18, 15, 4420, 817, 30023, 13, 17101, 264, 13041, 92197, 11, 323, 1273, 279, 13041, 1283, 17233, 13, 3197, 279, 5306, 9315, 315, 279, 13041, 374, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 11, 279, 13041, 374, 5527, 311, 387, 4429, 700, 315, 279, 23387, 13, 17757, 279, 57685, 448, 24649, 46399, 11, 323, 1077, 432, 2444, 369, 220, 18, 15, 4420, 1573, 13480, 13, 151645], "pred": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2835433623307941, "g_worst_claim": 0.501600710550944, "g_content": 1.3943735341556738, "g_traj_mean": 1.239280343055725}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 264, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 11, 1191, 553, 855, 383, 1095, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 