{"id": "291", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit.\n2. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards.\n3. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound.\n4. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking.\n5. When the internal temperature of the meat reaches 150 degrees Fahrenheit, cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\n\nSo, the steps to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven are: preheat the oven, place the roast in a shallow baking pan, cook for 20-30 minutes per pound, check the internal temperature, cover and let it sit before serving.", "pred": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack, with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack, with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "cot": "[\"To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\", \"To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack, with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\", \"Preheat your oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\", \"Preheat your oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Place the frozen pork loin roast in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer to test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.\"]", "time_sec": 20.524, "generation_time_seconds": 19.7834, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7288, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 264, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 11, 1191, 553, 855, 383, 1095, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 13, 10224, 279, 19690, 35067, 76960, 304, 264, 25600, 27815, 7215, 389, 1909, 315, 264, 926, 14725, 29659, 448, 279, 8664, 315, 279, 35067, 76960, 12880, 43954, 13, 12514, 279, 35067, 76960, 369, 911, 220, 17, 15, 12, 18, 15, 4420, 817, 30023, 13, 17101, 264, 13041, 92197, 11, 323, 1273, 279, 13041, 1283, 17233, 13, 3197, 279, 5306, 9315, 315, 279, 13041, 374, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 11, 279, 13041, 374, 5527, 311, 387, 4429, 700, 315, 279, 23387, 13, 17757, 279, 57685, 448, 24649, 46399, 11, 323, 1077, 432, 2444, 369, 220, 18, 15, 4420, 1573, 13480, 13, 151645], "pred": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2795162720551796, "g_worst_claim": 0.5279156684875488, "g_content": 1.398880880387103, "g_traj_mean": 1.239791989326477}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 4296, 264, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 11, 855, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 13, 10771, 279, 19690, 35067, 76960, 304, 264, 25600, 27815, 7215, 389, 1909, 315, 264, 926, 14725, 29659, 11, 448, 279, 8664, 315, 279, 35067, 76960, 12880, 43954, 13, 12514, 279, 35067, 76960, 369, 911, 220, 17, 15, 12, 18, 15, 4420, 817, 30023, 13, 17101, 264, 13041, 92197, 11, 323, 1273, 279, 13041, 1283, 17233, 13, 3197, 279, 5306, 9315, 315, 279, 13041, 374, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 11, 279, 13041, 374, 5527, 311, 387, 4429, 700, 315, 279, 23387, 13, 17757, 279, 57685, 448, 24649, 46399, 11, 323, 1077, 432, 2444, 369, 220, 18, 15, 4420, 1573, 13480, 13, 151645], "pred": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, preheat the oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Place the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack, with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer, and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil, and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.247760967507413, "g_worst_claim": 0.2799649437268575, "g_content": 1.2761221567789713, "g_traj_mean": 1.13956618309021}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [4703, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 13, 10224, 279, 19690, 35067, 76960, 304, 264, 25600, 27815, 7215, 389, 1909, 315, 264, 926, 14725, 29659, 448, 279, 8664, 12880, 43954, 13, 12514, 279, 35067, 76960, 369, 911, 220, 17, 15, 12, 18, 15, 4420, 817, 30023, 13, 17101, 264, 13041, 92197, 323, 1273, 279, 13041, 1283, 17233, 13, 3197, 279, 5306, 9315, 315, 279, 13041, 374, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 11, 279, 13041, 374, 5527, 311, 387, 4429, 700, 315, 279, 23387, 13, 17757, 279, 57685, 448, 24649, 46399, 323, 1077, 432, 2444, 369, 220, 18, 15, 4420, 1573, 13480, 13, 151645], "pred": "Preheat your oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Put the frozen pork loin in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer and test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready to be taken out of the oven. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2962335126418993, "g_worst_claim": 0.8175832430521647, "g_content": 1.727981420663687, "g_traj_mean": 1.3174914121627808}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [4703, 19963, 697, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 13, 10771, 279, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 264, 25600, 27815, 7215, 389, 1909, 315, 264, 926, 14725, 29659, 448, 279, 8664, 12880, 43954, 13, 12514, 279, 35067, 76960, 369, 911, 220, 17, 15, 12, 18, 15, 4420, 817, 30023, 13, 17101, 264, 13041, 92197, 311, 1273, 279, 13041, 1283, 17233, 13, 3197, 279, 5306, 9315, 315, 279, 13041, 374, 220, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 68723, 11, 279, 13041, 374, 5527, 13, 17757, 279, 57685, 448, 24649, 46399, 323, 1077, 432, 2444, 369, 220, 18, 15, 4420, 1573, 13480, 13, 151645], "pred": "Preheat your oven to 350 degrees Fahrenheit. Place the frozen pork loin roast in a shallow baking pan on top of a roasting rack with the fat facing upwards. Cook the pork loin for about 20-30 minutes per pound. Insert a meat thermometer to test the meat after cooking. When the internal temperature of the meat is 150 degrees Fahrenheit, the meat is ready. Cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2346672361547297, "g_worst_claim": 0.820475959777832, "g_content": 1.6534674072265625, "g_traj_mean": 1.2361396551132202}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 73.42, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "294", "question": "what is the proper way to fertilize your grass", "gt": "To properly fertilize your grass, you should fertilize at the beginning of the growing season for your specific grass type. For warm season grasses, this would be when the grass turns green in the early spring. You should also know the type of fertilizer to use based on the type of grass you have and do a pH soil test to ensure the fertilizer has the appropriate pH for your soil. Once you've determined the correct fertilizer and timing, apply it in a perpendicular pattern and check the lawn after application by stepping on the turf. If the leaf blade bounces back up, the lawn is in good shape, but if it lays flat, you've over-fertilized.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can ensure that your grass receives the proper amount of fertilizer at the right time, promoting healthy growth.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "By following these steps, you can ensure that your grass receives the proper amount of fertilizer at the right time, promoting healthy growth.", "cot": "[\"The proper way to fertilize your grass involves several steps:\\n\\n1. **Timing**: Fertilize at the right time of year, specifically at the beginning of the growing season. This timing is crucial for different types of grasses. For example, warm season grasses should be fertilized when the grass begins to turn green at the beginning of spring.\\n\\n2. **Type of Grass**: Knowing the type of grass you have is essential because it determines the type of fertilizer needed and how often it should be applied.\\n\\n3. **Soil pH Test**: Conduct a pH soil test to measure the alkalinity or acidity of the soil. This test helps to determine the appropriate pH level for your fertilizer.\\n\\n4. **Lawn Measurement**: Measure your lawn to ensure you apply the correct amount of fertilizer.\\n\\n5. **Application**: Apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern. After applying, step on the turf to check if the leaf blade bounces back up. If it lays flat, you have over-fertilized.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that your grass receives the proper amount of fertilizer at the right time, promoting healthy growth.\", \"The proper way to fertilize your grass involves timing the fertilizer application correctly, knowing the type of grass you have, and ensuring the soil pH is suitable. It's recommended to fertilize warm season grasses when the grass begins to turn green at the beginning of spring. Additionally, it's important to measure your lawn and apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern, stepping on the turf to check if the leaf blade bounces back up or lays flat to determine if you have over-fertilized.\", \"Based on the provided passages, the proper way to fertilize your grass involves several key steps:\\n\\n1. **Timing**: Fertilize at the right time of year, specifically at the beginning of the growing season for warm season grasses when the grass begins to turn green at the beginning of spring.\\n\\n2. **Type of Grass**: Understand the type of grass you have, as the type will determine the type of fertilizer needed and how often it should be applied.\\n\\n3. **pH Soil Test**: Conduct a pH soil test to measure the alkalinity or acidity of the soil. This step helps to determine the appropriate pH for your fertilizer and ensures the soil conditions are right for optimal grass growth.\\n\\n4. **Measure Your Lawn**: Measure the size of your lawn to determine the amount of fertilizer needed.\\n\\n5. **Application**: Apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern. Check that the leaf blade bounces back up when you step on the turf. If it lays flat, you have over-fertilized, which can harm your grass.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that your grass is fertilized properly, promoting healthy growth and maintaining a lush lawn.\", \"The proper way to fertilize your grass involves several key steps:\\n\\n1. Timing the Fertilization: You should fertilize at the right time of year, specifically at the beginning of the growing season. This timing varies depending on the type of grass you have. For example, warm season grasses should be fertilized when they start to turn green at the beginning of spring.\\n\\n2. Understanding Your Grass Type: Knowing the type of grass in your lawn is crucial because different types of grass require different types of fertilizers and fertilization intervals. This information can help tailor your fertilization strategy to the specific needs of your grass.\\n\\n3. Conducting a Soil Test: Performing a pH soil test is important as it measures the alkalinity or acidity of the soil. This test helps in determining the optimal pH level for your fertilizer and ensures that the nutrients in the fertilizer are most effective.\\n\\n4. Measuring the Lawn: Measuring the size of your lawn will help in calculating the correct amount of fertilizer needed. This ensures that you neither under- nor over-fertilize, which could lead to poor grass health.\\n\\n5. Applying the Fertilizer: When applying the fertilizer, distribute it evenly across the lawn. After applying, check the lawn by stepping on it. If the leaf blade bounces back up, it indicates that you have applied the right amount of fertilizer. If the blade lays flat, you have over-fertilized, which can harm your grass.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that your grass is fertilized properly, promoting healthy growth and maintaining a vibrant lawn.\"]", "time_sec": 32.357, "generation_time_seconds": 31.6401, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7086, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 6169, 1616, 311, 35114, 551, 697, 16359, 17601, 3807, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 62805, 95518, 434, 85695, 551, 518, 279, 1290, 882, 315, 1042, 11, 11689, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 279, 7826, 3200, 13, 1096, 18405, 374, 16587, 369, 2155, 4494, 315, 16359, 288, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 8205, 3200, 16359, 288, 1265, 387, 35114, 1506, 979, 279, 16359, 12033, 311, 2484, 6176, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 10464, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 929, 315, 39946, 95518, 57633, 279, 943, 315, 16359, 498, 614, 374, 7565, 1576, 432, 26569, 279, 943, 315, 64291, 4362, 323, 1246, 3545, 432, 1265, 387, 9251, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 4416, 321, 36043, 3393, 95518, 49835, 264, 36043, 17171, 1273, 311, 6629, 279, 65687, 13489, 476, 96926, 315, 279, 17171, 13, 1096, 1273, 8609, 311, 8253, 279, 8311, 36043, 2188, 369, 697, 64291, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 43, 6379, 54240, 95518, 34104, 697, 36025, 311, 5978, 498, 3796, 279, 4396, 3311, 315, 64291, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 4988, 95518, 20552, 279, 64291, 304, 264, 76833, 5383, 13, 4636, 18950, 11, 3019, 389, 279, 58990, 311, 1779, 421, 279, 15933, 24838, 293, 29944, 1182, 705, 13, 1416, 432, 56522, 10063, 11, 498, 614, 916, 2220, 85695, 1506, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 5978, 429, 697, 16359, 21189, 279, 6169, 3311, 315, 64291, 518, 279, 1290, 882, 11, 22136, 9314, 6513, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can ensure that your grass receives the proper amount of fertilizer at the right time, promoting healthy growth.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1897733707482798, "g_worst_claim": 0.26206067029167623, "g_content": 1.6284054710751488, "g_traj_mean": 1.1393134593963623}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6169, 1616, 311, 35114, 551, 697, 16359, 17601, 18405, 279, 64291, 3766, 12440, 11, 14063, 279, 943, 315, 16359, 498, 614, 11, 323, 22573, 279, 17171, 36043, 374, 14452, 13, 1084, 594, 11102, 311, 35114, 551, 8205, 3200, 16359, 288, 979, 279, 16359, 12033, 311, 2484, 6176, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 10464, 13, 22406, 11, 432, 594, 2989, 311, 6629, 697, 36025, 323, 3796, 279, 64291, 304, 264, 76833, 5383, 11, 35467, 389, 279, 58990, 311, 1779, 421, 279, 15933, 24838, 293, 29944, 1182, 705, 476, 56522, 10063, 311, 8253, 421, 498, 614, 916, 2220, 85695, 1506, 13, 151645], "pred": "The proper way to fertilize your grass involves timing the fertilizer application correctly, knowing the type of grass you have, and ensuring the soil pH is suitable. It's recommended to fertilize warm season grasses when the grass begins to turn green at the beginning of spring. Additionally, it's important to measure your lawn and apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern, stepping on the turf to check if the leaf blade bounces back up or lays flat to determine if you have over-fertilized.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3159043544396494, "g_worst_claim": 0.4544857442378998, "g_content": 2.2445519187233667, "g_traj_mean": 1.5540690422058105}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 279, 6169, 1616, 311, 35114, 551, 697, 16359, 17601, 3807, 1376, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 62805, 95518, 434, 85695, 551, 518, 279, 1290, 882, 315, 1042, 11, 11689, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 279, 7826, 3200, 369, 8205, 3200, 16359, 288, 979, 279, 16359, 12033, 311, 2484, 6176, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 10464, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 929, 315, 39946, 95518, 70894, 279, 943, 315, 16359, 498, 614, 11, 438, 279, 943, 686, 8253, 279, 943, 315, 64291, 4362, 323, 1246, 3545, 432, 1265, 387, 9251, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 79, 39, 75519, 3393, 95518, 49835, 264, 36043, 17171, 1273, 311, 6629, 279, 65687, 13489, 476, 96926, 315, 279, 17171, 13, 1096, 3019, 8609, 311, 8253, 279, 8311, 36043, 369, 697, 64291, 323, 25351, 279, 17171, 4682, 525, 1290, 369, 22823, 16359, 6513, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 32236, 4615, 68392, 95518, 34104, 279, 1379, 315, 697, 36025, 311, 8253, 279, 3311, 315, 64291, 4362, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 4988, 95518, 20552, 279, 64291, 304, 264, 76833, 5383, 13, 4248, 429, 279, 15933, 24838, 293, 29944, 1182, 705, 979, 498, 3019, 389, 279, 58990, 13, 1416, 432, 56522, 10063, 11, 498, 614, 916, 2220, 85695, 1506, 11, 892, 646, 11428, 697, 16359, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 5978, 429, 697, 16359, 374, 35114, 1506, 10277, 11, 22136, 9314, 6513, 323, 20337, 264, 57267, 36025, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can ensure that your grass is fertilized properly, promoting healthy growth and maintaining a lush lawn.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9391809976720424, "g_worst_claim": 0.11197814074429599, "g_content": 1.4162155433937356, "g_traj_mean": 0.9740064740180969}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6169, 1616, 311, 35114, 551, 697, 16359, 17601, 3807, 1376, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 70813, 279, 434, 85695, 2022, 25, 1446, 1265, 35114, 551, 518, 279, 1290, 882, 315, 1042, 11, 11689, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 279, 7826, 3200, 13, 1096, 18405, 34227, 11649, 389, 279, 943, 315, 16359, 498, 614, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 8205, 3200, 16359, 288, 1265, 387, 35114, 1506, 979, 807, 1191, 311, 2484, 6176, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 10464, 382, 17, 13, 45451, 4615, 39946, 3990, 25, 57633, 279, 943, 315, 16359, 304, 697, 36025, 374, 16587, 1576, 2155, 4494, 315, 16359, 1373, 2155, 4494, 315, 35114, 12230, 323, 35114, 2022, 26992, 13, 1096, 1995, 646, 1492, 50956, 697, 35114, 2022, 8282, 311, 279, 3151, 3880, 315, 697, 16359, 382, 18, 13, 49835, 287, 264, 75519, 3393, 25, 69648, 264, 36043, 17171, 1273, 374, 2989, 438, 432, 10953, 279, 65687, 13489, 476, 96926, 315, 279, 17171, 13, 1096, 1273, 8609, 304, 25597, 279, 22823, 36043, 2188, 369, 697, 64291, 323, 25351, 429, 279, 36393, 304, 279, 64291, 525, 1429, 7373, 382, 19, 13, 2157, 68674, 279, 68392, 25, 2157, 68674, 279, 1379, 315, 697, 36025, 686, 1492, 304, 37614, 279, 4396, 3311, 315, 64291, 4362, 13, 1096, 25351, 429, 498, 13866, 1212, 12, 6329, 916, 2220, 85695, 551, 11, 892, 1410, 2990, 311, 7852, 16359, 2820, 382, 20, 13, 89601, 279, 434, 85695, 3135, 25, 3197, 18950, 279, 64291, 11, 16417, 432, 41047, 3941, 279, 36025, 13, 4636, 18950, 11, 1779, 279, 36025, 553, 35467, 389, 432, 13, 1416, 279, 15933, 24838, 293, 29944, 1182, 705, 11, 432, 14807, 429, 498, 614, 9251, 279, 1290, 3311, 315, 64291, 13, 1416, 279, 24838, 56522, 10063, 11, 498, 614, 916, 2220, 85695, 1506, 11, 892, 646, 11428, 697, 16359, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 5978, 429, 697, 16359, 374, 35114, 1506, 10277, 11, 22136, 9314, 6513, 323, 20337, 264, 32976, 36025, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can ensure that your grass is fertilized properly, promoting healthy growth and maintaining a vibrant lawn.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7202260198429499, "g_worst_claim": 0.038206501440568405, "g_content": 0.9255048479352679, "g_traj_mean": 0.6862756013870239}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 10.99, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "295", "question": "what is the proper way to fertilize your grass", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to fertilize your grass is to:\n\n1. Fertilize at the right time of year, which is at the beginning of the growing season, and varies for different types of grasses.\n2. Choose a fertilizer that is suitable for your type of grass and soil pH, as determined by a soil test.\n3. Apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern, avoiding over-fertilization, which can be determined by checking if the leaf blades bounce back up after being stepped on.", "pred": "1. Determine the right time of year to fertilize, which is typically at the beginning of the growing season for warm season grasses when the grass begins to turn green at the start of spring.\n2. Choose the appropriate fertilizer based on the type of grass you have. Different types of grasses require different fertilizers.\n3. Conduct a pH soil test to determine the soil's alkalinity or acidity, which helps in selecting the correct pH for your fertilizer.\n4. Measure the size of your lawn to ensure you have the right amount of fertilizer.\n5. Apply the fertilizer using a perpendicular pattern, and test the application by stepping on the turf. If the leaf blade bounces back up, it indicates that the lawn is receiving the right amount of fertilizer. If it lays flat, it means the lawn has been over-fertilized.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Determine the right time of year to fertilize, which is typically at the beginning of the growing season for warm season grasses when the grass begins to turn green at the start of spring.\n2. Choose the appropriate fertilizer based on the type of grass you have. Different types of grasses require different fertilizers.\n3. Conduct a pH soil test to determine the soil's alkalinity or acidity, which helps in selecting the correct pH for your fertilizer.\n4. Measure the size of your lawn to ensure you have the right amount of fertilizer.\n5. Apply the fertilizer using a perpendicular pattern, and test the application by stepping on the turf. If the leaf blade bounces back up, it indicates that the lawn is receiving the right amount of fertilizer. If it lays flat, it means the lawn has been over-fertilized.", "cot": "[\"The proper way to fertilize your grass involves several steps:\\n\\n1. **Timing**: Fertilize at the right time of year, specifically at the beginning of the growing season. This timing is crucial for different types of grasses. For example, warm season grasses should be fertilized when the grass begins to turn green at the beginning of spring.\\n\\n2. **Type of Grass**: Knowing the type of grass you have is essential because it determines the type of fertilizer needed and how often it should be applied.\\n\\n3. **Soil pH Test**: Conduct a pH soil test to measure the alkalinity or acidity of the soil. This test helps to determine the appropriate pH level for your fertilizer.\\n\\n4. **Lawn Measurement**: Measure your lawn to ensure you apply the correct amount of fertilizer.\\n\\n5. **Application**: Apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern. After applying, step on the turf to check if the leaf blade bounces back up. If it lays flat, you have over-fertilized.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that your grass receives the proper amount of fertilizer at the right time, promoting healthy growth.\", \"The proper way to fertilize your grass includes timing the fertilizer at the beginning of the growing season, knowing your grass type to determine the appropriate fertilizer type and frequency, conducting a pH soil test to match the fertilizer's pH to the soil's condition, and measuring the lawn size to apply the correct amount of fertilizer. Additionally, applying the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern and testing the turf by stepping on the leaf blade to ensure it bounces back to check for over-fertilization.\", \"The proper way to fertilize your grass, as stated in the provided passages, involves several key steps:\\n\\n1. **Timing the Fertilization**: You should fertilize at the right time of the year, specifically at the beginning of the growing season. This timing is crucial as it varies depending on the type of grass you have. For warm season grasses, fertilization should begin when the grass starts to turn green at the start of spring.\\n\\n2. **Knowing Your Grass Type**: Understanding the type of grass you have is essential because it determines the type of fertilizer needed and the frequency of application. This step is emphasized in both passage 1 and passage 2.\\n\\n3. **Conducting a Soil Test**: A pH soil test is necessary to measure the alkalinity or acidity of the soil. This information helps in determining the appropriate pH for the fertilizer you will use, ensuring it is effective for your grass type. This detail is mentioned in passage 2.\\n\\n4. **Measuring the Lawn**: Measuring the size of your lawn is important to determine the amount of fertilizer needed. This step is part of the process outlined in passage 1.\\n\\n5. **Applying the Fertilizer**: Once the correct type, amount, and timing are determined, the next step is to apply the fertilizer. This involves pouring in the rest of the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern over the lawn. After application, step on the turf to check if the leaf blade bounces back up, which indicates the lawn is in good shape. If it lays flat, it suggests that you have over-fertilized, which is detailed in passage 3.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that you fertilize your grass properly and effectively, promoting healthy growth and maintaining a lush lawn.\", \"The proper way to fertilize your grass involves several steps:\\n\\n1. Determine the right time of year to fertilize, which is typically at the beginning of the growing season for warm season grasses when the grass begins to turn green at the start of spring.\\n2. Choose the appropriate fertilizer based on the type of grass you have. Different types of grasses require different fertilizers.\\n3. Conduct a pH soil test to determine the soil's alkalinity or acidity, which helps in selecting the correct pH for your fertilizer.\\n4. Measure the size of your lawn to ensure you have the right amount of fertilizer.\\n5. Apply the fertilizer using a perpendicular pattern, and test the application by stepping on the turf. If the leaf blade bounces back up, it indicates that the lawn is receiving the right amount of fertilizer. If it lays flat, it means the lawn has been over-fertilized.\"]", "time_sec": 32.508, "generation_time_seconds": 31.8685, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6323, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 6169, 1616, 311, 35114, 551, 697, 16359, 17601, 3807, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 62805, 95518, 434, 85695, 551, 518, 279, 1290, 882, 315, 1042, 11, 11689, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 279, 7826, 3200, 13, 1096, 18405, 374, 16587, 369, 2155, 4494, 315, 16359, 288, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 8205, 3200, 16359, 288, 1265, 387, 35114, 1506, 979, 279, 16359, 12033, 311, 2484, 6176, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 10464, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 929, 315, 39946, 95518, 57633, 279, 943, 315, 16359, 498, 614, 374, 7565, 1576, 432, 26569, 279, 943, 315, 64291, 4362, 323, 1246, 3545, 432, 1265, 387, 9251, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 4416, 321, 36043, 3393, 95518, 49835, 264, 36043, 17171, 1273, 311, 6629, 279, 65687, 13489, 476, 96926, 315, 279, 17171, 13, 1096, 1273, 8609, 311, 8253, 279, 8311, 36043, 2188, 369, 697, 64291, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 43, 6379, 54240, 95518, 34104, 697, 36025, 311, 5978, 498, 3796, 279, 4396, 3311, 315, 64291, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 4988, 95518, 20552, 279, 64291, 304, 264, 76833, 5383, 13, 4636, 18950, 11, 3019, 389, 279, 58990, 311, 1779, 421, 279, 15933, 24838, 293, 29944, 1182, 705, 13, 1416, 432, 56522, 10063, 11, 498, 614, 916, 2220, 85695, 1506, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 5978, 429, 697, 16359, 21189, 279, 6169, 3311, 315, 64291, 518, 279, 1290, 882, 11, 22136, 9314, 6513, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can ensure that your grass receives the proper amount of fertilizer at the right time, promoting healthy growth.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1892672061971497, "g_worst_claim": 0.2570010634029613, "g_content": 1.6325452532087052, "g_traj_mean": 1.141851544380188}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6169, 1616, 311, 35114, 551, 697, 16359, 5646, 18405, 279, 64291, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 279, 7826, 3200, 11, 14063, 697, 16359, 943, 311, 8253, 279, 8311, 64291, 943, 323, 11639, 11, 30374, 264, 36043, 17171, 1273, 311, 2432, 279, 64291, 594, 36043, 311, 279, 17171, 594, 2971, 11, 323, 28990, 279, 36025, 1379, 311, 3796, 279, 4396, 3311, 315, 64291, 13, 22406, 11, 18950, 279, 64291, 304, 264, 76833, 5383, 323, 7497, 279, 58990, 553, 35467, 389, 279, 15933, 24838, 311, 5978, 432, 293, 29944, 1182, 311, 1779, 369, 916, 2220, 85695, 2022, 13, 151645], "pred": "The proper way to fertilize your grass includes timing the fertilizer at the beginning of the growing season, knowing your grass type to determine the appropriate fertilizer type and frequency, conducting a pH soil test to match the fertilizer's pH to the soil's condition, and measuring the lawn size to apply the correct amount of fertilizer. Additionally, applying the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern and testing the turf by stepping on the leaf blade to ensure it bounces back to check for over-fertilization.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3910453321576428, "g_worst_claim": 0.7216787338256836, "g_content": 2.2201836768617023, "g_traj_mean": 1.468601942062378}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6169, 1616, 311, 35114, 551, 697, 16359, 11, 438, 10982, 304, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 17601, 3807, 1376, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 62805, 279, 434, 85695, 2022, 95518, 1446, 1265, 35114, 551, 518, 279, 1290, 882, 315, 279, 1042, 11, 11689, 518, 279, 7167, 315, 279, 7826, 3200, 13, 1096, 18405, 374, 16587, 438, 432, 34227, 11649, 389, 279, 943, 315, 16359, 498, 614, 13, 1752, 8205, 3200, 16359, 288, 11, 35114, 2022, 1265, 3161, 979, 279, 16359, 8471, 311, 2484, 6176, 518, 279, 1191, 315, 10464, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 95521, 4615, 39946, 3990, 95518, 45451, 279, 943, 315, 16359, 498, 614, 374, 7565, 1576, 432, 26569, 279, 943, 315, 64291, 4362, 323, 279, 11639, 315, 3766, 13, 1096, 3019, 374, 45628, 304, 2176, 21085, 220, 16, 323, 21085, 220, 17, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 1109, 1058, 287, 264, 75519, 3393, 95518, 362, 36043, 17171, 1273, 374, 5871, 311, 6629, 279, 65687, 13489, 476, 96926, 315, 279, 17171, 13, 1096, 1995, 8609, 304, 25597, 279, 8311, 36043, 369, 279, 64291, 498, 686, 990, 11, 22573, 432, 374, 7373, 369, 697, 16359, 943, 13, 1096, 7716, 374, 9733, 304, 21085, 220, 17, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 7823, 68674, 279, 68392, 95518, 2157, 68674, 279, 1379, 315, 697, 36025, 374, 2989, 311, 8253, 279, 3311, 315, 64291, 4362, 13, 1096, 3019, 374, 949, 315, 279, 1882, 32640, 304, 21085, 220, 16, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 2164, 6711, 279, 434, 85695, 3135, 95518, 9646, 279, 4396, 943, 11, 3311, 11, 323, 18405, 525, 10838, 11, 279, 1790, 3019, 374, 311, 3796, 279, 64291, 13, 1096, 17601, 50413, 304, 279, 2732, 315, 279, 64291, 304, 264, 76833, 5383, 916, 279, 36025, 13, 4636, 3766, 11, 3019, 389, 279, 58990, 311, 1779, 421, 279, 15933, 24838, 293, 29944, 1182, 705, 11, 892, 14807, 279, 36025, 374, 304, 1661, 6083, 13, 1416, 432, 56522, 10063, 11, 432, 13230, 429, 498, 614, 916, 2220, 85695, 1506, 11, 892, 374, 11682, 304, 21085, 220, 18, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 5978, 429, 498, 35114, 551, 697, 16359, 10277, 323, 13444, 11, 22136, 9314, 6513, 323, 20337, 264, 57267, 36025, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can ensure that you fertilize your grass properly and effectively, promoting healthy growth and maintaining a lush lawn.", "groundin