{"id": "296", "question": "what are examples of potential and kinetic energy?", "gt": "Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane in flight, due to its large mass and fast velocity, and a baseball thrown by a pitcher, which can have a large amount of kinetic energy due to its fast velocity. Examples of potential energy include gravitational potential energy, which is the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, and elastic potential energy. Other activities like a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit also involve potential and kinetic energy.", "pred": "Examples of kinetic energy include a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, and a satellite in orbit. An example of potential energy is the energy stored in an object due to its vertical position or height.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Examples of kinetic energy include a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, and a satellite in orbit. An example of potential energy is the energy stored in an object due to its vertical position or height.", "cot": "[\"Examples of potential energy include the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, such as a ball on top of a hill. Examples of kinetic energy include the energy a body possesses by its motion, such as a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit.\", \"Examples of kinetic energy include a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, and a satellite in orbit. An example of potential energy is the energy stored in an object due to its vertical position or height.\", \"Potential energy examples include:\\n1. Gravitational potential energy: An object is stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height.\\nKinetic energy examples include:\\n1. An airplane in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity.\\n2. A baseball thrown by a pitcher, having a small mass and fast velocity.\", \"Examples of Potential Energy and Kinetic Energy: Potential energy includes the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, which is illustrated by the examples of a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, and a satellite in orbit. Kinetic energy, on the other hand, is the energy a body possesses by its motion. Examples of kinetic energy include the energy of an airplane in flight due to its fast velocity, the energy of a baseball thrown by a pitcher due to its fast velocity, and the energy of an object moving across a surface due to its motion.\"]", "time_sec": 15.245, "generation_time_seconds": 14.6891, "selection_time_seconds": 0.5486, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [40381, 315, 4650, 4802, 2924, 279, 4802, 9768, 304, 458, 1633, 438, 279, 1102, 315, 1181, 12140, 2309, 476, 2608, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 4935, 389, 1909, 315, 264, 23946, 13, 25311, 315, 70323, 4802, 2924, 279, 4802, 264, 2487, 49226, 553, 1181, 11379, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 1803, 7218, 11, 264, 4935, 20097, 11, 264, 14796, 35512, 11, 458, 33780, 4303, 11, 31227, 304, 458, 61368, 6118, 11, 323, 264, 23210, 304, 26507, 13, 151645], "pred": "Examples of potential energy include the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, such as a ball on top of a hill. Examples of kinetic energy include the energy a body possesses by its motion, such as a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5074428233520065, "g_worst_claim": 0.0585462212562561, "g_content": 1.620326668875558, "g_traj_mean": 1.306837558746338}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [40381, 315, 70323, 4802, 2924, 264, 1803, 7218, 11, 264, 4935, 20097, 11, 264, 14796, 35512, 11, 458, 33780, 4303, 11, 323, 264, 23210, 304, 26507, 13, 1527, 3110, 315, 4650, 4802, 374, 279, 4802, 9768, 304, 458, 1633, 4152, 311, 1181, 12140, 2309, 476, 2608, 13, 151645], "pred": "Examples of kinetic energy include a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, and a satellite in orbit. An example of potential energy is the energy stored in an object due to its vertical position or height.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5038536884166576, "g_worst_claim": 0.7442358732223511, "g_content": 1.7953960100809734, "g_traj_mean": 1.3400187492370605}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [95611, 4802, 10295, 2924, 510, 16, 13, 2825, 43110, 1663, 4650, 4802, 25, 1527, 1633, 374, 9768, 304, 458, 1633, 438, 279, 1102, 315, 1181, 12140, 2309, 476, 2608, 624, 67127, 5298, 4802, 10295, 2924, 510, 16, 13, 1527, 42924, 304, 10971, 4152, 311, 1181, 3460, 3072, 323, 4937, 15435, 624, 17, 13, 362, 19507, 14989, 553, 264, 40970, 11, 3432, 264, 2613, 3072, 323, 4937, 15435, 13, 151645], "pred": "Potential energy examples include:\n1. Gravitational potential energy: An object is stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height.\nKinetic energy examples include:\n1. An airplane in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity.\n2. A baseball thrown by a pitcher, having a small mass and fast velocity.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2763557757306063, "g_worst_claim": 0.8787201642990112, "g_content": 1.51948732648577, "g_traj_mean": 1.1195311546325684}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [40381, 315, 53957, 12354, 323, 30891, 5298, 12354, 25, 53957, 4802, 5646, 279, 4802, 9768, 304, 458, 1633, 438, 279, 1102, 315, 1181, 12140, 2309, 476, 2608, 11, 892, 374, 35662, 553, 279, 10295, 315, 264, 1803, 7218, 11, 264, 4935, 20097, 11, 264, 14796, 35512, 11, 458, 33780, 4303, 11, 323, 264, 23210, 304, 26507, 13, 30891, 5298, 4802, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 374, 279, 4802, 264, 2487, 49226, 553, 1181, 11379, 13, 25311, 315, 70323, 4802, 2924, 279, 4802, 315, 458, 42924, 304, 10971, 4152, 311, 1181, 4937, 15435, 11, 279, 4802, 315, 264, 19507, 14989, 553, 264, 40970, 4152, 311, 1181, 4937, 15435, 11, 323, 279, 4802, 315, 458, 1633, 7218, 3941, 264, 7329, 4152, 311, 1181, 11379, 13, 151645], "pred": "Examples of Potential Energy and Kinetic Energy: Potential energy includes the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, which is illustrated by the examples of a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, and a satellite in orbit. Kinetic energy, on the other hand, is the energy a body possesses by its motion. Examples of kinetic energy include the energy of an airplane in flight due to its fast velocity, the energy of a baseball thrown by a pitcher due to its fast velocity, and the energy of an object moving across a surface due to its motion.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2354416633639829, "g_worst_claim": 0.14830242097377777, "g_content": 1.7524740284886853, "g_traj_mean": 1.1133935451507568}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.93, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "297", "question": "what are examples of potential and kinetic energy?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, examples of potential energy include an object's gravitational potential energy due to its vertical position or height, and elastic potential energy stored in objects due to their deformation. Examples of kinetic energy include an airplane's kinetic energy in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity, a baseball's kinetic energy due to its fast velocity despite its small mass, and the kinetic energy possessed by objects in motion such as cars, balls, rivers, athletes, amusement park rides, and satellites in orbit.", "pred": "Examples of potential energy include the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, such as a ball on top of a hill. Examples of kinetic energy include the energy a body possesses by its motion, such as a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Examples of potential energy include the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, such as a ball on top of a hill. Examples of kinetic energy include the energy a body possesses by its motion, such as a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit.", "cot": "[\"Examples of potential energy include the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, such as a ball on top of a hill. Examples of kinetic energy include the energy a body possesses by its motion, such as a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit.\", \"Examples of potential energy include the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, such as the energy of a satellite in orbit. Examples of kinetic energy include the energy a body possesses by its motion, such as the energy of a car moving, a ball rolling, or a river flowing.\", \"Answer:The examples of potential energy include gravitational potential energy in an object due to its vertical position or height. An example of kinetic energy includes an airplane with a large amount of kinetic energy due to its large mass and fast velocity.\", \"Potential energy examples from the passages include:\\n1. Energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height.\\n2. Energy stored in any body.\\nKinetic energy examples from the passages include:\\n1. Energy a body possesses by its motion.\\n2. Energy due to an object's mass and velocity.\\nExamples of kinetic energy include:\\n1. An airplane in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity.\\n2. A baseball thrown by a pitcher due to its fast velocity.\\n3. A car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, a satellite in orbit.\"]", "time_sec": 14.828, "generation_time_seconds": 14.2083, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6129, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [40381, 315, 4650, 4802, 2924, 279, 4802, 9768, 304, 458, 1633, 438, 279, 1102, 315, 1181, 12140, 2309, 476, 2608, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 4935, 389, 1909, 315, 264, 23946, 13, 25311, 315, 70323, 4802, 2924, 279, 4802, 264, 2487, 49226, 553, 1181, 11379, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 1803, 7218, 11, 264, 4935, 20097, 11, 264, 14796, 35512, 11, 458, 33780, 4303, 11, 31227, 304, 458, 61368, 6118, 11, 323, 264, 23210, 304, 26507, 13, 151645], "pred": "Examples of potential energy include the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, such as a ball on top of a hill. Examples of kinetic energy include the energy a body possesses by its motion, such as a car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, rides in an amusement park, and a satellite in orbit.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5033048131793896, "g_worst_claim": 0.062125486135482785, "g_content": 1.5957705906459263, "g_traj_mean": 1.2885198593139648}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [40381, 315, 4650, 4802, 2924, 279, 4802, 9768, 304, 458, 1633, 438, 279, 1102, 315, 1181, 12140, 2309, 476, 2608, 11, 1741, 438, 279, 4802, 315, 264, 23210, 304, 26507, 13, 25311, 315, 70323, 4802, 2924, 279, 4802, 264, 2487, 49226, 553, 1181, 11379, 11, 1741, 438, 279, 4802, 315, 264, 1803, 7218, 11, 264, 4935, 20097, 11, 476, 264, 14796, 35512, 13, 151645], "pred": "Examples of potential energy include the energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height, such as the energy of a satellite in orbit. Examples of kinetic energy include the energy a body possesses by its motion, such as the energy of a car moving, a ball rolling, or a river flowing.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9859250655880679, "g_worst_claim": 0.7663920879364013, "g_content": 1.2652744424754176, "g_traj_mean": 1.0236858129501343}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 74045, 10295, 315, 4650, 4802, 2924, 69919, 4650, 4802, 304, 458, 1633, 4152, 311, 1181, 12140, 2309, 476, 2608, 13, 1527, 3110, 315, 70323, 4802, 5646, 458, 42924, 448, 264, 3460, 3311, 315, 70323, 4802, 4152, 311, 1181, 3460, 3072, 323, 4937, 15435, 13, 151645], "pred": "The examples of potential energy include gravitational potential energy in an object due to its vertical position or height. An example of kinetic energy includes an airplane with a large amount of kinetic energy due to its large mass and fast velocity.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2032462188175748, "g_worst_claim": 1.152945563906715, "g_content": 1.3498741432472512, "g_traj_mean": 1.175052523612976}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [95611, 4802, 10295, 504, 279, 46769, 2924, 510, 16, 13, 12354, 9768, 304, 458, 1633, 438, 279, 1102, 315, 1181, 12140, 2309, 476, 2608, 624, 17, 13, 12354, 9768, 304, 894, 2487, 624, 67127, 5298, 4802, 10295, 504, 279, 46769, 2924, 510, 16, 13, 12354, 264, 2487, 49226, 553, 1181, 11379, 624, 17, 13, 12354, 4152, 311, 458, 1633, 594, 3072, 323, 15435, 624, 40381, 315, 70323, 4802, 2924, 510, 16, 13, 1527, 42924, 304, 10971, 4152, 311, 1181, 3460, 3072, 323, 4937, 15435, 624, 17, 13, 362, 19507, 14989, 553, 264, 40970, 4152, 311, 1181, 4937, 15435, 624, 18, 13, 362, 1803, 7218, 11, 264, 4935, 20097, 11, 264, 14796, 35512, 11, 458, 33780, 4303, 11, 264, 23210, 304, 26507, 13, 151645], "pred": "Potential energy examples from the passages include:\n1. Energy stored in an object as the result of its vertical position or height.\n2. Energy stored in any body.\nKinetic energy examples from the passages include:\n1. Energy a body possesses by its motion.\n2. Energy due to an object's mass and velocity.\nExamples of kinetic energy include:\n1. An airplane in flight due to its large mass and fast velocity.\n2. A baseball thrown by a pitcher due to its fast velocity.\n3. A car moving, a ball rolling, a river flowing, an athlete running, a satellite in orbit.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6038445585902832, "g_worst_claim": 0.15132997930049896, "g_content": 1.4288480243985615, "g_traj_mean": 1.2591767311096191}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 42.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "298", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is needed. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot, ensuring hot water is always available. Alternatively, recirculating pumps can be used to rapidly pull hot water from a water heater, while simultaneously sending cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. These systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or a motion sensor. However, it should be noted that heat loss from the pipes can occur, requiring the water heater to use more fuel.", "pred": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. The pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. The pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "cot": "[\"To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\", \"When a homeowner turns on a faucet, the cooled water sitting in the pipes circulates to the faucet first, so the homeowner has to wait for hot water. A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\", \"to make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is installed. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, and it circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\", \"To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. The pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\"]", "time_sec": 14.356, "generation_time_seconds": 13.745, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6065, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 11, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 374, 1483, 13, 1096, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 304, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 576, 13834, 4225, 23156, 419, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13, 1096, 19259, 6337, 315, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 25351, 429, 4017, 3015, 374, 2677, 2500, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4316175438999348, "g_worst_claim": 0.7237024837070041, "g_content": 1.5466781415437396, "g_traj_mean": 1.4809303283691406}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, 