{"id": "300", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "To make a hot water heater circulate, one can install a recirculation system. The system consists of a pump that pulls hot water from the water heater and simultaneously sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. This ensures that hot water is always available without having to wait for it to circulate naturally. Recirculation systems can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.", "pred": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "cot": "[\"To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\", \"To make a hot water heater circulate, you can use a pump and a circulation system. A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\", \"Hot water heaters circulate hot water by using pumps to pull hot water from the water heater and simultaneously send cool water back to the water heater to be reheated and reused.\", \"Hot water heaters can be circulated by using circulating pumps. These pumps pull hot water from the water heater and simultaneously send cool water back to the hot water lines, where it is reheated and reused.\"]", "time_sec": 11.571, "generation_time_seconds": 10.6997, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8653, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 11, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 374, 1483, 13, 1096, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 304, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 576, 13834, 4225, 23156, 419, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13, 1096, 19259, 6337, 315, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 25351, 429, 4017, 3015, 374, 2677, 2500, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5016235314163509, "g_worst_claim": 0.9808194902208116, "g_content": 1.5233368120695416, "g_traj_mean": 1.5260664224624634}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 11, 498, 646, 990, 264, 13834, 323, 264, 34755, 1849, 13, 362, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 304, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 1096, 19259, 6337, 315, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 25351, 429, 4017, 3015, 374, 2677, 2500, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make a hot water heater circulate, you can use a pump and a circulation system. A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1313975695141503, "g_worst_claim": -0.027080824971199034, "g_content": 1.5547459125518799, "g_traj_mean": 1.335452914237976}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [20170, 3015, 81367, 4225, 6334, 4017, 3015, 553, 1667, 42775, 311, 6815, 4017, 3015, 504, 279, 3015, 42238, 323, 24303, 3624, 7010, 3015, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 311, 387, 47206, 657, 323, 68743, 13, 151645], "pred": "Hot water heaters circulate hot water by using pumps to pull hot water from the water heater and simultaneously send cool water back to the water heater to be reheated and reused.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4600298200334823, "g_worst_claim": 1.4600298200334823, "g_content": 1.9282168512759001, "g_traj_mean": 1.4105106592178345}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [20170, 3015, 81367, 646, 387, 62873, 553, 1667, 53728, 42775, 13, 4220, 42775, 6815, 4017, 3015, 504, 279, 3015, 42238, 323, 24303, 3624, 7010, 3015, 1182, 311, 279, 4017, 3015, 5128, 11, 1380, 432, 374, 47206, 657, 323, 68743, 13, 151645], "pred": "Hot water heaters can be circulated by using circulating pumps. These pumps pull hot water from the water heater and simultaneously send cool water back to the hot water lines, where it is reheated and reused.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.708895375718286, "g_worst_claim": 1.4789865667169744, "g_content": 2.29137388865153, "g_traj_mean": 1.6465842723846436}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.11, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "301", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how you can make a hot water heater circulate:\n\n1. Install a recirculating pump: As described in passage 3, a recirculating pump can rapidly pull hot water from the water heater and send cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused.\n2. Use a demand-based system: According to passage 3, demand systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor. This means that the pump will only run when there is a demand for hot water, rather than constantly running.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to make a hot water heater circulate, but rather describe the concept of circulation and the different types of systems used to achieve it.", "pred": "According to the passage, hot water heaters circulate by using a hot water circulation pump. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "According to the passage, hot water heaters circulate by using a hot water circulation pump. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "cot": "[\"To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\", \"Using a hot water circulation pump, a homeowner can make the water heater circulate. The pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line, ensuring that hot water is always available. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\", \"Answer: To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump continuously circulates this water through the water heater, ensuring that hot water is always available. Additionally, recirculating pumps rapidly pull hot water from the water heater and send cool water back to be reheated and reused, making the process more efficient and requiring less energy.\", \"Answer: According to the passage, hot water heaters circulate by using a hot water circulation pump. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\"]", "time_sec": 14.008, "generation_time_seconds": 13.5067, "selection_time_seconds": 0.4966, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 11, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 374, 1483, 13, 1096, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 304, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 576, 13834, 4225, 23156, 419, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13, 1096, 19259, 6337, 315, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 25351, 429, 4017, 3015, 374, 2677, 2500, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back 