{"id": "303", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"how to make hot water heater circulate\":\n\nA hot water circulation pump can be used to circulate water through the hot water heater and ensure that hot water is always available. The pump sends cooled water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line and circulates it through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. Additionally, demand systems can be controlled by the push of a button, a timer, or motion sensor to activate the pump and circulate the water.", "pred": "The hot water heater circulates using a pump. The pump circulates the water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot, ensuring that hot water is always available.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The hot water heater circulates using a pump. The pump circulates the water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot, ensuring that hot water is always available.", "cot": "[\"To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\", \"The hot water heater circulates using a pump. The pump circulates the water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot, ensuring that hot water is always available.\", \"Answer: A hot water circulation pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. A pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.\", \"The hot water heater circulates through a hot water circulation pump which sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. This pump ensures that hot water is always available by continuously circulating water through the water heater.\"]", "time_sec": 12.256, "generation_time_seconds": 11.4005, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8483, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 264, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 11, 264, 4017, 3015, 34755, 13834, 374, 1483, 13, 1096, 13834, 21308, 7010, 3015, 304, 279, 31175, 1182, 311, 279, 3015, 42238, 1526, 264, 470, 1555, 13, 576, 13834, 4225, 23156, 419, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 13, 1096, 19259, 6337, 315, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 25351, 429, 4017, 3015, 374, 2677, 2500, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make a hot water heater circulate, a hot water circulation pump is used. This pump sends cool water in the pipes back to the water heater through a return line. The pump circulates this water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot. This continuous loop of water through the water heater ensures that hot water is always available.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4208942690705941, "g_worst_claim": 0.890310181511773, "g_content": 1.49366589596397, "g_traj_mean": 1.4853074550628662}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 23156, 1667, 264, 13834, 13, 576, 13834, 4225, 23156, 279, 3015, 1526, 279, 3015, 42238, 438, 4362, 311, 2506, 432, 4017, 11, 22573, 429, 4017, 3015, 374, 2677, 2500, 13, 151645], "pred": "The hot water heater circulates using a pump. The pump circulates the water through the water heater as needed to keep it hot, ensuring that hot water is always available.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1772471252609702, "g_worst_claim": 0.9322224259376526, "g_content": 1.3355588411030017, "g_traj_mean": 1.212599754333496}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 362, 4017, 3015, 