{"id": "304", "question": "what causes watermelons to explode", "gt": "Watermelons can explode due to external pressure, such as when a bunch of rubber bands are placed around the middle of the watermelon, causing potential energy to build up and eventually cause the watermelon to explode. Another cause of watermelon explosions is the buildup of gas inside the watermelon due to rotting. This increases the internal pressure and when the skin of the watermelon can no longer hold the gas inside, it will explode.", "pred": "The process of rotting can cause watermelons to explode. As the watermelon rots, the gas inside it slowly increases, leading to an increase in pressure. When the pressure becomes too great for the watermelon's skin to hold, it will explode.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The process of rotting can cause watermelons to explode. As the watermelon rots, the gas inside it slowly increases, leading to an increase in pressure. When the pressure becomes too great for the watermelon's skin to hold, it will explode.", "cot": "[\"The watermelon explodes due to the build-up of gas inside it as it rots. This gas increases the pressure inside the watermelon, and when the skin of the watermelon is no longer strong enough to hold the gas inside, it will explode.\", \"The process of rotting can cause watermelons to explode. As the watermelon rots, the gas inside it slowly increases, leading to an increase in pressure. When the pressure becomes too great for the watermelon's skin to hold, it will explode.\", \"Answer: The watermelon explodes because the gas inside the watermelon builds up due to the rotting process. As the gas increases, the pressure inside the watermelon continues to rise. When the watermelon's skin can no longer withstand the pressure, it bursts, often spraying nearby surfaces with the contents of the watermelon.\", \"The watermelon explodes due to the pressure buildup from rotting inside. As the gas slowly increases due to the rotting, the pressure continues to increase. When the skin of the watermelon is no longer strong enough to hold the gas inside, it will explode, often spraying all nearby surfaces with rotten water melon.\"]", "time_sec": 12.122, "generation_time_seconds": 11.6251, "selection_time_seconds": 0.4901, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 3015, 71118, 93913, 4152, 311, 279, 1936, 5239, 315, 6819, 4766, 432, 438, 432, 926, 2576, 13, 1096, 6819, 12703, 279, 7262, 4766, 279, 3015, 71118, 11, 323, 979, 279, 6787, 315, 279, 3015, 71118, 374, 902, 5021, 3746, 3322, 311, 3331, 279, 6819, 4766, 11, 432, 686, 15758, 13, 151645], "pred": "The watermelon explodes due to the build-up of gas inside it as it rots. This gas increases the pressure inside the watermelon, and when the skin of the watermelon is no longer strong enough to hold the gas inside, it will explode.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9795091520275987, "g_worst_claim": 0.22423176765441893, "g_content": 1.8203379313151042, "g_traj_mean": 1.0546209812164307}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 1882, 315, 5749, 1280, 646, 5240, 3015, 27127, 2382, 311, 15758, 13, 1634, 279, 3015, 71118, 926, 2576, 11, 279, 6819, 4766, 432, 13970, 12703, 11, 6388, 311, 458, 5263, 304, 7262, 13, 3197, 279, 7262, 9044, 2238, 2244, 369, 279, 3015, 71118, 594, 6787, 311, 3331, 11, 432, 686, 15758, 13, 151645], "pred": "The process of rotting can cause watermelons to explode. As the watermelon rots, the gas inside it slowly increases, leading to an increase in pressure. When the pressure becomes too great for the watermelon's skin to hold, it will explode.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.903092660170335, "g_worst_claim": 0.3360854148864746, "g_content": 1.377577694979581, "g_traj_mean": 0.7949805855751038}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 576, 3015, 