{"id": "325", "question": "how well do patterned rollers work", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it appears that patterned rollers can work well for creating textured finishes on walls, as they can produce a random pattern of texture that is often desired in faux finishing techniques. The third passage provides instructions for creating a DIY texture roller by modifying an existing roller pad with rubber bands to create clumps and random patterns, which can be used to apply paint and create a textured finish.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"How well do patterned rollers work?\" is:\n\nThey can work well for creating textured finishes on walls, especially when used with faux finishing techniques.", "pred": "Based on the information provided, homemade texture or decorative paint rollers can work better than commercial ones for faux finishes that rely on applying a random pattern of texture to your walls. For example, a Basic Texture Roller creates a random pattern by stretching and twisting rubber bands around a 1-inch or thicker nap roller pad. This approach allows for more flexibility and creativity in applying the texture.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the information provided, homemade texture or decorative paint rollers can work better than commercial ones for faux finishes that rely on applying a random pattern of texture to your walls. For example, a Basic Texture Roller creates a random pattern by stretching and twisting rubber bands around a 1-inch or thicker nap roller pad. This approach allows for more flexibility and creativity in applying the texture.", "cot": "[\"Based on the information provided in the passages, patterned rollers, such as the homemade texture or decorative paint rollers, can work well for applying random patterns of texture to walls. However, the effectiveness of patterned rollers can vary depending on the specific type of roller and the texture being applied. For example, the Dermaroller mentioned in passage 2 seems to work better on certain areas of the face than on the neck and chest, and it is suggested that it works best when used with serums or moisturizers.\", \"Based on the information provided in the passage, patterned rollers can be effective for certain purposes. The passage mentions that homemade texture or decorative paint rollers can work better than commercial ones because they can apply a random pattern, which is useful for faux finishes. However, the specific effectiveness of patterned rollers is not clearly stated, and the focus is more on how homemade rollers can be beneficial. Therefore, the answer is: \\\"Unable to answer based on given passages.\\\"\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Based on the information provided, homemade texture or decorative paint rollers can work better than commercial ones for faux finishes that rely on applying a random pattern of texture to your walls. For example, a Basic Texture Roller creates a random pattern by stretching and twisting rubber bands around a 1-inch or thicker nap roller pad. This approach allows for more flexibility and creativity in applying the texture.\"]", "time_sec": 14.912, "generation_time_seconds": 14.0265, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8781, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 1995, 3897, 304, 279, 46769, 11, 5383, 291, 88613, 11, 1741, 438, 279, 35333, 10434, 476, 45436, 6177, 88613, 11, 646, 975, 1632, 369, 18950, 4194, 12624, 315, 10434, 311, 14285, 13, 4354, 11, 279, 26279, 315, 5383, 291, 88613, 646, 13289, 11649, 389, 279, 3151, 943, 315, 28451, 323, 279, 10434, 1660, 9251, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 75408, 277, 69396, 9733, 304, 21085, 220, 17, 4977, 311, 975, 2664, 389, 3654, 5671, 315, 279, 3579, 1091, 389, 279, 12975, 323, 15138, 11, 323, 432, 374, 11827, 429, 432, 4278, 1850, 979, 1483, 448, 1420, 6237, 476, 53802, 12230, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the information provided in the passages, patterned rollers, such as the homemade texture or decorative paint rollers, can work well for applying random patterns of texture to walls. However, the effectiveness of patterned rollers can vary depending on the specific type of roller and the texture being applied. For example, the Dermaroller mentioned in passage 2 seems to work better on certain areas of the face than on the neck and chest, and it is suggested that it works best when used with serums or moisturizers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6882075450814154, "g_worst_claim": 0.260809442271357, "g_content": 2.541689771286985, "g_traj_mean": 1.5341147184371948}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 1995, 3897, 304, 279, 21085, 11, 5383, 291, 88613, 646, 387, 7373, 369, 3654, 9895, 13, 576, 21085, 33845, 429, 35333, 10434, 476, 45436, 6177, 88613, 646, 975, 2664, 1091, 8353, 6174, 1576, 807, 646, 3796, 264, 4194, 5383, 11, 892, 374, 5390, 369, 50427, 33036, 13, 4354, 11, 279, 3151, 26279, 315, 5383, 291, 88613, 374, 537, 9355, 10982, 11, 323, 279, 5244, 374, 803, 389, 1246, 35333, 88613, 646, 387, 23699, 13, 15277, 11, 279, 4226, 374, 25, 330, 17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 1189, 151645], "pred": "\"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9449836170654654, "g_worst_claim": 0.10722405115763346, "g_content": 1.8794215809215198, "g_traj_mean": 1.092437744140625}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.17215359210968018, "g_worst_claim": -0.17215359210968018, "g_content": -0.26914846897125244, "g_traj_mean": -0.1530570536851883}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 1995, 3897, 11, 35333, 10434, 476, 45436, 6177, 88613, 646, 975, 2664, 1091, 8353, 6174, 369, 50427, 33036, 429, 17188, 389, 18950, 264, 4194, 5383, 315, 10434, 311, 697, 14285, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 264, 14625, 18757, 44542, 11450, 264, 4194, 5383, 553, 41849, 323, 79554, 22674, 20892, 2163, 264, 220, 16, 24241, 476, 58784, 25859, 28451, 11016, 13, 1096, 5486, 6147, 369, 803, 24177, 323, 27597, 304, 18950, 279, 10434, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the information provided, homemade texture or decorative paint rollers can work better than commercial ones for faux finishes that rely on applying a random pattern of texture to your walls. For example, a Basic Texture Roller creates a random pattern by stretching and twisting rubber bands around a 1-inch or thicker nap roller pad. This approach allows for more flexibility and creativity in applying the texture.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9551606109203437, "g_worst_claim": 0.4935587002680852, "g_content": 3.531818478606468, "g_traj_mean": 2.3921821117401123}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 30.25, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "329", "question": "how to boil potatoes for easy peeling", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how to boil potatoes for easy peeling:\n\nPassage 1 recommends boiling the potatoes until they are tender, then transferring them to an ice water bath to stop the cooking process. After cooling, the skin can be easily peeled off. This method takes 15 minutes to cook the potatoes and 5 seconds to peel each one.\n\nPassage 2 suggests peeling the potatoes before cooking, as their skin can be tough and papery. However, no specific instructions are provided for peeling.\n\nPassage 3 provides a step-by-step guide for peeling cooked potatoes. The method involves scoring the potatoes all the way around the center, boiling them for about 15 minutes, then placing them in an ice water bath to cool. Once cooled, the skin can be easily removed. This method takes about 30 minutes total time.\n\nTherefore, based on the provided passages, the best way to boil potatoes for easy peeling is to boil them until tender, then transfer them to an ice water bath to stop the cooking process and make the skin easier to remove. Scoring the potatoes before boiling can also help loosen the skin for easier peeling.", "pred": "Step 1.) Bring a pot of water to a boil.\nStep 2.) With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\nStep 3.) Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\nStep 4.) Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\nStep 5.) Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\nStep 6.) Remove your potatoe from the water and remove the skin.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Step 1.) Bring a pot of water to a boil.\nStep 2.) With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\nStep 3.) Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\nStep 4.) Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\nStep 5.) Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\nStep 6.) Remove your potatoe from the water and remove the skin.", "cot": "[\"To boil potatoes for easy peeling, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\\n2. With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\\n6. Remove your potatoe from the water and remove the skin.\", \"To boil potatoes for easy peeling, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\\n2. With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\\n6. Remove your potatoe from the water and remove the skin.\\n\\nThis method helps the potatoes cool down quickly, making the skin easier to peel.\", \"Step 1.) Bring a pot of water to a boil.\\nStep 2.) With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\\nStep 3.) Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\\nStep 4.) Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\\nStep 5.) Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\\nStep 6.) Remove your potatoe from the water and remove the skin.\", \"To boil potatoes for easy peeling, follow these steps:\\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\\n2. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\\n3. Place the scored potatoes in the boiling water and cook for about 15 minutes.\\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water.\\n5. Once the potatoes are cooked, transfer them to the ice water.\\n6. After a few seconds, the potatoes should be cool enough to handle. Remove the skin.\"]", "time_sec": 19.772, "generation_time_seconds": 18.9082, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8565, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 43690, 34167, 369, 4135, 1051, 20058, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 39124, 264, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 17, 13, 3085, 264, 21430, 11, 5456, 697, 34167, 678, 279, 1616, 2163, 279, 4126, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3338, 323, 43690, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 476, 773, 624, 19, 13, 31166, 264, 19212, 315, 9853, 3015, 323, 1992, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3015, 624, 20, 13, 4492, 812, 432, 2163, 369, 264, 2421, 6486, 1101, 3322, 773, 429, 432, 748, 7010, 3322, 311, 3705, 624, 21, 13, 10783, 697, 38734, 68, 504, 279, 3015, 323, 4057, 279, 6787, 13, 151645], "pred": "To boil potatoes for easy peeling, follow these steps:\n\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\n2. With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\n6. Remove your potatoe from the water and remove the skin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5734092896947494, "g_worst_claim": 0.16766762733459473, "g_content": 1.5840994652281417, "g_traj_mean": 1.6203830242156982}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 43690, 34167, 369, 4135, 1051, 20058, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 39124, 264, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 17, 13, 3085, 264, 21430, 11, 5456, 697, 34167, 678, 279, 1616, 2163, 279, 4126, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3338, 323, 43690, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 476, 773, 624, 19, 13, 31166, 264, 19212, 315, 9853, 3015, 323, 1992, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3015, 624, 20, 13, 4492, 812, 432, 2163, 369, 264, 2421, 6486, 1101, 3322, 773, 429, 432, 748, 7010, 3322, 311, 3705, 624, 21, 13, 10783, 697, 38734, 68, 504, 279, 3015, 323, 4057, 279, 6787, 382, 1986, 1714, 8609, 279, 34167, 7010, 1495, 6157, 11, 3259, 279, 6787, 8661, 311, 57112, 13, 151645], "pred": "This method helps the potatoes cool down quickly, making the skin easier to peel.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.346234428394991, "g_worst_claim": 0.16766762733459473, "g_content": 1.4052351542881556, "g_traj_mean": 1.4545046091079712}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 6138, 39124, 264, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 8304, 220, 17, 6138, 3085, 264, 21430, 11, 5456, 697, 34167, 678, 279, 1616, 2163, 279, 4126, 624, 8304, 220, 18, 6138, 10771, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3338, 323, 43690, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 476, 773, 624, 8304, 220, 19, 6138, 31166, 264, 19212, 315, 9853, 3015, 323, 1992, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3015, 624, 8304, 220, 20, 6138, 4492, 812, 432, 2163, 369, 264, 2421, 6486, 1101, 3322, 773, 429, 432, 748, 7010, 3322, 311, 3705, 624, 8304, 220, 21, 6138, 10783, 697, 38734, 68, 504, 279, 3015, 323, 4057, 279, 6787, 13, 151645], "pred": "Step 1.) Bring a pot of water to a boil.\nStep 2.) With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\nStep 3.) Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\nStep 4.) Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\nStep 5.) Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\nStep 6.) Remove your potatoe from the water and remove the skin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7440293845372676, "g_worst_claim": 0.94725341796875, "g_content": 1.8059018723508145, "g_traj_mean": 1.6463611125946045}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 43690, 34167, 369, 4135, 1051, 20058, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 39124, 264, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 17, 13, 18115, 279, 34167, 678, 279, 1616, 2163, 279, 4126, 448, 264, 21430, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 16548, 34167, 304, 279, 49837, 3015, 323, 4296, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 31166, 264, 19212, 315, 9853, 3015, 624, 20, 13, 9646, 279, 34167, 525, 29105, 11, 8317, 1105, 311, 279, 9853, 3015, 624, 21, 13, 4636, 264, 2421, 6486, 11, 279, 34167, 1265, 387, 7010, 3322, 311, 3705, 13, 10783, 279, 6787, 13, 151645], "pred": "To boil potatoes for easy peeling, follow these steps:\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\n2. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n3. Place the scored potatoes in the boiling water and cook for about 15 minutes.\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water.\n5. Once the potatoes are cooked, transfer them to the ice water.\n6. After a few seconds, the potatoes should be cool enough to handle. Remove the skin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8293643607033623, "g_worst_claim": -0.19408535957336426, "g_content": 1.027813769401388, "g_traj_mean": 0.77370685338974}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 23.71, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "331", "question": "how to boil potatoes for easy peeling", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to boil potatoes for easy peeling:\n\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\n2. Score your potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\n6. Remove your potato from the water and remove the skin.\n\nThe ice water bath helps to stop the cooking process and cool down the potatoes quickly, making the skin easier to peel off.", "pred": "To boil potatoes for easy peeling, bring a pot of water to a boil, score your potatoes all the way around the center, place them in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place the potatoes in the water, then remove them and peel the skin easily.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To boil potatoes for easy peeling, bring a pot of water to a boil, score your potatoes all the way around the center, place them in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place the potatoes in the water, then remove them and peel the skin easily.", "cot": "[\"To boil potatoes for easy peeling, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\\n2. With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\\n6. Remove your potatoe from the water and remove the skin.\", \"Answer:[Bring a pot of water to a boil. Score your potatoes all the way around the center. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle. Remove your potatoe from the water and remove the skin.]\", \"Answer: To boil potatoes for easy peeling, bring a pot of water to a boil, score your potatoes all the way around the center, place them in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place the potatoes in the water, then remove them and peel the skin easily.\", \"Boil until tender, then transfer to an ice water bath. When cool, peel off skin.\"]", "time_sec": 14.051, "generation_time_seconds": 13.428, "selection_time_seconds": 0.616, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 43690, 34167, 369, 4135, 1051, 20058, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 39124, 264, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 17, 13, 3085, 264, 21430, 11, 5456, 697, 34167, 678, 279, 1616, 2163, 279, 4126, 624, 18, 13, 10771, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3338, 323, 43690, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 476, 773, 624, 19, 13, 31166, 264, 19212, 315, 9853, 3015, 323, 1992, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3015, 624, 20, 13, 4492, 812, 432, 2163, 369, 264, 2421, 6486, 1101, 3322, 773, 429, 432, 748, 7010, 3322, 311, 3705, 624, 21, 13, 10783, 697, 38734, 68, 504, 279, 3015, 323, 4057, 279, 6787, 13, 151645], "pred": "To boil potatoes for easy peeling, follow these steps:\n\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\n2. With a knife, score your potatoes all the way around the center.\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\n6. Remove your potatoe from the water and remove the skin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5887851760300815, "g_worst_claim": 0.2094065546989441, "g_content": 1.5612268650785406, "g_traj_mean": 1.6140011548995972}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 7259, 64527, 264, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 13, 18115, 697, 34167, 678, 279, 1616, 2163, 279, 4126, 13, 10771, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3338, 323, 43690, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 476, 773, 13, 31166, 264, 19212, 315, 9853, 3015, 323, 1992, 697, 34167, 304, 279, 3015, 13, 4492, 812, 432, 2163, 369, 264, 2421, 6486, 1101, 3322, 773, 429, 432, 748, 7010, 3322, 311, 3705, 13, 10783, 697, 38734, 68, 504, 279, 3015, 323, 4057, 279, 6787, 24719, 151645], "pred": "[Bring a pot of water to a boil. Score your potatoes all the way around the center. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle. Remove your potatoe from the water and remove the skin.]", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1241580800250177, "g_worst_claim": 1.2510041629566866, "g_content": 2.442777797154018, "g_traj_mean": 2.05141544342041}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 2014, 43690, 34167, 369, 4135, 1051, 20058, 11, 4446, 264, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 11, 5456, 697, 34167, 678, 279, 1616, 2163, 279, 4126, 11, 1992, 1105, 304, 279, 3338, 323, 43690, 369, 911, 220, 16, 20, 4420, 13, 31166, 264, 19212, 315, 9853, 3015, 323, 1992, 279, 34167, 304, 279, 3015, 11, 1221, 4057, 1105, 323, 57112, 279, 6787, 6707, 13, 151645], "pred": "To boil potatoes for easy peeling, bring a pot of water to a boil, score your potatoes all the way around the center, place them in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place the potatoes in the water, then remove them and peel the skin easily.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2090095274662844, "g_worst_claim": 0.18484588464101157, "g_content": 1.5629051208496094, "g_traj_mean": 1.2099529504776}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1233, 321, 3080, 27582, 11, 1221, 8317, 311, 458, 9853, 3015, 8885, 13, 3197, 7010, 11, 57112, 1007, 6787, 13, 151645], "pred": "Boil until tender, then transfer to an ice water bath. When cool, peel off skin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.6584391117095945, "g_worst_claim": 1.7054994106292725, "g_content": 2.766776614718967, "g_traj_mean": 2.298166275024414}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 56.07, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "332", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, first, check common tick hiding places such as inside and behind the dog's ears and around the eyes. Once you locate a tick, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the tick's head where it attaches to the skin. If you plan to use your fingers, wear gloves. Pull on the tick gently and steadily to avoid leaving part of the tick's mouth behind, which can cause an infection. Regular use of tick control products can also prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation. Flea and tick shampoos can kill the ticks that are already on your pet.", "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can follow these steps: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If the tick is difficult to remove, it may be best to take the dog to the veterinarian for professional removal.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can follow these steps: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If the tick is difficult to remove, it may be best to take the dog to the veterinarian for professional removal.", "cot": "[\"To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can use tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. These products are designed to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Additionally, you should regularly check your dog's body, especially in areas like inside and behind the ears, and around the eyes, where ticks often hide. If you find a tick, use tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull it off gently and steadily. Wearing gloves during the removal process can help prevent the spread of any diseases the tick may carry.\", \"To get rid of ticks from dogs, you should check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, as these are favorite tick hiding places. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily to avoid causing an infection if the tick's mouth is left behind.\\n\\nAdditionally, the best way to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog is by using tick control products regularly. Consult your veterinarian to choose the most suitable product for your dog and your situation. Your veterinarian can also provide information on common diseases in your area that can pose a risk to your dog.\", \"To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can follow these steps: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If the tick is difficult to remove, it may be best to take the dog to the veterinarian for professional removal.\", \"To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can remove them by using tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, pulling on the tick gently and steadily. It is also recommended to use tick control products regularly, as advised by a veterinarian.\"]", "time_sec": 18.202, "generation_time_seconds": 17.5115, "selection_time_seconds": 0.685, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 646, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 11102, 553, 697, 81240, 13, 4220, 3871, 525, 6188, 311, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 13, 22406, 11, 498, 1265, 15502, 1779, 697, 5562, 594, 2487, 11, 5310, 304, 5671, 1075, 4766, 323, 4815, 279, 24230, 11, 323, 2163, 279, 6414, 11, 1380, 29957, 3545, 10265, 13, 1416, 498, 1477, 264, 9341, 11, 990, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 323, 6815, 432, 1007, 29273, 323, 41971, 13, 467, 13678, 35416, 2337, 279, 16652, 1882, 646, 1492, 5358, 279, 8865, 315, 894, 18808, 279, 9341, 1231, 6777, 13, 151645], "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can use tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. These products are designed to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Additionally, you should regularly check your dog's body, especially in areas like inside and behind the ears, and around the eyes, where ticks often hide. If you find a tick, use tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull it off gently and steadily. Wearing gloves during the removal process can help prevent the spread of any diseases the tick may carry.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8436890561450057, "g_worst_claim": 0.08634178837140401, "g_content": 0.8671485612977226, "g_traj_mean": 0.792936384677887}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 1265, 1779, 4766, 323, 4815, 279, 5562, 594, 24230, 323, 2163, 1181, 6414, 11, 438, 1493, 525, 6930, 9341, 25037, 7482, 13, 5443, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 13, 41062, 35416, 421, 498, 3119, 311, 990, 697, 19225, 311, 4057, 279, 9341, 13, 31828, 389, 279, 9341, 29273, 323, 41971, 311, 5648, 14381, 458, 18873, 421, 279, 9341, 594, 10780, 374, 2115, 4815, 382, 49574, 11, 279, 1850, 1616, 311, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 374, 553, 1667, 9341, 2524, 3871, 15502, 13, 19960, 697, 81240, 311, 5157, 279, 1429, 14452, 1985, 369, 697, 5562, 323, 697, 6534, 13, 4615, 81240, 646, 1083, 3410, 1995, 389, 4185, 18808, 304, 697, 3082, 429, 646, 17040, 264, 5214, 311, 697, 5562, 13, 151645], "pred": "Additionally, the best way to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog is by using tick control products regularly. Consult your veterinarian to choose the most suitable product for your dog and your situation. Your veterinarian can also provide information on common diseases in your area that can pose a risk to your dog.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4405556556409, "g_worst_claim": 0.8221697807312012, "g_content": 1.757049560546875, "g_traj_mean": 1.407961130142212}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 25, 5443, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 13, 41062, 35416, 421, 498, 3119, 311, 990, 697, 19225, 311, 4057, 279, 9341, 13, 31828, 389, 279, 9341, 29273, 323, 41971, 13, 1416, 279, 9341, 374, 5000, 311, 4057, 11, 432, 1231, 387, 1850, 311, 1896, 279, 5562, 311, 279, 81240, 369, 6584, 16652, 13, 151645], "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can follow these steps: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If the tick is difficult to remove, it may be best to take the dog to the veterinarian for professional removal.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0150236743099896, "g_worst_claim": 0.009991556406021118, "g_content": 1.4187525068010602, "g_traj_mean": 1.0360517501831055}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 646, 4057, 1105, 553, 1667, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 11, 22266, 389, 279, 9341, 29273, 323, 41971, 13, 1084, 374, 1083, 11102, 311, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 15502, 11, 438, 25104, 553, 264, 81240, 13, 151645], "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can remove them by using tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, pulling on the tick gently and steadily. It is also recommended to use tick control products regularly, as advised by a veterinarian.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3238065414906175, "g_worst_claim": 0.8327773550282354, "g_content": 1.372607707977295, "g_traj_mean": 1.1736048460006714}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.2, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "334", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, follow these steps: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If you yank the tick away from your dog too quickly, you’ll leave part of the tick’s mouth behind, which can cause an infection. The best way to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog is by using tick control products regularly. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation. Your veterinarian is also aware of diseases that are common in your area and can pose a risk to your dog.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, follow these steps: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If you yank the tick away from your dog too quickly, you’ll leave part of the tick’s mouth behind, which can cause an infection. The best way to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog is by using tick control products regularly. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation. Your veterinarian is also aware of diseases that are common in your area and can pose a risk to your dog.", "cot": "[\"To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can use tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. These products are designed to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Additionally, you should regularly check your dog's body, especially in areas like inside and behind the ears, and around the eyes, where ticks often hide. If you find a tick, use tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull it off gently and steadily. Wearing gloves during the removal process can help prevent the spread of any diseases the tick may carry.\", \"To get rid of ticks from dogs, follow these steps: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If you yank the tick away from your dog too quickly, you’ll leave part of the tick’s mouth behind, which can cause an infection. The best way to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog is by using tick control products regularly. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation. Your veterinarian is also aware of diseases that are common in your area and can pose a risk to your dog.\", \"Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Pull on the tick gently and steadily.\", \"To get rid of ticks from dogs, use tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. The best products can be used regularly to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Additionally, check inside and behind the ears and around the eyes, as these are favorite hiding places for ticks. Remove ticks by using tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and gently pull it away.\"]", "time_sec": 17.853, "generation_time_seconds": 16.807, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0399, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 646, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 11102, 553, 697, 81240, 13, 4220, 3871, 525, 6188, 311, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 13, 22406, 11, 498, 1265, 15502, 1779, 697, 5562, 594, 2487, 11, 5310, 304, 5671, 1075, 4766, 323, 4815, 279, 24230, 11, 323, 2163, 279, 6414, 11, 1380, 29957, 3545, 10265, 13, 1416, 498, 1477, 264, 9341, 11, 990, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 4