tick gently and steadily. If you yank the tick away from your dog too quickly, you’ll leave part of the tick’s mouth behind, which can cause an infection. The best way to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog is by using tick control products regularly. Your veterinarian can advise you about the best product for your dog and your situation. Your veterinarian is also aware of diseases that are common in your area and can pose a risk to your dog.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4700383263667143, "g_worst_claim": 0.47580329577128094, "g_content": 1.964019283171623, "g_traj_mean": 1.5489556789398193}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [10253, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 13, 31828, 389, 279, 9341, 29273, 323, 41971, 13, 151645], "pred": "Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Pull on the tick gently and steadily.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.610871366092137, "g_worst_claim": 1.5096771717071533, "g_content": 2.5944841702779136, "g_traj_mean": 1.645039677619934}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 11102, 553, 697, 81240, 13, 576, 1850, 3871, 646, 387, 1483, 15502, 311, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 13, 22406, 11, 1779, 4766, 323, 4815, 279, 24230, 323, 2163, 279, 6414, 11, 438, 1493, 525, 6930, 25037, 7482, 369, 29957, 13, 10783, 29957, 553, 1667, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 323, 29273, 6815, 432, 3123, 13, 151645], "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, use tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. The best products can be used regularly to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Additionally, check inside and behind the ears and around the eyes, as these are favorite hiding places for ticks. Remove ticks by using tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and gently pull it away.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0681326917433671, "g_worst_claim": 0.666623408977802, "g_content": 1.156340901444598, "g_traj_mean": 0.9895622730255127}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "335", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how to get rid of ticks from dogs:\n\n1. Check inside and behind the dog's ears and around its eyes, which are common hiding places for ticks. (Passage 1)\n2. Use tick control products recommended by a veterinarian to prevent ticks from attaching to the dog. (Passage 2)\n3. Remove ticks from the dog using a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. (Passage 1)\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages whether there are any specific products or methods for getting rid of ticks from dogs that are already infested.", "pred": "Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily.", "cot": "[\"To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can use tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. These products are designed to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Additionally, you should regularly check your dog's body, especially in areas like inside and behind the ears, and around the eyes, where ticks often hide. If you find a tick, use tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull it off gently and steadily. Wearing gloves during the removal process can help prevent the spread of any diseases the tick may carry.\", \"Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily.\", \"To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can use tick control products recommended by a veterinarian. The best way to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog is by using these products regularly. If you need to remove a tick, follow the steps: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.\", \"To get rid of ticks from dogs, it is recommended to use tick control products, which can be advised by a veterinarian. This is the best way to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Additionally, regularly checking inside and behind the ears and around the eyes is crucial as these are favorite tick hiding places. To remove a tick, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and gently pull it away. It is also recommended to wear gloves when removing ticks to prevent skin contact.\"]", "time_sec": 17.603, "generation_time_seconds": 16.6595, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9364, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 646, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 11102, 553, 697, 81240, 13, 4220, 3871, 525, 6188, 311, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 13, 22406, 11, 498, 1265, 15502, 1779, 697, 5562, 594, 2487, 11, 5310, 304, 5671, 1075, 4766, 323, 4815, 279, 24230, 11, 323, 2163, 279, 6414, 11, 1380, 29957, 3545, 10265, 13, 1416, 498, 1477, 264, 9341, 11, 990, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 323, 6815, 432, 1007, 29273, 323, 41971, 13, 467, 13678, 35416, 2337, 279, 16652, 1882, 646, 1492, 5358, 279, 8865, 315, 894, 18808, 279, 9341, 1231, 6777, 13, 151645], "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can use tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. These products are designed to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Additionally, you should regularly check your dog's body, especially in areas like inside and behind the ears, and around the eyes, where ticks often hide. If you find a tick, use tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull it off gently and steadily. Wearing gloves during the removal process can help prevent the spread of any diseases the tick may carry.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8552876543673602, "g_worst_claim": 0.09828373789787292, "g_content": 0.8787145794562574, "g_traj_mean": 0.8065956234931946}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [10253, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 13, 41062, 35416, 421, 498, 3119, 311, 990, 697, 19225, 311, 4057, 279, 9341, 13, 31828, 389, 279, 9341, 29273, 323, 41971, 13, 151645], "pred": "Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.661583932619246, "g_worst_claim": 1.5704447031021118, "g_content": 2.508332704242907, "g_traj_mean": 1.6740145683288574}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 646, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 11102, 553, 264, 81240, 13, 576, 1850, 1616, 311, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 374, 553, 1667, 1493, 3871, 15502, 13, 1416, 498, 1184, 311, 4057, 264, 9341, 11, 1795, 279, 7354, 25, 5443, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 13, 31828, 389, 279, 9341, 29273, 323, 41971, 13, 41062, 35416, 421, 498, 3119, 311, 990, 697, 19225, 311, 4057, 279, 9341, 13, 151645], "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can use tick control products recommended by a veterinarian. The best way to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog is by using these products regularly. If you need to remove a tick, follow the steps: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1145111475706444, "g_worst_claim": 0.6772270202636719, "g_content": 1.2242136223371638, "g_traj_mean": 1.1196130514144897}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 432, 374, 11102, 311, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 11, 892, 646, 387, 25104, 553, 264, 81240, 13, 1096, 374, 279, 1850, 1616, 311, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 13, 22406, 11, 15502, 13295, 4766, 323, 4815, 279, 24230, 323, 2163, 279, 6414, 374, 16587, 438, 1493, 525, 6930, 9341, 25037, 7482, 13, 2014, 4057, 264, 9341, 11, 990, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 323, 29273, 6815, 432, 3123, 13, 1084, 374, 1083, 11102, 311, 9850, 35416, 979, 17592, 29957, 311, 5358, 6787, 3645, 13, 151645], "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, it is recommended to use tick control products, which can be advised by a veterinarian. This is the best way to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Additionally, regularly checking inside and behind the ears and around the eyes is crucial as these are favorite tick hiding places. To remove a tick, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and gently pull it away. It is also recommended to wear gloves when removing ticks to prevent skin contact.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0324725948328322, "g_worst_claim": 0.54074584113227, "g_content": 1.2530641742781097, "g_traj_mean": 1.0068256855010986}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 23.4, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "337", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to get rid of ticks from dogs:\n\n1. Check your dog's body thoroughly, especially in areas like inside and behind the ears, around the eyes, and other favorite tick hiding places.\n2. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and wear gloves if needed.\n3. Pull on the tick gently and steadily, making sure not to yank it away from your dog too quickly.\n4. Regularly use tick control products on your dog, as recommended by your veterinarian, to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog in the first place.\n\nIf you have any further questions or concerns, consult your veterinarian for advice.", "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, you should follow specific steps: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If you yank the tick away from your dog too quickly, you’ll leave part of the tick’s mouth behind, which can cause an infection. Additionally, the best way to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog is by the regular use of tick control products.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, you should follow specific steps: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If you yank the tick away from your dog too quickly, you’ll leave part of the tick’s mouth behind, which can cause an infection. Additionally, the best way to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog is by the regular use of tick control products.", "cot": "[\"To get rid of ticks from dogs, you can use tick control products recommended by your veterinarian. These products are designed to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog. Additionally, you should regularly check your dog's body, especially in areas like inside and behind the ears, and around the eyes, where ticks often hide. If you find a tick, use tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull it off gently and steadily. Wearing gloves during the removal process can help prevent the spread of any diseases the tick may carry.\", \"To prevent ticks from attaching to your dog, it is best to use tick control products regularly. You should consult your veterinarian for advice about the most appropriate product for your dog and your specific situation.\", \"To get rid of ticks from dogs, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull on the tick gently and steadily. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.\", \"Answer: To get rid of ticks from dogs, you should follow specific steps: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If you yank the tick away from your dog too quickly, you’ll leave part of the tick’s mouth behind, which can cause an infection. Additionally, the best way to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog is by the regular use of tick control products.\"]", "time_sec": 15.167, "generation_time_seconds": 14.3564, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8015, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 646, 990, 9341, 2524, 3871, 11102, 553, 697, 81240, 13, 4220, 3871, 525, 6188, 311, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 13, 22406, 11, 498, 1265, 15502, 1779, 697, 5562, 594, 2487, 11, 5310, 304, 5671, 1075, 4766, 323, 4815, 279, 24230, 11, 323, 2163, 279, 6414, 11, 1380, 29957, 3545, 10265, 13, 1416, 498, 1477, 264, 9341, 11, 990, 