645], "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin and pull on the tick gently and steadily. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4732972639926354, "g_worst_claim": 1.3047993100922683, "g_content": 1.6525431093962297, "g_traj_mean": 1.4378241300582886}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 2014, 633, 9279, 315, 29957, 504, 12590, 11, 498, 1265, 1795, 3151, 7354, 25, 5443, 264, 6716, 315, 14545, 10125, 388, 311, 33377, 279, 1968, 315, 279, 9341, 1380, 432, 84503, 311, 279, 6787, 13, 41062, 35416, 421, 498, 3119, 311, 990, 697, 19225, 311, 4057, 279, 9341, 13, 31828, 389, 279, 9341, 29273, 323, 41971, 13, 1416, 498, 379, 1180, 279, 9341, 3123, 504, 697, 5562, 2238, 6157, 11, 498, 4700, 5274, 949, 315, 279, 9341, 748, 10780, 4815, 11, 892, 646, 5240, 458, 18873, 13, 22406, 11, 279, 1850, 1616, 311, 5358, 29957, 504, 71808, 311, 697, 5562, 374, 553, 279, 5792, 990, 315, 9341, 2524, 3871, 13, 151645], "pred": "To get rid of ticks from dogs, you should follow specific steps: Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin. Wear gloves if you plan to use your fingers to remove the tick. Pull on the tick gently and steadily. If you yank the tick away from your dog too quickly, you’ll leave part of the tick’s mouth behind, which can cause an infection. Additionally, the best way to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog is by the regular use of tick control products.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4167680494589991, "g_worst_claim": 0.4902377128601074, "g_content": 1.4938206481933594, "g_traj_mean": 1.4151784181594849}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 54.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "338", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "To make ribs, start by removing the membrane from the bottom of the ribs with a knife. Place the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover them. Afterwards, line a baking pan with heavy duty foil. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer for heat circulation on all sides. Mix mustard and liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to make sure it adheres to the meat. To grill the ribs, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium and remove the ribs from the foil. Place them meaty-side up on the grill and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook for another 5 minutes. Continue this process until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through with grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "pred": "By following these detailed steps, you can prepare ribs using both grilling and oven-cooking techniques.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "By following these detailed steps, you can prepare ribs using both grilling and oven-cooking techniques.", "cot": "[\"To make ribs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Grill Method:**\\n   - **Preparation:** Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - **Cooking:** Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. **Oven Method:**\\n   - **Preparation:** Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece. Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover. Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\\n   - **Cooking:** Season the ribs by mixing the mustard and the liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides. Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat. Bake the ribs in the oven until they are cooked through.\\n\\nThese methods provide a detailed guide on how to prepare ribs using both grilling and oven-cooking techniques.\", \"To make ribs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. If using a grill, preheat it to medium temperature. Place the ribs meaty-side up on the grill and brush them with some sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes, then flip and cook for another 5 minutes. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the ribs are heated through, have grill marks, and the sauce has thickened. This will take a total of 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. If using an oven, remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start pulling it off near the narrow end. Place the ribs in a resealable bag and add enough BBQ sauce to cover them. Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil, overlapping it to form a tent.\\n\\n3. Season the ribs by mixing mustard and liquid smoke if using, and brushing the ribs on both sides. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to ensure the rub adheres to the rib meat. \\n\\nBy following these detailed steps, you can prepare ribs using both grilling and oven-cooking techniques.\", \"There are several ways to make ribs, including grilling and oven-cooking. One way to grill ribs is to heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F), remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes, flip and brush the ribs, and cook another 5 minutes. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce thickens and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks. Another way to make ribs is to lay the ribs on top of a rack in a single layer, season them with dry rub, and cook them in the oven.\", \"To make ribs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece.\\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\\n3. Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\\n4. Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n5. Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce.\\n6. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes.\\n7. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\\n8. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer. This arrangement allows for heat circulations on all sides of the ribs.\\n9. Season the ribs: Mix the mustard and the liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides. Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\\n\\nAnswer: [Follow the steps above to make ribs]\"]", "time_sec": 36.533, "generation_time_seconds": 35.3758, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1472, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 55149, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 6464, 483, 6730, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 3070, 4703, 35135, 66963, 26070, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 256, 481, 3070, 58382, 287, 66963, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 11, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 323, 15625, 1105, 448, 1045, 315, 279, 19187, 13, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 429