175, 6193, 11, 3200, 1105, 448, 9058, 10273, 11, 323, 4296, 1105, 304, 279, 23387, 13, 151645], "pred": "There are several ways to make ribs, including grilling and oven-cooking. One way to grill ribs is to heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F), remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes, flip and brush the ribs, and cook another 5 minutes. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce thickens and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks. Another way to make ribs is to lay the ribs on top of a rack in a single layer, season them with dry rub, and cook them in the oven.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2534339655265605, "g_worst_claim": 0.5470801762172154, "g_content": 1.6615070104599, "g_traj_mean": 1.2251458168029785}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 55149, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 13, 5443, 264, 21430, 311, 1191, 432, 3143, 279, 15026, 835, 11, 323, 6815, 1007, 304, 825, 6573, 624, 17, 13, 10224, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 13, 2691, 14016, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 624, 18, 13, 7083, 279, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 14189, 46399, 13, 5443, 11260, 315, 49817, 46399, 311, 1281, 264, 15632, 624, 19, 13, 26070, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 20, 13, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 11, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 323, 15625, 1105, 448, 1045, 315, 279, 19187, 624, 21, 13, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 40284, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 323, 4296, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 22, 13, 15003, 311, 4296, 11, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 11, 3080, 279, 19187, 702, 12045, 6758, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 11, 369, 264, 2790, 1081, 9400, 882, 315, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 43924, 279, 55149, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 29659, 304, 264, 3175, 6193, 13, 1096, 26112, 6147, 369, 8628, 4225, 7455, 389, 678, 11067, 315, 279, 55149, 624, 24, 13, 14263, 279, 55149, 25, 19219, 279, 64307, 323, 279, 14473, 16205, 11, 421, 1667, 11, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 389, 2176, 11067, 13, 15515, 35144, 279, 55149, 448, 279, 9058, 10273, 323, 3272, 29273, 311, 1281, 2704, 279, 10273, 34951, 288, 311, 279, 20131, 13041, 382, 16141, 25, 508, 12480, 279, 7354, 3403, 311, 1281, 55149, 60, 151645], "pred": "Follow the steps above to make ribs", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7752636496008456, "g_worst_claim": 0.251403550306956, "g_content": 2.2103323529857075, "g_traj_mean": 1.6348704099655151}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.36, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "339", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "To make ribs, start by removing the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Then, brush both sides of the ribs with a mixture of mustard and liquid smoke. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to ensure it sticks to the meat. Next, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium and place the ribs on the grill, meaty-side up. Brush the ribs with sauce, cover the grill, and cook for 5 minutes. Flip the ribs, brush with more sauce, and cook for another 5 minutes. Repeat this process, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce thickens and the ribs are heated through with grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "pred": "Both methods require specific instructions and steps to properly prepare the ribs. The choice between grilling and oven-cooking depends on personal preference and desired cooking method.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Both methods require specific instructions and steps to properly prepare the ribs. The choice between grilling and oven-cooking depends on personal preference and desired cooking method.", "cot": "[\"To make ribs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Grill Method:**\\n   - **Preparation:** Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - **Cooking:** Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. **Oven Method:**\\n   - **Preparation:** Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece. Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover. Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\\n   - **Cooking:** Season the ribs by mixing the mustard and the liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides. Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat. Bake the ribs in the oven until they are cooked through.\\n\\nThese methods provide a detailed guide on how to prepare ribs using both grilling and oven-cooking techniques.\", \"There are two main methods to make ribs: grilling and oven-cooking.\\n\\nGrilling ribs:\\n\\n1. Heat the grill to medium temperature (350°F to 450°F).\\n2. Place the ribs on the grill, meaty-side up.\\n3. Brush the ribs with some sauce.\\n4. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes.\\n5. Flip the ribs and brush them again.\\n6. Repeat steps 4 and 5 every 5 minutes until the ribs are heated through, have grill marks, and the sauce has thickened, which takes a total of 20 minutes.\\n\\nOven-cooking ribs:\\n\\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\\n2. Season the ribs by mixing mustard, liquid smoke (if using), and dry rub. Brush the ribs on both sides and pat gently to ensure the rub adheres to the meat.\\n3. Place the ribs in a resealable bag and cover them with BBQ sauce.\\n4. Line a baking pan with heavy-duty foil, overlapping the foil to create a tent.\\n\\nBoth methods require specific instructions and steps to properly prepare the ribs. The choice between grilling and oven-cooking depends on personal preference and desired cooking method.\", \"To make ribs, you can use one of two methods: grilling or oven-cooking.\\n\\n**Grilling:**\\n1. Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n2. Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce.\\n3. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes.\\n4. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\\n\\n**Oven-cooking:**\\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece.\\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\\n3. Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\\n\\nAdditionally, for oven-cooking, you can season the ribs by mixing mustard and liquid smoke if using, and brushing the ribs on both sides. Then, sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\", \"To make ribs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Preparation**: Prepare the ribs by removing the membrane from the bottom. This membrane can be tough and is best removed before cooking. Use a knife to start at the narrow end and pull it off in one piece.\\n\\n2. **Seasoning**: Place the ribs in a resealable bag and add enough BBQ sauce to cover them completely. This step helps infuse the ribs with flavor as they cook.\\n\\n3. **Cooking**: Line a baking pan with heavy-duty foil, overlapping it to create a tent. This setup helps to trap the moisture and keeps the ribs tender and juicy during cooking.\\n\\nFollow these steps to ensure your ribs are well-prepared and flavorful.\"]", "time_sec": 35.74, "generation_time_seconds": 35.0634, "selection_time_seconds": 0.67, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 55149, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 6464, 483, 6730, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 3070, 4703, 35135, 66963, 26070, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 256, 481, 3070, 58382, 287, 66963, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 11, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 323, 15625, 1105, 448, 1045, 315, 279, 19187, 13, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 