1449, 220, 20, 4420, 11, 3080, 279, 19187, 702, 12045, 6758, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 11, 369, 264, 2790, 1081, 9400, 882, 315, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 382, 334, 46, 1037, 22471, 10746, 25, 1019, 16, 13, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 13, 5443, 264, 21430, 311, 1191, 432, 3143, 279, 15026, 835, 11, 323, 6815, 1007, 304, 825, 6573, 624, 17, 13, 10224, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 13, 2691, 14016, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 624, 18, 13, 7083, 279, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 14189, 46399, 13, 5443, 11260, 315, 49817, 46399, 311, 1281, 264, 15632, 382, 49574, 11, 369, 23387, 22471, 10746, 11, 498, 646, 3200, 279, 55149, 553, 26792, 64307, 323, 14473, 16205, 421, 1667, 11, 323, 76726, 279, 55149, 389, 2176, 11067, 13, 5005, 11, 84847, 279, 55149, 448, 264, 9058, 10273, 323, 3272, 29273, 311, 1281, 2704, 279, 10273, 34951, 288, 311, 279, 20131, 13041, 13, 151645], "pred": "Additionally, for oven-cooking, you can season the ribs by mixing mustard and liquid smoke if using, and brushing the ribs on both sides. Then, sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8519502365040947, "g_worst_claim": 0.6341872811317444, "g_content": 2.3005281645676185, "g_traj_mean": 1.6375176906585693}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 55149, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 4703, 35135, 95518, 31166, 279, 55149, 553, 17592, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 13, 1096, 38554, 646, 387, 11045, 323, 374, 1850, 6963, 1573, 17233, 13, 5443, 264, 21430, 311, 1191, 518, 279, 15026, 835, 323, 6815, 432, 1007, 304, 825, 6573, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 34860, 287, 95518, 10771, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 323, 912, 3322, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 1105, 6587, 13, 1096, 3019, 8609, 4132, 810, 279, 55149, 448, 17172, 438, 807, 4296, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 58382, 287, 95518, 7083, 264, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 54518, 46399, 11, 49817, 432, 311, 1855, 264, 15632, 13, 1096, 6505, 8609, 311, 22862, 279, 31157, 323, 13598, 279, 55149, 27582, 323, 55053, 2337, 17233, 382, 12480, 1493, 7354, 311, 5978, 697, 55149, 525, 1632, 21334, 7212, 323, 93531, 13, 151645], "pred": "Follow these steps to ensure your ribs are well-prepared and flavorful.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9142263181386017, "g_worst_claim": -0.28085068861643475, "g_content": 1.1930696857509329, "g_traj_mean": 0.8425655961036682}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 4.49, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "340", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make ribs:\n\nTo grill the ribs:\n\n1. Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium temperature (350°F to 450°F).\n2. Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce.\n3. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes.\n4. Flip and brush the ribs and cook for another 5 minutes.\n5. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\n\nTo prepare the ribs before grilling:\n\n1. Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer.\n2. Season the ribs by mixing the mustard and liquid smoke (if using), and brushing the ribs on both sides.\n3. Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\n\nFor oven-cooked BBQ ribs:\n\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs.\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag.\n3. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover the ribs.\n4. Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil.\n5. Place the ribs in the baking pan and bake at 350°F for 2-3 hours, or until the ribs are tender and the meat starts to pull away from the bone.", "pred": "These steps provide a comprehensive method for preparing both grilled and oven-cooked ribs, using the information derived from the given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "These steps provide a comprehensive method for preparing both grilled and oven-cooked ribs, using the information derived from the given passages.", "cot": "[\"To make ribs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Grill Method:**\\n   - **Preparation:** Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - **Cooking:** Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. **Oven Method:**\\n   - **Preparation:** Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece. Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover. Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\\n   - **Cooking:** Season the ribs by mixing the mustard and the liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides. Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat. Bake the ribs in the oven until they are cooked through.\\n\\nThese methods provide a detailed guide on how to prepare ribs using both grilling and oven-cooking techniques.\", \"Based on the provided passages, here is how to make ribs:\\n\\n1. **Preparation**: \\n   - **Grilled Ribs (Passage 1)**: For grilled ribs, first preheat the grill to medium heat (350°F to 450°F). Remove the ribs from their foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened, the ribs are heated through, and have grill marks. This process takes a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\\n   - **Oven-cooked Ribs (Passage 3)**: For oven-cooked ribs, remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs and place them in a resealable bag with sufficient BBQ sauce to cover. Line a baking pan with heavy-duty foil, overlapping it to make a tent.\\n\\n2. **Seasoning and Cooking**:\\n   - **Grilled Ribs**: After grilling, season the ribs by mixing mustard and liquid smoke (if using) and brush the ribs on both sides. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and gently pat to ensure the rub adheres well to the rib meat.\\n   - **Oven-cooked Ribs**: After preparing the ribs in the bag, place them in the oven and cook until the ribs are tender. The exact cooking time will depend on the oven's temperature and the desired level of doneness, but it is generally recommended to cook at 350°F until the ribs are tender.\\n\\nThese steps provide a comprehensive method for preparing both grilled and oven-cooked ribs, using the information derived from the given passages.\", \"To make ribs, first lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer. Season them by mixing mustard and liquid smoke, if using, and brushing the ribs on both sides. Then sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to ensure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\", \"To make ribs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece.\\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\\n3. Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\\n4. To grill the ribs, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F). Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\"]", "time_sec": 35.035, "generation_time_seconds": 34.2686, "selection_time_seconds": 0.761, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 55149, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 6464, 483, 6730, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 3070, 4703, 35135, 66963, 26070, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 256, 481, 3070, 58382, 287, 66963, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 11, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 323, 15625, 1105, 448, 1045, 315, 279, 19187, 13, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 40284, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 323, 4296, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 15003, 311, 4296, 11, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 11, 3080, 279, 19187, 702, 12045, 6758, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 11, 369, 264, 2790, 1081, 9400, 882, 315, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 46, 1037, 6730, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 3070, 4703, 35135, 66963, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 13, 5443, 264, 21430, 311, 1191, 432, 3143, 279, 15026, 835, 11, 323, 6815, 1007, 304, 825, 6573, 13, 10224, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 13, 2691, 14016, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 13, 7083, 279, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 14189, 46399, 13, 5443, 11260, 315, 49817, 46399, 311, 1281, 264, 15632, 624, 256, 481, 3070, 58382, 287, 66963, 14263, 279, 55149, 553, 26792, 279, 64307, 323, 279, 14473, 16205, 11, 421, 1667, 11, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 389, 2176, 11067, 13, 15515, 35144, 279, 55149, 448, 279, 9058, 10273, 323, 3272, 29273, 311, 1281, 2704, 279, 10273, 34951, 288, 311, 279, 20131, 13041, 13, 52074, 279, 55149, 304, 279, 23387, 3080, 807, 525, 29105, 1526, 382, 9485, 5413, 3410, 264, 11682, 8474, 389, 1246, 311, 10549, 55149, 1667, 2176, 1081, 9400, 323, 23387, 22471, 10746, 12538, 13, 151645], "pred": "These methods provide a detailed guide on how to prepare ribs using both grilling and oven-cooking techniques.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6920492944173506, "g_worst_claim": 0.24364366134007773, "g_content": 2.3322308252728177, "g_traj_mean": 1.5317904949188232}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 1588, 374, 1246, 311, 1281, 55149, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 4703, 35135, 95518, 715, 256, 481, 3070, 6464, 4374, 431, 54