ve method for preparing both grilled and oven-cooked ribs, using the information derived from the given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.13469556165794, "g_worst_claim": -0.04191205236646864, "g_content": 1.5001992003558433, "g_traj_mean": 1.006439208984375}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 55149, 11, 1156, 10962, 279, 55149, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 29659, 304, 264, 3175, 6193, 13, 14263, 1105, 553, 26792, 64307, 323, 14473, 16205, 11, 421, 1667, 11, 323, 76726, 279, 55149, 389, 2176, 11067, 13, 5005, 84847, 279, 55149, 448, 264, 9058, 10273, 323, 3272, 29273, 311, 5978, 279, 10273, 34951, 288, 311, 279, 20131, 13041, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make ribs, first lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer. Season them by mixing mustard and liquid smoke, if using, and brushing the ribs on both sides. Then sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to ensure the rub adheres to the rib meat.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8305382127197618, "g_worst_claim": 1.123328685760498, "g_content": 2.3403772814520476, "g_traj_mean": 1.8132487535476685}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 55149, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 13, 5443, 264, 21430, 311, 1191, 432, 3143, 279, 15026, 835, 11, 323, 6815, 1007, 304, 825, 6573, 624, 17, 13, 10224, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 13, 2691, 14016, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 624, 18, 13, 7083, 279, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 14189, 46399, 13, 5443, 11260, 315, 49817, 46399, 311, 1281, 264, 15632, 624, 19, 13, 2014, 39058, 279, 55149, 11, 8628, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 568, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 11, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 323, 15625, 1105, 448, 1045, 315, 279, 19187, 13, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 40284, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 323, 4296, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 15003, 311, 4296, 11, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 11, 3080, 279, 19187, 702, 12045, 6758, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 11, 369, 264, 2790, 1081, 9400, 882, 315, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece.\n2. Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover.\n3. Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\n4. To grill the ribs, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F). Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.722002247490034, "g_worst_claim": 0.2515660524368286, "g_content": 2.190557370240661, "g_traj_mean": 1.619020700454712}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 6.17, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "341", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can make ribs:\n\nStep 1: Prepare the ribs\n\n* Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs (passage 3)\n* Season the ribs with a dry rub and mustard mixture (passage 2)\n\nStep 2: Grill the ribs\n\n* Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium heat (passage 1)\n* Place the ribs meaty-side up on the grill and brush with some of the sauce (passage 1)\n* Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes, then flip and brush the ribs with more sauce (passage 1)\n* Continue to cook and flip every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through (passage 1)\n\nTotal grilling time: 20 minutes\n\nNote: The passages do not mention the temperature at which to cook the ribs, but a medium heat of 350°F to 450°F is suggested.", "pred": "To make ribs, you can grill them by heating the grill to medium, placing the ribs meaty-side up, brushing with sauce, and flipping every 5 minutes until they're heated through and have grill marks. You can also cook them in the oven by removing the membrane, covering them with BBQ sauce, lining the pan with foil, and creating a tent. Alternatively, you can season the ribs by laying them in a single layer, brushing with mustard and liquid smoke, and sprinkling with a dry rub.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To make ribs, you can grill them by heating the grill to medium, placing the ribs meaty-side up, brushing with sauce, and flipping every 5 minutes until they're heated through and have grill marks. You can also cook them in the oven by removing the membrane, covering them with BBQ sauce, lining the pan with foil, and creating a tent. Alternatively, you can season the ribs by laying them in a single layer, brushing with mustard and liquid smoke, and sprinkling with a dry rub.", "cot": "[\"To make ribs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Grill Method:**\\n   - **Preparation:** Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - **Cooking:** Remove the ribs from the foil, place them meaty-side up on the grill, and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes. Flip and brush the ribs and cook another 5 minutes. Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. **Oven Method:**\\n   - **Preparation:** Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece. Put the ribs in a resealable bag. Add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover. Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil. Use plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\\n   - **Cooking:** Season the ribs by mixing the mustard and the liquid smoke, if using, and brush the ribs on both sides. Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to make sure the rub adheres to the rib meat. Bake the ribs in the oven until they are cooked through.\\n\\nThese methods provide a detailed guide on how to prepare ribs using both grilling and oven-cooking techniques.\", \"To make ribs, first, remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece. Next, put the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover. After that, line the baking pan with heavy duty foil, using plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.\", \"To make ribs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Grill method** (from passage 1):\\n   - Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium (350°F to 450°F).\\n   - Place the ribs meaty-side up on the grill.\\n   - Brush them with sauce and cover the grill for 5 minutes.\\n   - Flip and brush again, then cook for another 5 minutes.\\n   - Continue to cook, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through and have grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\\n\\n2. **Oven method** (from passage 3):\\n   - **Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs**.\\n   - **Put the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover**.\\n   - **Line the baking pan with heavy duty foil** and make sure it overlaps enough to create a tent.\\n\\n3. **Seasoning method** (from passage 2):\\n   - Lay the ribs on top of the rack in a single layer.\\n   - Season the ribs: Mix the mustard and the liquid smoke if using, and brush the ribs on both sides.\\n   - Sprinkle the ribs with the dry rub and pat gently to ensure the rub adheres to the rib meat.\\n\\nAnswer: To make ribs, you can grill them by heating the grill to medium, placing the ribs meaty-side up, brushing with sauce, and flipping every 5 minutes until they're heated through and have grill marks. You can also cook them in the oven by removing the membrane, covering them with BBQ sauce, lining the pan with foil, and creating a tent. Alternatively, you can season the ribs by laying them in a single layer, brushing with mustard and liquid smoke, and sprinkling with a dry rub.\", \"Answer: To make ribs, first preheat the grill to medium (350°F to 450°F). Place the ribs meaty-side up on the grill and brush them with some of the sauce. Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes, flip, brush again, and cook another 5 minutes. Repeat these steps every 5 minutes until the sauce has thickened, and the ribs have grill marks, making a total grilling time of 20 minutes.\\n\\nAnother method is to lay the ribs on top of a rack in a single layer to allow heat circulation on all sides. Season the ribs by mixing mustard and liquid smoke if using, and brush the ribs on both sides. Then, sprinkle the ribs with dry rub and pat gently to ensure the rub adheres.\\n\\nFor oven-cooked BBQ ribs, remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs and put them in a resealable bag with sufficient BBQ sauce to cover. Line the baking pan with heavy-duty foil and make a tent with plenty of overlapping foil.\"]", "time_sec": 35.736, "generation_time_seconds": 34.7456, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9842, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 55149, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 6464, 483, 6730, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 3070, 4703, 35135, 66963, 26070, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 256, 481, 3070, 58382, 287, 66963, 10783, 279, 55149, 504, 279, 46399, 11, 1992, 1105, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 11, 323, 15625, 1105, 448, 1045, 315, 279, 19187, 13, 17757, 279, 39058, 323, 4296, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 40284, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 323, 4296, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 13, 15003, 311, 4296, 11, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 11, 3080, 279, 19187, 702, 12045, 6758, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 11, 369, 264, 2790, 1081, 9400, 882, 315, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 46, 1037, 6730, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 3070, 4703, 35135, 66963, 10783, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 13, 5443, 264, 21430, 311, 1191, 432, 3143, 279, 15026, 835, 11, 323, 6815, 1007, 304, 825, 6573, 13, 10224, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 13, 2691, 14016, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 13, 7083, 279, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 14189, 46399, 13, 5443, 11260, 315, 49817, 46399, 311, 1281, 264, 15632, 624, 256, 481, 3070, 58382, 287, 66963, 14263, 279, 55149, 553, 26792, 279, 64307, 323, 279, 14473, 16205, 11, 421, 1667, 11, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 389, 2176, 11067, 13, 15515, 35144, 279, 55149, 448, 279, 9058, 10273, 323, 3272, 29273, 311, 1281, 2704, 279, 10273, 34951, 288, 311, 279, 20131, 13041, 13, 52074, 279, 55149, 304, 279, 23387, 3080, 807, 525, 29105, 1526, 382, 9485, 5413, 3410, 264, 11682, 8474, 389, 1246, 311, 10549, 55149, 1667, 2176, 1081, 9400, 323, 23387, 22471, 10746, 12538, 13, 151645], "pred": "These methods provide a detailed guide on how to prepare ribs using both grilling and oven-cooking techniques.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7008381745470325, "g_worst_claim": 0.2402175466219584, "g_content": 2.345701913984995, "g_traj_mean": 1.5376416444778442}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 55149, 11, 1156, 11, 4057, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 13, 5443, 264, 21430, 311, 1191, 432, 3143, 279, 15026, 835, 11, 323, 6815, 1007, 304, 825, 6573, 13, 9295, 11, 2182, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 323, 912, 14016, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 13, 4636, 429, 11, 1555, 279, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 14189, 46399, 11, 1667, 11260, 315, 49817, 46399, 311, 1281, 264, 15632, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make ribs, first, remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Use a knife to start it near the narrow end, and pull off in one piece. Next, put the ribs in a resealable bag and add sufficient BBQ sauce to cover. After that, line the baking pan with heavy duty foil, using plenty of overlapping foil to make a tent.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.2094660922242944, "g_worst_claim": 1.0844844818115233, "g_content": 2.974310591414168, "g_traj_mean": 2.291508913040161}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 55149, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 6464, 483, 1714, 334, 320, 1499, 21085, 220, 16, 982, 256, 481, 26070, 264, 6819, 476, 60103, 39058, 311, 11051, 320, 18, 20, 15, 58472, 311, 220, 19, 20, 15, 58472, 4292, 256, 481, 10771, 279, 55149, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 389, 279, 39058, 624, 256, 481, 32988, 1105, 448, 19187, 323, 3421, 279, 39058, 369, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 256, 481, 40284, 323, 15625, 1549, 11, 1221, 4296, 369, 2441, 220, 20, 4420, 624, 256, 481, 15003, 311, 4296, 11, 64661, 323, 76726, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 11, 3080, 279, 19187, 702, 12045, 6758, 323, 279, 55149, 525, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 11, 369, 264, 2790, 1081, 9400, 882, 315, 220, 17, 15, 4420, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 46, 1037, 1714, 334, 320, 1499, 21085, 220, 18, 982, 256, 481, 3070, 13021, 279, 38554, 504, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 55149, 334, 624, 256, 481, 3070, 19103, 279, 55149, 304, 264, 312, 325, 278, 480, 8968, 323, 912, 14016, 45277, 19187, 311, 3421, 334, 624, 256, 481, 3070, 2460, 279, 27815, 7215, 448, 8811, 14189, 46399, 334, 323, 1281, 2704, 432, 76007, 3322, 311, 1855, 264, 15632, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 34860, 287, 1714, 334, 320, 1499, 21085, 220, 17, 982, 256, 481, 43924, 279, 55149, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 29659, 304, 264, 3175, 6193, 624, 256, 481, 14263, 279, 55149, 25, 19219, 279, 64307, 323, 279, 14473, 16205, 421, 1667, 11, 323, 15625, 279, 55149, 389, 2176, 11067, 624, 256, 481, 15515, 35144, 279, 55149, 448, 279, 9058, 10273, 323, 3272, 29273, 311, 5978, 279, 10273, 34951, 288, 311, 279, 20131, 13041, 382, 16141, 25, 2014, 1281, 55149, 11, 498, 646, 39058, 1105, 553, 23579, 279, 39058, 311, 11051, 11, 24047, 279, 55149, 13041, 88, 24067, 705, 11, 76726, 448, 19187, 11, 323, 64661, 1449, 220, 20, 4420, 3080, 807, 2299, 31713, 1526, 323, 614, 39058, 15423, 13, 1446, 646, 1083, 4296, 1105, 304, 279, 23387, 553, 17592, 279, 38554, 11, 18202, 1105, 448, 45277, 19187, 11, 35371, 279, 7215, 448, 46399, 11, 323, 6825, 264, 15632, 13, 38478, 11, 498, 646, 3200, 279, 55149, 553, 34644, 1105, 304, 264, 3175, 6193, 11, 76726, 448, 64307, 323, 14473, 16205, 11, 323, 50698, 2718, 448, 264, 9058, 10273, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make ribs, you can grill them by heating the grill to medium, placing the ribs meaty-side up, brushing with sauce, and flipping every 5 minutes until they're heated through and have grill marks. You can also cook them in the oven by removing the membrane, covering them with BBQ sauce, lining the pan with foil, and creating a tent. Alternatively, you can season the ribs by laying them in a single layer, brushing with mustard and liquid smoke, and sprinkling with a dry rub.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9079736565970653, "g_worst_claim": -0.17535182145925668, "g_c