{"Token-F1": 32.89, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "342", "question": "when you have a bowel movement do you lose weight", "gt": "While you may technically lose a small amount of weight after a bowel movement, this does not come from a loss of body fat. The decrease in body weight does not come from fat loss in stools, but rather from the elimination of undigested food and waste. Weight loss is primarily tied to your caloric intake and expenditure, not bowel movements. Unless your scale is highly accurate, you're unlikely to notice a difference in your body weight before and after a bowel movement.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages", "cot": "[\"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages\", \"No, you do not lose weight when you have a bowel movement.\", \"Based on the information provided in the passages, having a bowel movement does not cause a significant loss of weight. The weight loss is a result of creating a calorie deficit, which forces the body to burn stored fat for energy. The feces do not contribute to the loss of body weight because the fat found in feces comes from dietary fat intake that is not properly absorbed due to possible malabsorption conditions. Therefore, the weight loss is not attributed to the bowel movement itself but rather to the overall caloric intake and expenditure.\"]", "time_sec": 9.917, "generation_time_seconds": 9.2379, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6688, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.14315165579319, "g_worst_claim": -0.14315165579319, "g_content": -0.22648971080780028, "g_traj_mean": -0.1271870732307434}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.16178066389901297, "g_worst_claim": -0.16178066389901297, "g_content": -0.22648971080780028, "g_traj_mean": -0.1119016706943512}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [2753, 11, 498, 653, 537, 9052, 4680, 979, 498, 614, 264, 65258, 7203, 13, 151645], "pred": "No, you do not lose weight when you have a bowel movement.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.35048443930489676, "g_worst_claim": 0.35048443930489676, "g_content": -0.0029506157152354717, "g_traj_mean": 0.345619261264801}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 1995, 3897, 304, 279, 46769, 11, 3432, 264, 65258, 7203, 1558, 537, 5240, 264, 5089, 4709, 315, 4680, 13, 576, 4680, 4709, 374, 264, 1102, 315, 6825, 264, 51603, 28187, 11, 892, 8437, 279, 2487, 311, 8231, 9768, 8664, 369, 4802, 13, 576, 53961, 288, 653, 537, 16792, 311, 279, 4709, 315, 2487, 4680, 1576, 279, 8664, 1730, 304, 53961, 288, 4041, 504, 33525, 8664, 22881, 429, 374, 537, 10277, 41001, 4152, 311, 3204, 8641, 3435, 65081, 4682, 13, 15277, 11, 279, 4680, 4709, 374, 537, 29606, 311, 279, 65258, 7203, 5086, 714, 4751, 311, 279, 8084, 1620, 26359, 22881, 323, 44326, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the information provided in the passages, having a bowel movement does not cause a significant loss of weight. The weight loss is a result of creating a calorie deficit, which forces the body to burn stored fat for energy. The feces do not contribute to the loss of body weight because the fat found in feces comes from dietary fat intake that is not properly absorbed due to possible malabsorption conditions. Therefore, the weight loss is not attributed to the bowel movement itself but rather to the overall caloric intake and expenditure.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7891959279344408, "g_worst_claim": 0.24468262990315756, "g_content": 1.293905141402264, "g_traj_mean": 0.8256321549415588}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "343", "question": "when you have a bowel movement do you lose weight", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that having a bowel movement does not result in weight loss. Weight loss is primarily determined by caloric intake and expenditure, not by bowel movements.", "pred": "Based on the provided passages:\n\nWhen you have a bowel movement, you do not lose weight. The weight change is minimal and not significant due to the scale's inaccuracy, and the body fat loss is not directly related to a bowel movement. Instead, weight loss occurs when there is a calorie deficit, meaning the body burns more calories than it consumes, leading to the utilization of stored body fat for energy.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the provided passages:\n\nWhen you have a bowel movement, you do not lose weight. The weight change is minimal and not significant due to the scale's inaccuracy, and the body fat loss is not directly related to a bowel movement. Instead, weight loss occurs when there is a calorie deficit, meaning the body burns more calories than it consumes, leading to the utilization of stored body fat for energy.", "cot": "[\"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"No, you do not lose weight when you have a bowel movement. The weight you lose after having a bowel movement is not due to a loss of body fat in your stools. Instead, it is due to the weight of the food and drink you have consumed throughout the day, which your body uses for energy. Your caloric intake and expenditure, rather than your bowel movements, are tied to healthy weight loss.\", \"No, you do not lose weight when you have a bowel movement.\", \"Based on the provided passages:\\n\\nWhen you have a bowel movement, you do not lose weight. The weight change is minimal and not significant due to the scale's inaccuracy, and the body fat loss is not directly related to a bowel movement. Instead, weight loss occurs when there is a calorie deficit, meaning the body burns more calories than it consumes, leading to the utilization of stored body fat for energy.\"]", "time_sec": 12.127, "generation_time_seconds": 11.2797, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8425, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.1481694132089615, "g_worst_claim": -0.1481694132089615, "g_content": -0.23183789253234863, "g_traj_mean": -0.13161666691303253}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [2753, 11, 498, 653, 537, 9052, 4680, 979, 498, 614, 264, 65258, 7203, 13, 576, 4680, 498, 9052, 1283, 3432, 264, 65258, 7203, 374, 537, 4152, 311, 264, 4709, 315, 2487, 8664, 304, 697, 89772, 13, 12090, 11, 432, 374, 4152, 311, 279, 4680, 315, 279, 3607, 323, 7027, 498, 614, 25983, 6814, 279, 1899, 11, 892, 697, 2487, 5711, 369, 4802, 13, 4615, 1620, 26359, 22881, 323, 44326, 11, 4751, 1091, 697, 65258, 19029, 11, 525, 17339, 311, 9314, 4680, 4709, 13, 151645], "pred": "No, you do not lose weight when you have a bowel movement. The weight you lose after having a bowel movement is not due to a loss of body fat in your stools. Instead, it is due to the weight of the food and drink you have consumed throughout the day, which your body uses for energy. Your caloric intake and expenditure, rather than your bowel movements, are tied to healthy weight loss.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3190626359384001, "g_worst_claim": 0.27011966705322266, "g_content": 1.4886438706341911, "g_traj_mean": 1.0569651126861572}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [2753, 11, 498, 653, 537, 9052, 4680, 979, 498, 614, 264, 65258, 7203, 13, 151645], "pred": "No, you do not lose weight when you have a bowel movement.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.40723787035260883, "g_worst_claim": 0.4072378