{"id": "344", "question": "when you have a bowel movement do you lose weight", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the answer is: No, having a bowel movement does not cause weight loss. The passages state that body weight loss comes from creating a calorie deficit, not from losing body fat in stools. Additionally, the fat in stools is not derived from body fat, but rather from dietary fat intake that is not properly absorbed. Therefore, hopping on the bathroom scale before and after a bowel movement will not accurately reflect any weight loss due to the bowel movement itself.", "pred": "Based on the information provided in the passages, the weight lost from a bowel movement does not come from a loss of body fat. Instead, it results from the excretion of dietary fats that were not properly absorbed. Therefore, having a bowel movement does not result in a noticeable loss of body weight.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the information provided in the passages, the weight lost from a bowel movement does not come from a loss of body fat. Instead, it results from the excretion of dietary fats that were not properly absorbed. Therefore, having a bowel movement does not result in a noticeable loss of body weight.", "cot": "[\"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Based on the information provided in the passages, the weight lost from a bowel movement does not come from a loss of body fat. Instead, it results from the excretion of dietary fats that were not properly absorbed. Therefore, having a bowel movement does not result in a noticeable loss of body weight.\", \"No, you do not lose weight when you have a bowel movement.\", \"No, having a bowel movement typically does not lead to noticeable weight loss. This is because the weight loss is not due to the excretion of body fat, but rather a result of a calorie deficit, which forces the body to burn stored fat. While a small amount of fat may be found in feces, this is not considered a significant source of fat loss.\"]", "time_sec": 10.626, "generation_time_seconds": 9.6954, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9216, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.1477830559015274, "g_worst_claim": -0.1477830559015274, "g_content": -0.23121836185455322, "g_traj_mean": -0.13130667805671692}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 1995, 3897, 304, 279, 46769, 11, 279, 4680, 5558, 504, 264, 65258, 7203, 1558, 537, 2525, 504, 264, 4709, 315, 2487, 8664, 13, 12090, 11, 432, 3059, 504, 279, 505, 88690, 315, 33525, 49027, 429, 1033, 537, 10277, 41001, 13, 15277, 11, 3432, 264, 65258, 7203, 1558, 537, 1102, 304, 264, 42326, 4709, 315, 2487, 4680, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the information provided in the passages, the weight lost from a bowel movement does not come from a loss of body fat. Instead, it results from the excretion of dietary fats that were not properly absorbed. Therefore, having a bowel movement does not result in a noticeable loss of body weight.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7437861242325478, "g_worst_claim": 0.27320129731122184, "g_content": 1.304394501906175, "g_traj_mean": 0.7352325320243835}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [2753, 11, 498, 653, 537, 9052, 4680, 979, 498, 614, 264, 65258, 7203, 13, 151645], "pred": "No, you do not lose weight when you have a bowel movement.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.3723632948739188, "g_worst_claim": 0.3723632948739188, "g_content": -0.006489407736808062, "g_traj_mean": 0.36410799622535706}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [2753, 11, 3432, 264, 65258, 7203, 11136, 1558, 537, 2990, 311, 42326, 4680, 4709, 13, 1096, 374, 1576, 279, 4680, 4709, 374, 537, 4152, 311, 27