{"id": "350", "question": "what political, economic and social effects have on the united states", "gt": "The passages provided offer some insights into the political, economic, and social effects of various events in the history of the United States.\n\nPassage 1 highlights the impact of immigration on the country, indicating that it has shaped the nation since its early days. Immigration has contributed to the diversity of the population, cultural exchange, and the development of the economy.\n\nPassage 2 discusses the long-term effects of Reconstruction, which include the continuation of racial discrimination, segregation, and unequal access to employment opportunities for African Americans. This period saw the introduction of crop lien work contracts, which kept many African Americans in a state of virtual slavery.\n\nPassage 3 discusses the economic and political effects of the Civil War. The war brought economic unity to the country, as the South transitioned from a semi-subsistence economy to a market-based economy, and industrialization gained momentum. The passage also notes that important political changes accompanied the maintenance of national unity.\n\nBased on these passages, we can infer that the political, economic, and social effects of these historical events in the United States include:\n\n1. Immigration: Shaping the nation's population, culture, and economy.\n2. Reconstruction: Continued racial discrimination, segregation, and unequal access to employment opportunities for African Americans.\n3. Civil War: Economic unity, industrialization, and political changes that maintained national unity.\n\nTherefore, the political, economic, and social effects of these events in the United States include increased diversity, economic growth, and the continued struggle for racial equality.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"]", "time_sec": 6.766, "generation_time_seconds": 5.9625, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7958, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.062335189431905746, "g_worst_claim": -0.062335189431905746, "g_content": -0.10130831003189086, "g_traj_mean": -0.05541565641760826}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.062335189431905746, "g_worst_claim": -0.062335189431905746, "g_content": -0.10130831003189086, "g_traj_mean": -0.05541565641760826}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.062335189431905746, "g_worst_claim": -0.062335189431905746, "g_content": -0.10130831003189086, "g_traj_mean": -0.05541565641760826}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.062335189431905746, "g_worst_claim": -0.062335189431905746, "g_content": -0.10130831003189086, "g_traj_mean": -0.05541565641760826}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 2.38, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 6.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "351", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Company goodwill is a business asset that is created when a business provides good service or product to their customers, leading to customer trust. This trust results in repeat customers and positive word-of-mouth, which can increase a company's customer base and retain old clients. Goodwill represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation of the business possesses. It is important because it can attract investors and future buyers, and it is an advantage of the reputation and connection with customers which tends to make that connection permanent.", "pred": "Company goodwill is the value of a business's reputation and customer connections, which can be described as the total advantage of the business's reputation and customer trust. This reputation and customer trust create a permanent connection with customers, and the value of this connection is known as goodwill. Goodwill is important because it can increase a company's customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Company goodwill is the value of a business's reputation and customer connections, which can be described as the total advantage of the business's reputation and customer trust. This reputation and customer trust create a permanent connection with customers, and the value of this connection is known as goodwill. Goodwill is important because it can increase a company's customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.", "cot": "[\"Company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. It is an intangible asset that represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the business possesses. Goodwill is important because it can increase a company's customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.\", \"Company goodwill refers to the reputation and connection a business has with its customers, combined with the circumstances that make this connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the business possesses. Goodwill is important because it can increase a business's customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.\", \"Goodwill is the reputation and connection customers have with a business, which tends to make that connection permanent. It is important because it increases customer base, retains customers, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers.\", \"Company goodwill is the value of a business's reputation and customer connections, which can be described as the total advantage of the business's reputation and customer trust. This reputation and customer trust create a permanent connection with customers, and the value of this connection is known as goodwill. Goodwill is important because it can increase a company's customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.\"]", "time_sec": 13.793, "generation_time_seconds": 12.9503, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8325, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [14491, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 6785, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 429, 264, 2562, 702, 7881, 916, 882, 13, 1084, 374, 458, 526, 60086, 9329, 429, 10868, 279, 897, 315, 279, 32364, 311, 6310, 429, 279, 829, 323, 17011, 315, 279, 2562, 49226, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 1576, 432, 646, 5263, 264, 2813, 594, 6002, 2331, 11, 14060, 2310, 8239, 11, 9320, 14823, 11, 323, 9320, 3853, 22630, 13, 151645], "pred": "Company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. It is an intangible asset that represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the business possesses. Goodwill is important because it can increase a company's customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.170452609121949, "g_worst_claim": 0.5992460932050433, "g_content": 2.7205148584702434, "g_traj_mean": 1.4745903015136719}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [14491, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 17011, 323, 3633, 264, 2562, 702, 448, 1181, 6310, 11, 10856, 448, 279, 13161, 429, 1281, 419, 3633, 15330, 13, 1084, 10868, 279, 897, 315, 279, 32364, 311, 6310, 429, 279, 829, 323, 17011, 315, 279, 2562, 49226, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 1576, 432, 646, 5263, 264, 2562, 594, 6002, 2331, 11, 14060, 2310, 8239, 11, 9320, 14823, 11, 323, 9320, 3853, 22630, 13, 151645], "pred": "Company goodwill refers to the reputation and connection a business has with its customers, combined with the circumstances that make this connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the business possesses. Goodwill is important because it can increase a business's customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.3175116715702666, "g_worst_claim": 0.777573721749442, "g_content": 3.3782929813160614, "g_traj_mean": 1.907893419265747}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [15216, 14387, 374, 279, 17011, 323, 3633, 6310, 614, 448, 264, 2562, 11, 892, 27236, 311, 1281, 429, 3633, 15330, 13, 1084, 374, 2989, 1576, 432, 12703, 6002, 2331, 11, 51844, 6310, 11, 60091, 14823, 11, 323, 60091, 3853, 22630, 13, 151645], "pred": "Goodwill is the reputation and connection customers have with a business, which tends to make that connection permanent. It is important because it increases customer base, retains customers, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0562090398239614, "g_worst_claim": 0.3468747138977051, "g_content": 3.8489131927490234, "g_traj_mean": 2.13689923286438}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [14491, 81646, 374, 279, 897, 315, 264, 2562, 594, 17011, 323, 6002, 13234, 11, 892, 646, 387, 7481, 438, 279, 2790, 9423, 315, 279, 2562, 594, 17011, 323, 6002, 6950, 13, 1096, 17011, 323, 6002, 6950, 1855, 264, 15330, 3633, 448, 6310, 11, 323, 279, 897, 315, 419, 3633, 374, 3881, 438, 81646, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 1576, 432, 646, 5263, 264, 2813, 594, 6002, 2331, 11, 14060, 2310, 8239, 11, 9320, 14823, 11, 323, 9320, 3853, 22630, 13, 151645], "pred": "Company goodwill is the value of a business's reputation and customer connections, which can be described as the total advantage of the business's reputation and customer trust. This reputation and customer trust create a permanent connection with customers, and the value of this connection is known as goodwill. Goodwill is important because it can increase a company's customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7851885458273775, "g_worst_claim": 0.20336593281139026, "g_content": 2.2548583984375, "g_traj_mean": 1.2964421510696411}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 58.95, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "353", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Based on the given passages, goodwill can be understood as a business asset that comes from a positive reputation and good connections with customers. It can be increased through providing good service or products, resulting in loyal and repeat customers who also spread positive reviews about the business. This goodwill attracts new customers, investors, and future buyers, making it an important factor in business success.", "pred": "Company goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers that tend to make that connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it increases customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Company goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers that tend to make that connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it increases customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers.", "cot": "[\"Company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. It is an intangible asset that represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the business possesses. Goodwill is important because it can increase a company's customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.\", \"Company goodwill refers to the value of the reputation and connection with customers that tends to make that connection permanent. It represents the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses, which can increase customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.\", \"Company goodwill is the positive reputation and connection with customers, as well as the circumstances that tend to make that connection permanent. It represents the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the company possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it can increase customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.\", \"Company goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers that tend to make that connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it increases customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers.\"]", "time_sec": 13.308, "generation_time_seconds": 12.5408, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7621, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [14491, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 6785, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 429, 264, 2562, 702, 7881, 916, 882, 13, 1084, 374, 458, 526, 60086, 9329, 429, 10868, 279, 897, 315, 279, 32364, 311, 6310, 429, 279, 829, 323, 17011, 315, 279, 2562, 49226, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 1576, 432, 646, 5263, 264, 2813, 594, 6002, 2331, 11, 14060, 2310, 8239, 11, 9320, 14823, 11, 323, 9320, 3853, 22630, 13, 151645], "pred": "Company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. It is an intangible asset that represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the business possesses. Goodwill is important because it can increase a company's customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1728763947451024, "g_worst_claim": 0.5765269143240792, "g_content": 2.708138858570772, "g_traj_mean": 1.4765032529830933}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [14491, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 897, 315, 279, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 429, 27236, 311, 1281, 429, 3633, 15330, 13, 1084, 10868, 279, 32364, 311, 279, 6310, 892, 279, 829, 323, 17011, 49226, 11, 892, 646, 5263, 6002, 2331, 11, 14060, 2310, 8239, 11, 9320, 14823, 11, 323, 9320, 3853, 22630, 13, 151645], "pred": "Company goodwill refers to the value of the reputation and connection with customers that tends to make that connection permanent. It represents the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses, which can increase customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.7391834262817625, "g_worst_claim": 2.1896114349365234, "g_content": 4.129676273890904, "g_traj_mean": 2.67171573638916}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [14491, 81646, 374, 279, 6785, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 11, 438, 1632, 438, 279, 13161, 429, 8376, 311, 1281, 429, 3633, 15330, 13, 1084, 10868, 279, 32364, 311, 6310, 429, 279, 829, 323, 17011, 315, 279, 2813, 49226, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 304, 2562, 1576, 432, 646, 5263, 6002, 2331, 11, 14060, 2310, 8239, 11, 9320, 14823, 11, 323, 9320, 3853, 22630, 13, 151645], "pred": "Company goodwill is the positive reputation and connection with customers, as well as the circumstances that tend to make that connection permanent. It represents the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the company possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it can increase customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.4024602234383403, "g_worst_claim": 1.4572858076829176, "g_content": 3.430026892459754, "g_traj_mean": 2.163445234298706}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [14491, 81646, 374, 279, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 429, 8376, 311, 1281, 429, 3633, 15330, 13, 1084, 10868, 279, 897, 315, 279, 32364, 311, 279, 6310, 892, 279, 829, 323, 17011, 49226, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 304, 2562, 1576, 432, 12703, 6002, 2331, 11, 51844, 2310, 8239, 11, 60091, 14823, 11, 323, 60091, 3853, 22630, 13, 151645], "pred": "Company goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers that tend to make that connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it increases customer base, retains old clients, attracts investors, and attracts future buyers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.7873901494967392, "g_worst_claim": 1.6647316614786785, "g_content": 4.297360738118489, "g_traj_mean": 2.721421480178833}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 29.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "354", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, I can confidently answer the following questions:\n\nWhat is company goodwill?\nCompany goodwill refers to the positive image and reputation of a business that is built over time through providing quality products or services, satisfying customers, and building strong relationships with them. Goodwill is a valuable asset for any business as it helps to attract new customers, retain existing ones, and attract investors.\n\nWhy is goodwill important in business?\nGoodwill is important in business because it helps to build trust and loyalty among customers, which leads to long-term relationships and repeat business. A strong reputation and goodwill can also make a business more attractive to potential investors and buyers. Additionally, goodwill can help a business to stand out from its competitors and establish a unique identity in the marketplace.", "pred": "Company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. It is an intangible asset that represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the business possesses. Goodwill is important because it can increase a company's customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. It is an intangible asset that represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the business possesses. Goodwill is important because it can increase a company's customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.", "cot": "[\"Company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. It is an intangible asset that represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the business possesses. Goodwill is important because it can increase a company's customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.\", \"Company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection a business has with its customers, which can lead to increased customer base and retention, attracting investors and future buyers. It is important because it creates a trust between the business and its customers, leading to repeat customers and positive word-of-mouth marketing.\", \"Goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers, which tend to make the connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses.\", \"Goodwill is the reputation and connection a business has with customers. This can include things like good service, products the customers trust, and repeat customers. Goodwill is important because it can attract investors, retain old clients, and help increase the customer base. It represents the value of the business to the customers and can help make the connection with them permanent.\"]", "time_sec": 12.596, "generation_time_seconds": 11.7842, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8022, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [14491, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 6785, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 429, 264, 2562, 702, 7881, 916, 882, 13, 1084, 374, 458, 526, 60086, 9329, 429, 10868, 279, 897, 315, 279, 32364, 311, 6310, 429, 279, 829, 323, 17011, 315, 279, 2562, 49226, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 1576, 432, 646, 5263, 264, 2813, 594, 6002, 2331, 11, 14060, 2310, 8239, 11, 9320, 14823, 11, 323, 9320, 3853, 22630, 13, 151645], "pred": "Company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. It is an intangible asset that represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the business possesses. Goodwill is important because it can increase a company's customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1632793801529964, "g_worst_claim": 0.6199502263750348, "g_content": 2.7261659958783317, "g_traj_mean": 1.4770961999893188}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [14491, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 6785, 17011, 323, 3633, 264, 2562, 702, 448, 1181, 6310, 11, 892, 646, 2990, 311, 7172, 6002, 2331, 323, 37131, 11, 50547, 14823, 323, 3853, 22630, 13, 1084, 374, 2989, 1576, 432, 11450, 264, 6950, 1948, 279, 2562, 323, 1181, 6310, 11, 6388, 311, 13153, 6310, 323, 6785, 3409, 8668, 91039, 8493, 13, 151645], "pred": "Company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection a business has with its customers, which can lead to increased customer base and retention, attracting investors and future buyers. It is important because it creates a trust between the business and its customers, leading to repeat customers and positive word-of-mouth marketing.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5056346581198952, "g_worst_claim": 0.566787372935902, "g_content": 2.446789332798549, "g_traj_mean": 1.3212100267410278}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [15216, 14387, 374, 279, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 11, 892, 8376, 311, 1281, 279, 3633, 15330, 13, 1084, 10868, 279, 897, 315, 279, 32364, 311, 279, 6310, 892, 279, 829, 323, 17011, 49226, 13, 151645], "pred": "Goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers, which tend to make the connection permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to the customers which the name and reputation possesses.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 3.2626149570240695, "g_worst_claim": 2.8164657592773437, "g_content": 5.799451192220052, "g_traj_mean": 3.0224485397338867}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [15216, 14387, 374, 279, 17011, 323, 3633, 264, 2562, 702, 448, 6310, 13, 1096, 646, 2924, 2513, 1075, 1661, 2473, 11, 3871, 279, 6310, 6950, 11, 323, 13153, 6310, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 1576, 432, 646, 9320, 14823, 11, 14060, 2310, 8239, 11, 323, 1492, 5263, 279, 6002, 2331, 13, 1084, 10868, 279, 897, 315, 279, 2562, 311, 279, 6310, 323, 646, 1492, 1281, 279, 3633, 448, 1105, 15330, 13, 151645], "pred": "Goodwill is the reputation and connection a business has with customers. This can include things like good service, products the customers trust, and repeat customers. Goodwill is important because it can attract investors, retain old clients, and help increase the customer base. It represents the value of the business to the customers and can help make the connection with them permanent.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5075105526290096, "g_worst_claim": 0.24640309810638428, "g_content": 2.742283540613511, "g_traj_mean": 1.4405062198638916}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "356", "question": "what is company goodwill and why important", "gt": "Based on the given passages, company goodwill refers to the positive feelings and loyalty of customers towards a business, gained through providing good services or products, building trust, and creating a strong reputation. Goodwill is important because it can increase customer retention, attract new customers, and make the business more attractive to investors and potential buyers.\n\nAccording to passage 3, goodwill is an intangible asset that represents the value of a business's reputation and customer connections, which can make the connection between the business and its customers permanent.\n\nTherefore, goodwill is important for businesses because it can lead to increased customer loyalty, positive word-of-mouth advertising, and higher sales, ultimately contributing to the long-term success and growth of the business.", "pred": "Goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers formed from providing good service or products, which can lead to repeat customers and word-of-mouth advertising. It is important because it helps increase customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and future buyers, thus enhancing the overall value of the business.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers formed from providing good service or products, which can lead to repeat customers and word-of-mouth advertising. It is important because it helps increase customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and future buyers, thus enhancing the overall value of the business.", "cot": "[\"Company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. It is an intangible asset that represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the business possesses. Goodwill is important because it can increase a company's customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.\", \"Company goodwill refers to the positive reputation or goodwill of a business among its customers and the broader public. It's essentially the value that a company's name, reputation, and customer connections carry. This goodwill is important for several reasons:\\n\\n1. **Customer Retention and Acquisition**: Goodwill helps in attracting and retaining customers. It fosters a sense of loyalty among customers who have had a positive experience with the company. For instance, if a business consistently provides good service, customers are more likely to return and recommend the business to others.\\n\\n2. **Investor Attraction**: Investors are often attracted to businesses with a strong reputation and goodwill. A well-known and reputable company is seen as a more secure and stable investment option, as it has a proven track record of satisfying customers and generating profit.\\n\\n3. **Attracting Future Buyers**: Goodwill also plays a significant role when a business is being sold. A company with a high level of goodwill is more likely to command a higher price when sold to investors or potential buyers. This is because the goodwill represents the company's established customer base, brand loyalty, and reputation, all of which can contribute to future revenue and profit.\\n\\n4. **Enhanced Competition**: A business with a high level of goodwill can have an advantage over competitors. It can attract new customers more easily and retain existing ones more effectively, leading to a larger customer base and potentially higher market share.\\n\\nOverall, goodwill is crucial for a company's long-term success as it directly impacts customer loyalty, investor confidence, and the company's ability to compete in the market.\", \"Company goodwill refers to the reputation and connections with customers, as well as the circumstances that make these connections permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the business possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it can increase customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.\", \"Goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers formed from providing good service or products, which can lead to repeat customers and word-of-mouth advertising. It is important because it helps increase customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and future buyers, thus enhancing the overall value of the business.\"]", "time_sec": 21.475, "generation_time_seconds": 20.5662, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9008, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [14491, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 6785, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 429, 264, 2562, 702, 7881, 916, 882, 13, 1084, 374, 458, 526, 60086, 9329, 429, 10868, 279, 897, 315, 279, 32364, 311, 6310, 429, 279, 829, 323, 17011, 315, 279, 2562, 49226, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 1576, 432, 646, 5263, 264, 2813, 594, 6002, 2331, 11, 14060, 2310, 8239, 11, 9320, 14823, 11, 323, 9320, 3853, 22630, 13, 151645], "pred": "Company goodwill refers to the positive reputation and connection with customers that a business has developed over time. It is an intangible asset that represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the business possesses. Goodwill is important because it can increase a company's customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1699340210821396, "g_worst_claim": 0.6106125286647252, "g_content": 2.7347557965446923, "g_traj_mean": 1.4734697341918945}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [14491, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 6785, 17011, 476, 81646, 315, 264, 2562, 4221, 1181, 6310, 323, 279, 26829, 584, 13, 1084, 594, 15791, 279, 897, 429, 264, 2813, 594, 829, 11, 17011, 11, 323, 6002, 13234, 6777, 13, 1096, 81646, 374, 2989, 369, 3807, 7966, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 12792, 10392, 2939, 323, 72371, 95518, 7684, 14387, 8609, 304, 50547, 323, 50010, 6310, 13, 1084, 36313, 388, 264, 5530, 315, 31783, 4221, 6310, 879, 614, 1030, 264, 6785, 3139, 448, 279, 2813, 13, 1752, 2867, 11, 421, 264, 2562, 20699, 5707, 1661, 2473, 11, 6310, 525, 803, 4363, 311, 470, 323, 6934, 279, 2562, 311, 3800, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 33876, 269, 2411, 26425, 95518, 69533, 525, 3545, 28023, 311, 9675, 448, 264, 3746, 17011, 323, 81646, 13, 362, 1632, 21309, 323, 55840, 2813, 374, 3884, 438, 264, 803, 9767, 323, 15175, 9162, 2999, 11, 438, 432, 702, 264, 16622, 3754, 3255, 315, 36054, 6310, 323, 23163, 11372, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 1655, 2144, 287, 12498, 88707, 95518, 7684, 14387, 1083, 11088, 264, 5089, 3476, 979, 264, 2562, 374, 1660, 6088, 13, 362, 2813, 448, 264, 1550, 2188, 315, 81646, 374, 803, 4363, 311, 3210, 264, 5080, 3349, 979, 6088, 311, 14823, 476, 4650, 22630, 13, 1096, 374, 1576, 279, 81646, 10868, 279, 2813, 594, 9555, 6002, 2331, 11, 6741, 31783, 11, 323, 17011, 11, 678, 315, 892, 646, 16792, 311, 3853, 12957, 323, 11372, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 57468, 4874, 41221, 95518, 362, 2562, 448, 264, 1550, 2188, 315, 81646, 646, 614, 458, 9423, 916, 27550, 13, 1084, 646, 9320, 501, 6310, 803, 6707, 323, 14060, 6350, 6174, 803, 13444, 11, 6388, 311, 264, 8131, 6002, 2331, 323, 13581, 5080, 3081, 4332, 382, 27489, 11, 81646, 374, 16587, 369, 264, 2813, 594, 1293, 9663, 2393, 438, 432, 5961, 24905, 6002, 31783, 11, 29593, 12136, 11, 323, 279, 2813, 594, 5726, 311, 20259, 304, 279, 3081, 13, 151645], "pred": "Overall, goodwill is crucial for a company's long-term success as it directly impacts customer loyalty, investor confidence, and the company's ability to compete in the market.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.31634210658299805, "g_worst_claim": -0.0614581823348999, "g_content": 0.47136703491210935, "g_traj_mean": 0.29643213748931885}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [14491, 81646, 19257, 311, 279, 17011, 323, 13234, 448, 6310, 11, 438, 1632, 438, 279, 13161, 429, 1281, 1493, 13234, 15330, 13, 1084, 10868, 279, 897, 315, 279, 32364, 311, 6310, 429, 279, 829, 323, 17011, 315, 279, 2562, 49226, 13, 7684, 14387, 374, 2989, 304, 2562, 1576, 432, 646, 5263, 6002, 2331, 11, 14060, 2310, 8239, 11, 9320, 14823, 11, 323, 9320, 3853, 22630, 13, 151645], "pred": "Company goodwill refers to the reputation and connections with customers, as well as the circumstances that make these connections permanent. It represents the value of the attraction to customers that the name and reputation of the business possesses. Goodwill is important in business because it can increase customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and attract future buyers.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.484189439213092, "g_worst_claim": 1.4243816962608924, "g_content": 3.4099558049982246, "g_traj_mean": 2.2197153568267822}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [15216, 14387, 374, 279, 17011, 323, 3633, 448, 6310, 14122, 504, 8241, 1661, 2473, 476, 3871, 11, 892, 646, 2990, 311, 13153, 6310, 323, 3409, 8668, 91039, 12876, 13, 1084, 374, 2989, 1576, 432, 8609, 5263, 6002, 2331, 11, 14060, 2310, 8239, 11, 9320, 14823, 11, 323, 3853, 22630, 11, 8450, 46494, 279, 8084, 897, 315, 279, 2562, 13, 151645], "pred": "Goodwill is the reputation and connection with customers formed from providing good service or products, which can lead to repeat customers and word-of-mouth advertising. It is important because it helps increase customer base, retain old clients, attract investors, and future buyers, thus enhancing the overall value of the business.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.031940237169061, "g_worst_claim": 0.48243257734510636, "g_content": 2.972858560496363, "g_traj_mean": 1.6889426708221436}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 36.04, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "357", "question": "What’s the difference between ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy?", "gt": "An ad hominem fallacy occurs when someone attacks the character, motive, or other personal attribute of the person making an argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. This is often done to invalidate their arguments by associating their character with the soundness of their argument. On the other hand, the poisoning the well fallacy, which is a type of ad hominem attack, occurs when a person's integrity or intelligence is attacked before the merits of a case can be considered, effectively redirecting the discussion to the faults of one of the parties.", "pred": "The ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. An example of this is when someone attacks the person's intelligence or integrity before discussing the merits of their argument. The poisoning the well fallacy is similar, but it occurs before the merits of a case can be considered. It redirects a discussion to the faults of one of the parties.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. An example of this is when someone attacks the person's intelligence or integrity before discussing the merits of their argument. The poisoning the well fallacy is similar, but it occurs before the merits of a case can be considered. It redirects a discussion to the faults of one of the parties.", "cot": "[\"The ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. An example of this is when someone attacks the person's intelligence or integrity before discussing the merits of their argument. The poisoning the well fallacy is similar, but it occurs before the merits of a case can be considered. It redirects a discussion to the faults of one of the parties.\", \"The ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making an argument, rather than attacking the argument itself. In contrast, the poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack on a person's integrity or intelligence that occurs before the merits of a case can be considered, redirecting the discussion to the faults of one of the parties.\", \"An ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making an argument rather than addressing the argument itself. The poisoning the well fallacy, on the other hand, is a specific type of ad hominem attack where a person’s integrity or intelligence is attacked before the merits of a case can be discussed, effectively redirecting attention to those faults instead of the argument.\", \"The ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. An abusive ad hominem involves attacking the traits of an opponent as a means to invalidate their arguments. The poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack on a person's integrity or intelligence that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered. It redirects a discussion to the faults of one of the parties, creating a bias against one party before the argument can be properly evaluated.\"]", "time_sec": 16.458, "generation_time_seconds": 15.6919, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7565, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 993, 4998, 68413, 4399, 2757, 17601, 22818, 279, 3668, 11, 45994, 11, 476, 1008, 8201, 315, 279, 1697, 3259, 279, 5693, 11, 4751, 1091, 22818, 279, 5693, 5961, 13, 1527, 3110, 315, 419, 374, 979, 4325, 8776, 279, 1697, 594, 11229, 476, 16614, 1573, 24392, 279, 49832, 315, 862, 5693, 13, 576, 51136, 279, 1632, 4399, 2757, 374, 4428, 11, 714, 432, 13666, 1573, 279, 49832, 315, 264, 1142, 646, 387, 6509, 13, 1084, 71171, 264, 10219, 311, 279, 56690, 315, 825, 315, 279, 9677, 13, 151645], "pred": "The ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. An example of this is when someone attacks the person's intelligence or integrity before discussing the merits of their argument. The poisoning the well fallacy is similar, but it occurs before the merits of a case can be considered. It redirects a discussion to the faults of one of the parties.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4444760866703372, "g_worst_claim": 0.28165766927931046, "g_content": 2.2084143789190995, "g_traj_mean": 1.4183940887451172}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 993, 4998, 68413, 4399, 2757, 17601, 22818, 279, 3668, 11, 45994, 11, 476, 1008, 8201, 315, 279, 1697, 3259, 458, 5693, 11, 4751, 1091, 22818, 279, 5693, 5086, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 279, 51136, 279, 1632, 4399, 2757, 374, 458, 993, 4998, 68413, 3359, 389, 264, 1697, 594, 16614, 476, 11229, 429, 13666, 1573, 279, 49832, 315, 264, 1142, 646, 387, 6509, 11, 6423, 287, 279, 10219, 311, 279, 56690, 315, 825, 315, 279, 9677, 13, 151645], "pred": "The ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making an argument, rather than attacking the argument itself. In contrast, the poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack on a person's integrity or intelligence that occurs before the merits of a case can be considered, redirecting the discussion to the faults of one of the parties.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4228126958196308, "g_worst_claim": 0.4654836177825928, "g_content": 2.478740692138672, "g_traj_mean": 1.5175610780715942}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [2082, 993, 4998, 68413, 4399, 2757, 17601, 22818, 279, 3668, 11, 45994, 11, 476, 1008, 8201, 315, 279, 1697, 3259, 458, 5693, 4751, 1091, 27020, 279, 5693, 5086, 13, 576, 51136, 279, 1632, 4399, 2757, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 374, 264, 3151, 943, 315, 993, 4998, 68413, 3359, 1380, 264, 1697, 748, 16614, 476, 11229, 374, 18349, 1573, 279, 49832, 315, 264, 1142, 646, 387, 14078, 11, 13444, 6423, 287, 6529, 311, 1846, 56690, 4518, 315, 279, 5693, 13, 151645], "pred": "An ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making an argument rather than addressing the argument itself. The poisoning the well fallacy, on the other hand, is a specific type of ad hominem attack where a person’s integrity or intelligence is attacked before the merits of a case can be discussed, effectively redirecting attention to those faults instead of the argument.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9783298385994774, "g_worst_claim": 0.06009726013456072, "g_content": 1.4996614198426943, "g_traj_mean": 1.0566596984863281}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 993, 4998, 68413, 4399, 2757, 17601, 22818, 279, 3668, 11, 45994, 11, 476, 1008, 8201, 315, 279, 1697, 3259, 279, 5693, 11, 4751, 1091, 22818, 279, 5693, 5961, 13, 1527, 42558, 993, 4998, 68413, 17601, 22818, 279, 24055, 315, 458, 14704, 438, 264, 3363, 311, 39943, 862, 5977, 13, 576, 51136, 279, 1632, 4399, 2757, 374, 458, 993, 4998, 68413, 3359, 389, 264, 1697, 594, 16614, 476, 11229, 429, 4990, 1992, 1573, 279, 49832, 315, 264, 1142, 646, 387, 6509, 13, 1084, 71171, 264, 10219, 311, 279, 56690, 315, 825, 315, 279, 9677, 11, 6825, 264, 15470, 2348, 825, 4614, 1573, 279, 5693, 646, 387, 10277, 25070, 13, 151645], "pred": "The ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. An abusive ad hominem involves attacking the traits of an opponent as a means to invalidate their arguments. The poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack on a person's integrity or intelligence that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered. It redirects a discussion to the faults of one of the parties, creating a bias against one party before the argument can be properly evaluated.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5674844633619336, "g_worst_claim": 0.4410302979605539, "g_content": 2.3918662880951502, "g_traj_mean": 1.6269387006759644}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 69.31, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "358", "question": "What’s the difference between ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the difference between ad hominem fallacy and poisoning the well fallacy is that ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attribute of the person making the argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. On the other hand, poisoning the well fallacy is an ad hominem attack that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered, specifically attacking a person's integrity or intelligence to redirect the discussion towards their faults.", "pred": "Both fallacies are often used to distract from the actual issues at hand and to undermine the credibility of the argument being presented.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Both fallacies are often used to distract from the actual issues at hand and to undermine the credibility of the argument being presented.", "cot": "[\"The ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. An example of this is when someone attacks the person's intelligence or integrity before discussing the merits of their argument. The poisoning the well fallacy is similar, but it occurs before the merits of a case can be considered. It redirects a discussion to the faults of one of the parties.\", \"Both ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy involve attacking the person to which the argument is directed instead of attacking the argument itself. However, the poisoning the well fallacy is a specific form of ad hominem fallacy that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered, while ad hominem fallacy can occur at any point in the argument. In other words, ad hominem fallacy is a broader term that encompasses both the poisoning the well fallacy and any other ad hominem attacks on the character or other attributes of the person making the argument.\", \"The ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy are both types of ad hominem attacks, but they differ in their timing and approach.\\n\\nAd hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument to invalidate their argument, rather than addressing the argument directly.\\n\\nPoisoning the well fallacy, on the other hand, involves attacking the integrity or intelligence of one of the parties before the merits of the case can be considered. This type of fallacy redirects a discussion to the faults of one of the parties, making it more difficult to evaluate the actual content of the argument.\\n\\nBoth fallacies are often used to distract from the actual issues at hand and to undermine the credibility of the argument being presented.\", \"The ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attribute of the person making the argument rather than attacking the argument directly. An example of an ad hominem fallacy is when someone dismisses an argument by attacking the person who made it, rather than addressing the argument itself. \\n\\nThe poisoning the well fallacy occurs when someone attacks the integrity or intelligence of a person before the merits of a case can be considered. This redirects the discussion to the faults of one of the parties. An example of the poisoning the well fallacy is when someone tries to discredit a person's argument by attacking their character, thereby making them seem less credible and less likely to be believed on their merits.\\n\\nIn summary, the main difference between the ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy is that the ad hominem fallacy focuses on the character of the person making the argument, while the poisoning the well fallacy focuses on attacking the person's integrity or intelligence before the argument can be evaluated.\"]", "time_sec": 23.015, "generation_time_seconds": 22.4963, "selection_time_seconds": 0.5127, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 993, 4998, 68413, 4399, 2757, 17601, 22818, 279, 3668, 11, 45994, 11, 476, 1008, 8201, 315, 279, 1697, 3259, 279, 5693, 11, 4751, 1091, 22818, 279, 5693, 5961, 13, 1527, 3110, 315, 419, 374, 979, 4325, 8776, 279, 1697, 594, 11229, 476, 16614, 1573, 24392, 279, 49832, 315, 862, 5693, 13, 576, 51136, 279, 1632, 4399, 2757, 374, 4428, 11, 714, 432, 13666, 1573, 279, 49832, 315, 264, 1142, 646, 387, 6509, 13, 1084, 71171, 264, 10219, 311, 279, 56690, 315, 825, 315, 279, 9677, 13, 151645], "pred": "The ad hominem fallacy involves attacking the character, motive, or other attributes of the person making the argument, rather than attacking the argument directly. An example of this is when someone attacks the person's intelligence or integrity before discussing the merits of their argument. The poisoning the well fallacy is similar, but it occurs before the merits of a case can be considered. It redirects a discussion to the faults of one of the parties.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3748516124161692, "g_worst_claim": 0.26384933789571124, "g_content": 2.10207788567794, "g_traj_mean": 1.3587470054626465}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [20629, 993, 4998, 68413, 4399, 2757, 323, 279, 51136, 279, 1632, 4399, 2757, 21058, 22818, 279, 1697, 311, 892, 279, 5693, 374, 15540, 4518, 315, 22818, 279, 5693, 5086, 13, 4354, 11, 279, 51136, 279, 1632, 4399, 2757, 374, 264, 3151, 1352, 315, 993, 4998, 68413, 4399, 2757, 429, 4990, 1992, 1573, 279, 49832, 315, 264, 1142, 646, 387, 6509, 11, 1393, 993, 4998, 68413, 4399, 2757, 646, 12170, 518, 894, 1459, 304, 279, 5693, 13, 758, 1008, 4244, 11, 993, 4998, 68413, 4399, 2757, 374, 264, 26829, 4647, 429, 69910, 2176, 279, 51136, 279, 1632, 4399, 2757, 323, 894, 1008, 993, 4998, 68413, 8776, 389, 279, 3668, 476, 1008, 8201, 315, 279, 1697, 3259, 279, 5693, 13, 151645], "pred": "Both ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy involve attacking the person to which the argument is directed instead of attacking the argument itself. However, the poisoning the well fallacy is a specific form of ad hominem fallacy that takes place before the merits of a case can be considered, while ad hominem fallacy can occur at any point in the argument. In other words, ad hominem fallacy is a broader term that encompasses both the poisoning the well fallacy and any other ad hominem attacks on the character or other attributes of the person making the argument.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.3673740800333077, "g_worst_claim": -0.04324435790379842, "g_content": 0.5700432337247409, "g_traj_mean": 0.41015106439590454}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 993, 4998, 68413, 4399, 2757, 323, 279, 51136, 279, 1632, 4399, 2757, 525, 2176, 4494, 315, 993, 4998, 68413, 8776, 11, 714, 807, 1745, 304, 862, 18405, 323, 5486, 382, 2589, 4998, 68413, 4399, 2757, 17601, 22818, 279, 3668, 11, 45994, 11, 476, 1008, 8201, 315, 279, 1697, 3259, 279, 5693, 311, 39943, 862, 5693, 11, 4751, 1091, 27020, 279, 5693, 5961, 382, 32904, 3335, 287, 279, 1632, 4399, 2757, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 17601, 22818, 279, 16614, 476, 11229, 315, 825, 315, 279, 9677, 1573, 279, 49832, 315, 279, 1142, 646, 387, 6509, 13, 1096, 943, 315, 4399, 2757, 71171, 264, 10219, 311, 279, 56690, 315, 825, 315, 279, 9677, 11, 3259, 432, 803, 5000, 311, 15442, 279, 5042, 2213, 315, 279, 5693, 382, 20629, 4399, 26030, 525, 3545, 1483, 311, 63817, 504, 279, 5042, 4714, 518, 1424, 323, 311, 41947, 279, 37669, 315, 279, 5693, 1660, 10449, 13, 151645], "pred": "Both fallacies are often used to distract from the actual issues at hand and to undermine the credibility of the argument being presented.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7491962598756217, "g_worst_claim": -0.09571292877197266, "g_content": 1.