{"id": "367", "question": "what is the difference between a rock and a stone", "gt": "Based on the given passages, a rock is defined as the hard material of the earth's crust that is normally exposed on the surface or underlying the soil. On the other hand, a stone is described as a smaller piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. The passages also mention that rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. Additionally, stones can be pelted easily, while rocks cannot. Therefore, the main difference between a rock and a stone is their size, with rocks being larger and stones being smaller and easier to handle.", "pred": "Rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. Rock can be described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand. On the other hand, stone is just a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. The stones can be pelted easily but one cannot do so with rocks.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. Rock can be described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand. On the other hand, stone is just a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. The stones can be pelted easily but one cannot do so with rocks.", "cot": "[\"Rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. Rocks can be described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand, while stones are just a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. Additionally, stones can be pelted easily, but one cannot do so with rocks.\", \"Rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. 2. Rock can be described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand. On the other hand, stone is just a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. 3. The stones can be pelted easily but one cannot do so with rocks.\", \"Rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. Rock can be described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand. On the other hand, stone is just a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. The stones can be pelted easily but one cannot do so with rocks.\", \"The difference between a rock and a stone lies in their size and composition. A rock, as defined in the passages, is the hard material of the earth’s crust, which is normally exposed on the surface of the earth or sometimes underlying the soil. It is typically larger and harder than a stone. A stone, on the other hand, is a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. It is made from rocks and is smaller in size compared to a rock. Additionally, the passage mentions that stones can be pelted easily, unlike rocks.\"]", "time_sec": 16.058, "generation_time_seconds": 15.1377, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9123, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [49, 25183, 525, 1865, 315, 9155, 26210, 323, 26210, 525, 1865, 504, 23035, 13, 68031, 646, 387, 7481, 438, 264, 3460, 6573, 315, 9798, 429, 374, 5000, 311, 387, 11691, 304, 279, 1424, 11, 1393, 26210, 525, 1101, 264, 2613, 6573, 476, 1051, 59880, 429, 646, 387, 11691, 304, 279, 1424, 13, 22406, 11, 26210, 646, 387, 281, 3818, 291, 6707, 11, 714, 825, 4157, 653, 773, 448, 23035, 13, 151645], "pred": "Rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. Rocks can be described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand, while stones are just a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. Additionally, stones can be pelted easily, but one cannot do so with rocks.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.241050143544636, "g_worst_claim": 1.4225601620144315, "g_content": 3.348292032877604, "g_traj_mean": 2.178255558013916}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [49, 25183, 525, 1865, 315, 9155, 26210, 323, 26210, 525, 1865, 504, 23035, 13, 220, 17, 13, 9127, 646, 387, 7481, 438, 264, 3460, 6573, 315, 9798, 429, 374, 5000, 311, 387, 11691, 304, 279, 1424, 13, 1913, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 9798, 374, 1101, 264, 2613, 6573, 476, 1051, 59880, 429, 646, 387, 11691, 304, 279, 1424, 13, 220, 18, 13, 576, 26210, 646, 387, 281, 3818, 291, 6707, 714, 825, 4157, 653, 773, 448, 23035, 13, 151645], "pred": "Rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. 2. Rock can be described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand. On the other hand, stone is just a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. 3. The stones can be pelted easily but one cannot do so with rocks.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.405071821934035, "g_worst_claim": 1.4300562914680033, "g_content": 3.410435994466146, "g_traj_mean": 2.220489025115967}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [49, 25183, 525, 1865, 315, 9155, 26210, 323, 26210, 525, 1865, 504, 23035, 13, 9127, 646, 387, 7481, 438, 264, 3460, 6573, 315, 9798, 429, 374, 5000, 311, 387, 11691, 304, 279, 1424, 13, 1913, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 9798, 374, 1101, 264, 2613, 6573, 476, 1051, 59880, 429, 646, 387, 11691, 304, 279, 1424, 13, 576, 26210, 646, 387, 281, 3818, 291, 6707, 714, 825, 4157, 653, 773, 448, 23035, 13, 151645], "pred": "Rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. Rock can be described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand. On the other hand, stone is just a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. The stones can be pelted easily but one cannot do so with rocks.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.3965930864590557, "g_worst_claim": 1.441100513233858, "g_content": 3.465051466418851, "g_traj_mean": 2.2294788360595703}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 264, 6946, 323, 264, 9798, 15448, 304, 862, 1379, 323, 18037, 13, 362, 6946, 11, 438, 4512, 304, 279, 46769, 11, 374, 279, 2588, 3684, 315, 279, 9393, 748, 39612, 11, 892, 374, 14279, 14900, 389, 279, 7329, 315, 279, 9393, 476, 7025, 16533, 279, 17171, 13, 1084, 374, 11136, 8131, 323, 15750, 1091, 264, 9798, 13, 362, 9798, 11, 389, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 374, 264, 2613, 6573, 476, 1051, 59880, 429, 646, 387, 11691, 304, 279, 1424, 13, 1084, 374, 1865, 504, 23035, 323, 374, 9155, 304, 1379, 7707, 311, 264, 6946, 13, 22406, 11, 279, 21085, 33845, 429, 26210, 646, 387, 281, 3818, 291, 6707, 11, 19836, 23035, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between a rock and a stone lies in their size and composition. A rock, as defined in the passages, is the hard material of the earth’s crust, which is normally exposed on the surface of the earth or sometimes underlying the soil. It is typically larger and harder than a stone. A stone, on the other hand, is a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. It is made from rocks and is smaller in size compared to a rock. Additionally, the passage mentions that stones can be pelted easily, unlike rocks.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3335918875598403, "g_worst_claim": 0.3360898017883301, "g_content": 2.159943787947945, "g_traj_mean": 1.2937694787979126}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.1, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "368", "question": "what is the difference between a rock and a stone", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main difference between a rock and a stone is their size. Rocks are typically larger and more massive than stones, which are smaller and more fragmented.\n\nPassage 1 states that rocks are often used to refer to something solid, large, and grounded, such as a mountain or palisade, while stones are often used to refer to small pieces of rock or pebbles. Passage 2 defines rocks as the hard material of the earth's crust that is exposed on the surface of the earth or underlying the soil, while stones are smaller fragments of rock that can be carried in the hand.\n\nPassage 3 further clarifies the distinction by stating that rocks are made up of smaller stones, while stones are made from rocks. Additionally, rocks are described as being difficult to carry in the hand, while stones are small enough to be carried easily.\n\nIn summary, while both rocks and stones are made of the same material, they differ in size and usage. Rocks are generally larger and more massive, while stones are smaller and more fragmented.", "pred": "Rocks can be described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand, while stones are just small pieces or pebbles that can be carried in the hand. Additionally, stones can be pelted easily, but rocks cannot. The difference between rocks and stones is that rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Rocks can be described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand, while stones are just small pieces or pebbles that can be carried in the hand. Additionally, stones can be pelted easily, but rocks cannot. The difference between rocks and stones is that rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks.", "cot": "[\"Rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. Rocks can be described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand, while stones are just a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. Additionally, stones can be pelted easily, but one cannot do so with rocks.\", \"Rocks can be described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand, while stones are just small pieces or pebbles that can be carried in the hand. Additionally, stones can be pelted easily, but rocks cannot. The difference between rocks and stones is that rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks.\", \"Rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. A rock can be described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand, while stones are just small pieces or pebbles that can be carried in the hand.\", \"Rocks are made of smaller stones and are described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand, while stones are just small pieces or pebbles that can be carried in the hand.\"]", "time_sec": 12.622, "generation_time_seconds": 11.8354, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7803, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [49, 25183, 525, 1865, 315, 9155, 26210, 323, 26210, 525, 1865, 504, 23035, 13, 68031, 646, 387, 7481, 438, 264, 3460, 6573, 315, 9798, 429, 374, 5000, 311, 387, 11691, 304, 279, 1424, 11, 1393, 26210, 525, 1101, 264, 2613, 6573, 476, 1051, 59880, 429, 646, 387, 11691, 304, 279, 1424, 13, 22406, 11, 26210, 646, 387, 281, 3818, 291, 6707, 11, 714, 825, 4157, 653, 773, 448, 23035, 13, 151645], "pred": "Rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. Rocks can be described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand, while stones are just a small piece or pebble that can be carried in the hand. Additionally, stones can be pelted easily, but one cannot do so with rocks.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.262648572618999, "g_worst_claim": 1.4323726230197482, "g_content": 3.343212381998698, "g_traj_mean": 2.197232961654663}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [49, 25183, 646, 387, 7481, 438, 264, 3460, 6573, 315, 9798, 429, 374, 5000, 311, 387, 11691, 304, 279, 1424, 11, 1393, 26210, 525, 1101, 2613, 9666, 476, 1051, 6066, 642, 429, 646, 387, 11691, 304, 279, 1424, 13, 22406, 11, 26210, 646, 387, 281, 3818, 291, 6707, 11, 714, 23035, 4157, 13, 576, 6672, 1948, 23035, 323, 26210, 374, 429, 23035, 525, 1865, 315, 9155, 26210, 323, 26210, 525, 1865, 504, 23035, 13, 151645], "pred": "Rocks can be described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand, while stones are just small pieces or pebbles that can be carried in the hand. Additionally, stones can be pelted easily, but rocks cannot. The difference between rocks and stones is that rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9003866604396273, "g_worst_claim": 1.1662475949242002, "g_content": 2.5611014366149902, "g_traj_mean": 1.7213234901428223}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [49, 25183, 525, 1865, 315, 9155, 26210, 323, 26210, 525, 1865, 504, 23035, 13, 362, 6946, 646, 387, 7481, 438, 264, 3460, 6573, 315, 9798, 429, 374, 5000, 311, 387, 11691, 304, 279, 1424, 11, 1393, 26210, 525, 1101, 2613, 9666, 476, 1051, 6066, 642, 429, 646, 387, 11691, 304, 279, 1424, 13, 151645], "pred": "Rocks are made of smaller stones and stones are made from rocks. A rock can be described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand, while stones are just small pieces or pebbles that can be carried in the hand.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.162693326435392, "g_worst_claim": 1.2401371002197266, "g_content": 2.9506120681762695, "g_traj_mean": 2.0095465183258057}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [49, 25183, 525, 1865, 315, 9155, 26210, 323, 525, 7481, 438, 264, 3460, 6573, 315, 9798, 429, 374, 5000, 311, 387, 11691, 304, 279, 1424, 11, 1393, 26210, 525, 1101, 2613, 9666, 476, 1051, 6066, 642, 429, 646, 387, 11691, 304, 279, 1424, 13, 151645], "pred": "Rocks are made of smaller stones and are described as a large piece of stone that is difficult to be carried in the hand, while stones are just small pieces or pebbles that can be carried in the hand.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0040410889519586, "g_worst_claim": 1.3974521425035265, "g_content": 3.3519811128315173, "g_traj_mean": 2.0549752712249756}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.54, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "375", "question": "what is dmso used for", "gt": "DMSO, or dimethyl sulfoxide, is used in a variety of ways both industrially and medically. Industrially, it is used as an antifreeze and a solvent for numerous chemicals. Medically, DMSO is applied to the skin as an anti-inflammatory and general pain reliever, most commonly for muscles and joints. It is also used to promote healing for minor cuts, burns, soft tissue damage, local tissue death, and skin ulcers. DMSO has the unique ability to penetrate skin and tissue, allowing it to enter the bloodstream.", "pred": "DMSO, or dimethyl sulfoxide, is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent for various chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation. It is particularly effective for muscle and joint pain relief when applied topically. DMSO has also been used to promote healing, with reports of speeding up recovery from minor cuts, burns, and other soft tissue damage.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "DMSO, or dimethyl sulfoxide, is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent for various chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation. It is particularly effective for muscle and joint pain relief when applied topically. DMSO has also been used to promote healing, with reports of speeding up recovery from minor cuts, burns, and other soft tissue damage.", "cot": "[\"DMSO, or dimethyl sulfoxide, is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent for various chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation. It is particularly effective for muscle and joint pain relief when applied topically. DMSO has also been used to promote healing, with reports of speeding up recovery from minor cuts, burns, and other soft tissue damage.\", \"DMSO, or dimethyl sulfoxide, is used for a wide range of medical applications. It is used for relieving pain, reducing swelling, inflammation, and many more. It has been used successfully for a variety of ailments, including burns, scleroderma, and other conditions. It is also used to promote healing, particularly for minor cuts and burns, and has been shown to speed up recovery.\", \"DMSO, or dimethyl sulfoxide, is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It acts as an anti-inflammatory and is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and treat a variety of medical ailments. It is also used to promote healing and is applied to the skin to treat minor cuts, burns, and other skin ulcers. DMSO has been used to treat soft tissue damage, local tissue death, and burns.\", \"DMSO, or dimethyl sulfoxide, is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and manage inflammation. It has been applied topically on the skin to penetrate skin and tissue and enter the bloodstream. DMSO is also used for promoting healing, including minor cuts, burns, and soft tissue damage. It has been used in several studies for the treatment of skin ulcers and burns. It is an excellent anti-inflammatory and has many uses as a general pain reliever.\"]", "time_sec": 17.515, "generation_time_seconds": 16.659, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8468, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [35, 4826, 46, 11, 476, 5103, 41872, 25774, 15011, 577, 11, 374, 1483, 369, 264, 6884, 2088, 315, 6457, 9895, 13, 1084, 374, 1483, 438, 458, 3196, 333, 27633, 323, 68896, 369, 5257, 25266, 304, 12785, 8357, 13, 758, 15712, 11, 422, 4826, 46, 374, 1483, 311, 47739, 6646, 11, 7949, 54207, 11, 323, 36040, 13, 1084, 374, 7945, 7373, 369, 15747, 323, 10284, 6646, 15957, 979, 9251, 1909, 2673, 13, 422, 4826, 46, 702, 1083,