 used in several studies for the treatment of skin ulcers and burns. It is an excellent anti-inflammatory and has many uses as a general pain reliever.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2071875322705519, "g_worst_claim": 0.49607666333516437, "g_content": 2.1109929292098335, "g_traj_mean": 1.2447998523712158}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.1, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "380", "question": "what is dmso used for", "gt": "Based on the given passages, DMSO is used for various purposes, including:\n\n1. Industrial uses: As an antifreeze and solvent for a wide range of chemicals.\n2. Medical uses: To relieve pain, reduce swelling and inflammation, promote healing, and treat a variety of medical ailments such as burns, scleroderma, and soft tissue damage.\n3. Pain relief: For muscles and joints, and as a general pain reliever applied to the skin.\n4. Skin care: To penetrate skin and tissue and enter the bloodstream.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What is DMSO used for?\" can be summarized as: DMSO is used for various industrial, medical, and personal care purposes, including pain relief, wound healing, and skin care.", "pred": "DMSO is used for a variety of purposes, including industrial applications such as an antifreeze and solvent, and medical uses such as relieving pain, reducing swelling, inflammation, and promoting healing. It has been used for burns, scleroderma, muscles and joints pain relief, and soft tissue damage.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "DMSO is used for a variety of purposes, including industrial applications such as an antifreeze and solvent, and medical uses such as relieving pain, reducing swelling, inflammation, and promoting healing. It has been used for burns, scleroderma, muscles and joints pain relief, and soft tissue damage.", "cot": "[\"DMSO, or dimethyl sulfoxide, is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent for various chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation. It is particularly effective for muscle and joint pain relief when applied topically. DMSO has also been used to promote healing, with reports of speeding up recovery from minor cuts, burns, and other soft tissue damage.\", \"DMSO, or dimethyl sulfoxide, is used for a wide range of purposes. It is used as an antifreeze, a solvent, and has a variety of medical uses. It is particularly effective for reducing pain, reducing swelling, and treating inflammation. It is also used to promote healing and has been shown to be effective in treating soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and burns.\", \"DMSO (Dimethyl Sulfoxide) is used for a variety of medical purposes. It is utilized as an antifreeze, solvent, and has medical applications. It is known for its ability to penetrate skin and tissue, making it effective for relieving pain, reducing swelling, and inflammation. DMSO is commonly used for minor cuts and burns, and has been used in studies for soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and burns. It is also used to promote healing and is effective as an anti-inflammatory.\", \"DMSO is used for a variety of purposes, including industrial applications such as an antifreeze and solvent, and medical uses such as relieving pain, reducing swelling, inflammation, and promoting healing. It has been used for burns, scleroderma, muscles and joints pain relief, and soft tissue damage.\"]", "time_sec": 16.107, "generation_time_seconds": 15.4842, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6173, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [35, 4826, 46, 11, 476, 5103, 41872, 25774, 15011, 577, 11, 374, 1483, 369, 264, 6884, 2088, 315, 6457, 9895, 13, 1084, 374, 1483, 438, 458, 3196, 333, 27633, 323, 68896, 369, 5257, 25266, 304, 12785, 8357, 13, 758, 15712, 11, 422, 4826, 46, 374, 1483, 311, 47739, 6646, 11, 7949, 54207, 11, 323, 36040, 13, 1084, 374, 7945, 7373, 369, 15747, 323, 10284, 6646, 15957, 979, 9251, 1909, 2673, 13, 422, 4826, 46, 702, 1083, 1012, 1483, 311, 11926, 21052, 11, 448, 6682, 315, 57575, 705, 13351, 504, 8922, 15104, 11, 43054, 11, 323, 1008, 8413, 19847, 5557, 13, 151645], "pred": "DMSO, or dimethyl sulfoxide, is used for a wide range of medical purposes. It is used as an antifreeze and solvent for various chemicals in industrial applications. In medicine, DMSO is used to relieve pain, reduce swelling, and inflammation. It is particularly effective for muscle and joint pain relief when applied topically. DMSO has also been used to promote healing, with reports of speeding up recovery from minor cuts, burns, and other soft tissue damage.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1105271914614905, "g_worst_claim": 0.5700844128926595, "g_content": 1.6596253557903011, "g_traj_mean": 1.1022053956985474}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [35, 4826, 46, 11, 476, 5103, 41872, 25774, 15011, 577, 11, 374, 1483, 369, 264, 6884, 2088, 315, 9895, 13, 1084, 374, 1483, 438, 458, 3196, 333, 27633, 11, 264, 68896, 11, 323, 702, 264, 8045, 315, 6457, 5711, 13, 1084, 374, 7945, 7373, 369, 17719, 6646, 11, 17719, 54207, 11, 323, 26625, 36040, 13, 1084, 374, 1083, 1483, 311, 11926, 21052, 323, 702, 1012, 6839, 311, 387, 7373, 304, 26625, 8413, 19847, 5557, 11, 2205, 19847, 4545, 11, 6787, 8557, 16832, 11, 323, 43054, 13, 151645], "pred": "DMSO, or dimethyl sulfoxide, is used for a wide range of purposes. It is used as an antifreeze, a solvent, and has a variety of medical uses. It is particularly effective for reducing pain, reducing swelling, and treating inflammation. It is also used to promote healing and has been shown to be effective in treating soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and burns.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5006227442592082, "g_worst_claim": 0.6599747657775878, "g_content": 1.8682869805230036, "g_traj_mean": 1.0989923477172852}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [35, 4826, 46, 320, 10344, 41872, 45862, 15011, 577, 8, 374, 1483, 369, 264, 8045, 315, 6457, 9895, 13, 1084, 374, 33616, 438, 458, 3196, 333, 27633, 11, 68896, 11, 323, 702, 6457, 8357, 13, 1084, 374, 3881, 369, 1181, 5726, 311, 63755, 6787, 323, 19847, 11, 3259, 432, 7373, 369, 58544, 4405, 6646, 11, 17719, 54207, 11, 323, 36040, 13, 422, 4826, 46, 374, 16626, 1483, 369, 8922, 15104, 323, 43054, 11, 323, 702, 1012, 1483, 304, 7822, 369, 8413, 19847, 5557, 11, 2205, 19847, 4545, 11, 6787, 8557, 16832, 11, 323, 43054, 13, 1084, 374, 1083, 1483, 311, 11926, 21052, 323, 374, 7373, 438, 458, 7147, 66495, 13, 151645], "pred": "DMSO (Dimethyl Sulfoxide) is used for a variety of medical purposes. It is utilized as an antifreeze, solvent, and has medical applications. It is known for its ability to penetrate skin and tissue, making it effective for relieving pain, reducing swelling, and inflammation. DMSO is commonly used for minor cuts and burns, and has been used in studies for soft tissue damage, local tissue death, skin ulcers, and burns. It is also used to promote healing and is effective as an anti-inflammatory.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5686644638024283, "g_worst_claim": 0.5904314120610555, "g_content": 2.3336528431285513, "g_traj_mean": 1.2368234395980835}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [35, 4826, 46, 374, 1483, 369, 264, 8045, 315, 9895, 11, 2670, 12785, 8357, 1741, 438, 458, 3196, 333, 27633, 323, 68896, 11, 323, 6457, 5711, 1741, 438, 58544, 4405, 6646, 11, 17719, 54207, 11, 36040, 11, 323, 22136, 21052, 13, 1084, 702, 1012, 1483, 369, 43054, 11, 56119, 261, 4316, 1728, 11, 23648, 323, 34258, 6646, 15957, 11, 323, 8413, 19847, 5557, 13, 151645], "pred": "DMSO is used for a variety of purposes, including industrial applications such as an antifreeze and solvent, and medical uses such as relieving pain, reducing swelling, inflammation, and promoting healing. It has been used for burns, scleroderma, muscles and joints pain relief, and soft tissue damage.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.170637730288643, "g_worst_claim": 0.5263302326202393, "g_content": 2.148999955919054, "g_traj_mean": 1.3195252418518066}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.28, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "381", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, first click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. Then, switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. Click on the Sort option. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data. Alternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool to sort all worksheets.", "pred": "Note: These steps are applicable to Excel's built-in sorting functionality. If you need to perform more complex sorting tasks or are not familiar with macros, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool for a more efficient and user-friendly experience.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Note: These steps are applicable to Excel's built-in sorting functionality. If you need to perform more complex sorting tasks or are not familiar with macros, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool for a more efficient and user-friendly experience.", "cot": "[\"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select all the data in your worksheet by clicking on the \\\"Select All\\\" button at the intersection of your row and column headings. This will highlight all the cells in your worksheet, confirming that they are selected.\\n\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the \\\"Sort & Filter\\\" group. Click on the \\\"Sort\\\" option.\\n\\n3. Click on the \\\"Sort By\\\" drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n\\n4. After selecting the column, click on the \\\"OK\\\" button. The data should now be sorted alphabetically.\\n\\nAlternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool, which can sort all worksheets easily. Kutools for Excel includes more than 120 handy Excel tools and is free to try with no limitation in 30 days.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, one can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool, which can easily sort all worksheets. Alternatively, one can use the built-in Sort feature in Excel. First, click on the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen. Then click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu. In the Sort window, select the data that you wish to sort by. For example, to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z), select the Product column and click on the OK button. The data should now be sorted alphabetically when you return to the spreadsheet.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Click on the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\\n2. Click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu.\\n3. When the Sort window appears, select the data that you wish to sort by. For example, in this case, the Product column (column B) is selected for sorting in alphabetical order.\\n4. Click on the OK button. Now, the data should be sorted alphabetically.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Open your Excel file.\\n2. Click on the Data tab at the top of the screen.\\n3. In the Sort & Filter group, click on the Sort button.\\n4. In the Sort window, select the data that you wish to sort by, in this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B).\\n5. Choose the sorting order, in this case, Alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n6. Click on the OK button.\\n7. The data will now be sorted alphabetically.\\n\\nNote: These steps are applicable to Excel's built-in sorting functionality. If you need to perform more complex sorting tasks or are not familiar with macros, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool for a more efficient and user-friendly experience.\"]", "time_sec": 24.929, "generation_time_seconds": 24.1871, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7369, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 678, 279, 821, 304, 697, 36636, 553, 18458, 389, 279, 330, 3379, 2009, 1, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 1096, 686, 11167, 678, 279, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 11, 48996, 429, 807, 525, 4091, 382, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 330, 10231, 609, 12339, 1, 1874, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 330, 10231, 1, 2999, 382, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 330, 10231, 3216, 1, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 13, 576, 5036, 7866, 311, 279, 69452, 31969, 304, 279, 1156, 2802, 315, 697, 821, 13, 758, 419, 3110, 11, 582, 1366, 311, 3378, 553, 279, 5643, 3250, 320, 6229, 425, 8, 304, 83298, 1973, 320, 32, 311, 1863, 3593, 19, 13, 4636, 26301, 279, 3250, 11, 4205, 389, 279, 330, 3925, 1, 3137, 13, 576, 821, 1265, 1431, 387, 10615, 27790, 2673, 382, 92014, 11, 498, 646, 990, 730, 1535, 3069, 369, 21029, 594, 15967, 60472, 5392, 11, 892, 646, 3378, 678, 67525, 6707, 13, 730, 1535, 3069, 369, 21029, 5646, 803, 1091, 220, 16, 17, 15, 25163, 21029, 7375, 323, 374, 1910, 311, 1430, 448, 902, 20278, 304, 220, 18, 15, 2849, 13, 151645], "pred": "Alternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool, which can sort all worksheets easily. Kutools for Excel includes more than 120 handy Excel tools and is free to try with no limitation in 30 days.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3605525751864607, "g_worst_claim": 0.0076108090579509735, "g_content": 2.013273669827369, "g_traj_mean": 1.3863354921340942}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 825, 64