, 1973, 624, 19, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 10402, 3137, 13, 4695, 11, 279, 821, 1265, 387, 10615, 27790, 2673, 13, 151645], "pred": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Click on the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\n2. Click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu.\n3. When the Sort window appears, select the data that you wish to sort by. For example, in this case, the Product column (column B) is selected for sorting in alphabetical order.\n4. Click on the OK button. Now, the data should be sorted alphabetically.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1944597320066364, "g_worst_claim": 0.005428151786327362, "g_content": 1.2628413836161296, "g_traj_mean": 1.0921661853790283}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 697, 21029, 1034, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 2885, 5651, 518, 279, 1909, 315, 279, 4171, 624, 18, 13, 758, 279, 15967, 609, 12339, 1874, 11, 4205, 389, 279, 15967, 3137, 624, 19, 13, 758, 279, 15967, 3241, 11, 3293, 279, 821, 429, 498, 6426, 311, 3378, 553, 11, 304, 419, 3110, 11, 582, 1366, 311, 3378, 553, 279, 5643, 3250, 320, 6229, 425, 4292, 20, 13, 22201, 279, 28273, 1973, 11, 304, 419, 1142, 11, 62797, 938, 1973, 320, 32, 311, 1863, 4292, 21, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 10402, 3137, 624, 22, 13, 576, 821, 686, 1431, 387, 10615, 27790, 2673, 382, 9112, 25, 4220, 7354, 525, 8415, 311, 21029, 594, 5798, 3419, 28273, 14944, 13, 1416, 498, 1184, 311, 2736, 803, 6351, 28273, 9079, 476, 525, 537, 11285, 448, 37714, 11, 498, 646, 990, 730, 1535, 3069, 369, 21029, 594, 15967, 60472, 5392, 369, 264, 803, 11050, 323, 1196, 21896, 3139, 13, 151645], "pred": "Note: These steps are applicable to Excel's built-in sorting functionality. If you need to perform more complex sorting tasks or are not familiar with macros, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool for a more efficient and user-friendly experience.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6230085467387523, "g_worst_claim": -0.2320341169834137, "g_content": 1.0326421167943385, "g_traj_mean": 0.7326456308364868}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 19.28, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "382", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "Passage 3 provides the necessary information to answer the question. To arrange an excel sheet alphabetically, click on the Select All button, switch to the Data tab, locate the Sort & Filter group, click on the Sort option, and then select the desired column to sort by.", "pred": "These steps provide a clear and effective way to sort data in an Excel sheet alphabetically, using the built-in features of the software.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "These steps provide a clear and effective way to sort data in an Excel sheet alphabetically, using the built-in features of the software.", "cot": "[\"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select all the data in your worksheet by clicking on the \\\"Select All\\\" button at the intersection of your row and column headings. This will highlight all the cells in your worksheet, confirming that they are selected.\\n\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the \\\"Sort & Filter\\\" group. Click on the \\\"Sort\\\" option.\\n\\n3. Click on the \\\"Sort By\\\" drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n\\n4. After selecting the column, click on the \\\"OK\\\" button. The data should now be sorted alphabetically.\\n\\nAlternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool, which can sort all worksheets easily. Kutools for Excel includes more than 120 handy Excel tools and is free to try with no limitation in 30 days.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet will highlight to confirm they're selected.\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. Click on the Sort option.\\n3. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n4. In the Sort window, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n5. Click on the OK button. Now, when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted alphabetically.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can use the Sort tool in Microsoft Excel. First, select the entire data set by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. This will highlight all cells in your worksheet, confirming that they are selected. Then, switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. Click on the Sort option to open the Sort window. In the Sort window, select the column by name that you want to sort by. For example, if you want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order, you would select column B from the drop-down menu. Finally, click on the OK button to sort the data. The data should now be arranged in alphabetical order.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Click on the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\\n2. Click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu.\\n3. In the Sort window, select the column you wish to sort by. For example, if you want to sort by the Product column (column B), select it.\\n4. Choose the sorting order you prefer. In this case, select to sort in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n5. Click on the OK button to apply the sorting.\\n6. When you return to the spreadsheet, the data should now be sorted alphabetically.\\n\\nThese steps provide a clear and effective way to sort data in an Excel sheet alphabetically, using the built-in features of the software.\"]", "time_sec": 27.579, "generation_time_seconds": 26.6211, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9507, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 678, 279, 821, 304, 697, 36636, 553, 18458, 389, 279, 330, 3379, 2009, 1, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 1096, 686, 11167, 678, 279, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 11, 48996, 429, 807, 525, 4091, 382, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 330, 10231, 609, 12339, 1, 1874, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 330, 10231, 1, 2999, 382, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 330, 10231, 3216, 1, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 13, 576, 5036, 7866, 311, 279, 69452, 31969, 304, 279, 1156, 2802, 315, 697, 821, 13, 758, 419, 3110, 11, 582, 1366, 311, 3378, 553, 279, 5643, 3250, 320, 6229, 425, 8, 304, 83298, 1973, 320, 32, 311, 1863, 3593, 19, 13, 4636, 26301, 279, 3250, 11, 4205, 389, 279, 330, 3925, 1, 3137, 13, 576, 821, 1265, 1431, 387, 10615, 27790, 2673, 382, 92014, 11, 498, 646, 990, 730, 1535, 3069, 369, 21029, 594, 15967, 60472, 5392, 11, 892, 646, 3378, 678, 67525, 6707, 13, 730, 1535, 3069, 369, 21029, 5646, 803, 1091, 220, 16, 17, 15, 25163, 21029, 7375, 323, 374, 1910, 311, 1430, 448, 902, 20278, 304, 220, 18, 15, 2849, 13, 151645], "pred": "Alternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool, which can sort all worksheets easily. Kutools for Excel includes more than 120 handy Excel tools and is free to try with no limitation in 30 days.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3848293710047366, "g_worst_claim": 0.11188759803771972, "g_content": 2.0408103696761595, "g_traj_mean": 1.4108169078826904}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 8