{"id": "383", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "To arrange an excel sheet alphabetical, one can follow these steps:\n\n1. Select the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\n2. Click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu.\n3. When the Sort window appears, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\n4. Click on the OK button.\n5. The data should now be sorted in alphabetical order.", "pred": "Note: If you prefer not to use macros or prefer another way, you can try Kutools for Excel, which includes more than 120 handy Excel tools and provides a Sort Sheets tool that can sort all worksheets easily. It is free to try with no limitation for 30 days.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Note: If you prefer not to use macros or prefer another way, you can try Kutools for Excel, which includes more than 120 handy Excel tools and provides a Sort Sheets tool that can sort all worksheets easily. It is free to try with no limitation for 30 days.", "cot": "[\"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select all the data in your worksheet by clicking on the \\\"Select All\\\" button at the intersection of your row and column headings. This will highlight all the cells in your worksheet, confirming that they are selected.\\n\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the \\\"Sort & Filter\\\" group. Click on the \\\"Sort\\\" option.\\n\\n3. Click on the \\\"Sort By\\\" drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n\\n4. After selecting the column, click on the \\\"OK\\\" button. The data should now be sorted alphabetically.\\n\\nAlternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool, which can sort all worksheets easily. Kutools for Excel includes more than 120 handy Excel tools and is free to try with no limitation in 30 days.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps:\\n1. Click on the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\\n2. Click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu.\\n3. In the Sort window, select the data that you wish to sort by. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n4. Click on the OK button.\\nBy following these steps, the data in the selected column will be arranged in alphabetical order.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select the entire data in your worksheet by clicking on the \\\"Select All\\\" button at the intersection of your row and column headings. This will highlight all the cells in your worksheet.\\n2. Switch to the \\\"Data\\\" tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the \\\"Sort & Filter\\\" group. Click on the \\\"Sort\\\" option.\\n3. In the \\\"Sort\\\" menu, click on the \\\"Sort By\\\" drop-down menu and select a column by name. This will allow you to choose the column you want to sort by.\\n4. After selecting the column, choose the sorting order (A to Z for ascending, Z to A for descending) to sort your data alphabetically. Click on the \\\"OK\\\" button to apply the changes. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted alphabetically.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Click on the \\\"Data\\\" tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\\n2. Click on the \\\"Sort\\\" button and select \\\"Custom Sort\\\" from the popup menu.\\n3. When the \\\"Sort\\\" window appears, select the data that you wish to sort by.\\n4. In this example, to sort by the \\\"Product\\\" column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z), select the \\\"Product\\\" column.\\n5. Click on the \\\"OK\\\" button.\\n6. Now when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted alphabetically.\\n\\nNote: If you prefer not to use macros or prefer another way, you can try Kutools for Excel, which includes more than 120 handy Excel tools and provides a Sort Sheets tool that can sort all worksheets easily. It is free to try with no limitation for 30 days.\"]", "time_sec": 26.995, "generation_time_seconds": 26.2204, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7685, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 678, 279, 821, 304, 697, 36636, 553, 18458, 389, 279, 330, 3379, 2009, 1, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 1096, 686, 11167, 678, 279, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 11, 48996, 429, 807, 525, 4091, 382, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 330, 10231, 609, 12339, 1, 1874, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 330, 10231, 1, 2999, 382, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 330, 10231, 3216, 1, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 13, 576, 5036, 7866, 311, 279, 69452, 31969, 304, 279, 1156, 2802, 315, 697, 821, 13, 758, 419, 3110, 11, 582, 1366, 311, 3378, 553, 279, 5643, 3250, 320, 6229, 425, 8, 304, 83298, 1973, 320, 32, 311, 1863, 3593, 19, 13, 4636, 26301, 279, 3250, 11, 4205, 389, 279, 330, 3925, 1, 3137, 13, 576, 821, 1265, 1431, 387, 10615, 27790, 2673, 382, 92014, 11, 498, 646, 990, 730, 1535, 3069, 369, 21029, 594, 15967, 60472, 5392, 11, 892, 646, 3378, 678, 67525, 6707, 13, 730, 1535, 3069, 369, 21029, 5646, 803, 1091, 220, 16, 17, 15, 25163, 21029, 7375, 323, 374, 1910, 311, 1430, 448, 902, 20278, 304, 220, 18, 15, 2849, 13, 151645], "pred": "Alternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool, which can sort all worksheets easily. Kutools for Excel includes more than 