{"id": "384", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically:\n\nPassage 1 suggests using Kutools for Excel, which provides a Sort Sheets tool to easily sort all worksheets in alphabetical order. However, if you prefer not to use macros or Kutools, Passage 2 provides an alternative method using the built-in Sort feature in Excel.\n\nTo sort an Excel sheet alphabetically using the built-in Sort feature, follow these steps:\n\n1. Select the data you wish to sort by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu and select the column you wish to sort by (e.g., Product column in alphabetical order - A to Z).\n5. Click OK.\n\nOnce you have completed these steps, the data in your Excel sheet will be sorted alphabetically.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide sufficient information to clarify how to arrange an Excel sheet numerically.", "pred": "Alternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool, which can sort all worksheets easily. Kutools for Excel includes more than 120 handy Excel tools and is free to try with no limitation in 30 days.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Alternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool, which can sort all worksheets easily. Kutools for Excel includes more than 120 handy Excel tools and is free to try with no limitation in 30 days.", "cot": "[\"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select all the data in your worksheet by clicking on the \\\"Select All\\\" button at the intersection of your row and column headings. This will highlight all the cells in your worksheet, confirming that they are selected.\\n\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the \\\"Sort & Filter\\\" group. Click on the \\\"Sort\\\" option.\\n\\n3. Click on the \\\"Sort By\\\" drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n\\n4. After selecting the column, click on the \\\"OK\\\" button. The data should now be sorted alphabetically.\\n\\nAlternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool, which can sort all worksheets easily. Kutools for Excel includes more than 120 handy Excel tools and is free to try with no limitation in 30 days.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. This will highlight all the cells in your worksheet.\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\\n3. Click on the Sort option.\\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n5. Click on the OK button.\\n6. After completing these steps, the data in the selected column will be sorted alphabetically when you return to the spreadsheet.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet highlight to confirm they're selected.\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\\n3. Click on the Sort option.\\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n\\nOnce you have selected the column by name and clicked on it, a drop-down menu will appear. Choose the option that arranges the data in alphabetical order (A to Z) or the other way around (Z to A) based on your preference.\\n\\nAfter selecting the sorting option, click on the OK button to apply the changes. When you return to the spreadsheet, the data should now be sorted in the chosen alphabetical order.\\n\\nIf you prefer to use Kutools for Excel, you can use its Sort Sheets tool to easily sort all worksheets. Kutools for Excel includes more than 120 handy Excel tools and can be free to try for 30 days with no limitations.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Click on the \\\"Data\\\" tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\\n2. Select the data you want to sort by clicking on the \\\"Sort\\\" button.\\n3. In the \\\"Sort\\\" window, choose the column you want to sort by (for example, column B for the Product column).\\n4. Select the sorting order (in this case, alphabetical order, A to Z).\\n5. Click the \\\"OK\\\" button to complete the sorting process.\\n\\nNow, when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be arranged alphabetically.\"]", "time_sec": 27.862, "generation_time_seconds": 27.0953, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7604, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 678, 279, 821, 304, 697, 36636, 553, 18458, 389, 279, 330, 3379, 2009, 1, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 1096, 686, 11167, 678, 279, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 11, 48996, 429, 807, 525, 4091, 382, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 330, 10231, 609, 12339, 1, 1874, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 330, 10231, 1, 2999, 382, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 330, 10231, 3216, 1, 5943, 14875, 5022, 311, 3293, 264, 3250, 553, 829, 13, 576, 5036, 7866, 311, 279, 69452, 31969, 304, 279, 1156, 2802, 315, 6