{"id": "385", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically:\n\nPassage 2:\n\n1. Select the Data tab from the toolbar at the top of the screen.\n2. Click on the Sort button and select Custom Sort from the popup menu.\n3. Select the data that you wish to sort by (in this case, the Product column (column B)) and choose alphabetical order (A to Z).\n4. Click on the OK button.\n\nPassage 3:\n\n1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings to select all the cells in the worksheet.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\n\nTherefore, to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can use either method described above.", "pred": "In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z). Click on the OK button. Now, when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z). Click on the OK button. Now, when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.", "cot": "[\"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select all the data in your worksheet by clicking on the \\\"Select All\\\" button at the intersection of your row and column headings. This will highlight all the cells in your worksheet, confirming that they are selected.\\n\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the \\\"Sort & Filter\\\" group. Click on the \\\"Sort\\\" option.\\n\\n3. Click on the \\\"Sort By\\\" drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data. In this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z).\\n\\n4. After selecting the column, click on the \\\"OK\\\" button. The data should now be sorted alphabetically.\\n\\nAlternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool, which can sort all worksheets easily. Kutools for Excel includes more than 120 handy Excel tools and is free to try with no limitation in 30 days.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select all the cells in your worksheet by clicking on the \\\"Select All\\\" button at the intersection of your row and column headings. This will highlight all the cells in your data.\\n\\n2. Switch to the \\\"Data\\\" tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon. In the \\\"Sort & Filter\\\" group, click on the \\\"Sort\\\" option. This will open the \\\"Sort\\\" window.\\n\\n3. In the \\\"Sort\\\" window, click on the \\\"Sort By\\\" drop-down menu. Select the column by name that you want to sort by. For example, if you want to sort by the \\\"Product\\\" column (column B), select it from the drop-down menu.\\n\\n4. After selecting the column, click on the \\\"OK\\\" button. The data in your Excel sheet will now be sorted alphabetically based on the selected column.\\n\\nThis method allows you to sort your data by any column, and it will be sorted in ascending order (A to Z). If you want to sort in descending order (Z to A), you can check the \\\"Z to A\\\" checkbox in the \\\"Sort\\\" window before clicking \\\"OK\\\".\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, you can follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Select the Data tab**: At the top of the screen, click on the \\\"Data\\\" tab within the Excel toolbar. This tab provides various options related to data manipulation.\\n\\n2. **Locate and Click Sort**: Within the Data tab, find the \\\"Sort & Filter\\\" group. Click on the \\\"Sort\\\" button to bring up the sorting options.\\n\\n3. **Choose the Column to Sort By**: A dropdown menu will appear under the \\\"Sort By\\\" option. Here, select the column you wish to sort alphabetically. For instance, if you want to sort by the Product column, which is represented by column B, choose this column from the dropdown list.\\n\\n4. **Click OK**: After selecting the column, click the \\\"OK\\\" button to apply the sorting. The data in your Excel sheet will now be arranged alphabetically based on the selected column.\\n\\nThis process allows you to easily organize your data in Excel, making it easier to find and work with specific entries.\", \"To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. The cells in your worksheet will highlight to confirm they're selected.\\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. Click on the Sort option.\\n3. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data.\\n\\nIn this example, we want to sort by the Product column (column B) in alphabetical order (A to Z). Click on the OK button. Now, when you return to the spreadsheet, the data should be sorted.\"]", "time_sec": 30.214, "generation_time_seconds": 29.4083, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7976, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 30893, 458, 21029, 10834, 27790, 2673, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 678, 279, 821, 304, 697, 36636, 553, 18458, 389, 279, 330, 3379, 2009, 1, 3137, 518, 279, 19246, 315, 697, 2802, 323, 3250, 69452, 13, 1096, 686, 11167, 678, 279, 7761, 304, 697, 36636, 11, 48996, 429, 807, 525, 4091, 382, 17, 13, 15586, 311, 279, 2885, 5651, 304, 279, 5100, 21029, 44567, 323, 24523, 279, 330, 10231, 609, 12339, 1, 1874, 13, 9189, 389,