{"id": "395", "question": "why should we serve others", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"Why should we serve others?\"\n\nWe should serve others because it is a way to show love and kindness to everyone, even those who may not treat us well. Serving others is an expression of our love for God and our desire to be like Him. When we truly know God, our natural response is a desire to love and serve Him in return, and serving others is a way to do so. Additionally, serving others without self-serving motives and expecting nothing in return allows us to serve out of love and build stronger character muscles.\n\nTherefore, serving others is not only a way to show love and kindness, but it is also a way to deepen our relationship with God and grow in our faith.", "pred": "We should serve others because it is a part of the Christian life, which is one of service to others. We should use every opportunity to serve others, even if it means going the extra mile. Serving others can help them in ways that they appreciate and find useful.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "We should serve others because it is a part of the Christian life, which is one of service to others. We should use every opportunity to serve others, even if it means going the extra mile. Serving others can help them in ways that they appreciate and find useful.", "cot": "[\"We should serve others because it is a part of the Christian life, which is one of service to others. We should use every opportunity to serve others, even if it means going the extra mile. Serving others can help them in ways that they appreciate and find useful.\", \"We should serve others because we are called to love and serve God, which is a central tenet of the Christian life. Love your neighbour as yourself (Matthew 22:39). The Christian life is one of service to others, where we show love and kindness to everyone, even to those who do not treat us well. We can serve others in many ways, and we should ensure that we use every opportunity that we can. We should serve God because we know Him; an inherent part of knowing Him is a desire to serve Him. It's always been God's intention to make us like His Son, Jesus (Romans 8:29).\", \"Based on the information provided in the passages, we should serve others as a reflection of our love for God. Serving others with the intention of pleasing God is a way to demonstrate our commitment to following His teachings and to build and strengthen our character muscles.\", \"Based on the information provided in the given passages, we should serve others because it aligns with the Christian life of service and love, as taught in Matthew 22:39. By serving others, we demonstrate love and kindness, even to those who do not treat us well. We can serve others in various ways and should take every opportunity to do so. The spirit of service should be evident in all aspects of our work, such as providing a \\\"Second Mile Service\\\" by going the extra mile for our customers and employers.\\n\\nFurthermore, serving others is a way to serve God, as the Bible makes clear that when a person is in a real relationship with God, they will serve Him. This is because knowing God, who is love (1 John 4:8), leads to a natural desire to love and serve Him in return. To truly serve others, we must do so out of love with no stipulations or expectations of anything in return, as this leads to greater rewards than serving others with self-serving motives.\"]", "time_sec": 19.92, "generation_time_seconds": 18.7847, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1282, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1654, 1265, 8683, 3800, 1576, 432, 374, 264, 949, 315, 279, 8876, 2272, 11, 892, 374, 825, 315, 2473, 311, 3800, 13, 1205, 1265, 990, 1449, 6638, 311, 8683, 3800, 11, 1496, 421, 432, 3363, 2087, 279, 4960, 14587, 13, 71643, 3800, 646, 1492, 1105, 304, 5510, 429, 807, 15401, 323, 1477, 5390, 13, 151645], "pred": "We should serve others because it is a part of the Christian life, which is one of service to others. We should use every opportunity to serve others, even if it means going the extra mile. Serving others can help them in ways that they appreciate and find useful.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7281724975222634, "g_worst_claim": 1.063693682352702, "g_content": 2.7101235961914063, "g_traj_mean": 1.7179573774337769}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1654, 1265, 8683, 3800, 1576, 582, 525, 2598, 311, 2948, 323, 8683, 4264, 11, 892, 374, 264, 8622, 5779, 295, 315, 279, 8876, 2272, 13, 10689, 697, 21922, 438, 6133, 320, 49888, 220, 17, 17, 25, 18, 24, 568, 576, 8876, 2272, 374, 825, 315, 2473, 311, 3800, 11, 1380, 582, 1473, 2948, 323, 44872, 311, 5019, 11, 1496, 311, 1846, 879, 653, 537, 4228, 601, 1632, 13, 1205, 646, 8683, 3800, 304, 1657, 5510, 11, 323, 582, 1265, 5978, 429, 582, 990, 1449, 6638, 429, 582, 646, 13, 1205, 1265, 8683, 4264, 1576, 582, 1414, 20426, 26, 458, 36988, 949, 315, 14063, 20426, 374, 264, 12591, 311, 8683, 20426, 13, 1084, 594, 2677, 1012, 4264, 594, 14602, 311, 1281, 601, 1075, 5301, 11840, 11, 10588, 320, 44359, 596, 220, 23, 25, 17, 24, 568, 151645], "pred": "We should serve others because we are called to love and serve God, which is a central tenet of the Christian life. Love your neighbour as yourself (Matthew 22:39). The Christian life is one of service to others, where we show love and kindness to everyone, even to those who do not treat us well. We can serve others in many ways, and we should ensure that we use every opportunity that we can. We should serve God because we know Him; an inherent part of knowing Him is a desire to serve Him. It's always been God's intention to make us like His Son, Jesus (Romans 8:29).", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6408057129530407, "g_worst_claim": 0.6633820056915283, "g_content": 2.0684736719671286, "g_traj_mean": 1.662695288658142}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 1995, 3897, 304, 279, 46769, 11, 582, 1265, 8683, 3800, 438, 264, 21844, 315, 1039, 2948, 369, 4264, 13, 71643, 3800, 448, 279, 14602, 315, 53699, 4264, 374, 264, 1616, 311, 19869, 1039, 15155, 311, 2701, 5301, 44472, 323, 311, 1936, 323, 19681, 1039, 3668, 23648, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the information provided in the passages, we should serve others as a reflection of our love for God. Serving others with the intention of pleasing God is a way to demonstrate our commitment to following His teachings and to build and strengthen our character muscles.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8816158098081869, "g_worst_claim": 0.37270209524366593, "g_content": 1.5222738514775815, "g_traj_mean": 0.9429753422737122}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 1995, 3897, 304, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 582, 1265, 8683, 3800, 1576, 432, 5285, 82, 448, 279, 8876, 2272, 315, 2473, 323, 2948, 11, 438, 15599, 304, 18939, 220, 17, 17, 25, 18, 24, 13, 3216, 13480, 3800, 11, 582, 19869, 2948, 323, 44872, 11, 1496, 311, 1846, 879, 653, 537, 4228, 601, 1632, 13, 1205, 646, 8683, 3800, 304, 5257, 5510, 323, 1265, 1896, 1449, 6638, 311, 653, 773, 13, 576, 8913, 315, 2473, 1265, 387, 29476, 304, 678, 13566, 315, 1039, 975, 11, 1741, 438, 8241, 264, 330, 15666, 38597, 5362, 1, 553, 2087, 279, 4960, 14587, 369, 1039, 6310, 323, 22426, 382, 56317, 11, 13480, 3800, 374, 264, 1616, 311, 8683, 4264, 11, 438, 279, 16947, 3643, 2797, 429, 979, 264, 1697, 374, 304, 264, 1931, 5025, 448, 4264, 11, 807, 686, 8683, 20426, 13, 1096, 374, 1576, 14063, 4264, 11, 879, 374, 2948, 320, 16, 3757, 220, 19, 25, 23, 701, 11508, 311, 264, 5810, 12591, 311, 2948, 323, 8683, 20426, 304, 470, 13, 2014, 9428, 8683, 3800, 11, 582, 1969, 653, 773, 700, 315, 2948, 448, 902, 42673, 7455, 476, 16665, 315, 4113, 304, 470, 11, 438, 419, 11508, 311, 7046, 21160, 1091, 13480, 3800, 448, 656, 85986, 51040, 13, 151645], "pred": "Furthermore, serving others is a way to serve God, as the Bible makes clear that when a person is in a real relationship with God, they will serve Him. This is because knowing God, who is love (1 John 4:8), leads to a natural desire to love and serve Him in return. To truly serve others, we must do so out of love with no stipulations or expectations of anything in return, as this leads to greater rewards than serving others with self-serving motives.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3348704737069923, "g_worst_claim": 0.2739940583705902, "g_content": 1.9747868680405891, "g_traj_mean": 1.453057885169983}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 19.35, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 4.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "399", "question": "temperature bucharest", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the current temperature in Bucharest, Romania is:\n\nPassage 1 does not provide real-time weather data, so I cannot find the current temperature in Bucharest.\n\nPassage 2 provides a map of UK weather warnings and flood warnings, but it does not provide information on the temperature in Bucharest.\n\nPassage 3 provides general information about the climate in Bucharest, including the average monthly weather patterns, but it does not provide the current temperature. Therefore, I am unable to answer your question based on these passages.", "pred": "Bucharest has a humid continental climate, and the temperatures can vary significantly throughout the year. In winter, temperatures can drop below freezing, sometimes reaching as low as minus 20 °C (4 °F). During the summer months of July and August, the average temperature is around 23 °C (73 °F), but it can rise to as high as 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F) in mid-summer.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Bucharest has a humid continental climate, and the temperatures can vary significantly throughout the year. In winter, temperatures can drop below freezing, sometimes reaching as low as minus 20 °C (4 °F). During the summer months of July and August, the average temperature is around 23 °C (73 °F), but it can rise to as high as 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F) in mid-summer.", "cot": "[\"Bucharest has a humid continental climate. Winters can get windy and temperatures often dip below 0 °Celsius (32 °Fahrenheit), sometimes even dropping to minus 20 °C (4 °F). In summer (July and August), the average temperature is around 23 °C (73 °F). Temperatures often reach 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F) in mid-summer.\", \"The average temperature in Bucharest, Romania, has a range of 23 °C (73 °F) in the summer months of July and August. It often dips below freezing during the winter, sometimes even reaching minus 20 °C (4 °F).\", \"Bucharest has a humid continental climate, and the temperatures can vary significantly throughout the year. In winter, temperatures can drop below freezing, sometimes reaching as low as minus 20 °C (4 °F). During the summer months of July and August, the average temperature is around 23 °C (73 °F), but it can rise to as high as 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F) in mid-summer.\", \"The average temperature in Bucharest, Romania, is around 23 °C (73 °F) in summer (July and August). Temperatures can reach up to 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F) in mid-summer. Winters can get windy, and temperatures often dip below 0 °Celsius (32 °Fahrenheit), sometimes even dropping to minus 20 °C (4 °F).\"]", "time_sec": 17.232, "generation_time_seconds": 16.5947, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6298, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [33, 1387, 15432, 702, 264, 65938, 57536, 9977, 13, 467, 49940, 646, 633, 92921, 323, 19879, 3545, 23604, 3685, 220, 15, 36286, 34, 40247, 320, 18, 17, 36286, 37, 47910, 701, 7025, 1496, 25100, 311, 27283, 220, 17, 15, 36286, 34, 320, 19, 36286, 37, 568, 758, 7324, 320, 28427, 323, 6156, 701, 279, 5461, 9315, 374, 2163, 220, 17, 18, 36286, 34, 320, 22, 18, 36286, 37, 568, 74683, 2789, 3545, 5545, 220, 18, 20, 36286, 34, 320, 24, 20, 36286, 37, 8, 311, 220, 19, 15, 36286, 34, 320, 16, 15, 19, 36286, 37, 8, 304, 5099, 12, 62566, 13, 151645], "pred": "Bucharest has a humid continental climate. Winters can get windy and temperatures often dip below 0 °Celsius (32 °Fahrenheit), sometimes even dropping to minus 20 °C (4 °F). In summer (July and August), the average temperature is around 23 °C (73 °F). Temperatures often reach 35 °C (95 °F) to 40 °C (104 °F) in mid-summer.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5941803044972367, "g_worst_claim": 0.5558985471725464, "g_content": 1.786798604329427, "g_traj_mean": 1.4428958892822266}}, 