{"id": "401", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "To remove the door panel on a 2006 Chevy, first remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup and one in the middle of the inside door handle. Additionally, there's a pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place which needs to be removed. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off. Ensure to remove all screws and clips in the door panel and gently pull the panel away from the frame. Finally, remove any wiring connections and the panel will come off the frame.", "pred": "To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin that holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door. An instructional video has also been enclosed below that shows this entire process and where everything's located.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin that holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door. An instructional video has also been enclosed below that shows this entire process and where everything's located.", "cot": "[\"To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin that holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.\", \"2006 Chevy Impala owners can remove the door panel by removing the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, the one in the middle of the inside door handle, and the pin on the outer edge of the door. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the panel off, and use a screwdriver to remove all screws and clips in the panel.\", \"To remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevrolet HHR, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Locate and Remove Screws and Pins**:\\n   - Remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup.\\n   - Locate and remove the screw in the middle of the inside door handle.\\n   - Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\\n\\n2. **Use a Door Panel Removal Tool**:\\n   - Pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door using a door panel removal tool.\\n\\n3. **Remove Screws and Clips**:\\n   - Use a screwdriver to remove all screws and clips in the door panel.\\n   - Gently pull the panel away from the frame.\\n\\n4. **Disconnect Wiring**:\\n   - Remove any wiring connections to ensure there are no electrical issues during removal.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can safely remove the door panel from your 2006 Chevrolet HHR.\", \"To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin that holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door. An instructional video has also been enclosed below that shows this entire process and where everything's located.\"]", "time_sec": 20.711, "generation_time_seconds": 19.7263, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9743, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4057, 279, 14