 to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.\", \"To remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevrolet HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin that holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.\", \"To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin that holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.\"]", "time_sec": 17.704, "generation_time_seconds": 16.6965, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9991, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 4057, 279, 14639, 6006, 6945, 304, 697, 57298, 472, 17088, 11, 498, 686, 1184, 311, 4057, 279, 1378, 44922, 7407, 4766, 315, 279, 6006, 6815, 10525, 11, 323, 1052, 594, 1083, 825, 304, 279, 6149, 315, 279, 4766, 6006, 3705, 13, 1913, 279, 15955, 6821, 315, 279, 6006, 1052, 594, 1083, 264, 8983, 429, 9982, 279, 6945, 304, 1992, 11, 498, 686, 1184, 311, 4057, 429, 13, 5005, 990, 264, 6006, 6945, 16652, 5392, 311, 81279, 279, 6006, 6945, 1007, 315, 279, 472, 17088, 14639, 6006, 13, 151645], "pred": "To remove the rear door panel in your Chevy HHR, you will need to remove the two screws located inside of the door pull cup, and there's also one in the middle of the inside door handle. On the outer edge of the door there's also a pin that holds the panel in place, you will need to remove that. Then use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.135217259561