es": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1501085891887532, "g_worst_claim": 1.1457945959908622, "g_content": 2.8950729370117188, "g_traj_mean": 2.225297451019287}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.15, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "408", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "gt": "To make panko crumbs, preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C). Push torn pieces or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 degrees F for 6 to 8 minutes, shaking the sheet twice during baking. Remove from the oven and cool completely.", "pred": "Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. Place all of the ingredients into a blender carafe, cover and pulse until coarse crumbs form, about 2 minutes. Spread the crumbs evenly on 2 half sheet pans and bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes.Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes, and then transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks. Recipe courtesy of Alton Brown, 2011.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. Place all of the ingredients into a blender carafe, cover and pulse until coarse crumbs form, about 2 minutes. Spread the crumbs evenly on 2 half sheet pans and bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes.Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes, and then transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks. Recipe courtesy of Alton Brown, 2011.", "cot": "[\"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 F degrees until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n4. Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n5. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\\n\\nThese steps will result in panko crumbs that are dry but not toasted, suitable for various culinary uses.\", \"Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. Place all of the ingredients into a blender carafe, cover and pulse until coarse crumbs form, about 2 minutes. Spread the crumbs evenly on 2 half sheet pans and bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes.Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes, and then transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks. Recipe courtesy of Alton Brown, 2011.\", \"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\\n2. Push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n6. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and allow the crumbs to cool completely.\\n\\nThese steps ensure that the bread is turned into coarse crumbs that are ready for use in various recipes.\", \"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees Fahrenheit (150 degrees Celsius).\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to create coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake the crumbs in the preheated oven until they are dry but not toasted, which usually takes about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n5. Shake the baking sheet twice during the baking process to ensure even drying.\\n6. Remove the crumbs from the oven and allow them to cool completely.\\n\\nThese steps should result in panko crumbs that are perfect for coating or breading foods.\"]", "time_sec": 22.548, "generation_time_seconds": 21.763, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7749, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 281, 92852, 96577, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 2