p to 2 weeks. Recipe courtesy of Alton Brown, 2011.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.749656122795005, "g_worst_claim": 0.4882634026663644, "g_content": 1.9549636840820312, "g_traj_mean": 1.5879210233688354}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 281, 92852, 96577, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 22950, 21145, 9666, 315, 16002, 1526, 279, 52362, 287, 13364, 315, 264, 3607, 17654, 311, 1281, 49247, 96577, 624, 18, 13, 47716, 279, 96577, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 624, 19, 13, 52074, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 279, 96577, 525, 9058, 714, 537, 92872, 11, 369, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 72323, 279, 27815, 10834, 10917, 2337, 27815, 311, 5978, 1496, 45379, 624, 21, 13, 10783, 279, 27815, 10834, 504, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 96577, 311, 7010, 6587, 382, 9485, 7354, 5978, 429, 279, 16002, 374, 6519, 1119, 49247, 96577, 429, 525, 5527, 369, 990, 304, 5257, 18627, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps ensure that the bread is turned into coarse crumbs that are ready for use in various recipes.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0499625725711144, "g_worst_claim": 0.3526657422383626, "g_content": 1.2809475884921309, "g_traj_mean": 0.9631732106208801}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 281, 92852, 96577, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 12348, 68723, 320, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 61347, 4292, 17, 13, 22950, 26757, 315, 4158, 16002, 1526, 279, 52362, 287, 13364, 315, 264, 3607, 17654, 311, 1855, 49247, 96577, 624, 18, 13, 47716, 279, 96577, 41047, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 624, 19, 13, 52074, 279, 96577, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 525, 9058, 714, 537, 92872, 11, 892, 5990, 4990, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 72323, 279, 27815, 10834, 10917, 2337, 279, 27815, 1882, 311, 5978, 1496, 45379, 624, 21, 13, 10783, 279, 96577, 504, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 1105, 311, 7010, 6587, 382, 9485, 7354, 1265, 1102, 304, 281, 92852, 96577, 429, 525, 4727, 369, 40294, 476, 293, 6154, 15298, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps should result in panko crumbs that are perfect for coating or breading foods.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.847254768606105, "g_worst_claim": 0.09263257847891913, "g_content": 1.1031601394432178, "g_traj_mean": 0.7813570499420166}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 26.8, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 4.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "409", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make panko crumbs:\n\nPassage 1 states to push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Then, spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake in a preheated oven until they are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\n\nPassage 2 provides similar instructions, stating to push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Then, spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300°F until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\n\nPassage 3 provides additional information, suggesting to preheat the oven to 300°F before making the crumbs. The passage also recommends using a blender carafe to pulse the bread until coarse crumbs form, and then spreading the crumbs evenly on two half-sheet pans and baking until they just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes. After cooling the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes, transfer them to an airtight container and store them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\n\nTherefore, to make panko crumbs based on the provided passages, you can use a food processor or blender to shred or pulse bread into coarse crumbs, and then bake them in a preheated oven until they are dry but not toasted.", "pred": "1 Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n2 Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 F degrees until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\n3 Shake the sheet twice during baking.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1 Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n2 Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 F degrees until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\n3 Shake the sheet twice during baking.", "cot": "[\"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 F degrees until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n4. Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n5. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\\n\\nThese steps will result in panko crumbs that are dry but not toasted, suitable for various culinary uses.\", \"1) Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F.\\n2) Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3) Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 F degrees until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n4) Shake the sheet twice during baking.\", \"1 Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n2 Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 F degrees until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n3 Shake the sheet twice during baking.\", \"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps based on the provided passages:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 F degrees until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n4. Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs.\\n5. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\\n\\nBy following these specific steps, you can achieve the desired texture and consistency for panko crumbs.\"]", "time_sec": 19.064, "generation_time_seconds": 17.9722, "selection_time_seconds": 1.083, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 2