{"id": "410", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Torn pieces of bread are pushed through the shredding disk of a food processor to create coarse crumbs.\n3. The crumbs are spread on a baking sheet.\n4. The sheet is baked in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes.\n5. The sheet is shaken twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n6. After baking, the crumbs are removed from the oven and allowed to cool completely.\n\nAlternatively, according to passage 2, you can also make panko crumbs by:\n\n1. Pushing chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to create coarse crumbs.\n2. Spreading the crumbs on a baking sheet and baking at 300 degrees F until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes.\n3. Shaking the sheet twice during baking.\n4. Being careful not to let the crumbs brown.\n\nFinally, passage 3 provides a third method for making panko crumbs, which involves blending the ingredients in a blender carafe and baking them on half sheet pans until they are crisp and lightly browned.", "pred": "To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300°F (150°C).\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300°F until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for about 6 to 8 minutes.\n4. Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n5. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and allow the crumbs to cool completely.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300°F (150°C).\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300°F until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for about 6 to 8 minutes.\n4. Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n5. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and allow the crumbs to cool completely.", "cot": "[\"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 F degrees until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n4. Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n5. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\\n\\nThese steps will result in panko crumbs that are dry but not toasted, suitable for various culinary uses.\", \"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. \\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs evenly on 2 half sheet pans.\\n4. Bake the crumbs in the preheated oven until they just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes.\\n5. Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes.\\n6. Transfer the cooled crumbs to an airtight container.\\n7. Store the panko crumbs at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\\n\\nNote: The recipe is courtesy of Alton Brown, 2011.\", \"Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs. Spread the crumbs evenly on 2 half sheet pans and bake until the crumbs just begin to brown and are crisp, about 5 minutes. Cool the crumbs on the pans for 15 to 20 minutes, and then transfer to an airtight container and store at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\", \"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300°F (150°C).\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300°F until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n4. Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n5. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and allow the crumbs to cool completely.\"]", "time_sec": 21.256, "generation_time_seconds": 20.2808, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9676, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 281, 92852, 96577, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 22950, 26757, 315, 4158, 16002, 1526, 279, 52362, 287, 13364, 315, 264, 3607, 17654, 311, 1281, 49247, 96577, 624, 18, 13, 47716, 279, 96577, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 323, 22544, 518, 220, 18, 15, 15, 434, 12348, 3080, 279, 96577, 525, 9058, 714, 537, 92872, 11, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 72323, 279, 10834, 10917, 2337, 27815, 311, 5978, 1496, 45379, 624, 20, 13, 10783, 504, 279, 23387, 323, 7010, 6587, 382, 9485, 7354, 686, 1102, 304, 281, 92852, 96577, 429, 525, 9058, 714, 537, 92872, 11, 14452, 369, 5257, 57341, 5711, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps will result in panko crumbs that are dry but not toasted, suitable for various culinary uses.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2115601347808411, "g_worst_claim": 0.46220024426778156, "g_content": 1.6023458242416382, "g_traj_mean": 1.1758744716644287}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 281, 92852, 96577, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 12348, 434, 13, 715, 17, 13, 22950, 26757, 315, 4158, 16002, 1526, 279, 52362, 287, 13364, 315, 264, 3607, 17654, 311, 1281, 49247, 96577, 624, 18, 13, 47716, 279, 96577, 41047, 389, 220, 17, 4279, 10834, 63783, 624, 19, 13, 52074, 279, 96577, 304, 279, 855, 383, 657, 23387, 3080, 807, 1101, 3161, 311, 13876, 323, 525, 41854, 11, 911, 220, 20, 4420, 6