264, 3607, 17654, 311, 1281, 49247, 96577, 624, 18, 13, 47716, 279, 96577, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 323, 22544, 518, 220, 18, 15, 15, 58472, 3080, 279, 96577, 525, 9058, 714, 537, 92872, 11, 369, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 72323, 279, 10834, 10917, 2337, 27815, 311, 5978, 1496, 45379, 624, 20, 13, 10783, 279, 27815, 10834, 504, 279, 23387, 323, 2138, 279, 96577, 311, 7010, 6587, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300°F (150°C).\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300°F until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for about 6 to 8 minutes.\n4. Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n5. Remove the baking sheet from the oven and allow the crumbs to cool completely.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.205266758468416, "g_worst_claim": 0.23679180145263673, "g_content": 1.6064472198486328, "g_traj_mean": 1.0890029668807983}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.15, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "411", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Push torn pieces of bread or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake in preheated oven until crumbs are dry but not toasted, 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs.\n5. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\n\nIf you want to store the panko crumbs for later use, you can transfer them to an airtight container and keep them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "These steps will result in panko crumbs that are suitable for various cooking applications.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "These steps will result in panko crumbs that are suitable for various cooking applications.", "cot": "[\"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 F degrees until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n4. Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n5. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\\n\\nThese steps will result in panko crumbs that are dry but not toasted, suitable for various culinary uses.\", \"To make panko crumbs, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\\n2. Push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\\n4. Bake in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n5. Shake the sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n6. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\\n\\nThese steps provide a simple and effective method for making panko crumbs, which can be used in various cooking applications such as coating or adding texture to dishes.\", \"To make panko crumbs, you need to:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees Fahrenheit (150 degrees Celsius).\\n\\n2. Push torn pieces of bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\\n\\n4. Bake the crumbs in the preheated oven until they are dry but not toasted, which takes about 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the baking sheet twice during baking to ensure even drying.\\n\\n5. Remove the crumbs from the oven and let them cool completely.\\n\\nThese steps will result in panko crumbs that are suitable for various cooking applications.\", \"1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\\n2. Push chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet and bake at 300 F degrees until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, about 6 to 8 minutes.\\n4. Shake the sheet twice during baking.\\n5. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\"]", "time_sec": 21.684, "generation_time_seconds": 20.8178, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8569, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 281, 92852, 96577, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 4968, 19963, 279, 23387, 311, 220, 18, 15, 15, 12348, 434, 320, 16, 20, 15, 12348, 356, 4292, 17, 13, 22950, 26757, 315, 4158, 16002, 1526, 279, 52362, 287, 13364, 315, 264, 3607, 17654, 311, 1281, 49247, 96577, 624, 18, 13, 47716, 279, 96577, 389, 264, 27815, 10834, 323, 22544, 518, 220, 18, 15, 15, 434, 12348, 3080, 279, 96577, 525, 9058, 714, 537, 92872, 11, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 4420, 624, 19, 13, 7232