{"id": "422", "question": "what is a upc description", "gt": "A UPC description refers to the Universal Product Code, a barcode symbology used extensively in multiple countries including the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and in Europe. It is used for tracking trade items in stores. UPC consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. It is primarily used for scanning of trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.", "pred": "A UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology that is widely used for tracking trade items in stores. Specifically, it consists of 12 numeric digits, which are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning items at the point of sale according to GS1 specifications.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "A UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology that is widely used for tracking trade items in stores. Specifically, it consists of 12 numeric digits, which are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning items at the point of sale according to GS1 specifications.", "cot": "[\"The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology that is widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe and other countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits, that are uniquely assigned to each trade item.\", \"A UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe and other countries. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC, along with related EAN barcode, is primarily used for scanning trade items at the point of sale according to GS1 specifications.\", \"The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology that is widely used in various countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. It is used for scanning trade items at the point of sale according to GS1 specifications.\", \"A UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology that is widely used for tracking trade items in stores. Specifically, it consists of 12 numeric digits, which are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is primarily used for scanning items at the point of sale according to GS1 specifications.\"]", "time_sec": 13.875, "generation_time_seconds": 13.1578, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7118, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 25500, 5643, 6119, 320, 3124, 34, 8, 374, 264, 49407, 66654, 2449, 429, 374, 13570, 1483, 304, 279, 3639, 4180, 11, 6864, 11, 3639, 15072, 11, 8330, 11, 1532, 16911, 11, 304, 4505, 323, 1008, 5837, 369, 14849, 6559, 3589, 304, 10533, 13, 1084, 17167, 315, 220, 16, 17, 24064, 18509, 11, 429, 525, 41229, 12607, 311, 1817, 6559, 1509, 13, 151645], "pred": "The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology that is widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe and other countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits, that are uniquely assigned to each trade item.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3431396448250972, "g_worst_claim": 0.42131249109903973, "g_content": 1.4884439665695717, "g_traj_mean": 1.2191951274871826}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [32, 95129, 320, 58278, 5643, 6119, 8, 374, 264, 49407, 66654, 2449, 13570, 1483, 304, 279, 3639, 4180, 11, 6864, 11, 3639, 15072, 11, 8330, 11, 1532, 16911, 11, 304, 4505, 323, 1008, 5837, 13, 1084, 17167, 315, 220, 16, 17, 24064, 18509, 429, 525, 41229, 12607, 311, 1817, 6559, 1509, 13, 576, 95129, 11, 3156, 448, 5435, 468, 1093, 49407, 11, 374, 15503, 1483, 369, 35101, 6559, 3589, 518