{"id": "423", "question": "what is a upc description", "gt": "A UPC description refers to the Universal Product Code, which is a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item and is mainly used for scanning items at the point of sale.", "pred": "The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and other countries. It consists of 12 numeric digits and is used for tracking trade items in stores. The UPC is mainly used for scanning at the point of sale.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and other countries. It consists of 12 numeric digits and is used for tracking trade items in stores. The UPC is mainly used for scanning at the point of sale.", "cot": "[\"The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology that is widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe and other countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits, that are uniquely assigned to each trade item.\", \"A UPC (Universal Product Code) is a barcode symbology widely used for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits, uniquely assigned to each item, and is used primarily for scanning at the point of sale.\", \"The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and other countries. It consists of 12 numeric digits and is used for tracking trade items in stores. The UPC is mainly used for scanning at the point of sale.\", \"UPC stands for Universal Product Code. It is a barcode symbology widely used in the United States, Canada, Unite