{"id": "425", "question": "what is a upc description", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, an UPDescription is:\n\n1. A barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores, consisting of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. (Passage 1)\n2. A process involving receiving a specimen bottle from a member, ensuring it contains a minimum of 30 milliliters of urine, initialing the label in the member's presence, and verifying the information on the label and DD Form 2624 (a military form). (Passage 2)\n3. A barcode partner that provides GS1 Originated UPC and EAN codes, as well as a toll-free number and positive customer reviews. (Passage 3)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "A Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology that is widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe and other countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is used for scanning of trade items at the point of sale and is related to the EAN barcode.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "A Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology that is widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe and other countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is used for scanning of trade items at the point of sale and is related to the EAN barcode.", "cot": "[\"The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology that is widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe and other countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits, that are uniquely assigned to each trade item.\", \"The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits, each uniquely assigned to a trade item. The UPC is widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and other countries. It is used to scan trade items at the point of sale.\", \"A Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology used for tracking trade items in stores and is widely used in the United States, Canada, the United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, Europe, and other countries. It consists of 12 numeric digits, uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is used for scanning at the point of sale.\", \"A Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology that is widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe and other countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. The UPC is used for scanning of trade items at the point of sale and is related to the EAN barcode.\"]", "time_sec": 15.117, "generation_time_seconds": 14.4085, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6979, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 25500, 5643, 6119, 320, 3124, 34, 8, 374, 264, 49407, 66654, 2449, 429, 374, 13570, 1483, 304, 279, 3639, 4180, 11, 6864, 11, 3639, 15072, 11, 8330, 11, 1532, 16911, 11, 304, 4505, 323, 1008, 5837, 369, 14849, 6559, 3589, 304, 10533, 13, 1084, 17167, 315, 220, 16, 17, 24064, 18509, 11, 429, 525, 41229, 12607, 311, 1817, 6559, 1509, 13, 151645], "pred": "The Universal Product Code (UPC) is a barcode symbology that is widely used in the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, in Europe and other countries for tracking trade items in stores. It consists of 12 numeric digits, that are uniquely assigned to each trade item.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.268015247603458, "g_worst_claim": 0.41600215435028076, "g_content": 1.3684221465012123,