{"id": "439", "question": "how to find someone in france", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to find someone in France:\n\n1. Use a people search website specifically designed for France, such as People Search France.\n2. Check the French white pages (in English) at PagesJaunes.fr. Instead of typing Paris in the City field, write IDF (or Ile de France) in the Dept district or region field to search for the person in Paris and its suburbs.\n3. Post a missed connection (MC) on Paris Craigslist.\n4. Visit the Pages Blanches (the French version of the white pages) at PagesJaunes.fr. Enter the last name of the person you're searching for in the Nom field, and optionally enter a first name in the Prenom field. Enter address information, if known, in the Ou section. Click Trouver to search for the name. The search results will display name, address, and phone number for all listings that match your search criteria.", "pred": "To find someone in France, you can use the French white pages (in English) at http://www.pagesjaunes.fr/pb.cgi?lang=en. When searching, instead of typing Paris in the City field, write IDF (or Ile de France) in the Dept district or region field. This will search for the person in Paris and its suburbs. Additionally, you can try posting an MC (missed connection) on Paris Craigslist (http://paris.craigslist.org/cgi-bin/pers...", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To find someone in France, you can use the French white pages (in English) at http://www.pagesjaunes.fr/pb.cgi?lang=en. When searching, instead of typing Paris in the City field, write IDF (or Ile de France) in the Dept district or region field. This will search for the person in Paris and its suburbs. Additionally, you can try posting an MC (missed connection) on Paris Craigslist (http://paris.craigslist.org/cgi-bin/pers...", "cot": "[\"To find someone in France, you can use the French white pages (in English) at http://www.pagesjaunes.fr/pb.cgi?lang=en. When searching, instead of typing Paris in the City field, write IDF (or Ile de France) in the Dept district or region field. This will search for the person in Paris and its suburbs. Additionally, you can try posting an MC (missed connection) on Paris Craigslist (http://paris.craigslist.org/cgi-bin/pers...\", \"To find someone in France, you can use the French white pages (in English) at http://www.pagesjaunes.fr/pb.cgi?lang=en. To search effectively, enter the last name of the person in the Nom field. Optionally, you can also enter a first name in the Prenom field, and any known address information in the Ou section. Clicking on the Trouver button will display a list of matching names, addresses, and phone numbers. If you are searching within Paris and its suburbs, you can specify IDF or Ile de France in the Dept district or region field instead of typing Paris in the City field.\", \"To find someone in France, you can start by visiting the website www.pagesjaunes.fr, which is the French version of the white pages. Enter the last name of the person you're searching for in the Nom field. You can enter a first name in the Prenom field. Enter address information, if known, in the Ou section. Otherwise, leave it blank to search the entire country. Click Trouver to search for the name. The search results will display the name, address, and phone number for all listings that match your search criteria.\", \"To find someone in France, you can visit the website www.pagesjaunes.fr, the Pages Blanches, which is the French version of the white pages. Enter the last name of the person you're searching for in the Nom field. You can also try searching for the person using the French white pages (in English) at http://www.pagesjaunes.fr/pb.cgi?lang=en.\"]", "time_sec": 18.519, "generation_time_seconds": 17.7352, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7778, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": 