 in France, you can use the French white pages (in English) at http://www.pagesjaunes.fr/pb.cgi?lang=en. To search effectively, enter the last name of the person in the Nom field. Optionally, you can also enter a first name in the Prenom field, and any known address information in the Ou section. Clicking on the Trouver button will display a list of matching names, addresses, and phone numbers. If you are searching within Paris and its suburbs, you can specify IDF or Ile de France in the Dept district or region field instead of typing Paris in the City field.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6757674570953764, "g_worst_claim": 0.10788240283727646, "g_content": 2.727148223341557, "g_traj_mean": 1.8466743230819702}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1477, 4325, 304, 9625, 11, 498, 646, 1191, 553, 16721, 279, 3910, 8438, 37980, 5580, 8531, 18798, 11, 892, 374, 279, 8585, 2319, 315, 279, 4158, 6816, 13, 11252, 279, 1537, 829, 315, 279, 1697, 498, 2299, 15039, 369, 304, 279, 36900, 2070, 13, 1446, 646, 3725, 264, 1156, 829, 304, 279, 393, 44843, 2070, 13, 11252, 2621, 1995, 11, 421, 3881, 11, 304, 279, 68227, 3772, 13, 18214, 11, 5274, 432, 10113, 311, 2711, 279, 4453, 3146, 13, 9189, 41682, 423, 311, 2711, 369, 279, 829, 13, 576, 2711, 3059, 686, 3037, 279, 829, 11, 2621, 11, 323, 4540, 1372, 369, 678, 25465, 429, 2432, 697, 2711, 12890, 13, 151645], "pred": "To find someone in France, you can start by visiting the website www.pagesjaunes.fr, which is the French version of the white pages. Enter the last name of the person you're searching for in the Nom field. You can enter a first name in the Prenom field. Enter address information, if known, in the Ou section. Otherwise, leave it blank to search the entire country. Click Trouver to search for the name. The search results will display the name, address, and phone number for all listings that match your search criteria.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8520893857936664, "g_worst_claim": 1.1084353446960449, "g_content": 2.440165710449219, "g_traj_mean": 1.6465429067611694}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1477, 4325, 304, 9625, 11, 498, 646, 3947, 279, 3910, 8438, 37980, 5580, 8531, 18798, 11, 279, 21772, 2502, 82181, 11, 892, 374, 279, 8585, 2319, 315, 279, 4158, 6816, 13, 11252, 279, 1537, 829, 315, 279, 1697, 498, 2299, 15039, 369, 304, 279, 36900, 2070, 13, 1446, 646, 1083, 1430, 15039, 369, 279, 1697, 1667, 279, 8585, 4158, 6816, 320, 258, 6364, 8, 518, 1758, 1110, 2136, 37980, 5580, 8531, 18798, 4322, 65, 59014, 30, 5205, 61757, 13, 151645], "pred": "To find someone in France, you can visit the website www.pagesjaunes.fr, the Pages Blanches, which is the French version of the white pages. Enter the last name of the person you're searching for in the Nom field. You can also try searching for the person using the French white pages (in English) at http://www.pagesjaunes.fr/pb.cgi?lang=en.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.991632015719226, "g_worst_claim": 1.182170581817627, "g_content": 2.6019309997558593, "g_traj_mean": 1.8612706661224365}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 47.55, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "440", "question": "how are forest fires beneficial to conifers like jack pines?", "gt": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they help in the regeneration of the forest. Fires consume dead and decaying vegetation, clearing the way for new growth. Jack pines rely on fire to spread their seeds. They produce seratonous (resin-filled) cones that remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin, causing the cones to open and the seeds to fall or blow out. Furthermore, fires can disrupt the growth of other trees like spruce, providing an advantage to the more fire-tolerant jack pines and allowing them to proliferate.", "pred": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they consume dead, decaying vegetation accumulating on the forest floor, thereby clearing the way for new growth. Some species, such as the jack pine, even rely on fire to spread their seeds. The jack pine produces seratonous (resin-filled) cones that are very durable. The cones remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin. Then the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they consume dead, decaying vegetation accumulating on the forest floor, thereby clearing the way for new growth. Some species, such as the jack pine, even rely on fire to spread their seeds. The jack pine produces seratonous (resin-filled) cones that are very durable. The cones remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin. Then the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out.", "cot": "[\"Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they consume dead, decaying vegetation accumulating on the forest floor, thereby clearing the way for new growth. Some species, such as the jack pine, even rely on fire to spread their seeds. The jack pine produces seratonous (resin-filled) cones that are very durable. The cones remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin. Then the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out.\", \"Forest fires benefit conifers like jack pines by providing conditions for new growth and seed dispersal. For instance, the jack pine, which produces seratonous cones that are very durable, relies on fire to spread its seeds. When a fire occurs, the resin in the cones melts, causing the cones to pop open and release the seeds. This process allows the jack pine to regrow and proliferate in regions where it has been displaced by other conifers, such as the spruce.\", \"Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines in several ways:\\n\\n1. **Seed Germination**: Jack pines produce serotonous cones that are very durable. These cones remain dormant until a fire occurs, which melts the resin inside. This melts cause the cones to release their seeds. This process is essential for the jack pine's survival, as it is one of the few conifer species that can regenerate from seeds following a forest fire.\\n\\n2. **Clearing the Way for New Growth**: Fires consume dead, decaying vegetation on the forest floor, clearing the way for new growth. This process reduces competition from other species and allows young trees, including jack pines, to establish themselves more effectively.\\n\\n3. **Maintaining Ecological Balance**: In areas where spruce trees are abundant, jack pines and aspens can begin to die out. However, when a fire occurs and disturbs this cycle, the more fire-tolerant jack pines and aspens regain the advantage and begin to proliferate again. This helps maintain an ecological balance within the forest.\\n\\nIn summary, forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines by facilitating seed germination, clearing the forest floor for new growth, and maintaining ecological balance.\", \"Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they consume dead, decaying vegetation, clearing the way for new growth. Some species, such as the jack pine, even rely on fire to spread their seeds. The jack pine produces seratonous cones that remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin. Then the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out. In the Canadian boreal forest, aspen and jack pine are the most important 'pioneer species'.\"]", "time_sec": 22.384, "generation_time_seconds": 21.4809, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8932, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [49578, 26084, 525, 23699, 311, 390, 98813, 1075, 25072, 281, 1543, 1576, 807, 24057, 5593, 11, 1622, 17270, 53732, 91585, 389, 279, 13638, 6422, 11, 27492, 32750, 279, 1616, 369, 501, 6513, 13, 4329, 9419, 11, 1741, 438, 279, 25072, 33597, 11, 1496, 17188, 389, 3940, 311, 8865, 862, 19056, 13, 576, 25072, 33597, 18644, 1420, 23535, 782, 320, 416, 258, 43418, 8, 86892, 429, 525, 1602, 26128, 13, 576, 86892, 7146, 88360, 3080, 264, 3940, 13666, 323, 98091, 279, 53514, 13, 5005, 279, 86892, 2420, 1787, 323, 279, 19056, 4399, 476, 12244, 700, 13, 151645], "pred": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they consume dead, decaying vegetation accumulating on the forest floor, thereby clearing the way for new growth. Some species, such as the jack pine, even rely on fire to spread their seeds. The jack pine produces seratonous (resin-filled) cones that are very durable. The cones remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin. Then the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7433020221626656, "g_worst_claim": 0.5674682060877482, "g_content": 2.2699128786722818, "g_traj_mean": 1.9739192724227905}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [49578, 26084, 8760, 390, 98813, 1075, 25072, 281, 1543, 553, 8241, 4682, 369, 501, 6513, 323, 10320, 78735, 278, 13, 1752, 2867, 11, 279, 25072, 33597, 11, 892, 18644, 1420, 23535, 782, 86892, 429, 525, 