res": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6687744864775746, "g_worst_claim": 0.549941619237264, "g_content": 2.0998929341634116, "g_traj_mean": 1.9772015810012817}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 68.38, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "443", "question": "how are forest fires beneficial to conifers like jack pines?", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines in several ways:\n\n1. Fire helps to clear the way for new growth by consuming dead, decaying vegetation on the forest floor, creating a clean slate for seed germination and seedling establishment (Passage 2).\n2. Jack pine seeds are adapted to fire, as they are stored in serotinous cones that only open after a fire has melted the resin holding them closed. This allows the seeds to disperse and establish new populations (Passage 2).\n3. Fire can create a favorable environment for jack pine and aspen regrowth by reducing competition from other tree species, such as spruce, which have better access to sunlight while shading the other trees (Passage 3).\n\nTherefore, forest fires can benefit jack pines by providing a means of seed dispersal and creating conditions that promote their growth and regeneration.", "pred": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they consume dead, decaying vegetation accumulating on the forest floor, thereby clearing the way for new growth. Some species, such as the jack pine, even rely on fire to spread their seeds. The jack pine produces seratonous (resin-filled) cones that are very durable. The cones remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin. Then the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they consume dead, decaying vegetation accumulating on the forest floor, thereby clearing the way for new growth. Some species, such as the jack pine, even rely on fire to spread their seeds. The jack pine produces seratonous (resin-filled) cones that are very durable. The cones remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin. Then the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out.", "cot": "[\"Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they consume dead, decaying vegetation accumulating on the forest floor, thereby clearing the way for new growth. Some species, such as the jack pine, even rely on fire to spread their seeds. The jack pine produces seratonous (resin-filled) cones that are very durable. The cones remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin. Then the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out.\", \"Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they help clear the way for new growth. The heat from the fire melts the resin in the seratonous cones of the jack pine, causing them to pop open and release the seeds. This process helps regenerate the forest by allowing new seedlings to grow in the cleared area. Additionally, fires can help maintain the balance of the forest ecosystem by allowing certain species, such as aspen and jack pine, to proliferate in areas where spruce trees are abundant.\", \"Forest fires can be beneficial to conifers like jack pines in several ways. Firstly, fires can clear the forest floor, making it easier for new growth to occur. Secondly, some species of conifers, such as the jack pine, rely on fire to spread their seeds. The cones of the jack pine are seratonous, meaning they are filled with resin. This resin is very durable and remains dormant until a fire occurs. When a fire melts the resin, the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out, allowing them to spread to new areas. Finally, fires can disrupt the cycle of other trees, such as spruce, which can allow the more fire-tolerant jack pine and aspen to regain an advantage and proliferate.\", \"Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they consume dead, decaying vegetation, clearing the way for new growth. Additionally, some species, such as the jack pine, rely on fire to spread their seeds. The jack pine produces seratonous cones that remain dormant until a fire occurs, at which point the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out.\"]", "time_sec": 19.087, "generation_time_seconds": 18.2338, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8465, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [49578, 26084, 525, 23699, 311, 390, 98813, 1075, 25072, 281, 1543, 1576, 807, 24057, 5593, 11, 1622, 17270, 53732, 91585, 389, 279, 13638, 6422, 11, 27492, 32750, 279, 1616, 369, 501, 6513, 13, 4329, 9419, 11, 1741, 438, 279, 25072, 33597, 11, 1496, 17188, 389, 3940, 311, 8865, 862, 19056, 13, 576, 25072, 33597, 18644, 1420, 23535, 782, 320, 416, 258, 43418, 8, 86892, 429, 525, 1602, 26128, 13, 576, 86892, 7146, 88360, 3080, 264, 3940, 13666, 323, 98091, 279, 53514, 13, 5005, 279, 86892, 2420, 1787, 323, 279, 19056, 4399, 476, 12244, 700, 13, 151645], "pred": "Forest fires are beneficial to conifers like jack pines because they consume dead, decaying vegetation accumulating on the forest floor, thereby clearing the way for new growth. Some species, such as the jack pine, even rely on fire to spread their seeds. The jack pine produces seratonous (resin-filled) cones that are very durable. The cones remain dormant until a fire occurs and melts the resin. Then the cones pop open and the seeds fall or blow out.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7433020221626656, "g_worst_claim": 0.5674682060877482, "g_content": 2.2699128786722818, "g_traj_mean": 1.9739192724227905}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [49578, 26084, 525, 23699, 311, 390, 98813, 1075, 25072, 281, 1543, 1576, 807, 1492, 2797, 279, 1616, 369, 501, 6513, 13, 576, 8628, 504, 279, 3940, 98091, 279, 53514, 304, 279, 1420, 23535, 782, 86892, 315, 279, 25072, 33597, 11, 14381, 1105, 311, 2420, 1787, 323, 4879, 279, 19056, 13, 1096, 1882, 8609, 79451, 279, 13638, 553, 10693, 501, 10320, 18812, 311, 3063, 304, 279, 22949, 3082, 13, 22406, 11, 26084, 646, 1492, 10306, 279, 8172, 315, 279, 13638, 24982, 5