{"id": "451", "question": "how is a caldera different from a crater", "gt": "A caldera is a large depression created by volcanic activity when a chamber of magma and lava empties, causing the overlying rocks to collapse. It is formed by the collapsing of the ground. On the other hand, a crater is a bowl-shaped structure at the top of a volcano around the opening used for the eruption of magma and lava. It is formed by the sinking in of rocks due to high pressure.", "pred": "A caldera is a large, circular depression that forms at the top of a volcano when the magma chamber collapses, whereas a crater is formed by the impact of a meteorite and can range in size from very small to several hundred km across.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "A caldera is a large, circular depression that forms at the top of a volcano when the magma chamber collapses, whereas a crater is formed by the impact of a meteorite and can range in size from very small to several hundred km across.", "cot": "[\"A caldera is a large, circular depression formed at the top of a volcano when the magma chamber collapses, while a crater is caused by impacts from meteorites and can range in size from very small to several hundred km across.\", \"A caldera is a large, circular depression that forms at the top of a volcano when the magma chamber collapses, whereas a crater is formed by the impact of a meteorite and can range in size from very small to several hundred km across.\", \"A caldera is a large, circular depression formed at the top of a volcano when the magma chamber collapses, while a crater is caused by impacts from meteorites and can range in size from very small to several hundred km across.\", \"A caldera is a large (at least one km across), circular depression formed at the top of a volcano when the magma chamber collapses, whereas a crater is caused by impacts from meteorites and can range in size from very small to several hundred km across.\"]", "time_sec": 11.868, "generation_time_seconds": 10.9498, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9115, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [32, 1620, 97903, 374, 264, 3460, 11, 26931, 18210, 14122, 518, 279, 1909, 315, 264, 65206, 979, 279, 63505, 24220, 86358, 11, 1393, 264, 74707, 374, 8881, 553, 24905, 504, 41042, 3611, 323, 646, 2088, 304, 1379, 504, 1602, 2613, 311, 3807, 7739, 13136, 3941, 13, 151645], "pred": "A caldera is a large, circular depression formed at the top of a volcano when the magma chamber collapses, while a crater is caused by impacts from meteorites and can range in size from very small to several hundred km across.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5326140888153563, "g_worst_claim": 1.1877037048339845, "g_content": 2.1105067513205786, "g_traj_mean": 1.5856170654296875}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [32, 1620, 97903, 374, 264, 3460, 11, 26931, 18210, 429, 7586, 518, 279, 1909, 315, 264, 65206, 979, 279, 63505, 24220, 86358, 11, 19853, 264, 74707, 374, 14122, 553, 279, 5421, 315, 264, 41042, 632, 323, 646, 2088, 304, 1379, 504, 1602, 2613, 311, 3807, 7739, 13136, 3941, 13, 151645], "pred": "A caldera is a large, circular depression that forms at the top of a volcano when the magma chamber collapses, whereas a crater is formed by the impact of a meteorite and can range in size from very small to several hundred km across.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.200588219331734, "g_worst_claim": 0.7625350952148438, "g_content": 1.5787361808445142, "g_traj_mean": 1.1580209732055664}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [32, 1620, 97903, 374, 264, 3460, 11, 26931, 18210, 14122, 518, 279, 1909, 315, 264, 65206, 979, 279, 63505, 24220, 86358, 11, 1393, 264, 74707, 374, 8881, 553, 24905, 504, 41042, 3611, 323, 646, 2088, 304, 1379, 504, 1602, 2613, 311, 3807, 7739, 13136, 3941, 13, 151645], "pred": "A caldera is a large, ci