{"id": "471", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "gt": "Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, has no discernible taste or smell, and has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking. On the other hand, unrefined coconut oil is made from fresh coconut flesh, carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma, and has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F.", "pred": "The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their production process, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil, which has a smoking point of 350 degrees F, making it a better choice for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized and loses its signature coconut flavor, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their production process, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil, which has a smoking point of 350 degrees F, making it a better choice for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized and loses its signature coconut flavor, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.", "cot": "[\"The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their production process, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts, while unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it a better option for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\", \"The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their preparation and characteristics. Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts and loses its coconut flavor and aroma during the refining process. On the other hand, unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from fresh coconuts and retains its distinct coconut flavor and aroma. Additionally, refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point (450 degrees F) compared to unrefined coconut oil (350 degrees F), making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying.\", \"The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their preparation, aroma, flavor, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point (450 degrees F) compared to unrefined coconut oil (350 degrees F), making it a better option for high-temperature cooking methods. Unrefined coconut oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma, whereas refined coconut oil has no discernible taste or smell due to the deodorization process.\", \"The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their production process, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil, which has a smoking point of 350 degrees F, making it a better choice for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized and loses its signature coconut flavor, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\"]", "time_sec": 23.674, "generation_time_seconds": 22.9833, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6841, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 37191, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 15448, 304, 862, 5670, 1882, 11, 12656, 11, 323, 8628, 24098, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 31620, 1062, 443, 6128, 11, 1393, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 11, 1083, 3881, 438, 10526, 476, 35899, 33457, 5590, 11, 374, 1865, 504, 7722, 1062, 443, 6128, 13, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 12460, 54179, 323, 17172, 11, 892, 374, 5558, 2337, 279, 73185, 1882, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 5080, 19578, 1459, 315, 220, 19, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 7707, 311, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 594, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 11, 3259, 432, 264, 2664, 2999, 369, 1550, 12, 34558, 17233, 5413, 1741, 438, 86096, 13, 22406, 11, 37191, 33457, 5590, 374, 409, 48917, 1506, 11, 12942, 304, 902, 41545, 1238, 12656, 476, 22068, 11, 19853, 650, 1097, 1589, 5590, 23377, 264, 23034, 33457, 17172, 323, 54179, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their production process, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts, while unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it a better option for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0235840996378434, "g_worst_claim": 0.07786315679550171, "g_content": 1.2647569334352171, "g_traj_mean": 0.9709584712982178}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 37191, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 15448, 304, 862, 17975, 323, 17452, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 31620, 1062, 443, 6128, 323, 32191, 1181, 33457, 17172, 323, 54179, 2337, 279, 73185, 1882, 13, 1913, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 11, 1083, 3881, 438, 10526, 476, 35899, 33457, 5590, 11, 374, 1865, 504, 7722, 1062, 443, 6128, 323, 51844, 1181, 12460, 33457, 17172, 323, 54179, 13, 22406, 11, 37191, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 5080, 19578, 1459, 320, 19, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 8, 7707, 311, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 320, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 701, 3259, 432, 14452, 369, 1550, 12, 34558, 17233, 5413, 1741, 438, 86096, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their preparation and characteristics. Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts and loses its coconut flavor and aroma during the refining process. On the other hand, unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from fresh coconuts and retains its distinct coconut flavor and aroma. Additionally, refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point (450 degrees F) compared to unrefined coconut oil (350 degrees F), making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.624691027607561, "g_worst_claim": 0.34000829549936146, "g_content": 0.9048146565755208, "g_traj_mean": 0.6858289241790771}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 37191, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 15448, 304, 862, 17975, 11, 54179, 11, 17172, 11, 323, 8628, 24098, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 31620, 33457, 13779, 11, 1393, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 24955, 315, 7722, 1062, 443, 6128, 13, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 12460, 54179, 323, 17172, 11, 892, 374, 5558, 2337, 279, 73185, 1882, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 5080, 19578, 1459, 320, 19, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 8, 7707, 311, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 320, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 701, 3259, 432, 264, 2664, 2999, 369, 1550, 12, 34558, 17233, 5413, 13, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 23377, 264, 23034, 33457, 17172, 323, 54179, 11, 19853, 37191, 33457, 5590, 702, 902, 41545, 1238, 12656, 476, 22068, 4152, 311, 279, 409, 48917, 2022, 1882, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their preparation, aroma, flavor, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point (450 degrees F) compared to unrefined coconut oil (350 degrees F), making it a better option for high-temperature cooking methods. Unrefined coconut oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma, whereas refined coconut oil has no discernible taste or smell due to the deodorization process.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9702179105903379, "g_worst_claim": 0.52