{"id": "473", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil is the process used to extract it. Refined coconut oil is extracted from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is extracted from the flesh of the fresh coconut. Another difference is that refined coconut oil has a higher smoke point and is therefore better suited for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized and has no taste or smell, while unrefined oil retains its distinctive coconut flavor and aroma.", "pred": "In summary, the key differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are their aroma, flavor, and heat tolerance, with refined oil being more suitable for high-temperature cooking due to its higher smoking point and lack of coconut aroma, and unrefined oil retaining its characteristic coconut flavor and aroma.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "In summary, the key differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are their aroma, flavor, and heat tolerance, with refined oil being more suitable for high-temperature cooking due to its higher smoking point and lack of coconut aroma, and unrefined oil retaining its characteristic coconut flavor and aroma.", "cot": "[\"The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their production process, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts, while unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it a better option for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\", \"Relying on the information provided in the passages:\\n\\n1. **Aroma and Flavor**: Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining.\\n2. **Smoking Point**: Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, whereas unrefined coconut oil has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F. This makes refined coconut oil more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.\\n3. **Taste**: Refined coconut oil is deodorized and loses its coconut flavor, resulting in no discernible taste or smell. On the other hand, unrefined coconut oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\\n\\nIn summary, the key differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are their aroma, flavor, and heat tolerance, with refined oil being more suitable for high-temperature cooking due to its higher smoking point and lack of coconut aroma, and unrefined oil retaining its characteristic coconut flavor and aroma.\", \"The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their preparation methods, taste, and smoking points. Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. In contrast, unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts and has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined coconut oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\", \"The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil is the taste, aroma, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit and has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, whereas unrefined coconut oil, made from the flesh of fresh coconuts, has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining. Refined coconut oil has a greater heat tolerance and can be a better option for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Unrefined coconut oil is better for low-temperature cooking methods such as stir-frying and baking.\"]", "time_sec": 25.826, "generation_time_seconds": 25.1283, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6922, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 37191, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 15448, 304, 862, 5670, 1882, 11, 12656, 11, 323, 8628, 24098, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 31620, 1062, 443, 6128, 11, 1393, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 11, 1083, 3881, 438, 10526, 476, 35899, 33457, 5590, 11, 374, 1865, 504, 7722, 1062, 443, 6128, 13, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 12460, 54179, 323, 17172, 11, 892, 374, 5558, 2337, 279, 73185, 1882, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 5080, 19578, 1459, 315, 220, 19, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 7707, 311, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 594, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 11, 3259, 432, 264, 2664, 2999, 369, 1550, 12, 34558, 17233, 5413, 1741, 438, 86096, 13, 22406, 11, 37191, 33457, 5590, 374, 409, 48917, 1506, 11, 12942, 304, 902, 41545, 1238, 12656, 476, 22068, 11, 19853, 650, 1097, 1589, 5590, 23377, 264, 23034, 33457, 17172, 323, 54179, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their production process, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts, while unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it a better option for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.029937793139245, "g_worst_claim": 0.08452773094177246, "g_content": 1.29536755054028, "g_traj_mean": 0.9830189347267151}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [49, 974, 287, 389, 279, 1995, 3897, 304, 279, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 32, 56984, 323, 64999, 95518, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 12460, 54179, 323, 17172, 429, 374, 5558, 2337, 73185, 624, 17, 13, 3070, 10673, 10746, 5126, 95518, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 5080, 19578, 1459, 315, 220, 19, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 11, 19853, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 4722, 19578, 1459, 315, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 13, 1096, 3643, 37191, 33457, 5590, 803, 14452, 369, 1550, 12, 34558, 17233, 5413, 1075, 86096, 624, 18, 13, 3070, 51, 5525, 95518, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 374, 409, 48917, 1506, 323, 32191, 1181, 33457, 17172, 11, 12942, 304, 902, 41545, 1238, 12656, 476, 22068, 13, 1913, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 23377, 264, 23034, 33457, 17172, 323, 54179, 382, 641, 12126, 11, 279, 1376, 11799, 1948, 37191, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 525, 862, 54179, 11, 17172, 11, 323, 8628, 24098, 11, 448, 37191, 5590, 1660, 803, 14452, 369, 1550, 12, 34558, 17233, 4152, 311, 1181, 5080, 19578, 1459, 323, 6853, 315, 33457, 54179, 11, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 5590, 50010, 1181, 28583, 33457, 17172, 323, 54179, 13, 151645], "pred": "In summary, the key differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are their aroma, flavor, and heat tolerance, with refined oil being more suitable for high-temperature cooking due to its higher smoking point and lack of coconut aroma, and unrefined oil retaining its characteristic coconut flavor and aroma.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8367042226178204, "g_worst_claim": 0.04922790112702743, "g_content": 0.9639554264569523, "g_traj_mean": 0.7488411664962769}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 37191, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 15448, 304, 862, 17975, 5413, 11, 12656, 11, 323, 19578, 3501, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 31620, 33457, 13779, 323, 702, 264, 5080, 19578, 1459, 315, 220, 19, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 11, 3259, 432, 14452, 369, 1550, 12, 34558, 17233, 5413, 1741, 438, 86096, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 11, 1083, 3881, 438, 10526, 476, 35899, 33457, 5590, 11, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 24955, 315, 7722, 1062, 443, 6128, 323, 702, 264, 4722, 19578, 1459, 315, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 13, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 12460, 54179, 323, 17172, 11, 892, 374, 5558, 2337, 279, 73185, 1882, 13, 22406, 11, 37191, 33457, 5590, 374, 409, 48917, 1506, 11, 12942, 304, 902, 41545, 1238, 12656, 476, 22068, 11, 19853, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 23377, 264, 23034, 33457, 17172, 323, 54179, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their preparation methods, taste, and smoking points. Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit and has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. In contrast, unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts and has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined coconut oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9742951335548432, "g_worst_claim": 0.3297247886657715, "g_content": 1.2850277549342106, "g_traj_mean": 0.9083817005157471}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 37191, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 374, 279, 12656, 11, 54179, 11, 323, 8628, 24098, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 31620, 33457, 13779, 323, 702, 264, 5080, 19578, 1459, 315, 220, 19, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 11, 19853, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 11, 1865, 504, 279, 24955, 315, 7722, 1062, 443, 6128, 11, 702, 264, 4722, 19578, 1459, 315, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 13, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 12460, 54179, 323, 17172, 429, 374, 5558, 2337, 73185, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 7046, 8628, 24098, 323, 646, 387, 264, 2664, 2999, 369, 1550, 12, 34558, 17233, 5413, 1741, 438, 86096, 13, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 374, 2664, 369, 3347, 12, 34558, 17233, 5413, 1741, 438, 23065, 2220, 27509, 323, 27815, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil is the taste, aroma, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit and has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F, whereas unrefined coconut oil, made from the flesh of fresh coconuts, has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees F. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining. Refined coconut oil has a greater heat tolerance and can be a better option for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Unrefined coconut oil is better for low-temperature cooking methods such as stir-frying and baking.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8517750513943763, "g_worst_claim": -0.27646764119466144, "g_content": 1.2544756496653837, "g_traj_mean": 0.8554558157920837}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 36.73, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "474", "question": "what is the difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are:\n\n1. Source: Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts.\n2. Aroma and flavor: Unrefined coconut oil retains its distinct aroma and flavor, while refined coconut oil loses these qualities during the refining process.\n3. Smoking point: Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point (450 degrees F) than unrefined coconut oil (350 degrees F), making it more suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying.\n\nTherefore, the main differences between refined and unrefined coconut oil are their source, aroma, flavor, and smoking point.", "pred": "The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their taste, aroma, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts and has a high smoking point of 450 degrees Fahrenheit, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. It has lost its coconut flavor and aroma due to the refining process. On the other hand, unrefined coconut oil comes from fresh coconuts and has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees Fahrenheit. It retains its distinct coconut flavor and aroma, but has a milder coconut taste compared to the full-bodied flavor of refined coconut oil.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their taste, aroma, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts and has a high smoking point of 450 degrees Fahrenheit, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. It has lost its coconut flavor and aroma due to the refining process. On the other hand, unrefined coconut oil comes from fresh coconuts and has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees Fahrenheit. It retains its distinct coconut flavor and aroma, but has a milder coconut taste compared to the full-bodied flavor of refined coconut oil.", "cot": "[\"The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their production process, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts, while unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it a better option for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\", \"Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil, also called pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of the fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining.\", \"The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their preparation methods, smoking points, and flavors. Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit and has a smoking point of 450 degrees F, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods like frying. On the other hand, unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of fresh coconuts and has a smoking point of 350 degrees F. Unrefined coconut oil retains its distinct aroma and flavor, which are lost during the refining process. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized and has no discernible taste or smell, while unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.\", \"The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their taste, aroma, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts and has a high smoking point of 450 degrees Fahrenheit, making it suitable for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. It has lost its coconut flavor and aroma due to the refining process. On the other hand, unrefined coconut oil comes from fresh coconuts and has a lower smoking point of 350 degrees Fahrenheit. It retains its distinct coconut flavor and aroma, but has a milder coconut taste compared to the full-bodied flavor of refined coconut oil.\"]", "time_sec": 21.111, "generation_time_seconds": 20.3115, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7949, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 37191, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 15448, 304, 862, 5670, 1882, 11, 12656, 11, 323, 8628, 24098, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 31620, 1062, 443, 6128, 11, 1393, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 11, 1083, 3881, 438, 10526, 476, 35899, 33457, 5590, 11, 374, 1865, 504, 7722, 1062, 443, 6128, 13, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 12460, 54179, 323, 17172, 11, 892, 374, 5558, 2337, 279, 73185, 1882, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 5080, 19578, 1459, 315, 220, 19, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 7707, 311, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 594, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 11, 3259, 432, 264, 2664, 2999, 369, 1550, 12, 34558, 17233, 5413, 1741, 438, 86096, 13, 22406, 11, 37191, 33457, 5590, 374, 409, 48917, 1506, 11, 12942, 304, 902, 41545, 1238, 12656, 476, 22068, 11, 19853, 650, 1097, 1589, 5590, 23377, 264, 23034, 33457, 17172, 323, 54179, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between refined and unrefined coconut oil lies in their production process, taste, and heat tolerance. Refined coconut oil is made from dried coconuts, while unrefined coconut oil, also known as pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor, which is lost during the refining process. Refined coconut oil has a higher smoking point of 450 degrees F compared to unrefined coconut oil's 350 degrees F, making it a better option for high-temperature cooking methods such as frying. Additionally, refined coconut oil is deodorized, resulting in no discernible taste or smell, whereas unrefined oil carries a mild coconut flavor and aroma.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.04601387527121, "g_worst_claim": 0.07960230112075806, "g_content": 1.323243574662642, "g_traj_mean": 1.004795789718628}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [3945, 1589, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 31620, 33457, 13779, 11, 1393, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 11, 1083, 2598, 10526, 476, 35899, 33457, 5590, 11, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 24955, 315, 279, 7722, 1062, 443, 6128, 13, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 702, 264, 12460, 54179, 323, 17172, 429, 374, 5558, 2337, 73185, 13, 151645], "pred": "Refined coconut oil is made from the dried coconut fruit, while unrefined coconut oil, also called pure or virgin coconut oil, is made from the flesh of the fresh coconuts. Unrefined coconut oil has a distinct aroma and flavor that is lost during refining.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3616202804888664, "g_worst_claim": 0.8201243082682291, "g_content": 2.0755281801576966, "g_traj_mean": 1.3441381454467773}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 37191, 323, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 15448, 304, 862, 17975, 5413, 11, 19578, 3501, 11, 323, 31423, 13, 431, 4006, 33457, 5590, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 31620, 33457, 13779, 323, 702, 264, 19578, 1459, 315, 220, 19, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 11, 3259, 432, 14452, 369, 1550, 12, 34558, 17233, 5413, 1075, 86096, 13, 1913, 279, 1008, 1424, 11, 650, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 11, 1083, 3881, 438, 10526, 476, 35899, 33457, 5590, 11, 374, 1865, 504, 279, 24955, 315, 7722, 1062, 443, 6128, 323, 702, 264, 19578, 1459, 315, 220, 18, 20, 15, 12348, 434, 13, 1230, 1097, 1589, 33457, 5590, 51844, 1181, 12460, 54179, 323, 17172, 11, 892, 525, 5558, 2