{"id": "480", "question": "change of address u.s. postal service", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"change of address u.s. postal service\":\n\nTo change your address with the U.S. Postal Service, you can visit the USPS website (moversguide.usps.com), call the USPS Call Center (1-800-ASK-USPS), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office. You can also use the USPS change of address feature to notify up to 100 organizations, including the Postal Service, with secure encryption technology to protect your data.", "pred": "The U.S. Postal Service offers a fast, versatile, and secure way to change your address, which can be done in as little as 1 minute. The service enables you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service (USPS) and ensures your data is safe with the latest encryption technologies. You can complete the U.S. Postal Service Official Change of Address form online, visit https://moversguide.usps.com/ to safeguard your personal information with identity validation by a simple $1 charge to your credit or debit card, or call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777).", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The U.S. Postal Service offers a fast, versatile, and secure way to change your address, which can be done in as little as 1 minute. The service enables you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service (USPS) and ensures your data is safe with the latest encryption technologies. You can complete the U.S. Postal Service Official Change of Address form online, visit https://moversguide.usps.com/ to safeguard your personal information with identity validation by a simple $1 charge to your credit or debit card, or call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777).", "cot": "[\"The U.S. Postal Service offers a change of address service that can be completed in as little as 1 minute. This service allows you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service (USPS). The service is secure, using the latest encryption technologies to ensure your data is safe. You can complete the change of address form online, or you can visit https://moversguide.usps.com/, call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office.\", \"The U.S. Postal Service offers a fast and versatile service to change your address in as little as one minute. You can notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service. The service uses secure encryption technologies to ensure your data is safe. To change your address, you can visit https://moversguide.usps.com/, call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575 at any U.S. Post Office.\", \"The U.S. Postal Service offers a change of address service that allows you to update your postal service address in as little as 1 minute. This feature is versatile, enabling you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service. The service is secure, using the latest encryption technologies to ensure the safety of your data. To change your address, you can visit https://moversguide.usps.com/, call the USPS Call Center at 1-800-ASK-USPS (1-800-275-8777), or fill out and submit PS Form 3575, which can be picked up at any U.S. Post Office.\", \"The U.S. Postal Service offers a fast, versatile, and secure way to change your address, which can be done in as little as 1 minute. The service enables you to notify up to 100 organizations in addition to the Postal Service (USPS) and ensures your data is safe with the latest encryption technologies. You can complete the U.S. Postal Service Official Change of Address form online, visit https://moversguide.usps.com/ to safeguard your personal information with identity validation by a simple $1 charge to 