{"id": "501", "question": "factors that cause oily skin", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the factors that cause oily skin are primarily genetic/hereditary factors and hormonal shifts in the body. Diet and poor hygiene/topical applications have a limited effect on the oiliness of the skin. Combination skin, which is a mix of oily and dry/normal areas, can also contribute to oily skin in certain areas such as the T-zone.", "pred": "Genetics, hormonal shifts, poor hygiene and topical applications, natural phenomenon, and combination skin.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Genetics, hormonal shifts, poor hygiene and topical applications, natural phenomenon, and combination skin.", "cot": "[\"Based on the provided passages, the factors that cause oily skin include:\\n\\n1. **Genetics**: Oily skin is hereditary, meaning if your parents have oily skin, there is a high likelihood that you will too. This is a significant factor mentioned in both passage 1 and passage 2.\\n\\n2. **Hormonal Shifts**: If your oily skin comes and goes, it may be more related to hormonal changes in your body rather than genetics. This is mentioned in passage 1.\\n\\n3. **Poor Hygiene and Topical Applications**: The passage 2 suggests that oily skin can be due to poor hygiene and the use of certain topical applications, although it does not provide specific details on these factors.\\n\\n4. **Natural Phenomenon**: The passage 2 also mentions that oily skin can be a natural phenomenon, not necessarily caused by external factors like diet or lifestyle.\\n\\n5. **Combination Skin**: Some people have combination skin, which can produce oily skin in certain areas, such as the T-zone (nose, forehead, and chin). This is mentioned in passage 3.\\n\\nAnswer: Genetics, hormonal shifts, poor hygiene and topical applications, natural phenomenon, and combination skin.\", \"Factors that cause oily skin can be attributed to genetics, hormonal shifts, and poor hygiene. Diet plays a minor role, as suggested by the myth that greasy foods like pizza can cause oily skin, but clinical studies indicate that diet does not significantly affect skin oiliness.\", \"Genetics\", \"Based on the provided passage, the factors that cause oily skin include:\\n\\n1. Genetic inheritance: If your parents have oily skin, you are likely to inherit this trait.\\n2. Hormonal shifts: Oily skin that comes and goes may be more related to hormonal changes in your body rather than genetics.\\n3. Diet: While diet can affect acne, it does not cause oily skin. \\n4. Poor hygiene: Oily skin may be due to poor hygiene practices.\\n5. Topical applications: Certain topical treatments or products may contribute to oily skin.\\n\\nIt's important to note that oily skin is typically characterized by skin that feels 'oily' or appears 'shiny', particularly on the face.\"]", "time_sec": 19.373, "generation_time_seconds": 18.5593, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8028, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 279, 9363, 429, 5240, 77471, 6787, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 9967, 24279, 95518, 506, 1541, 6787, 374, 1059, 94354, 11, 7290, 421, 697, 6562, 614, 77471, 6787, 11, 1052, 374, 264, 1550, 28636, 429, 498, 686, 2238, 13, 1096, 374, 264, 5089, 8168, 9733, 304, 2176, 21085, 220, 16, 323, 21085, 220, 17, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 39, 493, 24202, 26510, 82, 95518, 1416, 697, 77471, 6787, 4041, 323, 5780, 11, 432, 1231, 387, 803, 5435, 311, 73118, 4344, 304, 697, 2487, 4751, 1091, 55004, 13, 1096, 374, 9733, 304, 21085, 220, 16, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 84103, 10112, 42212, 323, 6909, 938, 31525, 95518, 576, 21085, 220, 17, 13230, 429, 77471, 6787, 646, 387, 4152, 311, 7852, 51956, 323, 279, 990, 315, 3654, 65276, 8357, 11, 7892, 432, 1558, 537, 3410, 3151, 3565, 389, 1493, 9363, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 54281, 68783, 6297, 263, 95518, 576, 21085, 220, 17, 1083, 33845, 429, 77471, 6787, 646, 387, 264, 5810, 24844, 11, 537, 14312, 8881, 553, 9250, 9363, 1075, 9968, 476, 18899, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 36192, 2554, 26951, 95518, 4329, 1251, 614, 10601, 6787, 11, 892, 646, 8193, 77471, 6787, 304, 3654, 5671, 11, 1741, 438, 279, 350, 77763, 320, 77, 960, 11, 51254, 11, 323, 45075, 568, 1096, 374, 9733, 304, 21085, 220, 18, 382, 16141, 25, 83286, 11, 73118, 28635, 11, 7852, 51956, 323, 65276, 8357, 11, 5810, 24844, 11, 323, 10601, 6787, 13, 151645], "pred": "Genetics, hormonal shifts, poor hygiene and topical applications, natural phenomenon, and combination skin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6028955497027535, "g_worst_claim": -0.044021621346473694, "g_content": 1.0822160584586007, "g_traj_mean": 0.7503721117973328}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [97769, 429, 5240, 77471, 6787, 646, 387, 29606, 311, 55004, 11, 73118, 28635, 11, 323, 7852, 51956, 13, 26212, 11088, 264, 8922, 3476, 11, 438, 11827, 553, 279, 21163, 429, 2816, 6405, 15298, 1075, 22502, 646, 5240, 77471, 6787, 11, 714, 14490, 7822, 13216, 429, 9968, 1558, 537, 11941, 7802, 6787, 5590, 1880, 13, 151645], "pred": "Factors that cause oily skin can be attributed to genetics, hormonal shifts, and poor hygiene. Diet plays a minor role, as suggested by the myth that greasy foods like pizza can cause oily skin, but clinical studies indicate that diet does not significantly affect skin oiliness.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.163612177490672, "g_worst_claim": 0.5070076669965472, "g_content": 1.3821027278900146, "g_traj_mean": 0.9102944135665894}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [9967, 24279, 151645], "pred": "Genetics", "grounding_scores": null}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 21085, 11, 279, 9363, 429, 5240, 77471, 6787, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 74126, 41822, 25, 1416, 697, 6562, 614, 77471, 6787, 11, 498, 525, 4363, 311, 23749, 419, 17567, 624, 17, 13, 91108, 24202, 28635, 25, 506, 1541, 6787, 429