{"id": "503", "question": "factors that cause oily skin", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the main factors that contribute to oily skin are:\n\n1. Genetics: According to passage 1, oily skin is hereditary, meaning that if one's parents have oily skin, they are more likely to experience it themselves.\n2. Hormonal shifts: Passage 1 suggests that hormonal changes in the body can cause oily skin to come and go.\n3. Diet: While diet can aggravate acne, it does not directly cause oily skin, according to passage 1.\n4. Poor hygiene: Passage 2 mentions that poor hygiene and topical applications can contribute to oily skin.\n5. Combination skin: Passage 3 defines different skin types, including combination skin, which can be prone to oily skin in certain areas, such as the T-zone.\n\nThere is no additional information provided in the passages to suggest other factors that might contribute to oily skin. Therefore, the answer to the question is based on the information provided in the passages.", "pred": "Other factors not mentioned in the provided passage include the type of skin care products used, environmental factors, and lifestyle habits.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Other factors not mentioned in the provided passage include the type of skin care products used, environmental factors, and lifestyle habits.", "cot": "[\"Based on the provided passages, the factors that cause oily skin include:\\n\\n1. **Genetics**: Oily skin is hereditary, meaning if your parents have oily skin, there is a high likelihood that you will too. This is a significant factor mentioned in both passage 1 and passage 2.\\n\\n2. **Hormonal Shifts**: If your oily skin comes and goes, it may be more related to hormonal changes in your body rather than genetics. This is mentioned in passage 1.\\n\\n3. **Poor Hygiene and Topical Applications**: The passage 2 suggests that oily skin can be due to poor hygiene and the use of certain topical applications, although it does not provide specific details on these factors.\\n\\n4. **Natural Phenomenon**: The passage 2 also mentions that oily skin can be a natural phenomenon, not necessarily caused by external factors like diet or lifestyle.\\n\\n5. **Combination Skin**: Some people have combination skin, which can produce oily skin in certain areas, such as the T-zone (nose, forehead, and chin). This is mentioned in passage 3.\\n\\nAnswer: Genetics, hormonal shifts, poor hygiene and topical applications, natural phenomenon, and combination skin.\", \"Based on the information provided in the passages, the factors that cause oily skin include:\\n\\n1. Genetics: The truth is that oily skin is hereditary. People with oily skin often wonder what they're doing to cause the problem, but the truth is they should probably blame their genes. This is supported by the statement, \\\"If your mom or dad has oily skin, chances are you will, too.\\\"\\n\\n2. Hormonal shifts: If your oily skin comes and goes, it may have less to do with genes and more to do with hormonal shifts in your body. This is supported by the statement, \\\"However, if your oily skin comes and goes, it may have less to do with genes and more to do with hormonal shifts in your body.\\\"\\n\\n3. Diet: Although diet can aggravate acne, it doesn't cause oily skin. Diet can play a role in the oiliness of the skin, but it is not the primary cause. This is supported by the statement, \\\"Diet can aggravate acne, but it doesn't cause oily skin.\\\"\\n\\n4. Hygiene and topical applications: It is important to identify if the oiliness is a natural phenomenon or due to poor hygiene and topical applications. This is supported by the statement, \\\"It is important to first identify if this 'oiliness' is a natural phenomenon or due to poor hygiene and topical applications.\\\"\\n\\n5. Combination skin: Some people have combination skin, which can produce overly dilated pores, blackheads, and shiny skin. This is supported by the statement, \\\"Combination skin can produce: 1 Overly dilated pores. 2 Blackheads. 3 Shiny skin.\\\"\\n\\nAnswer:[Genetics, hormonal shifts, diet, hygiene and topical applications, combination skin]\", \"Based on the provided passage, the factors that cause oily skin include:\\n\\n1. Heredity: The passage states that \\\"oily skin is hereditary,\\\" and if one's parents have oily skin, there is a high chance that the individual will also have it.\\n\\n2. Hormonal shifts: The passage mentions that \\\"if your oily skin comes and goes, it may have less to do with genes and more to do with hormonal shifts in your body.\\\"\\n\\n3. Diet: While the passage does not explicitly state that diet causes oily skin, it does mention that \\\"diet can aggravate acne, but it doesn't cause oily skin,\\\" suggesting that diet may have an indirect effect on oily skin.\\n\\nOther factors not mentioned in the provided passage include the type of skin care products used, environmental factors, and lifestyle habits.\", \"Factors that cause oily skin include genetics, hormonal shifts, and poor hygiene. Diet can aggravate acne but does not directly cause oily skin.\"]", "time_sec": 30.812, "generation_time_seconds": 29.5552, "selection_time_seconds": 1.2515, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 279, 9363, 429, 5240, 77471, 6787, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 9967, 24279, 95518, 506, 1541, 6787, 374, 1059, 94354, 11, 7290, 421, 697, 6562, 614, 77471, 6787, 11, 1052, 374, 264, 1550, 28636, 429, 498, 686, 2238, 13, 1096, 374, 264, 5089, 8168, 9733, 304, 2176, 21085, 220, 16, 323, 21085, 220, 17, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 39, 493, 24202, 26510, 82, 95518, 1416, 697, 77471, 6787, 4041, 323, 5780, 11, 432, 1231, 387, 803, 5435, 311, 73118, 4344, 304, 697, 2487, 4751, 1091, 55004, 13, 1096, 374, 9733, 304, 21085, 220, 16, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 84103, 10112, 42212, 323, 6909, 938, 31525, 95518, 576, 21085, 220, 17, 13230, 429, 77471, 6787, 646, 387, 4152, 311, 7852, 51956, 323, 279, 990, 315, 3654, 65276, 8357, 11, 7892, 432, 1558, 537, 3410, 3151, 3565, 389, 1493, 9363, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 54281, 68783, 6297, 263, 95518, 576, 21085, 220, 17, 1083, 33845, 429, 77471, 6787, 646, 387, 264, 5810, 24844, 11, 537, 14312, 8881, 553, 9250, 9363, 1075, 9968, 476, 18899, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 36192, 2554, 26951, 95518, 4329, 1251, 614, 10601, 6787, 11, 892, 646, 8193, 77471, 6787, 304, 3654, 5671, 11, 1741, 438, 279, 350, 77763, 320, 77, 960, 11, 51254, 11, 323, 45075, 568, 1096, 374, 9733, 304, 21085, 220, 18, 382, 16141, 25, 83286, 11, 73118, 28635, 11, 7852, 51956, 323, 65276, 8357, 11, 5810, 24844, 11, 323, 10601, 6787, 13, 151645], "pred": "Genetics, hormonal shifts, poor hygiene and topical applications, natural phenomenon, and combination skin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6184317184692033, "g_worst_claim": -0.04718161125977834, "g_content": 1.1300005231584822, "g_traj_mean": 0.770540714263916}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 1995, 3897, 304, 279, 46769, 11, 279, 9363, 429, 5240, 77471, 6787, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 83286, 25, 576, 8046, 374, 429, 77471, 6787, 374, 1059, 94354, 13, 8853, 448, 77471, 6787, 3545, 5775, 1128, 807, 2299, 3730, 311, 5240, 279, 3491, 11, 714, 279, 8046, 374, 807, 1265, 4658, 18555, 862, 20727, 13, 1096, 374, 7248, 553, 279, 5114, 11, 330, 2679, 697, 3368, 476, 17760, 702, 77471, 6787, 11, 16963, 525, 498, 686, 11, 2238, 2217, 17, 13, 91108, 24202, 28635, 25, 1416, 697, 77471, 6787, 4041, 323, 5780, 11, 432, 1231, 614, 2686, 311, 653, 448, 20727, 323, 803, 311, 653, 448, 73118, 28635, 304, 697, 2487, 13, 1096, 374, 7248, 553, 279, 5114, 11, 330, 11209, 11, 421, 697, 77471, 6787, 4041, 323, 5780, 11, 432, 1231, 614, 2686, 311, 653, 448, 20727, 323, 803, 311, 653, 448, 73118, 28635, 304, 697, 2487, 2217, 18, 13, 26212, 25, 10328, 9968, 646, 44941, 349, 45805, 11, 432, 3171, 944, 5240, 77471, 6787, 13, 26212, 646, 1486, 264, 3476, 304, 279, 5590, 1880, 315, 279, 6787, 11, 714, 432, 374, 537, 279, 6028, 5240, 13, 1096, 374, 7248, 553, 279, 5114, 11, 330, 35, 3891, 646, 44941, 349, 45805, 11, 714, 432, 3171, 944, 5240, 77471, 6787, 2217, 19, 13, 10112, 42212, 323, 65276, 8357, 25, 1084, 374, 2989, 311, 10542, 421, 279, 5590, 1880, 374, 264, 5810, 24844, 476, 4152, 311, 7852, 51956, 323, 65276, 8357, 13, 1096, 374, 7248, 553, 279, 5114, 11, 330, 2132, 374, 2989, 311, 1156, 10542, 421, 419, 364, 73813, 1880, 6, 374, 264, 5810, 24844, 476, 4152, 311, 7852, 51956, 323, 65276, 8357, 2217, 20, 13, 85856, 6787, 25, 4329, 1251, 614, 10601, 6787, 11, 892, 646, 8193, 38432, 18840, 657, 70928, 11, 3691, 35810, 11, 323, 41199, 6787, 13, 1096, 374, 7248, 553, 279, 5114, 11, 330, 36192, 2554, 6787, 646, 8193, 25, 220, 16, 6065, 398, 18840, 657, 70928, 13, 220, 17, 5235, 35810, 13, 220, 18, 1417, 6441, 6787, 2217, 16141, 7259, 9967, 24279, 11, 73118, 28635, 11, 9968, 11, 51956, 323, 65276, 8357, 11, 10601, 6787, 60, 151645], "pred": "Genetics, hormonal shifts, diet, hygiene and topical applications, combination skin", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8421498643704305, "g_worst_claim": -0.03556536138057709, "g_content": 1.4354611249037192, "g_traj_mean": 0.9789977073669434}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 21085, 11, 279, 9363, 429, 5240, 77471, 6787, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 6252, 291, 487, 25, 576, 21085, 5302, 429, 330, 78, 1541, 6787, 374, 1059, 94354, 1335, 323, 421, 825, 594, 6562, 614, 77471, 6787, 11, 1052, 374, 264, 1550, 6012, 429, 279, 3842, 686, 1083, 614, 432, 382, 17, 13, 91108, 24202, 28635, 25, 576, 21085, 33845, 429, 330, 333, 697, 77471, 6787, 4041, 323, 5780, 11, 432, 1231, 614, 2686, 311, 653, 448, 20727, 323, 803, 311, 653, 448, 73118, 28635, 304, 697, 2487, 2217, 18, 13, 26212, 25, 5976, 279, 21085, 1558, 537, 20975, 1584, 429, 9968, 11137, 77471, 6787, 11, 432, 1558, 6286, 429, 330, 93842, 646, 44941, 349, 45805, 11, 714, 432, 3171, 944, 5240, 77471, 6787, 1335, 22561, 429, 9968, 1231, 614, 458, 24614, 2456, 389, 77471, 6787, 382, 11409, 9363, 537, 9733, 304, 279, 3897, 21085, 2924, 279, 943, 315, 6787, 2453, 3871, 1483, 11, 12158, 9363, 11, 323, 18899, 25785, 13, 151645], "pred": "Other factors not mentioned in the provided passage include the type of skin care products used, environmental factors, and lifestyle habits.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.6567332672322642, "g_worst_claim": -0.25032562017440796, "g_content": 0.9718070652173914, "g_traj_mean": 0.741829514503479}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [97769, 429, 5240, 77471, 6787, 2924, 55004, 11, 73118, 28635, 11, 323, 7852, 51956, 13, 26212, 646, 44941, 349, 45805, 714, 1558, 537, 5961, 5240, 77471, 6787, 13, 151645], "pred": "Factors that cause oily skin include genetics, hormonal shifts, and poor hygiene. Diet can aggravate acne but does not directly cause oily skin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7927532692750296, "g_worst_claim": 1.2551320791244507, "g_content": 2.578684189740349, "g_traj_mean": 1.6350293159484863}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 11.11, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "504", "question": "what are the characteristics of tropical rainforest floor", "gt": "The floor of a tropical rainforest biome is characterized by a fast rate of decay due to the heat and moisture. This decay provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow. Various types of fruits, nuts, herbs, and mushrooms grow on the rainforest floor. Additionally, vines and ferns grow all over the rainforest, including the floor, helping to connect the various layers of the biome.", "pred": "tropical rainforest floor is characterized by an abundance of vegetation including herbs, ferns, mushrooms, and diverse plants and trees. It is also noted for its rich nutrients resulting from the rapid decomposition of dead plants and animals, which supports the growth of new vegetation.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "tropical rainforest floor is characterized by an abundance of vegetation including herbs, ferns, mushrooms, and diverse plants and trees. It is also noted for its rich nutrients resulting from the rapid decomposition of dead plants and animals, which supports the growth of new vegetation.", "cot": "[\"Based on the provided passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include:\\n\\n1. **High Rainfall**: Tropical rainforests receive a significant amount of rainfall, with some areas getting up to 400 inches of rain annually. This high rainfall contributes to the humid climate and supports the growth of various plants and fungi.\\n\\n2. **Humid Climate**: The climate in tropical rainforests is very humid due to the constant moisture from the rain. This humidity is crucial for the survival of many plant species that thrive in such conditions.\\n\\n3. **Decomposition of Dead Matter**: The rapid decomposition of dead plants and animals on the floor provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow. This nutrient-rich environment supports a diverse range of flora and fauna.\\n\\n4. **Presence of Vines and Ferns**: Vines and ferns are common on the floor of tropical rainforests. These plants help to connect the various layers of the biome, providing support and habitat for other organisms.\\n\\n5. **Diverse Plant Life**: The floor of the tropical rainforest is home to a variety of plants, including herbs, mushrooms, and various types of fruits and nuts. For example, bananas grow on vines in this biome.\\n\\n6. **Support for Other Organisms**: The floor provides a habitat for a range of organisms, from small insects to larger animals, which rely on the floor for food and shelter.\\n\\nThese characteristics collectively contribute to the rich biodiversity and unique ecosystem of the tropical rainforest.\", \"The tropical rainforest floor is characterized by dense vegetation, including various types of plants such as vines, ferns, and mushrooms. These plants are adapted to the high humidity and rainfall typical of the tropical rainforest environment. For example, bananas grow on vines in the tropical rainforest biome. The floor also supports a diverse array of fungi and other microorganisms that decompose fallen plants and animals, contributing to the nutrient-rich soil. This nutrient cycle is crucial for the growth of other plants, as mentioned in the passage.\", \"tropical rainforest floor is characterized by an abundance of vegetation including herbs, ferns, mushrooms, and diverse plants and trees. It is also noted for its rich nutrients resulting from the rapid decomposition of dead plants and animals, which supports the growth of new vegetation.\", \"Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include the presence of various plants and animals. The floor is home to herbs, mushrooms, and various types of fruits and nuts that grow on the plants and in the trees. An example provided is bananas, which grow on vines in the tropical rainforest biome. The floor is also characterized by the rapid decay of plant and animal matter due to the warm and humid conditions, providing nutrients for other plants to grow from.\"]", "time_sec": 23.089, "generation_time_seconds": 22.2628, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8191, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 279, 17452, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 11976, 21911, 13464, 95518, 70243, 11174, 1324, 36279, 5258, 264, 5089, 3311, 315, 52858, 11, 448, 1045, 5671, 3709, 705, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 14924, 315, 11174, 29071, 13, 1096, 1550, 52858, 42972, 311, 279, 65938, 9977, 323, 11554, 279, 6513, 315, 5257, 10779, 323, 80440, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 48519, 307, 30536, 95518, 576, 9977, 304, 34048, 11174, 1324, 36279, 374, 1602, 65938, 4152, 311, 279, 6783, 31157, 504, 279, 11174, 13, 1096, 37093, 374, 16587, 369, 279, 19661, 315, 1657, 6008, 9419, 429, 40872, 304, 1741, 4682, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 4900, 316, 3487, 315, 15021, 33364, 95518, 576, 11048, 65166, 315, 5593, 10779, 323, 9898, 389, 279, 6422, 5707, 9080, 36393, 369, 1008, 10779, 311, 3063, 13, 1096, 49023, 40847, 4573, 11554, 264, 16807, 2088, 315, 80988, 323, 98914, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 89169, 315, 647, 1543, 323, 25987, 82, 95518, 647, 1543, 323, 87024, 82, 525, 4185, 389, 279, 6422, 315, 34048, 11174, 1324, 36279, 13, 4220, 10779, 1492, 311, 4564, 279, 5257, 13617, 315, 279, 83610, 11, 8241, 1824, 323, 38546, 369, 1008, 43204, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 35, 8034, 17838, 9414, 95518, 576, 6422, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 374, 2114, 311, 264, 8045, 315, 10779, 11, 2670, 41293, 11, 47151, 11, 323, 5257, 4494, 315, 25322, 323, 29949, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 67342, 3063, 389, 85429, 304, 419, 83610, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 7916, 369, 6944, 10762, 13664, 95518, 576, 6422, 5707, 264, 38546, 369, 264, 2088, 315, 43204, 11, 504, 2613, 40811, 311, 8131, 9898, 11, 892, 17188, 389, 279, 6422, 369, 3607, 323, 22906, 382, 9485, 17452, 44825, 16792, 311, 279, 9080, 72019, 323, 4911, 24982, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 13, 151645], "pred": "These characteristics collectively contribute to the rich biodiversity and unique ecosystem of the tropical rainforest.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8051799162196067, "g_worst_claim": 0.03673127293586731, "g_content": 1.139082022592531, "g_traj_mean": 0.6690711975097656}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 374, 31871, 553, 27950, 53732, 11, 2670, 5257, 4494, 315, 10779, 1741, 438, 85429, 11, 87024, 82, 11, 323, 47151, 13, 4220, 10779, 525, 29364, 311, 279, 1550, 37093, 323, 52858, 14260, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 4573, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 67342, 3063, 389, 85429, 304, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 83610, 13, 576, 6422, 1083, 11554, 264, 16807, 1334, 315, 80440, 323, 1008, 8003, 75891, 429, 28502, 2900, 20866, 10779, 323, 9898, 11, 28720, 311, 279, 49023, 40847, 17171, 13, 1096, 49023, 10775, 374, 16587, 369, 279, 6513, 315, 1008, 10779, 11, 438, 9733, 304, 279, 21085, 13, 151645], "pred": "The tropical rainforest floor is characterized by dense vegetation, including various types of plants such as vines, ferns, and mushrooms. These plants are adapted to the high humidity and rainfall typical of the tropical rainforest environment. For example, bananas grow on vines in the tropical rainforest biome. The floor also supports a diverse array of fungi and other microorganisms that decompose fallen plants and animals, contributing to the nutrient-rich soil. This nutrient cycle is crucial for the growth of other plants, as mentioned in the passage.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7204844391633303, "g_worst_claim": 0.000174592352575726, "g_content": 1.0476218243034519, "g_traj_mean": 0.6694642305374146}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [83, 50072, 11174, 50655, 6422, 374, 31871, 553, 458, 36392, 315, 53732, 2670, 41293, 11, 87024, 82, 11, 47151, 11, 323, 16807, 10779, 323, 12408, 13, 1084, 374, 1083, 10342, 369, 1181, 9080, 36393, 12942, 504, 279, 11048, 65166, 315, 5593, 10779, 323, 9898, 11, 892, 11554, 279, 6513, 315, 501, 53732, 13, 151645], "pred": "tropical rainforest floor is characterized by an abundance of vegetation including herbs, ferns, mushrooms, and diverse plants and trees. It is also noted for its rich nutrients resulting from the rapid decomposition of dead plants and animals, which supports the growth of new vegetation.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.899447379718747, "g_worst_claim": 0.7888981103897095, "g_content": 1.4577507019042968, "g_traj_mean": 0.8914539813995361}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 46769, 11, 279, 17452, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 2924, 279, 9362, 315, 5257, 10779, 323, 9898, 13, 576, 6422, 374, 2114, 311, 41293, 11, 47151, 11, 323, 5257, 4494, 315, 25322, 323, 29949, 429, 3063, 389, 279, 10779, 323, 304, 279, 12408, 13, 1527, 3110, 3897, 374, 67342, 11, 892, 3063, 389, 85429, 304, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 83610, 13, 576, 6422, 374, 1083, 31871, 553, 279, 11048, 30715, 315, 6008, 323, 9864, 4925, 4152, 311, 279, 8205, 323, 65938, 4682, 11, 8241, 36393, 369, 1008, 10779, 311, 3063, 504, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include the presence of various plants and animals. The floor is home to herbs, mushrooms, and various types of fruits and nuts that grow on the plants and in the trees. An example provided is bananas, which grow on vines in the tropical rainforest biome. The floor is also characterized by the rapid decay of plant and animal matter due to the warm and humid conditions, providing nutrients for other plants to grow from.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.195109882097517, "g_worst_claim": 0.40871585499156604, "g_content": 1.6559484730596128, "g_traj_mean": 1.1298458576202393}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 31.43, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "507", "question": "what are the characteristics of tropical rainforest floor", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor are:\n\n1. High levels of rainfall, with some areas receiving up to 400 inches of rain annually.\n2. High humidity due to the large amount of rainfall.\n3. Abundant vegetation, including tall trees, vines, ferns, herbs, mushrooms, fruits, and nuts.\n4. Quick decay of plant and animal matter due to the heat and moisture, which provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow.\n5. Presence of bananas growing on vines.\n\nTherefore, the tropical rainforest floor is characterized by high rainfall, humidity, and lush vegetation, with a diverse array of plant species and a rapid rate of decay and nutrient cycling.", "pred": "These characteristics collectively contribute to the rich biodiversity and unique ecosystem of the tropical rainforest.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "These characteristics collectively contribute to the rich biodiversity and unique ecosystem of the tropical rainforest.", "cot": "[\"Based on the provided passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include:\\n\\n1. **High Rainfall**: Tropical rainforests receive a significant amount of rainfall, with some areas getting up to 400 inches of rain annually. This high rainfall contributes to the humid climate and supports the growth of various plants and fungi.\\n\\n2. **Humid Climate**: The climate in tropical rainforests is very humid due to the constant moisture from the rain. This humidity is crucial for the survival of many plant species that thrive in such conditions.\\n\\n3. **Decomposition of Dead Matter**: The rapid decomposition of dead plants and animals on the floor provides rich nutrients for other plants to grow. This nutrient-rich environment supports a diverse range of flora and fauna.\\n\\n4. **Presence of Vines and Ferns**: Vines and ferns are common on the floor of tropical rainforests. These plants help to connect the various layers of the biome, providing support and habitat for other organisms.\\n\\n5. **Diverse Plant Life**: The floor of the tropical rainforest is home to a variety of plants, including herbs, mushrooms, and various types of fruits and nuts. For example, bananas grow on vines in this biome.\\n\\n6. **Support for Other Organisms**: The floor provides a habitat for a range of organisms, from small insects to larger animals, which rely on the floor for food and shelter.\\n\\nThese characteristics collectively contribute to the rich biodiversity and unique ecosystem of the tropical rainforest.\", \"The characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include the presence of herbs, mushrooms, and a variety of fruits and nuts. These plants help to connect the various layers found in the biome. For example, there are herbs and mushrooms that grow on the floor, and various types of fruits and nuts grow on the plants and in the trees.\", \"Based on the provided passages, the characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include:\\n\\n1. Abundance of Vines and Ferns: Vines and ferns are prevalent on the floor of the tropical rainforest, helping to connect the various layers found in the biome.\\n2. Variety of Plants and Mushrooms: Various types of fruits and nuts grow on the plants and in the trees. Additionally, herbs and mushrooms are found on the floor.\\n3. Decay and Nutrients: Due to the heat and moisture, plants and animals that die rot quickly, providing rich nutrients for other plants to grow from.\\n\\nIn summary, the tropical rainforest floor is characterized by a diverse array of plants, including vines, ferns, fruits, nuts, herbs, and mushrooms. The rapid decay of organic matter due to the heat and moisture also supports a rich ecosystem with ample nutrients for growth.\", \"Floor of the tropical rainforest biome is covered with various types of vegetation such as herbs, mushrooms, and vines. Some examples of plants found on the floor include bananas. The floor is also a place where dead plants and animals rot quickly due to the heat and moisture, providing rich nutrients for other plants to grow from.\"]", "time_sec": 24.165, "generation_time_seconds": 23.5424, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6162, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 279, 17452, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 11976, 21911, 13464, 95518, 70243, 11174, 1324, 36279, 5258, 264, 5089, 3311, 315, 52858, 11, 448, 1045, 5671, 3709, 705, 311, 220, 19, 15, 15, 14924, 315, 11174, 29071, 13, 1096, 1550, 52858, 42972, 311, 279, 65938, 9977, 323, 11554, 279, 6513, 315, 5257, 10779, 323, 80440, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 48519, 307, 30536, 95518, 576, 9977, 304, 34048, 11174, 1324, 36279, 374, 1602, 65938, 4152, 311, 279, 6783, 31157, 504, 279, 11174, 13, 1096, 37093, 374, 16587, 369, 279, 19661, 315, 1657, 6008, 9419, 429, 40872, 304, 1741, 4682, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 4900, 316, 3487, 315, 15021, 33364, 95518, 576, 11048, 65166, 315, 5593, 10779, 323, 9898, 389, 279, 6422, 5707, 9080, 36393, 369, 1008, 10779, 311, 3063, 13, 1096, 49023, 40847, 4573, 11554, 264, 16807, 2088, 315, 80988, 323, 98914, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 89169, 315, 647, 1543, 323, 25987, 82, 95518, 647, 1543, 323, 87024, 82, 525, 4185, 389, 279, 6422, 315, 34048, 11174, 1324, 36279, 13, 4220, 10779, 1492, 311, 4564, 279, 5257, 13617, 315, 279, 83610, 11, 8241, 1824, 323, 38546, 369, 1008, 43204, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 35, 8034, 17838, 9414, 95518, 576, 6422, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 374, 2114, 311, 264, 8045, 315, 10779, 11, 2670, 41293, 11, 47151, 11, 323, 5257, 4494, 315, 25322, 323, 29949, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 67342, 3063, 389, 85429, 304, 419, 83610, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 7916, 369, 6944, 10762, 13664, 95518, 576, 6422, 5707, 264, 38546, 369, 264, 2088, 315, 43204, 11, 504, 2613, 40811, 311, 8131, 9898, 11, 892, 17188, 389, 279, 6422, 369, 3607, 323, 22906, 382, 9485, 17452, 44825, 16792, 311, 279, 9080, 72019, 323, 4911, 24982, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 13, 151645], "pred": "These characteristics collectively contribute to the rich biodiversity and unique ecosystem of the tropical rainforest.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8004707156641777, "g_worst_claim": 0.028888123109936714, "g_content": 1.1196218720564606, "g_traj_mean": 0.6595261693000793}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 17452, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 2924, 279, 9362, 315, 41293, 11, 47151, 11, 323, 264, 8045, 315, 25322, 323, 29949, 13, 4220, 10779, 1492, 311, 4564, 279, 5257, 13617, 1730, 304, 279, 83610, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 1052, 525, 41293, 323, 47151, 429, 3063, 389, 279, 6422, 11, 323, 5257, 4494, 315, 25322, 323, 29949, 3063, 389, 279, 10779, 323, 304, 279, 12408, 13, 151645], "pred": "The characteristics of the tropical rainforest floor include the presence of herbs, mushrooms, and a variety of fruits and nuts. These plants help to connect the various layers found in the biome. For example, there are herbs and mushrooms that grow on the floor, and various types of fruits and nuts grow on the plants and in the trees.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.662332654166055, "g_worst_claim": 1.213294809514826, "g_content": 2.744254557291667, "g_traj_mean": 1.6613683700561523}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 279, 17452, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 2924, 1447, 16, 13, 3680, 97581, 315, 647, 1543, 323, 25987, 82, 25, 647, 1543, 323, 87024, 82, 525, 45841, 389, 279, 6422, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 11, 10476, 311, 4564, 279, 5257, 13617, 1730, 304, 279, 83610, 624, 17, 13, 70732, 315, 49198, 323, 58105, 9750, 25, 39641, 4494, 315, 25322, 323, 29949, 3063, 389, 279, 10779, 323, 304, 279, 12408, 13, 22406, 11, 41293, 323, 47151, 525, 1730, 389, 279, 6422, 624, 18, 13, 97286, 323, 18372, 31830, 25, 23662, 311, 279, 8628, 323, 31157, 11, 10779, 323, 9898, 429, 2746, 5749, 6157, 11, 8241, 9080, 36393, 369, 1008, 10779, 311, 3063, 504, 382, 641, 12126, 11, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 6422, 374, 31871, 553, 264, 16807, 1334, 315, 10779, 11, 2670, 85429, 11, 87024, 82, 11, 25322, 11, 29949, 11, 41293, 11, 323, 47151, 13, 576, 11048, 30715, 315, 17356, 4925, 4152, 311, 279, 8628, 323, 31157, 1083, 11554, 264, 9080, 24982, 448, 41753, 36393, 369, 6513, 13, 151645], "pred": "In summary, the tropical rainforest floor is characterized by a diverse array of plants, including vines, ferns, fruits, nuts, herbs, and mushrooms. The rapid decay of organic matter due to the heat and moisture also supports a rich ecosystem with ample nutrients for growth.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1373113967530226, "g_worst_claim": 0.04808791194643293, "g_content": 1.6938448986375187, "g_traj_mean": 0.9721260070800781}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [51444, 315, 279, 34048, 11174, 50655, 83610, 374, 9761, 448, 5257, 4494, 315, 53732, 1741, 438, 41293, 11, 47151, 11, 323, 85429, 13, 4329, 10295, 315, 10779, 1730, 389, 279, 6422, 2924, 67342, 13, 576, 6422, 374, 1083, 264, 1992, 1380, 5593, 10779, 323, 9898, 5749, 6157, 4152, 311, 279, 8628, 323, 31157, 11, 8241, 9080, 36393, 369, 1008, 10779, 311, 3063, 504, 13, 151645], "pred": "Floor of the tropical rainforest biome is covered with various types of vegetation such as herbs, mushrooms, and vines. Some examples of plants found on the floor include bananas. The floor is also a place where dead plants and animals rot quickly due to the heat and moisture, providing rich nutrients for other plants to grow from.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.419971381052576, "g_worst_claim": 1.268295955657959, "g_content": 2.2129921913146973, "g_traj_mean": 1.4410150051116943}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 9.3, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "508", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "gt": "Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and contain more of the tenderloin or fillet than sirloin steaks. They are essentially a larger version of the T-Bone steak, carved from a larger portion of the tenderloin. On the other hand, the sirloin steak is a steak cut from the back of the animal, continuing off the short loin from which T-bone, porterhouse, and club steaks are cut. The sirloin is divided into several different types of steak.", "pred": "The difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks.", "cot": "[\"The difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks.\", \"The difference between a sirloin steak and a porterhouse steak lies in the cutting location. A sirloin steak is cut from the back of the animal, which continues off the short loin. In contrast, a porterhouse steak is cut from further back on the sirloin, resulting in a larger slice that includes a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet compared to a T-bone steak. This difference in cutting location leads to a corresponding price difference between the two steaks.\", \"Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin, containing a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet.\", \"Sirloin steak is a steak cut from the back of the animal, while Porterhouse steak is cut from further back on the sirloin, containing more of the tenderloin.\"]", "time_sec": 12.589, "generation_time_seconds": 11.7432, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8425, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 323, 87186, 7675, 48959, 374, 429, 37937, 7675, 4087, 9810, 525, 3931, 504, 4623, 1182, 389, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 323, 8916, 6644, 264, 2699, 803, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 476, 1461, 1149, 1091, 350, 7671, 603, 4087, 9810, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8061466217041016, "g_worst_claim": 1.8061466217041016, "g_content": 2.368394724527995, "g_traj_mean": 1.7720972299575806}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 264, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 323, 264, 87186, 7675, 48959, 15448, 304, 279, 14376, 3728, 13, 362, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 374, 3931, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 9864, 11, 892, 9539, 1007, 279, 2805, 76960, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 264, 87186, 7675, 48959, 374, 3931, 504, 4623, 1182, 389, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 11, 12942, 304, 264, 8131, 15983, 429, 5646, 264, 2699, 803, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 476, 1461, 1149, 7707, 311, 264, 350, 1455, 603, 48959, 13, 1096, 6672, 304, 14376, 3728, 11508, 311, 264, 12159, 3349, 6672, 1948, 279, 1378, 4087, 9810, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between a sirloin steak and a porterhouse steak lies in the cutting location. A sirloin steak is cut from the back of the animal, which continues off the short loin. In contrast, a porterhouse steak is cut from further back on the sirloin, resulting in a larger slice that includes a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet compared to a T-bone steak. This difference in cutting location leads to a corresponding price difference between the two steaks.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4903316907690145, "g_worst_claim": 0.7861147608075824, "g_content": 2.185725784301758, "g_traj_mean": 1.3395559787750244}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [7084, 261, 7675, 4087, 9810, 525, 3931, 504, 4623, 1182, 389, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 11, 8482, 264, 2699, 803, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 476, 1461, 1149, 13, 151645], "pred": "Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin, containing a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9211245225026057, "g_worst_claim": 1.73316896878756, "g_content": 4.178417205810547, "g_traj_mean": 1.8932350873947144}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [50190, 385, 258, 48959, 374, 264, 48959, 3931, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 9864, 11, 1393, 37937, 7675, 48959, 374, 3931, 504, 4623, 1182, 389, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 11, 8482, 803, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 13, 151645], "pred": "Sirloin steak is a steak cut from the back of the animal, while Porterhouse steak is cut from further back on the sirloin, containing more of the tenderloin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4712855484750538, "g_worst_claim": 0.8233230710029602, "g_content": 3.154459733229417, "g_traj_mean": 1.5528991222381592}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 47.89, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "509", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that porterhouse steak is a larger version of T-Bone steak and it contains more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steak.", "pred": "Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks", "cot": "[\"The difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks.\", \"The difference between the sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that the porterhouse steak is cut from further back on the sirloin and contains a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet compared to the sirloin steak.\", \"Sirloin steak is cut from the rear back portion of the animal while the Porterhouse steak is cut from the larger portion of the tenderloin.\", \"Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks\"]", "time_sec": 10.519, "generation_time_seconds": 9.5346, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9784, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 323, 87186, 7675, 48959, 374, 429, 37937, 7675, 4087, 9810, 525, 3931, 504, 4623, 1182, 389, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 323, 8916, 6644, 264, 2699, 803, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 476, 1461, 1149, 1091, 350, 7671, 603, 4087, 9810, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7847537994384766, "g_worst_claim": 1.7847537994384766, "g_content": 2.2937477111816404, "g_traj_mean": 1.7493312358856201}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 323, 87186, 7675, 48959, 374, 429, 279, 87186, 7675, 48959, 374, 3931, 504, 4623, 1182, 389, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 323, 5610, 264, 2699, 803, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 476, 1461, 1149, 7707, 311, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between the sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that the porterhouse steak is cut from further back on the sirloin and contains a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet compared to the sirloin steak.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3058518390266263, "g_worst_claim": 1.3058518390266263, "g_content": 1.9750103670008041, "g_traj_mean": 1.2729660272598267}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [50190, 385, 258, 48959, 374, 3931, 504, 279, 14639, 1182, 13348, 315, 279, 9864, 1393, 279, 37937, 7675, 48959, 374, 3931, 504, 279, 8131, 13348, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 13, 151645], "pred": "Sirloin steak is cut from the rear back portion of the animal while the Porterhouse steak is cut from the larger portion of the tenderloin.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5876611278903099, "g_worst_claim": 1.5876611278903099, "g_content": 3.7858690115121694, "g_traj_mean": 1.5455560684204102}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [7084, 261, 7675, 4087, 9810, 525, 3931, 504, 4623, 1182, 389, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 323, 8916, 6644, 264, 2699, 803, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 476, 1461, 1149, 1091, 350, 7671, 603, 4087, 9810, 151645], "pred": "Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.2499361310686385, "g_worst_claim": 2.2499361310686385, "g_content": 3.4445343017578125, "g_traj_mean": 2.224644660949707}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "510", "question": "what is the difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it appears that the main difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is their location within the sirloin muscle. Sirloin steaks are cut from the back of the animal and continue off the short loin from which other cuts such as T-bone and porterhouse steaks are made. On the other hand, porterhouse steaks are specifically carved from the larger portion of the tenderloin and therefore have more of the tenderloin or fillet compared to T-bone steaks. However, the passages suggest that both sirloin and porterhouse steaks may be referred to as the same thing or as a large version of the T-bone due to their similarity in appearance and taste.", "pred": "The difference between a sirloin steak and a porterhouse steak is that a sirloin steak is cut from the back of the animal, while a porterhouse steak is cut from the short loin area and contains a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The difference between a sirloin steak and a porterhouse steak is that a sirloin steak is cut from the back of the animal, while a porterhouse steak is cut from the short loin area and contains a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet.", "cot": "[\"The difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks.\", \"The difference between a sirloin steak and a porterhouse steak is that a sirloin steak is cut from the back of the animal, while a porterhouse steak is cut from the short loin area and contains a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet.\", \"Porterhouse steak is cut from further back on the sirloin than a T-bone steak, and therefore contains a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet.\", \"Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks.\"]", "time_sec": 11.077, "generation_time_seconds": 10.2597, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8102, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 323, 87186, 7675, 48959, 374, 429, 37937, 7675, 4087, 9810, 525, 3931, 504, 4623, 1182, 389, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 323, 8916, 6644, 264, 2699, 803, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 476, 1461, 1149, 1091, 350, 7671, 603, 4087, 9810, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between sirloin steak and porterhouse steak is that Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8188384373982747, "g_worst_claim": 1.8188384373982747, "g_content": 2.3941469828287762, "g_traj_mean": 1.78715980052948}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 6672, 1948, 264, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 323, 264, 87186, 7675, 48959, 374, 429, 264, 27048, 385, 258, 48959, 374, 3931, 504, 279, 1182, 315, 279, 9864, 11, 1393, 264, 87186, 7675, 48959, 374, 3931, 504, 279, 2805, 76960, 3082, 323, 5610, 264, 2699, 803, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 476, 1461, 1149, 13, 151645], "pred": "The difference between a sirloin steak and a porterhouse steak is that a sirloin steak is cut from the back of the animal, while a porterhouse steak is cut from the short loin area and contains a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0697921707396165, "g_worst_claim": 0.8036770656191069, "g_content": 2.145049476623535, "g_traj_mean": 1.0379267930984497}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [7084, 261, 7675, 48959, 374, 3931, 504, 4623, 1182, 389, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 1091, 264, 350, 1455, 603, 48959, 11, 323, 8916, 5610, 264, 2699, 803, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 476, 1461, 1149, 13, 151645], "pred": "Porterhouse steak is cut from further back on the sirloin than a T-bone steak, and therefore contains a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.518806621006557, "g_worst_claim": 1.490220206124442, "g_content": 2.8733169555664064, "g_traj_mean": 1.4948608875274658}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [7084, 261, 7675, 4087, 9810, 525, 3931, 504, 4623, 1182, 389, 279, 27048, 385, 258, 323, 8916, 6644, 264, 2699, 803, 315, 279, 27582, 385, 258, 476, 1461, 1149, 1091, 350, 7671, 603, 4087, 9810, 13, 151645], "pred": "Porterhouse steaks are cut from further back on the sirloin and therefore contain a bit more of the tenderloin or fillet than T-Bone steaks.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1655171712239585, "g_worst_claim": 2.1655171712239585, "g_content": 3.310773468017578, "g_traj_mean": 2.12668514251709}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.3, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "516", "question": "history of the word gemini", "gt": "Sure! Here's a brief history of the word Gemini based on the given passages:\n\nThe word \"Gemini\" comes from Latin, meaning \"twins.\" The constellation Gemini was first mentioned in Aristotle's Meteorologica over 300 years BC. In Greek mythology, the twins represented in Gemini are Castor and Pollux, who share the same mother, Leda, but have different fathers. The constellation Gemini is not in the same position as the constellation of Gemini and is a mutable sign that announces change and rules the time of year when Taurus spring has ended.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you need further clarification or if there's anything else I can help you with.", "pred": "The first known reference of the Gemini constellation was in Aristotle’s Meteorologica, over 300 years BC. He mentions that he observed an occulting a star in Gemini and speaks of observing Jupiter in conjunction with it.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The first known reference of the Gemini constellation was in Aristotle’s Meteorologica, over 300 years BC. He mentions that he observed an occulting a star in Gemini and speaks of observing Jupiter in conjunction with it.", "cot": "[\"The first known reference of the Gemini constellation was in Aristotle’s Meteorologica, over 300 years BC. He mentions that he observed an occulting a star in Gemini and speaks of observing Jupiter in conjunction with it.\", \"The word \\\"Gemini\\\" is a Latin word for twins and is one of the constellations that looks like its name would suggest. The first known reference of the Gemini constellation was in Aristotle’s Meteorologica, over 300 years BC.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"The word \\\"Gemini\\\" is a Latin word for twins. It is one of the constellations that actually look like its name would suggest. The first known reference of the Gemini constellation was in Aristotle’s Meteorologica, over 300 years BC. He mentions that he observed an occulting a star in Gemini and speaks of observing Jupiter in conjunction with it.\"]", "time_sec": 11.116, "generation_time_seconds": 10.6119, "selection_time_seconds": 0.4972, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 1156, 3881, 5785, 315, 279, 85711, 82386, 572, 304, 77901, 748, 39632, 1609, 3001, 11, 916, 220, 18, 15, 15, 1635, 18040, 13, 1260, 33845, 429, 566, 13166, 458, 73826, 287, 264, 6774, 304, 85711, 323, 21191, 315, 44971, 49689, 304, 31446, 448, 432, 13, 151645], "pred": "The first known reference of the Gemini constellation was in Aristotle’s Meteorologica, over 300 years BC. He mentions that he observed an occulting a star in Gemini and speaks of observing Jupiter in conjunction with it.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.848618333989924, "g_worst_claim": 1.6541721820831299, "g_content": 4.487837138928865, "g_traj_mean": 3.103910446166992}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 3409, 330, 95040, 6591, 1, 374, 264, 19458, 3409, 369, 43636, 323, 374, 825, 315, 279, 733, 613, 804, 429, 5868, 1075, 1181, 829, 1035, 4190, 13, 576, 1156, 3881, 5785, 315, 279, 85711, 82386, 572, 304, 77901, 748, 39632, 1609, 3001, 11, 916, 220, 18, 15, 15, 1635, 18040, 13, 151645], "pred": "The word \"Gemini\" is a Latin word for twins and is one of the constellations that looks like its name would suggest. The first known reference of the Gemini constellation was in Aristotle’s Meteorologica, over 300 years BC.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.954913638886951, "g_worst_claim": 1.5771732330322266, "g_content": 2.5094993228004094, "g_traj_mean": 1.9428755044937134}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.17654186487197876, "g_worst_claim": -0.17654186487197876, "g_content": -0.2809211492538452, "g_traj_mean": -0.15697315335273743}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 3409, 330, 95040, 6591, 1, 374, 264, 19458, 3409, 369, 43636, 13, 1084, 374, 825, 315, 279, 733, 613, 804, 429, 3520, 1401, 1075, 1181, 829, 1035, 4190, 13, 576, 1156, 3881, 5785, 315, 279, 85711, 82386, 572, 304, 77901, 748, 39632, 1609, 3001, 11, 916, 220, 18, 15, 15, 1635, 18040, 13, 1260, 33845, 429, 566, 13166, 458, 73826, 287, 264, 6774, 304, 85711, 323, 21191, 315, 44971, 49689, 304, 31446, 448, 432, 13, 151645], "pred": "The word \"Gemini\" is a Latin word for twins. It is one of the constellations that actually look like its name would suggest. The first known reference of the Gemini constellation was in Aristotle’s Meteorologica, over 300 years BC. He mentions that he observed an occulting a star in Gemini and speaks of observing Jupiter in conjunction with it.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.3257855818429536, "g_worst_claim": 1.3540936983548677, "g_content": 3.460510746125252, "g_traj_mean": 2.5310966968536377}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 18.18, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "518", "question": "how do raffles work", "gt": "Raffles work by selling tickets to participants, who have the opportunity to win prizes. The specific details and mechanics of a raffle can vary. In a reverse raffle, participants purchase tickets with numbers on them, and the last ticket drawn wins the main prize. In a 50-50 draw, tickets are sold during an event, and 50% of the proceeds go to the winner of a random draw, while the other 50% is allocated for a charitable purpose. In some cases, raffles may also offer additional opportunities to win prizes, such as cash tip board raffles.", "pred": "Raffles work by selling tickets for a prize or a set of prizes. The proceeds from the sales of the tickets are put into a prize pool. The winner of the raffle is usually selected by drawing a single ticket at random.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Raffles work by selling tickets for a prize or a set of prizes. The proceeds from the sales of the tickets are put into a prize pool. The winner of the raffle is usually selected by drawing a single ticket at random.", "cot": "[\"Raffles work by selling tickets to participants, who have a chance to win a prize. The prize pool is determined by the total amount of money collected from ticket sales. The winner is usually selected randomly, and the prize is awarded to the lucky ticket holder.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Raffles typically involve the sale of tickets to participants, who then draw numbers that correspond to prize numbers. The winner of the raffle is determined by a random draw, and the prize is awarded to the ticket holder whose number matches the winning number.\", \"Raffles work by selling tickets for a prize or a set of prizes. The proceeds from the sales of the tickets are put into a prize pool. The winner of the raffle is usually selected by drawing a single ticket at random.\"]", "time_sec": 10.48, "generation_time_seconds": 9.6679, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8005, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [49, 80535, 975, 553, 11236, 14403, 311, 13026, 11, 879, 614, 264, 6012, 311, 3164, 264, 21882, 13, 576, 21882, 7314, 374, 10838, 553, 279, 2790, 3311, 315, 3220, 14548, 504, 11727, 6625, 13, 576, 13632, 374, 5990, 4091, 26618, 11, 323, 279, 21882, 374, 21328, 311, 279, 17605, 11727, 11839, 13, 151645], "pred": "Raffles work by selling tickets to participants, who have a chance to win a prize. The prize pool is determined by the total amount of money collected from ticket sales. The winner is usually selected randomly, and the prize is awarded to the lucky ticket holder.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.4687901347144513, "g_worst_claim": -0.03677376833829013, "g_content": 0.7592915755051833, "g_traj_mean": 0.4269387722015381}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.2111014872789383, "g_worst_claim": -0.2111014872789383, "g_content": -0.33745884895324707, "g_traj_mean": -0.1877022534608841}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [49, 80535, 11136, 21058, 279, 6278, 315, 14403, 311, 13026, 11, 879, 1221, 4038, 5109, 429, 7866, 311, 21882, 5109, 13, 576, 13632, 315, 279, 435, 44090, 374, 10838, 553, 264, 4194, 4038, 11, 323, 279, 21882, 374, 21328, 311, 279, 11727, 11839, 6693, 1372, 9071, 279, 10987, 1372, 13, 151645], "pred": "Raffles typically involve the sale of tickets to participants, who then draw numbers that correspond to prize numbers. The winner of the raffle is determined by a random draw, and the prize is awarded to the ticket holder whose number matches the winning number.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.3931272806391328, "g_worst_claim": -0.19254708290100098, "g_content": 0.6038492584228515, "g_traj_mean": 0.3413570523262024}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [49, 80535, 975, 553, 11236, 14403, 369, 264, 21882, 476, 264, 738, 315, 37408, 13, 576, 33455, 504, 279, 6625, 315, 279, 14403, 525, 2182, 1119, 264, 21882, 7314, 13, 576, 13632, 315, 279, 435, 44090, 374, 5990, 4091, 553, 13330, 264, 3175, 11727, 518, 4194, 13, 151645], "pred": "Raffles work by selling tickets for a prize or a set of prizes. The proceeds from the sales of the tickets are put into a prize pool. The winner of the raffle is usually selected by drawing a single ticket at random.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.3953238495035109, "g_worst_claim": 0.05677334701313692, "g_content": 0.8309198107038226, "g_traj_mean": 0.3697417676448822}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 29.27, "GAVIE-Rel": 7.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "519", "question": "how do raffles work", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how raffles work:\n\n1. Reverse Raffle: In this type of raffle, the numbers on the entry tickets are drawn in reverse order, starting with the last number and ending with the first number. For example, if there are 55 entries, the last number drawn wins the grand prize, followed by the next-to-last number, and so on until the first number. Each entry ticket costs $50, and a table of 20 individuals constitutes one complete ticket worth $1,000 and two $500 prizes (for the early bird drawing and the first ticket pulled).\n2. 50-50 Draw: This is a raffle held during a single day at a specific event. Tickets are sold to patrons throughout the event by roving staff with handheld electronic devices. The gross proceeds of 50-50 tickets sold at the event go into a prize pool, and 50% of the prize pool is awarded to the winner of a random draw that takes place at the end of the event. The remaining 50% goes to a charitable purpose chosen by the sporting club.\n3. Additional Raffles: In addition to the main raffle, there may be additional raffles for drinks and dinner. These raffles are not included in the original ticket price and require separate entry fees. One of these raffles offers the chance to win $10,000!\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "Raffles work by selling tickets to participants, who have a chance to win a prize. The prize pool is determined by the total amount of money collected from ticket sales. The winner is usually selected randomly, and the prize is awarded to the lucky ticket holder.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Raffles work by selling tickets to participants, who have a chance to win a prize. The prize pool is determined by the total amount of money collected from ticket sales. The winner is usually selected randomly, and the prize is awarded to the lucky ticket holder.", "cot": "[\"Raffles work by selling tickets to participants, who have a chance to win a prize. The prize pool is determined by the total amount of money collected from ticket sales. The winner is usually selected randomly, and the prize is awarded to the lucky ticket holder.\", \"Raffles are a type of lottery game in which participants buy tickets with a chance to win prizes. The basic principle is that the more tickets you buy, the higher your chances of winning. In a standard raffle, all the tickets are drawn at the end of the event, and the winner is determined by a random selection.\", \"Raffles typically involve the sale of tickets for a chance to win a prize. In a reverse raffle, the ticket numbers are from 1 to approximately 55, and tickets are $50 each. A table of 20 individuals constitutes one complete ticket at $1000, and there are two $500 prizes (one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pulled). In a 50-50 draw, tickets are sold throughout an event, and the gross proceeds go into a prize pool. 50% of the prize pool goes to the winner of the random draw, while the remaining 50% is set aside for a charitable purpose.\", \"Raffles typically involve the purchase of tickets for a chance to win a prize. In a reverse raffle, the reverse raffle is a raffle but backwards. Your entry ticket has a number on it from 1 to approximately 55. Tickets are $50 each and a table consists of 20 individuals, which constitutes one complete ticket at $1000. and two $500 prizes (one for the early bird drawing and one for the first ticket pulled). individuals totaling twenty. In a 50-50 draw, the gross proceeds of 50-50 tickets sold at the event go into a prize pool. 50% of the prize pool will go to the winner of the random draw which occurs towards the end of the event. The remaining 50% will be set aside for a charitable purpose chosen by the sporting club.\"]", "time_sec": 19.237, "generation_time_seconds": 18.6444, "selection_time_seconds": 0.5876, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [49, 80535, 975, 553, 11236, 14403, 311, 13026, 11, 879, 614, 264, 6012, 311, 3164, 264, 21882, 13, 576, 21882, 7314, 374, 10838, 553, 279, 2790, 3311, 315, 3220, 14548, 504, 11727, 6625, 13, 576, 13632, 374, 5990, 4091, 26618, 11, 323, 279, 21882, 374, 21328, 311, 279, 17605, 11727, 11839, 13, 151645], "pred": "Raffles work by selling tickets to participants, who have a chance to win a prize. The prize pool is determined by the total amount of money collected from ticket sales. The winner is usually selected randomly, and the prize is awarded to the lucky ticket holder.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.3743890774327439, "g_worst_claim": -0.018973446705124596, "g_content": 0.6314301123985877, "g_traj_mean": 0.35207033157348633}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [49, 80535, 525, 264, 943, 315, 38239, 1809, 304, 892, 13026, 3695, 14403, 448, 264, 6012, 311, 3164, 37408, 13, 576, 6770, 17508, 374, 429, 279, 803, 14403, 498, 3695, 11, 279, 5080, 697, 16963, 315, 10987, 13, 758, 264, 5297, 435, 44090, 11, 678, 279, 14403, 525, 14764, 518, 279, 835, 315, 279, 1538, 11, 323, 279, 13632, 374, 10838, 553, 264, 4194, 6589, 13, 151645], "pred": "Raffles are a type of lottery game in which participants buy tickets with a chance to win prizes. The basic principle is that the more tickets you buy, the higher your chances of winning. In a standard raffle, all the tickets are drawn at the end of the event, and the winner is determined by a random selection.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.2485367312489822, "g_worst_claim": -0.019054925441741942, "g_content": 0.5679552996600116, "g_traj_mean": 0.26958155632019043}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [49, 80535, 11136, 21058, 279, 6278, 315, 14403, 369, 264, 6012, 311, 3164, 264, 21882, 13, 758, 264, 9931, 435, 44090, 11, 279, 11727, 5109, 525, 504, 220, 16, 311, 13187, 220, 20, 20