{"id": "530", "question": "how does ez pass charges work", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here is how E-ZPass charging works:\n\nWhen you sign up for E-ZPass, a certain amount is charged to your credit card to establish a balance (specifically, $100 for the EZ-Tag and $25 for the TX-Tag). This balance is used to pay for tolls as you drive through toll lanes. When you drive through a toll booth, the toll tag mounted on your windshield is read by the antennae, and your E-ZPass account is charged the appropriate amount. The amount is deducted from your balance. If your balance falls below a certain threshold ($10 for the TX-Tag), E-ZPass will charge your credit card an additional $100 or $25 to top up your balance.", "pred": "E-ZPass charges work as follows:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "E-ZPass charges work as follows:", "cot": "[\"E-ZPass charges work by reading the toll tag mounted on the vehicle's windshield as it enters the toll lane. The system then charges the proper amount to the E-ZPass account. If the vehicle does not have a toll tag, it is classified as a violator and cameras take photos of the license plate for processing.\", \"Answer: E-ZPass charges work as follows:\\n\\n1. When your vehicle enters a toll lane, the E-ZPass toll tag mounted on your vehicle's windshield is read by the antennae.\\n2. The system charges your E-ZPass account the proper amount based on the toll.\\n3. Feedback is provided to you on an electronic display.\\n\\nIf your vehicle does not have a toll tag, the system will classify you as a violator, and cameras will take photos of your license plate for processing.\", \"In the given passages, the E-ZPass charging process is not fully explained, but we can infer from the information provided. E-ZPass charges work by using a toll tag that is mounted on the vehicle's windshield. The toll tag is read by antennae as the vehicle passes through a toll lane. The system then charges the vehicle's E-ZPass account for the correct amount of the toll. If the vehicle does not have a toll tag, it is classified as a violator, and cameras take photos of its license plate for processing.\", \"When your vehicle passes through a toll lane, the toll tag on your windshield is read by the antennae. Your E-ZPass account is then charged the appropriate amount based on the toll you have to pay. If you do not have a toll tag, you will be classified as a violator and cameras will take photos of your license plate for processing.\"]", "time_sec": 16.804, "generation_time_seconds": 16.2931, "selection_time_seconds": 0.5034, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [36, 11171, 12187, 10195, 975, 553, 5290, 279, 25851, 4772, 21810, 389, 279, 7310, 594, 73939, 438, 432, 28833, 279, 25851, 21272, 13, 576, 1849, 1221, 10195, 279, 6169, 3311, 311, 279, 468, 11171, 12187, 2692, 13, 1416, 279, 7310, 1558, 537, 614, 264, 25851, 4772, 11, 432, 374, 21091, 438, 264, 4634, 850, 323, 18139, 1896, 7249, 315, 279, 5723, 11968, 369, 8692, 13, 151645], "pred": "E-ZPass charges work by reading the toll tag mounted on the vehicle's windshield as it enters the toll lane. The system then charges the proper amount to the E-ZPass account. If the vehicle does not have a toll tag, it is classified as a violator and cameras take photos of the license plate for processing.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5655495880388899, "g_worst_claim": 1.1029509544372558, "g_content": 2.820453249174973, "g_traj_mean": 1.6221355199813843}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 468, 11171, 12187, 10195, 975, 438, 11017, 1447, 16, 13, 3197, 697, 7310, 28833, 264, 25851, 21272, 11, 279, 468, 11171, 12187, 25851, 4772, 21810, 389, 697, 7310, 594, 73939, 374, 1349, 553, 279, 71477, 5918, 624, 17, 13, 576, 1849, 10195, 697, 468, 11171, 12187, 2692, 279, 6169, 3311, 3118, 389, 279, 25851, 