{"id": "580", "question": "what do i do if i got my sperrys wet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, if your Sperry shoes get wet, it is recommended to use a leather conditioner to help revitalize the leather and infuse moisture back into it. This is especially important if you wash your shoes with detergent, as it tends to dry out the leather. If you don't have a leather conditioner on hand, you can use a suede bar or leather brush to clean the shoes. It's best to avoid getting light tan Sperry shoes wet, as water might stain them. However, if you do get them wet, using a suede bar or leather brush should help remove any stains.", "pred": "If your Sperrys get wet, you should let them air dry naturally. Avoid using a hair dryer or direct heat to dry them quickly, as this may cause the leather to crack or the suede to lose its texture. Once they are dry, you might want to use a leather conditioner to help preserve the leather and prevent it from becoming too dry.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "If your Sperrys get wet, you should let them air dry naturally. Avoid using a hair dryer or direct heat to dry them quickly, as this may cause the leather to crack or the suede to lose its texture. Once they are dry, you might want to use a leather conditioner to help preserve the leather and prevent it from becoming too dry.", "cot": "[\"If your Sperrys get wet, you can use a leather conditioner to revitalize the leather and infuse moisture back into it. This is especially important if you wash your Sperry shoes with detergent, as detergent has a tendency to dry the leather out.\", \"If your Sperrys get wet, you can dry them out using a suede bar and leather brush. These tools can prevent stains and help the leather recover from the water damage.\", \"If your Sperrys get wet, you should use a leather conditioner to revitalize the leather and infuse moisture back into it. This is especially important if you wash your Sperry shoes with detergent, as detergent has a tendency to dry out the leather.\", \"If your Sperrys get wet, you should let them air dry naturally. Avoid using a hair dryer or direct heat to dry them quickly, as this may cause the leather to crack or the suede to lose its texture. Once they are dry, you might want to use a leather conditioner to help preserve the leather and prevent it from becoming too dry.\"]", "time_sec": 12.137, "generation_time_seconds": 11.6444, "selection_time_seconds": 0.4843, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [2679, 697, 3089, 615, 1047, 633, 14401, 11, 498, 646, 990, 264, 17553, 64324, 311, 5772, 34313, 279, 17553, 323, 4132, 810, 31157, 1182, 1119, 432, 13, 1096, 374, 5310, 2989, 421, 498, 11369, 697, 3089, 5400, 15294, 448, 90134, 11, 438, 90134, 702, 264, 30854, 311, 9058, 279, 17553, 700, 13, 151645], "pred": "If your Sperrys get wet, you can use a leather conditioner to revitalize the leather and infuse moisture back into it. This is especially important if you wash your Sperry shoes with detergent, as detergent has a tendency to dry the leather out.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8227023506767523, "g_worst_claim": 1.5592101703990588, "g_content": 2.67054930187407, "g_traj_mean": 1.8279564380645752}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [2679, 697, 3089, 615, 1047, 633, 14401, 11, 498, 646, 9058, 1105, 700, 1667, 264, 96635, 3619, 323, 17553, 15625, 13, 4220, 7375, 646, 5358, 62463, 323, 1492, 279, 17553, 11731, 504, 279, 3015, 5557, 13, 151645], "pred": "If your Sperrys get wet, you can dry them out using a suede bar and leather brush. These tools can prevent stains and help the leather recover from the water damage.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5028014584484264, "g_worst_claim": 0.7719458262125651, "g_content": 1.9686299492331112, "g_traj_mean": 1.4254623651504517}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids