{"id": "609", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "To create employee schedules, start by making a list of all employees and the tasks they can perform. Then, create a chart with the work days and hours for each day. You can use scheduling software, a word processing program, or a sheet of paper to do this. Afterward, print out copies for employees or send schedules to their email accounts. It's also important to maintain a master schedule for making any necessary changes. Microsoft Excel can be used to create a work schedule for multiple employees, which can be modified as your business expands.", "pred": "1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\n5. Use scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or a sheet of paper to create the schedule.\n6. Consider using Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, as it allows you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\n5. Use scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or a sheet of paper to create the schedule.\n6. Consider using Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, as it allows you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.", "cot": "[\"To create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\\n5. Use scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or a sheet of paper to create the schedule.\\n6. Consider using Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, as it allows you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.\", \"Employee schedules can be created using scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or a sheet of paper. Here's what to do: 1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform [source: Coleman 2 ]. 2. Make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. 3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts. 4. Keep a master schedule for to make any changes.\", \"To create an employee schedule, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n\\nAfter this, you can print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts. For easier management and changes, you can use a scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees. This will allow you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.\", \"Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform. Make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts. Keep a master schedule for to make any changes.\"]", "time_sec": 17.191, "generation_time_seconds": 16.5383, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6428, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1855, 9364, 36769, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 7405, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 697, 8256, 323, 279, 21300, 807, 646, 2736, 6