{"id": "610", "question": "how to do employee schedules", "gt": "To create an employee schedule, start by making a list of all employees and their duties (Passage 2). Then, create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day (Passage 2). Print out copies of the schedule for employees or send them via email (Passage 3). If you need to make any changes, keep a master schedule and update it as needed (Passage 3). Microsoft Excel is a useful tool for creating schedules for multiple employees and can be used as your business grows (Passage 3). It's important to note that there may be other work laws that you need to follow, such as paying overtime if you schedule an employee more than 40 hours per week (Passage 1).", "pred": "1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\n2. Make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.", "cot": "[\"To create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\\n5. Use scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or a sheet of paper to create the schedule.\\n6. Consider using Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, as it allows you to continue using the schedule template as your business grows.\", \"To create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform. For example, if you have an employee named John, list him and his role as a cashier.\\n\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day. For instance, if John works Monday through Friday, you can create a column for each day and another column for the hours he works on that day.\\n\\n3. Print out copies of the schedule for your employees or send them to their email accounts. You can also keep a master schedule to make any changes as needed.\\n\\n4. Use scheduling software, a simple word processing program, or a sheet of paper to create the schedule. For example, you can use Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing you to continue to use the schedule template as your business grows.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can effectively create and manage employee schedules.\", \"1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\", \"To create employee schedules, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform.\\n2. Create a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.\\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\\n\\nMicrosoft Excel allows you to create a work schedule for multiple employees so you can continue to use the schedule template as your business grows.\"]", "time_sec": 18.278, "generation_time_seconds": 17.727, "selection_time_seconds": 0.5451, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1855, 9364, 36769, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 7405, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 697, 8256, 323, 279, 21300, 807, 646, 2736, 624, 17, 13, 4230, 264, 9487, 315, 279, 975, 2849, 323, 279, 4115, 369, 1817, 1899, 624, 18, 13, 8213, 700, 10993, 369, 8256, 476, 3624, 36769, 311, 9364, 2551, 9618, 624, 19, 13, 13655, 264, 7341, 9700, 369, 3259, 894, 4344, 624, 20, 13, 5443, 37852, 3162, 11, 264, 4285, 3409, 8692, 2025, 11, 476, 264, 10834, 315, 5567, 311, 1855, 279, 9700, 624, 21, 13, 21