he work days and the hours for each day.\n3. Print out copies for employees or send schedules to employee email accounts.\n4. Keep a master schedule for making any changes.\n5. If your business grows, you can use a software like Microsoft Excel to create a work schedule template for multiple employees.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8882938289234779, "g_worst_claim": 0.25379419326782227, "g_content": 2.1661962955556016, "g_traj_mean": 1.6968729496002197}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1855, 9364, 36769, 11, 825, 646, 990, 37852, 3162, 11, 264, 4285, 3409, 8692, 2025, 476, 264, 10834, 315, 5567, 13, 576, 1156, 3019, 374, 311, 1281, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 8256, 323, 279, 21300, 807, 646, 2736, 13, 9295, 11, 264, 9487, 1265, 387, 1865, 315, 975, 2849, 323, 279, 4115, 369, 1817, 1899, 13, 5100, 21029, 646, 387, 1483, 311, 1855, 264, 975, 9700, 369, 5248, 8256, 11, 10693, 279, 9700, 3811, 311, 387, 1483, 1496, 438, 279, 2562, 27715, 13, 151645], "pred": "To create employee schedules, one can use scheduling software, a simple word processing program or a sheet of paper. The first step is to make a list of all employees and the duties they can perform. Next, a chart should be made of work days and the hours for each day. Microsoft Excel can be used to create a work schedule for multiple employees, allowing the schedule template to be used even as the business grows.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.973895210050284, "g_worst_claim": 1.1684339311387804, "g_content": 2.2937098185221356, "g_traj_mean": 1.8760178089141846}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [2610, 646, 1281, 458, 9364, 9700, 1667, 37852, 3162, 11, 264, 4285, 3409, 8692, 2025, 476, 264, 10834, 315, 5567, 13, 5692, 594, 1128, 311, 653, 25, 220, 16, 7405, 264, 1140, 315, 678, 697, 8256, 323, 279, 21300, 807, 646, 2736, 508, 2427, 25, 49432, 220, 17, 936, 7405, 264, 9487, 315, 279, 975, 2849, 323, 279, 4115, 369, 1817, 1899, 13, 151645], "pred": "You can make an employee schedule using scheduling software, a simple word processing program or a sheet of paper. Here's what to do: 1 Make a list of all your employees and the duties they can perform [source: Coleman 2]. Make a chart of the work days and the hours for each day.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.4594901790866603, "g_worst_claim": 1.9624850409371513, "g_content": 2.941747029622396, "g_traj_mean": 2.5873913764953613}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 32.18, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "614", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "gt": "Based on the information given in the passages, to force remove a printer in devices and printers, you need to go to Control Panel, then click on Hardware and Sound, and then on Printers. Right-click the printer that you want to remove, and click Delete. If it doesn't delete, right-click it again, click Run as administrator, and then click Delete. If your printer is connected to your computer via a USB, disconnect the cable, turn the printer on and off again, and ensure it is in a ready state. If you used Print Manager or Printers folder to remove a printer or printer port, close these applications and stop and restart the Spooler Service.", "pred": "To force the removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Control Panel.\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\n3. Click on Printers.\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete.\n5. If the printer cannot be deleted, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\n\nThese steps will ensure that the printer is removed from the devices list and any associated Windows print drivers are uninstalled.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To force the removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Control Panel.\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\n3. Click on Printers.\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete.\n5. If the printer cannot be deleted, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\n\nThese steps will ensure that the printer is removed from the devices list and any associated Windows print drivers are uninstalled.", "cot": "[\"To force the removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Open the Control Panel.\\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\\n3. Click on Printers.\\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete.\\n5. If the printer cannot be deleted, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\\n\\nThese steps will ensure that the printer is removed from the devices list and any associated Windows print drivers are uninstalled.\", \"To force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Click on the Start button to open the Start menu.\\n2. Click on Control Panel.\\n3. Click on Hardware and Sound.\\n4. Then click on Printers.\\n5. Right-click the printer that you want to remove and select Delete. If you can't delete the printer, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\", \"To force the removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Open Control Panel.\\n2. Navigate to Hardware and Sound.\\n3. Click on Printers.\\n4. Right-click on the printer you want to remove.\\n5. Click on Delete.\\n6. If you cannot delete the printer, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\\n\\nEnsure the printer is disconnected from the computer if it is connected via a USB cable, turn it off, and then turn it back on to make sure it is in a ready state. After these steps, the printer should be forcibly removed from the Devices and Printers list.\", \"To force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Remove the printer from the devices list**:\\n   - Go to the Start menu.\\n   - Navigate to Control Panel.\\n   - Click on Hardware and Sound.\\n   - Then click on Printers.\\n   - Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete.\\n   \\n2. **If the printer cannot be deleted**:\\n   - Right-click the printer again.\\n   - Select Run as administrator.\\n   - Click Delete.\\n\\nThese steps should help ensure that the printer is completely removed from the devices list.\"]", "time_sec": 18.99, "generation_time_seconds": 18.217, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7658, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 5344, 279, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 279, 7779, 18946, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 389, 36765, 323, 14594, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 8213, 388, 624, 19, 13, 10083, 28118, 279, 22380, 498, 1366, 311, 4057, 323, 3293, 10428, 624, 20, 13, 1416, 279, 22380, 4157, 387, 11062, 11, 1290, 28118, 432, 1549, 11, 3293, 6452, 438, 28093, 11, 323, 1221, 4205, 10428, 382, 9485, 7354, 686, 5978, 429, 279, 22380, 374, 6963, 504, 279, 7611, 1140, 323, 894, 5815, 5515, 1173, 11788, 525, 650, 49573, 13, 151645], "pred": "To force the removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Control Panel.\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\n3. Click on Printers.\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete.\n5. If the printer cannot be deleted, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\n\nThese steps will ensure that the printer is removed from the devices list and any associated Windows print drivers are uninstalled.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8056145086031968, "g_worst_claim": 0.21833883225917816, "g_content": 1.0284793687903362, "g_traj_mean": 0.7942590713500977}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5344, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 5145, 3137, 311, 1787, 279, 5145, 5022, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 389, 7779, 18946, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 36765, 323, 14594, 624, 19, 13, 5005, 4205, 389, 8213, 388, 624, 20, 13, 10083, 28118, 279, 22380, 429, 498, 1366, 311, 4057, 323, 3293, 10428, 13, 1416, 498, 646, 944, 3698, 279, 22380, 11, 1290, 28118, 432, 1549, 11, 3293, 6452, 438, 28093, 11, 323, 1221, 4205, 10428, 13, 151645], "pred": "To force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Click on the Start button to open the Start menu.\n2. Click on Control Panel.\n3. Click on Hardware and Sound.\n4. Then click on Printers.\n5. Right-click the printer that you want to remove and select Delete. If you can't delete the printer, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8294876921711823, "g_worst_claim": -0.013107487559318542, "g_content": 0.7130091667175293, "g_traj_mean": 0.6819909811019897}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5344, 279, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 7779, 18946, 624, 17, 13, 81739, 311, 36765, 323, 14594, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 8213, 388, 624, 19, 13, 10083, 28118, 389, 279, 22380, 498, 1366, 311, 4057, 624, 20, 13, 9189, 389, 10428, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 498, 4157, 3698, 279, 22380, 11, 1290, 28118, 432, 1549, 11, 3293, 6452, 438, 28093, 11, 323, 1221, 4205, 10428, 382, 64439, 279, 22380, 374, 39086, 504, 279, 6366, 421, 432, 374, 8433, 4566, 264, 11348, 14652, 11, 2484, 432, 1007, 11, 323, 1221, 2484, 432, 1182, 389, 311, 1281, 2704, 432, 374, 304, 264, 5527, 1584, 13, 4636, 1493, 7354, 11, 279, 22380, 1265, 387, 73823, 6963, 504, 279, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 1140, 13, 151645], "pred": "Ensure the printer is disconnected from the computer if it is connected via a USB cable, turn it off, and then turn it back on to make sure it is in a ready state. After these steps, the printer should be forcibly removed from the Devices and Printers list.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8344177787000328, "g_worst_claim": -0.04555858837233649, "g_content": 1.025677253460062, "g_traj_mean": 0.7759252786636353}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5344, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 13021, 279, 22380, 504, 279, 7611, 1140, 334, 510, 256, 481, 5994, 311, 279, 5145, 5022, 624, 256, 481, 81739, 311, 7779, 18946, 624, 256, 481, 9189, 389, 36765, 323, 14594, 624, 256, 481, 5005, 4205, 389, 8213, 388, 624, 256, 481, 10083, 28118, 279, 22380, 498, 1366, 311, 4057, 323, 3293, 10428, 624, 5872, 17, 13, 3070, 2679, 279, 22380, 4157, 387, 11062, 334, 510, 256, 481, 10083, 28118, 279, 22380, 1549, 624, 256, 481, 8427, 6452, 438, 28093, 624, 256, 481, 9189, 10428, 382, 9485, 7354, 1265, 1492, 5978, 429, 279, 22380, 374, 6587, 6963, 504, 279, 7611, 1140, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps should help ensure that the printer is completely removed from the devices list.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7078692004122374, "g_worst_claim": -0.19149071829659597, "g_content": 1.0181023279825847, "g_traj_mean": 0.6177176833152771}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.76, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "615", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "gt": "Passage 2 provides the necessary information to force removal of a printer in devices and printers. You can do this by first clicking on Control Panel, then selecting Hardware and Sound, followed by clicking on Printers. Right-click on the printer you want to remove and click Delete. If you are unable to delete the printer, right-click it again, click Run as administrator, and then click Delete.", "pred": "To force the removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Control Panel.\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\n3. Click on Printers.\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete.\n5. If the printer cannot be deleted, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\n\nThese steps will ensure that the printer is removed from the devices list and any associated Windows print drivers are uninstalled.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To force the removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Control Panel.\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\n3. Click on Printers.\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete.\n5. If the printer cannot be deleted, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\n\nThese steps will ensure that the printer is removed from the devices list and any associated Windows print drivers are uninstalled.", "cot": "[\"To force the removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Open the Control Panel.\\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\\n3. Click on Printers.\\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete.\\n5. If the printer cannot be deleted, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\\n\\nThese steps will ensure that the printer is removed from the devices list and any associated Windows print drivers are uninstalled.\", \"To force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Go to Control Panel.\\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\\n3. Then click on Printers.\\n4. Right-click the printer that you want to remove.\\n5. Click on Delete.\\n\\nIf you encounter any issues and cannot delete the printer, right-click the printer again and select \\\"Run as administrator.\\\" Afterward, click on \\\"Delete\\\" again to remove the printer forcefully.\\n\\nAnswer: To forcefully remove a printer in Devices and Printers, you need to follow the steps mentioned above, ensuring that you have administrative privileges when required.\", \"To force removal of a printer in devices and printers, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Right-click on the printer that you want to remove and select \\\"Delete\\\".\\n\\nIf the printer cannot be deleted, right-click on it again and select \\\"Run as administrator\\\", and then click \\\"Delete\\\" again.\", \"To force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\\n1. Open the Devices and Printers window from the Control Panel.\\n2. Locate the printer you want to remove.\\n3. Right-click the printer and select \\\"Delete.\\\"\\n4. If prompted, click \\\"Yes\\\" or \\\"OK\\\" to confirm the removal.\\n5. To ensure the printer is completely removed, you may need to restart your computer.\\n\\nAnswer:[To force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\\n1. Open the Devices and Printers window from the Control Panel.\\n2. Locate the printer you want to remove.\\n3. Right-click the printer and select \\\"Delete.\\\"\\n4. If prompted, click \\\"Yes\\\" or \\\"OK\\\" to confirm the removal.\\n5. To ensure the printer is completely removed, you may need to restart your computer.]\"]", "time_sec": 19.227, "generation_time_seconds": 18.5702, "selection_time_seconds": 0.651, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"ro