, 85978, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 5978, 429, 279, 22380, 374, 6587, 6963, 504, 697, 1849, 11, 2670, 894, 5815, 11788, 323, 894, 11348, 13234, 421, 8415, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you ensure that the printer is completely removed from your system, including any associated drivers and any USB connections if applicable.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.4462598573224921, "g_worst_claim": -0.29432711998621625, "g_content": 0.7957439422607422, "g_traj_mean": 0.44998955726623535}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [18573, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 646, 387, 16994, 553, 22535, 323, 92524, 279, 3089, 1749, 261, 5362, 13, 22406, 11, 498, 646, 4057, 279, 22380, 504, 279, 7611, 1140, 553, 1290, 28118, 287, 432, 323, 26301, 10428, 13, 1416, 279, 22380, 4157, 387, 11062, 11, 1290, 28118, 432, 1549, 323, 3293, 6452, 438, 28093, 1573, 33011, 432, 13, 151645], "pred": "Force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers can be achieved by stopping and restarting the Spooler Service. Additionally, you can remove the printer from the devices list by right-clicking it and selecting Delete. If the printer cannot be deleted, right-click it again and select Run as administrator before deleting it.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1083682919539624, "g_worst_claim": 0.7369548320770264, "g_content": 1.8396644592285156, "g_traj_mean": 1.0455713272094727}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 59.26, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.3, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "619", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the information provided in the passages, here are the steps to force remove a printer in Devices and Printers:\n\n1. Open Print Manager or Printers folder.\n2. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete. If you can't delete the printer, run the command with administrative privileges by right-clicking the printer again and selecting \"Run as administrator\" before deleting it.\n3. Alternatively, you can remove the printer from the devices list, uninstall the Windows print drivers, and disconnect the printer from the computer if it's connected via USB. Restart the Spooler Service after removing the printer or printer port.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "To force the removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Control Panel.\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\n3. Click on Printers.\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete.\n5. If the printer cannot be deleted, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\n\nThese steps will ensure that the printer is removed from the devices list and any associated Windows print drivers are uninstalled.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To force the removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Control Panel.\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\n3. Click on Printers.\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete.\n5. If the printer cannot be deleted, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\n\nThese steps will ensure that the printer is removed from the devices list and any associated Windows print drivers are uninstalled.", "cot": "[\"To force the removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Open the Control Panel.\\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\\n3. Click on Printers.\\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete.\\n5. If the printer cannot be deleted, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\\n\\nThese steps will ensure that the printer is removed from the devices list and any associated Windows print drivers are uninstalled.\", \"To force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Open the Devices and Printers window.\\n2. Locate the printer you want to remove.\\n3. Right-click on the printer and select \\\"Delete.\\\"\\n4. If the printer does not delete immediately, try right-clicking it again and selecting \\\"Run as administrator\\\" before clicking \\\"Delete\\\" to ensure proper removal.\\n\\nThese steps should help you remove the printer from the devices list effectively.\", \"To force the removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Open the Control Panel.\\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\\n3. Then, click on Printers.\\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove, and then click Delete.\\n5. If you can't delete the printer, right-click it again, click Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\\n\\nRemember to disconnect the printer's USB cable if it is connected, turn it off and on again, and make sure it is in a ready state.\", \"To force the removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, you should first remove the printer from the devices list. After that, you should uninstall any Windows print drivers using Windows Devices and Printers. Additionally, if your printer is connected to the computer with a USB cable, you should disconnect the cable from the printer. Once disconnected, turn the printer off and on again, and make sure that it is in a ready state.\"]", "time_sec": 17.786, "generation_time_seconds": 16.7575, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0231, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 5344, 279, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 279, 7779, 18946, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 389, 36765, 323, 14594, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 8213, 388, 624, 19, 13, 10083, 28118, 279, 22380, 498, 1366, 311, 4057, 323, 3293, 10428, 624, 20, 13, 1416, 279, 22380, 4157, 387, 11062, 11, 1290, 28118, 432, 1549, 11, 3293, 6452, 438, 28093, 11, 323, 1221, 4205, 10428, 382, 9485, 7354, 686, 5978, 429, 279, 22380, 374, 6963, 504, 279, 7611, 1140, 323, 894, 5815, 5515, 1173, 11788, 525, 650, 49573, 13, 151645], "pred": "To force the removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Control Panel.\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\n3. Click on Printers.\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete.\n5. If the printer cannot be deleted, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\n\nThese steps will ensure that the printer is removed from the devices list and any associated Windows print drivers are uninstalled.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.795378408116338, "g_worst_claim": 0.11771371215581894, "g_content": 1.0426659791365913, "g_traj_mean": 0.7938170433044434}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5344, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 279, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 3241, 624, 17, 13, 95210, 279, 22380, 498, 1366, 311, 4057, 624, 18, 13, 10083, 28118, 389, 279, 22380, 323, 3293, 330, 6435, 10040, 19, 13, 1416, 279, 22380, 1558, 537, 3698, 7069, 11, 1430, 1290, 28118, 287, 432, 1549, 323, 26301, 330, 6727, 438, 28093, 1, 1573, 18458, 330, 6435, 1, 311, 5978, 6169, 16652, 382, 9485, 7354, 1265, 1492, 498, 4057, 279, 22380, 504, 279, 7611, 1140, 13444, 13, 151645], "pred": "To force removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Devices and Printers window.\n2. Locate the printer you want to remove.\n3. Right-click on the printer and select \"Delete.\"\n4. If the printer does not delete immediately, try right-clicking it again and selecting \"Run as administrator\" before clicking \"Delete\" to ensure proper removal.\n\nThese steps should help you remove the printer from the devices list effectively.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.36732446037576916, "g_worst_claim": -0.1923232078552246, "g_content": 0.45176124572753906, "g_traj_mean": 0.42252621054649353}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5344, 279, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 5264, 279, 7779, 18946, 624, 17, 13, 9189, 389, 36765, 323, 14594, 624, 18, 13, 5005, 11, 4205, 389, 8213, 388, 624, 19, 13, 10083, 28118, 279, 22380, 498, 1366, 311, 4057, 11, 323, 1221, 4205, 10428, 624, 20, 13, 1416, 498, 646, 944, 3698, 279, 22380, 11, 1290, 28118, 432, 1549, 11, 4205, 6452, 438, 28093, 11, 323, 1221, 4205, 10428, 382, 28590, 311, 28969, 279, 22380, 594, 11348, 14652, 421, 432, 374, 8433, 11, 2484, 432, 1007, 323, 389, 1549, 11, 323, 1281, 2704, 432, 374, 304, 264, 5527, 1584, 13, 151645], "pred": "To force the removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, follow these steps:\n\n1. Open the Control Panel.\n2. Click on Hardware and Sound.\n3. Then, click on Printers.\n4. Right-click the printer you want to remove, and then click Delete.\n5. If you can't delete the printer, right-click it again, click Run as administrator, and then click Delete.\n\nRemember to disconnect the printer's USB cable if it is connected, turn it off and on again, and make sure it is in a ready state.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8869488244839118, "g_worst_claim": 0.11771371215581894, "g_content": 1.0033164978027345, "g_traj_mean": 0.8929734230041504}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 5344, 279, 16652, 315, 264, 22380, 304, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 11, 498, 1265, 1156, 4057, 279, 22380, 504, 279, 7611, 1140, 13, 4636, 429, 11, 498, 1265, 53635, 894, 5515, 1173, 11788, 1667, 5515, 40377, 323, 8213, 388, 13, 22406, 11, 421, 697, 22380, 374, 8433, 311, 279, 6366, 448, 264, 11348, 14652, 11, 498, 1265, 28969, 279, 14652, 504, 279, 22380, 13, 9646, 39086, 11, 2484, 279, 22380, 1007, 323, 389, 1549, 11, 323, 1281, 2704, 429, 432, 374, 304, 264, 5527, 1584, 13, 151645], "pred": "To force the removal of a printer in Devices and Printers, you should first remove the printer from the devices list. After that, you should uninstall any Windows print drivers using Windows Devices and Printers. Additionally, if your printer is connected to the computer with a USB cable, you should disconnect the cable from the printer. Once disconnected, turn the printer off and on again, and make sure that it is in a ready state.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.241354391548909, "g_worst_claim": 0.8446243074205186, "g_content": 1.7727774417761601, "g_traj_mean": 1.2704392671585083}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.48, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "620", "question": "how has it technology changed the workplace", "gt": "IT technology has significantly changed the workplace in several ways. It has improved efficiency and increased productivity, as it allows for a complete shift in how time is spent in the modern workplace. The continuous evolution of technology also changes how business is conducted and the dynamics of the workplace. Over the last 10 to 15 years, technology has drastically changed attitudes and processes in the workplace. Technology has also dramatically reshaped the average American workplace, allowing employees to interact with a global market and take work on the road.", "pred": "Technology has changed the workplace in several ways, including increased efficiency and productivity, a shift in how we spend our time, and the ability for employees to interact with a global market and take work on the road.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Technology has changed the workplace in several ways, including increased efficiency and productivity, a shift in how we spend our time, and the ability for employees to interact with a global market and take work on the road.", "cot": "[\"Technology has changed the workplace in several ways, including increased efficiency and productivity, a shift in how we spend our time, and the ability for employees to interact with a global market and take work on the road.\", \"Based on the passages, technology has significantly changed the workplace in several ways:\\n\\n1. **Efficiency and Increased Productivity**: The modern workplace has seen a complete shift in how time is spent, leading to more efficient processes and higher productivity. For example, the use of digital tools and automation has streamlined tasks, allowing employees to focus on more strategic and creative activities.\\n\\n2. **Attitudes and Processes**: Over the last 10 to 15 years, technology has transformed the attitude and processes of the workplace. This change has been so substantial that the office environment of the past is now obsolete, replaced by rapid technological advancement.\\n\\n3. **Global Interaction**: Technology has enabled employees to interact with a global market, facilitating remote work and collaboration across different time zones and countries. For instance, video conferencing tools like Zoom and Microsoft Teams have become essential for meetings and communication, even when team members are physically distant.\\n\\n4. **Rapid Technological Advancement**: The past couple of decades have witnessed dramatic technological changes in the workplace. This advancement has not only reshaped the office environment but also the way work is conducted. For example, the rise of cloud computing has allowed businesses to access and store data securely from anywhere, making it easier to manage and collaborate on projects.\\n\\nThese changes have collectively transformed the workplace, making it more dynamic, efficient, and connected.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"The workplace has been transformed by technology in several ways. It has increased efficiency and productivity, allowing employees to interact with a global market and even take work out on the road.\"]", "time_sec": 17.013, "generation_time_seconds": 16.0209, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9827, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [62407, 702, 5497, 279, 26368, 304, 3807, 5510, 11, 2670, 7172, 15024, 323, 25148, 11, 264, 6407, 304, 1246, 582, 8329, 1039, 882, 11, 323, 279, 5726, 369, 8256, 311, 16282, 448, 264, 3644, 3081, 323, 1896, 975, 389, 279, 5636, 13, 151645], "pred": "Technology has changed the workplace in several ways, including increased efficiency and productivity, a shift in how we spend our time, and the ability for employees to interact with a global market and take work on the road.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.953375859393014, "g_worst_claim": 0.6136871576309204, "g_content": 2.846870231628418, "g_traj_mean": 2.0828230381011963}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 46769, 11, 5440, 702, 11941, 5497, 279, 26368, 304, 3807, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 46588, 10387, 323, 61597, 5643, 1927, 95518, 576, 6481, 26368, 702, 3884, 264, 4583, 6407, 304, 1246, 882, 374, 7391, 11, 6388, 311, 803, 11050, 11364, 323, 5080, 25148, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 990, 315, 7377, 7375, 323, 32662, 702, 74060, 9079, 11, 10693, 8256, 311, 5244, 389, 803, 18580, 323, 11521, 7488, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 10456, 20590, 323, 62303, 95518, 6065, 279, 1537, 220, 16, 15, 311, 220, 16, 20, 1635, 11, 5440, 702, 23507, 279, 18915, 323, 11364, 315, 279, 26368, 13, 1096, 2297, 702, 1012, 773, 11924, 429, 279, 5163, 4573, 315, 279, 3267, 374, 1431, 46066, 11, 12575, 553, 11048, 29016, 49825, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 11646, 42707, 95518, 11791, 702, 8970, 8256, 311, 16282, 448, 264, 3644, 3081, 11, 67265, 8699, 975, 323, 20031, 3941, 2155, 882, 25395, 323, 5837, 13, 1752, 2867, 11, 2766, 48743, 11373, 7375, 1075, 37529, 323, 5100, 39613, 614, 3635, 7565, 369, 16261, 323, 10535, 11, 1496, 979, 2083, 3613, 525, 21893, 28727, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 49, 43121, 7001, 5729, 12325, 16480, 95518, 576, 3267, 5625, 315, 10793, 614, 31026, 21771, 29016, 4344, 304, 279, 26368, 13, 1096, 49825, 702, 537, 1172, 63693, 10185, 279, 5163, 4573, 714, 1083, 279, 1616, 975, 374, 13075, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 10000, 315, 9437, 24231, 702, 5420, 9675, 311, 2615, 323, 3553, 821, 51023, 504, 12379, 11, 3259, 432, 8661, 311, 10091, 323, 50596, 389, 7079, 382, 9485, 4344, 614, 44825, 23507, 279, 26368, 11, 3259, 432, 803, 8741, 11, 11050, 11, 323, 8433, 13, 151645], "pred": "These changes have collectively transformed the workplace, making it more dynamic, efficient, and connected.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8092121042800056, "g_worst_claim": 0.09010882938609403, "g_content": 1.177834392464074, "g_traj_mean": 0.7908912897109985}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": -0.5495170950889587, "g_worst_claim": -0.5495170950889587, "g_content": -0.8761549949645996, "g_traj_mean": -0.4884907901287079}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 26368, 702, 1012, 23507, 553, 5440, 304, 3807, 5510, 13, 1084, 702, 7172, 15024, 323, 25148, 11, 10693, 8256, 311, 16282, 448, 264, 3644, 3081, 323, 1496, 1896, 975, 700, 389, 279, 5636, 13, 151645], "pred": "The workplace has been transformed by technology in several ways. It has increased efficiency and productivity, allowing employees to interact with a global market and even take work out on the road.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3720800913652151, "g_worst_claim": 0.6711185319083077, "g_content": 2.3437055699965534, "g_traj_mean": 1.663129448890686}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 46.34, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "625", "question": "how has it technology changed the workplace", "gt": "Based on the given passages, technology has changed the workplace in several ways, including:\n\n1. Increased efficiency and productivity: Technology has enabled automation of many tasks, allowing employees to focus on more complex and creative work, leading to increased productivity.\n2. Changes in workplace dynamics: Technology has transformed the way people communicate and collaborate in the workplace, enabling remote work and virtual teams.\n3. Rapid advancements: Technology has rapidly advanced in recent years, allowing employees to access new tools and resources, and adapt to changing market conditions.\n4. Global connectivity: Technology has enabled employees to interact with a global market and work remotely, allowing for greater flexibility and mobility.\n\nTherefore, technology has had a significant impact on the modern workplace, transforming the way people work, communicate, and collaborate.", "pred": "Technology has changed the workplace in several ways for the better. Firstly, technology has improved efficiency and increased productivity in the workplace. This can be seen in the shift in how we spend our time. Secondly, the continuous evolution of technology has transformed the environment, changing the dynamics of the workplace and what we perceive as possible. Finally, rapid technological advancement has allowed employees to interact with a global market and even take work out on the road.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Technology has changed the workplace in several ways for the better. Firstly, technology has improved efficiency and increased productivity in the workplace. This can be seen in the shift in how we spend our time. Secondly, the continuous evolution of technology has transformed the environment, changing the dynamics of the workplace and what we perceive as possible. Finally, rapid technological advancement has allowed employees to interact with a global market and even take work out on the road.", "cot": "[\"Technology has changed the workplace in several ways, including increased efficiency and productivity, a shift in how we spend our time, and the ability for employees to interact with a global market and take work on the road.\", \"Technology has transformed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, altering the dynamics and processes of the workplace, and allowing employees to interact with a global market.\", \"Technology has drastically changed the attitude and processes of the workplace. For example, the modern workplace has experienced a complete shift in how we spend our time, leading to increased efficiency and productivity. It also allows employees to interact with a global market and even take work out on the road.\", \"Technology has changed the workplace in several ways for the better. Firstly, technology has improved efficiency and increased productivity in the workplace. This can be seen in the shift in how we spend our time. Secondly, the continuous evolution of technology has transformed the environment, changing the dynamics of the workplace and what we perceive as possible. Finally, rapid technological advancement has allowed employees to interact with a global market and even take work out on the road.\"]", "time_sec": 11.649, "generation_time_seconds": 11.0642, "selection_time_seconds": 0.5778, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [62407, 702, 5497, 279, 26368, 304, 3807, 5510, 11, 2670, 7172, 15024, 323, 25148, 11, 264, 6407, 304, 1246, 582, 8329, 1039, 882, 11, 323, 279, 5726, 369, 8256, 311, 16282, 448, 264, 3644, 3081, 323, 1896, 975, 389, 279, 5636, 13, 151645], "pred": "Technology has changed the workplace in several ways, including increased efficiency and productivity, a shift in how we spend our time, and the ability for employees to interact with a global market and take work on the road.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0048471656110554, "g_worst_claim": 0.6083762248357137, "g_content": 2.9163530349731444, "g_traj_mean": 2.12705397605896}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [62407, 702, 23507, 279, 26368, 553, 7703, 15024, 323, 25148, 11, 59823, 279, 29195, 323, 11364, 315, 279, 26368, 11, 323, 10693, 8256, 311, 16282, 448, 264, 3644, 3081, 13, 151645], "pred": "Technology has transformed the workplace by increasing efficiency and productivity, altering the dynamics and processes of the workplace, and allowing employees to interact with a global market.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0595861614753903, "g_worst_claim": 1.677670045332475, "g_content": 3.061827850341797, "g_traj_mean": 1.9894827604293823}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [62407, 702, 47763, 5497, 279, 18915, 323, 11364, 315, 279, 26368, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 6481, 26368, 702, 10321, 264, 4583, 6407, 304, 1246, 582, 8329, 1039, 882, 11, 6388, 311, 7172, 15024, 323, 25148, 13, 1084, 1083, 6147, 8256, 311, 16282, 448, 264, 3644, 3081, 323, 1496, 1896, 975, 700, 389, 279, 5636, 13, 151645], "pred": "Technology has drastically changed the attitude and processes of the workplace. For example, the modern workplace has experienced a complete shift in how we spend our time, leading to increased efficiency and productivity. It also allows employees to interact with a global market and even take work out on the road.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.471806259920125, "g_worst_claim": 1.3435841969081335, "g_content": 3.909067224573206, "g_traj_mean": 2.4167046546936035}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [62407, 702, 5497, 279, 26368, 304, 3807, 5510, 369, 279, 2664, 13, 76695, 11, 5440, 702, 12944, 15024, 323, 7172, 25148, 304, 279, 26368, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 3884, 304, 279, 6407, 304, 1246, 582, 8329, 1039, 882, 13, 71031, 11, 279, 19259, 15379, 315, 5440, 702, 23507, 279, 4573, 11, 10018, 279, 29195, 315, 279, 26368, 323, 1128, 582, 44393, 438, 3204, 13, 17375, 11, 11048, 29016, 49825, 702, 5420, 8256, 311, 16282, 448, 264, 3644, 3081, 323, 1496, 1896, 975, 700, 389, 279, 5636, 13, 151645], "pred": "Technology has changed the workplace in several ways for the better. Firstly, technology has improved efficiency and increased productivity in the workplace. This can be seen in the shift in how we spend our time. Secondly, the continuous evolution of technology has transformed the environment, changing the dynamics of the workplace and what we perceive as possible. Finally, rapid technological advancement has allowed employees to interact with a global market and even take work out on the road.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1038445345052588, "g_worst_claim": 0.8133128773082386, "g_content": 3.1606626964750744, "g_traj_mean": 2.110795736312866}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.78, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "627", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "gt": "To guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay close to them when they are near the three-point line, actively sliding your feet to minimize shot opportunities (passage 1). It is important to create a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to defend against a tall player (passage 3).", "pred": "To guard a tall person in basketball, one should stay as close as possible to the tall player near the three-point line. It is important to actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To guard a tall person in basketball, one should stay as close as possible to the tall player near the three-point line. It is important to actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.", "cot": "[\"To guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay as close as possible to them, actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent, and minimize shot opportunities.\", \"To guard a tall person in basketball, it's important to maintain proximity to a skilled tall player and actively slide your feet from side to side.\", \"To guard a tall person in basketball, one should stay as close as possible to the tall player near the three-point line. It is important to actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.\", \"To guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay as close as possible to them near the three-point line. Actively slide your feet from side to side to minimize their shot opportunities. Additionally, when defending against a tall player, you should keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player. This technique is supported by an experienced basketball player in a free video on basketball defense uploaded on September 26, 2008.\"]", "time_sec": 12.46, "generation_time_seconds": 11.5272, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9278, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 7616, 264, 16217, 1697, 304, 19240, 11, 498, 1265, 4717, 438, 3265, 438, 3204, 311, 1105, 11, 22040, 14983, 697, 7541, 504, 3108, 311, 3108, 311, 4717, 3143, 697, 14704, 11, 323, 29337, 6552, 10488, 13, 151645], "pred": "To guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay as close as possible to them, actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent, and minimize shot opportunities.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.228437739610672, "g_worst_claim": 1.0960451364517212, "g_content": 2.470441394382053, "g_traj_mean": 2.005133628845215}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 7616, 264, 16217, 1697, 304, 19240, 11, 432, 594, 2989, 311, 10306, 36743, 311, 264, 25530, 16217, 2781, 323, 22040, 14983, 697, 7541, 504, 3108, 311, 3108, 13, 151645], "pred": "To guard a tall person in basketball, it's important to maintain proximity to a skilled tall player and actively slide your feet from side to side.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5540951121421087, "g_worst_claim": 1.0960451364517212, "g_content": 1.8529809315999348, "g_traj_mean": 1.6810134649276733}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 7616, 264, 16217, 1697, 304, 19240, 11, 825, 1265, 4717, 438, 3265, 438, 3204, 311, 279, 16217, 2781, 3143, 279, 2326, 16574, 1555, 13, 1084, 374, 2989, 311, 22040, 14983, 697, 7541, 504, 3108, 311, 3108, 311, 4717, 3143, 697, 14704, 323, 29337, 6552, 10488, 13, 151645], "pred": "To guard a tall person in basketball, one should stay as close as possible to the tall player near the three-point line. It is important to actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6961581199139413, "g_worst_claim": 1.0960451364517212, "g_content": 2.2933343505859374, "g_traj_mean": 1.847089171409607}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 7616, 264, 16217, 1697, 304, 19240, 11, 498, 1265, 4717, 438, 3265, 438, 3204, 311, 1105, 3143, 279, 2326, 16574, 1555, 13, 3218, 3132, 14983, 697, 7541, 504, 3108, 311, 3108, 311, 29337, 862, 6552, 10488, 13, 22406, 11, 979, 28169, 2348, 264, 16217, 2781, 11, 498, 1265, 2506, 264, 63685, 1948, 279, 14024, 323, 279, 15183, 2781, 13, 1096, 14762, 374, 7248, 553, 458, 10321, 19240, 2781, 304, 264, 1910, 2766, 389, 19240, 9055, 22853, 389, 6122, 220, 17, 21, 11, 220, 17, 15, 15, 23, 13, 151645], "pred": "To guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay as close as possible to them near the three-point line. Actively slide your feet from side to side to minimize their shot opportunities. Additionally, when defending against a tall player, you should keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player. This technique is supported by an experienced basketball player in a free video on basketball defense uploaded on September 26, 2008.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7618614478461527, "g_worst_claim": 0.8903962241278754, "g_content": 2.7237535134339943, "g_traj_mean": 1.840721607208252}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 58.46, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "628", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "gt": "To guard a tall person in basketball, you can stay as close as possible to them near the three-point line, actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent, and minimize shot opportunities. Additionally, you can keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player and defend against them with tips from an experienced basketball player.", "pred": "To guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay as close as possible to a tall, skilled shooter and actively slide your feet from side to side to minimize shot opportunities. According to Kareem Abdul-Jabbar Jr., a 6’6 guard, you've got to go with the cards you are dealt, meaning you should use your height advantage if you are tall yourself.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "To guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay as close as possible to a tall, skilled shooter and actively slide your feet from side to side to minimize shot opportunities. According to Kareem Abdul-Jabbar Jr., a 6’6 guard, you've got to go with the cards you are dealt, meaning you should use your height advantage if you are tall yourself.", "cot": "[\"To guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay as close as possible to them, actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent, and minimize shot opportunities.\", \"To guard a tall person in basketball, keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player. The key is to stay as close as possible to the tall, skilled shooter when you guard him near the three-point line and actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.\", \"To guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay as close as possible to a tall, skilled shooter and actively slide your feet from side to side to minimize shot opportunities. According to Kareem Abdul-Jabbar Jr., a 6’6 guard, you've got to go with the cards you are dealt, meaning you should use your height advantage if you are tall yourself.\", \"To guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay as close as possible to them, especially near the three-point line. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize their shot opportunities.\"]", "time_sec": 12.448, "generation_time_seconds": 11.8155, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6249, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 7616, 264, 16217, 1697, 304, 19240, 11, 498, 1265, 4717, 438, 3265, 438, 3204, 311, 1105, 11, 22040, 14983, 697, 7541, 504, 3108, 311, 3108, 311, 4717, 3143, 697, 14704, 11, 323, 29337, 6552, 10488, 13, 151645], "pred": "To guard a tall person in basketball, you should stay as close as possible to them, actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent, and minimize shot opportunities.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.297378878082548, "g_worst_claim": 1.2036968231201173, "g_content": 2.4910055796305337, "g_traj_mean": 2.035299777984619}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 7616, 264, 16217, 1697, 304, 19240, 11, 2506, 264, 63685, 1948, 279, 14024, 323, 279, 15183, 2781, 13, 576, 1376, 374, 311, 4717, 438, 3265, 438, 3204, 311, 279, 16217, 11, 25530, 31571, 979, 498, 7616, 1435, 3143, 279, 2326, 16574, 1555, 323, 22040, 14983, 697, 7541, 504, 3108, 311, 3108, 311, 4717, 3143, 697, 14704, 323, 29337, 6552, 10488, 13, 151645], "pred": "To guard a tall person in basketball, keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player. The key is to stay as close as possible to the tall, skilled shooter when you guard him near the three-point line and actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.1038404412341842, "g_worst_claim": 1.280598521232605, "g_content"