 to side to stay near the opponent and minimize shot opportunities. Additionally, keeping a wedge between the basket and the offensive player can help in defending against a tall player.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.768100310885717, "g_worst_claim": 1.3081176280975342, "g_content": 2.405748240152995, "g_traj_mean": 1.8961946964263916}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [38102, 438, 3265, 438, 3204, 311, 279, 16217, 1697, 979, 498, 7616, 1435, 3143, 279, 2326, 16574, 1555, 13, 3218, 3132, 14983, 697, 7541, 504, 3108, 311, 3108, 311, 4717, 3143, 697, 14704, 323, 29337, 6552, 10488, 13, 151645], "pred": "Stay as close as possible to the tall person when you guard him near the three-point line. Actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.6537358133416427, "g_worst_claim": 2.5391592728464225, "g_content": 3.5813629150390627, "g_traj_mean": 2.6084554195404053}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 56.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "632", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "gt": "The nervous system and endocrine system are both critical to maintaining homeostasis in the body by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems. They both use chemical messengers, although their method of transmission and release differs. The nervous system is made of interconnected neuron cells and uses electrochemical pulses for signal transmission. In contrast, the endocrine system is made of discrete glands that use hormones for signal transmission and utilizes the circulatory system to carry these signals.", "pred": "Differences:\n- The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\n- Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the Endocrine System, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\n- The nervous system is continuous with interconnected cells, while organs of the Endocrine System are discrete and not physically connected.\n- The nervous system uses neurons for signal transmission, whereas the Endocrine System utilizes the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Differences:\n- The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\n- Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the Endocrine System, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\n- The nervous system is continuous with interconnected cells, while organs of the Endocrine System are discrete and not physically connected.\n- The nervous system uses neurons for signal transmission, whereas the Endocrine System utilizes the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "cot": "[\"Similarities:\\n1. Both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n3. Chemical messengers are important in both systems.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the Endocrine System, it is done by hormones.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the Endocrine System are discrete and not physically connected.\\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the Endocrine System uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\", \"Similarities:\\n- Both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating activities.\\n- Both are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n- Chemical messengers are important in both systems, although their method of transmission and release differs.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n- The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\\n- Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the Endocrine System, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\\n- The nervous system is continuous with interconnected cells, while organs of the Endocrine System are discrete and not physically connected.\\n- The nervous system uses neurons for signal transmission, whereas the Endocrine System utilizes the circulatory system to transmit signals.\", \"Similarities: \\n- Both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\\n- Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n- Chemical messengers are important in both systems.\\n\\nDifferences: \\n- The nervous system is made up of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made up of glands.\\n- Transmission is performed by electrochemical pulses in the nervous system, whereas hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\\n- The nervous system is continuous and the cells are interconnected, while the organs of the endocrine system are not physically connected and are discrete.\\n- The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, whereas the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\", \"Similarities:\\n- Both systems are dedicated to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\\n- Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n- Chemical messengers are important in both systems.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n- The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\\n- Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, while hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\\n- The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are not physically connected and are discrete in nature.\\n- The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\"]", "time_sec": 24.185, "generation_time_seconds": 23.4246, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7537, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 510, 16, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 315, 1008, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 624, 18, 13, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 382, 35, 58326, 510, 16, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 48284, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 374, 1865, 315, 81275, 624, 17, 13, 47025, 304, 279, 22596, 1849, 374, 10660, 553, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 19853, 304, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 11, 432, 374, 2814, 553, 43215, 624, 18, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 11, 448, 7761, 82316, 11, 19853, 279, 35753, 315, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 525, 43179, 323, 537, 21893, 8433, 624, 19, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 59780, 33213, 311, 29282, 17289, 11, 1393, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 5711, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 29282, 17289, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the Endocrine System, it is done by hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the Endocrine System are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the Endocrine System uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5368869658983058, "g_worst_claim": 0.44095892906188966, "g_content": 2.125693334292059, "g_traj_mean": 1.3227605819702148}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 510, 12, 11733, 5942, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 7488, 624, 12, 11733, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 624, 12, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 11, 7892, 862, 1714, 315, 18368, 323, 4879, 43542, 382, 35, 58326, 510, 12, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 48284, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 374, 1865, 315, 81275, 624, 12, 47025, 304, 279, 22596, 1849, 374, 10660, 553, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 19853, 304, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 11, 432, 374, 2814, 553, 25266, 3881, 438, 43215, 624, 12, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 448, 82316, 7761, 11, 1393, 35753, 315, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 525, 43179, 323, 537, 21893, 8433, 624, 12, 576, 22596, 1849, 5711, 33213, 369, 8286, 18368, 11, 19853, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 59780, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 29282, 17289, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences:\n- The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\n- Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the Endocrine System, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\n- The nervous system is continuous with interconnected cells, while organs of the Endocrine System are discrete and not physically connected.\n- The nervous system uses neurons for signal transmission, whereas the Endocrine System utilizes the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5206415373651794, "g_worst_claim": 0.5377377782549176, "g_content": 2.537853914148667, "g_traj_mean": 1.4827357530593872}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 25, 715, 12, 11733, 5942, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 315, 1008, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 624, 12, 11733, 5942, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 624, 12, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 382, 35, 58326, 25, 715, 12, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 1865, 705, 315, 48284, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 374, 1865, 705, 315, 81275, 624, 12, 47025, 374, 10660, 553, 24394, 30956, 65457, 304, 279, 22596, 1849, 11, 19853, 43215, 525, 8480, 369, 8286, 18368, 304, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 624, 12, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 323, 279, 7761, 525, 82316, 11, 1393, 279, 35753, 315, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 525, 537, 21893, 8433, 323, 525, 43179, 624, 12, 576, 22596, 1849, 59780, 33213, 311, 29282, 17289, 11, 19853, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 5711, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 29282, 17289, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences: \n- The nervous system is made up of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made up of glands.\n- Transmission is performed by electrochemical pulses in the nervous system, whereas hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\n- The nervous system is continuous and the cells are interconnected, while the organs of the endocrine system are not physically connected and are discrete.\n- The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, whereas the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2874931403726395, "g_worst_claim": 0.18171390295028686, "g_content": 2.241262099322151, "g_traj_mean": 1.2501572370529175}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 510, 12, 11733, 5942, 525, 12235, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 315, 1008, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 624, 12, 11733, 5942, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 624, 12, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 382, 35, 58326, 510, 12, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 48284, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 81275, 624, 12, 47025, 304, 279, 22596, 1849, 374, 10660, 553, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 1393, 43215, 525, 8480, 369, 8286, 18368, 304, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 624, 12, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 11, 448, 7761, 82316, 11, 19853, 279, 35753, 315, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 525, 537, 21893, 8433, 323, 525, 43179, 304, 6993, 624, 12, 576, 22596, 1849, 59780, 33213, 311, 29282, 17289, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 5711, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 29282, 17289, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences:\n- The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n- Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, while hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\n- The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are not physically connected and are discrete in nature.\n- The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4469784119030489, "g_worst_claim": 0.23059076733059353, "g_content": 2.2320323270909928, "g_traj_mean": 1.345738410949707}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.45, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "633", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "gt": "The nervous system and endocrine system have both similarities and differences. \n\nSimilarities:\n1. Both systems are dedicated to maintaining homeostasis and coordinating the activities of cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\n3. Chemical messengers play a crucial role in both systems.\n\nDifferences:\n1. The nervous system is composed of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made up of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system occurs through electrochemical pulses, while chemical hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\n3. The nervous system utilizes interconnected cells to transmit signals, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system transmits signals through neurons, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "pred": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission is performed by electrochemical pulses in the nervous system, whereas chemicals known as hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are not physically connected and are discrete in nature.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system for transmitting signals.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission is performed by electrochemical pulses in the nervous system, whereas chemicals known as hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are not physically connected and are discrete in nature.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system for transmitting signals.", "cot": "[\"Similarities:\\n1. Both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n3. Chemical messengers are important in both systems.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the Endocrine System, it is done by hormones.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the Endocrine System are discrete and not physically connected.\\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the Endocrine System uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\", \"Similarities:\\n1. Both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n3. Chemical messengers are important in both systems, although their method of transmission and release differs.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\\n2. Transmission is performed by electrochemical pulses in the nervous system, whereas chemicals known as hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are not physically connected and are discrete in nature.\\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system for transmitting signals.\", \"Similarities:\\n1. Both systems are involved in maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n3. Chemical messengers are crucial in both systems, though they differ in their method of transmission and release.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is achieved through electrochemical pulses, whereas transmission in the endocrine system is handled by hormones.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with interconnected cells, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons for signal transmission, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\", \"Similarities:\\n1. Both the nervous system and the endocrine system are involved in maintaining homeostasis.\\n2. Both systems use chemical messengers.\\n3. Negative feedback mechanisms are employed by both systems to regulate activities.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas hormones in the endocrine system are responsible for signal transmission.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\\n4. The nervous system transmits signals using neurons, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\"]", "time_sec": 25.74, "generation_time_seconds": 24.8807, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8528, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 510, 16, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 315, 1008, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 624, 18, 13, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 382, 35, 58326, 510, 16, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 48284, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 374, 1865, 315, 81275, 624, 17, 13, 47025, 304, 279, 22596, 1849, 374, 10660, 553, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 19853, 304, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 11, 432, 374, 2814, 553, 43215, 624, 18, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 11, 448, 7761, 82316, 11, 19853, 279, 35753, 315, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 525, 43179, 323, 537, 21893, 8433, 624, 19, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 59780, 33213, 311, 29282, 17289, 11, 1393, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 5711, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 29282, 17289, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the Endocrine System, it is done by hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the Endocrine System are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the Endocrine System uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5255413652929577, "g_worst_claim": 0.4215541839599609, "g_content": 2.113636800687607, "g_traj_mean": 1.3120611906051636}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 510, 16, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 315, 1008, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 624, 18, 13, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 11, 7892, 862,