22596, 1849, 374, 16994, 1526, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 19853, 18368, 304, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 374, 17608, 553, 43215, 624, 18, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 11, 448, 82316, 7761, 11, 19853, 279, 35753, 315, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 525, 43179, 323, 537, 21893, 8433, 624, 19, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 59780, 33213, 369, 8286, 18368, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 5711, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 29282, 17289, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is achieved through electrochemical pulses, whereas transmission in the endocrine system is handled by hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with interconnected cells, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons for signal transmission, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3814749370342307, "g_worst_claim": 0.2476835780673557, "g_content": 1.753798086431962, "g_traj_mean": 1.1355355978012085}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 510, 16, 13, 11733, 279, 22596, 1849, 323, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 525, 6398, 304, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 5942, 990, 11483, 9435, 14886, 624, 18, 13, 50857, 11055, 23783, 525, 19446, 553, 2176, 5942, 311, 36277, 7488, 382, 35, 58326, 510, 16, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 48284, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 81275, 624, 17, 13, 47025, 304, 279, 22596, 1849, 374, 10660, 553, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 19853, 43215, 304, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 525, 8480, 369, 8286, 18368, 624, 18, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 11, 448, 7761, 82316, 11, 19853, 279, 35753, 315, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 525, 43179, 323, 537, 21893, 8433, 624, 19, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 1356, 44703, 17289, 1667, 33213, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 5711, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 29282, 17289, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas hormones in the endocrine system are responsible for signal transmission.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system transmits signals using neurons, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2079189533995802, "g_worst_claim": 0.1465807557106018, "g_content": 1.6334402005966395, "g_traj_mean": 1.004951000213623}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 67.13, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "634", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "gt": "Based on the given passages, we can see that the nervous system and endocrine system have some similarities and differences. \n\nSimilarities:\n- Both systems are responsible for maintaining homeostasis in the body.\n- Both systems use chemical messengers to coordinate and regulate the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n- Negative feedback mechanisms are used to regulate both systems.\n\nDifferences:\n- The nervous system is made up of neuron cells while the endocrine system is made up of glands.\n- Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses while transmission in the endocrine system is done through chemicals called hormones.\n- The nervous system is a continuous network of interconnected cells while the endocrine system consists of discrete organs that are not physically connected.\n- The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "pred": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is made up of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made up of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with interconnected cells, unlike the endocrine system's discrete organs.\n4. The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is made up of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made up of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with interconnected cells, unlike the endocrine system's discrete organs.\n4. The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "cot": "[\"Similarities:\\n1. Both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n3. Chemical messengers are important in both systems.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the Endocrine System, it is done by hormones.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the Endocrine System are discrete and not physically connected.\\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the Endocrine System uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\", \"Similarities:\\n1. Both systems are involved in maintaining homeostasis.\\n2. Both systems utilize chemical messengers for coordination.\\n3. Both systems have negative feedback mechanisms.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n1. The nervous system is made up of neurons, while the endocrine system consists of glands.\\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is achieved through electrochemical pulses, whereas it is through chemicals called hormones in the endocrine system.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with interconnected cells, while the endocrine organs are discrete and not physically connected.\\n4. The nervous system transmits signals through neurons, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\", \"Similarities:\\n1. Both the nervous system and endocrine system are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n3. Chemical messengers are important in both systems.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n1. The nervous system is made up of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made up of glands.\\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with interconnected cells, unlike the endocrine system's discrete organs.\\n4. The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\", \"Similarities:\\n1. Both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n3. Chemical messengers are important in both systems.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, while in the Endocrine System, hormones are responsible for signal transmission.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous and the cells are interconnected, whereas the organs of the Endocrine System are not physically connected and are discrete in nature.\\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, whereas the Endocrine System uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\\n5. The method of transmission and release of chemical messengers differs in the two systems.\"]", "time_sec": 25.063, "generation_time_seconds": 24.3331, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7236, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 510, 16, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 315, 1008, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 624, 18, 13, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 382, 35, 58326, 510, 16, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 48284, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 374, 1865, 315, 81275, 624, 17, 13, 47025, 304, 279, 22596, 1849, 374, 10660, 553, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 19853, 304, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 11, 432, 374, 2814, 553, 43215, 624, 18, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 11, 448, 7761, 82316, 11, 19853, 279, 35753, 315, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 525, 43179, 323, 537, 21893, 8433, 624, 19, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 59780, 33213, 311, 29282, 17289, 11, 1393, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 5711, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 29282, 17289, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the Endocrine System, it is done by hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the Endocrine System are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the Endocrine System uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5094551100000673, "g_worst_claim": 0.4621151924133301, "g_content": 2.0716559005110233, "g_traj_mean": 1.2968251705169678}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 510, 16, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 6398, 304, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 5942, 28066, 11483, 9435, 14886, 369, 37693, 624, 18, 13, 11733, 5942, 614, 8225, 11055, 23783, 382, 35, 58326, 510, 16, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 1865, 705, 315, 33213, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 17167, 315, 81275, 624, 17, 13, 47025, 304, 279, 22596, 1849, 374, 16994, 1526, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 19853, 432, 374, 1526, 25266, 2598, 43215, 304, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 624, 18, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 11, 448, 82316, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 35753, 525, 43179, 323, 537, 21893, 8433, 624, 19, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 1356, 44703, 17289, 1526, 33213, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 5711, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 29282, 17289, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is made up of neurons, while the endocrine system consists of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is achieved through electrochemical pulses, whereas it is through chemicals called hormones in the endocrine system.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with interconnected cells, while the endocrine organs are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system transmits signals through neurons, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1567970991715655, "g_worst_claim": 0.024936215952038765, "g_content": 1.4972354949466766, "g_traj_mean": 0.924159824848175}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 510, 16, 13, 11733, 279, 22596, 1849, 323, 835, 77638, 1849, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 315, 1008, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 624, 18, 13, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 382, 35, 58326, 510, 16, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 1865, 705, 315, 48284, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 374, 1865, 705, 315, 81275, 624, 17, 13, 47025, 304, 279, 22596, 1849, 374, 10660, 553, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 19853, 304, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 11, 432, 374, 2814, 553, 25266, 3881, 438, 43215, 624, 18, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 11, 448, 82316, 7761, 11, 19836, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 594, 43179, 35753, 624, 19, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 5711, 33213, 311, 29282, 17289, 11, 1393, 279, 835, 77638, 1849, 5711, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 29282, 17289, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is made up of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made up of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the endocrine system, it is done by chemicals known as hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with interconnected cells, unlike the endocrine system's discrete organs.\n4. The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.273727405743721, "g_worst_claim": 0.19381978511810302, "g_content": 1.693379050806949, "g_traj_mean": 1.0717295408248901}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 510, 16, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 315, 1008, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 624, 18, 13, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 382, 35, 58326, 510, 16, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 48284, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 374, 1865, 315, 81275, 624, 17, 13, 47025, 304, 279, 22596, 1849, 374, 10660, 553, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 1393, 304, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 11, 43215, 525, 8480, 369, 8286, 18368, 624, 18, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 323, 279, 7761, 525, 82316, 11, 19853, 279, 35753, 315, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 525, 537, 21893, 8433, 323, 525, 43179, 304, 6993, 624, 19, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 59780, 33213, 311, 29282, 17289, 11, 19853, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 5711, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 29282, 17289, 624, 20, 13, 576, 1714, 315, 18368, 323, 4879, 315, 11483, 9435, 14886, 43542, 304, 279, 1378, 5942, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, while in the Endocrine System, hormones are responsible for signal transmission.\n3. The nervous system is continuous and the cells are interconnected, whereas the organs of the Endocrine System are not physically connected and are discrete in nature.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, whereas the Endocrine System uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\n5. The method of transmission and release of chemical messengers differs in the two systems.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.504107148088139, "g_worst_claim": 0.16900103432791574, "g_content": 2.149478687959559, "g_traj_mean": 1.329899549484253}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 63.38, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "635", "question": "similarity and difference between nervous system and endocrine system", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are the key similarities and differences between the nervous system and the endocrine system:\n\nSimilarities:\n\n* Both systems are involved in maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\n* Both systems use chemical messengers (neurotransmitters and hormones) to transmit signals.\n* Both systems have negative feedback mechanisms to regulate their function.\n\nDifferences:\n\n* The nervous system is made up of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is composed of glands.\n* Transmission of signals occurs through electrical impulses in the nervous system, while hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the endocrine system.\n* The nervous system has a continuous structure, with cells connected to each other, while the endocrine system consists of discrete organs not physically connected to each other.\n* The nervous system uses neurons to transmit signals, while the endocrine system relies on the circulatory system to transmit signals.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is composed of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas the endocrine system uses hormones as chemical signals.\n3. In the nervous system, cells are interconnected continuously, whereas the organs in the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system transmits signals using neurons, in contrast to the endocrine system which uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is composed of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas the endocrine system uses hormones as chemical signals.\n3. In the nervous system, cells are interconnected continuously, whereas the organs in the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system transmits signals using neurons, in contrast to the endocrine system which uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "cot": "[\"Similarities:\\n1. Both systems are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n3. Chemical messengers are important in both systems.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the Endocrine System, it is done by hormones.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the Endocrine System are discrete and not physically connected.\\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the Endocrine System uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\", \"Similarities:\\n1. Both the nervous system and endocrine system are devoted to maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n3. Chemical messengers are important in both systems, although their method of transmission and release differs in the two systems.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\\n2. Transmission is performed by electrochemical pulses in the nervous system, while hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the Endocrine System.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous with interconnected cells, whereas the organs of the Endocrine System are discrete and not physically connected.\\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, whereas the Endocrine System uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\", \"Similarities:\\n1. Both systems are involved in maintaining homeostasis by coordinating and regulating the activities of other cells, tissues, organs, and systems.\\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n3. Chemical messengers are important in both systems, although their method of transmission and release differs in the two systems.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\\n2. Transmission is performed by the electrochemical pulses in the nervous system, while Chemicals known as hormones are responsible for signal transmission in the Endocrine System.\\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the Endocrine System are discrete and not physically connected.\\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, whereas the circulatory system is used by the Endocrine System to transmit signals.\", \"Similarities:\\n1. Both the nervous system and endocrine system contribute to maintaining homeostasis.\\n2. Both systems are regulated by negative feedback mechanisms.\\n3. Chemical messengers are significant in both systems.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n1. The nervous system is composed of neuron cells, while the endocrine system is made of glands.\\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas the endocrine system uses hormones as chemical signals.\\n3. In the nervous system, cells are interconnected continuously, whereas the organs in the endocrine system are discrete and not physically connected.\\n4. The nervous system transmits signals using neurons, in contrast to the endocrine system which uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.\"]", "time_sec": 26.281, "generation_time_seconds": 25.3542, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9173, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 510, 16, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 315, 1008, 7761, 11, 38781, 11, 35753, 11, 323, 5942, 624, 17, 13, 11733, 5942, 525, 34219, 553, 8225, 11055, 23783, 624, 18, 13, 35324, 9435, 14886, 525, 2989, 304, 2176, 5942, 382, 35, 58326, 510, 16, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 1865, 315, 48284, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 374, 1865, 315, 81275, 624, 17, 13, 47025, 304, 279, 22596, 1849, 374, 10660, 553, 24394, 30956, 65457, 11, 19853, 304, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 11, 432, 374, 2814, 553, 43215, 624, 18, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 374, 19259, 11, 448, 7761, 82316, 11, 19853, 279, 35753, 315, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 525, 43179, 323, 537, 21893, 8433, 624, 19, 13, 576, 22596, 1849, 59780, 33213, 311, 29282, 17289, 11, 1393, 279, 3972, 77638, 739, 5711, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 29282, 17289, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences:\n1. The nervous system is made of neuron cells, while the Endocrine System is made of glands.\n2. Transmission in the nervous system is performed by electrochemical pulses, whereas in the Endocrine System, it is done by hormones.\n3. The nervous system is continuous, with cells interconnected, whereas the organs of the Endocrine System are discrete and not physically connected.\n4. The nervous system utilizes neurons to transmit signals, while the Endocrine System uses the circulatory system to transmit signals.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5248458659922384, "g_worst_claim": 0.44913134574890134, "g_content": 2.0984806426583904, "g_traj_mean": 1.3101388216018677}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 510, 16, 13, 11733, 279, 22596, 1849, 323, 835, 77638, 1849, 525, 28229, 311, 20337, 2114, 535, 10718, 553, 65415, 323, 57399, 279, 7488, 3