cs": {"Token-F1": 36.36, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "641", "question": "differences and similarities between red and white blood cells", "gt": "Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are found in the blood and are part of the circulatory system. They are both formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow and contain cell membranes and cytoplasm. The main difference is their functions. RBCs are responsible for delivering oxygen from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while WBCs are part of the immune system and help the body combat diseases, viruses, etc.", "pred": "Red blood cells (RBCs) are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissues in the body. White blood cells (WBCs) are part of the immune system and help the body combat diseases and viruses. Both RBCs and WBCs circulate in the blood and are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Red blood cells (RBCs) are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissues in the body. White blood cells (WBCs) are part of the immune system and help the body combat diseases and viruses. Both RBCs and WBCs circulate in the blood and are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.", "cot": "[\"Similarities: - Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood. - Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\\n\\nDifferences: - Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\", \"Similarities:\\n- Both red blood cells and white blood cells are formed elements of blood.\\n- Both red blood cells and white blood cells can be carried by blood from one part to another part of our body.\\n- The red blood cells and white blood cells are found in the circulatory system.\\n- Both have cell membranes and cytoplasm.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n- Red blood cells (RBCs) carry oxygen and are responsible for the oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body. They are part of the circulatory system.\\n- White blood cells (WBCs) are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc. They are crucial in fighting infections.\", \"Similarities: - Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood. - RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\\n\\nDifferences: - RBCs are responsible for the oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while WBCs are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc. - RBCs circulate in the fluids in the blood vessels and are pumped by the heart, while WBCs are carried by blood from one part to another.\", \"Red blood cells (RBCs) are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissues in the body. White blood cells (WBCs) are part of the immune system and help the body combat diseases and viruses. Both RBCs and WBCs circulate in the blood and are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\"]", "time_sec": 19.655, "generation_time_seconds": 18.6849, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9634, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 25, 481, 11733, 2518, 6543, 7761, 320, 49, 4897, 82, 8, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 320, 54, 4897, 82, 8, 525, 14122, 5424, 315, 6543, 13, 481, 11733, 431, 4897, 82, 323, 467, 4897, 82, 525, 14122, 504, 59117, 573, 63532, 19101, 7761, 304, 279, 2518, 17240, 82648, 382, 35, 58326, 25, 481, 3731, 6543, 7761, 525, 8480, 369, 23552, 9691, 504, 279, 44174, 311, 279, 19847, 304, 279, 2487, 11, 1393, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 949, 315, 279, 22077, 1849, 323, 1492, 279, 2487, 12610, 8457, 11, 40968, 11, 4992, 13, 151645], "pred": "Similarities: - Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood. - Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\n\nDifferences: - Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1607895090527167, "g_worst_claim": 1.0153208645907315, "g_content": 2.0627935500372026, "g_traj_mean": 1.2186613082885742}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 510, 12, 11733, 2518, 6543, 7761, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 14122, 5424, 315, 6543, 624, 12, 11733, 2518, 6543, 7761, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 646, 387, 11691, 553, 6543, 504, 825, 949, 311, 2441, 949, 315, 1039, 2487, 624, 12, 576, 2518, 6543, 7761, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 1730, 304, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 624, 12, 11733, 614, 2779, 78248, 323, 9503, 98605, 10530, 382, 35, 58326, 510, 12, 3731, 6543, 7761, 320, 49, 4897, 82, 8, 6777, 23552, 323, 525, 8480, 369, 279, 23552, 9691, 504, 279, 44174, 311, 279, 19847, 304, 279, 2487, 13, 2379, 525, 949, 315, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 624, 12, 5807, 6543, 7761, 320, 54, 4897, 82, 8, 525, 949, 315, 279, 22077, 1849, 323, 1492, 279, 2487, 12610, 8457, 11, 40968, 11, 4992, 13, 2379, 525, 16587, 304, 10805, 28920, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences:\n- Red blood cells (RBCs) carry oxygen and are responsible for the oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body. They are part of the circulatory system.\n- White blood cells (WBCs) are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc. They are crucial in fighting infections.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1059945542988179, "g_worst_claim": 0.2918765885489328, "g_content": 1.711668534712358, "g_traj_mean": 1.1758396625518799}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 25, 481, 11733, 2518, 6543, 7761, 320, 49, 4897, 82, 8, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 320, 54, 4897, 82, 8, 525, 14122, 5424, 315, 6543, 13, 481, 431, 4897, 82, 323, 467, 4897, 82, 525, 14122, 504, 59117, 573, 63532, 19101, 7761, 304, 279, 2518, 17240, 82648, 382, 35, 58326, 25, 481, 431, 4897, 82, 525, 8480, 369, 279, 23552, 9691, 504, 279, 44174, 311, 279, 19847, 304, 279, 2487, 11, 1393, 467, 4897, 82, 525, 949, 315, 279, 22077, 1849, 323, 1492, 279, 2487, 12610, 8457, 11, 40968, 11, 4992, 13, 481, 431, 4897, 82, 4225, 6334, 304, 279, 55306, 304, 279, 6543, 29980, 323, 525, 61354, 553, 279, 4746, 11, 1393, 467, 4897, 82, 525, 11691, 553, 6543, 504, 825, 949, 311, 2441, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences: - RBCs are responsible for the oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while WBCs are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc. - RBCs circulate in the fluids in the blood vessels and are pumped by the heart, while WBCs are carried by blood from one part to another.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2440911728693207, "g_worst_claim": 0.9824232373918805, "g_content": 2.391674041748047, "g_traj_mean": 1.2712846994400024}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [6033, 6543, 7761, 320, 49, 4897, 82, 8, 525, 8480, 369, 23552, 9691, 504, 279, 44174, 311, 279, 38781, 304, 279, 2487, 13, 5807, 6543, 7761, 320, 54, 4897, 82, 8, 525, 949, 315, 279, 22077, 1849, 323, 1492, 279, 2487, 12610, 18808, 323, 40968, 13, 11733, 431, 4897, 82, 323, 467, 4897, 82, 4225, 6334, 304, 279, 6543, 323, 525, 14122, 504, 59117, 573, 63532, 19101, 7761, 304, 279, 2518, 17240, 82648, 13, 151645], "pred": "Red blood cells (RBCs) are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissues in the body. White blood cells (WBCs) are part of the immune system and help the body combat diseases and viruses. Both RBCs and WBCs circulate in the blood and are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9421802060697884, "g_worst_claim": 0.7309930665152413, "g_content": 1.6404009732333096, "g_traj_mean": 0.9236416816711426}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 77.11, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "643", "question": "differences and similarities between red and white blood cells", "gt": "Based on the given passages, we can see that the primary difference between red and white blood cells is their respective functions within the body. Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery to tissues, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help combat diseases and viruses. However, both types of cells share some common features, such as being formed elements of blood, being formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow, having a cell membrane and cytoplasm, and circulating in the fluids in blood vessels, which is pumped by the heart.", "pred": "Similarities: - RBCs, WBCs are formed elements of blood. - RBCs, WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow.\n\nDifferences: - RBCs are responsible for the oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while WBCs are a part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Similarities: - RBCs, WBCs are formed elements of blood. - RBCs, WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow.\n\nDifferences: - RBCs are responsible for the oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while WBCs are a part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.", "cot": "[\"Similarities: - Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood. - Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\\n\\nDifferences: - Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\", \"Similarities: Red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are both formed elements of blood. RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\\n\\nDifferences: RBCs and WBCs have distinct functions and properties. Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to tissues in the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help combat disease, viruses, etc. White blood cells can be carried by blood from one part to another, whereas RBCs primarily circulate in the circulatory system.\", \"Similarities: - RBCs, WBCs are formed elements of blood. - RBCs, WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow.\\n\\nDifferences: - RBCs are responsible for the oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while WBCs are a part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\", \"Similarities:\\n- Red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are both formed elements of blood.\\n- Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\\n\\nDifferences:\\n- Red blood cells are responsible for the oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are a part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\\n- Red blood cells carry oxygen throughout the body, whereas white blood cells are involved in fighting infections.\"]", "time_sec": 18.86, "generation_time_seconds": 17.8973, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9564, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 25, 481, 11733, 2518, 6543, 7761, 320, 49, 4897, 82, 8, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 320, 54, 4897, 82, 8, 525, 14122, 5424, 315, 6543, 13, 481, 11733, 431, 4897, 82, 323, 467, 4897, 82, 525, 14122, 504, 59117, 573, 63532, 19101, 7761, 304, 279, 2518, 17240, 82648, 382, 35, 58326, 25, 481, 3731, 6543, 7761, 525, 8480, 369, 23552, 9691, 504, 279, 44174, 311, 279, 19847, 304, 279, 2487, 11, 1393, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 949, 315, 279, 22077, 1849, 323, 1492, 279, 2487, 12610, 8457, 11, 40968, 11, 4992, 13, 151645], "pred": "Similarities: - Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are formed elements of blood. - Both RBCs and WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow.\n\nDifferences: - Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1579525166563263, "g_worst_claim": 0.986414909362793, "g_content": 2.0426490420386907, "g_traj_mean": 1.2161900997161865}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 25, 3731, 6543, 7761, 320, 49, 4897, 82, 8, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 320, 54, 4897, 82, 8, 525, 2176, 14122, 5424, 315, 6543, 13, 431, 4897, 82, 323, 467, 4897, 82, 525, 14122, 504, 59117, 573, 63532, 19101, 7761, 304, 279, 2518, 17240, 82648, 382, 35, 58326, 25, 431, 4897, 82, 323, 467, 4897, 82, 614, 12460, 5746, 323, 5888, 13, 3731, 6543, 7761, 525, 8480, 369, 23552, 9691, 504, 279, 44174, 311, 38781, 304, 279, 2487, 11, 1393, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 949, 315, 279, 22077, 1849, 323, 1492, 12610, 8457, 11, 40968, 11, 4992, 13, 5807, 6543, 7761, 646, 387, 11691, 553, 6543, 504, 825, 949, 311, 2441, 11, 19853, 431, 4897, 82, 15503, 4225, 6334, 304, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences: RBCs and WBCs have distinct functions and properties. Red blood cells are responsible for oxygen delivery from the lungs to tissues in the body, while white blood cells are part of the immune system and help combat disease, viruses, etc. White blood cells can be carried by blood from one part to another, whereas RBCs primarily circulate in the circulatory system.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.961108098698331, "g_worst_claim": 0.12697620689868927, "g_content": 1.5891014099121095, "g_traj_mean": 1.0012686252593994}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 25, 481, 431, 4897, 82, 11, 467, 4897, 82, 525, 14122, 5424, 315, 6543, 13, 481, 431, 4897, 82, 11, 467, 4897, 82, 525, 14122, 504, 59117, 573, 63532, 19101, 7761, 304, 2518, 17240, 82648, 382, 35, 58326, 25, 481, 431, 4897, 82, 525, 8480, 369, 279, 23552, 9691, 504, 279, 44174, 311, 279, 19847, 304, 279, 2487, 11, 1393, 467, 4897, 82, 525, 264, 949, 315, 279, 22077, 1849, 323, 1492, 279, 2487, 12610, 8457, 11, 40968, 11, 4992, 13, 151645], "pred": "Similarities: - RBCs, WBCs are formed elements of blood. - RBCs, WBCs are formed from pluripotent stem cells in red bone marrow.\n\nDifferences: - RBCs are responsible for the oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while WBCs are a part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9206075178137147, "g_worst_claim": 1.0033547719319662, "g_content": 2.6480836868286133, "g_traj_mean": 1.5552842617034912}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [34402, 1361, 510, 12, 3731, 6543, 7761, 320, 49, 4897, 82, 8, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 320, 54, 4897, 82, 8, 525, 2176, 14122, 5424, 315, 6543, 624, 12, 11733, 431, 4897, 82, 323, 467, 4897, 82, 525, 14122, 504, 59117, 573, 63532, 19101, 7761, 304, 279, 2518, 17240, 82648, 382, 35, 58326, 510, 12, 3731, 6543, 7761, 525, 8480, 369, 279, 23552, 9691, 504, 279, 44174, 311, 279, 19847, 304, 279, 2487, 11, 1393, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 264, 949, 315, 279, 22077, 1849, 323, 1492, 279, 2487, 12610, 8457, 11, 40968, 11, 4992, 624, 12, 3731, 6543, 7761, 6777, 23552, 6814, 279, 2487, 11, 19853, 4158, 6543, 7761, 525, 6398, 304, 10805, 28920, 13, 151645], "pred": "Differences:\n- Red blood cells are responsible for the oxygen delivery from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while white blood cells are a part of the immune system and help the body combat disease, viruses, etc.\n- Red blood cells carry oxygen throughout the body, whereas white blood cells are involved in fighting infections.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0080453459261243, "g_worst_claim": 0.6188066959381103, "g_content": 1.7679939270019531, "g_traj_mean": 1.1116582155227661}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 42.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "644", "question": "how to plant a potato that has sprouted", "gt": "To plant a potato that has sprouted, first cut large potatoes into chunks with two or three eyes each, being careful not to break the long sprouts. Place these chunks on a tray and let them dry out in a cool, dark place overnight. Small, sprouted potatoes can be planted whole. Next, prepare your planting area by turning the soil over with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches, removing any large rocks or debris. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep. Cut your potatoes into cubes of about 1 to 2 inches, making sure to leave a sprout on each cube. Place these cubes in the trench, sprouted side facing up, spaced about 6 to 8 inches apart. Cover the potatoes with compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings. Water the potatoes thoroughly and regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Finally, add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, keeping it at least 4 inches away from the sprouting potato vines. This mulch will help keep the soil cool and maintain a consistent moisture level.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can successfully plant a sprouted potato and ensure it grows well.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "By following these steps, you can successfully plant a sprouted potato and ensure it grows well.", "cot": "[\"To plant a sprouted potato, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Soil**: Turn the soil over in your planned planting area with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches and break the dirt up finely. Remove any large rocks and other debris while hoeing. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep.\\n\\n2. **Cut the Potato**: Cut the sprouted potato into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. Nonsprouted sections should have two or three eyes on each.\\n\\n3. **Plant the Cubes**: Place the cubes into the bottom of the trench, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches. Place the sprouted or eye side of the cubes facing up.\\n\\n4. **Cover with Compost and Soil**: Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings.\\n\\n5. **Maintain Moisture and Mulch**: Water the potatoes thoroughly and continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines. Mulch keeps the soil cool while maintaining a consistent moisture level.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can successfully plant a sprouted potato and ensure it grows well.\", \"Answer: If a potato has sprouted, it should be cut into chunks with two or three eyes each. These chunks should be placed on a tray or cookie sheet and set in a cool, dark location overnight so the cut ends can dry out. Small potatoes can be planted whole. The potatoes should be watered thoroughly and continued to be watered regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. A 4-inch layer of mulch should be added around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines. Mulch helps to keep the soil cool while maintaining a consistent moisture level.\", \"To plant a potato that has sprouted, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Prepare the soil: Turn the soil over in your planned planting area with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches and break the dirt up finely. Remove any large rocks and other debris while hoeing. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep.\\n\\n2. Cut the sprouted potato: Cut the sprouted potato into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. Nonsprouted sections should have two or three eyes on each.\\n\\n3. Place the cubes in the trench: Cut your potatoes into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. Nonsprouted sections should have two or three eyes on each. Place the cubes into the bottom of the trench, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches. Place the sprouted or eye side of the cubes facing up.\\n\\n4. Cover and replace soil: Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings.\\n\\nThis method ensures that the sprouted potato is planted correctly and has the best chance of growing into a healthy plant.\", \"1. Cut large, sprouted potatoes into chunks with two or three eyes each, using a sharp knife, being careful to not break the long sprouts. Place the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet, and set them in a cool, dark location overnight so the cut ends can dry out. Small potatoes can be planted whole.ater the potatoes thoroughly. Continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines. Mulch keeps the soil cool while maintaining a consistent moisture level.\"]", "time_sec": 30.688, "generation_time_seconds": 29.7924, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8879, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 6008, 264, 8151, 18533, 38734, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 75519, 95518, 11999, 279, 17171, 916, 304, 697, 12909, 47014, 3082, 448, 264, 45876, 476, 11956, 261, 311, 264, 7990, 315, 220, 16, 17, 14924, 323, 1438, 279, 25284, 705, 60702, 13, 10783, 894, 3460, 23035, 323, 1008, 33998, 1393, 45876, 287, 13, 37969, 264, 53252, 911, 220, 19, 14924, 6884, 323, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 5538, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 37666, 279, 77603, 95518, 19649, 279, 8151, 18533, 38734, 1119, 54104, 11, 911, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 14924, 389, 1817, 3108, 11, 9380, 264, 8151, 411, 389, 1817, 23739, 13, 451, 2382, 649, 18533, 14158, 1265, 614, 1378, 476, 2326, 6414, 389, 1817, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 54647, 279, 18030, 288, 95518, 10771, 279, 54104, 1119, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 53252, 11, 49445,