 tray or cookie sheet and set in a cool, dark location overnight so the cut ends can dry out. Small potatoes can be planted whole. The potatoes should be watered thoroughly and continued to be watered regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. A 4-inch layer of mulch should be added around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines. Mulch helps to keep the soil cool while maintaining a consistent moisture level.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6693370582973388, "g_worst_claim": 0.827797359890408, "g_content": 2.0819862002418157, "g_traj_mean": 1.6440740823745728}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 6008, 264, 38734, 429, 702, 8151, 18533, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 17171, 25, 11999, 279, 17171, 916, 304, 697, 12909, 47014, 3082, 448, 264, 45876, 476, 11956, 261, 311, 264, 7990, 315, 220, 16, 17, 14924, 323, 1438, 279, 25284, 705, 60702, 13, 10783, 894, 3460, 23035, 323, 1008, 33998, 1393, 45876, 287, 13, 37969, 264, 53252, 911, 220, 19, 14924, 6884, 323, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 5538, 382, 17, 13, 19649, 279, 8151, 18533, 38734, 25, 19649, 279, 8151, 18533, 38734, 1119, 54104, 11, 911, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 14924, 389, 1817, 3108, 11, 9380, 264, 8151, 411, 389, 1817, 23739, 13, 451, 2382, 649, 18533, 14158, 1265, 614, 1378, 476, 2326, 6414, 389, 1817, 382, 18, 13, 10771, 279, 54104, 304, 279, 53252, 25, 19649, 697, 34167, 1119, 54104, 11, 911, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 14924, 389, 1817, 3108, 11, 9380, 264, 8151, 411, 389, 1817, 23739, 13, 451, 2382, 649, 18533, 14158, 1265, 614, 1378, 476, 2326, 6414, 389, 1817, 13, 10771, 279, 54104, 1119, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 53252, 11, 49445, 1817, 23739, 504, 279, 1008, 553, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 13, 10771, 279, 8151, 18533, 476, 7912, 3108, 315, 279, 54104, 12880, 705, 382, 19, 13, 17757, 323, 8290, 17171, 25, 17757, 279, 34167, 448, 264, 6193, 315, 56723, 323, 1221, 8290, 279, 25284, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 6008, 819, 382, 1986, 1714, 25351, 429, 279, 8151, 18533, 38734, 374, 38341, 12440, 323, 702, 279, 1850, 6012, 315, 7826, 1119, 264, 9314, 6008, 13, 151645], "pred": "This method ensures that the sprouted potato is planted correctly and has the best chance of growing into a healthy plant.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1477542444939877, "g_worst_claim": 0.0206522395213445, "g_content": 1.6300992965698242, "g_traj_mean": 1.2703622579574585}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16, 13, 19649, 3460, 11, 8151, 18533, 34167, 1119, 26757, 448, 1378, 476, 2326, 6414, 1817, 11, 1667, 264, 17232, 21430, 11, 1660, 16585, 311, 537, 1438, 279, 1293, 8151, 11672, 13, 10771, 279, 38734, 26757, 389, 264, 34688, 476, 12544, 10834, 11, 323, 738, 1105, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 6319, 3728, 24398, 773, 279, 3931, 10335, 646, 9058, 700, 13, 14994, 34167, 646, 387, 38341, 4361, 13, 962, 279, 34167, 26364, 13, 15003, 72741, 15502, 979, 279, 17171, 374, 9058, 311, 279, 5796, 13, 2691, 264, 220, 19, 24241, 6193, 315, 15602, 331, 2163, 279, 10779, 11, 22266, 432, 1182, 518, 3245, 220, 19, 14924, 504, 279, 8151, 10909, 38734, 85429, 13, 29351, 331, 13598, 279, 17171, 7010, 1393, 20337, 264, 12966, 31157, 2188, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Cut large, sprouted potatoes into chunks with two or three eyes each, using a sharp knife, being careful to not break the long sprouts. Place the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet, and set them in a cool, dark location overnight so the cut ends can dry out. Small potatoes can be planted whole.ater the potatoes thoroughly. Continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines. Mulch keeps the soil cool while maintaining a consistent moisture level.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.384451847593817, "g_worst_claim": 0.993363652910505, "g_content": 2.763666788736979, "g_traj_mean": 2.182201862335205}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.59, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "645", "question": "how to plant a potato that has sprouted", "gt": "To plant a sprouted potato, cut it into chunks with two or three eyes each. Place the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet and let them dry out overnight. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep in a prepared planting area. Place the sprouted or eye side of the potato chunks facing up, separating each chunk by about 6 to 8 inches. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top. Water the potatoes thoroughly and continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants to keep the soil cool and maintain moisture.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can successfully plant a sprouted potato and ensure it grows well.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "By following these steps, you can successfully plant a sprouted potato and ensure it grows well.", "cot": "[\"To plant a sprouted potato, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Soil**: Turn the soil over in your planned planting area with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches and break the dirt up finely. Remove any large rocks and other debris while hoeing. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep.\\n\\n2. **Cut the Potato**: Cut the sprouted potato into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. Nonsprouted sections should have two or three eyes on each.\\n\\n3. **Plant the Cubes**: Place the cubes into the bottom of the trench, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches. Place the sprouted or eye side of the cubes facing up.\\n\\n4. **Cover with Compost and Soil**: Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings.\\n\\n5. **Maintain Moisture and Mulch**: Water the potatoes thoroughly and continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines. Mulch keeps the soil cool while maintaining a consistent moisture level.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can successfully plant a sprouted potato and ensure it grows well.\", \"Answer: To plant a sprouted potato, you should first turn the soil over in the planned planting area to a depth of 12 inches and break the dirt up finely. Remove any large rocks and other debris while hoeing. Next, dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep. For planting multiple rows, space them apart by about 24 to 36 inches. Cut the sprouted potato into cubes, each about 1 to 2 inches on each side, with the sprout or eye side facing up. Place the cubes into the bottom of the trench, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings.\", \"1. Cut the sprouted potato into chunks, making sure each chunk has two or three eyes.\\n2. Place the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet and set them in a cool, dark location overnight to dry out the cut ends.\\n3. After drying, water the potato chunks thoroughly.\\n4. Continue to water regularly when the soil is dry to the touch.\\n5. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines.\\n6. To plant, turn the soil over in your planned planting area to a depth of 12 inches and break the dirt up finely.\\n7. Remove any large rocks and other debris while hoeing.\\n8. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep.\\n9. If planting more than one row, space them apart by about 24 to 36 inches.\\n10. Cut your potatoes into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube.\\n11. Nonsprouted sections should have two or three eyes on each.\\n12. Place the cubes into the bottom of the trench, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches.\\n13. Place the sprouted or eye side of the cubes facing up.\\n14. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings.\", \"To plant a sprouted potato, first turn the soil over in your planned planting area with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches and break the dirt up finely. Remove any large rocks and other debris while hoeing. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep.If you're going to plant more than one row, space them apart by about 24 to 36 inches.Cut your potatoes into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. Nonsprouted sections should have two or three eyes on each.Place the cubes into the bottom of the trench, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches. Place the sprouted or eye side of the cubes facing up.Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings.\"]", "time_sec": 36.68, "generation_time_seconds": 35.5294, "selection_time_seconds": 1.1443, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 6008, 264, 8151, 18533, 38734, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 75519, 95518, 11999, 279, 17171, 916, 304, 697, 12909, 47014, 3082, 448, 264, 45876, 476, 11956, 261, 311, 264, 7990, 315, 220, 16, 17, 14924, 323, 1438, 279, 25284, 705, 60702, 13, 10783, 894, 3460, 23035, 323, 1008, 33998, 1393, 45876, 287, 13, 37969, 264, 53252, 911, 220, 19, 14924, 6884, 323, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 5538, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 37666, 279, 77603, 95518, 19649, 279, 8151, 18533, 38734, 1119, 54104, 11, 911, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 14924, 389, 1817, 3108, 11, 9380, 264, 8151, 411, 389, 1817, 23739, 13, 451, 2382, 649, 18533, 14158, 1265, 614, 1378, 476, 2326, 6414, 389, 1817, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 54647, 279, 18030, 288, 95518, 10771, 279, 54104, 1119, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 53252, 11, 49445, 1817, 23739, 504, 279, 1008, 553, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 