220, 19, 14924, 6884, 323, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 5538, 624, 18, 13, 1416, 498, 2299, 2087, 311, 6008, 803, 1091, 825, 2802, 11, 3550, 1105, 10747, 553, 911, 220, 17, 19, 311, 220, 18, 21, 14924, 624, 19, 13, 19649, 697, 34167, 1119, 54104, 11, 911, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 14924, 389, 1817, 3108, 11, 9380, 264, 8151, 411, 389, 1817, 23739, 13, 451, 2382, 649, 18533, 14158, 1265, 614, 1378, 476, 2326, 6414, 389, 1817, 624, 20, 13, 10771, 279, 54104, 1119, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 53252, 11, 49445, 1817, 23739, 504, 279, 1008, 553, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 13, 10771, 279, 8151, 18533, 476, 7912, 3108, 315, 279, 54104, 12880, 705, 624, 21, 13, 17757, 279, 34167, 448, 264, 6193, 315, 56723, 323, 1221, 8290, 279, 25284, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 6008, 819, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 7790, 6008, 264, 8151, 18533, 38734, 323, 5978, 1181, 6513, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can successfully plant a sprouted potato and ensure its growth.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4299825898794052, "g_worst_claim": -0.013319455087184906, "g_content": 1.888762443296371, "g_traj_mean": 1.4846551418304443}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 2014, 6008, 264, 8151, 18533, 38734, 11, 1156, 3931, 279, 3460, 11, 8151, 18533, 34167, 1119, 26757, 448, 1378, 476, 2326, 6414, 1817, 13, 10771, 279, 38734, 26757, 389, 264, 34688, 476, 12544, 10834, 11, 323, 738, 1105, 304, 264, 7010, 11, 6319, 3728, 24398, 773, 279, 3931, 10335, 646, 9058, 700, 13, 4636, 72741, 279, 34167, 26364, 11, 3060, 72741, 15502, 979, 279, 17171, 374, 9058, 311, 279, 5796, 13, 5005, 11, 4078, 264, 53252, 911, 220, 19, 14924, 6884, 323, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 5538, 304, 279, 47014, 3082, 13, 19649, 697, 34167, 1119, 54104, 11, 911, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 14924, 389, 1817, 3108, 11, 9380, 264, 8151, 411, 389, 1817, 23739, 13, 10771, 279, 54104, 1119, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 53252, 11, 49445, 1817, 23739, 504, 279, 1008, 553, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 13, 10771, 279, 8151, 18533, 476, 7912, 3108, 315, 279, 54104, 12880, 705, 13, 17757, 279, 34167, 448, 264, 6193, 315, 56723, 323, 1221, 8290, 279, 25284, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 6008, 819, 13, 151645], "pred": "To plant a sprouted potato, first cut the large, sprouted potatoes into chunks with two or three eyes each. Place the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet, and set them in a cool, dark location overnight so the cut ends can dry out. After watering the potatoes thoroughly, continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Then, dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep in the planting area. Cut your potatoes into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. Place the cubes into the bottom of the trench, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches. Place the sprouted or eye side of the cubes facing up. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7671637996371037, "g_worst_claim": 0.6974456621252972, "g_content": 2.2497636795043947, "g_traj_mean": 1.6296508312225342}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 7.55, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.4, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "647", "question": "how to plant a potato that has sprouted", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to plant a potato that has sprouted:\n\n1. Cut the sprouted potato into chunks with two or three eyes each, making sure to not break the long sprouts.\n2. Allow the cut ends to dry out overnight in a cool, dark location.\n3. Plant the potato chunks or whole potatoes in well-draining soil, spacing them 24 to 36 inches apart.\n4. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep, and place the potato pieces in the bottom of the trench with the sprouted side facing up.\n5. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings.\n\nNote that the passages do not provide specific information on how to care for the potatoes after planting, such as watering and fertilization.", "pred": "This method ensures that the sprouted potato is planted correctly for optimal growth.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "This method ensures that the sprouted potato is planted correctly for optimal growth.", "cot": "[\"To plant a sprouted potato, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Soil**: Turn the soil over in your planned planting area with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches and break the dirt up finely. Remove any large rocks and other debris while hoeing. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep.\\n\\n2. **Cut the Potato**: Cut the sprouted potato into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. Nonsprouted sections should have two or three eyes on each.\\n\\n3. **Plant the Cubes**: Place the cubes into the bottom of the trench, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches. Place the sprouted or eye side of the cubes facing up.\\n\\n4. **Cover with Compost and Soil**: Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings.\\n\\n5. **Maintain Moisture and Mulch**: Water the potatoes thoroughly and continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants, pulling it back at least 4 inches from the sprouting potato vines. Mulch keeps the soil cool while maintaining a consistent moisture level.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can successfully plant a sprouted potato and ensure it grows well.\", \"Answer: To plant a sprouted potato, follow these steps:\\n1. Prepare the planting area: Turn the soil over with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches, breaking the dirt up finely and removing any large rocks and debris.\\n2. Create a trench: Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep.\\n3. Cut the potatoes: Cut the sprouted potato into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. Nonsprouted sections should have two or three eyes on each.\\n4. Plant the cubes: Place the cubes into the bottom of the trench, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches, with the sprouted or eye side facing up.\\n5. Cover the planting area: Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings.\", \"Planting a sprouted potato involves several steps to ensure healthy growth. First, turn the soil over in your planned planting area with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches and break the dirt up finely. Remove any large rocks and other debris while hoeing. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep. If you're going to plant more than one row, space them apart by about 24 to 36 inches. Cut your potatoes into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. Nonsprouted sections should have two or three eyes on each. Place the cubes into the bottom of the trench, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches. Place the sprouted or eye side of the cubes facing up. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings. This method ensures that each sprouted potato cube is properly placed and has enough space to grow its roots.\", \"To plant a sprouted potato:\\n\\n1. Prepare the soil: Use a hoe or tiller to turn the soil over to a depth of 12 inches and break it up finely. Remove large rocks and debris.\\n\\n2. Create a trench: Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep. If planting multiple rows, space them apart by about 24 to 36 inches.\\n\\n3. Prepare the potatoes: Cut the potatoes into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. For nonsprouted sections, leave two or three eyes on each cube.\\n\\n4. Plant the potatoes: Place the cubes into the bottom of the trench, separating each cube by about 6 to 8 inches, with the sprouted or eye side facing up. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost.\\n\\n5. Finish planting: Replace the dirt on top of the plantings to complete the process.\\n\\nThis method ensures that the sprouted potato is planted correctly for optimal growth.\"]", "time_sec": 34.601, "generation_time_seconds": 33.6838, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9106, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 6008, 264, 8151, 18533, 38734, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 75519, 95518, 11999, 279, 17171, 916, 304, 697, 12909, 47014, 3082, 448, 264, 45876, 476, 11956, 261, 311, 264, 7990, 315, 220, 16, 17, 14924, 323, 1438, 279, 25284, 705, 60702, 13, 10783, 894, 3460, 23035, 323, 1008, 33998, 1393, 45876, 287, 13, 37969, 264, 53252, 911, 220, 19, 14924, 6884, 323, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 5538, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 37666, 279, 77603, 95518, 19649, 279, 8151, 18533, 38734, 1119, 54104, 11, 911, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 14924, 389, 1817, 3108, 11, 9380, 264, 8151, 411, 389, 1817, 23739, 13, 451, 2382, 649, 18533, 14158, 1265, 614, 1378, 476, 2326, 6414, 389, 1817, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 54647, 279, 18030, 288, 95518, 10771, 279, 54104, 1119,