1, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 11, 448, 279, 8151, 18533, 476, 7912, 3108, 12880, 705, 624, 20, 13, 17757, 279, 47014, 3082, 25, 17757, 279, 34167, 448, 264, 6193, 315, 56723, 323, 1221, 8290, 279, 25284, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 6008, 819, 13, 151645], "pred": "To plant a sprouted potato, follow these steps:", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3717648842097034, "g_worst_claim": -0.1455542246500651, "g_content": 1.7953627253153237, "g_traj_mean": 1.37676203250885}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [54647, 287, 264, 8151, 18533, 38734, 17601, 3807, 7354, 311, 5978, 9314, 6513, 13, 5512, 11, 2484, 279, 17171, 916, 304, 697, 12909, 47014, 3082, 448, 264, 45876, 476, 11956, 261, 311, 264, 7990, 315, 220, 16, 17, 14924, 323, 1438, 279, 25284, 705, 60702, 13, 10783, 894, 3460, 23035, 323, 1008, 33998, 1393, 45876, 287, 13, 37969, 264, 53252, 911, 220, 19, 14924, 6884, 323, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 5538, 13, 1416, 498, 2299, 2087, 311, 6008, 803, 1091, 825, 2802, 11, 3550, 1105, 10747, 553, 911, 220, 17, 19, 311, 220, 18, 21, 14924, 13, 19649, 697, 34167, 1119, 54104, 11, 911, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 14924, 389, 1817, 3108, 11, 9380, 264, 8151, 411, 389, 1817, 23739, 13, 451, 2382, 649, 18533, 14158, 1265, 614, 1378, 476, 2326, 6414, 389, 1817, 13, 10771, 279, 54104, 1119, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 53252, 11, 49445, 1817, 23739, 504, 279, 1008, 553, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 13, 10771, 279, 8151, 18533, 476, 7912, 3108, 315, 279, 54104, 12880, 705, 13, 17757, 279, 34167, 448, 264, 6193, 315, 56723, 323, 1221, 8290, 279, 25284, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 6008, 819, 13, 1096, 1714, 25351, 429, 1817, 8151, 18533, 38734, 23739, 374, 10277, 9099, 323, 702, 3322, 3550, 311, 3063, 1181, 19703, 13, 151645], "pred": "Planting a sprouted potato involves several steps to ensure healthy growth. First, turn the soil over in your planned planting area with a hoe or tiller to a depth of 12 inches and break the dirt up finely. Remove any large rocks and other debris while hoeing. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep. If you're going to plant more than one row, space them apart by about 24 to 36 inches. Cut your potatoes into cubes, about 1 to 2 inches on each side, leaving a sprout on each cube. Nonsprouted sections should have two or three eyes on each. Place the cubes into the bottom of the trench, separating each cube from the other by about 6 to 8 inches. Place the sprouted or eye side of the cubes facing up. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top of the plantings. This method ensures that each sprouted potato cube is properly placed and has enough space to grow its roots.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5702033368482264, "g_worst_claim": 0.5453311375209263, "g_content": 2.116134964792352, "g_traj_mean": 1.5564919710159302}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 6008, 264, 8151, 18533, 38734, 1447, 16, 13, 31166, 279, 17171, 25, 5443, 264, 45876, 476, 11956, 261, 311, 2484, 279, 17171, 916, 311, 264, 7990, 315, 220, 16, 17, 14924, 323, 1438, 432, 705, 60702, 13, 10783, 3460, 23035, 323, 33998, 382, 17, 13, 4230, 264, 53252, 25, 37969, 264, 53252, 911, 220, 19, 14924, 6884, 323, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 5538, 13, 1416, 47014, 5248, 6978, 11, 3550, 1105, 10747, 553, 911, 220, 17, 19, 311, 220, 18, 21, 14924, 382, 18, 13, 31166, 279, 34167, 25, 19649, 279, 34167, 1119, 54104, 11, 911, 220, 16, 311, 220, 17, 14924, 389, 1817, 3108, 11, 9380, 264, 8151, 411, 389, 1817, 23739, 13, 1752, 31695, 649, 18533, 14158, 11, 5274, 1378, 476, 2326, 6414, 389, 1817, 23739, 382, 19, 13, 17838, 279, 34167, 25, 10771, 279, 54104, 1119, 279, 5622, 315, 279, 53252, 11, 49445, 1817, 23739, 553, 911, 220, 21, 311, 220, 23, 14924, 11, 448, 279, 8151, 18533, 476, 7912, 3108, 12880, 705, 13, 17757, 279, 34167, 448, 264, 6193, 315, 56723, 382, 20, 13, 35533, 47014, 25, 29558, 279, 25284, 389, 1909, 315, 279, 6008, 819, 311, 4583, 279, 1882, 382, 1986, 1714, 25351, 429, 279, 8151, 18533, 38734, 374, 38341, 12440, 369, 22823, 6513, 13, 151645], "pred": "This method ensures that the sprouted potato is planted correctly for optimal growth.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.443506038804733, "g_worst_claim": 0.5523111343383789, "g_content": 1.7993823179264659, "g_traj_mean": 1.2344602346420288}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 4.04, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "648", "question": "color of urin meaning", "gt": "The color of urine can indicate various health conditions. Normal urine is typically pale yellow, due to the pigment urochrome. If kidney diseases are present, the filtration and re-absorption stages of urine production may be malfunctioning, altering this pale color. Red urine is typically a sign of blood in the urine, which can indicate serious conditions like infections or cancer. Deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. Foods and medications can also affect urine color, with beets, berries, and fava beans being among the most likely to cause changes.", "pred": "The normal color of urine is pale yellow, and this color is due to the pigment urochrome.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The normal color of urine is pale yellow, and this color is due to the pigment urochrome.", "cot": "[\"The color of urine can vary based on several factors. A normal urine color is typically pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, the color can be affected by various conditions and factors such as:\\n\\n1. **Blood in the Urine**: If there is blood in the urine, it can produce a dramatic color change, often turning the urine red. This can be a sign of serious conditions like infections or cancer, and it is important to consult a doctor or urologist.\\n\\n2. **Porphyria**: Deep purple urine is a characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. This condition is caused by an abnormal accumulation of porphyrins in the body, which can lead to the production of purple urine.\\n\\n3. **Food and Medications**: Certain foods and medications can also change the color of urine. For example, beets, berries, and fava beans are among the foods most likely to affect urine color. Medications like rifampin, which is used to treat tuberculosis, can also cause urine to turn a reddish or orange color.\\n\\n4. **Kidney Diseases**: In cases of kidney diseases, the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production can malfunction, leading to changes in urine color. This can result in a darker or lighter urine color than normal.\\n\\nIn summary, the color of urine can vary due to blood, certain medical conditions, dietary factors, and medications.\", \"Normal color of urine is pale yellow due to the pigment urochrome.\", \"The normal color of urine is pale yellow, and this color is due to the pigment urochrome.\", \"The color of urine is often described as pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, this color can change due to various factors, including certain medications, foods, and conditions such as porphyria, an inherited disorder of red blood cells.\"]", "time_sec": 17.452, "generation_time_seconds": 16.9511, "selection_time_seconds": 0.4968, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 1894, 315, 39235, 646, 13289, 3118, 389, 3807, 9363, 13, 362, 4622, 39235, 1894, 374, 11136, 27539, 13753, 11, 892, 374, 4152, 311, 279, 76578, 575, 299, 31902, 13, 4354, 11, 279, 1894, 646, 387, 11495, 553, 5257, 4682, 323, 9363, 1741, 438, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 51486, 304, 279, 16809, 482, 95518, 1416, 1052, 374, 6543, 304, 279, 39235, 11, 432, 646, 8193, 264, 21771, 1894, 2297, 11, 3545, 13054, 279, 39235, 2518, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 264, 1841, 315, 6001, 4682, 1075, 28920, 476, 9387, 11, 323, 432, 374, 2989, 311, 8498, 264, 10668, 476, 575, 299, 839, 380, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 28097, 12700, 4204, 95518, 18183, 24932, 39235, 374, 264, 28583, 315, 4154, 12700, 4204, 11, 264, 8848, 11, 26990, 19267, 315, 2518, 6543, 7761, 13, 1096, 2971, 374, 8881, 553, 458, 34563, 45735, 315, 4154, 759, 10920, 1330, 304, 279, 2487, 11, 892, 646, 2990, 311, 279, 5670, 315, 24932, 39235, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 26746, 323, 12566, 804, 95518, 34111, 15298, 323, 29910, 646, 1083, 2297, 279, 1894, 315, 39235, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 387, 1415, 11, 62394, 11, 323, 282, 2907, 26896, 525, 4221, 279, 15298, 1429, 4363, 311, 7802, 39235, 1894, 13, 12566, 804, 1075, 36924, 1121, 258, 11, 892, 374, 1483, 311, 4228, 87134, 11, 646, 1083, 5240, 39235, 311, 2484, 264, 62144, 812, 476, 18575, 1894, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 98508, 3437, 69574, 95518, 758, 5048, 315, 37942, 18808, 11, 279, 74938, 323, 42910, 312, 96410, 65081, 17628, 315, 39235, 5670, 646, 71187, 11, 6388, 311, 4344, 304, 39235, 1894, 13, 1096, 646, 1102, 304, 264, 39030, 476, 29573, 39235, 1894, 1091, 4622, 382, 641, 12126, 11, 279, 1894, 315, 39235, 646, 13289, 4152, 311, 6543, 11, 3654, 6457, 4682, 11, 33525, 9363, 11, 323, 29910, 13, 151645], "pred": "In summary, the color of urine can vary due to blood, certain medical conditions, dietary factors, and medications.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8240583064693768, "g_worst_claim": -0.2420233658381871, "g_content": 1.333270286446187, "g_traj_mean": 0.8687210083007812}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [12206, 1894, 315, 39235, 374, 27539, 13753, 4152, 311, 279, 76578, 575, 299, 31902, 13, 151645], "pred": "Normal color of urine is pale yellow due to the pigment urochrome.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7885732014973958, "g_worst_claim": 1.7885732014973958, "g_content": 3.1152706146240234, "g_traj_mean": 1.6809446811676025}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 4622, 1894, 315, 39235, 374, 27539, 13753, 11, 323, 419, 1894, 374, 4152, 311, 279, 76578, 575, 299, 31902, 13, 151645], "pred": "The normal color of urine is pale yellow, and this color is due to the pigment urochrome.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8157844675911798, "g_worst_claim": 1.0874674320220947, "g_content": 2.371230867173937, "g_traj_mean": 1.6459964513778687}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 1894, 315, 39235, 374, 3545, 7481, 438, 27539, 13753, 11, 892, 374, 4152, 311, 279, 76578, 575, 299, 31902, 13, 4354, 11, 419, 1894, 646, 2297, 4152, 311, 5257, 9363, 11, 2670, 3654, 29910, 11, 15298, 11, 323, 4682, 1741, 438, 4154, 12700, 4204, 11, 458, 26990, 19267, 315, 2518, 6543, 7761, 13, 151645], "pred": "The color of urine is often described as pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, this color can change due to various factors, including certain medications, foods, and conditions such as porphyria, an inherited disorder of red blood cells.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.111695189187021, "g_worst_claim": 0.6282943378795277, "g_content": 1.476767578125, "g_traj_mean": 1.039313793182373}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 22.5, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "649", "question": "color of urin meaning", "gt": "The color of urine can indicate different health conditions. Red urine may indicate the presence of blood and could be a sign of an infection or cancer. Deep purple urine can be a characteristic of porphyria, a rare disorder. The normal color of urine is pale yellow due to the pigment urochrome.", "pred": "The color of urine can vary due to different factors. A normal urine color is pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, if there is blood in the urine, it can produce a dramatic color change, turning the urine red. This could be a sign of a serious condition like an infection or cancer, and a visit to a doctor or urologist is warranted. In contrast, deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare inherited disorder of red blood cells. Additionally, certain foods like beets, berries, and fava beans can change urine color, as can pigments and other compounds from medications.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "The color of urine can vary due to different factors. A normal urine color is pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, if there is blood in the urine, it can produce a dramatic color change, turning the urine red. This could be a sign of a serious condition like an infection or cancer, and a visit to a doctor or urologist is warranted. In contrast, deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare inherited disorder of red blood cells. Additionally, certain foods like beets, berries, and fava beans can change urine color, as can pigments and other compounds from medications.", "cot": "[\"The color of urine can vary based on several factors. A normal urine color is typically pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, the color can be affected by various conditions and factors such as:\\n\\n1. **Blood in the Urine**: If there is blood in the urine, it can produce a dramatic color change, often turning the urine red. This can be a sign of serious conditions like infections or cancer, and it is important to consult a doctor or urologist.\\n\\n2. **Porphyria**: Deep purple urine is a characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. This condition is caused by an abnormal accumulation of porphyrins in the body, which can lead to the production of purple urine.\\n\\n3. **Food and Medications**: Certain foods and medications can also change the color of urine. For example, beets, berries, and fava beans are among the foods most likely to affect urine color. Medications like rifampin, which is used to treat tuberculosis, can also cause urine to turn a reddish or orange color.\\n\\n4. **Kidney Diseases**: In cases of kidney diseases, the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production can malfunction, leading to changes in urine color. This can result in a darker or lighter urine color than normal.\\n\\nIn summary, the color of urine can vary due to blood, certain medical conditions, dietary factors, and medications.\", \"Answer: The color of urine can indicate various health conditions or factors influencing its appearance. Pale yellow is the normal color of urine, due to the pigment urochrome. A red or deep purple color can indicate more serious issues such as blood in the urine (red) or porphyria (deep purple), respectively. Pink, brown, or cloudy urine might suggest different medical conditions or dietary influences.\", \"The color of urine can vary due to different factors. A normal urine color is pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, if there is blood in the urine, it can produce a dramatic color change, turning the urine red. This could be a sign of a serious condition like an infection or cancer, and a visit to a doctor or urologist is warranted. In contrast, deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare inherited disorder of red blood cells. Additionally, certain foods like beets, berries, and fava beans can change urine color, as can pigments and other compounds from medications.\", \"The normal color of urine is pale yellow due to the pigment urochrome. This color can be altered in cases of kidney diseases when the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunctioning. Red urine can indicate the presence of blood in the urine, which may be a sign of a serious issue like an infection or cancer and requires a visit to a doctor or urologist. Deep purple urine is a characteristic of porphyria, a rare inherited disorder of red blood cells. The color of urine can also be affected by pigments and compounds from certain foods and medications, such as beets, berries, and fava beans.\"]", "time_sec": 25.257, "generation_time_seconds": 24.3618, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8909, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 1894, 315, 39235, 646, 13289, 3118, 389, 3807, 9363, 13, 362, 4622, 39235, 1894, 374, 11136, 27539, 13753, 11, 892, 374, 4152, 311, 279, 76578, 575, 299, 31902, 13, 4354, 11, 279, 1894, 646, 387, 11495, 553, 5257, 4682, 323, 9363, 1741, 438, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 51486, 304, 279, 16809, 482, 95518, 1416, 1052, 374, 6543, 304, 279, 39235, 11, 432, 646, 8193, 264, 21771, 1894, 2297, 11, 3545, 13054, 279, 39235, 2518, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 264, 1841, 315, 6001, 4682, 1075, 28920, 476, 9387, 11, 323, 432, 374, 2989, 311, 8498, 264, 10668, 476, 575, 299, 839, 380, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 28097, 12700, 4204, 95518, 18183, 24932, 39235, 374, 264, 28583, 315, 4154, 12700, 4204, 11, 264, 8848, 11, 26990, 19267, 315, 2518, 6543, 7761, 13, 1096, 2971, 374, 8881, 553, 458, 34563, 45735, 315, 4154, 759, 10920, 1330, 304, 279, 2487, 11, 892, 646, 2990, 311, 279, 5670, 315, 24932, 39235, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 26746, 323, 12566, 804, 95518, 34111, 15298, 323, 29910, 646, 1083, 2297, 279, 1894, 315, 39235, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 387, 1415, 11, 62394, 11, 323, 282, 2907, 26896, 525, 4221, 279, 15298, 1429, 4363, 311, 7802, 39235, 1894, 13, 12566, 804, 1075, 36924, 1121, 258, 11, 892, 374, 1483, 311, 4228, 87134, 11, 646, 1083, 5240, 39235, 311, 2484, 264, 62144, 812, 476, 18575, 1894, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 98508, 3437, 69574, 95518, 758, 5048, 315, 37942, 18808, 11, 279, 74938, 323, 42910, 312, 96410, 65081, 17628, 315, 39235, 5670, 646, 71187, 11, 6388, 311, 4344, 304, 39235, 1894, 13, 1096, 646, 1102, 304, 264, 39030, 476, 29573, 39235, 1894, 1091, 4622, 382, 641, 12126, 11, 279, 1894, 315, 39235, 646, 13289, 4152, 311, 6543, 11, 3654, 6457, 4682, 11, 33525, 9363, 11, 323, 29910, 13, 151645], "pred": "In summary, the color of urine can vary due to blood, certain medical conditions, dietary factors, and medications.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.8309844531961333, "g_worst_claim": -0.2100222451346261, "g_content": 1.3358213510086288, "g_traj_mean": 0.8705361485481262}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 576, 1894, 315, 39235, 646, 13216, 5257, 2820, 4682, 476, 9363, 65600, 1181, 11094, 13, 12349, 13753, 374, 279, 4622, 1894, 315, 39235, 11, 4152, 311, 279, 76578, 575, 299, 31902, 13, 362, 2518, 476, 5538, 24932, 1894, 646, 13216, 803, 6001, 4714, 1741, 438, 6543, 304, 279, 39235, 320, 1151, 8, 476, 4154, 12700, 4204, 320, 32880, 24932, 701, 15576, 13, 26119, 11, 13876, 11, 476, 73549, 39235, 2578, 4190, 2155, 6457, 4682, 476, 33525, 33353, 13, 151645], "pred": "The color of urine can indicate various health conditions or factors influencing its appearance. Pale yellow is the normal color of urine, due to the pigment urochrome. A red or deep purple color can indicate more serious issues such as blood in the urine (red) or porphyria (deep purple), respectively. Pink, brown, or cloudy urine might suggest different medical conditions or dietary influences.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.939286693738622, "g_worst_claim": 0.2182160218556722, "g_content": 1.4008046104794456, "g_traj_mean": 0.9127780199050903}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 1894, 315, 39235, 646, 13289, 4152, 311, 2155, 9363, 13, 362, 4622, 39235, 1894, 374, 27539, 13753, 11, 892, 374, 4152, 311, 279, 76578, 575, 299, 31902, 13, 4354, 11, 421, 1052, 374, 6543, 304, 279, 39235, 11, 432, 646, 8193, 264, 21771, 1894, 2297, 11, 13054, 279, 39235, 2518, 13, 1096, 1410, 387, 264, 1841, 315, 264, 6001, 2971, 1075, 458, 18873, 476, 9387, 11, 323, 264, 3947, 311, 264, 10668, 476, 575, 299, 839, 380, 374, 73180, 13, 758, 12872, 11, 5538, 24932, 39235, 374, 458, 24588, 28583, 315, 4154, 12700, 4204, 11, 264, 8848, 26990, 19267, 315, 2518, 6543, 7761, 13, 22406, 11, 3654, 15298, 1075, 387, 1415, 11, 62394, 11, 323, 282, 2907, 26896, 646, 2297, 39235, 1894, 11, 438, 646, 23694, 1368, 323, 1008, 31146, 504, 29910, 13, 151645], "pred": "The color of urine can vary due to different factors. A normal urine color is pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, if there is blood in the urine, it can produce a dramatic color change, turning the urine red. This could be a sign of a serious condition like an infection or cancer, and a visit to a doctor or urologist is warranted. In contrast, deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare inherited disorder of red blood cells. Additionally, certain foods like beets, berries, and fava beans can change urine color, as can pigments and other compounds from medications.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2714190104809862, "g_worst_claim": 0.5652035713195801, "g_content": 1.8758201599121094, "g_traj_mean": 1.285704493522644}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 4622, 1894, 315, 39235, 374, 27539, 13753, 4152, 311, 279, 76578, 575, 299, 31902, 13, 1096, 1894, 646, 387, 28752, 304, 5048, 315, 37942, 18808, 979, 279, 74938, 323, 42910, 312, 96410, 65081, 17628, 315, 39235, 5670, 525, 71187, 287, 13, 3731, 39235, 646, 13216, 279, 9362, 315, 6543, 304, 279, 39235, 11, 892, 1231, 387, 264, 1841, 315, 264, 6001, 4265, 1075, 458, 18873, 476, 9387, 323, 7460, 264, 3947, 311, 264, 10668, 476, 575, 299, 839, 380, 13, 18183, 24932, 39235, 374, 264, 28583, 315, 4154, 12700, 4204, 11, 264, 8848, 26990, 19267, 315, 2518, 6543, 7761, 13, 576, 1894, 315, 39235, 646, 1083, 387, 11495, 553, 23694, 1368, 323, 31146, 504, 3654, 15298, 323, 29910, 11, 1741, 438, 387, 1415, 11, 62394, 11, 323, 282, 2907, 26896, 13, 151645], "pred": "The normal color of urine is pale yellow due to the pigment urochrome. This color can be altered in cases of kidney diseases when the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production are malfunctioning. Red urine can indicate the presence of blood in the urine, which may be a sign of a serious issue like an infection or cancer and requires a visit to a doctor or urologist. Deep purple urine is a characteristic of porphyria, a rare inherited disorder of red blood cells. The color of urine can also be affected by pigments and compounds from certain foods and medications, such as beets, berries, and fava beans.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5891560117661232, "g_worst_claim": 0.7212882041931152, "g_content": 2.4320573650422643, "g_traj_mean": 1.6365445852279663}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.85, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.8, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "650", "question": "color of urin meaning", "gt": "Based on the given passages, we know that red urine can indicate blood in the urine and can potentially be a sign of something serious like an infection or cancer. On the other hand, deep purple urine is associated with porphyria, a rare genetic disorder. The normal color of urine is pale yellow due to the pigment urochrome, but its color may change due to various factors such as kidney diseases. Therefore, the color of urine can provide important information about one's health and should be monitored closely.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "[\"The color of urine can vary based on several factors. A normal urine color is typically pale yellow, which is due to the pigment urochrome. However, the color can be affected by various conditions and factors such as:\\n\\n1. **Blood in the Urine**: If there is blood in the urine, it can produce a dramatic color change, often turning the urine red. This can be a sign of serious conditions like infections or cancer, and it is important to consult a doctor or urologist.\\n\\n2. **Porphyria**: Deep purple urine is a characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. This condition is caused by an abnormal accumulation of porphyrins in the body, which can lead to the production of purple urine.\\n\\n3. **Food and Medications**: Certain foods and medications can also change the color of urine. For example, beets, berries, and fava beans are among the foods most likely to affect urine color. Medications like rifampin, which is used to treat tuberculosis, can also cause urine to turn a reddish or orange color.\\n\\n4. **Kidney Diseases**: In cases of kidney diseases, the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production can malfunction, leading to changes in urine color. This can result in a darker or lighter urine color than normal.\\n\\nIn summary, the color of urine can vary due to blood, certain medical conditions, dietary factors, and medications.\", \"Based on the provided passages, the color of urine can be affected by various factors, including health conditions and dietary choices. Normal urine color is typically pale yellow due to the pigment urochrome. However, certain conditions can alter this color, such as kidney diseases, which may change the filtration and selective re-absorption stages of urine production, leading to an altered color.\\n\\nAdditionally, the passage mentions that deep purple urine is an identifying characteristic of porphyria, a rare, inherited disorder of red blood cells. Foods such as beets, berries, and fava beans can also affect urine color due to pigments and other compounds found in these foods.\\n\\nMoreover, the passage discusses that seeing red urine can be a sign of blood in the urine and may indicate serious health issues like infections or cancer, suggesting that the color red is a warning sign of potential health problems.\\n\\nIn summary, urine color can vary based on health conditions and dietary factors, with normal urine being pale yellow due to urochrome. Red urine may signal blood in the urine, which could indicate a serious health issue, while deep purple urine is associated with porphyria, a rare genetic disorder.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"The color of urine can vary based on several factors. Normal urine is typically a pale yellow color due to the pigment urochrome. However, different colors can indicate various health conditions. For example, red or pink urine may indicate the presence of blood in the urine, which could be a sign of an infection or cancer. Deep purple urine is characteristic of porphyria, a rare inherited disorder of red blood cells. Also, certain foods and medications can change urine color, such as beets, berries, and fava beans making it appear red. It's important to note that a significant color change in urine should prompt a visit to a doctor or urologist.\"]", "time_sec": 27.236, "generation_time_seconds": 26.3606, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8701, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [785, 1894, 315, 39235, 646, 13289, 3118, 389, 3807, 9363, 13, 362, 4622, 39235, 1894, 374, 11136, 27539, 13753, 11, 892, 374, 4152, 311, 279, 76578, 575, 299, 31902, 13, 4354, 11, 279, 1894, 646, 387, 11495, 553, 5257, 4682, 323, 9363, 1741, 438, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 51486, 304, 279, 16809, 482, 95518, 1416, 1052, 374, 6543, 304, 279, 39235, 11, 432, 646, 8193, 264, 21771, 1894, 2297, 11, 3545, 13054, 279, 39235, 2518, 13, 1096, 646, 387, 264, 1841, 315, 6001, 4682, 1075, 28920, 476, 9387, 11, 323, 432, 374, 2989, 311, 8498, 264, 10668, 476, 575, 299, 839, 380, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 28097, 12700, 4204, 95518, 18183, 24932, 39235, 374, 264, 28583, 315, 4154, 12700, 4204, 11, 264, 8848, 11, 26990, 19267, 315, 2518, 6543, 7761, 13, 1096, 2971, 374, 8881, 553, 458, 34563, 45735, 315, 4154, 759, 10920, 1330, 304, 279, 2487, 11, 892, 646, 2990, 311, 279, 5670, 315, 24932, 39235, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 26746, 323, 12566, 804, 95518, 34111, 15298, 323, 29910, 646, 1083, 2297, 279, 1894, 315, 39235, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 387, 1415, 11, 62394, 11, 323, 282, 2907, 26896, 525, 4221, 279, 15298, 1429, 4363, 311, 7802, 39235, 1894, 13, 12566, 804, 1075, 36924, 1121, 258, 11, 892, 374, 1483, 311, 4228, 87134, 11, 646, 1083, 5240, 39235, 311, 2484, 264, 62144, 812, 476, 18575, 1894, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 98508, 3437, 69574, 95518, 758, 5048, 315, 37942, 18808, 11, 279, 74938, 323, 42910, 312, 96410, 65081, 17628, 315, 39235, 5670, 646, 71187, 11, 6388, 311, 4344, 304, 39235, 1894, 13, 1096, 646, 1102, 304, 264, 39030, 476, 29573, 39235, 1894, 1091, 4622, 382, 641, 12126, 11, 279, 1894, 315, 39235, 646, 13289, 4152, 311, 6543, 11, 3654, 6457, 4682, 11,