 624, 17, 13, 29279, 279, 3015, 304, 279, 17196, 374, 8205, 11, 537, 2238, 4017, 11, 323, 7949, 279, 6396, 311, 5648, 12503, 19049, 624, 18, 13, 44856, 697, 6869, 26364, 624, 19, 13, 20552, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 61932, 320, 9096, 279, 1379, 315, 264, 51249, 8, 311, 697, 32452, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 697, 6869, 13, 1752, 5021, 6869, 11, 3614, 1526, 432, 448, 697, 19225, 311, 5358, 259, 17248, 624, 20, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 61932, 700, 6587, 11, 1667, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 894, 9664, 259, 17248, 624, 21, 13, 20552, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 1616, 438, 279, 61932, 11, 10693, 432, 311, 7146, 389, 697, 6869, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 22, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 64324, 700, 448, 7010, 3015, 624, 23, 13, 30841, 697, 6869, 29273, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 11, 30426, 55935, 311, 5358, 5557, 624, 24, 13, 5443, 264, 6869, 46622, 311, 6587, 9058, 697, 6869, 11, 22573, 902, 31157, 374, 2115, 304, 279, 6869, 311, 5648, 82426, 432, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Choose the right shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Ensure the water in the shower is warm, not too hot, and reduce the flow to avoid splashing.\n3. Wet your hair thoroughly.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) to your palm and work it through your hair. For longer hair, comb through it with your fingers to prevent tangles.\n5. Rinse the shampoo out completely, using a wide-tooth comb to remove any remaining tangles.\n6. Apply conditioner in the same way as the shampoo, allowing it to remain on your hair for a few minutes.\n7. Rinse the conditioner out with cool water.\n8. Dry your hair gently with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing to prevent damage.\n9. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, ensuring no moisture is left in the hair to avoid weakening it.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0508719611652697, "g_worst_claim": -0.2764447033405304, "g_content": 1.2645328228290265, "g_traj_mean": 0.9749778509140015}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 7.92, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "655", "question": "how to properly clean your hair", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are the steps to properly clean your hair:\n\n1. Rinse your hair completely with warm water, then use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair (Passage 1, step 6).\n2. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type, and apply a nickel-sized amount of shampoo into the palm of your hand while in the shower (Passage 2, steps 1-3). Work the shampoo through your hair without piling it up on your head, and avoid tangling it while it's still wet.\n3. After applying shampoo, rinse your hair thoroughly with warm water, and then comb through it with your fingers to remove any remaining tangles (Passage 1, step 7).\n4. Apply a conditioner to your hair, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes before rinsing it out with cool water (Passage 1, step 8).\n5. To dry your hair, gently pat it with a towel or wrap it around your head to absorb excess water, avoiding rubbing it vigorously with a towel (Passage 3).\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide instructions on how to style or dry your hair after cleaning it.", "pred": "Follow the steps outlined above to properly clean your hair.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Follow the steps outlined above to properly clean your hair.", "cot": "[\"To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly to avoid splashing.\\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\\n10. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, wrapping a towel or patting it gently to soak the water from the hair.\", \"To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select the appropriate shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. Make sure the shower water is warm, not too hot, and adjust the flow to avoid splashing.\\n3. Thoroughly wet your hair and apply a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) to your hand, working it through your hair with your fingers to reduce tangles.\\n4. Rinse the hair completely.\\n5. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\\n6. Apply a conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n7. Rinse the hair with cool water.\\n8. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing it back and forth or in circles to prevent damage.\\n9. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair.\\n\\nAnswer: [Follow the steps outlined above to properly clean your hair.]\", \"To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Use the right shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. Make sure the water temperature is warm but not too hot, and turn the shower flow down a bit to avoid splashing.\\n3. Thoroughly wet your hair.\\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) to your palm and work it through your hair, combing with your fingers to reduce tangles if your hair is long.\\n5. Rinse the shampoo completely.\\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if your hair is longer.\\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n8. Rinse the hair thoroughly with cool water and comb through it again.\\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion rather than rubbing it back and forth or in circles, to avoid causing damage.\", \"To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select the appropriate shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. Ensure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and adjust the flow to avoid splashing.\\n3. Thoroughly wet your hair.\\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) and work it through your hair, combing through it to reduce tangles if your hair is longer.\\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\\n6. If your hair is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo and let it remain on for a few minutes.\\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water.\\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion rather than rubbing it back and forth or in circles with a towel.\\n10. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, ensuring you handle your hair with proper care to avoid damage.\"]", "time_sec": 32.861, "generation_time_seconds": 31.7982, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0534, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 10277, 4240, 697, 6869, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 279, 6169, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 624, 17, 13, 7405, 2704, 279, 3015, 304, 279, 17196, 374, 8205, 11, 714, 537, 2238, 4017, 11, 323, 2484, 279, 6396, 1495, 10078, 311, 5648, 12503, 19049, 624, 18, 13, 663, 14438, 398, 14401, 279, 6869, 624, 19, 13, 20552, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 61932, 320, 9096, 279, 1379, 315, 264, 51249, 8, 311, 279, 32452, 315, 697, 1424, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 279, 6869, 11, 3614, 287, 1526, 432, 448, 697, 19225, 311, 7949, 259, 17248, 624, 20, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 624, 21, 13, 5443, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 421, 279, 6869, 374, 5021, 624, 22, 13, 20552, 264, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 498, 9251, 279, 61932, 11, 10693, 432, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 323, 3614, 1526, 432, 1549, 624, 24, 13, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 11, 30426, 55935, 279, 6869, 1182, 323, 13241, 476, 304, 25362, 448, 264, 42613, 311, 5358, 5557, 624, 16, 15, 13, 5443, 264, 6869, 46622, 311, 6587, 9058, 697, 6869, 11, 41195, 264, 42613, 476, 3272, 1280, 432, 29273, 311, 60692, 279, 3015, 504, 279, 6869, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly to avoid splashing.\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\n10. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, wrapping a towel or patting it gently to soak the water from the hair.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5538018626574492, "g_worst_claim": 0.4574516216913859, "g_content": 1.8437012317133885, "g_traj_mean": 1.4067184925079346}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 10277, 4240, 697, 6869, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 279, 8311, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 624, 17, 13, 7405, 2704, 279