 11566, 438, 279, 61932, 11, 10693, 432, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 26364, 448, 7010, 3015, 323, 3614, 1526, 432, 1549, 624, 24, 13, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 4751, 1091, 55935, 432, 1182, 323, 13241, 476, 304, 25362, 11, 311, 5648, 14381, 5557, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Use the right shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Make sure the water temperature is warm but not too hot, and turn the shower flow down a bit to avoid splashing.\n3. Thoroughly wet your hair.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) to your palm and work it through your hair, combing with your fingers to reduce tangles if your hair is long.\n5. Rinse the shampoo completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if your hair is longer.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair thoroughly with cool water and comb through it again.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion rather than rubbing it back and forth or in circles, to avoid causing damage.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.324538211307598, "g_worst_claim": 0.238466477394104, "g_content": 1.534429657325316, "g_traj_mean": 1.2711889743804932}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 10277, 4240, 697, 6869, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 279, 8311, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 624, 17, 13, 29279, 279, 3015, 304, 279, 17196, 374, 8205, 11, 714, 537, 2238, 4017, 11, 323, 7500, 279, 6396, 311, 5648, 12503, 19049, 624, 18, 13, 663, 14438, 398, 14401, 697, 6869, 624, 19, 13, 20552, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 61932, 320, 9096, 264, 51249, 27835, 3311, 8, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 697, 6869, 11, 3614, 287, 1526, 432, 311, 7949, 259, 17248, 421, 697, 6869, 374, 5021, 624, 20, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 624, 21, 13, 1416, 697, 6869, 374, 5021, 11, 990, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 624, 22, 13, 20552, 264, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 498, 9251, 279, 61932, 323, 1077, 432, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 624, 24, 13, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 4751, 1091, 55935, 432, 1182, 323, 13241, 476, 304, 25362, 448, 264, 42613, 624, 16, 15, 13, 5443, 264, 6869, 46622, 311, 6587, 9058, 697, 6869, 11, 22573, 498, 3705, 697, 6869, 448, 6169, 2453, 311, 5648, 5557, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Select the appropriate shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Ensure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and adjust the flow to avoid splashing.\n3. Thoroughly wet your hair.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) and work it through your hair, combing through it to reduce tangles if your hair is longer.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. If your hair is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo and let it remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion rather than rubbing it back and forth or in circles with a towel.\n10. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, ensuring you handle your hair with proper care to avoid damage.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.524807382219012, "g_worst_claim": 0.4574516216913859, "g_content": 1.7524051063939146, "g_traj_mean": 1.3443430662155151}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 6.85, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "656", "question": "how to properly clean your hair", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to properly clean your hair:\n\n1. Rinse your hair completely with water.\n2. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\n3. Apply a conditioner and allow it to remain on for a few minutes.\n4. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n5. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles.\n\nAdditionally, it is recommended to use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair after washing, and to be gentle when handling wet hair to prevent damage.", "pred": "1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly to avoid splashing.\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\n10. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, wrapping a towel or patting it gently to soak the water from the hair.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly to avoid splashing.\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\n10. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, wrapping a towel or patting it gently to soak the water from the hair.", "cot": "[\"To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly to avoid splashing.\\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\\n10. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, wrapping a towel or patting it gently to soak the water from the hair.\", \"1) Make sure to select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2) While in the shower, make sure your water is warm, but not too hot. Turn the flow down just a bit so you're not splashing all over the place.\\n3) Thoroughly wet the hair.\\n4) Apply a bit of shampoo into the palm of your hand (a nickel sized amount is usually just about right) and work it through the hair. If your hair is longer, don't pile it up on your head, instead comb through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\\n5) Rinse the hair completely and, if the hair is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\\n6) Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo. Allow the conditioner to remain on for a few minutes.\\n7) Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\\n8) Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion. Never rub the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel as this will cause damage to the hair.\", \"1) First, make sure to use the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type. 2) While in the shower, ensure the water is warm but not too hot. Adjust the flow to be just a bit, so you're not splashing. 3) Thoroughly wet your hair. 4) Apply shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) and work it through your hair. 5) Rinse thoroughly. 6) After rinsing, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if it is longer. 7) Apply conditioner in the same way you applied the shampoo and let it remain on for a few minutes. 8) Rinse the hair again with cool water. 9) Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles. 10) After drying, use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, handling it with care to avoid damage.\", \"1) Start by ensuring you select the right shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2) Turn the shower water to a warm but not too hot temperature and adjust the flow to avoid splashing.\\n3) Thoroughly wet the hair by applying water directly onto it.\\n4) Apply a small amount of shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) and work it through your hair, combing with your fingers to reduce tangles.\\n5) Rinse the hair completely to remove all shampoo and conditioner.\\n6) Use a wide-tooth comb to remove any remaining tangles and smooth the hair.\\n7) Apply conditioner to the hair in the same manner as shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n8) Rinse the hair with cool water and comb it through again.\\n9) Dry the hair by gently patting it with a towel, avoiding rubbing it back and forth or in circles as this can cause damage.\\n10) Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, making sure to handle it gently to avoid damaging the wet hair.\"]", "time_sec": 33.078, "generation_time_seconds": 31.7272, "selection_time_seconds": 1.3367, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 10277, 4240, 697, 6869, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 279, 6169, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 624, 17, 13, 7405, 2704, 279, 3015, 304, 279, 17196, 374, 8205, 11, 714, 537, 2238, 4017, 11, 323, 2484, 279, 6396, 1495, 10078, 311, 5648, 12503, 19049, 624, 18, 13, 663, 14438, 398, 14401, 279, 6869, 624, 19, 13, 20552, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 61932, 320, 9096, 279, 1379, 315, 264, 51249, 8, 311, 279, 32452, 315, 697, 1424, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 279, 6869, 11, 3614, 287, 1526, 432, 448, 697, 19225, 311, 7949, 259, 17248, 624, 20, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 624, 21, 13, 5443, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 421, 279, 6869, 374, 5021, 624, 22, 13, 20552, 264, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 498, 9251, 279, 61932, 11, 10693, 432, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 323, 3614, 1526, 432, 1549, 624, 24, 13, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 11, 30426, 55935, 279, 6869, 1182, 323, 13241, 476, 304, 25362, 448, 264, 42613, 311, 5358, 5557, 624, 16, 15, 13, 5443, 264, 6869, 46622, 311, 6587, 9058, 697, 6869, 11, 41195, 264, 42613, 476, 3272, 1280, 432, 29273, 311, 60692, 279, 3015, 504, 279, 6869, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly to avoid splashing.\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\n10. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, wrapping a towel or patting it gently to soak the water from the hair.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5538018626574492, "g_worst_claim": 0.4574516216913859, "g_content": 1.8437012317133885, "g_traj_mean": 1.4067184925079346}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16, 8, 7405, 2704, 311, 3293, 279, 6169, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 624, 17, 8, 5976, 304, 279, 17196, 11, 1281, 2704, 697, 3015, 374, 8205, 11, 714, 537, 2238, 4017, 13, 11999, 279, 6396, 1495, 1101, 264, 2699, 773, 498, 2299, 537, 12503, 19049, 678, 916, 279, 1992, 624, 18, 8, 663, 14438, 398, 14401, 279, 6869, 624, 19, 8, 20552, 264, 2699, 315, 61932, 1119, 279, 32452, 315, 697, 1424, 320, 64, 51249, 29287, 3311, 374, 5990, 1101, 911, 1290, 8, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 279, 6869, 13, 1416, 697, 6869, 374, 5021, 11, 1513, 944, 26306, 432, 705, 389, 697, 1968, 11, 4518, 3614, 1526, 432, 448, 697, 19225, 311, 7949, 259, 17248, 624, 20, 8, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 323, 11, 421, 279, 6869, 374, 5021, 11, 990, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 624, 21, 8, 20552, 264, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 498, 9251, 279, 61932, 13, 26530, 279, 64324, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 22, 8, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 323, 3614, 1526, 432, 1549, 624, 23, 8, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 13, 14695, 10273, 279, 6869, 1182, 323, 13241, 476, 304, 25362, 448, 264, 42613, 438, 419, 686, 5240, 5557, 311, 279, 6869, 13, 151645], "pred": "1) Make sure to select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2) While in the shower, make sure your water is warm, but not too hot. Turn the flow down just a bit so you're not splashing all over the place.\n3) Thoroughly wet the hair.\n4) Apply a bit of shampoo into the palm of your hand (a nickel sized amount is usually just about right) and work it through the hair. If your hair is longer, don't pile it up on your head, instead comb through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n5) Rinse the hair completely and, if the hair is longer, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\n6) Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo. Allow the conditioner to remain on for a few minutes.\n7) Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n8) Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion. Never rub the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel as this will cause damage to the hair.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6638440159034278, "g_worst_claim": 0.7412691116333008, "g_content": 2.0392879363029235, "g_traj_mean": 1.6476688385009766}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16, 8, 5512, 11, 1281, 2704, 311, 990, 279, 6169, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 13, 220, 17, 8, 5976, 304, 279, 17196, 11, 5978, 279, 3015, 374, 8205, 714, 537, 2238, 4017, 13, 27196, 279, 6396, 311, 387, 1101, 264, 2699, 11, 773, 498, 2299, 537, 12503, 19049, 13, 220, 18, 8, 663, 14438, 398, 14401, 697, 6869, 13, 220, 19, 8, 20552, 61932, 320, 9096, 264, 51249, 27835, 3311, 8, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 697, 6869, 13, 220, 20, 8, 57368, 325, 26364, 13, 220, 21, 8, 4636, 96039, 287, 11, 990, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 421, 432, 374, 5021, 13, 220, 22, 8, 20552, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 1616, 498, 9251, 279, 61932, 323, 1077, 432, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 13, 220, 23, 8, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 1549, 448, 7010, 3015, 13, 220, 24, 8, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 11, 30426, 55935, 279, 6869, 1182, 323, 13241, 476, 304, 25362, 13, 220, 16, 15, 8, 4636, 45379, 11, 990, 264, 6869, 46622, 311, 6587, 9058, 697, 6869, 11, 11589, 432, 448, 2453, 311, 5648, 5557, 13, 151645], "pred": "1) First, make sure to use the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type. 2) While in the shower, ensure the water is warm but not too hot. Adjust the flow to be just a bit, so you're not splashing. 3) Thoroughly wet your hair. 4) Apply shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) and work it through your hair. 5) Rinse thoroughly. 6) After rinsing, use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if it is longer. 7) Apply conditioner in the same way you applied the shampoo and let it remain on for a few minutes. 8) Rinse the hair again with cool water. 9) Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles. 10) After drying, use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, handling it with care to avoid damage.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2158729070535756, "g_worst_claim": -0.26921045780181885, "g_content": 1.5679682114545037, "g_traj_mean": 1.1348800659179688}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16, 8, 5145, 553, 22573, 498, 3293, 279, 1290, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 624, 17, 8, 11999, 279, 17196, 3015, 311, 264, 8205, 714, 537, 2238, 4017, 9315, 323, 7500, 279, 6396, 311, 5648, 12503, 19049, 624, 18, 8, 663, 14438, 398, 14401, 279, 6869, 553, 18950, 3015, 5961, 8630, 432, 624, 19, 8, 20552, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 61932, 320, 9096, 264, 51249, 27835, 3311, 8, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 697, 6869, 11, 3614, 287, 448, 697, 19225, 311, 7949, 259, 17248, 624, 20, 8, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 311, 4057, 678, 61932, 323, 64324, 624, 21, 8, 5443, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 894, 9664, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 624, 22, 8, 20552, 64324, 311, 279, 6869, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 438, 61932, 11, 10693, 432, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 23, 8, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 323, 3614, 432, 1526, 1549, 624, 24, 8, 30841, 279, 6869, 553, 29273, 3272, 1280, 432, 448, 264, 42613, 11, 30426, 55935, 432, 1182, 323, 13241, 476, 304, 25362, 438, 419, 646, 5240, 5557, 624, 16, 15, 8, 5443, 264, 6869, 46622, 311, 6587, 9058, 697, 6869, 11, 3259, 2704, 311, 3705, 432, 29273, 311, 5648, 33346, 279, 14401, 6869, 13, 151645], "pred": "1) Start by ensuring you select the right shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2) Turn the shower water to a warm but not too hot temperature and adjust the flow to avoid splashing.\n3) Thoroughly wet the hair by applying water directly onto it.\n4) Apply a small amount of shampoo (about a nickel-sized amount) and work it through your hair, combing with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n5) Rinse the hair completely to remove all shampoo and conditioner.\n6) Use a wide-tooth comb to remove any remaining tangles and smooth the hair.\n7) Apply conditioner to the hair in the same manner as shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8) Rinse the hair with cool water and comb it through again.\n9) Dry the hair by gently patting it with a towel, avoiding rubbing it back and forth or in circles as this can cause damage.\n10) Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, making sure to handle it gently to avoid damaging the wet hair.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1995187037497306, "g_worst_claim": 0.1640428134373256, "g_content": 1.6091962101483586, "g_traj_mean": 1.1335961818695068}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.0, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "657", "question": "how to properly clean your hair", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to properly clean your hair:\n\n1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Wet your hair thoroughly.\n3. Apply a nickel-sized amount of shampoo into the palm of your hand and work it through your hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles if your hair is longer.\n4. Rinse the hair completely and use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair.\n5. Apply conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo and allow it to remain on for a few minutes.\n6. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n7. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing it back and forth or in circles.\n8. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair.\n\nTherefore, the steps to properly clean your hair are:\n\n1. Choose the right products.\n2. Wet your hair.\n3. Shampoo your hair.\n4. Rinse and detangle.\n5. Condition your hair.\n6. Rinse and comb.\n7. Dry your hair with a towel.\n8. Use a hair dryer.", "pred": "1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly to avoid splashing.\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\n10. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, wrapping a towel or patting it gently to soak the water from the hair.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly to avoid splashing.\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\n10. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, wrapping a towel or patting it gently to soak the water from the hair.", "cot": "[\"To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly to avoid splashing.\\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\\n10. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, wrapping a towel or patting it gently to soak the water from the hair.\", \"To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Select the appropriate shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm but not too hot and adjust the flow to avoid splashing.\\n3. Thoroughly wet your hair.\\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) to your hand and work it through your hair.\\n5. If your hair is longer, comb through it with your fingers instead of piling it on your head to reduce tangles.\\n6. Allow the shampoo to remain on your hair for a few minutes.\\n7. Rinse the shampoo thoroughly.\\n8. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo and let it sit for a few minutes.\\n9. Rinse the conditioner thoroughly.\\n10. Use a towel to blot the water from your hair, avoiding rubbing with the towel.\\n11. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, using a patting or stroking motion rather than rubbing with a towel.\\n12. If needed, use a wide-tooth comb to remove any remaining tangles and smooth the hair before drying.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can ensure that your hair is properly cleansed and cared for.\", \"To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n1. Select the appropriate shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm but not too hot, and adjust the flow to prevent splashing.\\n3. Thoroughly wet your hair.\\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) to your hand and work it through your hair, combing through longer hair to reduce tangles.\\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if your hair is longer.\\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion. Avoid rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\\n10. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, taking care not to rub the hair with the dryer.\", \"To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Select the Right Products**: Choose a shampoo and conditioner suitable for your hair type. This ensures that your hair is cleaned effectively without causing harm.\\n\\n2. **Warm Water Preparation**: Make sure the water in the shower is warm but not too hot. Adjust the water flow to minimize splashing and ensure a gentle cleaning process.\\n\\n3. **Wetting the Hair**: Thoroughly wet your hair to prepare it for the shampoo.\\n\\n4. **Apply Shampoo**: Take a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) in your hand and work it through your hair. For longer hair, comb it through with your fingers to prevent tangles.\\n\\n5. **Rinse Thoroughly**: Rinse the shampoo completely from your hair. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove any tangles and smooth the hair.\\n\\n6. **Conditioning**: Apply conditioner in the same manner as the shampoo. Let it remain on for a few minutes for better absorption.\\n\\n7. **Rinse Conditioner**: Rinse the conditioner out thoroughly.\\n\\n8. **Dry Hair**: Dry your hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion (not rubbing). Use a hair dryer to finish drying your hair. Avoid rubbing with a towel as it can damage your hair.\\n\\n9. **Post-Care**: Ensure you handle your hair with care after drying to maintain its health and beauty.\"]", "time_sec": 38.15, "generation_time_seconds": 37.1114, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0306, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 10277, 4240, 697, 6869, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 279, 6169, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 624, 17, 13, 7405, 2704, 279, 3015, 304, 279, 17196, 374, 8205, 11, 714, 537, 2238, 4017, 11, 323, 2484, 279, 6396, 1495, 10078, 311, 5648, 12503, 19049, 624, 18, 13, 663, 14438, 398, 14401, 279, 6869, 624, 19, 13, 20552, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 61932, 320, 9096, 279, 1379, 315, 264, 51249, 8, 311, 279, 32452, 315, 697, 1424, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 279, 6869, 11, 3614, 287, 1526, 432, 448, 697, 19225, 311, 7949, 259, 17248, 624, 20, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 624, 21, 13, 5443, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 421, 279, 6869, 374, 5021, 624, 22, 13, 20552, 264, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 498, 9251, 279, 61932, 11, 10693, 432, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 323, 3614, 1526, 432, 1549, 624, 24, 13, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 11, 30426, 55935, 279, 6869, 1182, 323, 13241, 476, 304, 25362, 448, 264, 42613, 311, 5358, 5557, 624, 16, 15, 13, 5443, 264, 6869, 46622, 311, 6587, 9058, 697, 6869, 11, 41195, 264, 42613, 476, 3272, 1280, 432, 29273, 311, 60692, 279, 3015, 504, 279, 6869, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Select the proper shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm, but not too hot, and turn the flow down slightly to avoid splashing.\n3. Thoroughly wet the hair.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) to the palm of your hand and work it through the hair, combing through it with your fingers to reduce tangles.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if the hair is longer.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion, avoiding rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\n10. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, wrapping a towel or patting it gently to soak the water from the hair.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.544227764813831, "g_worst_claim": 0.4793189525604248, "g_content": 1.83858819101371, "g_traj_mean": 1.398268699645996}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 10277, 4240, 697, 6869, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 8427, 279, 8311, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 624, 17, 13, 7405, 2704, 279, 3015, 304, 279, 17196, 374, 8205, 714, 537, 2238, 4017, 323, 7500, 279, 6396, 311, 5648, 12503, 19049, 624, 18, 13, 663, 14438, 398, 14401, 697, 6869, 624, 19, 13, 20552, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 61932, 320, 9096, 279, 1379, 315, 264, 51249, 8, 311, 697, 1424, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 697, 6869, 624, 20, 13, 1416, 697, 6869, 374, 5021, 11, 3614, 1526, 432, 448, 697, 19225, 4518, 315, 281, 7979, 432, 389, 697, 1968, 311, 7949, 259, 17248, 624, 21, 13, 26530, 279, 61932, 311, 7146, 389, 697, 6869, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 22, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 61932, 26364, 624, 23, 13, 20552, 264, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 498, 9251, 279, 61932, 323, 1077, 432, 2444, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 24, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 64324, 26364, 624, 16, 15, 13, 5443, 264, 42613, 311, 80882, 279, 3015, 504, 697, 6869, 11, 30426, 55935, 448, 279, 42613, 624, 16, 16, 13, 5443, 264, 6869, 46622, 311, 6587, 9058, 697, 6869, 11, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 4751, 1091, 55935, 448, 264, 42613, 624, 16, 17, 13, 1416, 4362, 11, 990, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 894, 9664, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 1573, 45379, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 5978, 429, 697, 6869, 374, 10277, 34194, 291, 323, 41677, 369, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can ensure that your hair is properly cleansed and cared for.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9760574109512985, "g_worst_claim": 0.08531512532915388, "g_content": 1.174555691805753, "g_traj_mean": 0.8829246163368225}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 10277, 4240, 697, 6869, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 8427, 279, 8311, 61932, 323, 64324, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 624, 17, 13, 7405, 2704, 279, 3015, 304, 279, 17196, 374, 8205, 714, 537, 2238, 4017, 11, 323, 7500, 279, 6396, 311, 5358, 12503, 19049, 624, 18, 13, 663, 14438, 398, 14401, 697, 6869, 624, 19, 13, 20552, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 61932, 320, 9096, 279, 1379, 315, 264, 51249, 8, 311, 697, 1424, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 697, 6869, 11, 3614, 287, 1526, 5021, 6869, 311, 7949, 259, 17248, 624, 20, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 6587, 624, 21, 13, 5443, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 421, 697, 6869, 374, 5021, 624, 22, 13, 20552, 264, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 498, 9251, 279, 61932, 11, 10693, 432, 311, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 624, 23, 13, 57368, 325, 279, 6869, 448, 7010, 3015, 323, 3614, 1526, 432, 1549, 624, 24, 13, 30841, 279, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 13, 34006, 55935, 279, 6869, 1182, 323, 13241, 476, 304, 25362, 448, 264, 42613, 311, 5358, 5557, 624, 16, 15, 13, 5443, 264, 6869, 46622, 311, 6587, 9058, 697, 6869, 11, 4633, 2453, 537, 311, 10273, 279, 6869, 448, 279, 46622, 13, 151645], "pred": "To properly clean your hair, follow these steps:\n1. Select the appropriate shampoo and conditioner for your hair type.\n2. Make sure the water in the shower is warm but not too hot, and adjust the flow to prevent splashing.\n3. Thoroughly wet your hair.\n4. Apply a small amount of shampoo (about the size of a nickel) to your hand and work it through your hair, combing through longer hair to reduce tangles.\n5. Rinse the hair completely.\n6. Use a wide-tooth comb to remove tangles and smooth the hair if your hair is longer.\n7. Apply a conditioner in the same manner you applied the shampoo, allowing it to remain on for a few minutes.\n8. Rinse the hair with cool water and comb through it again.\n9. Dry the hair with a towel using a patting or stroking motion. Avoid rubbing the hair back and forth or in circles with a towel to prevent damage.\n10. Use a hair dryer to completely dry your hair, taking care not to rub the hair with the dryer.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5678836173350934, "g_worst_claim": 0.5769498745600382, "g_content": 1.7414871369949494, "g_traj_mean": 1.317592978477478}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 10277, 4240, 697, 6869, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 3379, 279, 10083, 15530, 95518, 22201, 264, 61932, 323, 64324, 14452, 369, 697, 6869, 943, 13, 1096, 25351, 429, 697, 6869, 374, 27722, 13444, 2041, 14381, 11428, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 95275, 9959, 73335, 95518, 7405, 2704, 279, 3015, 304, 279, 17196, 374, 8205, 714, 537, 2238, 4017, 13, 27196, 279, 3015, 6396, 311, 29337, 12503, 19049, 323, 5978, 264, 21700, 15826, 1882, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 54, 295, 1280, 279, 25697, 95518, 663, 14438, 398, 14401, 697, 6869, 311, 10549, 432, 369, 279, 61932, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 28497, 1417, 47595, 95518, 11778, 264, 2613, 3311, 315, 61932, 320, 9096, 279, 1379, 315, 264, 51249, 8, 304, 697, 1424, 323, 975, 432, 1526, 697, 6869, 13, 1752, 5021, 6869, 11, 3614, 432, 1526, 448, 697, 19225, 311, 5358, 259, 17248, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 49, 258, 325, 663, 14438, 398, 95518, 57368, 325, 279, 61932, 6587, 504, 697, 6869, 13, 5443, 264, 6884, 4686, 8767, 3614, 311, 4057, 894, 259, 17248, 323, 10876, 279, 6869, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 10547, 287, 95518, 20552, 64324, 304, 279, 1852, 11566, 438, 279, 61932, 13, 6771, 432, 7146, 389, 369, 264, 2421, 4420, 369, 2664, 43125, 382, 22, 13, 3070, 49, 258, 325, 15180, 261, 95518, 57368, 325, 279, 64324, 700, 26364, 382, 23, 13, 3070, 85215, 25697, 95518, 30841, 697, 6869, 448, 264, 42613, 1667, 264, 3272, 1280, 476, 30411, 10566, 11379, 320, 1921, 55935, 568, 5443, 264, 6869, 46622, 311, 6248, 45379, 697, 6869, 13, 34006, 55935, 448, 264, 42613, 438, 432, 646, 5557, 697, 6869, 382, 24, 13, 3070, 4133, 7658, 546, 95518, 29279, 498, 3705, 697, 6869, 448, 2453, 1283, 45379, 311, 10306, 1181, 2820, 323, 13143, 13, 151645], "pred": "9. **Post-Care**: Ensure you handle your hair with care after drying to maintain its health and beauty.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9835390437969189, "g_worst_claim": 0.04821075384433453, "g_content": 1.1659645257994187, "g_traj_mean": 0.8427766561508179}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 65.83, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "659", "question": "vinegar uses for dogs", "gt": "Vinegar can be used to improve a dog's skin and coat, clean out their ears, repel fleas, and soothe itchy ears.", "pred": "These uses are derived directly from the provided passages and do not require external knowledge.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "These uses are derived directly from the provided passages and do not require external knowledge.", "cot": "[\"Based on the provided passages, vinegar can be used for dogs in several ways:\\n\\n1. **Improving Skin and Coat Health**: Vinegar can be used as a rinse to improve the skin and coat health of dogs. For example, a mixture of 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water can be used as a final rinse to rejuvenate the coat and help balance the dog's skin pH levels.\\n\\n2. **Repelling Fleas**: Vinegar can be sprayed on the dog's coat to repel fleas. This is mentioned in the second passage as a method to fight fleas.\\n\\n3. **Soothing Itchy Ears**: Vinegar can be used to soothe itchy ears in dogs. The third passage suggests diluting apple cider vinegar with 50 percent water and using a cotton swab or gauze pad soaked in this solution to address itchy ears. If the itchy ears persist, it may indicate an allergic reaction to something in the dog's diet.\\n\\nThese uses are supported by the information provided in the passages and do not require external knowledge.\", \"Based on the provided passages, vinegar can be used for dogs in several ways:\\n\\n1. To improve the dog's skin and coat health. According to passage 1, mixing 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water can be used as a final rinse to rejuvenate the dog's coat and balance its skin pH levels. This method is mentioned to be a personal favorite for achieving a shiny, healthy coat.\\n\\n2. To repel fleas from the dog's coat. As stated in passage 2, spraying apple cider vinegar (ACV) on the dog's coat is an effective way to repel fleas.\\n\\n3. To soothe itchy ears. Passage 3 mentions that diluting apple cider vinegar with 50% water can provide a solution for itchy ears in dogs. It suggests using a cotton swab or gauze pad soaked in this diluted vinegar to treat the itchy ears. If the itchy ears persist, it might indicate a dietary allergy.\\n\\n4. To clean out the dog's ears. Although not explicitly stated in the passages, it is a common practice to use apple cider vinegar as an ear cleaning solution for dogs.\\n  \\n5. To bathe in an ACV-soap mixture to fight fleas. According to passage 2, bathing the dog in a mixture of ACV and soap can be an effective way to deal with fleas.\\n\\n6. To normalize the pH balance of the dog's skin. Passage 1 suggests using vinegar as a full-strength spray to normalize the pH balance of the dog's skin.\\n\\nThese uses are derived directly from the provided passages and do not require external knowledge.\", \"vinegar uses for dogs include:\\n\\n1. Improving the dog's skin and coat: Mix 1 cup of vinegar with 2-4 cups of water and use as a final rinse to rejuvenate the coat and help balance your dog’s skin pH levels.\\n\\n2. Cleaning out the dog's ears: Diluting apple cider vinegar with 50 percent water provides a solution for itchy ears. Just use a cotton swab or gauze pad soaked in the diluted vinegar.\\n\\n3. Repelling fleas: Spray your dog's coat with vinegar to repel fleas.\\n\\n4. Fighting fleas: Bathe your dog in an ACV-soap mixture to fight fleas.\\n\\n5. Soothing itchy skin: Using vinegar can soothe itchy skin and coat.\\n\\nAnswer: vinegar uses for dogs include improving skin and coat, cleaning ears, repelling fleas, fighting fleas, and soothing itchy skin\", \"Vinegar is used for dogs for several purposes based on the provided passages. First, it is used to improve a dog's skin and coat by mixing it with water and using it as a final rinse. Vinegar can also be used to normalize the pH balance of a dog's skin when sprayed full-strength on the coat. Additionally, vinegar can be used to soothe itchy ears by diluting it with water and applying it to the ears with a cotton swab or gauze pad.\"]", "time_sec": 33.039, "generation_time_seconds": 32.0865, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9449, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 46105, 646, 387, 1483, 369, 12590, 304, 3807, 5510, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 47842, 4405, 26951, 323, 67767, 6267, 95518, 49695, 12164, 646, 387, 1483, 438, 264, 73241, 311, 7269, 279, 6787, 323, 22875, 2820, 315, 12590, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 264, 20980, 315, 220, 16, 10525, 315, 46105, 448, 220, 17, 12, 19, 25374, 315, 3015, 646, 387, 1483, 438, 264, 1590, 73241, 311, 72384, 349, 279, 22875, 323, 1492, 8172, 279, 5562, 594, 6787, 36043, 5866, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 18327, 6293, 46690, 300, 95518, 49695, 12164, 646, 387, 77621, 389, 279, 5562, 594, 22875, 311, 2064, 301, 12962, 300, 13, 1096, 374, 9733, 304, 279, 2086, 21085, 438, 264, 1714, 311, 4367, 12962, 300, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 50, 38413, 1084, 57964, 468, 1561, 95518, 49695, 12164, 646, 387, 1483, 311, 43176, 1782, 432, 57964, 24230, 304, 12590, 13, 576, 4843, 21085, 13230, 18840, 10607, 23268, 65055, 46105, 448, 220, 20, 15, 3266, 3015, 323, 1667, 264, 23522, 2021, 370, 476, 342, 2863, 2986, 11016, 68875, 304, 419, 6291, 311, 2621, 432, 57964, 24230, 13, 1416, 279, 432, 57964, 24230, 22334, 11, 432, 1231, 13216, 458, 56496, 12720, 311, 2494, 304, 279, 5562, 594, 9968, 382, 9485, 5711, 525, 7248, 553, 279, 1995, 3897, 304, 279, 46769, 323, 653, 537, 1373, 9250, 6540, 13, 151645], "pred": "These uses are supported by the information provided in the passages and do not require external knowledge.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0688936237413844, "g_worst_claim": 0.289536714553833, "g_content": 1.516325867291793, "g_traj_mean": 1.03109872341156}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 46105, 646, 387, 1