, 9255, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 369, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 624, 20, 13, 9646, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 498, 646, 2987, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 624, 2679, 498, 1366, 311, 1281, 264, 2155, 17172, 11, 498, 646, 1191, 448, 264, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 323, 7500, 279, 11116, 27079, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make ice cream, you need to start with a base such as a vanilla ice cream base. For a cream-based ice cream, you can follow these steps:\n1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved.\n2. Heat the mix just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and chill it thoroughly for at least 2 hours.\n4. Pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\n5. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can either serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\nIf you want to make a different flavor, you can start with a vanilla ice cream base and adjust the recipe accordingly.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4468664357844951, "g_worst_claim": 0.7413173403058734, "g_content": 1.6394211789394946, "g_traj_mean": 1.1707216501235962}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 64192, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 1119, 264, 19187, 848, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 279, 13163, 702, 55667, 624, 17, 13, 26070, 279, 20980, 1101, 3080, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 624, 18, 13, 23200, 279, 4017, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 3460, 28990, 10525, 624, 19, 13, 64192, 304, 32065, 8649, 323, 36301, 279, 20980, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 624, 20, 13, 25968, 279, 83942, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 624, 21, 13, 11999, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 24232, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 369, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 624, 22, 13, 3197, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 498, 646, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved.\n2. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\n3. Transfer the hot cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup.\n4. Stir in vanilla extract and chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\n5. Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker.\n6. Turn on the ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\n7. When the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4335473803515826, "g_worst_claim": 0.18539289236068726, "g_content": 1.558207612879136, "g_traj_mean": 1.1876848936080933}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 1191, 553, 26792, 697, 2331, 11, 892, 646, 387, 264, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 13, 5005, 15963, 13966, 1075, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 304, 264, 19187, 848, 916, 3347, 8628, 11, 53954, 3080, 279, 13163, 13772, 18186, 13, 26070, 279, 20980, 1101, 3080, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 13, 23200, 279, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 323, 36301, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 369, 220, 17, 4115, 13, 64192, 304, 32065, 8649, 11, 1221, 4914, 279, 83942, 12644, 20980, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 369, 911, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 13, 9646, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 1573, 13480, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make ice cream, start by mixing your base, which can be a vanilla ice cream base. Then combine ingredients like sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat, stirring until the sugar dissolves. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and chill thoroughly, at least for 2 hours. Stir in vanilla extract, then pour the chilled cream mixture into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for about 20 to 25 minutes. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours before serving.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2228729895736736, "g_worst_claim": 0.30289026896158855, "g_content": 1.555971494862731, "g_traj_mean": 1.1109323501586914}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 1, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 77.16, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "696", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "To make ice cream, stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar dissolves. Heat the mixture until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Then, pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for about 20 to 25 minutes. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and put it in the freezer for 2 to 3 hours to ripen.", "pred": "Once the mix is chilled, pour it into an ice cream maker and turn it on according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Once the mix is chilled, pour it into an ice cream maker and turn it on according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "cot": "[\"To make ice cream, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Base**: Start by mixing your base. A good vanilla ice cream base is recommended. You can make a variety of flavors by starting with this base. Cream-based ice cream is icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream.\\n\\n2. **Chill the Mix**: Chill the mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours. This step is crucial for ensuring the ice cream sets properly.\\n\\n3. **Churn the Ice Cream**: Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker. Turn on the machine and churn according to the manufacturer's directions. This process typically takes 20 to 25 minutes.\\n\\n4. **Serve or Ripen**: Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can create a delicious batch of ice cream.\", \"To make ice cream, follow these steps according to the provided passages:\\n\\n1. Begin by making the ice cream base. A good vanilla ice cream base is recommended. If you want a cream-based ice cream, it will be a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream.\\n\\n2. For a cream-based vanilla ice cream, combine sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan. Stir until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture over low heat until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\\n\\n3. Transfer the heated cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup. Chill the mixture thoroughly in the refrigerator for at least two hours.\\n\\n4. Once the mixture is chilled, pour it into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's directions. Typically, this process takes about 20 to 25 minutes.\\n\\n5. When the ice cream is softly frozen, it's ready to serve. You can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can create a delicious ice cream base from which you can develop various flavors.\", \"To make ice cream, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved. \\n2. Heat just until mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\\n3. Transfer cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup.\\n4. Stir in vanilla extract and chill mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\\n\\nOnce the mix is chilled, pour it into an ice cream maker and turn it on according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\", \"To make ice cream, follow these steps based on the provided passages:\\n\\n1. **Preparation of Base:**\\n   - **Step 1:** Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker.\\n   - **Step 2:** Turn on the ice cream maker according to the manufacturer's directions and churn the ice cream mix for 20 to 25 minutes.\\n\\n2. **Ripening (Optional):**\\n   - **Step 3:** When the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately. Alternatively, cover the ice cream with a piece of plastic wrap and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours before serving.\\n\\n3. **Alternative Base Preparation (Optional):**\\n   - **Step 4:** If making a different flavor, start with a good vanilla ice cream base. You can make various flavors by using this base as a starting point.\\n   - **Step 5:** Cream-based ice cream will be icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream.\\n\\nThese steps provide a basic guide for making ice cream. The choice of the base and additional ingredients can vary based on personal preference.\"]", "time_sec": 31.814, "generation_time_seconds": 30.8729, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9329, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 5351, 95518, 5145, 553, 26792, 697, 2331, 13, 362, 1661, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 374, 11102, 13, 1446, 646, 1281, 264, 8045, 315, 31423, 553, 5916, 448, 419, 2331, 13, 29700, 5980, 9853, 12644, 374, 17902, 1268, 323, 29573, 1091, 16564, 567, 5980, 9853, 12644, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 1143, 483, 279, 19219, 95518, 86489, 279, 6514, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 13, 1096, 3019, 374, 16587, 369, 22573, 279, 9853, 12644, 7289, 10277, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 1143, 399, 279, 19939, 29700, 95518, 25968, 279, 83942, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 13, 11999, 389, 279, 5662, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 13, 1096, 1882, 11136, 4990, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 60421, 476, 35437, 268, 95518, 9646, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 498, 646, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 1855, 264, 17923, 7162, 315, 9853, 12644, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can create a delicious batch of ice cream.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.183370311816737, "g_worst_claim": 0.21585159301757811, "g_content": 1.5732813363123421, "g_traj_mean": 1.1313403844833374}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 4092, 311, 279, 3897, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 18597, 553, 3259, 279, 9853, 12644, 2331, 13, 362, 1661, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 374, 11102, 13, 1416, 498, 1366, 264, 12644, 5980, 9853, 12644, 11, 432, 686, 387, 264, 2699, 17902, 1268, 323, 29573, 1091, 16564, 567, 5980, 9853, 12644, 382, 17, 13, 1752, 264, 12644, 5980, 32065, 9853, 12644, 11, 15963, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 304, 264, 19187, 848, 13, 64192, 3080, 279, 13163, 702, 55667, 13, 26070, 279, 20980, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 432, 374, 4017, 323, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 382, 18, 13, 23200, 279, 31713, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 3460, 28990, 10525, 13, 86489, 279, 20980, 26364, 304, 279, 44944, 369, 518, 3245, 1378, 4115, 382, 19, 13, 9646, 279, 20980, 374, 83942, 11, 4914, 432, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 13, 45302, 11, 419, 1882, 4990, 911, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 382, 20, 13, 3197, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 432, 594, 5527, 311, 8683, 13, 1446, 646, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 1855, 264, 17923, 9853, 12644, 2331, 504, 892, 498, 646, 2225, 5257, 31423, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can create a delicious ice cream base from which you can develop various flavors.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.0418623832475322, "g_worst_claim": 0.21535497903823853, "g_content": 1.3967428916741993, "g_traj_mean": 1.0446757078170776}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 64192, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 1119, 264, 19187, 848, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 13163, 702, 55667, 13, 715, 17, 13, 26070, 1101, 3080, 6514, 374, 4017, 323, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 624, 18, 13, 23200, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 1741, 438, 264, 3460, 28990, 10525, 624, 19, 13, 64192, 304, 32065, 8649, 323, 36301, 6514, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 382, 12522, 279, 6514, 374, 83942, 11, 4914, 432, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 323, 2484, 432, 389, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 369, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 13, 3197, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 13, 151645], "pred": "Once the mix is chilled, pour it into an ice cream maker and turn it on according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6096733397802554, "g_worst_claim": 0.4760265350341797, "g_content": 1.8565826416015625, "g_traj_mean": 1.4444206953048706}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 3118, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 4703, 35135, 315, 5351, 25, 1019, 256, 481, 3070, 8304, 220, 16, 66963, 25968, 9255, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 624, 256, 481, 3070, 8304, 220, 17, 66963, 11999, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 24232, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 323, 80869, 279, 9853, 12644, 6514, 369, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 49, 573, 6019, 320, 15309, 1648, 1019, 256, 481, 3070, 8304, 220, 18, 66963, 3197, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 498, 646, 8683, 432, 7069, 13, 38478, 11, 3421, 279, 9853, 12644, 448, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 1573, 13480, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 75763, 5351, 73335, 320, 15309, 1648, 1019, 256, 481, 3070, 8304, 220, 19, 66963, 1416, 3259, 264, 2155, 17172, 11, 1191, 448, 264, 1661, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 13, 1446, 646, 1281, 5257, 31423, 553, 1667, 419, 2331, 438, 264, 5916, 1459, 624, 256, 481, 3070, 8304, 220, 20, 66963, 29700, 5980, 9853, 12644, 686, 387, 17902, 1268, 323, 29573, 1091, 16564, 567, 5980, 9853, 12644, 382, 9485, 7354, 3410, 264, 6770, 8474, 369, 3259, 9853, 12644, 13, 576, 5754, 315, 279, 2331, 323, 5107, 13966, 646, 13289, 3118, 389, 4345, 21933, 13, 151645], "pred": "These steps provide a basic guide for making ice cream. The choice of the base and additional ingredients can vary based on personal preference.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.9801395556422756, "g_worst_claim": 0.05281919782811945, "g_content": 1.2620834488052506, "g_traj_mean": 0.8613581657409668}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.36, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "697", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "To make ice cream, pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn according to manufacturer's instructions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours. For a creamy and flavorful base, stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, stir in vanilla extract, and chill it thoroughly before using it as a base for your desired ice cream flavor.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can make a variety of ice cream flavors, both cream-based and custard-based.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "By following these steps, you can make a variety of ice cream flavors, both cream-based and custard-based.", "cot": "[\"To make ice cream, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Base**: Start by mixing your base. A good vanilla ice cream base is recommended. You can make a variety of flavors by starting with this base. Cream-based ice cream is icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream.\\n\\n2. **Chill the Mix**: Chill the mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours. This step is crucial for ensuring the ice cream sets properly.\\n\\n3. **Churn the Ice Cream**: Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker. Turn on the machine and churn according to the manufacturer's directions. This process typically takes 20 to 25 minutes.\\n\\n4. **Serve or Ripen**: Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can create a delicious batch of ice cream.\", \"To make ice cream, start by mixing sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container and chill it thoroughly, at least 2 hours. Once chilled, pour the mixture into your ice cream maker, turn it on, and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or wrap a piece of plastic wrap on top and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\", \"To make ice cream, you need to first make the base. For this you need to stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container such a large measuring cup. Then, stir in vanilla extract and chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\", \"To make ice cream, you can follow these steps using the information provided in the passages:\\n\\n1. For cream-based ice cream, mix the base. According to passage 3, a good vanilla ice cream base is easy to make. It is said to be a bit icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream. This recipe makes one quart of ice cream, so double it if you need more.\\n\\n2. For custard-based ice cream, follow the instructions from passage 1. Pour the cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn it according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and put it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\\n\\n3. For the ice cream mix, follow the instructions from passage 2. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup. Stir in vanilla extract and chill the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can make a variety of ice cream flavors, both cream-based and custard-based.\"]", "time_sec": 26.845, "generation_time_seconds": 26.2157, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6249, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 5351, 95518, 5145, 553, 26792, 697, 2331, 13, 362, 1661, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 374, 11102, 13, 1446, 646, 1281, 264, 8045, 315, 31423, 553, 5916, 448, 419, 2331, 13, 29700, 5980, 9853, 12644, 374, 17902, 1268, 323, 29573, 1091, 16564, 567, 5980, 9853, 12644, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 1143, 483, 279, 19219, 95518, 86489, 279, 6514, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 13, 1096, 3019, 374, 16587, 369, 22573, 279, 9853, 12644, 7289, 10277, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 1143, 399, 279, 19939, 29700, 95518, 25968, 279, 83942, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 13, 11999, 389, 279, 5662, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 13, 1096, 1882, 11136, 4990, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 60421, 476, 35437, 268, 95518, 9646, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 498, 646, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 1855, 264, 17923, 7162, 315, 9853, 12644, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can create a delicious batch of ice cream.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1935513525682317, "g_worst_claim": 0.2342529773712158, "g_content": 1.6108023903586648, "g_traj_mean": 1.1418379545211792}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 1191, 553, 26792, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 304, 264, 19187, 848, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 279, 13163, 702, 55667, 13, 26070, 1101, 3080, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 13, 23200, 279, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 323, 36301, 432, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 13, 9646, 83942, 11, 4914, 279, 20980, 1119, 697, 9853, 12644, 24232, 11, 2484, 432, 389, 11, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 369, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 13, 3197, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 15061, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 389, 1909, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make ice cream, start by mixing sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container and chill it thoroughly, at least 2 hours. Once chilled, pour the mixture into your ice cream maker, turn it on, and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or wrap a piece of plastic wrap on top and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.292965567142184, "g_worst_claim": 0.02567813131544325, "g_content": 1.7273626963297526, "g_traj_mean": 1.2545437812805176}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 498, 1184, 311, 1156, 1281, 279, 2331, 13, 1752, 419, 498, 1184, 311, 23065, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 1119, 264, 19187, 848, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 279, 13163, 702, 55667, 13, 26070, 279, 20980, 1101, 3080, 432, 374, 4017, 323, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 13, 23200, 279, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 1741, 264, 3460, 28990, 10525, 13, 5005, 11, 23065, 304, 32065, 8649, 323, 36301, 279, 20980, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make ice cream, you need to first make the base. For this you need to stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat the mixture just until it is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container such a large measuring cup. Then, stir in vanilla extract and chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3883850971596283, "g_worst_claim": 0.7171110312143961, "g_content": 1.9315006344817405, "g_traj_mean": 1.4777257442474365}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1667, 279, 1995, 3897, 304, 279, 46769, 1447, 16, 13, 1752, 12644, 5980, 9853, 12644, 11, 6514, 279, 2331, 13, 10548, 311, 21085, 220, 18, 11, 264, 1661, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 374, 4135, 311, 1281, 13, 1084, 374, 1053, 311, 387, 264, 2699, 17902, 1268, 323, 29573, 1091, 16564, 567, 5980, 9853, 12644, 13, 1096, 11116, 3643, 825, 40276, 315, 9853, 12644, 11, 773, 1990, 432, 421, 498, 1184, 803, 382, 17, 13, 1752, 16564, 567, 5980, 9853, 12644, 11, 1795, 279, 11221, 504, 21085, 220, 16, 13, 25968, 279, 9255, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 323, 80869, 432, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 369, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 13, 9646, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 498, 646, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 2182, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 382, 18, 13, 1752, 279, 9853, 12644, 6514, 11, 1795, 279, 11221, 504, 21085, 220, 17, 13, 64192, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 1119, 264, 19187, 848, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 279, 13163, 702, 55667, 13, 26070, 1101, 3080, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 13, 23200, 279, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 1741, 438, 264, 3460, 28990, 10525, 13, 64192, 304, 32065, 8649, 323, 36301, 279, 6514, 26364, 369, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 1281, 264, 8045, 315, 9853, 12644, 31423, 11, 2176, 12644, 5980, 323, 16564, 567, 5980, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can make a variety of ice cream flavors, both cream-based and custard-based.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3452456405742563, "g_worst_claim": 0.19836385548114777, "g_content": 1.7458188623414004, "g_traj_mean": 1.2559102773666382}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 6.45, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 5.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "698", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how you can make ice cream:\n\nPassage 1 provides instructions for making ice cream using an ice cream maker. To make ice cream, pour cold ice cream mix into the ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to the manufacturer's directions (usually 20-25 minutes). Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer for 2-3 hours to ripen.\n\nPassage 2 provides a recipe for making ice cream from scratch. To make ice cream, stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Then, heat the mixture until a small ring of foam appears around the edges. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup and stir in vanilla extract. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours before serving.\n\nPassage 3 provides general instructions for making ice cream bases. To make ice cream, you will need to start with a good vanilla ice cream base. This type of base is made with cream rather than custard, and it results in a lighter and less icy texture. To make one quart of ice cream, you will need to double the recipe.\n\nTherefore, to summarize:\n\nTo make ice cream using an ice cream maker:\n\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into the ice cream maker and turn on the machine.\n2. Churn the ice cream according to the manufacturer's directions (usually 20-25 minutes).\n3. Serve the ice cream immediately or place it in the freezer for 2-3 hours to ripen.\n\nTo make ice cream from scratch:\n\n1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk together in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved.\n2. Heat the mixture until a small ring of foam appears around the edges.\n3. Transfer the mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract.\n4. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours before serving.\n", "pred": "Make ice cream by following the steps in the passage. Start by pouring cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn it according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or cover it with plastic wrap and place it in the freezer to ripen.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Make ice cream by following the steps in the passage. Start by pouring cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn it according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or cover it with plastic wrap and place it in the freezer to ripen.", "cot": "[\"To make ice cream, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Base**: Start by mixing your base. A good vanilla ice cream base is recommended. You can make a variety of flavors by starting with this base. Cream-based ice cream is icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream.\\n\\n2. **Chill the Mix**: Chill the mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours. This step is crucial for ensuring the ice cream sets properly.\\n\\n3. **Churn the Ice Cream**: Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker. Turn on the machine and churn according to the manufacturer's directions. This process typically takes 20 to 25 minutes.\\n\\n4. **Serve or Ripen**: Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can create a delicious batch of ice cream.\", \"To make ice cream, follow these steps:\\n1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved. 2. Heat just until mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. 3. Transfer cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup. 4. Stir in vanilla extract and chill mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours. 5. Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. 6. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\", \"Make ice cream by following the steps in the passage. Start by pouring cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn it according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or cover it with plastic wrap and place it in the freezer to ripen.\", \"Ingredients: sugar, cream, and milk\\n\\nMethod:\\n\\n1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan until the sugar has dissolved.\\n2. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup.\\n4. Stir in vanilla extract and chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\\n5. Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker.\\n6. Turn on the machine and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\\n7. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\"]", "time_sec": 24.106, "generation_time_seconds": 23.3127, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7873, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 5351, 95518, 5145, 553, 26792, 697, 2331, 13, 362, 1661, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 374, 11102, 13, 1446, 646, 1281, 264, 8045, 315, 31423, 553, 5916, 448, 419, 2331, 13, 29700, 5980, 9853, 12644, 374, 17902, 1268, 323, 29573, 1091, 16564, 567, 5980, 9853, 12644, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 1143, 483, 279, 19219, 95518, 86489, 279, 6514, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 13, 1096, 3019, 374, 16587, 369, 22573, 279, 9853, 12644, 7289, 10277, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 1143, 399, 279, 19939, 29700, 95518, 25968, 279, 83942, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 13, 11999, 389, 279, 5662, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 13, 1096, 1882, 11136, 4990, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 60421, 476, 35437, 268, 95518, 9646, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 498, 646, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 1855, 264, 17923, 7162, 315, 9853, 12644, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can create a delicious batch of ice cream.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1858706834115824, "g_worst_claim": 0.2552683353424072, "g_content": 1.5986241812657829, "g_traj_mean": 1.1351205110549927}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 64192, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 1119, 264, 19187, 848, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 13163, 702, 55667, 13, 220, 17, 13, 26070, 1101, 3080, 6514, 374, 4017, 323, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 13, 220, 18, 13, 23200, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 1741, 438, 264, 3460, 28990, 10525, 13, 220, 19, 13, 64192, 304, 32065, 8649, 323, 36301, 6514, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 13, 220, 20, 13, 25968, 279, 83942, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 11, 2484, 389, 279, 5662, 11, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 13963, 594, 17961, 369, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 13, 220, 21, 13, 3197, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 8683, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 304, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make ice cream, follow these steps:\n1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved. 2. Heat just until mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. 3. Transfer cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup. 4. Stir in vanilla extract and chill mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours. 5. Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker, turn on the machine, and churn according to manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. 6. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place in freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6036705193575347, "g_worst_claim": 0.48029975096384686, "g_content": 1.8717530413371761, "g_traj_mean": 1.4365015029907227}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [8078, 9853, 12644, 553, 2701, 279, 7354, 304, 279, 21085, 13, 5145, 553, 50413, 9255, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 323, 80869, 432, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 369, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 13, 9646, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 3421, 432, 448, 12188, 15061, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 13, 151645], "pred": "Make ice cream by following the steps in the passage. Start by pouring cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and churn it according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve it immediately or cover it with plastic wrap and place it in the freezer to ripen.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2872416114095073, "g_worst_claim": 1.2004649513646175, "g_content": 2.1284830429974724, "g_traj_mean": 1.2659363746643066}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [45747, 25, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 271, 3523, 1447, 16, 13, 64192, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 304, 264, 19187, 848, 3080, 279, 13163, 702, 55667, 624, 17, 13, 26070, 279, 20980, 1101, 3080, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 624, 18, 13, 23200, 279, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 11, 1741, 438, 264, 3460, 28990, 10525, 624, 19, 13, 64192, 304, 32065, 8649, 323, 36301, 279, 20980, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 624, 20, 13, 25968, 279, 83942, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 624, 21, 13, 11999, 389, 279, 5662, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 369, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 624, 22, 13, 9646, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 8683, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 13, 151645], "pred": "1. Stir sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan until the sugar has dissolved.\n2. Heat the mixture just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge.\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, such as a large measuring cup.\n4. Stir in vanilla extract and chill the mixture thoroughly, at least 2 hours.\n5. Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker.\n6. Turn on the machine and churn according to the manufacturer's directions for 20 to 25 minutes.\n7. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.5137293396055247, "g_worst_claim": -0.16717805645682596, "g_content": 1.805698776245117, "g_traj_mean": 1.186510443687439}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 21.43, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "699", "question": "How do you make ice cream", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can make ice cream:\n\n1. Pour cold ice cream mix into an ice cream maker and turn on the machine, following the manufacturer's instructions (passage 1).\n2. Stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until sugar has dissolved, then heat just until a small ring of foam appears around the edge (passage 2).\n3. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container and stir in vanilla extract before chilling the mix thoroughly for at least 2 hours (passage 2).\n4. Once the ice cream base is ready, pour it into the ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's instructions (passage 1).\n5. When the ice cream is softly frozen, serve immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours (passage 1).\n\nNote that the passages do not provide a specific recipe for making ice cream, but rather provide general steps and tips for making ice cream using an ice cream maker.", "pred": "By following these steps, you can create a delicious batch of ice cream.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "By following these steps, you can create a delicious batch of ice cream.", "cot": "[\"To make ice cream, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Base**: Start by mixing your base. A good vanilla ice cream base is recommended. You can make a variety of flavors by starting with this base. Cream-based ice cream is icier and lighter than custard-based ice cream.\\n\\n2. **Chill the Mix**: Chill the mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours. This step is crucial for ensuring the ice cream sets properly.\\n\\n3. **Churn the Ice Cream**: Pour the chilled ice cream mix into an ice cream maker. Turn on the machine and churn according to the manufacturer's directions. This process typically takes 20 to 25 minutes.\\n\\n4. **Serve or Ripen**: Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on the ice cream and place it in the freezer to ripen for 2 to 3 hours.\\n\\nBy following these steps, you can create a delicious batch of ice cream.\", \"To make ice cream, start by mixing your base. For a creamy texture, use a vanilla ice cream base. If you want a lighter flavor, you can mix with cream. Heat the base, add sugar, cream, milk, and vanilla extract. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Then pour the chilled mix into an ice cream maker, turn it on, and churn the ice cream according to the manufacturer's directions, which usually takes 20 to 25 minutes. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on it and freeze it for 2 to 3 hours to allow it to ripen further.\", \"To make ice cream, first, stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat just until the mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup, and stir in vanilla extract. Then, chill the mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours. If you want more ice cream, double the recipe.\", \"To make ice cream, start by heating a mixture of sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Then, transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, chill it thoroughly, and stir in vanilla extract.\"]", "time_sec": 20.773, "generation_time_seconds": 19.7184, "selection_time_seconds": 1.0473, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 5351, 95518, 5145, 553, 26792, 697, 2331, 13, 362, 1661, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 374, 11102, 13, 1446, 646, 1281, 264, 8045, 315, 31423, 553, 5916, 448, 419, 2331, 13, 29700, 5980, 9853, 12644, 374, 17902, 1268, 323, 29573, 1091, 16564, 567, 5980, 9853, 12644, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 1143, 483, 279, 19219, 95518, 86489, 279, 6514, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 13, 1096, 3019, 374, 16587, 369, 22573, 279, 9853, 12644, 7289, 10277, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 1143, 399, 279, 19939, 29700, 95518, 25968, 279, 83942, 9853, 12644, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 13, 11999, 389, 279, 5662, 323, 80869, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 13, 1096, 1882, 11136, 4990, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 60421, 476, 35437, 268, 95518, 9646, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 498, 646, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 279, 9853, 12644, 323, 1992, 432, 304, 279, 49585, 311, 23288, 268, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 382, 1359, 2701, 1493, 7354, 11, 498, 646, 1855, 264, 17923, 7162, 315, 9853, 12644, 13, 151645], "pred": "By following these steps, you can create a delicious batch of ice cream.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1965849119248952, "g_worst_claim": 0.282256555557251, "g_content": 1.624540540907118, "g_traj_mean": 1.1416985988616943}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 1191, 553, 26792, 697, 2331, 13, 1752, 264, 46885, 10434, 11, 990, 264, 32065, 9853, 12644, 2331, 13, 1416, 498, 1366, 264, 29573, 17172, 11, 498, 646, 6514, 448, 12644, 13, 26070, 279, 2331, 11, 912, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 14074, 11, 323, 32065, 8649, 13, 86489, 279, 20980, 26364, 369, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 13, 5005, 4914, 279, 83942, 6514, 1119, 458, 9853, 12644, 24232, 11, 2484, 432, 389, 11, 323, 80869, 279, 9853, 12644, 4092, 311, 279, 13963, 594, 17961, 11, 892, 5990, 4990, 220, 17, 15, 311, 220, 17, 20, 4420, 13, 9646, 279, 9853, 12644, 374, 56050, 19690, 11, 498, 646, 8683, 432, 7069, 476, 1992, 264, 6573, 315, 12188, 15061, 5961, 389, 432, 323, 29930, 432, 369, 220, 17, 311, 220, 18, 4115, 311, 2138, 432, 311, 23288, 268, 4623, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make ice cream, start by mixing your base. For a creamy texture, use a vanilla ice cream base. If you want a lighter flavor, you can mix with cream. Heat the base, add sugar, cream, milk, and vanilla extract. Chill the mixture thoroughly for at least 2 hours. Then pour the chilled mix into an ice cream maker, turn it on, and churn the ice cream according to the manufacturer's directions, which usually takes 20 to 25 minutes. Once the ice cream is softly frozen, you can serve it immediately or place a piece of plastic wrap directly on it and freeze it for 2 to 3 hours to allow it to ripen further.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.04221790594284, "g_worst_claim": 0.2598245143890381, "g_content": 1.4904725943038712, "g_traj_mean": 1.1238927841186523}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 1156, 11, 23065, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 1119, 264, 19187, 848, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 279, 13163, 702, 55667, 13, 26070, 1101, 3080, 279, 6514, 374, 4017, 323, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 13, 23200, 279, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 1741, 438, 264, 3460, 28990, 10525, 11, 323, 23065, 304, 32065, 8649, 13, 5005, 11, 36301, 279, 6514, 26364, 11, 518, 3245, 220, 17, 4115, 13, 1416, 498, 1366, 803, 9853, 12644, 11, 1990, 279, 11116, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make ice cream, first, stir sugar, cream, and milk into a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved. Heat just until the mix is hot and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container such as a large measuring cup, and stir in vanilla extract. Then, chill the mix thoroughly, at least 2 hours. If you want more ice cream, double the recipe.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6822638694823735, "g_worst_claim": 0.7985902786254883, "g_content": 2.1768502322110264, "g_traj_mean": 1.6405553817749023}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [1249, 1281, 9853, 12644, 11, 1191, 553, 23579, 264, 20980, 315, 13163, 11, 12644, 11, 323, 14074, 304, 264, 19187, 848, 916, 3347, 8628, 3080, 279, 13163, 702, 55667, 323, 264, 2613, 10058, 315, 31083, 7952, 2163, 279, 6821, 13, 5005, 11, 8317, 279, 12644, 20980, 311, 264, 4914, 480, 5476, 11, 36301, 432, 26364, 11, 323, 23065, 304, 32065, 8649, 13, 151645], "pred": "To make ice cream, start by heating a mixture of sugar, cream, and milk in a saucepan over low heat until the sugar has dissolved and a small ring of foam appears around the edge. Then, transfer the cream mixture to a pourable container, chill it thoroughly, and stir in vanilla extract.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.3782593369483946, "g_worst_claim": 0.841044545173645, "g_content": 1.9999043782552084, "g_traj_mean": 1.5958048105239868}}], "selected_rollout": 2, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 8.57, "GAVIE-Rel": 10.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 10.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "701", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "gt": "Children learn various skills and concepts through water play. It aids in the development of gross motor skills as they engage in activities like running through sprinklers or filling and pouring water from buckets. Water play also facilitates academic learning in areas such as science and math. Children learn about the concept of floating and sinking, and understand that different objects have different buoyancies. In math, they learn about measurement by determining the amount of water that fits into a bucket, and concepts of more and less by comparing water levels in different buckets. Water play also promotes creativity, allowing children to use their imagination.", "pred": "Children learn various skills and concepts through water play, including gross motor skills, academic learning, and creativity. For example, they can learn about floating and sinking, measuring water, and using their imagination.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Children learn various skills and concepts through water play, including gross motor skills, academic learning, and creativity. For example, they can learn about floating and sinking, measuring water, and using their imagination.", "cot": "[\"Children learn various skills and concepts through water play, including gross motor skills, academic learning, and creativity. For example, they can learn about floating and sinking, measuring water, and using their imagination.\", \"Children learn a variety of things through water play. They improve their gross motor skills by running through sprinklers or filling and pouring water, they gain academic skills like floating and sinking concepts in science, and measuring amounts of water in math. Water play also encourages creativity as children pretend and use their imagination while playing with water.\", \"Answer: Children learn several things through water play, including gross motor skills, academic learning, and creativity. For example, they can learn about floating and sinking in science, and about measuring in math. They can also pretend and use their imagination.\", \"Children can learn about gross motor skills, academic learning, science, and creativity through water play.\"]", "time_sec": 10.996, "generation_time_seconds": 10.0933, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8957, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [11539, 3960, 5257, 7361, 323, 18940, 1526, 3015, 1486, 11, 2670, 19952, 8872, 7361, 11, 14250, 6832, 11, 323, 27597, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 807, 646, 3960, 911, 19057, 323, 61093, 11, 28990, 3015, 11, 323, 1667, 862, 27799, 13, 151645], "pred": "Children learn various skills and concepts through water play, including gross motor skills, academic learning, and creativity. For example, they can learn about floating and sinking, measuring water, and using their imagination.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9628039724296993, "g_worst_claim": 0.5721889138221741, "g_content": 2.1993175853382456, "g_traj_mean": 1.3928070068359375}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [11539, 3960, 264, 8045, 315, 2513, 1526, 3015, 1486, 13, 2379, 7269, 862, 19952, 8872, 7361, 553, 4303, 1526, 50698, 9254, 476, 21274, 323, 50413, 3015, 11, 807, 8722, 14250, 7361, 1075, 19057, 323, 61093, 18940, 304, 8038, 11, 323, 28990, 14713, 315, 3015, 304, 6888, 13, 9959, 1486, 1083, 36067, 27597, 438, 2841, 34740, 323, 990, 862, 27799, 1393, 5619, 448, 3015, 13, 151645], "pred": "Children learn a variety of things through water play. They improve their gross motor skills by running through sprinklers or filling and pouring water, they gain academic skills like floating and sinking concepts in science, and measuring amounts of water in math. Water play also encourages creativity as children pretend and use their imagination while playing with water.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.6164463562123916, "g_worst_claim": 1.0375275611877441, "g_content": 2.1850610681482263, "g_traj_mean": 1.5508915185928345}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16141, 25, 15044, 3960, 3807, 2513, 1526, 3015, 1486, 11, 2670, 19952, 8872, 7361, 11, 14250, 6832, 11, 323, 27597, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 807, 646, 3960, 911, 19057, 323, 61093, 304, 8038, 11, 323, 911, 28990, 304, 6888, 13, 2379, 646, 1083, 34740, 323, 990, 862, 27799, 13, 151645], "pred": "Children learn several things through water play, including gross motor skills, academic learning, and creativity. For example, they can learn about floating and sinking in science, and about measuring in math. They can also pretend and use their imagination.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.8414065952654237, "g_worst_claim": 0.7747303485870362, "g_content": 2.2702811559041343, "g_traj_mean": 1.3715956211090088}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [11539, 646, 3960, 911, 19952, 8872, 7361, 11, 14250, 6832, 11, 8038, 11, 323, 27597, 1526, 3015, 1486, 13, 151645], "pred": "Children can learn about gross motor skills, academic learning, science, and creativity through water play.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.2197920348909164, "g_worst_claim": 0.533062219619751, "g_content": 3.1092889959161933, "g_traj_mean": 1.690765619277954}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.67, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.5, "GAVIE-Acc": 8.5, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "702", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "gt": "Children learn various skills and concepts through water play. They develop gross motor skills by running through sprinklers and pouring water. Water play also provides opportunities for academic learning, such as understanding concepts like floating and sinking, measuring water, and comparing quantities. Additionally, water play encourages creativity and imagination as children pretend and engage in imaginative play with water.", "pred": "children learn with water play gross motor skills, academic learning, and creativity.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "children learn with water play gross motor skills, academic learning, and creativity.", "cot": "[\"Children learn various skills and concepts through water play, including gross motor skills, academic learning, and creativity. For example, they can learn about floating and sinking, measuring water, and using their imagination.\", \"Children learn various skills through water play. They develop gross motor skills by running through sprinklers or filling buckets with water and pouring it out. Water play also aids in academic learning, specifically in science, where children learn about floating and sinking, and in math, where they learn about measuring and comparing amounts of water. Additionally, it encourages creativity as children use their imagination while playing with water.\", \"children learn with water play gross motor skills, academic learning, and creativity.\", \"children learn gross motor skills, academic learning, science, and math.\"]", "time_sec": 11.041, "generation_time_seconds": 10.2663, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7691, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [11539, 3960, 5257, 7361, 323, 18940, 1526, 3015, 1486, 11, 2670, 19952, 8872, 7361, 11, 14250, 6832, 11, 323, 27597, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 807, 646, 3960, 911, 19057, 323, 61093, 11, 28990, 3015, 11, 323, 1667, 862, 27799, 13, 151645], "pred": "Children learn various skills and concepts through water play, including gross motor skills, academic learning, and creativity. For example, they can learn about floating and sinking, measuring water, and using their imagination.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.9333238138092887, "g_worst_claim": 0.5316842794418335, "g_content": 2.2215192968195137, "g_traj_mean": 1.401490330696106}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [11539, 3960, 5257, 7361, 1526, 3015, 1486, 13, 2379, 2225, 19952, 8872, 7361, 553, 4303, 1526, 50698, 9254, 476, 21274, 42112, 448, 3015, 323, 50413, 432, 700, 13, 9959, 1486, 1083, 51697, 304, 14250, 6832, 11, 11689, 304, 8038, 11, 1380, 2841, 3960, 911, 19057, 323, 61093, 11, 323, 304, 6888, 11, 1380, 807, 3960, 911, 28990, 323, 26297, 14713, 315, 3015, 13, 22406, 11, 432, 36067, 27597, 438, 2841, 990, 862, 27799, 1393, 5619, 448, 3015, 13, 151645], "pred": "Children learn various skills through water play. They develop gross motor skills by running through sprinklers or filling buckets with water and pouring it out. Water play also aids in academic learning, specifically in science, where children learn about floating and sinking, and in math, where they learn about measuring and comparing amounts of water. Additionally, it encourages creativity as children use their imagination while playing with water.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.2463753495897565, "g_worst_claim": 0.8635894775390625, "g_content": 1.778263473510742, "g_traj_mean": 1.2319672107696533}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [5864, 3960, 448, 3015, 1486, 19952, 8872, 7361, 11, 14250, 6832, 11, 323, 27597, 13, 151645], "pred": "children learn with water play gross motor skills, academic learning, and creativity.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 3.250583542717828, "g_worst_claim": 2.087339825100369, "g_content": 3.6654132843017577, "g_traj_mean": 2.2277872562408447}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [5864, 3960, 19952, 8872, 7361, 11, 14250, 6832, 11, 8038, 11, 323, 6888, 13, 151645], "pred": "children learn gross motor skills, academic learning, science, and math.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 3.5193320115407305, "g_worst_claim": 2.6077221234639487, "g_content": 3.8304540846082897, "g_traj_mean": 2.4023940563201904}}], "selected_rollout": 3, "random_sel_rollout": 2, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.04, "GAVIE-Rel": 9.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 7.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "705", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "gt": "Based on the given passages, children learn the following through water play:\n\n1. Gross motor skills: Running, pouring, and manipulating water helps develop fine and gross motor skills. (Passage 1)\n2. Science concepts: Floating and sinking, measurement, and experimentation with different objects in water. (Passage 1)\n3. Creativity and imagination: Water play encourages children to use their imagination and engage in pretend play. (Passage 1)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not mention any other specific academic learning outcomes beyond gross motor skills, science concepts, and creativity.", "pred": "- Gross motor skills: Children engage in activities like running through sprinklers, filling and pouring water, which helps develop their physical abilities.\n- Academic skills:\n  - Science: They learn concepts such as floating and sinking by observing different objects in water.\n  - Math: Children can practice measuring and compare quantities of water by filling buckets with varying amounts.\n- Creativity: Water play encourages imaginative play, allowing children to think creatively and use their imaginations.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "- Gross motor skills: Children engage in activities like running through sprinklers, filling and pouring water, which helps develop their physical abilities.\n- Academic skills:\n  - Science: They learn concepts such as floating and sinking by observing different objects in water.\n  - Math: Children can practice measuring and compare quantities of water by filling buckets with varying amounts.\n- Creativity: Water play encourages imaginative play, allowing children to think creatively and use their imaginations.", "cot": "[\"Children learn various skills and concepts through water play, including gross motor skills, academic learning, and creativity. For example, they can learn about floating and sinking, measuring water, and using their imagination.\", \"children learn gross motor skills, academic learning, science, math, creativity, and discovery learning from water play.\", \"Children learn several things with water play from the given passages:\\n\\n1. **Gross Motor Skills**: Water play involves activities like running through sprinklers, filling and pouring buckets, which help children develop their gross motor skills.\\n\\n2. **Academic Learning**:\\n   - **Science**: Children learn about floating and sinking, understanding the principles of buoyancy and density.\\n   - **Math**: They learn to measure amounts of water by filling buckets with different quantities, understanding more and less, and concepts of volume.\\n\\n3. **Creativity**: Water play encourages children to use their imagination, pretend, and express their creativity.\\n\\nThese points are directly supported by the text, without adding external information.\", \"Children learn a variety of things through water play, including:\\n\\n- Gross motor skills: Children engage in activities like running through sprinklers, filling and pouring water, which helps develop their physical abilities.\\n- Academic skills:\\n  - Science: They learn concepts such as floating and sinking by observing different objects in water.\\n  - Math: Children can practice measuring and compare quantities of water by filling buckets with varying amounts.\\n- Creativity: Water play encourages imaginative play, allowing children to think creatively and use their imaginations.\"]", "time_sec": 14.889, "generation_time_seconds": 14.0968, "selection_time_seconds": 0.7872, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [11539, 3960, 5257, 7361, 323, 18940, 1526, 3015, 1486, 11, 2670, 19952, 8872, 7361, 11, 14250, 6832, 11, 323, 27597, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 807, 646, 3960, 911, 19057, 323, 61093, 11, 28990, 3015, 1