5], "pred": "This method ensures that the egg is poached evenly and the yolk remains intact, resulting in a perfectly domed-shaped egg.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7891584861744914, "g_worst_claim": 0.03430876135826111, "g_content": 1.2228054719812729, "g_traj_mean": 0.7595972418785095}}], "selected_rollout": 1, "random_sel_rollout": 3, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 11.36, "GAVIE-Rel": 8.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 9.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "719", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "gt": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\n\n1. Begin by bringing a large pot of water to a boil.\n2. Gently slide an egg into your silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the egg's yolk.\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring that the pod stays upright and no water gets inside.\n4. Cover the pot with a tight-fitting lid and allow the egg to cook for 6 minutes.\n5. After 6 minutes, remove the lid from the pot and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to carefully lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.", "pred": "This process ensures a perfectly poached egg every time.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "This process ensures a perfectly poached egg every time.", "cot": "[\"To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Pod**: Lightly oil the PoachPod before use. This helps prevent the egg from sticking to the pod.\\n\\n2. **Crack the Egg**: Crack an egg into the oiled PoachPod, being careful not to break the yolk.\\n\\n3. **Float the Pod**: Carefully float the PoachPod in a pot of boiling water. Ensure the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\\n\\n4. **Cook the Egg**: Cover the pot with a tight-fitting lid and let the egg cook for about 4-6 minutes.\\n\\n5. **Remove the Pod**: After the egg is cooked, remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod out of the hot water.\\n\\n6. **Release the Egg**: Flip the PoachPod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\\n\\nThis method ensures that the egg is poached evenly and the yolk remains intact.\", \"1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide the egg into your silicone poaching pod, being careful not to break the egg's yolk.\\n3. Carefully float the poaching pod in the boiling water, making sure the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\\n4. Cover the pot with the lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\\n5. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\\n6. Flip the poaching pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release your poached egg onto the plate.\", \"To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. **Prepare the Pod**: Lightly oil the silicone pod before using it.\\n2. **Crack the Egg**: Crack the egg into the oiled pod.\\n3. **Float the Pod**: Gently place the pod into a saucepan of simmering water.\\n4. **Cover the Pod**: Ensure the pod stays upright in the water and no water gets into the pod.\\n5. **Cook**: Cover the pan with a tight-fitting lid and let the egg cook for about 4-6 minutes.\\n6. **Remove the Pod**: Use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\\n7. **Release the Egg**: Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\\n\\nThis process ensures a perfectly poached egg every time.\", \"To poach an egg using a PoachPod, follow these steps:\\n1. Bring a large pot of water to a boil.\\n2. Crack an egg and gently slide it into the silicone poaching pod, taking care not to break the egg's yolk.\\n3. Float the poaching pod in the boiling water, ensuring the pod stays upright and no water gets into the pod.\\n4. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for six minutes.\\n5. Remove the lid and use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the poaching pod out of the hot water.\\n6. Flip the pod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate.\\n\\nNote: The instructions provided in Passage 2 do not specify whether the pod needs to be lightly oiled before use, which is a common step in poaching eggs. It is advisable to lightly oil the pod before cracking the egg into it to prevent sticking.\"]", "time_sec": 28.773, "generation_time_seconds": 27.9157, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8516, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [1249, 3193, 610, 458, 18636, 1667, 264, 13808, 610, 23527, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 16, 13, 3070, 50590, 279, 16821, 95518, 8658, 398, 5590, 279, 13808, 610, 23527, 1573, 990, 13, 1096, 8609, 5358, 279, 18636, 504, 36972, 311, 279, 7509, 382, 17, 13, 3070, 16001, 473, 279, 41213, 95518, 54945, 458, 18636, 1119, 279, 297, 2181, 13808, 610, 23527, 11, 1660, 16585, 537, 311, 1438, 279, 379, 22604, 382, 18, 13, 3070, 5442, 279, 16821, 95518, 10627, 3641, 2224, 279, 13808, 610, 23527, 304, 264, 3338, 315, 49837, 3015, 13, 29279, 279, 7509, 26558, 48585, 323, 902, 3015, 5221, 1119, 279, 7509, 382, 19, 13, 3070, 58382, 279, 41213, 95518, 17757, 279, 3338, 448, 264, 10296, 2220, 14810, 26334, 323, 1077, 279, 18636, 4296, 369, 911, 220, 19, 12, 21, 4420, 382, 20, 13, 3070, 13021, 279, 16821, 95518, 4636, 279, 18636, 374, 29105, 11, 4057, 279, 26334, 323, 990, 264, 3460, 1739, 15521, 45505, 476, 259, 13181, 311, 11893, 279, 13808, 610, 23527, 700, 315, 279, 4017, 3015, 382, 21, 13, 3070, 16077, 279, 41213, 95518, 40284, 279, 13808, 610, 23527, 35841, 1495, 916, 264, 11968, 323, 29273, 3493, 389, 279, 5622, 311, 4879, 279, 3193, 3854, 18636, 8630, 279, 11968, 382, 1986, 1714, 25351, 429, 279, 18636, 374, 3193, 3854, 41047, 323, 279, 379, 22604, 8458, 34439, 13, 151645], "pred": "This method ensures that the egg is poached evenly and the yolk remains intact.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.7947160817248526, "g_worst_claim": 0.10630215207735698, "g_content": 1.2980755515720532, "g_traj_mean": 0.8278675675392151}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [16, 13, 39124, 264, 3460, 3338, 315, 3015, 311, 264, 43690, 624, 17, 