{"id": "732", "question": "how do you process the air you breathe before it gets to your lungs?", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the process of processing the air we breathe before it reaches the lungs involves the following steps:\n\n1. The diaphragm muscle contracts to take air into the lungs, moving down from the bottom of the rib cage towards the abdominal region. (Passage 1)\n2. The process of breathing involves the exchange of gases between the body and the outside environment, occurring in the lungs. (Passage 2)\n3. Increasing the volume of the thoracic cavity, including the lungs, decreases the air pressure in the lungs below the atmospheric pressure, forcing air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing us to inhale. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, the main steps in processing the air we breathe before it reaches the lungs are:\n\n1. Contraction of the diaphragm muscle to draw air into the lungs.\n2. Exchange of gases between the body and the outside environment in the lungs.\n3. Expansion of the thoracic cavity to decrease air pressure in the lungs and facilitate inhalation.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "Based on the given passage, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the cells of your body and the outside environment, which is the air. The passage also mentions that the process of breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transporting of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the given passage, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the cells of your body and the outside environment, which is the air. The passage also mentions that the process of breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transporting of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body.", "cot": "[\"Based on the information provided in the passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. This exchange occurs in the lungs. The process of breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The ventilation component takes center stage in enhancing therapeutic back exercise programs or successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy.\", \"Based on the given passage, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the cells of your body and the outside environment, which is the air. The passage also mentions that the process of breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transporting of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body.\", \"Based on the information provided in the passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases between the body's cells and the outside environment. The exchange of gases (oxygen and carbon dioxide) occurs in the lungs.\", \"The process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide that occurs between you, in particular, the cells of your body, and the outside environment, which is the air.\"]", "time_sec": 14.325, "generation_time_seconds": 13.7065, "selection_time_seconds": 0.6123, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0,