{"id": "733", "question": "how do you process the air you breathe before it gets to your lungs?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how the air you breathe is processed before it reaches your lungs:\n\nWhen you inhale, the diaphragm muscle contracts, moving down from the bottom of your rib cage towards your abdominal region, which causes the thoracic cavity to increase in volume. This decrease in air pressure in the lungs below atmospheric pressure forces air from the atmosphere into the lungs, causing you to inhale.\n\nTherefore, the air you breathe is processed by the diaphragm muscle before it reaches your lungs, which contracts to take air into the lungs and relax to let it out again. Additionally, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, such as oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment, which occurs in the lungs.", "pred": "Based on the information provided in the passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. This exchange occurs in the lungs. The process of breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The ventilation component takes center stage in enhancing therapeutic back exercise programs or successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "Based on the information provided in the passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. This exchange occurs in the lungs. The process of breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The ventilation component takes center stage in enhancing therapeutic back exercise programs or successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy.", "cot": "[\"Based on the information provided in the passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. This exchange occurs in the lungs. The process of breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The ventilation component takes center stage in enhancing therapeutic back exercise programs or successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy.\", \"The process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide that occurs between you, in particular, the cells of your body, and the outside environment, which is the air. This exchange happens in the lungs. In all, breathing has two components: Ventilation, or movement of oxygen into, and carbon dioxide, out of your lungs. Circulation, or transporting the oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body.\", \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\", \"Based on the provided passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between you and the outside environment. This exchange occurs in the lungs. The key components of this process are ventilation, which involves the movement of oxygen into the lungs and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which involves transporting the oxygen taken into the body to where it is needed. The passage also states that increasing the volume of the thoracic cavity can help increase the volume of the lungs, which can cause a decrease in the air pressure in the lungs below the atmospheric pressure, forcing air from the atmosphere into the lungs and causing you to inhale.\"]", "time_sec": 16.315, "generation_time_seconds": 15.486, "selection_time_seconds": 0.8225, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 1995, 3897, 304, 279, 46769, 11, 279, 1882, 315, 25938, 17601, 279, 9289, 315, 44512, 11, 31025, 23552, 323, 12499, 39489, 11, 1948, 279, 2487, 323, 279, 4889, 4573, 13, 1096, 9289, 13666, 304, 279, 44174, 13, 576, 1882, 315, 25938, 702, 1378, 6813, 25, 55134, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7203, 315, 23552, 1119, 323, 12499, 39489, 700, 315, 279, 44174, 11, 323, 34755, 11, 892, 374, 279, 7557, 315, 23552, 4429, 1119, 279, 2487, 2337, 55134, 311, 1380, 432, 374, 4362, 304, 279, 2487, 13, 576, 55134, 3692, 4990, 4126, 6430, 304, 46494, 36371, 1182, 10158, 7468, 476, 6849, 20239, 304, 264, 462, 31244, 60776, 15069, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the information provided in the passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between the body and the outside environment. This exchange occurs in the lungs. The process of breathing has two components: ventilation, which is the movement of oxygen into and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which is the transport of oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body. The ventilation component takes center stage in enhancing therapeutic back exercise programs or successful participation in a pro-active holistic therapy.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.4960006974786833, "g_worst_claim": 0.0273685140742196, "g_content": 3.2483144906850963, "g_traj_mean": 1.9852426052093506}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [785, 1882, 315, 25938, 17601, 279, 9289, 315, 44512, 11, 31025, 11, 23552, 323, 12499, 39489, 429, 13666, 1948, 498, 11, 304, 3953, 11, 279, 7761, 315, 697, 2487, 11, 323, 279, 4889, 4573, 11, 892, 374, 279, 3720, 13, 1096, 9289, 8573, 304, 279, 44174, 13, 758, 678, 11, 25938, 702, 1378, 6813, 25, 26407, 13455, 11, 476, 7203, 315, 23552, 1119, 11, 323, 12499, 39489, 11, 700, 315, 697, 44174, 13, 16338, 2914, 11, 476, 66657, 279, 23552, 4429, 1119, 279, 2487, 2337, 55134, 311, 1380, 432, 374, 4362, 304, 279, 2487, 13, 151645], "pred": "The process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely, oxygen and carbon dioxide that occurs between you, in particular, the cells of your body, and the outside environment, which is the air. This exchange happens in the lungs. In all, breathing has two components: Ventilation, or movement of oxygen into, and carbon dioxide, out of your lungs. Circulation, or transporting the oxygen taken into the body during ventilation to where it is needed in the body.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 2.0241210922696293, "g_worst_claim": 1.167499269757952, "g_content": 2.602650112575955, "g_traj_mean": 2.1812586784362793}}, {"rollout": 2, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 0.06599468737840652, "g_worst_claim": 0.06599468737840652, "g_content": 0.10402203798294067, "g_traj_mean": 0.058717768639326096}}, {"rollout": 3, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 3897, 46769, 11, 279, 1882, 315, 25938, 17601, 279, 9289, 315, 44512, 11, 31025, 23552, 323, 12499, 39489, 11, 1948, 498, 323, 279, 4889, 4573, 13, 1096, 9289, 13666, 304, 279, 44174, 13, 576, 1376, 6813, 315, 419, 1882, 525, 55134, 11, 892, 17601, 279, 7203, 315, 23552, 1119, 279, 44174, 323, 12499, 39489, 700, 315, 279, 44174, 11, 323, 34755, 11, 892, 17601, 66657, 279, 23552, 4429, 1119, 279, 2487, 311, 1380, 432, 374, 4362, 13, 576, 21085, 1083, 5302, 429, 7703, 279, 8123, 315, 279, 72733, 93157, 55329, 646, 1492, 5263, 279, 8123, 315, 279, 44174, 11, 892, 646, 5240, 264, 18472, 304, 279, 3720, 7262, 304, 279, 44174, 3685, 279, 44375, 7262, 11, 24913, 3720, 504, 279, 16566, 1119, 279, 44174, 323, 14381, 498, 311, 59437, 1574, 13, 151645], "pred": "Based on the provided passages, the process of breathing involves the exchange of gases, namely oxygen and carbon dioxide, between you and the outside environment. This exchange occurs in the lungs. The key components of this process are ventilation, which involves the movement of oxygen into the lungs and carbon dioxide out of the lungs, and circulation, which involves transporting the oxygen taken into the body to where it is needed. The passage also states that increasing the volume of the thoracic cavity can help increase the volume of the lungs, which can cause a decrease in the air pressure in the lungs below the atmospheric pressure, forcing air from the atmosphere into the lungs and causing you to inhale.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.1583476063236362, "g_worst_claim": 0.10594966014226277, "g_content": 1.938469327729324, "g_traj_mean": 1.2812131643295288}}], "selected_rollout": 0, "random_sel_rollout": 0, "rank_score": "g_content", "partner": "psg-borrow", "error": null, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 27.78, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "735", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "SMS stands for Short Message Service, commonly referred to as a text message, and allows you to send a text message of up to 160 characters to another device. MMS, which stands for Multimedia Messaging Service, is an evolution of SMS. It allows you to send messages that include pictures, video, or audio content to another device. MMS messages can carry a larger size of content up to 300KB. SMS is restricted to sending text-only messages, whereas MMS allows a combination of text, pictures, sounds, and videos.", "pred": "These differences highlight that while SMS is the foundational service for text messaging, MMS enhances this functionality by allowing users to communicate with a broader range of multimedia content.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "bon_grounding_random_sel", "raw_output": "These differences highlight that while SMS is the foundational service for text messaging, MMS enhances this functionality by allowing users to communicate with a broader range of multimedia content.", "cot": "[\"SMS allows you to send text only, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four.\", \"SMS stands for Short Message Service and is also commonly referred to as a text message. With a SMS, you can send a message of up to 160 characters to another device. Longer messages will automatically be split up into several parts. Most cell phones support this type of text messaging. MMS: MMS stands for Multimedia Messaging Service and this type of text messaging is an evolution of the SMS. With a MMS, you can send a message including pictures, video, or audio content to another device. It is most commonly used to send a photo taken with a camera phone to another phone.\", \"SMS (Short Message Service) and MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) are both types of text messaging services for mobile phones, but they have distinct differences:\\n\\n1. **Content Type**: SMS is restricted to text-only messages, whereas MMS allows for the sending of various types of content including pictures, videos, audio, and text. This means MMS is an evolution of SMS, providing more multimedia capabilities.\\n\\n2. **Message Size**: SMS messages are limited to up to 160 characters, with longer messages being split into several parts. MMS, on the other hand, can carry a larger amount of content. For example, MMS messages can include up to 300KB of content, which can extend to include files like WAV (audio), JPEG (pictures), and GIF (animated images).\\n\\n3. **Support and Usage**: Most cell phones support SMS, making it widely used for basic text communication. MMS is more commonly used for sending photos or videos, especially when a cell phone's camera is used to take and send images directly to another phone.\\n\\nThese differences highlight that while SMS is the foundational service for text messaging, MMS enhances this functionality by allowing users to communicate with a broader range of multimedia content.\", \"SMS allows you to send text, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four.\"]", "time_sec": 20.113, "generation_time_seconds": 19.1545, "selection_time_seconds": 0.9524, "record_process": true, "trajectories": [{"rollout": 0, "sampled": false, "token_ids": [65565, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 1467, 1172, 11, 1393, 386, 4826, 6147, 498, 311, 3624, 9185, 11, 10362, 11, 6803, 11, 1467, 11, 476, 894, 10601, 315, 279, 3040, 13, 151645], "pred": "SMS allows you to send text only, while MMS allows you to send pictures, sounds, videos, text, or any combination of the four.", "grounding_scores": {"g_mean_claim": 1.7423903942108154, "g_worst_claim": 0.36852145195007324, "g_content": 3.058225949605306, "g_traj_mean": 1.63688063621521}}, {"rollout": 1, "sampled": true, "token_ids": [65565, 13352, 369, 10698, 4856, 5362, 323, 374, 1083, 16626, 13862, 31